{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik","Jakobsen, Uffe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828575"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danskit kalaallit namminersorlutik oqartussaanerannut namminersulerusunnerannut aamma kiffaanngissuseqartumik peqatigiinnermut qisuariaataat nuummi tórshavnimilu akunnattoorfiit i gad u red naalagaaffeqatigiinnerup iluani akunnattoorfiit","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.diis.dk/ws/files/27748628/Dilemmaer_Rigsf_llesskabet_DIIS_Report_2025_12.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828575","ids":["ku-2ddc1a76-3e1f-4e57-81f1-4e427b7538e4"],"lang":"Kalaallisut","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AC1731C42AB531E9E78827FA07A9A073"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.diis.dk/ws/files/27748628/Dilemmaer_Rigsf_llesskabet_DIIS_Report_2025_12.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, International Relations"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Uffe","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"3253599b-6c78-4522-a1c6-87f06fe37df7","name":"Jakobsen, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0002-7114-1981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Naalagaaffeqatigiinnerup iluani akunnattoorfiit"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2ddc1a76-3e1f-4e57-81f1-4e427b7538e4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DANSKIT KALAALLIT NAMMINERSORLUTIK OQARTUSSAANERANNUT, NAMMINERSULERUSUNNERANNUT AAMMA 'KIFFAANNGISSUSEQARTUMIK PEQATIGIINNERMUT' QISUARIAATAAT: NUUMMI TÓRSHAVNIMILU AKUNNATTOORFIIT i Gad, U (red.) Naalagaaffeqatigiinnerup iluani akunnattoorfiit","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828575","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Cardiogenic shock (CS) is associated with high mortality and medical therapies have failed to improve survival. Treatment with lactate is associated with improved cardiac function which may benefit this condition. Comprehensive hemodynamic assessment of lactate administration in CS is lacking, and the mechanisms underlying the cardiovascular effects of lactate in CS have not yet been elucidated. In this study we aimed to study the cardiovascular and cardiometabolic effects of treatment with lactate in experimental ischemic CS. Methods: In a randomized, blinded design, 20 female pigs (60 kg) were studied. Left main coronary artery microsphere injections were used to cause CS, defined as a 30% reduction in CO or mixed venous saturation (SvO2). Subjects were randomized to receive either intravenous exogenous lactate or euvolemic, equimolar saline (control) for 180 min. Positive inotropic control with dobutamine was administered on top of ongoing treatment after 180 min. Extensive hemodynamic measurements were obtained from pulmonary artery and left ventricular (LV) pressure–volume catheterization. Furthermore, endomyocardial biopsies were analyzed for mitochondrial function and arterial, renal vein, and coronary sinus blood samples were collected. The primary endpoint was change in CO during 180 min of treatment. Results: Arterial lactate levels increased from 2.4 ± 1.1 to 7.7 ± 1.1 mmol/L (P < 0.001) during lactate infusion. CO increased by 0.7 L/min (P < 0.001) compared with control, due to increased stroke volume (P = 0.003). Notably, heart rate and mean arterial pressure did not differ significantly between treatments. End-systolic elastance (load independent contractility) was enhanced during lactate infusion (P = 0.048), together with LV ejection fraction (P = 0.009) and dP/dt(max) (P = 0.041). Arterial elastance (afterload) did not differ significantly (P = 0.12). This resulted in improved ventriculo-arterial coupling efficiency (P = 0.012). Cardiac mechanical efficiency (P = 0.003), diuresis (P = 0.016), and SvO2 (P = 0.018) were increased during lactate infusion. Myocardial mitochondrial complex I respiration was enhanced during lactate infusion compared with control (P = 0.04). Concomitant administration of dobutamine on top of lactate resulted in further hemodynamic improvements compared with control. Conclusions: Lactate infusion improved cardiac function and myocardial mitochondrial respiration in a porcine model of CS. The hemodynamic effects included increased CO mediated through stroke volume increase. These favorable cardiovascular effects may benefit patients with CS.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hørsdal, Oskar Kjærgaard","Ellegaard, Mark Stoltenberg","Larsen, Alexander Møller","Guldbrandsen, Halvor Østerby","Moeslund, Niels","Eifer Møller, Jacob","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Wiggers, Henrik","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Gopalasingam, Nigopan","Berg-Hansen, Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S02-086.61-804173"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hørsdal, Oskar Kjærgaard"],"keyword":["Animals","Cardiac Output","Cardiogenic shock","Cardiometabolic","Disease Models Animal","Female","Hemodynamics","Hemodynamics drug effects","Lactate","Lactic Acid blood","Mitochondrial function","Myocardial Ischemia drug therapy","Swine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lactate infusion improves cardiac function in a porcine model of ischemic cardiogenic shock","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-025-05346-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.61-804173","identifier":[{"id":"105000182414","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11907994","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40083003","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a4cbf075-564c-42bb-b328-946e2ebd13d7","sdu-afcb8d7f-9c9a-4d08-8952-9eaac890c7b0"],"keyword":["Animals","Cardiac output","Cardiogenic shock","Cardiometabolic","Disease Models, Animal","Female","Hemodynamics","Hemodynamics/drug effects","Infusions, Intravenous/methods","Lactate","Lactic Acid/blood","Mitochondrial function","Myocardial Ischemia/drug therapy","Shock, Cardiogenic/drug therapy","Swine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-444CD1194BC2A870A9F367381557AE94"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/287116087/s13054-025-05346-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-025-05346-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"no