o","key":"zaccagnapau","last":"Zaccagna","name":"Zaccagna, Fulvio","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16 17","corresponding":null,"first":"Vlad","key":"zahapau","last":"Zaha","name":"Zaha, Vlad","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Duan","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Duan","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"vigneronpau","last":"Vigneron","name":"Vigneron, Daniel","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40523079"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mrm.30570","issn":["07403194","15222594"],"issn_org":["07403194"],"issue":"4","journal":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","pages":"1386-1400","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","volume":"94"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008553914"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f17b5f08-25cc-4bc8-8f79-7731f3ff3a51"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Consensus recommendations for hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate MRI multi-center human studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816945","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background Antibiotic treatment of piglets after birth is commonly carried out due to concern for development of omphalitis leading to umbilical outpouchings and/or systemic infections. Among others, the portal of entry for bacterial infections includes the umbilical cord at birth. The aim was to characterise the histological and bacteriological pattern of manifestations in the umbilicus of piglets with omphalitis that died during the suckling period in a Danish herd. Results A total of 37 piglets found dead or euthanised due to sickness before weaning were included. Histopathological omphalitis was diagnosed in 13 of these piglets, and umbilical lesions and bacteria were most often observed in association with the umbilical blood vessels. Neutrophilic granulocyte infiltrations were observed in association with both umbilical arteries and the vein, occurring most frequently in the arteries. Escherichia coli and Trueperella pyogenes were the most commonly isolated bacteria from piglets with histopathological omphalitis. Conclusions Omphalitis in piglets was characterized by inflammation and presence of bacteria in the umbilical arteries and to a lesser extent the umbilical vein. Inflammation in urachus was not present.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","Hartmann, Katrine Top","Hansen, Mette Sif","Pedersen, Ken Steen","Larsen, Inge","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Olsen, John Elmerdahl","Kudirkiene, Egle","Barington, Kristiane"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828651"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"histopathological characterisation of omphalitis in piglets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-025-00826-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828651","identifier":[{"id":"105014746620","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40877961","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-373a4a49-efb3-446f-b35f-8bec00130536"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C408C971BCC4687E79D664B7812AB8C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-025-00826-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/463723832/Histopathological_characterisation_of_omphalitis_in_piglets.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Ø-Vet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie Amalie","key":"blirupplumsophieamaliepau","last":"Blirup-Plum","locid":"54f7ba11-2529-4cf7-adb1-139dfa0e4b53","name":"Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenhenrikelvangpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Saxmose","key":"nielsensørensaxmosepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8d00f12a-fe80-48ba-96c2-6769b91281e7","name":"Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","orcid":"0000-0003-2417-0787","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine Top","key":"hartmannkatrinetoppau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"24872909-edcd-41d3-ac0e-6d89e6fef67b","name":"Hartmann, Katrine Top","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Sif","key":"hansenmettesifpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"cf95e878-fe91-4715-b9f7-05fc972de6c6","name":"Hansen, Mette Sif","orcid":"0000-0002-8132-8475","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenkensteenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge","key":"larseningepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"82b09bf9-73d5-4c71-a3c1-01e66b0e9ebe","name":"Larsen, Inge","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-2241","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenjenspeterpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e550301c-f89e-4a8b-bf34-e6fc3b76ff37","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenjohnelmerdahlpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Egle","key":"kudirkieneeglepau","last":"Kudirkiene","name":"Kudirkiene, Egle","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristiane","key":"baringtonkristianepau","last":"Barington","locid":"0913e657-6538-4dea-a32f-5f97b7acc33c","name":"Barington, Kristiane","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40877961"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13028-025-00826-5","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","paperid":"42","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105014746620"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","ø-vet a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-373a4a49-efb3-446f-b35f-8bec00130536"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Histopathological characterisation of omphalitis in piglets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828651","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Cerebral palsy (CP) is a neurological disorder that impairs motor control and coordination, often leading to physical and social restrictions in daily activities. This single-arm feasibility study investigates the potential efficacy of virtual moderate- to high-intensity cycling at home among individuals with CP. Methods: Twenty-three individuals with CP (GMFCS I-IV; 16 males; mean age 26, range 13–58 years) were recruited for a 12-week home-based cycling intervention. The intervention included three weekly sessions, which could be completed either in an online coach-led group setting or independently, along with guidance for additional training. The primary focus was feasibility, addressed by retention, adherence, and safety. Efficacy was primarily evaluated using a functional threshold power test for cycling (FTP), the Timed Up and Go Test (TUG), and the Sit to Stand test (STS), assessed before and after the intervention, and secondly via self-reported questionnaires. Results: The intervention was demonstrated to be safe and feasible, with no adverse events reported. Retention was high, with only one dropout attributed to mononucleosis. The remaining 22 participants completed the study with a high attendance averaging 3.1 sessions/week [range 2–5]. Improvements were observed in the FTP test (67.2 ± 37.3 W, p < 0.001), the TUG test (2.1 ± 1.4 s, p < 0.001), and the STS test (3.9 ± 3.3 repetitions, p < 0.001) while self-reported fatigue, pain, sleep, well-being, and self-efficacy remained unchanged. Discussion: Our findings suggest that virtual cycling at home is a safe and feasible approach to engage in moderate- to high-intensity exercise, enhance physical capacity, and improve functional activity outcomes for individuals with activity limitations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lisbeth Hoejkjaer","Kirk, Henrik","Lorentzen, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829610"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cerebral palsy","Feasibility","High intensity exercise","Home based"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Neuropotentiale, Physiotherapy Clinic"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the feasibility and efficacy of coach led virtual home based cycling among individuals with cerebral palsy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fneur.2025.1604061","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829610","identifier":[{"id":"105012018402","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001539258100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC12306483","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40734819","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ab35dbb9-9bde-49cb-bd50-c60f9bd9b6bb"],"keyword":["cerebral palsy","feasibility","high-intensity exercise","home-based","virtual cycling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CE42464859B10DE8EC2F77E680C35C50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/459029534/fneur-1-1604061.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fneur.2025.1604061","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Motor Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Neuropotentiale, Physiotherapy Clinic"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lisbeth Hoejkjaer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"332b43b7-7a50-4c2e-be3e-371ab4d4b90f","name":"Larsen, Lisbeth Hoejkjaer","orcid":"0000-0002-1876-9876","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Henrik","key":"kirkpau","last":"Kirk","name":"Kirk, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jakob","key":"lorentzenpau","last":"Lorentzen","locid":"70660ba7-a635-4350-b486-ea6a118a0d3b","name":"Lorentzen, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-7634-0218","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40734819"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fneur.2025.1604061","issn":["16642295"],"journal":"Frontiers in Neurology","paperid":"1604061","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Neurology","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012018402"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab35dbb9-9bde-49cb-bd50-c60f9bd9b6bb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The feasibility and efficacy of coach-led virtual home-based cycling among individuals with cerebral palsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829610","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Subacromial pain syndrome is the leading cause of shoulder pain, commonly affecting the supraspinatus and infraspinatus rotator cuff muscles. Speckle-tracking ultrasonography offers a direct, non-invasive method to assess muscle function by measuring percentage deformation (strain) during contraction, but its application in patients with subacromial pain syndrome is unknown. The aim of the study was to investigate whether differences in muscle strain in the supraspinatus and infraspinatus muscles were associated with increasing external isometric muscle force in patients with subacromial pain syndrome. Methods: This cross-sectional study assessed 24 patients with subacromial pain syndrome using speckle-tracking ultrasonography during submaximal isometric contractions (20 % to 80 % of maximal voluntary isometric contraction) of the supraspinatus and infraspinatus muscles. Muscle strain was analyzed with the commercial EchoPAC™ software. Associations between strain and external isometric force were evaluated using repeated measures ANOVA and multiple linear regression analyses (adjustment for pain, sex, and age). Findings: Muscle strain generally increased with external loads (p < 0.001), except between 60 % and 80 % of maximal voluntary isometric contraction for supraspinatus (p = 0.12). Strain explained a large proportion of the variance in muscle force for both supraspinatus (r 2 = 0.55, p < 0.001) and infraspinatus (r 2 = 0.69, p < 0.001). Interpretation: Strain assessed via speckle-tracking ultrasonography explained a large proportion of the variation in supraspinatus and infraspinatus muscle force among patients with subacromial pain syndrome. However, from a clinical perspective, its diagnostic accuracy in distinguishing between healthy and pathological skeletal muscle conditions remains to be established.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Brekke, Anders Falk","Krag-Andersen, Katrine Kindtler","Frich, Lars Henrik","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","Jacobsen, Peter","Knold, Frederik Sylvest","Juhl, Carsten Bogh","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-097.27-823081"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Brekke, Anders Falk"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between speckle tracking ultrasonography and isometric load of shoulder muscles in patients with subacromial pain syndrome a cross sectional study","src":["pha","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2025.106616","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.27-823081","identifier":[{"id":"105010952092","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["pha-9d6a17f3-884a-48e5-b80a-00150f3fc6de","sdu-71459889-5cf1-45b0-bf02-9190c65f4f8d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D716A8FF8DE5CE19048C2C743B859E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2025.106616","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/293390034/PIIS0268003325001895.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev og Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Falk","key":"brekkepau","last":"Brekke","locid":"4061ee4c-9b8b-44c5-b878-5f731fd35547","name":"Brekke, Anders Falk","orcid":"0000-0002-4105-8722","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Kindtler","key":"kragandersenpau","last":"Krag-Andersen","locid":"953f4192-62de-4791-90af-a4d6caa3720d","name":"Krag-Andersen, Katrine Kindtler","orcid":"0009-0007-4028-7084","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"frichpau","last":"Frich","locid":"f5e4ebc5-0851-429f-ae70-b627b21b3d91","name":"Frich, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0147-4211","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kate Lykke","key":"lambertsenpau","last":"Lambertsen","locid":"d867cc02-bda7-455d-8d02-8b602e35e7b3","name":"Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","orcid":"0000-0001-9276-4902","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"5fe41651-1e1d-4097-8a6d-8f99d2fd9ee9","name":"Jacobsen, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Sylvest","key":"knoldpau","last":"Knold","locid":"955ae16e-d71f-4724-a5b1-5e00120ae90c","name":"Knold, Frederik Sylvest","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"9381fad1-5721-4b98-ac99-7df1c6e4d837","name":"Juhl, Carsten Bogh","name_org":"Juhl, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-8456-5364","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2025.106616","issn":["02680033","18791271"],"issn_org":["02680033"],"journal":"Clinical Biomechanics","paperid":"106616","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Biomechanics","volume":"128"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010952092"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-9d6a17f3-884a-48e5-b80a-00150f3fc6de","sdu-71459889-5cf1-45b0-bf02-9190c65f4f8d"],"src":["AB University College Absalon","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association between speckle-tracking ultrasonography and isometric load of shoulder muscles in patients with subacromial pain syndrome – A cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.27-823081","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The Copenhagen Hospital Biobank-chronic inflammatory disease—inflammatory bowel disease (CHB-CID: IBD) cohort contributes to genetic research in inflammatory bowel disease, including Crohn’s disease and ulcerative colitis. Of the 327,084 enrolled and genotyped individuals in the cohort, 10,626 have been diagnosed with IBD as of May 2023. The CHB-CID: IBD cohort includes both patients without IBD and healthy blood donors as control groups. Clinical data is collected from Danish registries and patient records, including details on hospital contacts, co-morbidities, medication, surgical procedures, and laboratory investigations. The cohort features a wide age range (> 18 years), extensive population coverage representative of Danish adults, and validated IBD diagnoses. Finally, the cohort benefits from continuous recruitment and regular updates of clinical information. The aim is to enhance IBD management and ultimately improve patients’ quality of life.","author_count":99,"contributors":["Darbani, Behrooz","Brodersen, Thorsten","Liljensøe, Anette","Sørensen, Signe Bek","Olsson-Svendsen, Josephine Bjergbæk","Buil, Alfonso","Kamal, Ahmed","Schork, Andrew J","Poulsen, Anja","Kjerulff, Bertram","Aagaard, Bitten","Lund, Britta Ørnfelt","Rittig, Charlotte Siggaard","Mikkelsen, Christina","Larsen, Daniel Millencourt","Westergaard, David","Rudbeck-Resdal, Ditte","Mikkelsen, Dorte Helenius","Randers, Else","Schiødt, Frank Vinholt","Hoffmann, Hans Jürgen","Jørgensen, Isabella Friis","Brandslund, Ivan","Brodersen, Jacob Broder","von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","Bay, Jakob Thaning","Nissen, Janna","Sørensen, Jeanette","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Dowsett, Joseph","Gladov, Josephine","Banasik, Karina","Kaspersen, Kathrine Agergård","Carlsen, Katrine","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Kellermann, Lauge","Christoffersen, Lea Arregui Nordahl","Quinn, Liam James Elgaard","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Larsen, Lone","Aamann, Luise","Andersen, Malene Rohr","Didriksen, Maria","Alexandraki, Maria Joanna","Thomsen, Marianne Kragh","Julsgaard, Mette","Nyegaard, Mette","Schwinn, Michael","Topholm-Bruun, Mie","Leite, Mikael Njai","Halling, Morten Lee","Pedersen, Natalia","Bonderup, Ole Kristian","Rohde, Palle Duun","Ovesen, Pernille Dige","Dessau, Ram Benny","Saboori, Sanaz","Holm-Christensen, Sofie","Bank, Steffen","Mikkelsen, Susan","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Werge, Thomas","Qvist, Niels","Sørensen, Erik","Burisch, Johan","Hetland, Merete Lund","Glintborg, Bente","Erikstrup, Christian","Brunak, Søren","Ullum, Henrik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","Andersen, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S03-094.41-813496"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Darbani, Behrooz"],"keyword":["Crohn s disease","Faecal Calprotectin","Genetic cohort","Genetic relatedness","Inflammatory bowel disease","Ulcerative colitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALK","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-ALK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cohort profile copenhagen hospital biobank chronic inflammatory disease inflammatory bowel disease chb cid ibd genetic cohort","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-025-01239-4","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by University of Southern Denmark. TARCID was funded by the Novo Nordisk Fonden (NNF15OC0016932, Vibeke Andersen), Knud og Edith Eriksens Mindefond (Vibeke Andersen), and Gigtforeningen (A2037, A3570, Vibeke Andersen). DBDS is funded by an annual grant from Bio- and Genome Bank Denmark. The initiation of DBDS was supported by the Danish Administrative Regions (02/2611) and the Danish Council for Independent Research (09\\u2013069412). Additionally, the DBDS is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF23OC0082015, NNF17OC0027864, and NNF17OC0027594). CHB sample collection was facilitated by the infrastructure of Bio- and Genome Bank Denmark. Furthermore, CHB is supported by the Department of Clinical Immunology, Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, Copenhagen, Denmark and by grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF23OC0082015, NNF17OC0027594) and Rigshospitalet Research Council (Framework grant). DRB was funded by the Danish Rheumatism Association and Danish Regions. Danish Regions are funding the continued collection of biological samples and clinical data. All personal fees and grants were received outside this work. Anja Poulsen reports research grants and personal fees from Janssen, Takeda, and MSD, personal fees from Bristol Myers Squibb, national coordinator of studies from Agomab, Boehringer Ingelheim and Bristol Myers. Bente Glintborg has received research grants (paid to institution) from AbbVie, Pfizer, BMS, Sandoz. Bente Glintborg chairs the DANBIO steering committee. Jacob Broder Brodersen has received consultation fee from Jansen-Cilag. Johan Burisch reports grants and personal fees from AbbVie, Janssen-Cilag, Takeda, Tillots Pharma, Bristol Myers Squibb, and MSD, personal fees from Celgene, Pfizer, Samsung Bioepis, Pharmacosmos, Ferring, Galapagos, and Eli Lilly, and grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation. Mette Julsgaard has received research grants from Takeda and the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF23OC0081717), has been on the advisory board of PharmaCosmos, has received consultation fee from Ferring and Takeda, and has received speaker\\u2019s fees from Tillotts Pharma, MSD, Ferring, and Takeda. Vibeke A ndersen has served as advisory board member for MSD (Merck). S\\u00F8ren Brunak has ownerships in Intomics A/S, Hoba Therapeutics Aps, Novo Nordisk A/S, Lundbeck A/S, ALK abello A/S, Eli Lilly and Co and managing board memberships in Proscion A/S and Intomics A/S. Thorsten Brodersen\\u2019s spouse currently holds incentive stock options in LEO Pharma A/S. All other authors declare no conflict of interest. We thank all the participating patients and blood donors who participate in DBDS, collaborating partners, blood centers, and the Danish hospitals for their valuable contributions. We thank deCODE genetic-Iceland for genotyping and imputation. S\\u00F8ren Brunak acknowledges Novo Nordisk Foundation (grants NNF17OC0027594 and NNF14CC0001). The authors wish to thank Ditlev Nytoft Rasmussen, Miriam Viktov Thygesen, and Gitte B. Fuusager for his contribution to TARCID."],"id":"S03-094.41-813496","identifier":[{"id":"105007672762","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40488802","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12263709","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-ed9ac142-b1da-4775-9fa9-c44d1679fa45","au-188bade2-a9a2-4d12-883d-5d064d52ff97","ku-8bde7dc9-711a-4d82-96b4-b5ea91d26a9a"],"keyword":["Crohn’s disease","Faecal Calprotectin","Genetic cohort","Genetic relatedness","Inflammatory bowel disease","Ulcerative colitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A8E9DB723037324D70D51C24E4FE2B02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-025-01239-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/787941589/Open_Access_Article.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/457149839/s10654-025-01239-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","coun