and Mental Health Disorders: Breaking the Cycle","title":"Abstract Book 14th Congress of The European Pain Federation EFIC"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-66ac37fe-c028-46d5-b5ba-f6c97fedf487"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Effects of Exercise and Pain Neuroscience Education on Sensitization in Patients with Chronic Pain after Total Knee Arthroplasty. : Secondary Analysis from Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814517","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Acute heart failure (AHF) is associated with high mortality and contemporary medical treatments provide limited benefits in survival. Emerging evidence suggests that exogenous ketone bodies may have beneficial cardiovascular effects in patients with heart failure. The KETO-AHF trial is designed to assess the clinical benefits of initiating ketone supplementation with 1,3-butanediol compared with placebo in patients hospitalized for AHF with reduced ejection fraction. METHODS: KETO-AHF is a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial investigating the effects of 1,3-butanediol (33 g three times daily) in patients hospitalized for AHF. Patients with symptoms and signs of AHF requiring intravenous loop diuretics and/or vasoactive treatment, elevated natriuretic peptides, and a left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%, whether de novo or known heart failure, will be enrolled within five days of hospital admission. Participants will be randomized 1:1 to receive either 1,3-butanediol or placebo for a 30-day treatment period. The study aims to enroll 125 patients in each group. The primary endpoint is a hierarchical composite of all-cause mortality, heart failure rehospitalization, six-minute walk test improvement, and reduction in NT-proBNP levels at 30 days. CONCLUSION: The KETO-AHF trial will provide insights into the effects of supplementation with the ketone body 1,3-butanediol in patients hospitalized for AHF.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Berg-Hansen, Kristoffer","Tinggaard, Andreas Bugge","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Jensen, Thomas Hvid","Gopalasingam, Nigopan","Larsen, Anders Hostrup","Møller, Niels","Böttcher, Morten","Hollingdal, Malene","Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","Antonsen, Lisbeth","Kondo, Toru","Jhund, Pardeep S","Borlaug, Barry A","Mebazaa, Alexandre","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Vraa, Søren","Grand, Johannes","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Wolsk, Emil","Schou, Morten","Wiggers, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-825797"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Japan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mayo Clinic Jacksonville, FL","Nagoya University","Universite Paris 5","University of Glasgow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"should exogenous ketone body supplementation be considered in patients hospitalized for acute heart failure rationale and design of the keto ahf trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-825797","identifier":[{"id":"40789530","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-909c9f82-9635-46c3-889a-612c9d3391f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9AD47C88543A5F657D27756591BDB2BA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Aarhus University Hospital","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus Uni