f Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"schmidtandersenpau","last":"Schmidt-Andersen","name":"Schmidt-Andersen, P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"N. N.","key":"boensvangpau","last":"Boensvang","name":"Boensvang, N. N.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"pouplierpau","last":"Pouplier","name":"Pouplier, A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"lykkedegnpau","last":"Lykkedegn","locid":"8ad1ec10-ae62-4571-90be-4680d1f12a80","name":"Lykkedegn, Sine","name_org":"Lykkedegn, S.","orcid":"0000-0003-3018-937X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H.","key":"haslepau","last":"Hasle","locid":"bde24b22-8663-440f-ae65-37d61f0a8975","name":"Hasle, Henrik","name_org":"Hasle, H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"K.","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","locid":"b909f13e-79e3-4363-aaff-e5a5ecbdf7ce","name":"Müller, Klaus","name_org":"Müller, K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"J.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"ba827c6e-b40b-461d-b241-5d43d576f0cd","name":"Christensen, Jan","name_org":"Christensen, J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1114-7465","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. K.","key":"fridhpau","last":"Fridh","name":"Fridh, M. K.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"H. B.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"88b48e37-454f-41e8-a110-a385dce66a6e","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","name_org":"Larsen, H. B.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/ecc/8305173","issn":["09615423","13652354"],"issn_org":["09615423"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Cancer Care","paperid":"8305173","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cancer Care","volume":"2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105006682447"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0227dbef-efc3-4211-82b9-8664fdd5eef7","ku-99e9ecb5-44c0-456d-849c-7c1b7feb7b1a","sdu-0c1e6667-9b0b-4704-a854-f10178910455"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exploring Motivation for Engaging in Exercise During the First Six Months of Childhood Cancer Treatment : A Qualitative Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.96-813528","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Purpose To explore content validity, construct validity, and reliability of anchor questions used to determine minimal important change (MIC), patient acceptable symptom state (PASS) and treatment failure (TF) in patients undergoing knee or hip arthroplasty. Methods A mixed-methods study from one public hospital. Evaluation of content validity involved applying thematic analysis to data from think-aloud interviews. To ascertain construct validity and reliability, we focused on patients who underwent surgery between 2016 and 2022 and had responded to preoperative and either 3-, 12- or 24-month postoperative questionnaires. Confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) was employed to assess present state bias (PSB), model fit, and reliability of the anchor questions. Results We conducted 18 interviews with patients aged 52 to 84 (10 female). Based on seven emerging themes from the content validity analysis, MIC and PASS anchor questions were considered relevant and comprehensible, while the TF anchor question had several problems. Data from 1197 to 2207 patients, with 3-, 12-, or 24-month postoperative responses, were used to evaluate construct validity. The median age was 69-70 years (56-59% female). PSB for MIC was between 54 and 73%, and reliability for the anchor questions was between 0.52 and 0.80 for all time points. The CFA models varied between good and poor fit. Conclusion The MIC and PASS anchor questions demonstrated a high degree of content validity, while it was questionable for TF. Construct validity was considered good to poor for PASS, but patients may consider their present state more than their preoperative state when responding to the MIC. Reliability was considered acceptable in both MIC and PASS.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Harris, Lasse Kindler","Larsen, Trine Schifter","Terluin, Berend","Lauridsen, Henrik Hein","Troelsen, Anders","Ingelsrud, Lina Holm"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-822965"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Harris, Lasse K"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam Public Health","Amsterdam Public Health Research Institute","Amsterdam UMC","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Vrije University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Anchor question","Construct validity","Content validity","Hip arthroplasty","Knee arthroplasty","Reliability"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anchor questions to improve patient reported outcome measure interpretability in patients undergoing knee or hip arthroplasty a mixed methods content validity construct validity and reliability study","src":["ku","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11136-025-03987-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.97-822965","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12274218","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105005097067","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40377835","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5ff89c1f-01c4-440b-ae10-0f53c7f00e65","ruc-a0749b42-693a-4f70-acf0-af183a520ff0","sdu-33d737d6-3725-445c-82ca-7e009d3e34f8"],"keyword":["Anchor question","Construct validity","Content validity","Hip arthroplasty","Knee arthroplasty","Reliability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-538DE5FCE4E9ED3C6A93A205258185EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/460347700/s11136-025-03987-y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://fi