{"abstract":"Afrapportering for følgeforskningen i forbindelse med Kompetenceudviklingsprogrammet Strategisk Byledelse for kommunale direktører, fagchefer og kommunalpolitikere","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jensen, Henrik Toft","Larsen, Majken Toftager"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811817"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Efteruddannelse","Følgeforskning","Strategisk byledelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strategisk byledelse følgeforskning afsluttende rapport kursusgennemførelse og kursusudvikling","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/109865993/SBL_slutrapport_25-03-04A.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811817","ids":["ruc-2e6a2d02-8a1a-440c-89d5-807a0703cd58"],"keyword":["Efteruddannelse","Følgeforskning","Kommunaldirektører","Strategisk byledelse"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-43F9584882C2FA0F39B3A25D160E71F4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/109865993/SBL_slutrapport_25-03-04A.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Mobility, Space, Place and Urban Studies (MOSPUS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d866383f-d187-46ec-9bce-88c4d27bc7d9","name":"Jensen, Henrik Toft","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Majken Toftager","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ec8eb20e-bd99-4097-9121-111a0b81eb67","name":"Larsen, Majken Toftager","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788791362835"],"pages":"142","place":"Roskilde","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","series":"MOSPUS Research Paper Serie","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-2e6a2d02-8a1a-440c-89d5-807a0703cd58"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Strategisk byledelse, Følgeforskning : Afsluttende rapport, kursusgennemførelse og kursusudvikling","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811817","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Understanding and quantifying total organic nitrogen (TON) concentrations in streams and their spatial variation is essential for accurately assessing their importance for total nitrogen (TN) loadings to coastal waters and the possible sources of TON in the landscape. Total organic nitrogen constitutes almost 20% of the TN riverine loadings to Danish coastal waters. We used environmental monitoring data from 390 stations across Denmark to calculate indirectly measured annual average TON concentrations using a wide range of predictor variables. We then trained a machine learning model to predict spatially distributed average annual TON concentrations in Danish streams, achieving a mean error of 0 mg L−1 and a root-mean-squared error of 0.20 mg L−1. The mean annual predicted (measured) TON concentrations in Danish streams were 0.84 (0.70) mg L−1, with a standard deviation of 0.36 (0.31) mg L−1. The model is primarily driven by mean elevation and the percentages of agricultural land, tile-drained areas, lakes and carbon-enriched soils in the catchment. The developed model contributes to our understanding of the spatial variation in annual TON concentrations in streams at a national scale, supporting our understanding of processes driving nitrogen cycling.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Rasmus Rumph","Larsen, Søren Erik","Tornbjerg, Henrik","Thodsen, Hans","Kronvang, Brian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-815842"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Rasmus Rumph"],"keyword":["Machine learning","Organic nitrogen","SHAP","XGBoost"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling annual total organic nitrogen concentrations in streams using machine learning at national scale","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2024WR039451","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-815842","identifier":[{"id":"105007615392","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5f81b147-8c10-4a66-81b3-ea0361662dc9"],"keyword":["SHAP","TON","machine learning","organic nitrogen","stream water quality","xgboost"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A67C76B81C793C4FEE8680E22984BE0B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2024WR039451","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Catchment Science and Environmental Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus R.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"1c662dec-6ebd-4a2d-9c22-06ce91b316dc","name":"Frederiksen, Rasmus Rumph","name_org":"Frederiksen, Rasmus R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Søren E.","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"tornbjergpau","last":"Tornbjerg","locid":"673f9989-b651-4f14-8190-b60c45f9cde2","name":"Tornbjerg, Henrik","orcid":"0009-0008-7385-7490","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"thodsenpau","last":"Thodsen","locid":"32bff5cf-3478-427f-a25a-edc45f21b300","name":"Thodsen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0002-6542-4934","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian","key":"kronvangpau","last":"Kronvang","locid":"7766931c-a3c9-4a38-9d22-e4cc3a2f4607","name":"Kronvang, Brian","orcid":"0000-0003-1165-1354","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1029/2024wr039451","issn":["00431397","19447973"],"issn_org":["00431397"],"issue":"6","journal":"Water Resources Research","paperid":"e2024WR039451","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Water Resources Research","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007615392"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5f81b147-8c10-4a66-81b3-ea0361662dc9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Modeling Annual Total Organic Nitrogen Concentrations in Streams Using Machine Learning at National Scale","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-815842","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Individuals with type 1 diabetes are at high risk of cardiovascular disease (CVD) and chronic kidney disease (CKD) even with optimal glycaemic control. The Steno 1 study will test a strategy of intensified care based on multifactorial intervention (MFI) including treatment with semaglutide, sotagliflozin and finerenone in high-risk individuals with type 1 diabetes. We hypothesize that this strategy will reduce major adverse cardiovascular endpoints (MACE), hospitalization for heart failure (HHF), progression of CKD and mortality. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The study is a prospective, cluster-randomized, open study with blinded endpoint evaluation. We will enrol 2000 high-risk individuals with type 1 diabetes of >10 years duration. All five Steno Diabetes Centres and 11 partner hospitals in Denmark will participate, with the addition of the Steno Diabetes Centres in Greenland and the Faroe Islands. Sites will be randomized either to receive guideline-recommended standard-of-care, or to receive the MFI. Eligible individuals with type 1 diabetes (≥40 years of age with presence of either CKD, CVD, HF, obesity or a >10% 5-year CVD risk determined by the Steno T1 Risk Engine) will be included. For the MFI group, the intervention will comprise more ambitious treatment targets for blood pressure and lipid levels, and in addition, participants will be allocated to semaglutide, sotagliflozin and/or finerenone based on phenotype. RESULTS AND CONCLUSIONS: The Steno 1 study will determine whether MFI is superior to standard care with respect to MACE, HHF progression of CKD, and mortality in individuals with type 1 diabetes and high risk of CVD.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Stougaard, Elisabeth B","Andersen, Mads R","Bagger, Jonatan I","Søndergaard, Esben","Østergaard, Jakob Appel","Curovic, Viktor R","Persson, Frederik","Almdal, Thomas","Mathiesen, Anne Sophie","Andries, Alin","Larsen, Mette Bohl","Nørgaard, Louise J","Dejgaard, Thomas F","Dørfinger, Gry H","Gustenhoff, Peter","Gæde, Peter H","Hamid, Yasmin H","Johannesen, Herborg L","Juhl, Claus B","Jørgensen, Marit E","Kielgast, Urd","Kofoed-Enevoldsen, Allan","Lindhardt, Morten","Mortensen, L S","Thomsen, Henrik Holm","Stidsen, Jacob","Sørensen, Lars P","Urhammer, Søren","Rossing, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824564"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"corpau":["Steno 1 Study Group"],"country":["Faroe Islands","Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Steno Diabetes Center Faroe Islands","Steno Diabetes Center Greenland"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the steno 000000000001 study multifactorial intervention to reduce cardiovascular disease in type 000000000001 diabetes rationale and protocol of the prospective randomized open labelled multicentre study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-824564","identifier":[{"id":"40726451","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1db3ba53-30ca-4ec1-a67a-ab46721b8d22"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-491E28A26E73669A1639834C827BC0B1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aa