{"abstract":"Podcast VIA Videre Hvad mon hvad mon bogstaverne: V A N E står for når Henrik Wøhlk underviser i hvordan Hr. Æsel får en ny vane. Vi diskuterer skabelse af vaner og identitet - et forsøg med transformativ entreprenørskabsdidaktik i undervisning","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Wøhlk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-831814"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adfærdsdesign","Identitet","Kultur","Nudge","Uddannelse professioner og erhverv","Vaner"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"henrik wøhlk om hr æsel får en ny vane via videre","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://open.spotify.com/episode/4e5FeA2dWi1T1HaOZji9c0","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-831814","ids":["via-4a071937-1f60-410c-82d0-cc0e3c6c6486"],"keyword":["Uddannelse, professioner og erhverv","adfærdsdesign","identitet","kultur","nudge","vaner"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-01E7291334CE166CB3F9C05205272DD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://open.spotify.com/episode/4e5FeA2dWi1T1HaOZji9c0","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, Forsk.center for professionsstudier","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, Program for Transformationer i Professioner og Uddannelser (TPU)","VIA, Uddannelser, Læreruddannelsen, HF og FIF-kurser, Læreruddannelsen Silkeborg team 2"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Wøhlk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ee25a99f-efad-420b-baff-7dadb13706de","name":"Larsen, Henrik Wøhlk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"VIA University College","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-4a071937-1f60-410c-82d0-cc0e3c6c6486"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Henrik Wøhlk om Hr. Æsel får en ny vane : VIA Videre","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-831814","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Glycolipid-lectin-driven endocytosis controls the formation of clathrin-independent carriers and the internalization of various cargos such as β1 integrin. Whether this process is regulated in a dynamic manner remained unexplored. Here we demonstrate that, within minutes, the epidermal growth factor triggers the galectin-driven endocytosis of cell-surface glycoproteins, such as integrins, that are key regulators of cell adhesion and migration. The onset of this process—mediated by the Na+/H+ antiporter NHE1 as well as the neuraminidases Neu1 and Neu3—requires the pH-triggered enzymatic removal of sialic acids whose presence otherwise prevents galectin binding. De-sialylated glycoproteins are then retrogradely transported to the Golgi apparatus where their glycan make-up is reset to regulate EGF-dependent invasive-cell migration. Further evidence is provided for a role of neuraminidases and galectin-3 in acidification-dependent bone resorption. Glycosylation at the cell surface thereby emerges as a dynamic and reversible regulatory post-translational modification that controls a highly adaptable trafficking pathway.","author_count":27,"contributors":["MacDonald, Ewan","Forrester, Alison","Valades-Cruz, Cesar A.","Madsen, Thomas Daugbjerg","Hetmanski, Joseph H.R.","Dransart, Estelle","Ng, Yeap","Godbole, Rashmi","Shp, Ananthan Akhil","Leconte, Ludovic","Chambon, Valérie","Ghosh, Debarpan","Pinet, Alexis","Bhatia, Dhiraj","Lombard, Bérangère","Loew, Damarys","Larsen, Martin R.","Leffler, Hakon","Lefeber, Dirk J.","Clausen, Henrik","Blangy, Anne","Caswell, Patrick","Shafaq-Zadah, Massiullah","Mayor, Satyajit","Weigert, Roberto","Wunder, Christian","Johannes, Ludger"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-804420"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Johannes, Ludger"],"country":["Belgium","China","France","India","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brunel University London","Chemical Biology of Membranes and Therapeutic Delivery Unit","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Donders Institute for Brain, Cognition and Behaviour","French Institute for Research in Computer Science and Automation","INSERM 1099","Indian Institute of Technology Gandhinagar","Institut Curie","Institut national de recherche en informatique et en automatique","Lund University","Montpellier University","National Cancer Institute","National Centre for Biological Sciences","National Institutes of Health","Radboud University Medical Center","Radboud University Nijmegen","Tata Institute of Fundamental Research","The University of Trans-Disciplinary Health Sciences and Technology","The University of Trans-disciplinary Health Sciences and Technology (TDU)","UMR 144","University of Manchester","University of Montpellier","University of Namur","University of Rennes","University of Warwick","WEL Research Institute","Wellcome Trust Centre for Cell-Matrix Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growth factor triggered de sialylation controls glycolipid lectin driven endocytosis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41556-025-01643-8","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-804420","identifier":[{"id":"39984654","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85218711814","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0e298d26-928f-4e68-b738-8c659f9f6250","sdu-5eb32fef-7404-4583-95c4-c1f7f0e7c1b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8DF5656569EB8E11B1E3