{"abstract":"Background MR-guided laser interstitial thermal therapy (LITT) is a minimally invasive neurosurgical treatment used for managing brain tumors and drug-resistant epilepsy. This study investigates the temporal pattern of blood-brain barrier (BBB) permeability following LITT in patients with tumors and epilepsy. Methods Twenty-three patients undergoing LITT (11 with brain tumors, 12 with non-tumor epilepsy) were enrolled. Dynamic Contrast-Enhanced Magnetic Resonance Imaging (DCE-MRI) and blood levels of glial fibrillary acidic protein (GFAP) were used to assess BBB permeability one day before and on days 1, 15, 30, and 45 post-LITT. Results Quantitative analysis using DCE-MRI demonstrated significant increases in perilesional BBB permeability on days 15, 30, and 45 postoperatively (P<.005), with no notable changes on the first postoperative day. The findings were robust with regards to region of interest selection, showing consistent increases in BBB permeability in patients with both brain tumors and epilepsy. Additionally, GFAP levels peaked significantly above baseline on the first postoperative day, maintaining elevated levels through day 45. Conclusions Quantitative DCE-MRI and GFAP blood levels demonstrate a prolonged window of increased perilesional BBB permeability following LITT, potentially enhancing the delivery and efficacy of therapeutic agents in patients with brain tumors.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Silas H.","Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","Larsen, Vibeke A.","Carlsen, Jonathan Frederik","Larsson, Henrik B W","Christoffersen, Christina","Rasmussen, Rune","Hansen, Adam Espe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830224"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blood brain barrier","Brain tumors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["DCCC Brain Tumor Center"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blood brain barrier disruption following mr guided laser interstitial thermal therapy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/noajnl/vdaf148","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830224","identifier":[{"id":"105011867650","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40718643","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12290448","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-f2d76f60-4de1-4125-b58d-0c82a5dc1bda"],"keyword":["MR-guided laser interstitial thermal therapy","blood-brain barrier","brain tumors","stereotactic laser ablation (SLA)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-22E4832E43C0E3EEC9F28C35ACD7DF01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/459370059/Blood-brain_barrier.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/noajnl/vdaf148","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DCCC Brain Tumor Center"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurosurgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Silas H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Silas H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","first":"Jane","key":"skjøthrasmussenpau","last":"Skjøth-Rasmussen","locid":"549d7d96-8a0c-4f6e-8a8e-2f9697a2aedc","name":"Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke A.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Jonathan F.","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","locid":"6507f93c-50e8-4070-9680-8c2415031f01","name":"Carlsen, Jonathan Frederik","name_org":"Carlsen, Jonathan F.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Henrik B.W.","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","locid":"3c09e175-dfd1-4df5-9132-536a42c19373","name":"Larsson, Henrik B W","name_org":"Larsson, Henrik B.W.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rune","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Rune","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40718643"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/noajnl/vdaf148","issn":["26322498"],"issue":"1","journal":"Neuro-Oncology Advances","paperid":"vdaf148","status":"p","title":"Neuro-Oncology Advances","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105011867650"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f2d76f60-4de1-4125-b58d-0c82a5dc1bda"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Blood-brain barrier disruption following MR-guided laser interstitial thermal therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830224","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarized 1-13C-pyruvate magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS) and MRS imaging (MRSI) offer noninvasive and real-time direct assessment of the altered metabolism of cancer cells known as the Warburg effect—a key hallmark of cancer. When combined with simultaneously acquired 18F-FDG PET in a PET/MR scanner, coined hyperPET by us, this dual-modality may unveil cancer-type specific glucose metabolic phenotypes with potential implications for patient prognostication, treatment-response assessment, and prediction. We here present the first human data of simultaneously acquired hyperpolarized MRS/MRSI and PET performed in a PET/MR scanner—and the first human hyperpolarized MRS/MRSI data from a patient with lymphoma.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Loft, Mathias","Clemmensen, Andreas","Christensen, Emil Nørgaard","Denholt, Charlotte Lund","Johannesen, Helle Hjorth","Gillings, Nic","Carlsen, Esben Andreas","Clausen, Malene Martini","Hutchings, Martin","Andersen, Thomas Lund","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Kjaer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S02-086.08-793569"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kjaer, Andreas"],"keyword":["1 C pyruvate","F FDG","Glycolysis","Lymphoma","PET MR","Warburg effect","hyperPET"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"first in human simultaneous hyperpolarized 000000000001 sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate magnetic resonance spectroscopy and sup 000000000018 sup f fdg pet hyperpet imaging of a patient with lymphoma","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85209366500","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.08-793569","identifier":[{"id":"85209366500","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39529265","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-bf3b5f09-b4cb-45b4-8093-7e185ae2e778","ku-287149f0-aa1f-4a2b-89d5-6c65f4b93130"],"keyword":["1-C-pyruvate","F-FDG","PET/MR","Warburg effect","glycolysis","hyperPET","hyperpolarized magnetic resonance","lymphoma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1919AE377BA718EA5151876CE42462F6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mathias","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft",