29265"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/rlu.0000000000005534","issn":["03639762","15360229"],"issn_org":["03639762"],"issue":"2","journal":"Clinical Nuclear Medicine","pages":"186-187","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nuclear Medicine","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209366500"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bf3b5f09-b4cb-45b4-8093-7e185ae2e778","ku-287149f0-aa1f-4a2b-89d5-6c65f4b93130"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"First-in-Human : Simultaneous Hyperpolarized 1-<sup>13</sup>C-Pyruvate Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy and <sup>18</sup>F-FDG PET (hyperPET) Imaging of a Patient With Lymphoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.08-793569","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) is highly lethal. Promoter hypermethylation of SFRP1 (phSFRP1) in cell-free DNA is an established prognostic biomarker in PDAC. We used digital droplet PCR (ddPCR) to examine whether the prognostic impact of phSFRP1 was allele fraction (AF) dependent. Methods: Prospectively collected plasma samples were analyzed blinded. Dual-strand methylation ddPCR assays were designed for SFRP1, with single-strand assay for the reference gene EPHA3. Patients were stratified into unmethylated SFRP1 (umSFRP1), low phSFRP1 AF (phSFRP1 low), and high phSFRP1 AF (phSFRP1 high). Survival was assessed with Kaplan–Meier curves. The 3-, 6-, and 12-month absolute risk difference (ARD) was calculated, and performance assessed with ROC analyses. Results: Overall, 354 patients were included. Patients with umSFRP1 (n=137) had a mOS of 9.1 months compared to 7.2 months in phSFRP1 low (n=78) and 3.4 months in phSFRP1 high (n=143, P<0.01). phSFRP1 high was associated with increased mortality at 3 (ARD 26%, 95%CI: 15, 37), 6 (ARD 37%, 95%CI: 26, 48), and 12 months (ARD 23%, 95%CI: 14, 33). phSFRP1 low was associated with increased mortality at 12 months (ARD 13%, 95%CI: 2, 25) but not at 3 (ARD -3%, 95%CI: -13, 8) or 6 months (ARD 3%, 95%CI: -10, 17). phSFRP1 significantly improved performance in predicting mortality compared to only clinical variables (AUC: 0.70-0.71 vs. 0.54-0.57). Discussion: Patients with phSFRP1 high had significantly shorter survival than phSFRP1 low or umSFRP1, indicating AF-dependent prognostic effects. phSFRP1 low had a worse prognosis than umSFRP1 at only 12 months, indicating dynamic changes. This could help personalize the treatment of PDAC.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Stubbe, Benjamin","Stoico, Malene Pontoppidan","Terp, Simone Karlsson","Madsen, Poul Henning","Lundbye-Christensen, Søren","Hansen, Carsten P","Poulsen, Laurids Østergaard","Rasmussen, Louise Skau","Yilmaz, Mette N","Jensen, Lars H","Hansen, Torben F","Pfeiffer, Per","Larsen, Anders Christian","Krarup, Henrik","Pedersen, Inge Søkilde","Hasselby, Jane P","Johansen, Astrid Z","Chen, Inna M","Johansen, Julia S","Thorlacius-Ussing, Ole","Henriksen, Stine Dam"],"cuid":["S02-099.08-813411"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stubbe, Benjamin"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Epigenetics","Liquid biopsy","Methylation","Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","Sfrp1"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"promoter hypermethylation of sfrp000000000001 is an allele fraction dependent prognostic biomarker in metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fonc.2025.1568386","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The author(s) declare that financial support was received for the research and/or publication of this article. This study was supported by two private foundations: The Speciall\\u00E6ge Heinrich Kopps foundation and the Svend Andersen Foundation. Acknowledgments"],"id":"S02-099.08-813411","identifier":[{"id":"105007624268","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12146188","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40492125","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-950bffdb-5817-48c3-b1fd-3a19b2ad959d","sdu-4b232519-ffbb-4a64-8093-7117e55f07da"],"keyword":["Sfrp1","biomarker","epigenetics","liquid biopsy","