:null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Thomas","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Christian Thomas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39182578"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cmi.2024.08.015","issn":["1198743X","14690691"],"issn_org":["1198743X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Clinical Microbiology and Infection","pages":"87-92","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Clinical Microbiology and Infection","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203787716"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-99d5dc1c-482f-4e49-b1b0-44d8e393d966","au-c1cb26da-8dc2-4d9a-8216-b9166b1452d0","sdu-7d5af62e-8de9-48fa-aefb-64d7a089d85f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Dexamethasone in adults with viral meningitis: an observational cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.93-803769","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose — Discharge on day of surgery after hip or knee arthroplasty is increasing, but whether this leads to an increase in the overall number of post-discharge healthcare system contacts is unknown. We aimed to investigate whether day-case surgery leads to increased patient-reported healthcare system contacts compared with non-day-case surgery within the first 30 days postoperatively. Methods — We performed a prospective multicenter study at seven fast-track centers from September 2022 to August 2023. Candidates for primary total hip arthroplasty (THA), total knee arthroplasty (TKA), or unicompartmental knee arthroplasty (UKA) were evaluated for day-case eligibility using pre-defined criteria. Patients received a survey 30 days postoperatively regarding any healthcare system contacts related to surgery. Planned healthcare visits were excluded. We used day-case eligible patients not discharged on day of surgery (inpatients) as control group. Results — Of 2,278 day-case eligible patients, 2,073 (91%) completed the survey, including 1,146 day-case patients (55%) and 927 inpatients (45%). The overall rate of health-care system contacts was 49% (95% confidence interval [CI] 45–51) in day-case patients compared with 52% (CI 49–56) in inpatients. Specific contacts included visits to a general practitioner (GP) or out-of-hours medical clinic (25% [CI 22–27] vs 32% [CI 29–35]), the emergency department (ED) (6% [CI 4–7] vs 7% [CI 5–8]), and outpatient clinics or wards (35% [CI 33–38] vs 35% [CI 32–38]). The most common reasons for all types of healthcare contacts were wound problems, prescription renewals, and pain management. Conclusion — Day-case hip and knee arthroplasties was not associated with increased healthcare system contacts within the first 30 days postoperatively.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hirsi, Abdullahi Abdirisak","Danielsen, Oddrún","Varnum, Claus","Jakobsen, Thomas","Andersen, Mikkel Rathsach","Bieder, Manuel Josef","Overgaard, Søren","Jørgensen, Christoffer Calov","Kehlet, Henrik","Gromov, Kirill","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S03-099.93-813315"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Hirsi, Abdullahi Abdirisak"],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty Replacement Hip","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee statistics numerical data","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Discharge statistics numerical data","Prospective Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"OT":["Center for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"day case hip and knee arthroplasty does not increase healthcare system contacts a prospective multicenter study in a public healthcare setting","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2025.43001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.93-813315","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11971722","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40099463","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105001156693","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-25e73c38-fdf7-44a6-b7c0-2dffbe253f04","ku-977d0077-6a74-45a2-b789-0bfd97f8d592","sdu-bc2b2f23-b3e8-46ee-aada-b4622747ba96"],"keyword":["Aged","Ambulatory Surgical Procedures/statistics & numerical data","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Hip","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/statistics & numerical data","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Discharge/statistics & numerical data","Prospective Studies"],"lang":"Engl