key":"gromovpau","last":"Gromov","locid":"efb84811-45bd-4724-97f5-e10d5b84525f","name":"Gromov, Kirill","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40099463"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/17453674.2025.43001","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"265-271","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001156693"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-25e73c38-fdf7-44a6-b7c0-2dffbe253f04","ku-977d0077-6a74-45a2-b789-0bfd97f8d592","sdu-bc2b2f23-b3e8-46ee-aada-b4622747ba96"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Day-case hip and knee arthroplasty does not increase healthcare system contacts : a prospective multicenter study in a public healthcare setting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.93-813315","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES: Multiple sclerosis (MS) is a CNS disease, characterized by demyelination, inflammation, and neurodegeneration. Recent advances in technology allow measurement of the axonal damage marker neurofilament light chain in peripheral blood. Two studies have shown that patients with MS have elevated neurofilament light levels before their first symptom, but longitudinal studies are lacking. We aimed to investigate the intraindividual neurofilament light dynamics during the presymptomatic phase of MS. METHODS: The Danish Blood Donor Study (DBDS) has stored plasma samples from blood donors for more than 10 years. We identified DBDS participants, who had subsequently been diagnosed with MS, and included all samples donated before their first demyelinating symptom (median 5.00 samples per case). As controls, we included 2 healthy donors per case. Plasma levels of neurofilament light were measured and compared with quality-of-life data. We used a Bayesian approach to derive estimates for the percentage of cases with presymptomatic increased neurofilament light levels. RESULTS: We observed that 12 (17%, 95% CI 9%-28%) of 69 presymptomatic MS donors had intermittently increased neurofilament light levels preclinically. Increased levels were present up to 9 years before clinical onset, also in primary progressive MS. Healthy donors and presymptomatic MS donors with and without increased neurofilament light levels reported equally high physical and mental well-being. Model-based estimates suggested that 55% of cases (95% credible interval [28%-87%]) had experienced increased presymptomatic neurofilament light levels. DISCUSSION: Patients with MS periodically sustain axonal injury up to 9 years before clinical onset, even in primary progressive disease. This most likely represents asymptomatic disease activity. Some or even all patients are affected by this intermittent axonal injury, prompting the need for further studies of the presymptomatic phase in relation to prognosis and as a therapeutic window of opportunity.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Britze, Josefine","Larsen, Margit Hørup","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Rosthøj, Susanne","Bach Søndergaard, Helle","Magyari, Melinda","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Aagaard, Bitten","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Erikstrup, Christian","Ullum, Henrik","Battistini, Jette Lautrup Frederiksen","Sellebjerg, Finn","Modvig, Signe"],"cuid":["S04-093.15-784786"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Modvig, Signe"],"keyword":["Adult","Asymptomatic Diseases","Biomarkers blood","Blood Donors","Denmark","Female","Humans","Longitudinal Studies","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple Sclerosis blood","Neurofilament Proteins blood","Prodromal Symptoms","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal dynamics of plasma neurofilament light in blood donors with preclinical multiple sclerosis","src":["aau","au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/NXI.0000000000200335","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study has received funding from The Multiple Sclerosis Foundation, The Jascha Foundation, The Dagmar-Marshall Foundation, The Direkt\\u00F8r Emil C. Hertz og Hustru Inger Hertz Foundation, The Torben og Alice Frimodts Foundation, and 