ournal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-093.15-784786","year":2025,"yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Our aim was to characterize the clinical presentation and outcome in adults with tick-borne encephalitis (TBE) and to determine the incidence and test activity of TBE in Denmark. METHODS: A nationwide prospective cohort study of all adults hospitalized with TBE at departments of infectious diseases in Denmark from 2015 to 2023. An age- and sex-matched cohort of herpes simplex virus type 1 (HSV-1) encephalitis patients was included to compare outcome. RESULTS: Fifty-two patients with TBE were included. Median age was 50 years, 32/52 (62%) were men, 1/52 (2%) was fully vaccinated against TBE at the time of infection, 29/52 (56%) were infected in Denmark. Upon admission 25/52 (48%) had meningitis, 27/52 (52%) encephalitis, three of the latter 3/52 (6%) with additional myelitis or radiculitis. Admission to the intensive care unit 6/52 (12%) and death 2/52 (4%) were associated with pre-existing comorbidities and older age. At 3-month follow-up, 16/50 (32%) had an unfavorable outcome (Glasgow Outcome Scale score 1-4) compared to 39/52 (75%) in the HSV-1 cohort. The most common residual symptoms at 6-month follow-up or later were headache, cognitive impairment, and fatigue. The TBE incidence increased from 0.03/100,000 in 2015 to 0.48/100,000 in 2023, and the test rate from 5.5/100,000 in 2015 to 14.4/100,000 in 2023, with a positivity rate of 0.6% in 2015 and 3.3% in 2023. CONCLUSION: The incidence of TBE in Denmark increased in the study period, with clinical characteristics and outcome of adult patients comparable to reports from other European countries.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Florescu, Anna Maria","Bryrup, Thomas","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Larsen, Lykke","Wiese, Lothar","Lüttichau, Hans Rudolf","Jepsen, Micha Phill Grønholm","Hansen, Birgitte Rønde","Østergaard, Christian","Søndergaard, Anja Vad","Andersen, Peter H S","Vestergaard, Lasse Skafte","Lassaunière, Ria","Fomsgaard, Anders","Jensen, Bo Bødker","Bodilsen, Jacob","Nielsen, Henrik","Lebech, Anne-Mette","Mens, Helene"],"cuid":["S04-094.44-803614"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Florescu, Anna Maria"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Clinical characteristics","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Encephalitis Tick Borne epidemiology","Female","Herpes simplex encephalitis","Humans","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Outcome","Prospective Studies","TBE","Test activity","Tick borne encephalitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tick borne encephalitis in adults in denmark a nationwide prospective cohort study from 000000002015 to 000000002023","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00415-025-12986-5","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by National Hospital"],"id":"S04-094.44-803614","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11876282","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"86000063538","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40029446","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-11c5ffe6-2ca1-497c-95ed-0d473a271f47","au-e576384c-561c-4a80-9285-8c3a66d0d3ba","ku-9a8b6797-6c12-420b-b869-6a763a2e2348","sdu-9d380fb5-fa6f-440a-add0-c042f085f98e"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Clinical characteristics","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Encephalitis, Tick-Borne/epidemiology","Female","Herpes simplex encephalitis","Humans","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Outcome","Pro