ental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8dcfbba3-02ab-4280-9725-ec8a39e09d2b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Mapping of seabed habitats and impacts of beam trawling and other demersal fisheries for spatial ecosystem-based management of the Jammer Bay (JAMBAY Executive Report)","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-775697","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) cerebral blood volume (CBV) measurements improve the diagnosis of recurrent gliomas. The study investigated the prognostic value of dynamic contrast-enhanced (DCE) CBV imaging in treated IDH wildtype glioblastoma when added to MRI or amino acid positron emission tomography (PET). METHODS: Hybrid [18F]FET PET/MRI with 2CXM (2-compartment exchange model) DCE from 86 adult patients with suspected recurrent or residual glioblastoma were retrospectively analyzed. High CBV tumor volume (VOLCBV), and contrast-enhancing (VOLCE) and [18F]FET active tumor (VOLFET) volumes were delineated. Absolute and fractional high CBV subvolumes within VOLCE and VOLFET were determined. Associations with overall survival (OS) were assessed by Cox analysis. RESULTS: Adjusted for methyltransferase gene status and steroid use all total tumor volumes were individually associated with shorter OS. Adding VOLCBV to VOLCE or VOLFET only the effect of VOLCBV was prognostic of OS (hazard ratio [HR] 1.327, P = .042 and 1.352, P = .011, respectively). High CBV subvolumes within both VOLCE and VOLFET were associated with shorter survival (HR 1.448, P = .042 and 1.416, P = .011, respectively), and the low CBV subvolumes with longer survival (HR 0.504, P = .002 and .365, P = .001, respectively). The fraction of VOLCE and VOLFET with high CBV was a strong predictor of OS with shorter median OS in upper versus lower tertiles (8.3 vs 14.5 months and 7.1 vs 15.6 months, respectively, both P < .001). CONCLUSIONS: The high CBV tumor volume was a strong prognosticator of survival and allowed for the separation of high- and low-risk subvolumes underlining the heterogeneous physiological environment represented in the contrast-enhancing or metabolically active tumor volumes of treated glioblastoma.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Henriksen, Otto Mølby","Muhic, Aida","Lundemann, Michael Juncker","Larsson, Henrik B W","Lindberg, Ulrich","Andersen, Thomas Lund","Hasselbalch, Benedikte","Møller, Søren","Marner, Lisbeth","Madsen, Karine","Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","Poulsen, Hans Skovgaard","Hansen, Adam Espe","Law, Ian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800146"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Danish Comprehensive Cancer Center"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"added prognostic value of dce blood volume imaging in patients with suspected recurrent or residual glioblastoma a hybrid sup 000000000018 sup f fet pet mri study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/noajnl/vdae196","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-800146","identifier":[{"id":"85219001710","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11632823","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39664680","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9e5f653f-88b1-4c72-a73e-363f93bd54b8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-692E963E09A48942FB89AE41A42B67F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/420981715/vdae196.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/noajnl/vdae196","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Comprehensive Cancer Center"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Otto Mølby","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Otto Mølby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Aida","key":"muhicpau","last":"Muhic","name":"Muhic, Aida","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Juncker","key":"lundemannpau","last":"Lundemann","name":"Lundemann, Michael Juncker","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Henrik Bo Wiberg","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","locid":"3c09e175-dfd1-4df5-9132-536a42c19373","name":"Larsson, Henrik B W","name_org":"Larsson, Henrik Bo Wiberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrich","key":"lindbergpau","last":"Lindberg","name":"Lindberg, Ulrich","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thomas Lund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"88c15341-15cb-46be-8481-09b7730d0c18","name":"Andersen, Thomas Lund","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Benedikte","key":"hasselbalchpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Benedikte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Søren","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lisbeth","key":"marnerpau","last":"Marner","locid":"bdc32ba4-8b70-4cae-807b-c3c8cfce3258","name":"Marner, Lisbeth","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karine","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Karine","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke Andrée","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hans Skovgaard","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Hans Skovgaard","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Adam Espe","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ian","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","locid":"fa2c54ee-d725-4edb-9918-8c6cbebfc84a","name":"Law, Ian","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39664680"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/noajnl/vdae196","issn":["26322498"],"issue":"1","journal":"Neuro-Oncology Advances","paperid":"vdae196","status":"p","title":"Neuro-Oncology Advances","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219001710"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9e5f653f-88b1-4c72-a73e-363f93bd54b8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Added prognostic value of DCE blood volume imaging in patients with suspected recurrent or residual glioblastoma - A hybrid [<sup>18</sup>F]FET PET/MRI study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-800146","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The DEX-2-TKA trial demonstrated that one and two doses of 24 mg intravenous dexamethasone reduced opioid consumption and pain after total knee arthroplasty (TKA). We aimed to investigate the prolonged effects of dexamethasone after the 48-h intervention period. DESIGN: This was a prospective, pre-planned questionnaire follow-up on postoperative days 3-7 of patients in the DEX-2-TKA trial that randomly received: DX1 (dexamethasone 24 mg + placebo), DX2 (dexamethasone 24 mg + dexamethasone 24 mg), and placebo (placebo + placebo) perioperatively and 24 h later. SETTING: A multicenter trial performed at five Danish hospitals. PARTICIPANTS: We analyzed 434 of 485 adult participants enrolled in the DEX-2-TKA trial. OUTCOME MEASURES: Primary outcome was difference between groups in average of all numerical rating scale (NRS) pain scores reported in the morning, at bedtime, and the daily average pain on postoperative days 3-7. Secondary outcomes were sleep quality and patient satisfaction. RESULTS: The median (interquartile range) pain intensity levels for postoperative days 3-7 were: DX2 3.2 (2.1-4.3); DX1 3.3 (2.3-4.1); and placebo 3.3 (2.5-4.7). Hodges-Lehmann median differences between groups were: 0 (95% confidence interval - 0.54 to 0.2), P = 0.38 between DX1 and placebo; 0.1 (-0.47 to 0.33), p = .87 between DX1 and DX2; and 0.1 (-0.6 to 0.13), p = .20 between DX2 and placebo. We found no relevant differences between groups on sleep quality on postoperative days 3-7 nor for patient satisfaction with the analgesic treatment. CONCLUSIONS: We found that neither one nor two doses of 24 mg intravenous dexamethasone demonstrated prolonged effects on overall pain or sleep quality on postoperative days 3-7 after total knee arthroplasty. We also found that dexamethasone had no effect on patient satisfaction. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: Clinicaltrials.gov NCT03506789 (main result trial).","author_count":14,"contributors":["Derby, Cecilie Bauer","Gasbjerg, Kasper Smidt","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Lunn, Troels Haxholdt","Pedersen, Niels Anker","Lindholm, Peter","Brorson, Stig","Schrøder, Henrik Morville","Thybo, Kasper Højgaard","Bagger, Jens","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Overgaard, Søren","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Mathiesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-088.84-725270"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Derby, Cecilie Bauer"],"keyword":["Adult","Analgesics Opioid","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee","Dexamethasone","Dexamethasone therapeutic use","Double Blind Method","Humans","Pain","Pain Postoperative drug therapy","Prospective Studies","Total knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prolonged effects of dexamethasone following total knee arthroplasty a pre planned sub study of the dex 000000000002 tka trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14319","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The main study was funded by Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted Hospitals' Research Fund, and received support from the Department of Anaesthesiology, Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted Hospitals, Denmark. The Present sub‐study received funding from The Zealand Region Research Foundation. The funder of the study had no role in the design and conduction of the study; collection, management, analysis, and interpretation of the data; preparation, review, or approval of the manuscript; and the decision to submit the manuscript for publication."],"id":