"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170850268"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","gildhøj private hospital","gildhøj privathospital"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d66db8ec-a02b-41a5-8b6f-94171ce49dc1","sdu-5916a85f-e3f7-4bee-828b-f1f1a7e460fa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prolonged effects of dexamethasone following total knee arthroplasty : A pre-planned sub-study of the DEX-2-TKA trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.84-725270","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We present a combined neutron diffraction and high-field muon spin rotation (μSR) study of the magnetically ordered and superconducting phases of the high-temperature superconductor La1.94Sr0.06CuO4+y [Tc=37.5(2) K] in a magnetic field applied perpendicular to the CuO2 planes. We observe a linear field-dependence of the intensity of the neutron diffraction peak that reflects the modulated antiferromagnetic stripe order. The magnetic volume fraction extracted from μSR data likewise increases linearly with applied magnetic field. The combination of these two observations allows us to unambiguously conclude that stripe-ordered regions grow in an applied field, whereas the stripe-ordered magnetic moment itself is field-independent. This contrasts with earlier suggestions that the field-induced neutron diffraction intensity in La-based cuprates is due to an increase in the ordered moment. We discuss a microscopic picture that is capable of reconciling these conflicting viewpoints.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Holm-Dahlin, S.","Larsen, Jeppe Stærk","Jacobsen, H.","Rømer, A. T.","Ţuţueanu, A. E.","Ahmad, M.","Grivel, Jean-Claude","Scheuermann, R.","Zimmermann, M. V.","Boehm, M.","Steffens, P.","Niedermayer, Ch","Pedersen, Kasper Steen","Christensen, Niels Bech","Wells, B. O.","Lefmann, K.","Udby, L."],"cuid":["S02-096.92-742195"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Electron Synchrotron","Institut Laue-Langevin","Paul Scherrer Institute","University of Connecticut","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"field induced electronic phase separation in the high temperature superconductor la sub 000000000001 000000000094 sub sr sub 000000000000 000000000006 sub cuo sub 000000000004 y sub","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.109.174517","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.92-742195","identifier":[{"id":"85193051953","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-803a5001-5287-411c-9dfa-c79fc45ed850","ku-7d285bac-6475-43ce-8edf-824635cd150f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-282AD86680E3FCE534CC6B4E56AD2747"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/362051967/PhysRevB.109.174517.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/394642562/PhysRevB.109.174517.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.109.174517","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2101.10672","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Condensed Matter Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affn