M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. C.","key":"grivelpau","last":"Grivel","locid":"51bcc82e-b9b4-4ef6-ac20-92431097c3cc","name":"Grivel, Jean-Claude","name_org":"Grivel, J. C.","orcid":"0000-0001-7835-9054","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"scheuermannpau","last":"Scheuermann","name":"Scheuermann, R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"M. V.","key":"zimmermannpau","last":"Zimmermann","name":"Zimmermann, M. V.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"boehmpau","last":"Boehm","name":"Boehm, M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"steffenspau","last":"Steffens","name":"Steffens, P.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ch","key":"niedermayerpau","last":"Niedermayer","name":"Niedermayer, Ch","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K. S.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"380dfdc8-c64b-4a34-9aa2-d86d7f9a1bb7","name":"Pedersen, Kasper Steen","name_org":"Pedersen, K. S.","orcid":"0000-0002-4381-4544","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"N. B.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"dbda3ad1-b77e-46ae-850d-5538bd230fb5","name":"Christensen, Niels Bech","name_org":"Christensen, N. B.","orcid":"0000-0001-6443-2142","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"B. O.","key":"wellspau","last":"Wells","name":"Wells, B. O.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"K.","key":"lefmannpau","last":"Lefmann","locid":"b7da4979-871d-4937-a274-d8126545849a","name":"Lefmann, Kim","name_org":"Lefmann, K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4282-756X","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L.","key":"udbypau","last":"Udby","locid":"00135d23-8276-4684-b6e9-20d4b3348326","name":"Udby, Linda","name_org":"Udby, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-2816-6825","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.109.174517","issn":["1550235X","24699950"],"issn_org":["24699950"],"issue":"17","journal":"Physical Review B","paperid":"174517","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193051953"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-803a5001-5287-411c-9dfa-c79fc45ed850","ku-7d285bac-6475-43ce-8edf-824635cd150f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Field-induced electronic phase separation in the high-temperature superconductor La<sub>1.94</sub>Sr<sub>0.06</sub>CuO<sub>4+y</sub>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.92-742195","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Social inequalities in colorectal cancer screening participation are evident. Barriers to screening participation include discomfort from diagnostic modalities. We aimed to describe the discomfort experienced from colonoscopy and colon capsule endoscopy (CCE) and investigate the discrepancy between expected and experienced discomfort stratified by socioeconomic status. Methods: A randomised controlled trial was conducted offering half of the colorectal cancer screening invitees the choice between CCE and colonoscopy after a positive faecal immunochemical test. This paper includes those who elected to undergo CCE. A positive CCE elicited referral for a therapeutic colonoscopy. Participants reported their discomfort from CCE and from any following colonoscopies in electronically distributed questionnaires. Discomfort was measured using visual analogue scales and compared between socioeconomic subgroups determined by educational level and income. Results: The experienced discomfort from CCE and colonoscopy differed significantly between educational levels but not income levels. The bowel preparation contributed the most to the experienced discomfort in both CCE and colonoscopy. The discrepancy between expected and experienced discomfort from colonoscopy increased with increasing educational and income levels. A similar trend was seen in CCE between educational levels but not income levels. Conclusions: None of the results indicated a higher discomfort in lower socioeconomic subgroups. Regardless of the investigation modality, the bowel preparation was the main contributor to experienced discomfort. The discrepancy between expected and experienced discomfort did not seem to be larger in lower socioeconomic subgroups, indicating that this is not a major barrier causing inequalities in screening uptake. This is the first study investigating individual discomfort discrepancy in both CCE and colonoscopy, while being able to stratify by socioeconomic status.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Deding, Ulrik","Bøggild, Henrik","Kaalby, Lasse","Hjelmborg, Jacob v. B.","Kobaek-Larsen, Morten","Thygesen, Marianne Kirstine","Schelde-Olesen, Benedicte","Bjørsum-Meyer, Thomas","Baatrup, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S02-097.75-767042"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["CareForColon2015 study group","on behalf of the CareForColon2015 study group"],"corresponding_author":["Deding, Ulrik"],"keyword":["Colon capsule endoscopy","Colonoscopy","Colorectal cancer screening","Inequality","Patient discomfort","Socioeconomic status"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic differences in discrepancies between expected and experienced discomfort from colonoscopy and colon capsule endoscopy","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e34274","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The CFC2015 trial was funded by OUH's innovation fund (grant R75-A3392), Aage and Johanne Louis-Hansen's Fond (grant 17-2B-1409), the Danish Cancer Society (grant R100-A6747), the Medtronic Research Foundation (grant ERP 2018\\u201311151), and the Excellence Centre in the Region of Southern Denmark (grant 18/48426) [31]. The funding sources had no role or impact on the design, methods, or conclusion drawn from this study.The authors declare the following financial interests/personal relationships which may be considered as potential competing interests:Gunnar Baatrup reports financial support was provided by OUH Innovation Fund. Gunnar Baatrup reports financial support was provided by Aage og Johanne Louis-Hansens Fond. Gunnar Baatrup reports financial support was provided by The Danish Cancer society. Gunnar Baatrup reports financial support was provided by The Medtronic Research Foundation. Gunnar Baatrup reports financial support was provided by The Region of Southern Denmark's Excellence Centre. The CFC2015 trial was funded by OUH\\u2019s innovation fund (grant R75-A3392), Aage and Johanne Louis-Hansen\\u2019s Fond (grant 17-2B-1409), the Danish Cancer Society (grant R100-A6747), the Medtronic Research Foundation (grant ERP 2018\\u201311151), and the Excellence Centre in the Region of Southern Denmark (grant 18/48426) 31 . The funding sources had no role or impact on the design, methods, or conclusion drawn from this study."],"id":"S02-097.75-767042","identifier":[{"id":"85198105124","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39100485","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11295845","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-d028ffc7-d51c-4ce8-bc6a-d76fc5b16aaa","sdu-0a109657-e9f1-4bbc-baf4-2c5d8d28b244"],"keyword":["Colon capsule endoscopy","Colonoscopy","Colorectal cancer screening","Inequality","Patient discomfort","Socioeconomic status"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7597E48FDADB284831E0CB71F2077E16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e34274","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/278606250/PIIS2405844024103052.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/734480854/1-s2.0-S2405844024103052-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Public Health and Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"careforcolon2015 study group","name":"CareForColon2015 study group","role":"oau"},{"affno":4,"key":"on behalf of the careforcolon2015 study group","name":"on behalf of the CareForColon2015 study group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"dedingpau","last":"Deding","locid":"ac9881cb-949b-4427-bf3e-8badf8905e2d","name":"Deding, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8263-2989","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"bøggildpau","last":"Bøggild","locid":"f78a6e0b-ac8c-47a0-9b70-8de3cdac496d","name":"Bøggild, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8934-5002","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Kaalby","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"0c8d2c97-bb94-4040-883e-f9d93c5f4327","name":"Kaalby, Lasse","name_org":"Møller, Lasse Kaalby","orcid":"0000-0002-6721-3604","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob von Bornemann","key":"hjelmborgpau","last":"Hjelmborg","locid":"7cec567c-2361-426a-8f47-f331d15d8c30","name":"Hjelmborg, Jacob","name_org":"Hjelmborg, Jacob von Bornemann","orcid":"0000-0001-9630-9149","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"kobaeklarsenpau","last":"Kobaek-Larsen","locid":"0f383fcc-0bd7-4c47-93b8-911d024157d6","name":"Kobaek-Larsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-5097-9283","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne K.","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"b71406f7-073f-4c45-920c-5984da19b5c8","name":"Thygesen, Marianne Kirstine","name_org":"Thygesen, Marianne K.","orcid":"0000-0002-1811-7405","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedicte","key":"scheldeolesenpau","last":"Schelde-Olesen","locid":"d4c5fc8a-5514-4191-abea-8b99f32e6cdc","name":"Schelde-Olesen, Benedicte","orcid":"0000-0001-7643-2350","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"bjørsummeyerpau","last":"Bjørsum-Meyer","locid":"3d8755ad-c3ff-4455-8e66-6929d3290ab5","name":"Bjørsum-Meyer, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-5253-0802","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar","key":"baatruppau","last":"Baatrup","locid":"3e62f6ae-0738-4c20-ac2f-3543bb12fa6b","name":"Baatrup, Gunnar","orcid":"0000-0003-0300-5766","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39100485"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e34274","issn":["24058440"],"issue":"14","journal":"Heliyon","paperid":"e34274","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Heliyon","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198105124"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d028ffc7-d51c-4ce8-bc6a-d76fc5b16aaa","sdu-0a109657-e9f1-4bbc-baf4-2c5d8d28b244"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Socioeconomic differences in discrepancies between expected and experienced discomfort from colonoscopy and colon capsule endoscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.75-767042","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: This study explored changes in pain-related parameters, occupational function, occupational balance, lifestyle factors, and self-perceived health status in adults with chronic high-impact pain participating in an occupational therapy lifestyle intervention. METHODS: This one-group longitudinal feasibility study was performed in three continuous feasibility rounds. The occupational therapists-led intervention targeted meaningful occupations, regular physical activity, and a healthy diet. The intervention contained individual and group sessions and was added to the standard multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment. Outpatients (n=40, 85 % females, 46.6 ± 10.9 years old) participated in the study between April 2019 and December 2021. The analysis includes data for 31 participants. Analysis of pre-post changes assessed after each feasibility round were performed for the outcomes: pain intensity, pain sensitivity and pain modulation (pressure pain threshold and tolerance, temporal summation of pain and conditioned pain modulation), pain self-efficacy, pain catastrophizing, motor and process skills, occupational balance, daily wake-time movement, daily walking steps, body mass index, waist circumference, blood pressure, and self-perceived health status. RESULTS: Improvements in motor skills (assessment of motor and process skills score=0.20 (1.37; 1.57), 95 % CI 0.01; 0.38) and temporal summation of pain (-1.19 (2.86; -1.67), 95 % CI -2.16; -0.22), but a decrease in pain tolerance (-7.110 (54.42; 47.32), 95 % CI -13.99; -0.22) were observed. Correlation analysis suggested moderate-to-very strong statistically significant relationships in several outcomes related to pain, health, pain coping, occupational balance, occupational functioning, body anthropometrics, and pain sensitivity. CONCLUSIONS: This study suggested that the lifestyle intervention would benefit motor skills while effects on other outcomes were unclear in adults with chronic pain. To confirm the findings, a randomized trial evaluating effectiveness is needed. Ethical committee number: SJ-307 Reg. Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT03903900.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard","Skou, Søren Thorgaard","Larsen, Anette Enemark","Polianskis, Romanas","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Petersen, Kristian Kjær-Staal","Østergaard, Anne Skov","Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","Søndergaard, Jens","Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup"],"cuid":["S03-096.47-703738"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard"],"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living","Adult","Chronic Pain therapy","Evaluation Study","Feasibility Studies","Female","Health behaviour","Health related quality of life","Healthy Lifestyle","Humans","Life Style","Male","Middle Aged","Occupational Therapy","Occupations","Pain Management","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"changes in pain daily occupations lifestyle and health following an occupational therapy lifestyle intervention a secondary analysis from a feasibility study in patients with chronic high impact pain","src":["aau","kp","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/sjpain-2023-0043","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Research funding: Grants from Region Zealand Health Research Fund (Reg. SJ-703); The University of Southern Denmark (Reg. under the applicant\\u2019s name, S. S. Nielsen); and The Danish Occupational Therapy Association (Reg. FF1-18- R76-A1690) financed the first author\\u2019s Ph.D.-study. Dr. Skou and Dr. Nielsen are funded by a program grant from Region Zealand (Exercise First). Dr. Skou is also funded by two grants from the European Union\\u2019s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program (MOBILIZE, grant agreement No. 801790; and ESCAPE, grant agreement No. 945377).","Research funding: Grants from Region Zealand Health Research Fund (Reg. SJ-703); The University of Southern Denmark (Reg. under the applicant’s name, S. S. Nielsen); and The Danish Occupational Therapy Association (Reg. FF1-18- R76-A1690) financed the first author’s Ph.D.-study. Dr. Skou and Dr. Nielsen are funded by a program grant from Region Zealand (Exercise First). Dr. Skou is also funded by two grants from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program (MOBILIZE, grant agreement No. 801790; and ESCAPE, grant agreement No. 945377)."],"id":"S03-096.47-703738","identifier":[{"id":"38037749","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85179119597","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8d8ae952-b608-4b0a-bee9-468bdedb7daa","kp-5849a72b-1238-432b-a40b-2e9fbcdf8f27","sdu-7a5b002a-bd9f-4d45-b489-2a70c923f2c6"],"keyword":["Adult","Chronic Pain/therapy","Feasibility Studies","Female","Humans","Life Style","Male","Middle Aged","Occupational Therapy","Occupations","activities of daily living","disease, health science and nursing","evaluation study","health behaviour","health-related quality of life","healthy lifestyle","pain management","pain managementon of pain (−1.19 (2.86","−1.67)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4F305356BA73BAF016BD82B5B4F1D88F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/693721789/10.1515_sjpain-2023-0043.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/sjpain-2023-0043","version":"P