atus":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","title_org":"Scandinavian journal of pain","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179119597"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8d8ae952-b608-4b0a-bee9-468bdedb7daa","kp-5849a72b-1238-432b-a40b-2e9fbcdf8f27","sdu-7a5b002a-bd9f-4d45-b489-2a70c923f2c6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KP University College Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Changes in pain, daily occupations, lifestyle, and health following an occupational therapy lifestyle intervention : a secondary analysis from a feasibility study in patients with chronic high-impact pain","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.47-703738","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Essential tremor (ET) is a prevalent neurological disorder with a largely unknown underlying biology. In this genome-wide association study meta-analysis, comprising 16,480 ET cases and 1,936,173 controls from seven datasets, we identify 12 sequence variants at 11 loci. Evaluating mRNA expression, splicing, plasma protein levels, and coding effects, we highlight seven putative causal genes at these loci, including CA3 and CPLX1. CA3 encodes Carbonic Anhydrase III and carbonic anhydrase inhibitors have been shown to decrease tremors. CPLX1, encoding Complexin-1, regulates neurotransmitter release. Through gene-set enrichment analysis, we identify a significant association with specific cell types, including dopaminergic and GABAergic neurons, as well as biological processes like Rho GTPase signaling. Genetic correlation analyses reveals a positive association between ET and Parkinson's disease, depression, and anxiety-related phenotypes. This research uncovers risk loci, enhancing our knowledge of the complex genetics of this common but poorly understood disorder, and highlights CA3 and CPLX1 as potential therapeutic targets.","author_count":74,"contributors":["Skuladottir, Astros Th.","Stefansdottir, Lilja","Halldorsson, Gisli H.","Stefansson, Olafur A.","Bjornsdottir, Anna","Jonsson, Palmi","Palmadottir, Vala","Thorgeirsson, Thorgeir E.","Walters, G. Bragi","Gisladottir, Rosa S.","Bjornsdottir, Gyda","Jonsdottir, Gudrun A.","Sulem, Patrick","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Knowlton, Kirk U.","Jones, David A.","Ottas, Aigar","Esko, Tõnu","Mägi, Reedik","Nelis, Mari","Hudjashov, Georgi","Pedersen, Ole B.","Didriksen, Maria","Brunak, Søren","Banasik, Karina","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Erikstrup, Christian","Bay, Jakob","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Brodersen, Thorsten","Burgdorf, Kristoffer","Chalmer, Mona Ameri","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Dowsett, Joseph","Feenstra, Bjarke","Geller, Frank","Gudbjartsson, Daniel","Hindhede, Lotte","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Jemec, Gregor","Aagaard, Bitten","Kaspersen, Katrine","Kjerulff, Bertram Dalskov","Kogelman, Lisette Johanna Antonia Rodian","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Louloudis, Ioannis","Lundgaard, Agnete","Mikkelsen, Susan","Mikkelsen, Christina","Nissen, Ioanna","Nyegaard, Mette","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Henriksen, Alexander Pil","Rohde, Palle Duun","Rostgaard, Klaus","Schwinn, Michael","Stefansson, Hreinn","Sørensen, Erik","Þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas","Westergaard, David","Haavik, Jan","Andreassen, Ole A.","Rye, David","Igland, Jannicke","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Milani, Lili A.","Nadauld, Lincoln D.","Stefansson, Hreinn","Stefansson, Kari"],"cuid":["S04-094.80-761550"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium","Estonian Biobank"],"corresponding_author":["Skuladottir, Astros Th"],"country":["Estonia","Iceland","Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Emory University","Estonian Biocentre","Haukeland University Hospital","Heilsuklasinn Clinic","Intermountain Healthcare","Intermountain Heart Institute","Intermountain Medical Center","Landspitali University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","Primary Children's Medical Center","Stanford University","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University of Bergen","University of Iceland","University of Oslo","University of Tartu","Western Norway University of Applied Sciences","deCODE Genetics"],"keyword":["Essential Tremor genetics","Genetic Loci","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Wesley Woods Health Center"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gwas meta analysis reveals key risk loci in essential tremor pathogenesis","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06207-4","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the participants in this study for their valuable contribution to research. We thank all investigators and colleagues who contributed to data collection, phenotypic characterization of clinical samples, genotyping, and analysis of the whole-genome association data. The Estonian dataset was funded by European Union through the European Regional Development Fund Project No. 2014-2020.4.01.15-0012 GENTRANSMED and by Estonian Research Council grant PRG1291. Data analysis of the Estonian dataset was carried out in part in the High-Performance Computing Center of University of Tartu. This research was conducted using the UK Biobank Resource (application number 42256)."],"id":"S04-094.80-761550","identifier":[{"id":"85191631915","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38671141","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11053069","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-0d15e1f7-ecb2-4609-847d-f0aa9b099fc9","au-7906fbdd-2712-4b1f-952c-fcf6ff905905","ku-81cb6d13-b61a-4632-a9ea-d54e1868d1ff","sdu-bfe6c8b0-1be8-4aaf-ac83-9c3b32ebf5db"],"keyword":["Essential Tremor/genetics","Genetic Loci","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome-Wide Association Study","Humans","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-D3ED21176302F44C0C15D9DB8CCDF6B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06207-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","