University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yupeng","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"2b1ccf6e-22a6-4eb4-a789-3dfc4348f5ad","name":"Zhao, Yupeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rie Beck","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","name_org":"Olin, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"søvsøszocskahansenpau","last":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen","name":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars G.","key":"hansonpau","last":"Hanson","locid":"6c7cc6f9-5b6a-47dc-bb02-efe208e52f16","name":"Hanson, Lars G.","orcid":"0000-0002-8204-6912","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of ISMRM 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-19cadc15-25d3-4446-88db-e09eea0b082e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Coronary angiography and myocardial perfusion MRI using hyperpolarized water","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-746317","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Activism has been a central theme in the study of Danish foreign policy after the Cold War. A common understanding is that there is an essential quality to activism. The assumption seems to be that the concept of activism has been particularly relevant in Danish foreign policy ever since Foreign Minister Ellemann-Jensen launched ‘active internationalism’ in 1989. However, there has been little interest in the way in which the term itself has been used in the Danish political sphere. The article examines the way the term is used. The analysis shows that ‘active’ (but never activism/activist) can be found in all government programs after 2009. However, there are no substantial political consequences of the articulation of ‘active’ since ‘active’ provides legitimacy to already existing political aims. On this background, the article raises the question of whether the unique research focus on Danish foreign policy activism is warranted Aktivisme har været et centralt tema i studiet af dansk udenrigspolitik efter den kolde krig. En almindelig forståelse er, at aktivisme i forskellige former er et iboende træk i dansk udenrigspolitik. Antagelsen synes at være, at begrebet aktivisme har været særligt relevant i dansk udenrigspolitik lige siden udenrigsminister Ellemann-Jensen lancerede ’aktiv internationalism’ i 1989. Der har dog været ringe interesse for den made, som selve begrebet har været brugt på i den danske politiske sfære. Artiklen undersøger den måde, udtrykket bruges på med særligt henblik på perioden efter 2009. Analysen viser, at ’aktivisme’/ ’aktivistisk’sjældent bruges. ’Aktiv’ kan imidlertid findes i alle regeringsprogrammer efter 2009. Der er dog ingen væsentlige politiske konsekvenser af artikulationen af ’aktiv’, da ’aktiv’ giver legitimitet til allerede eksisterende politiske mål inden for eksisterende udenrigspolitiske forståelser. På den baggrund rejser artiklen spørgsmålet om, hvorvidt det unikke forskningsfokus på dansk udenrigspolitisk aktivisme er berettiget.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747360"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish foreign policy activism mostly in the minds of the researchers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/395713591/Danish_Foreign_Policy_Review_2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747360","ids":["ku-047f1623-159e-4078-a37b-83f1217d528e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7DCAE7427AE4E1D218BD49362CF45E6B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.diis.dk/ws/files/24193492/Danish_Foreign_Policy_Review_2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/395713591/Danish_Foreign_Policy_Review_2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, International Relations"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788772361444","9788772361451"],"issn":["13972480"],"issue":"2024","pages":"76","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"DIIS","series":"Danish Foreign Policy Review","status":"p","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-047f1623-159e-4078-a37b-83f1217d528e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Danish foreign policy activism : mostly in the minds of the researchers?","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747360","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background The relationship between speckle tracking assessed global longitudinal strain (GLS) and Doppler-based echocardiography with basic physiological markers of cardiac function derived from pressure-volume loops is poorly elucidated. Objective We aimed to describe the association between LS and Doppler-based echocardiography and direct measurements of central haemodynamic parameters from conductance catheter-based pressure-volume loops in an animal model with increasing left ventricular (LV) dysfunction. Methods 12 Danish landrace female pigs (75-80 kg) were used. All instrumentations were performed percutaneously, including the conductance catheter in the LV. Progressive LV dysfunction was induced by embolisation through the left main coronary artery with microspheres every 3 min until a >50% reduction in cardiac output (CO) or mixed venous saturation (SvO 2), compared with baseline, or SvO 2 <30%. Echocardiography was performed at baseline and 90 s after each injection. Results With progressive LV dysfunction, mean CO decreased from 5.6±0.9 L/min to 2.1±0.9 L/min, and mean SvO 2 deteriorated from 61.1±7.9% to 35.3±6.1%. Mean LS and LV outflow tract velocity time integral (LVOT VTI) declined from -13.8±3.0% to -6.1±2.0% and 16.9±2.6 cm to 7.8±1.8 cm, respectively. LS and LVOT VTI showed the strongest correlation to stroke work in unadjusted linear regression (r 2 =0.53 and r 2 =0.49, respectively). LS correlated significantly with stroke volume, end-systolic elastance, systolic blood pressure, ventriculo-arterial coupling and arterial elastance. Conclusion In an animal model of acute progressive LV dysfunction, echocardiographic and conductance catheter-based measurements changed significantly. LS and LVOT VTI displayed the earliest and the largest alterations with increased myocardial damage and both correlated strongest with stroke work.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Peter H.","Linde, Louise","Gregers, Emilie","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-750924"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Peter H."],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Animals","Disease Models Animal","Echocardiography","Echocardiography Doppler methods","Female","Heart failure","Predictive Value of Tests","Shock Cardiogenic physiopathology","Swine","Ventricular Dysfunction Left physiopathology","Ventricular Function Left physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between speckle tracking echocardiography and pressure volume loops during cardiogenic shock development","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/openhrt-2023-002512","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-750924","identifier":[{"id":"85195036305","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38782543","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11116883","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-c49e3ce8-e862-478b-9a64-f707bfb9ade6"],"keyword":["Acute Coronary Syndrome","Animals","Disease Models, Animal","Echocardiography","Echocardiography, Doppler/methods","Female","Heart Failure","Predictive Value of Tests","Shock, Cardiogenic/physiopathology","Swine","Ventricular Dysfunction, Left/physiopathology","Ventricular Function, Left/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-03E98CBDF94A2BF2111320053E2775F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/264453001/e002512.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/openhrt-2023-002512","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Hartmund","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","name_org":"Frederiksen, Peter Hartmund","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie","key":"gregerspau","last":"Gregers","name":"Gregers, Emilie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Louise Junker","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"f71f56f5-4f36-4de5-a7ae-e5e51f101a83","name":"Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","orcid":"0000-0003-1542-3260","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole K.","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, Ole K.","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":"bankepau","last":"Banke","locid":"0d350637-c6ce-4cf8-82ba-e965da703690","name":"Banke, Ann","orcid":"0000-0002-1036-580X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordi Sanchez","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"fa82ce60-e408-4c0f-b013-151f87c6998c","name":"Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","orcid":"0000-0002-8345-204X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie L.","key":"povlsenpau","last":"Povlsen","locid":"085efe15-36a1-434b-9b9e-b4341cd84a0d","name":"Povlsen, Amalie Ling","name_org":"Povlsen, Amalie L.","orcid":"0000-0001-6044-8841","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c1f7b9d-9e43-45ec-aa4d-310cdce6686a","name":"Larsen, Jeppe P.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"2af194b2-635f-4b62-84c2-26bd7dc3263b","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","name_org":"Lassen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-7972-9192","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Moller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38782543"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/openhrt-2023-002512","issn":["20533624","2398595X"],"issn_org":["2398595X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Open Heart","paperid":"e002512","publisher":"BMJ","status":"p","title":"Open Heart","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195036305"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c49e3ce8-e862-478b-9a64-f707bfb9ade6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association between speckle tracking echocardiography and pressure-volume loops during cardiogenic shock development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-750924","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia (HH) of pancreatic origin includes congenital hyperinsulinism (CHI), insulinoma, insulinomatosis, and adult-onset non-insulinoma persistent hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia syndrome (NI-PHHS). In this review, we describe the genotype-histotype-phenotype correlations in HH and their therapeutic implications. CHI can occur from birth or later on in life. Histologically, diffuse CHI shows diffuse beta cell hypertrophy with a few giant nuclei per islet of Langerhans, most frequently caused by loss-of-function mutations in ABCC8 or KCNJ11. Focal CHI is histologically characterized by focal adenomatous hyperplasia consisting of confluent hyperplastic islets, caused by a paternal ABCC8/KCNJ11 mutation combined with paternal uniparental disomy of 11p15. CHI in Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome is caused by mosaic changes in the imprinting region 11p15.4-11p15.5, leading to segmental or diffuse overgrowth of endocrine tissue in the pancreas. Morphological mosaicism of pancreatic islets is characterized by occurence of hyperplastic (type 1) islets in one or a few lobules and small (type 2) islets in the entire pancreas. Other rare genetic causes of CHI show less characteristic or unspecific histology. HH with a predominant adult onset includes insulinomas, which are pancreatic insulin-producing endocrine neoplasms, in some cases with metastatic potential. Insulinomas occur sporadically or as part of multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1 due to MEN1 mutations. MAFA mutations may histologically lead to insulinomatosis with insulin-producing neuroendocrine microadenomas or neuroendocrine neoplasms. NI-PHHS is mainly seen in adults and shows slight histological changes in some patients, which have been defined as major and minor criteria. The genetic cause is unknown in most cases. The diagnosis of HH, as defined by genetic, histological, and phenotypic features, has important implications for patient management and outcome.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Annette Rønholt","Brusgaard, Klaus","Christesen, Henrik Thybo","Detlefsen, Sönke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-751036"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Detlefsen, Sönke"],"keyword":["Congenital Hyperinsulinism genetics","Congenital hyperinsulinism","Genetic Association Studies","Genotype","Histology","Humans","Hyperinsulinism genetics","Hypoglycemia genetics","Insulinoma","Mosaicism","Mutation","Nesidioblastosis","Pancreatic Neoplasms genetics","Phenotype","Somatic mutations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genotype histotype phenotype correlations in hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14670/HH-18-709","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-751036","identifier":[{"id":"38305063","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85197955023","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e0b9971d-59ca-416e-bc5a-01ba5331efed"],"keyword":["Adult-onset non-insulinoma persistent hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia syndrome","Congenital Hyperinsulinism/genetics","Congenital hyperinsulinism","Genetic Association Studies","Genotype","Histology","Humans","Hyperinsulinism/genetics","Hypoglycemia/genetics","Insulinoma","Insulinoma/genetics","Insulinomatosis","Mosaicism","Mutation","Nesidioblastosis","Pancreatic Neoplasms/genetics","Phenotype","Somatic mutations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1BF55D17F4CFBB2F0D35BAF33BB42023"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14670/HH-18-709","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/265742280/Larsen-39-817-844-2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Clinical Genome Center (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of SDCO - Steno Diabetes Center Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette Rønholt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"13f24d4f-41ec-48ad-862e-95fcf5b03f67","name":"Larsen, Annette Rønholt","orcid":"0000-0002-7105-4028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"brusgaardpau","last":"Brusgaard","locid":"81205519-e2e8-445f-9c7d-d74c189a9ab5","name":"Brusgaard, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0002-2096-4988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Thybo","key":"christesenpau","last":"Christesen","locid":"c8317e72-7a09-4c80-81e9-b69855b68e8f","name":"Christesen, Henrik Thybo","orcid":"0000-0001-5330-6853","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sönke","key":"detlefsenpau","last":"Detlefsen","locid":"6bbd570e-0f99-4ee0-a239-7433591decbd","name":"Detlefsen, Sönke","orcid":"0000-0002-9466-2333","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38305063"],"pub":{"doi":"10.14670/hh-18-709","issn":["02133911","16995848"],"issn_org":["02133911"],"issue":"7","journal":"Histology and Histopathology","pages":"817-844","publisher":"Histology and Histopathology","status":"p","title":"Histology and Histopathology","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197955023"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e0b9971d-59ca-416e-bc5a-01ba5331efed"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genotype-histotype-phenotype correlations in hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-751036","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A lack of instruments to assess patient safety climate within primary care exists. The objectives of this study were as follows: 1) To adapt the Danish hospital version of the Safety Attitudes Questionnaire (SAQ-DK) for use in primary care; 2) Test the internal consistency and the construct validity of this version; 3) Present benchmark data; and 4) Analyze variance. METHODS: The SAQ-DK was adapted for use in Danish primary care settings (SAQ-DK-PRIM) and distributed to healthcare staff members from nursing homes (N = 11), homecare units (N = 4) and healthcare units (N = 2), within the municipality of Aarhus, Central Denmark Region, Denmark. Face- and content validity were assessed. The construct validity was evaluated by a set of goodness-of-fit indices. The internal reliability was evaluated using the item-rest correlations, the inter-item correlations, and Cronbach's alpha (α). RESULTS: The adaptation process resulted in a questionnaire of 10 items. Eight hundred and thirty healthcare staffs participated (78% of the eligible respondents). In total 586 (70.6%) responses were complete and were included in the analysis. Goodness-of-fit indices from the confirmatory factor analysis showed: Chi2=46.90CFI=0.97, RMSEA = 0.063 (90% CI: 0.044-0.084), Probability RMSEA (p close)=0.12. Internal reliability was high (Cronbach's α=0.76). Proportions of participants with a positive attitude was 41.1% and did not differ between the healthcare services. Scale mean score was 70.19 (SD: 18.05) and differed between healthcare services. The safety climate scale scores did not vary according to healthcare service type. ICC was 0.68% indicating no clustering of scores by healthcare service type. CONCLUSION: Considering the questionnaire's applicability, short length, strengthened focus on one area of interest and validity, the SAQ-DK-PRIM can serve as a valuable tool for measuring patient safety climate within primary care settings in Denmark.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Juhl, Marie Haase","Olesen, Anne Estrup","Deilkås, Ellen Tveter","Bruun, Niels Henrik","Obling, Kirsten Høgh","Rytter, Nikoline","Larsen, Maya Damgaard","Kristensen, Solvejg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756676"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Olesen, Anne Estrup"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Denmark","Primary care","Questionnaire","Reliability","Validity","patient safety climate","patient safety culture"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Aarhus Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient safety climate in danish primary care adaption and validation of the danish safety attitudes questionnaire saq dk prim","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S470111","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Salary for the first author MHJ was covered by VELUX FONDEN (00034143) whom we greatly acknowledge for funding a study leading to this validation study."],"id":"S01-000.00-756676","identifier":[{"id":"39219748","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85203052050","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11365490","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-49138e81-e321-453c-8b5f-72b87b17f7db"],"keyword":["Denmark","patient safety climate","patient safety culture","primary care","questionnaire","reliability","validity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-8-C3FE4C99DAD3D86AF4AE132D115B3380"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S470111","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/744327780/Juhl_et_al._2024_._Patient_Safety_Climate_in_Danish_Primary_Care_-_Adaption_and_Validation_of_the_Danish_Safety_Attitudes_Questionnaire_SAQ-DK-PRIM_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Pharmacology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"akershus university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Akershus University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Aarhus Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Haase","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"6257b1fa-a780-4102-92be-8ff4e20fc319","name":"Juhl, Marie Haase","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Estrup","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"88951454-410c-4411-aeab-9706f3e3351c","name":"Olesen, Anne Estrup","orcid":"0000-0001-9365-1918","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen Tveter","key":"deilkåspau","last":"Deilkås","name":"Deilkås, Ellen Tveter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":