{"abstract":"Much of the value of a digital twin depends on the extent to which the twin is kept up to date with the state of its real-world counterpart. This chapter surveys sensing and communication methods that play a key role in maintaining this relationship. The sensors making real-world observations, the characteristics of the communications infrastructure (which will often be wireless), communications delays, frequency of observations and the use of techniques such as data compression all therefore have an impact on the qualities of the digital twin and the services it offers. Data arriving at the digital twin will make use of time-series databases. When multiple sensors are present it may also be necessary to consider sensor fusion or use deep learning for deriving the optimal solution for the data that has been sensed.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gomes, Cláudio","Lucani Rötter, Daniel Enrique","Iosifidis, Alexandros","Feng, Hao","Ejersbo, Henrik","Frasheri, Mirgita"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-763390"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Gomes, Cláudio"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GFS","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sensing and communication of data from the physical twin","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105006860860","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-763390","identifier":[{"id":"105006860860","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9fba4c9e-6ee0-4e6f-9aa1-cf2256993b39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Techn