{"abstract":"Background Genetic susceptibility to inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) has been widely studied, whereas the genetic contribution to disease progression over time remains largely unknown. In a unique population-based cohort, we explored if genetic susceptibility to IBD associated with disease course severity. Methods In a Danish nationwide cohort of 3688 patients with Crohn’s disease (CD), 4491 patients with ulcerative colitis (UC), and 9469 controls, we estimated polygenic scores (PGS) for IBD susceptibility. We then investigated the association between susceptibility PGS and severe versus less severe disease courses. Patients were categorized as having a severe disease course if needing I) at least two IBD-related hospitalizations exceeding two days, II) at least two IBD-related major surgeries, III) one hospitalization and one major surgery not overlapping in time, or IV) total use of minimum 5000 mg systemic corticosteroids within the first three years of diagnosis. Secondary analyses explored the association with other severity measures including inflammatory markers, exposure to biologics and immunomodulators, and time to hospitalization and major IBD-related surgery. Statistical analyses included logistic, linear, and Cox proportional hazards regression, and predictive modeling using random forest. Findings Patients with severe disease courses had higher susceptibility PGS than patients with less severe disease courses (CD: OR=1·27, P=7·73×10−10, UC: OR=1·35, P=7·29×10−17 per SD increase in susceptibility PGS). When comparing the highest versus lowest PGS quintile, we observed a hazard ratio (HR) for major surgery of 2·74 (P=7·19×10−18) in patients with CD and 2·04 (P=4·36×10−7) in patients with UC. A higher susceptibility PGS was also associated with longer and more frequent hospitalizations, higher levels of C-reactive protein, decreased hemoglobin, and a higher need for corticosteroids, immunomodulators, and biologic therapies. Interpretation Patients with a higher genetic burden for developing IBD also experience a more severe disease course, suggesting a shared genetic architecture between disease susceptibility and severity.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Vestergaard, Marie Vibeke","Allin, Kristine H.","Nøhr, Anne Krogh","Lominchar, Jesus Vicente Torresano","Christensen, Heidi Søgaard","Krarup, Henrik","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Jacobsen, Henrik Albæk","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Bækvad-Hansen, Marie","Brøndum, Rasmus Froberg","Bøgsted, Martin","Larsen, Lone","Sazonovs, Aleksejs","Jess, Tine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805194"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vestergaard, Marie Vibeke"],"keyword":["Allergy and Immunology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic risk of inflammatory bowel disease is associated with disease course severity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.11.01.24316569","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-805194","ids":["aau-81694fb2-43d9-480f-9782-1bfc523252d4"],"keyword":["allergy and immunology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-23C4CE8A6EB355BEA9CAFED77795F7F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.11.01.24316569","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Molecular Prediction of Inflammatory Bowel Disease"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Vibeke","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"13392224-0850-4c5f-941f-d3249a366824","name":"Vestergaard, Marie Vibeke","orcid":"0009-0006-1409-1945","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristine Højgaard","key":"allinpau","last":"Allin","locid":"eaf730c8-2c38-4a9c-ab42-d8a01518f4f2","name":"Allin, Kristine H.","name_org":"Allin, Kristine Højgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-6880-5759","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Krogh","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"86da955c-89a5-4127-90c7-2ef61a6eb0fd","name":"Nøhr, Anne Krogh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesus Vicente Torresano","key":"lomincharpau","last":"Lominchar","locid":"a71c3be5-000e-4610-b404-05477c1a5cdd","name":"Lominchar, Jesus Vicente Torresano","orcid":"0009-0009-9356-1504","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heidi Søgaard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"574adf09-0ad8-49f0-bbb2-0ad1da4ad722","name":"Christensen, Heidi Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2692-168X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"kraruppau","last":"Krarup","locid":"72b4ebce-12cf-4f92-bb97-c9a588b06d57","name":"Krarup, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-5294-2428","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaspar René","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Kaspar René","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Albæk","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"f8250b02-4973-4c0f-8791-b55cc62d8aa8","name":"Jacobsen, Henrik Albæk","orcid":"0000-0001-7939-0715","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"bybjerggrauholmpau","last":"Bybjerg-Grauholm","name":"Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"bækvadhansenpau","last":"Bækvad-Hansen","name":"Bækvad-Hansen, Marie","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Froberg","key":"brøndumpau","last":"Brøndum","locid":"54640c80-01cc-4b01-b4f4-d1aea74ee653","name":"Brøndum, Rasmus Froberg","orcid":"0000-0001-5537-6767","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"bøgstedpau","last":"Bøgsted","locid":"a51116b7-e9b7-4f83-a74b-2d76bb8b1475","name":"Bøgsted, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9192-1814","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dee3a5a6-2573-46b3-a97d-599871808a77","name":"Larsen, Lone","orcid":"0000-0003-4067-2381","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aleksejs","key":"sazonovspau","last":"Sazonovs","locid":"221a36f5-4c7a-4547-8a4f-f549ea99f8ae","name":"Sazonovs, Aleksejs","orcid":"0009-0002-2413-0451","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"jesspau","last":"Jess","locid":"ab65eac5-33fc-4361-882d-e595188169d3","name":"Jess, Tine","orcid":"0000-0002-4391-7332","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/2024.11.01.24316569","pages":"24","publisher":"medRxiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-81694fb2-43d9-480f-9782-1bfc523252d4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Genetic risk of inflammatory bowel disease is associated with disease course severity","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805194","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Six four-element balun topologies are introduced that enable complex impedance matching in addition to common-mode rejection. Design equations for these topologies are presented. Three of these networks are universal, while the other three are capable of performing only specific impedance transformations. Examples of these networks were designed and fabricated along with a traditional lattice balun network for an operating frequency of 300 MHz. These networks were verified through extensive electromagnetic simulations and by measuring the fabricated networks. The fabricated novel network examples were able to achieve common-mode rejection ratios above 20 dB, power wave reflection coefficients below -20 dB, and insertion losses of approximately 0.1 dB; these results were similar to or better than the performance of the fabricated traditional lattice balun. The design example networks also provided power matching and low insertion loss over a greater bandwidth compared to the fabricated traditional network. These networks will allow for the footprints of lumped-element balun circuitry to be reduced, which is particularly useful in integrated circuit design. These topologies are also expected to further increase radio-frequency (RF) circuit design flexibility by offering more alternative realizations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jepsen, Rasmus","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827370"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy"],"keyword":["Passive components and circuits"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"four element lc baluns for power matching arbitrary impedances","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S1759078724000722","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827370","identifier":[{"id":"85210561536","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-10f19765-11bd-4ce7-b5c2-6f9fd76194a5"],"keyword":["Passive components and circuits","RF front-ends"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2254F699D7C48398439B8ACF1D5FDC13"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/408621893/four-element-lc-baluns-for-power-matching-arbitrary-impedances.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S1759078724000722","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Alexander","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","locid":"aa87dc83-1462-4474-a3ce-2256db39cfcf","name":"Jepsen, Rasmus","name_org":"Jepsen, Rasmus Alexander","orcid":"0009-0000-5282-7470","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6