{"abstract":"Public sector organisations (PSOs) such as municipalities, regulatory bodies, and public utilities are key actors in sustainability transitions. However, the conceptualisation of their transformative capacity is underdeveloped, as several strands of literature pay attention to the topic but remain disjointed. The article takes stock of the literature, reviewing the strengths and weaknesses of the main approaches. Building from there, the article proposes a higher-order holistic conceptual framework based on three constitutive elements: roles, resources, and abilities. We conceptualise the transformative capacity of a public sector organisation as the interaction between its roles, resources, and abilities in the enactment of its transformative agency. This framework offers a granular analytical approach for future empirical studies, acknowledging the diversity of PSOs and sustainability transitions pathways. It also offers practical clues for more targeted efforts to build transformative capacity in PSOs, which is crucial for accelerating transitions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Borrás, Susana","Haakonsson, Stine Jessen","Hendriksen, Christian","Gerli, Francesco","Taudal Poulsen, René","Pallesen, Trine","Croxatto, Lucas Somavilla","Kugelberg, Susanna","Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-763914"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Borrás, Susana"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan","University College London (UCL)"],"keyword":["Bureaucracy","Capacity","Dynamic capabilities","Green sustainability","Public administration","Sustainability transitions"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["European Environment Agency"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the transformative capacity of public sector organisations in sustainability transitions","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eist.2024.100904","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-763914","identifier":[{"id":"85203822691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-7618f3d1-f682-4a3d-8a59-4175bb4a25f8"],"keyword":["Bureaucracy","Capacity","Dynamic capabilities","Green sustainability","Public administration","Sustainability transitions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B9ED0A0B14C124DAB019ED2DEDDA26C1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/108437777/1-s2.0-S2210422424000947-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eist.2024.100904","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London (UCL)","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["European Envi