","issn":["22104224","22104232"],"issn_org":["22104224"],"journal":"Environmental Innovation and Societal Transitions","paperid":"100904","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Environmental Innovation and Societal Transitions","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203822691"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-7618f3d1-f682-4a3d-8a59-4175bb4a25f8"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Transformative Capacity of Public Sector Organisations in Sustainability Transitions","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-763914","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In some applications, baluns need to provide useful DC characteristics, such as DC-blocking and DC-feeding in addition to common-mode rejection and impedance matching. This can be useful in handling DC biases without requiring extra biasing circuitry. The DC characteristics of three novel four-element complex conjugate matching LC-balun topologies as well as traditional lattice baluns are described in this paper. Design examples of the new four-element topologies were demonstrated experimentally. Traditional lattice networks were used for benchmarking. The novel four-element topologies exhibited similar or greater common-mode rejection while also providing power matching and useful DC characteristics.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jepsen, Rasmus","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Johansen, Tom Keinicke","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764230"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-26","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2024-09-24","title":"2024 European Microwave Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Baluns","Conjugate matching","LC circuits"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"four element lc balun topologies with inherent dc feeding and dc blocking properties and complex impedance matching","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-764230","ids":["dtu-60533882-ee0d-4581-837c-795b74e4ef7e"],"keyword":["Baluns","Complex impedance matching","Conjugate matching","DC characteristics","LC circuits","Passive circuits"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D088BB15CF0E17CEF3BDE66937919593"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","locid":"aa87dc83-1462-4474-a3ce-2256db39cfcf","name":"Jepsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0009-0000-5282-7470","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tom Keinicke","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"7b44a94d-ae22-4678-87e4-8024f351462c","name":"Johansen, Tom Keinicke","orcid":"0000-0001-8182-1051","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-60533882-ee0d-4581-837c-795b74e4ef7e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Four-Element LC-Balun Topologies with Inherent DC-Feeding and DC-Blocking Properties and Complex Impedance Matching","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764230","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Following the implementation of the fast-track protocol in total hip arthroplasty (THA), total knee arthroplasty (TKA), and unicompartmental knee arthroplasty (UKA), the median length of stay (LOS) has been significantly reduced without an increase in readmissions. However, it is unclear if the reduction in LOS is at the expense of an increase in nonhome discharge. The aim of this study was to investigate the discharge destination among THA, TKA, and UKA patients. METHODS: The prospective multicenter study included 6,856 patients undergoing primary THA, TKA, and UKA in a fast-track setting with an overall median LOS of one day. Outcomes were discharge destination, median LOS in each discharge destination category, and cause of rehabilitation center discharge. Data were gathered using preoperative questionnaires and a review of medical records. Discharge destination and LOS were registered at discharge. RESULTS: We found that 99% of patients had been discharged to their own homes, of which 21% had been discharged to their own homes with home care. There were 1% who were discharged to a rehabilitation facility and 0.1% who were discharged to a nursing home. The THA (1%, 95% confidence interval [CI] 0.7 to 1) and TKA (1%, 95% CI 0.9 to 2) had a significantly higher rate of discharge to a rehabilitation facility compared to UKA (0.1%, 95% CI 0.0 to 0.5). CONCLUSIONS: Despite a short LOS, 99% of patients were discharged to their own homes. Rehabilitation facility discharge was only 1% and was mostly caused by inadequate postoperative mobilization.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Lyndrup, Oliver","Kehlet, Henrik","Jørgensen, Christoffer C.","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Jakobsen, Thomas","Gromov, Kirill","Andersen, Mikkel R.","Bieder, Manuel","Overgaard, Søren","Varnum, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-785864"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lyndrup, Oliver"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Center for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discharge destination of patients in fast track primary hip and knee arthroplasty results from a prospective danish cohort","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2024.12.005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-785864","identifier":[{"id":"39653131","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85213940450","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-559df6ca-a277-473e-bce0-1d5fb902706a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B02F0EF134BA730F94E303EF06553842"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2024.12.005","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Center for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Regional Hospital Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc"