{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with Hb Mizuho may be splenectomized at a young age to decrease their need for blood transfusions. OBSERVATIONS: Transfusion-dependency decreased dramatically in a 4-year-old white boy with Hb Mizuho after splenectomy. Surprisingly, he developed reticulocytosis (>1000×10 9 /L) with a peak reticulocyte percentage of 49%, and erythrocyte abnormalities, including Heinz bodies, Howell-Jolly bodies, and basophilic stippling. Manual reticulocyte counting and flow cytometric measurement with anti-CD71 antibodies supported a truly elevated reticulocyte count. CONCLUSIONS: We propose possible explanations for the extreme reticulocytosis that arose postsplenectomy and compare the reticulocyte count in the present case with previously published cases.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bøttger, Helene Narvestad","Winther-Larsen, Anne","Thomsen, Jens Haugbølle","Dziegiel, Morten Hanefeld","Hansen, Anne Todsen","Hasle, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.56-751785"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Child Preschool","Hb Mizuho","Hemoglobinopathy","Humans","Male","Reticulocytosis","Splenectomy","Splenectomy adverse effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extreme reticulocytosis after splenectomy in a patient with hemoglobin mizuho","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181586201","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.56-751785","identifier":[{"id":"85181586201","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38011049","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c99ef507-da92-4683-b5d4-1c904acce126","ku-b31bb4b2-b6d2-432b-96c4-1546cc5dc381"],"keyword":["Child, Preschool","Erythrocyte Inclusions","Hb Mizuho","Hemoglobins, Abnormal","Humans","Male","Reticulocytosis","Splenectomy/adverse effects","hemoglobinopathy","splenectomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-789D566241162DDA71F17D165F6FAC95"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department for Clinical Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene","key":"narvestadbøttgerpau","last":"Narvestad-Bøttger","locid":"3a20c113-14f9-4df5-b0f9-cbd318f6876a","name":"Bøttger, Helene Narvestad","name_org":"Narvestad-Bøttger, Helene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"wintherlarsenpau","last":"Winther-Larsen","locid":"162faab4-e6ad-4fce-8149-eafe733901ec","name":"Winther-Larsen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-2763-595X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"haugbøllebjerrepau","last":"Haugbølle Bjerre","locid":"eb923f8e-6d71-4108-9c05-6c74fc0372ca","name":"Thomsen, Jens Haugbølle","name_org":"Haugbølle Bjerre, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Morten Hanefeld","key":"dziegielpau","last":"Dziegiel","locid":"b6f0eeae-f94d-49f7-99ce-621663db4773","name":"Dziegiel, Morten Hanefeld","orcid":"0000-0001-8034-1523","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Todsen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Anne Todsen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"haslepau","last":"Hasle","locid":"bde24b22-8663-440f-ae65-37d61f0a8975","name":"Hasle, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38011049"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mph.0000000000002790","issn":["10774114","15363678"],"issn_org":["10774114"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181586201"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c99ef507-da92-4683-b5d4-1c904acce126","ku-b31bb4b2-b6d2-432b-96c4-1546cc5dc381"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Extreme Reticulocytosis After Splenectomy in a Patient With Hemoglobin Mizuho","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.56-751785","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose This study examines the association between socioeconomic status and the occurrence of both cardiovascular diseases and mortality following retinal vein occlusion (RVO), a condition known to elevate the risk of cardiovascular health issues. Despite recognition of the impact socioeconomic factors might have on a patient's course through the healthcare system, its association with cardiovascular outcomes post-RVO has not previously been thoroughly explored. Design Nationwide cohort study. Methods We included all subjects with RVO from the Danish nationwide registries diagnosed between 2000 and 2018. Information was combined using a personal identification number each Danish resident is given at birth or upon immigration. We categorized participants by their socioeconomic levels to evaluate the five-year incidence rate of cardiovascular conditions and overall mortality. The analysis was further refined by sex and age groups to elucidate any differential impacts. Furthermore, the cumulative incidence was estimated using the Aalen-Johansen estimator and the differences between the socioeconomic groups were quantified using a cox proportional hazard model. Key quantitative results were summarized, including hazard rate ratios (HR), confidence intervals (CI), and p-values Results The cohort was comprised of 14,041 individuals with RVO. Our analysis revealed a relationship between educational attainment and cardiovascular health outcomes. Lower education levels were consistently linked with heightened risks of mortality, diabetes, ischemic heart disease, myocardial infarction, and peripheral artery disease following RVO. Individuals with a middle educational level also exhibited a higher prevalence of peripheral artery disease when compared to those with the highest education levels. In terms of income, the lowest earners faced increased risks across several categories, including mortality, diabetes, heart failure, ischemic heart disease, myocardial infarction, and peripheral artery disease, when compared to the highest-income earners. The middle-income group also showed elevated risks for mortality, heart failure, and peripheral artery disease. Being unmarried was additionally associated with higher risks of mortality and heart failure compared to being married. Conclusion Socioeconomic status was significantly associated with clinically relevant differences in post-RVO risk of cardiovascular diseases and death. Our data suggests that socioeconomic factors should be considered in the attempt to reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease and death in patients with RVO.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ørskov, Marie","Cehofski, Lasse Jørgensen","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Bek, Toke","Skjøth, Flemming","Vorum, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.96-792864"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ørskov, Marie"],"keyword":["All cause mortality","Cardiovascular Diseases","Epidemiology","Register based","Retinal vein occlusion","Socioeconomic Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic status and risk of cardiovascular diseases in patients with retinal vein occlusion a danish nationwide cohort study","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajoint.2024.100044","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.96-792864","identifier":[{"id":"85217034117","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4f86d62a-a8fc-48cf-a1cd-8663c8cd613f","sdu-0af2da5e-01c9-4831-957a-1b7acc6e0bd9"],"keyword":["All-cause mortality","Cardiovascular diseases","Epidemiology","Register-based","Retinal vein occlusion","Socioeconomic factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F4539047D71646AF603977A36E7FCAF6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajoint.2024.100044","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/767127519/_rskov_et_al_2024_Socioeconomic_status_and_risk_of_cardiovascular_diseases_in_patients_with_retinal_vein_occlusion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/268848591/1-s2.0-S2950253524000443-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Ophthalmology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Regional Hospital Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"ørskovpau","last":"Ørskov","locid":"98e0db01-70c1-4f44-821d-849ca9a135eb","name":"Ørskov, Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse Jørgensen","key":"cehofskipau","last":"Cehofski","locid":"6f64cca9-b033-40be-8aec-528e3a27453c","name":"Cehofski, Lasse Jørgensen","orcid":"0000-0002-2150-7754","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"c5b82991-3759-4612-a9e5-0cbcd14ec804","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","name":"Bek, Toke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"skjøthpau","last":"Skjøth","locid":"f1291811-a3a2-463f-8421-c2d2fb8b3644","name":"Skjøth, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0003-2975-647X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"vorumpau","last":"Vorum","locid":"60554352-1557-4c7b-905d-e4b7c7f8c94a","name":"Vorum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-7600-0731","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ajoint.2024.100044","issn":["29502535"],"issue":"3","journal":"AJO International","paperid":"100044","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"AJO International","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217034117"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4f86d62a-a8fc-48cf-a1cd-8663c8cd613f","sdu-0af2da5e-01c9-4831-957a-1b7acc6e0bd9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Socioeconomic status and risk of cardiovascular diseases in patients with retinal vein occlusion : A Danish nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.96-792864","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The neutrophil-to-lymphocyte ratio(NLR) is increased in chronic inflammation and myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPN). We hypothesize that NLR is associated with all-cause mortality and mortality by comorbidity burden in the general population and individuals with MPN. We included 835,430 individuals from The Danish General Suburban Population Study, general practitioners, and outpatient clinics. We investigated NLR on mortality stratified by prevalent and incident MPN, essential thrombocythemia (ET), polycythemia vera (PV), myelofibrosis (MF), comorbidity burden (CCI-score), and the Triple-A risk score using hazard ratio (HR) and 95% confidence interval (95%CI). NLR 1-1.9 was the reference level. During a median follow-up of 11.2 years, 197,802 deaths were recorded. All-cause mortality increased for a stepwise increasing NLR with a HR (95%CI) for NLR ≥ 6 of 2.06(2.03-2.09) for the whole population and 2.93(2.44-3.50) in prevalent MPN. ET, PV, and MF had a HR (95%CI) for NLR ≥ 2 of 2.14(1.71-2.69), 2.19(1.89-2.54), and 2.31(1.91-2.80). Results were similar for incident MPN. Mortality was higher for stepwise increasing NLR and CCI-score(pinteraction < 2×10-16), with a HR for NLR ≥ 6 of 2.23(2.17-2.29), 4.10(4.01-4.20), and 7.69(7.50-7.89), for CCI-score 0, 1-2, or ≥3. The Triple-A risk score demonstrated alignment with NLR. Increasing NLR and comorbidity burden were associated with lower survival in individuals without MPN but were even worse in prevalent and incident MPN, ET, PV, and MF.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Larsen, Morten Kranker","Skov, Vibe","Kjær, Lasse","Eickhardt-Dalbøge, Christina Schjellerup","Knudsen, Trine Alma","Kristiansen, Marie Hvelplund","Sørensen, Anders Lindholm","Wienecke, Troels","Andersen, Morten","Ottesen, Johnny T.","Gudmand-Høyer, Johanne","Snyder, Jordan Andrew","Andersen, Mikkel Porsborg","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Stiehl, Thomas","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Ellervik, Christina"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-742417"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard Medical School","Harvard University","RWTH Aachen University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neutrophil to lymphocyte ratio and all cause mortality with and without myeloproliferative neoplasms a danish longitudinal study","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41408-024-00994-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-742417","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10853217","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38331919","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184733321","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-eec1e90c-f7ef-4319-8f09-73a9098b83f8","ruc-275de21a-a9a2-447a-b99f-a91a2afcabbe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C7E8963121B9FD6679DA6063618FABF5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/383884160/s41408_024_00994_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/100660184/s41408-024-00994-z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41408-024-00994-z","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Cope