{"abstract":"The diagnosis of multiple myeloma requires detection of paraproteinemia and confirmation of monoclonal bone marrow infiltration, along with signs of end-organ damage. Despite the increasing prevalence, serum paraproteinemia is not routinely measured. We examined the relationship between alterations in routine hematological parameters and the development of paraproteinemia in a case-control study. Data was retrieved from a laboratory database in the capital region of Denmark between 01/01/2012 and 31/12/2022. Patients were included if they had a test for paraproteinemia (n = 134,740) and at least one prior hematological parameter (white blood cells, hemoglobin and platelet count) with a minimum follow-up of 1 year. Between 96,999 and 103,590 patients were included in each of the three hematological groups. We found white blood cell count and the presence of paraproteinemia followed an inverse J-shaped curve, with the highest presence below 3 × 109/L and above > 9 × 109/L. The adjusted OR below and above the nadir of 4 × 109/L was 1.61 (95% CI 1.25; 2.08, p < 0.0001) and 1.03 (95% CI 1.03; 1.04, p < 0.0001). Hemoglobin levels were inversely associated the presence of paraproteinemia, with the highest association below 6 mmol/L with an OR of 1.30 (95% CI 1.28; 1.32, p < 0.0001) adjusted for age and gender. Platelet count followed a U-shaped curve with the highest association at < 100 × 109/L. The adjusted OR below and above the nadir of 250 × 109/L was 1.13 (95% CI 1.10; 1.17, p < 0.0001) and 1.10 (95% CI 1.08; 1.12, p < 0.0001) respectively. In conclusion, all three parameters showed significant association with later paraproteinemia.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Røllum-Larsen, Jakob","Engell, Anna Elise","Diaz-delCastillo, Marta","Heegaard, Anne-Marie","Jørgensen, Henrik L"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-751770"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cancer development","Complete blood count","Multiple myeloma","Paraproteinemia","Retrospective study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Danish Spatial Imaging Consortium (DanSIC)"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of routine hematological parameters with the development of monoclonal gammopathies a case control study of 000000000134 000000000740 patients resubmitted to annals of hematology 000000000026 march 000000002024","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00277-024-05822-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-751770","identifier":[{"id":"38842565","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11283380","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195413320","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b5ef7c15-60dd-49ae-84fc-bcdf03c2d10e","ku-3d01089c-155e-439c-bb9b-1131b9ed1a1f"],"keyword":["Cancer development","Complete blood count","Multiple myeloma","Paraproteinemia","Retrospective study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-42A5D0F1BE73A81B6906A5E1B9F5B6B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/399830198/s00277_024_05822_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00277-024-05822-9","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Amager and Hvidovre Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Department of Forensic Medicine - Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Spatial Imaging Consortium (DanSIC)"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Translational and Clinical Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"røllumlarsenpau","last":"Røllum-Larsen","name":"Røllum-Larsen, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Elise","key":"engellpau","last":"Engell","name":"Engell, Anna Elise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marta","key":"diazdelcastillopau","last":"Diaz-delCastillo","locid":"7ea0571e-2b3f-494e-a3b9-327a6152059c","name":"Diaz-delCastillo, Marta","orcid":"0000-0001-7719-6839","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Anne Marie","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"3df3a4f8-75b8-48de-b580-5a44ddcf6afe","name":"Heegaard, Anne-Marie","name_org":"Heegaard, Anne Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Henrik Løvendahl","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cf84c34a-16a5-4a24-9667-bc1c2481e1a5","name":"Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38842565"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00277-024-05822-9","issn":["09395555","09458077"],"issn_org":["09395555"],"issue":"8","journal":"Annals of Hematology","pages":"3005-3013","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Annals of Hematology","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195413320"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b5ef7c15-60dd-49ae-84fc-bcdf03c2d10e","ku-3d01089c-155e-439c-bb9b-1131b9ed1a1f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association of routine hematological parameters with the development of monoclonal gammopathies : a case-control study of 134,740 patients : Resubmitted to annals of Hematology 26 March 2024","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-751770","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: Pulmonary arteriovenous malformations (PAVMs) may cause recurrent brain abscess. The primary aim was to determine the prevalence of PAVM amongst survivors of brain abscess. The proportion with cardiac right-to-left shunts was also assessed post hoc. METHODS: This was a cross-sectional population-based study of adult (≥18 years) survivors of cryptogenic bacterial brain abscess in Denmark from 2007 through 2016. Patients were invited for bubble-echocardiography to detect vascular right-to-left shunting and, if abnormal, subsequent computed tomography thorax for diagnosis of PAVM. Data are presented as n/N (%) or median with interquartile range (IQR). RESULTS: Study participation was accepted by 47/157 (30%) eligible patients amongst whom two did not appear for scheduled bubble-echocardiography. The median age of participants was 54 years (IQR 45-62) and 19/57 (33%) were females compared with 59 years (IQR 48-68, p = 0.05) and 41/85 females (48%, p = 0.22) in non-participants. Bubble-echocardiography was suggestive of shunt in 10/45 (22%) participants and PAVM was subsequently confirmed by computed tomography in one patient with grade 1 shunting. The corresponding prevalence of PAVM was 2% (95% confidence interval 0.06-11.8) amongst all examined participants. Another 9/45 (20%) were diagnosed with patent in persistent foramen ovale (n = 8) or atrial septum defect (n = 1), which is comparable with the overall prevalence of 25% amongst adults in the Danish background population. CONCLUSIONS: Undiagnosed PAVM amongst adult survivors of cryptogenic bacterial brain abscess is rare but may be considered in select patients. The prevalence of cardiac right-to-left shunts amongst brain abscess patients corresponds to the prevalence in the general population.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Bodilsen, Jacob","Madsen, Trine","Brandt, Christian Thomas","Müllertz, Katrine","Wiese, Lothar","Demirci, Semra Turan","Suhrs, Hannah Elena","Larsen, Lykke","Gill, Sabine Ute Alice","Hansen, Birgitte Rønde","Nilsson, Brian","Omland, Lars Haukali","Fosbøl, Emil","Kjeldsen, Anette Drøhse","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-724198"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["DASGIB study group","Danish Study Group of Infections of the Brain (DASGIB)"],"corresponding_author":["Bodilsen, Jacob"],"keyword":["Brain abscess","Cerebral abscess","HHT","Hereditary haemorrhagic telangiectasia","PAVM","PFO","Pulmonary arteriovenous malformation","Shunt"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pulmonary arteriovenous malformations in patients with previous brain abscess a cross sectional population based study","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ene.16176","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-724198","identifier":[{"id":"85178874619","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11235687","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38064178","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-72e93f03-0d93-483e-bae8-5456bebd8479","ku-cfbd7aa6-fdf7-4870-87b8-06a59abc488c","sdu-66053b99-50c8-4d75-b7d0-e60cc0298c9d"],"keyword":["HHT","PAVM","PFO","brain abscess","cerebral abscess","hereditary haemorrhagic telangiectasia","pulmonary arteriovenous malformation","shunt"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-661967B0BC9AAACC73FB699C05639994"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/687377458/Bodi