"Winther-Larsen","locid":"162faab4-e6ad-4fce-8149-eafe733901ec","name":"Winther-Larsen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-2763-595X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"nielsenchristianpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9d3632a4-4c78-4cc2-b3cd-56f987332e9c","name":"Nielsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5711-6595","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"olsenmariannepau","last":"Olsen","locid":"dc242145-c4fd-4904-a5d9-5765213006c5","name":"Olsen, Marianne","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"toftninapau","last":"Toft","name":"Toft, Nina","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Okkels Birk","key":"lorenzenmadsokkelsbirkpau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"b2af6b2c-fddc-4e6d-938b-8c25d45e0d80","name":"Lorenzen, Mads Okkels Birk","orcid":"0000-0002-3137-3809","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Heilmann","key":"jensenliseheilmannpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lise Heilmann","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Sif","key":"gudbrandsdottirsifpau","last":"Gudbrandsdottir","name":"Gudbrandsdottir, Sif","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"helbyjenspau","last":"Helby","name":"Helby, Jens","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Maria","key":"rossingmariapau","last":"Rossing","locid":"21caea2d-4f85-4f9b-bb36-a8ec34cac4a8","name":"Rossing, Maria","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 11 12","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"vanwijkrichardpau","last":"van Wijk","name":"van Wijk, Richard","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"petersenjesperpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jesper","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39085840"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13023-024-03298-4","issn":["17501172"],"issue":"1","journal":"Orphanet Journal of Rare Diseases","paperid":"284","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Orphanet Journal of Rare Diseases","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200050588"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bc12a0af-2898-42f1-bd92-a619f2c19806","au-91e45ff7-ac1c-4797-b074-407769615372","ku-e5b8486f-dd04-4293-b400-ee840bc5cc2f","sdu-a3985b47-bbe2-4685-89ae-4a2a573ec0a3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"DAHEAN : A Danish nationwide study ensuring quality assurance through real-world data for suspected hereditary anemia patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-755897","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Deep learning methods are revolutionizing natural science. In this study, we aim to apply such techniques to develop blood type prediction models based on cheap to analyze and easily scalable screening array genotyping platforms. METHODS: Combining existing blood types from blood banks and imputed screening array genotypes for ~111,000 Danish and 1168 Finnish blood donors, we used deep learning techniques to train and validate blood type prediction models for 36 antigens in 15 blood group systems. To account for missing genotypes a denoising autoencoder initial step was utilized, followed by a convolutional neural network blood type classifier. RESULTS: Two thirds of the trained blood type prediction models demonstrated an F1-accuracy above 99%. Models for antigens with low or high frequencies like, for example, Cw, low training cohorts like, for example, Cob, or very complicated genetic underpinning like, for example, RhD, proved to be more challenging for high accuracy (>99%) DL modeling. However, in the Danish cohort only 4 out of 36 models (Cob, Cw, D-weak, Kpa) failed to achieve a prediction F1-accuracy above 97%. This high predictive performance was replicated in the Finnish cohort. DISCUSSION: High accuracy in a variety of blood groups proves viability of deep learning-based blood type prediction using array chip genotypes, even in blood groups with nontrivial genetic underpinnings. These techniques are suitable for aiding in identifying blood donors with rare blood types by greatly narrowing down the potential pool of candidate donors before clinical grade confirmation.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Moslemi, Camous","Sækmose, Susanne","Larsen, Rune","Brodersen, Thorsten","Bay, Jakob T.","Didriksen, Maria","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Bruun, Mie T.","Dowsett, Joseph","Dinh, Khoa M.","Mikkelsen, Christina","Hyvärinen, Kati","Ritari, Jarmo","Partanen, Jukka","Ullum, Henrik","Erikstrup, Christian","Ostrowski, Sisse R.","Olsson, Martin L.","Pedersen, Ole B."],"cuid":["S05-100.00-766679"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Moslemi, Camous"],"country":["Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Finnish Red Cross","Finnish Red Cross Blood Service","Lund University","Office for Medical Services","Region Skåne","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["AI","Blood Donors","Blood Group Antigens genetics","Blood antigen","Blood types","Convolutional neural network","Deep learning","Denmark","Denoising autoencoder","Female","Finland","Genetic prediction","Genomics methods","Genotype","Humans","Illumina GSA","Male","Neural Networks Computer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a deep learning approach to prediction of blood group antigens from genomic data","src":["aau","au","ku","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/trf.18013","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the Danish Blood Donor Study for making data available for the research done in this publication. The collection of questionnaires was supported by the Independent Research Fund Denmark, project number 0214\\u201000127B. The genotypes of the Finnish blood donors were received from the Blood Service Biobank of the Finnish Red Cross Blood Service, Helsinki, Finland. We also thank Bloddonornes forskningsfond and A.P M\\u00F8ller Fonden for awarding this project research grants of DKK 64931 and 45000, respectively. SB was supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grants NNF17OC0027594 and NNF14CC0001)."],"id":"S05-100.00-766679","identifier":[{"id":"39268576","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85203695657","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4f9f608b-0303-44a0-81ff-d5b29ee88a03","au-50522a1c-a772-43cf-ba37-273fe15e2bf0","ku-84ae77b7-5e97-426b-9653-c9ac0a7a75ca","ruc-6608f10a-567c-44b0-a4e7-487b054de0a5","sdu-dfe236f4-64ee-47aa-9884-5bb074600aec"],"keyword":["AI","Blood Donors","Blood Group Antigens/genetics","Denmark","Female","Finland","Genomics/methods","Genotype","Humans","Illumina GSA","Male","Neural Networks, Computer","blood antigen","blood types","convolutional neural network","deep learning","denoising autoencoder","genetic prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-8-090FB3E340CB23E25972A7BA25EDB02C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/trf.18013","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/106583382/Transfusion_-_2024_-_Moslemi_-_A_deep_learning_approach_to_prediction_of_blood_group_antigens_from_genomic_data.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/754336085/Moslemi_et_al._2024_._A_deep_learning_approach_to_prediction_of_blood_group_antigens_from_genomic_data.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/277060437/Transfusion_-_2024_-_Moslemi_-_A_deep_learning_approach_to_prediction_of_blood_group_antigens_from_genomic_data.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.k