.","key":"baypau","last":"Bay","name":"Bay, Jakob T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"didriksenpau","last":"Didriksen","name":"Didriksen, Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaspar R.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"bc41abea-4b3e-473b-b7a6-8d2c7515f572","name":"Nielsen, Kaspar René","name_org":"Nielsen, Kaspar R.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie T.","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"f598dc3b-7b04-4769-bd48-496f0c8a2ec2","name":"Bruun, Mie Topholm","name_org":"Bruun, Mie T.","orcid":"0000-0002-8819-5388","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph","key":"dowsettpau","last":"Dowsett","name":"Dowsett, Joseph","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Khoa M.","key":"dinhpau","last":"Dinh","locid":"aa16c35a-5336-405a-94c0-eb6d9e53f7ba","name":"Dinh, Khoa Manh","name_org":"Dinh, Khoa M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1881-5673","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Christina","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 11","corresponding":null,"first":"Kati","key":"hyvärinenpau","last":"Hyvärinen","name":"Hyvärinen, Kati","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 11","corresponding":null,"first":"Jarmo","key":"ritaripau","last":"Ritari","name":"Ritari, Jarmo","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 11","corresponding":null,"first":"Jukka","key":"partanenpau","last":"Partanen","name":"Partanen, Jukka","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","name":"Ullum, Henrik","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","locid":"523ae417-65a9-46aa-b665-0d88271dc0b9","name":"Erikstrup, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6551-6647","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 13","first":"Sisse R.","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","name_org":"Ostrowski, Sisse R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14 15 16 17","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin L.","key":"olssonpau","last":"Olsson","name":"Olsson, Martin L.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 13","first":"Ole B.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0d43956a-6e43-42d7-8b29-4505d03ea5c8","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole B.","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39268576"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/trf.18013","issn":["00411132","15372995"],"issn_org":["00411132"],"issue":"11","journal":"Transfusion","pages":"2179-2195","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Transfusion","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203695657"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4f9f608b-0303-44a0-81ff-d5b29ee88a03","au-50522a1c-a772-43cf-ba37-273fe15e2bf0","ku-84ae77b7-5e97-426b-9653-c9ac0a7a75ca","ruc-6608f10a-567c-44b0-a4e7-487b054de0a5","sdu-dfe236f4-64ee-47aa-9884-5bb074600aec"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A deep learning approach to prediction of blood group antigens from genomic data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-100.00-766679","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A viruses (IAVs) originate from wild birds but have on several occasions jumped host barriers and are now also circulating in humans and mammals. The IAV host receptors (glycans with galactose linked to a sialic acid (SA) in an α2,3 or α2,6 linkage) are crucial host factors restricting inter-species transmission. In general, avian-origin IAVs show a preference for SA-α2,3 (avian receptor), whereas IAVs isolated from humans and pigs prefer SA-α2,6 (human receptor). N-acetylneuraminic acid (Neu5Ac) and N-glycolylneuraminic acid (Neu5Gc) are the two major SAs. Neu5Ac is expressed in all species, whereas Neu5Gc is only expressed in a limited number of domestic species such as pigs and horses, but not in humans. Despite that previous studies have shown that the IAV host receptor distribution appears to be similar in pigs and humans, none of these studies have investigated the expression of Neu5Gc-α2,6 in situ in porcine tissues. Thus, the aim of this study was to elucidate the distribution of IAV host receptors expressed in the porcine respiratory tract and relate the expression to the viral tropism of diverse host-adapted IAVs. The IAV receptor (SA-α2,3 and SA-α2,6) distribution and the presence of specifically Neu5Gc-α2,6 in the porcine nasal, tracheal, and lung tissues was investigated by lectin histochemistry. Furthermore, IAV immunohistochemistry was performed on tissues from pigs experimentally infected with IAVs, either adapted to pigs or humans, to investigate the significance of the IAV host receptors and the tropism of the diverse host-adapted IAVs. We document for the first time the expression of the avian receptor on the surface of the porcine nasal mucosa and an equal expression of Neu5Ac-α2,6 and Neu5Gc-α2,6 on the surface of the tracheal epithelium and alveoli. In all IAV-infected pigs, we found a low amount of IAV-positive cells in the trachea despite a high expression of the human receptor. Cumulatively, these findings suggest that optimal IAV replication involves a complex interplay between the viruses and their host receptors and that there might be other less clearly defined host factors that determine the site of replication.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kristensen, Charlotte","Larsen, Lars Erik","Trebbien, Ramona","Jensen, Henrik Elvang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719204"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Influenza A virus","Pigs","Receptor","Sialic acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the avian influenza a virus receptor sa α000000000002 000000000003 gal is expressed in the porcine nasal mucosa sustaining the pig as a mixing vessel for new influenza viruses","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.virusres.2023.199304","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719204","identifier":[{"id":"38142890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181827716","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10793167","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-084e6b84-ee71-42de-b21e-b16948ff1f6f"],"keyword":["Experimental infections","Host tropism","Influenza A virus","Pigs","Receptor","Sialic acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A28D8EFDAE68F29DB25A5DD5736795EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.virusres.2023.199304","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381842590/The_avian_influenza_A_virus_receptor_SA_2_3_Gal_is_expressed_in_the_porcine_nasal_mucosa_sustaining_the_pig_as_a_mixing_vessel_for_new_influenza_viruses.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38142890"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.virusres.2023.199304","issn":["01681702","09212590"],"issn_org":["01681702"],"journal":"Virus Research","paperid":"199304","status":"p","title":"Virus Research","volume":"340"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181827716"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-084e6b84-ee71-42de-b21e-b16948ff1f6f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The avian influenza A virus receptor SA-α2,3-Gal is expressed in the porcine nasal mucosa sustaining the pig as a mixing vessel for new influenza viruses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719204","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The popularity of chatbots, such as ChatGPT, has brought research attention to question answering systems, capable to generate natural language answers to user’s natural language queries. However, also in other kinds of systems, flexibility of querying, including but also going beyond the use of natural language, is an important feature. With this consideration in mind the paper presents a critical and comprehensive analysis of recent developments, trends and challenges of Flexible Query Answering Systems (FQASs). Flexible query answering is a multidisciplinary research field that is not limited to question answering in natural language, but comprises other query forms and interaction modalities, which aim to provide powerful means and techniques for better reflecting human preferences and intentions to retrieve relevant information. It adopts methods at the crossroad of several disciplines among which Information Retrieval (IR), databases, knowledge based systems, knowledge and data engineering, Natural Language Processing (NLP) and the semantic web may be mentioned. The analysis principles are inspired by the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analysis (PRISMA) framework, characterized by a top-down process, starting with relevant keywords for the topic of interest to retrieve relevant articles from meta-sources And complementing these articles with other relevant articles from seed sources Identified by a bottom-up process. to mine the retrieved publication data a network analysis is performed Which allows to present in a synthetic way intrinsic topics of the selected publications. issues dealt with are related to query answering methods Both model-based and data-driven (the latter based on either machine learning or deep learning) And to their needs for explainability and fairness to deal with big data Notably by taking into account data veracity. conclusions point out trends and challenges to help better shaping the future of the FQAS field.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andreasen, Troels","Bordogna, Gloria","De Tré, Guy","Kacprzyk, Janusz","Larsen, Henrik Legind","Zadrozny, Slawomir"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733189"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Italy","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ghent University","National Research Council of Italy","Polish Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Legind Technologies"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the power and potentials of flexible query answering systems a critical and comprehensive analysis","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.datak.2023.102246","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-733189","identifier":[{"id":"85178423344","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-62ff040d-d1d5-4c2a-a299-b92f9123be83"],"keyword":["Data-driven query answering","Flexible query answering","Model-based query answering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8E9039DEEE9121DD070CFFD216A65E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/100493684/The_Power_and_Potentials_of_Flexible_Query_Answering_Systems.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.datak.2023.102246","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"ghent university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pl","key":"polish academy of sciences","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polish Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Legind Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"f31701bc-1bef-45ac-b9fa-3e931672bcd4","name":"Andreasen, Troels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gloria","key":"bordognapau","last":"Bordogna","name":"Bordogna, Gloria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Guy","key":"detrépau","last":"De Tré","name":"De Tré, Guy","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Janusz","key":"kacprzykpau","last":"Kacprzyk","name":"Kacprzyk, Janusz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Henrik Legind","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik Legind","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Slawomir","key":"zadroznypau","last":"Zadrozny","name":"Zadrozny, Slawomir","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.datak.2023.102246","issn":["0169023X","18726933"],"issn_org":["0169023X"],"journal":"Data & Knowledge Engineering","paperid":"102246","status":"p","title":"Data & Knowledge Engineering","volume":"149"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178423344"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-62ff040d-d1d5-4c2a-a299-b92f9123be83"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The Power and Potentials of Flexible Query Answering Systems : a Critical and Comprehensive Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733189","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The article investigates whether the development of Greenland’s autonomy over the past 40 years can be fruitfully understood as a case of path dependency or, alternatively, as a series of changing equilibriums marked by critical junctures. The article addresses the following questions: 1) What were the drivers behind the establishment of Greenlandic home rule in 1979? 2) What were the drivers behind the establishment of Self Government in 2009? 3) What are the implications for today’s constitutional debate in Greenland? It is shown that the 1979 Greenland Home Rule Act followed from a critical juncture triggered by the Greenlandic ‘no’-vote on EU membership. The subsequent 2009 Greenland Self Government Act was, to a large extent, a consequence of endogenous change within a path dependency flowing from the Home Rule Act. The logic from home rule was carried over into self-government: the gradual transfer of policy areas to Greenlandic self-government when Greenland was willing and able to take over the policy areas. It is suggested that there is a potential tension between path dependency arising from the GSGA and intensified Greenlandic expressions of political identity which may challenge the GSGA logic, while there are still dynamics which pull towards the GSGA logic.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Uffe","Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738749"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the development of greenland s self government and independence in the shadow of the unitary state","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/2154896X.2024.2342117","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-738749","identifier":[{"id":"85191143622","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-19055d13-4c6c-45d3-bd87-7e0774eb5bd9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-965BA7EC4662B2309D373654D3B56CB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/2154896X.2024.2342117","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/395709147/The_development_of_Greenland_s_self_government_and_independence_in_the_shadow_of_the_unitary_state.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for Voting and Parties","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Political Theory","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Research Group on Climate, Environment and Change (REGROUP)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Uffe","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"3253599b-6c78-4522-a1c6-87f06fe37df7","name":"Jakobsen, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0002-7114-1981","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/2154896x.2024.2342117","issn":["2154896X","21548978"],"issn_org":["2154896X"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Polar Journal","pages":"9-27","status":"p","title":"The Polar Journal","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191143622"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-19055d13-4c6c-45d3-bd87-7e0774eb5bd9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The development of Greenland’s self-government and independence in the shadow of the unitary state","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738749","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Over long stretches of the north-east coast of Qeqertarsuaq (Disko), the sediments in the Nuussuaq Basin and their relations to the volcanic rocks are concealed beneath numerous landslides. Two cores south of Qullissat drilled by Falconbridge Ltd in 1994, targeting a native-iron-bearing igneous body assumed to be a sill, present well-preserved sections through the hidden succession. We have dated the sediments in the cores palynologically. The lower part comprises 115 m of deltaic deposits, including coal seams, of the Cretaceous Atane Formation, Qilakitsoq Member (late Turonian to early Coniacian age), which has not been recorded on Disko before. The two cores and five short coastal cliff sections are mutually correlatable and correlate further to the coal seams earlier mined at Qullissat; the coals are hereby dated for the first time. The Cretaceous rocks are overlain by 15 m of marine deposits, mainly mudstones, of the Danian Eqalulik Formation, with a hiatus of c. 24 million years. The igneous body of native-iron-bearing basaltic andesite has a thick, red-oxidised, vesiculated and brecciated top zone and is interpreted as a subaerial lava flow belonging to the Asuk Member of the Vaigat Formation. The flow has run perhaps up to 20 km from the eruption site to the sea, where it ponded and attained a thickness of 138 m, the thickest lava flow in the West Greenland Basalt Group. The flow is overlain by 22 m of non-marine sandstones and mudstones of the Atanikerluk Formation. The core correlation indicates the existence of a fault with c. 90 m vertical displacement between the two drill sites. The structural relations of the various parts of the Atane Formation along the north-east coast of Disko necessitate the assumption of another hidden, prevolcanic fault south of Qullissaaqqat.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Lotte Melchior","Pedersen, Gunver Krarup","Nøhr-Hansen, Henrik","Pedersen, Asger Ken","Bojesen-Koefoed, Jørgen A.","Sørensen, Erik Vest","Lindström, Sofie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738752"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a hidden succession revealed cretaceous and paleocene sediments and a native iron bearing lava flow in cores near qullissat disko west greenland","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34194/geusb.v57.8361","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-738752","identifier":[{"id":"85190600617","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1978fb52-97c4-4f24-b632-1c15401a9d91"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-19DD5D91C2B40EBFA090038C030BD8A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34194/geusb.v57.8361","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/389409547/GEUSB_A_8361_O.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte Melchior","key":"larsenlottemelchiorpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Lotte Melchior","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gunver Krarup","key":"pedersengunverkraruppau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Gunver Krarup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"nøhrhansenhenrikpau","last":"Nøhr-Hansen","name":"Nøhr-Hansen, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Asger Ken","key":"pedersenasgerkenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d0a604ff-9665-460a-80a1-fb7ed295e569","name":"Pedersen, Asger Ken","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen A.","key":"bojesenkoefoedjørgenapau","last":"Bojesen-Koefoed","name":"Bojesen-Koefoed, Jørgen A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik Vest","key":"sørensenerikvestpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Erik Vest","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Sofie","key":"lindströmsofiepau","last":"Lindström","locid":"9fd76168-ca33-4022-8ab9-d9d97f45c436","name":"Lindström, Sofie","orcid":"0000-0001-8278-1055","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34194/geusb.v57.8361","issn":["19044666","25972162"],"issn_org":["25972162"],"journal":"GEUS Bulletin","paperid":"8361","status":"p","title":"GEUS Bulletin","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190600617"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1978fb52-97c4-4f24-b632-1c15401a9d91"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A hidden succession revealed : Cretaceous and Paleocene sediments and a native-iron-bearing lava flow in cores near Qullissat, Disko, West Greenland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738752","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Cereal straw is a large biomass resource which may potentially be pretreated for biogas production by combined ensiling and storage. Five pilot-scale ensiling experiments were performed with straw of wheat, barley and rye, baled in midi-bales (0.9*1.2*2.0 m) with various water contents (17–68 %), ensiling additives and ensiling periods (173–230 days). The water content in the bales differed depending on previous precipitation but also the time of day for baling. Temperature in wet straw increased to 30 and 63 °C during storage for bales with and without wrapping, respectively, and mean dry weight loss was 5.1 ± 5.9 % and 10.5 ± 7.3 %, respectively. During storage, pH dropped significantly in wrapped straw bales but not in bales without wrapping. In wrapped straw without additives, pH after ensiling decreased significantly with increasing initial water content, indicating the importance of water content above 30–40 % for ensiling of straw. Besides a more rapid pH reduction when applying acetic acid, there was no significant effect of acetic and formic acid, lactic acid bacteria and brown juice on pH after storage. Ensiling of wet straw had a significant effect on biochemical methane potential (BMP) in some cases, with up to 32 % increase. There was limited effect of ensiling additives on BMP, whereas increasing water content in the straw significantly increased BMP. Improper wrapping of straw during storage reduced BMP with 17–30 %. Overall, proper wrapping and good ensiling of wet straw may result in up to 25 % extra methane yield whereas poor storage may result in up to 37 % loss.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ugilt Larsen, Søren","Møller, Henrik Bjarne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745248"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ugilt Larsen, Søren"],"keyword":["Additives","Anaerobic digestion","Biochemical methane potential","Silage","Storage loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"baling and ensiling of wet cereal straw as combined storage and pretreatment for biogas production","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2024.107294","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745248","identifier":[{"id":"85197024961","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bf993042-1361-44d1-943b-5be5c7f4e08e"],"keyword":["Additives","Anaerobic digestion","Biochemical methane potential","Silage","Storage loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47AEF053DC51CF0BF7FADB942D9A5A03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2024.107294","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/419932649/1-s2.0-S0961953424002472-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum - CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Finlandsgade 22"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Ugilt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6e72b743-5e26-4bcf-880a-16f77e1fc2a8","name":"Ugilt Larsen, Søren","name_org":"Larsen, Søren Ugilt","orcid":"0000-0002-1802-9106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bjarne","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"a2eda86a-cdac-4996-8db0-3cecfe51be12","name":"Møller, Henrik Bjarne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2024.107294","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","paperid":"107294","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","title_org":"Biomass and Bioenergy","volume":"187"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197024961"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bf993042-1361-44d1-943b-5be5c7f4e08e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Baling and ensiling of wet cereal straw as combined storage and pretreatment for biogas production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745248","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Large-scale reduction of greenhouse gasses is necessary to abate the climate crisis, for which technological development will pave the way. Advancing research from academia to industry is crucial for technological progress. Pilot scale studies are the intermediate step from bench to industry. New challenges arise during technology upscaling, many of which have not been previously described in the literature. This article provides a guide of the do's and don'ts to researchers venturing into pilot work. The learnings and experiences gained by working with pilot-scale CO2 capture plant are presented and discussed. This work outlines the process challenges encountered during the commissioning and operation of a CO2 capture pilot using 30 wt% MEA and with a capacity to capture one tonne CO2/day from flue gas. Conducting pilot work in industrial facilities and outside controlled lab environments comes with unexpected problems. The issues faced during our pilot work are presented along with troubleshooting strategies and possible solutions. This work can aid researchers in identifying and rectifying operational challenges and conducting successful pilot campaigns.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Vinjarapu, Sai Hema Bhavya","Løge, Isaac Appelquist","Neerup, Randi","Larsen, Anders Hellerup","Rasmussen, Gorm","Jørsboe, Jens Kristian","Villadsen, Sebastian Nis Bay","Jensen, Søren","Karlsson, Jakob Lindkvist","Kappel, Jannik","Lassen, Henrik","Blinksbjerg, Peter","von Solms, Nicolas","Fosbøl, Philip Loldrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-758958"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vinjarapu, Sai Hema Bhavya"],"keyword":["CO capture","Operation","Scale up"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Amager Ressourcecenter"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learnings from up scaling co sub 000000000002 sub capture challenges and experiences with pilot work","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ces.2024.120576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-758958","identifier":[{"id":"85200969700","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1a3c6d0e-caa1-4c50-8ac8-caf14e95a4c1"],"keyword":["CO capture","Challenges and learnings","Operation","Pilot work","Scale-up"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B7CC29EDD3E0EBC4920164AB3614C93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ces.2024.120576","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/372042721/1-s2.0-S0009250924008765-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CERE – Center for Energy Ressources Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Pentair Union Engineering A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":