urnal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-758958","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Weight gain is a common side effect of antidepressive treatment, causing distress among patients and caretakers as it can lead to treatment discontinuation and complications such as diabetes type II and cardiovascular disease. Vortioxetine is one of the newer antidepressants and the pharmacodynamics differ from the selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors. It is marketed as being weight neutral; however, there is little evidence as to why. In recent years, there has been an increased focus on the faecal microbiota and its impact on body weight and mental and physical health. In the current work, we examine the effect of vortioxetine on weight gain and faecal microbiota composition. Methods: Forty male C57BL/6NTac mice were primed for 8 weeks with a high-fat diet (Hfd) or control diet (Cd), followed by a 4-week period on the same diet and additional +/− vortioxetine 10 mg/kg/daily. Results: Vortioxetine reduced Hfd-induced weight gain (Hfd + V: 8.2%, Hfd − V: 12.7%; p = 0.0374) but did not affect weight gain of the control group (Cd + V: 7.54%, Cd − V: 7.56%; p = 0.4944). Significant differences in faecal microbiota were observed in mice who received vortioxetine. Conclusion: Vortioxetine caused significant changes to the faecal microbiota composition and appeared to limit Hfd-induced weight gain.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Corfitsen, Henrik Thyge","Bilde, Katrine","Rerup, Trine","Larsen, Agnete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-773474"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Corfitsen, Henrik Thyge"],"keyword":["Faecal microbiota","Mice","Vortioxetine","Weight Gain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of vortioxetine on faecal microbiota in high fat diet exposed mice a link to weight protection","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85200952060","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-773474","identifier":[{"id":"85200952060","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39129400","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b9ce79f1-5fdc-4e1b-9e85-2962acbf0386"],"keyword":["faecal microbiota","mice","vortioxetine","weight gain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-229D8CFAF077065B04DBFDCCEE006660"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Thyge","key":"corfitsenpau","last":"Corfitsen","locid":"720b5151-6df7-4103-bc8d-61abca4b031d","name":"Corfitsen, Henrik Thyge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"bildepau","last":"Bilde","name":"Bilde, Katrine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"reruppau","last":"Rerup","name":"Rerup, Trine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Agnete","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"31449996-34ed-426f-b5b6-78d753234c5b","name":"Larsen, Agnete","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39129400"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.14058","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"4","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"417-428","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","publisher_org":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","title_org":"Basic and Clinical Pharmacology and Toxicology","volume":"135"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200952060"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b9ce79f1-5fdc-4e1b-9e85-2962acbf0386"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effect of vortioxetine on faecal microbiota in high-fat diet-exposed mice—A link to weight protection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-773474","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
