,"pages":"546-555","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183051147"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","gildhøj private hospital","gildhøj privathospital"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-35f128a3-03ae-44bf-aaa6-b4347272257e","sdu-8a10abda-c0d6-438c-9ff7-319b804e9992"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations of dexamethasone's effect on morphine consumption after total knee arthroplasty—Subgroup analyses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.61-735475","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Water freely diffuses across cell membranes, making it suitable for measuring absolute tissue perfusion. In this study, we introduce an imaging method for conducting coronary artery angiography and quantifying myocardial perfusion across the entire heart using hyperpolarized water. Methods: 1H was hyperpolarized using dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) with UV-generated radicals. Submillimeter resolution coronary artery images were acquired as 2D projections using a spoiled GRE (SPGRE) sequence gated on diastole. Dynamic perfusion images were obtained with a multi-slice SPGRE with diastole gating, covering the entire heart. Perfusion values were analyzed through histograms, and the most frequent estimated perfusion value (the mode of the distribution), was compared with the average values for 15O water PET from the literature. Results: A liquid state polarization of 10% at the time of the injection and a 30 s T1 in D2O TRIS buffer were measured. Both coronary artery and dynamic perfusion images exhibited good quality. The main and small coronary artery branches were well resolved. The most frequent estimated perfusion value is around 0.6 mL/g/min, which is lower than the average values obtained from the literature for 15O-water PET (around 1.1 and 1.5 mL/g/min). Conclusions: The study successfully demonstrated the feasibility of achieving high-resolution, motion-free coronary artery angiography and 3D whole-heart quantitative myocardial perfusion using hyperpolarized water.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Zhao, Yupeng","Lerche, Mathilde H","Karlsson, Magnus","Olin, Rie Beck","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Aastrup, Malene","Redda, Mohsen","Laustsen, Christoffer","Hansen, Lars G.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-086.83-756040"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"keyword":["Coronary artery angiography","Myocardium","Perfusion","hyperpolarized MRI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized water for coronary artery angiography and whole heart myocardial perfusion quantification","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/tomography10070084","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the European Union\\u2019s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program; grant No 858149."],"id":"S02-086.83-756040","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11280581","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85199594677","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39058056","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8432b530-8a4c-49d5-8362-dfceaa4849fb","dtu-3e12f2b8-c3a3-4cfc-b3fc-716f1b7b174e"],"keyword":["coronary artery angiography","hyperpolarized MRI","myocardium","perfusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-38A45E160485FFD5915B73C682746231"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/385059825/tomography-10-00084.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/tomography10070084","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/373533748/tomography-10-00084-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yupeng","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"2b1ccf6e-22a6-4eb4-a789-3dfc4348f5ad","name":"Zhao, Yupeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rie Beck","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","name_org":"Olin, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"søvsøszocskahansenpau","last":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen","locid":"2ea5821e-bbda-4f7e-a18a-0b9eb3b993f0","name":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","orcid":"0000-0001-5512-9870","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene","key":"aastruppau","last":"Aastrup","locid":"90ad75dc-62b6-44b0-b090-65f92218e0e8","name":"Aas