{"abstract":"Solanum bulbocastanum is a wild diploid tuber-bearing plant. We here demonstrate transgene-free genome editing of S. bulbocastanum protoplasts and regeneration of gene-edited plants. We use ribonucleoproteins, consisting of Cas9 and sgRNA, assembled in vitro, to target a gene belonging to the nitrate and peptide transporter family. Four different sgRNAs were designed and we observed efficiency in gene-editing in the protoplast pool between 8.5% and 12.4%. Twenty-one plants were re-generated from microcalli developed from individual protoplasts. In three of the plants we found that the target gene had been edited. Two of the edited plants had deletion mutations introduced into both alleles, whereas one only had a mutation in one of the alleles. Our work demonstrates that protocols for the transformation of Solanum tuberosum can be optimized to be applied to a wild Solanum species.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Azariadis, Aristotelis","Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","Carlsen, Frida M.","Westberg, Ida","Brinch-Pedersen, Henrik","Pedersen, Bent L.","Hebelstrup, Kim"],"cuid":["S02-096.67-724730"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","Hebelstrup, Kim"],"keyword":["Genome editing","Protoplasts","de novo domestication","transgene free","wild potato"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a walk on the wild side genome editing of tuber bearing i solanum bulbocastanum i","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/plants13071044","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.67-724730","identifier":[{"id":"85190124991","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11013279","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"001201515500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"38611572","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-885a207d-9881-4f59-9c0e-c5745840f76e","ku-5a70ef57-6002-4bcd-ada8-287c89cec0de"],"keyword":["de novo domestication","genome editing","protoplasts","transgene free","wild potato"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5EFFCBF99D1A65C0C418340245C2DF36"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/389089405/plants_13_01044.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/plants13071044","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Glycobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aristotelis","key":"azariadispau","last":"Azariadis","locid":"119c6d83-cf75-40bb-adfb-2af86307f976","name":"Azariadis, Aristotelis","orcid":"0000-0002-4408-4125","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olga Agata","key":"andrzejczakpau","last":"Andrzejczak","locid":"591d74a1-7fcc-477e-a5e1-5edefd34ade0","name":"Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","orcid":"0000-0002-5178-5229","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frida M.","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","locid":"ccf0fcd3-f291-439c-9905-a1f538200fb5","name":"Carlsen, Frida Meijer","name_org":"Carlsen, Frida M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ida","key":"westbergpau","last":"Westberg","locid":"7a38dab4-effb-444d-9c26-2ac5a1b3cab3","name":"Westberg, Ida","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"brinchpedersenpau","last":"Brinch-Pedersen","locid":"b99acfd4-b212-450a-86a8-0d91eb9c1a15","name":"Brinch-Pedersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9773-8903","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bent L.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0d3fa717-88a9-444e-8096-3163ca10ec75","name":"Petersen, Bent Larsen","name_org":"Petersen, Bent L.","orcid":"0000-0002-2004-9077","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"hebelstruppau","last":"Hebelstrup","locid":"e20721de-154d-42bf-b85a-114d8097fbbf","name":"Hebelstrup, Kim","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38611572"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/plants13071044","issn":["22237747"],"issue":"7","journal":"Plants","paperid":"1044","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Plants","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190124991"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-885a207d-9881-4f59-9c0e-c5745840f76e","ku-5a70ef57-6002-4bcd-ada8-287c89cec0de"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Walk on the Wild Side: : Genome Editing of Tuber-Bearing <i>Solanum bulbocastanum</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.67-724730","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Up to 20% of patients develop chronic pain after total knee arthroplasty (TKA), yet there is a scarcity of effective interventions for this population. Objective: To evaluate whether neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education were superior to pain neuroscience education alone for patients with chronic pain after TKA. Design, Setting, and Participants: A superiority randomized clinical trial was conducted at 3 outpatient clinics at Aalborg University Hospital in Denmark. Participants with moderate-to-severe average daily pain intensity and no signs of prosthesis failure at least 1 year after primary TKA were included. Participant recruitment was initiated on April 12, 2019, and completed on October 31, 2022. The 12-month follow-up was completed on March 21, 2023. Interventions: The study included 24 sessions of supervised neuromuscular exercise (2 sessions per week for 12 weeks) and 2 total sessions of pain neuroscience education (6 weeks between each session) or the same pain neuroscience education sessions alone. The interventions were delivered in groups of 2 to 4 participants. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was change from baseline to 12 months using the mean score of the Knee Injury and Osteoarthritis Outcome Score, covering the 4 subscales pain, symptoms, activity of daily living, and knee-related quality of life (KOOS 4; scores range from 0 to 100, with higher scores indicating better outcomes). The outcome assessors and statistician were blinded. All randomized participants were included in the intention-to-treat analysis. Results: Among the 69 participants (median age, 67.2 years [IQR, 61.2-71.9 years]; 40 female [58%]) included in the study, 36 were randomly assigned to the neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education group, and 33 to the pain neuroscience education-alone group. The intention-to-treat analysis showed no between-group difference in change from baseline to 12 months for the KOOS 4 (7.46 [95% CI, 3.04-11.89] vs 8.65 [95% CI, 4.67-12.63] points; mean difference, -1.33 [95% CI, -7.59 to 4.92]; P =.68). Among the 46 participants who participated in the 12-month assessment in the 2 groups, 16 (34.8%) experienced a clinically important improvement (a difference of ≥10 points on the KOOS 4) with no between-group difference. No serious adverse events were observed. Conclusions and Relevance: In this randomized clinical trial, the results demonstrated that neuromuscular exercises and pain neuroscience education were not superior to pain neuroscience education alone in participants with chronic pain after TKA. Approximately one-third of the participants, regardless of intervention, experienced clinically important improvements. Future studies should investigate which patient characteristics indicate a favorable response to exercises and/or pain neuroscience education. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT03886259.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper B.","Skou, Søren Thorgaard","Laursen, Mogens","Bruun, Niels Henrik","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S02-099.76-741512"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jesper B."],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee adverse effects","Chronic Pain etiology","Denmark","Exercise Therapy methods","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neurosciences education","Osteoarthritis Knee surgery","Pain Management methods","Pain Measurement","Pain Postoperative etiology","Patient Education as Topic methods","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exercise and pain neuroscience education for patients with chronic pain after total knee arthroplasty a randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.12179","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding/Support: This work was supported by grant R168-A5619 from the Danish Rheumatism Association and by the Svend Andersen Foundation and the Lions Club Danmark (Dr Larsen) and by grants 801790 for payment to the University of Southern Denmark and 945377 for payment to the N\\u00E6stved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospital from the European Union\\u2019s Horizon 2020 research and innovati on program (Prof Skou).","This work was supported by grant R168-A5619 from the Danish Rheumatism Association and by the Svend Andersen Foundation and the Lions Club Danmark (Dr Larsen) and by grants 801790 for payment to the University of Southern Denmark and 945377 for payment to the Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospital from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovati on program (Prof Skou)."],"id":"S02-099.76-741512","identifier":[{"id":"38787559","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85194129295","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11127128","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-b3afe817-3ff7-423d-b49a-e93a3080002a","sdu-60df1a86-fd91-40d2-82e4-1128c56cc5f0"],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/adverse effects","Chronic Pain/etiology","Denmark","Exercise Therapy/methods","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neurosciences/education","Osteoarthritis, Knee/surgery","Pain Management/methods","Pain Measurement","Pain, Postoperative/etiology","Patient Education as Topic/methods","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8D28B029F8E8CA10A072B5D497DFE72B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263043139/larsen_2024_oi_240432_1716222773.26589.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/713079116/larsen_2024_oi_240432_1716222773.26589.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.12179","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Musculoskeletal Health and Implementation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Center for Muscle and Joint Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Danish centre for motivation and behaviour science","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Musculoskeletal Function and Physiotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper B","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"16d35f43-63eb-473e-a466-4f5a12d5f43f","name":"Larsen, Jesper Bie","name_org":"Larsen, Jesper B","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-7913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren T.","key":"skoupau","last":"Skou","locid":"656a59cf-32bc-4190-b072-4adf47d954c1","name":"Skou, Søren Thorgaard","name_org":"Skou, Søren T.","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-7059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"26102317-00ee-41ec-ae85-c7a3bde4c391","name":"Laursen, Mogens Berg","name_org":"Laursen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-2791-3921","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"c46a199e-22d6-4140-807a-33564453684f","name":"Bruun, Niels Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38787559"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.12179","issn":["25743805"],"issue":"5","journal":"JAMA network open","paperid":"e2412179","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA network open","title_org":"JAMA NETWORK OPEN","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194129295"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b3afe817-3ff7-423d-b49a-e93a3080002a","sdu-60df1a86-fd91-40d2-82e4-1128c56cc5f0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exercise and Pain Neuroscience Education for Patients With Chronic Pain After Total Knee Arthroplasty: A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.76-741512","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: In selected cases of cardiogenic shock, veno-arterial extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (V-A ECMO) is combined with trans valvular micro axial flow pumps (ECMELLA). Observational studies indicate that ECMELLA may reduce mortality but exposing the patient to two advanced mechanical support devices may affect the early inflammatory response. We aimed to explore inflammatory biomarkers in a porcine cardiogenic shock model managed with V-A ECMO or ECMELLA. Methods: Fourteen landrace pigs had acute myocardial infarction-induced cardiogenic shock with minimal arterial pulsatility by microsphere embolization and were afterwards managed 1:1 with either V-A ECMO or ECMELLA for 4 h. Serial blood samples were drawn hourly and analyzed for serum concentrations of interleukin 6 (IL-6), IL-8, tumor necrosis factor alpha, and serum amyloid A (SAA). Results: An increase in IL-6, IL-8, and SAA levels was observed during the experiment for both groups. At 2–4 h of support, IL-6 levels were higher in ECMELLA compared to V-A ECMO animals (difference: 1416 pg/ml, 1278 pg/ml, and 1030 pg/ml). SAA levels were higher in ECMELLA animals after 3 and 4 h of support (difference: 401 ng/ml and 524 ng/ml) and a significant treatment-by-time effect of ECMELLA on SAA was identified (p = 0.04). No statistical significant between-group differences were observed in carotid artery blood flow, urine output, and lactate levels. Conclusions: Left ventricular unloading with Impella during V-A ECMO resulted in a more extensive inflammatory reaction despite similar end-organ perfusion.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Gregers, Emilie","Frederiksen, Peter H.","Udesen, Nanna L.J.","Linde, Louise","Banke, Ann","Povlsen, Amalie L.","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Hassager, Christian","Jensen, Lisette O.","Lassen, Jens F.","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, Hanne B.","Heegaard, Peter M. H.","Møller, Jacob E."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735397"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gregers, Emilie"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Cardiogenic shock","ECMELLA","ECMO","Unloading of the left ventricle","Venoarterial extracorporeal membrane oxygenation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immediate inflammatory response to mechanical circulatory support in a porcine model of severe cardiogenic shock","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-024-00625-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-735397","identifier":[{"id":"38647741","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85191053969","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11035503","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-7be470cb-5537-487c-809c-a5428bf8bef9","sdu-58d98f09-8d5c-4099-a4e4-7b81d162b074"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Cardiogenic shock","ECMELLA","ECMO","Unloading of the left ventricle","Venoarterial extracorporeal membrane oxygenation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-27CF737E96C0241E419EF06BCBD5AEB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-024-00625-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/360251386/66284ef557bd3d98bcd5a76b.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Bio Facility","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology, Innate Immunology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie","key":"gregerspau","last":"Gregers","name":"Gregers, Emilie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter H.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna L.J.","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"f71f56f5-4f36-4de5-a7ae-e5e51f101a83","name":"Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","name_org":"Udesen, Nanna L.J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1542-3260","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":"bankepau","last":"Banke","locid":"0d350637-c6ce-4cf8-82ba-e965da703690","name":"Banke, Ann","orcid":"0000-0002-1036-580X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie L.","key":"povlsenpau","last":"Povlsen","locid":"085efe15-36a1-434b-9b9e-b4341cd84a0d","name":"Povlsen, Amalie Ling","name_org":"Povlsen, Amalie L.","orcid":"0000-0001-6044-8841","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c1f7b9d-9e43-45ec-aa4d-310cdce6686a","name":"Larsen, Jeppe P.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","name":"Hassager, Christian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette O.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, Lisette O.","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens F.","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"2af194b2-635f-4b62-84c2-26bd7dc3263b","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","name_org":"Lassen, Jens F.","orcid":"0000-0001-7972-9192","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne B.","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, Hanne B.","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter M.H.","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"f15c1dfb-4275-4369-9b2b-2af936d2e0e6","name":"Heegaard, Peter M. H.","name_org":"Heegaard, Peter M.H.","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-4932","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob E.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Møller, Jacob E.","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38647741"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40635-024-00625-8","issn":["2197425X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Intensive Care Medicine Experimental","paperid":"39","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Intensive Care Medicine Experimental","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191053969"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7be470cb-5537-487c-809c-a5428bf8bef9","sdu-58d98f09-8d5c-4099-a4e4-7b81d162b074"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Immediate inflammatory response to mechanical circulatory support in a porcine model of severe cardiogenic shock","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-735397","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Sex- and population-specific 99th percentiles of high-sensitivity cardiac troponin (hs-cTn) are recommended in guidelines although the evidence for a clinical utility is sparse. The DANSPOT trial will investigate the clinical effect of sex- and population-specific 99th percentiles of cTn. We report the 99th percentiles derived from this trial and their dependency on kidney function. METHODS: We used samples from healthy Danish blood donors and measured hemoglobin A1c, N-terminal pro-brain natriuretic peptide and creatinine, and calculated an estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR). We compared 2 cutoffs for the eGFR of healthy participants (60 vs 90 mL/min/1.73 m2). The cTn assays investigated were Siemens Atellica and Dimension Vista hs-cTnI, Abbott hs-cTnI, and Roche hs-cTnT. RESULTS: A total of 2287 participants were sampled, of which 71 (3.1%) were excluded due to a history of heart disease (n = 4), insufficient material (n = 7), or a screening biomarker (n = 60). Of the remaining 2216 participants, 1325 (59.8%) had an eGFR ≥90 mL/min/1.73 m2. Compared to a cutoff of 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 for eGFR, using 90 mL/min/1.73 m2 resulted in lower 99th percentiles for females; Siemens Vista (46 vs 70 ng/L), Abbott (14 vs 18 ng/L), and Roche cTnT (10 vs 13 ng/L), and decreased the number of measurements above the manufacturers' 99th percentiles for all assays. CONCLUSIONS: We present reference values for 4 cTn assays for eGFR cutoffs of 60 and 90 mL/min/1.73 m2. These cutoffs differ based on the eGFR threshold for inclusion indicating that any chosen cutoff is also valuable with moderately reduced kidney function.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Jørgensen, Nicoline","Kristensen, Jonas Henrik","Strandkjær, Nina","Kock, Thilde Olivia","Lange, Theis","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Nissen, Janna","Larsen, Margit Hørup","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Bor, Mustafa Vakur","Afzal, Shoaib","Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","Dahl, Morten","Hilsted, Linda","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Bundgaard, Henning","Iversen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-769173"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex and population specific 000000000099th percentiles of troponin for myocardial infarction in the danish population danspot","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85208513468","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-769173","identifier":[{"id":"39206666","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85208513468","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bafa198c-cfe0-476e-84a7-f31b1c35561a","sdu-ceb1c493-9503-4816-bc22-2a7e45d3770b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4B689DCAD163868B7F5D003CD7B4C836"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Thrombosis (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Bo","key":"hasselbalchpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicoline","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nicoline","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jonas","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"df224b9a-32e8-4372-a238-dd877319880c","name":"Kristensen, Jonas Henrik","name_org":"Kristensen, Jonas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"strandkjærpau","last":"Strandkjær","name":"Strandkjær, Nina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thilde Olivia","key":"kockpau","last":"Kock","name":"Kock, Thilde Olivia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Theis","key":"langepau","last":"Lange","locid":"e4664578-01fc-4a93-8efd-1dbffb72cdd6","name":"Lange, Theis","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-8347","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janna","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","name":"Nissen, Janna","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Margit Hørup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Margit Hørup","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Ole Birger Vesterager","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0d43956a-6e43-42d7-8b29-4505d03ea5c8","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mustafa Vakur","key":"borpau","last":"Bor","locid":"873c3bfb-3749-45f2-b63f-f1b9e5ae29b3","name":"Bor, Mustafa Vakur","orcid":"0000-0001-7596-8401","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shoaib","key":"afzalpau","last":"Afzal","name":"Afzal, Shoaib","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia Rørbæk","key":"kamstruppau","last":"Kamstrup","name":"Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Morten","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"f5409642-33da-4a45-8f34-725572c574fb","name":"Dahl, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-6686-312X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Linda","key":"hilstedpau","last":"Hilsted","name":"Hilsted, Linda","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Henning","key":"bundgaardpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"254c7f8d-79dd-4a5d-870f-3ed78cb56464","name":"Bundgaard, Henning","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kasper Karmark","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","name_org":"Iversen, Kasper Karmark","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39206666"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/jalm/jfae088","issn":["24757241"],"issn_org":["25769456"],"issue":"6","journal":"The Journal of Applied Laboratory Medicine","pages":"901-912","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Applied Laboratory Medicine","title_org":"The journal of applied laboratory medicine","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208513468"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bafa198c-cfe0-476e-84a7-f31b1c35561a","sdu-ceb1c493-9503-4816-bc22-2a7e45d3770b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sex and Population-Specific 99th Percentiles of Troponin for Myocardial Infarction in the Danish Population (DANSPOT)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-769173","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Perioperative glycaemic control is important. However, the complexity of guidelines for perioperative diabetes management is complicated due to different and novel antihyperglycaemic medications, limited procedure-specific data and lack of data from implemented fast-track regimens which otherwise are known to reduce morbidity and glucose homeostasis disturbances. Consequently, outcome in patients with diabetes mellitus (DM) after surgery and the influence of perioperative diabetes management on postoperative recovery remains poorly understood. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: A prospective observational multicentre study involving 8 arthroplasty centres across Denmark with a documented implemented fast-track programme (median length of hospitalisation (LOS) 1 day). We will collect detailed perioperative data including preoperative haemoglobin A1c and antidiabetic treatment in 1400 unselected consecutive patients with DM undergoing hip and knee arthroplasty from September 2022 to December 2025, enrolled after consent. Follow-up duration is 90 days after surgery. The primary outcome is the proportion of patients with DM with LOS >4 days and 90-day readmission rate after fast-track total hip arthroplasty (THA), total knee arthroplasty (TKA) and unicompartmental knee arthroplasty (UKA). The secondary outcome is the association between perioperative diabetes treatment and LOS >2 days, 90-day readmission rate, other patient demographics and Comprehensive Complication Index for patients with DM after THA/TKA/UKA in a fast-track regimen. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The study will follow the principles of the Declaration of Helsinki and ICH-Good Clinical Practice guideline. Ethical approval was not necessary as this is a non-interventional observational study on current practice. The trial is registered in the Region of Southern Denmark and on ClinicalTrials.gov. The main results and all substudies of this trial will be published in peer-reviewed international medical journals. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT05613439.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Issa, Luma Mahmoud","Kehlet, Henrik","Madsbad, Sten","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Varnum, Claus","Jakobsen, Thomas","Andersen, Mikkel Rathsach","Bieder, Manuel Josef","Overgaard, Søren","Hansen, Torben Bæk","Gromov, Kirill","Jørgensen, Christoffer Calov"],"cuid":["S03-099.80-741529"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Issa, Luma Mahmoud"],"keyword":["Arthroplasty Replacement Hip","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee","Denmark","Diabetes mellitus","Glycated Hemoglobin analysis","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents therapeutic use","Length of Stay statistics numerical data","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Observational Studies as Topic","Patient Readmission statistics numerical data","Postoperative Complications","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for a prospective multicentre cohort study to address the question whether diabetes and its management is still a risk factor in fast track joint arthroplasty","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-080232","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was funded by Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF21SA0073760)."],"id":"S03-099.80-741529","identifier":[{"id":"85191367095","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38658012","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11043738","type":"pmcid"}],"ids"