Lebech","locid":"f9b459b7-e203-4824-9d80-e7c0e5b56232","name":"Lebech, Anne Mette","name_org":"Lebech, Anne-Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0943-3289","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene","key":"menspau","last":"Mens","name":"Mens, Helene","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38761191"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00415-024-12392-3","issn":["03405354","09391517"],"issn_org":["03405354"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Neurology","pages":"4972-4981","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neurology","volume":"271"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193820634"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-abe48e15-05cf-4c03-8f91-3678dd63c04c","au-ea59f9d3-64de-40ee-89d3-357f4b4bb261","ku-7548c495-e7cb-4bd8-9b92-44544167eb56","sdu-9824aaaa-71ef-4ef0-82a9-654fdc8961ad"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Validation of a risk score to differentiate autoimmune and viral encephalitis: a Nationwide Cohort Study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-094.31-755880","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"What information should and can be transparent for artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms? This article examines the socio- technical and legal perspectives of transparency in relation to algorithmic decision-making in public administration. We show how transparency in AI can be understood in light of the various technologies and the challenges one may encounter. Despite some first steps in that direction, there exists so far no mature standard for documenting AI models. From a legal perspective, this article examined the applicable freedom of information (FOI) regimes across different jurisdictions, with a particular focus on Denmark and other Scandinavian countries. Despite notable differences, our findings show that the FOI regimes generally only grant access to existing documents, and that access can be denied on the basis of the wide proprietary interests and internal documents exemptions. This is why we ultimately conclude that the European data-protection framework and the proposed EU AI Act -with their far-reaching duties to document the functioning of AI systems -provide promising new avenues for research and insights into transparency in AI.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Olsen, Henrik Palmer","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Wiesener, Cornelius","Larsen, Matthias Smed","Flügge, Asbjørn Ammitzbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732653"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithm","Transparency","freedom of information"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the right to transparency in public governance freedom of information and the use of artificial intelligence by public agencies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632753","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-732653","identifier":[{"id":"85187807869","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e1be0e65-f781-469c-911e-89e446901939"],"keyword":["Transparency","administrative decision-making","algorithm","freedom of information"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CE58E040343BE1D42B395E59CF0BD9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/388020275/The_Right_to_Transparency.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632753","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Centre of Excellence for International Courts and Governance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Palmer","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d6151186-5867-4059-bc35-8e82ae4be33e","name":"Olsen, Henrik Palmer","orcid":"0000-0001-8486-8752","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Troels","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cornelius","key":"wiesenerpau","last":"Wiesener","locid":"e51ee645-3ce8-41f9-b9a4-918882937c3f","name":"Wiesener, Cornelius","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias Smed","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Matthias Smed","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asbjørn William","key":"ammitzbøllflüggepau","last":"Ammitzbøll Flügge","locid":"5924a30c-e320-4cf0-a5a2-226f7fc8f15e","name":"Flügge, Asbjørn Ammitzbøll","name_org":"Ammitzbøll Flügge, Asbjørn William","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3632753","issn":["26390175"],"issue":"1","journal":"Digital Government: Research and Practice","paperid":"8","status":"p","title":"Digital Government: Research and Practice","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187807869"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e1be0e65-f781-469c-911e-89e446901939"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Right to Transparency in Public Governance : Freedom of Information and the Use of Artificial Intelligence by Public Agencies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732653","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Peripheral cytokine levels may serve as biomarkers for treatment response and disease monitoring in patients with multiple sclerosis (pwMS). The objectives were to assess changes in plasma biomarkers in PwMS after 14 days of fampridine treatment and to explore correlations between changes in performance measures and plasma biomarkers. We included 27 PwMS, 14 women and 13 men, aged 52.0 ± 11.6 years, with a disease duration of 17 ± 8.5 years, and an Expanded Disability Status Scale of 6 [IQR 5.0/6.5]. Gait and hand function were assessed using performance tests completed prior to fampridine and after 14 days of treatment. Venous blood was obtained, and chemiluminescence analysis conducted to assess plasma cytokines and neurodegenerative markers. All performance measures demonstrated improvements. Biomarkers showed decreased tumor necrosis factor (TNF) receptor-2 levels. Associations were found between change scores in (i) Six Spot Step Test and Interleukin (IL)-2, IL-8, and IL-17 levels; (ii) timed 25-foot walk and interferon-γ, IL-2, IL-8, TNF-α, and neurofilament light levels, and (iii) 12-Item Multiple Sclerosis Walking Scale and IL-17 levels. The associations may reflect increased MS-related inflammatory activity rather than a fampridine-induced response or that a higher level of inflammation induces a better response to fampridine.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Thorning, Maria","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Frich, Lars Henrik","Madsen, Jonna Skov","Olsen, Dorte Aalund","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733483"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thorning, Maria"],"keyword":["Cytokines","Glial fibrillary acidic protein","Inflammation","Neurofilament light chain","Performance measures","Physical activity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance measures and plasma biomarker levels in patients with multiple sclerosis after 000000000014 days of fampridine treatment an explorative study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms25031592","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was funded by the University of Southern Denmark, the Region of Southern Denmark [grant number: 17/33583, 18/51851], Lounkaer Foundation, Augustinus’ Foundation [grant number: 18-0217], the Danish Multiple Sclerosis Society [grant number: A35607], Lily Benthine Lund’s Foundation [grant number: 5652], the Society of Multiple Sclerosis Patients on Funen, the Chief Physician Committee Research Foundation [grant number: 70-A3228], and the Promotion of Medical Science Foundation [grant number: 18-L-0369]. The study sponsors have had no involvement in the study or influence on reporting the results."],"id":"S01-000.00-733483","identifier":[{"id":"38338871","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10855557","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85184735886","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-08b1e348-4493-40f1-a6a3-13e2b864f9ee"],"keyword":["cytokines","glial fibrillary acidic protein","inflammation","neurofilament light chain","performance measures","physical activity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-72B582AD0FC3AE67BDF1554739E498A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms25031592","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/256188089/ijms-25-01592-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, BRIDGE - Brain Research - Inter Disciplinary Guided Excellence (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurosurgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Neurobiology Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"thorningpau","last":"Thorning","locid":"9cc3883b-fce8-4dc5-865d-03f5cbd05795","name":"Thorning, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kate Lykke","key":"lambertsenpau","last":"Lambertsen","locid":"d867cc02-bda7-455d-8d02-8b602e35e7b3","name":"Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","orcid":"0000-0001-9276-4902","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Boye","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"34f8d097-2b28-40a1-9415-5fe706340c6d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Boye","orcid":"0000-0001-6461-3787","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"frichpau","last":"Frich","locid":"f5e4ebc5-0851-429f-ae70-b627b21b3d91","name":"Frich, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0147-4211","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonna Skov","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"084866f4-85eb-4e1f-abc1-b09397af74e2","name":"Madsen, Jonna Skov","orcid":"0000-0001-6668-4714","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Aalund","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8a3114d0-466f-4593-aa7a-270ce4e6c796","name":"Olsen, Dorte Aalund","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Hvilsted","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e1703e06-01b8-4d46-a1d1-4c4d5af99fa5","name":"Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","orcid":"0000-0002-7319-1368","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38338871"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijms25031592","issn":["14220067","16616596"],"issn_org":["14220067"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","paperid":"1592","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184735886"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-08b1e348-4493-40f1-a6a3-13e2b864f9ee"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Performance Measures and Plasma Biomarker Levels in Patients with Multiple Sclerosis after 14 Days of Fampridine Treatment : An Explorative Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733483","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: We aimed to investigate \"pain without loosening\" as an indication for knee arthroplasty revisions and to screen for other indications potentially hidden in this category to improve future registration and enhance data quality in the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register. METHODS: We included 104 patients undergoing revision knee arthroplasty for the indication \"pain without loosening\" from 1 January 2016 to 31 December 2018 at five Danish centres. Medical records, radiographs and computed tomographies were reviewed. RESULTS: In 103 of 104 cases, we confirmed \"pain without loosening\" as an indication for revision. We found hidden indications in 44 cases; malposition of components (n = 19), stiffness (n = 13), progression of arthrosis (n = 6), instability (n = 3), liner dislocation (n = 1), residual cement (n = 1) and aseptic loosening (n = 1). The Kellgren-Lawrence arthrosis grades prior to primary knee arthroplasty were 1-2 (31%) and 3-4 (69%). CONCLUSIONS: The indication \"pain without loosening\" covered patients revised due to pain, but other hidden indications were also present. Stiffness and malposition of components were hidden indications and these are not provided as indication options in the DKR and other registers. The relatively high frequency of arthrosis grade 1-2 prior to primary knee arthroplasty is concerning and may explain the occurrence of knee pain without any other pathology present. FUNDING: The Danish Rheumatism Association, the Region of Southern Denmark, the Research Fund of Region Zeeland and Region of Southern Denmark, and the University of Southern Denmark. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Not relevant.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Schrøder, Henrik Morville","Troelsen, Anders","Andersen, Mikkel Rathsach","Rasmussen, Lasse Enkebølle","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733589"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain without loosening revisions of knee arthroplasties in the danish knee arthroplasty register","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A04230242","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-733589","identifier":[{"id":"38314731","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184402976","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-24933e7c-8c56-4836-8e5c-221b93f9f4f8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14E8006AA1B38F31130CF0D065C7122C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A04230242","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/255242146/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Orthopaedics (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2