{"author_count":11,"contributors":["Kristensen, Charlotte","Crumpton, Jeri-Carol","Larsen, Lars Erik","Helstad, Bjørg Skovmand","Torp, Charlotte","Polacek, Charlotta","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Trebbien, Ramona","Skovgaard, Kerstin","Webby, Richard J.","Ryt-Hansen, Pia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828542"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-02","place":"Brisbane, au","start":"2024-09-29","title":"Options XII","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","St. Jude Children’s Research Hospital"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mind boggling influenza a virus presence in the brain of inoculated pigs and ferrets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-828542","ids":["ku-28c7d96b-97ca-4f08-96b0-fcd0e7b7bc7b"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BAD15C26BD82726B39AB9423C5B5C06D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"st jude children s research hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"St. Jude Children’s Research Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jeri-Carol","key":"crumptonpau","last":"Crumpton","name":"Crumpton, Jeri-Carol","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bjørg Skovmand","key":"helstadpau","last":"Helstad","locid":"b2cc7fdf-93a5-4a6f-88b9-d12fbae7f34e","name":"Helstad, Bjørg Skovmand","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"torppau","last":"Torp","locid":"84d3f808-1f9d-406c-96f8-76cf2fd5f408","name":"Torp, Charlotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Charlotta","key":"polacekpau","last":"Polacek","name":"Polacek, Charlotta","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Kerstin","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Kerstin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard J.","key":"webbypau","last":"Webby","name":"Webby, Richard J.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-28c7d96b-97ca-4f08-96b0-fcd0e7b7bc7b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mind-Boggling : Influenza A Virus Presence in the Brain of Inoculated Pigs and Ferrets","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828542","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Obesity rates have nearly tripled in the past 50 years, and by 2030 more than 1 billion individuals worldwide are projected to be obese. This creates a significant economic strain due to the associated non-communicable diseases. The root cause is an energy expenditure imbalance, owing to an interplay of lifestyle, environmental, and genetic factors. Obesity has a polygenic genetic architecture; however, single genetic variants with large effect size are etiological in a minority of cases. These variants allowed the discovery of novel genes and biology relevant to weight regulation and ultimately led to the development of novel specific treatments. Methods: We used a case-control approach to determine metabolic differences between individuals homozygous for a loss-of-function genetic variant in the small integral membrane protein 1 (SMIM1) and the general population, leveraging data from five cohorts. Metabolic characterization of SMIM1−/− individuals was performed using plasma biochemistry, calorimetric chamber, and DXA scan. Findings: We found that individuals homozygous for a loss-of-function genetic variant in SMIM1 gene, underlying the blood group Vel, display excess body weight, dyslipidemia, altered leptin to adiponectin ratio, increased liver enzymes, and lower thyroid hormone levels. This was accompanied by a reduction in resting energy expenditure. Conclusion: This research identified a novel genetic predisposition to being overweight or obese. It highlights the need to investigate the genetic causes of obesity to select the most appropriate treatment given the large cost disparity between them. Funding: This work was funded by the National Institute of Health Research, British Heart Foundation, and NHS Blood and Transplant.","author_count":496,"contributors":["Stefanucci, Luca","Moslemi, Camous","Tomé, Ana R.","Virtue, Samuel","Bidault, Guillaume","Gleadall, Nicholas S.","Watson, Laura P.E.","Kwa, Jing E.","Burden, Frances","Farrow