{"abstract":"Objectives: Relevant knowledge is essential for informed choices about (non)participation in population-based cancer screening. Many instruments have been proposed to assess residents' knowledge about cancer screening programmes but their measurement properties are unknown. This systematic review aims to identify and critically evaluate the measurement properties of instruments to measure knowledge about cancer screening in individuals eligible for population-based screening. Methods: A literature search was undertaken in PubMed, PsycINFO, Embase, CINAHL, Scopus and Web of Science in August 2023. The review included any study reporting one or more measurement properties of the questionnaire or sub-scale used measuring knowledge of cancer screening including breast, colorectal and/or cervical cancer screening. Studies including males aged 45 or older and females aged 20 or older were included. Two independent reviewers screened the articles and assessed the included articles using the COnsensus-based Standards for the selection of health Measurement Instruments (COSMIN). Results: We included 24 instruments, which varied in number and characteristics of items. All instruments were assessed as having an inadequate instrument development. The results of structural validity, internal consistency, criterion validity and reliability were assessed as indeterminate, while construct validity and responsiveness were assessed as sufficient. Conclusion: This systematic review identified no instruments to measure knowledge about cancer screening where the measurement properties were sufficiently evaluated. There is a lack of focus on content validity and structural validity, and further validation of the instruments is needed. The results indicate a lack of shared understanding or agreement of what constitutes relevant knowledge about cancer screening.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stokholm, Rikke Nicoline","Stenholt, Louise","Lauridsen, Henrik Hein","Edwards, Adrian","Andersen, Berit","Larsen, Mette Bach"],"cuid":["S02-095.45-741765"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stokholm, Rikke Nicoline"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cardiff University"],"keyword":["Instrument","Knowledge","Measurement properties","Population based cancer screening","Systematic review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the validity of instruments to measure knowledge in population based cancer screening targeting individuals at average risk a systematic review","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85188585073","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.45-741765","identifier":[{"id":"85188585073","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38513839","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-355ca7a3-5321-47b2-80da-0ada281f82d4","sdu-a047be24-9728-4d34-91d4-bb52d88de4bc"],"keyword":["Instrument","Knowledge","Measurement properties","Population-based cancer screening","Systematic review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BF621947C8D2A6FCBAA3373ECCE69B39"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Public Health Programs, Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Center for Muscle and Joint Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"cardiff university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Cardiff University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Nicoline","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"e67ce5c2-cf5b-467c-bb54-3e199d9b388e","name":"Stokholm, Rikke Nicoline","orcid":"0000-0001-8618-4944","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"stenholtpau","last":"Stenholt","locid":"9f5dba20-5d9d-4bad-be31-8cd65c7331f2","name":"Stenholt, Louise","orcid":"0000-0001-5995-9564","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Hein","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"f7e4b9ef-9405-42c2-9a11-7a982af019c5","name":"Lauridsen, Henrik Hein","orcid":"0000-0001-5198-5215","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","locid":"1a1d0b1a-d7c0-4f44-8d35-248f5cff407f","name":"Edwards, Adrian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Berit","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4f64dc11-e5ca-4037-bbad-8ca533d841e4","name":"Andersen, Berit","orcid":"0000-0003-4074-6504","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"40b0a541-1654-4488-a108-499a4097e34a","name":"Larsen, Mette Bach","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38513839"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ypmed.2024.107940","issn":["00917435","10960260"],"issn_org":["00917435"],"journal":"Preventive Medicine","paperid":"107940","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Preventive Medicine","volume":"182"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188585073"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-355ca7a3-5321-47b2-80da-0ada281f82d4","sdu-a047be24-9728-4d34-91d4-bb52d88de4bc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The validity of instruments to measure knowledge in population-based cancer screening targeting individuals at average risk – A systematic review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.45-741765","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: An interdisciplinary team approach to patients in specialised palliative care is recommended; however, the composition of the professionals tends to vary, and the roles of physiotherapists and occupational therapists may be underestimated. We aimed to investigate patient-reported unmet needs, which potentially could benefit from physiotherapy and occupational therapy interventions in a specialised palliative care team. Methods: Adult patients with chronic advanced diseases referred to the Specialised Palliative Care Team at Copenhagen University Hospital, Rigshospitalet were enrolled in the study. The Three-Levels-of-Needs Questionnaire was used as primary outcome to assess symptom/problem intensity, symptom/problem burden and felt needs for 12 commonly reported symptoms/problems for patients referred to a specialised palliative care team. Furthermore, participants' level of distress, fatigue and physical activity, symptoms of anxiety and depression, and barriers towards the rehabilitation programme were registered with other measures. Results: In total, 43 of 67 (64%) patients participated. The majority of participants reported severe symptoms/problems concerning fatigue (81%), impaired physical activities (77%), carrying out work and daily activities (77%), pain (72%), and worries (58%). Furthermore, need for help was expressed concerning physical activities (79%), work and daily activities (77%), fatigue (70%), pain (65%), concentration (58%) and worries (51%). On average the patients characterised 6 (out of 12) symptoms/problems as severe. Conclusion: Patients referred to a specialised palliative care team reported extensive unmet needs concerning physical activities, work and daily activities, fatigue, pain, concentration and worries. Unmet needs that potentially could be alleviated by physiotherapists or occupational therapists implemented in the interdisciplinary team.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Høgdal, Nina","Eidemak, Inge","Sjøgren, Per","Larsen, Henrik","Sørensen, Jonas","Christensen, Jan"],"cuid":["S02-099.58-742281"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Høgdal, Nina"],"keyword":["Assessment of health care needs","Palliative care","Physical Examination","Quality of Life","Rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"occupational therapy and physiotherapy interventions in palliative care a cross sectional study of patient reported needs","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85094682610","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.58-742281","identifier":[{"id":"32788277","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85094682610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-27d8dc1e-dc95-4de6-9b52-4596b9667cc6","sdu-e540e178-534e-48ea-be07-c414001bf734"],"keyword":["assessment of health care needs","palliative care","physical examination","quality of life","rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-852B826B50302ECB71401ABF7A266F39"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, REHPA - The Danish Knowledge Centre for Rehabilitation and Palliative Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"høgdalpau","last":"Høgdal","name":"Høgdal, Nina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge","key":"eidemakpau","last":"Eidemak","name":"Eidemak, Inge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Per","key":"sjøgrenpau","last":"Sjøgren","locid":"a319b935-f316-4a9c-88b7-8cabd19b1952","name":"Sjøgren, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-3822-2958","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Jonas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"81ce9de9-9bb3-4306-b94d-675238ae41b4","name":"Christensen, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-1114-7465","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32788277"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjspcare-2020-002337","issn":["2045435X","20454368"],"issn_org":["2045435X"],"issue":"e1","journal":"BMJ Supportive & Palliative Care","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Supportive & Palliative Care","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094682610"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-27d8dc1e-dc95-4de6-9b52-4596b9667cc6","sdu-e540e178-534e-48ea-be07-c414001bf734"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Occupational therapy and physiotherapy interventions in palliative care : A cross-sectional study of patient-reported needs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.58-742281","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Clonal Hematopoiesis of Indeterminate Potential (CHIP) is associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases (CVD) and is a precursor stage to the BCR-ABL negative chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPNs). These diseases are acquired stem cell neoplasms, arising due to mutations in the hematopoietic stem cell. The most prevalent is the JAK2V617F (JAK2) mutation, which potently generates reactive oxygen species (ROS), and accordingly contributes greatly to the chronic inflammatory state and the increased risk of thrombosis in MPNs. The MPNs are largely underdiagnosed blood cancers with a long pre-diagnostic phase of several years, when the elevated blood cell counts are considered reactive to smoking, blood clots, infections or chronic inflammatory diseases. Since the JAK2 mutation as CHIP-JAK2 associates with an increased risk of CVD and an increased risk of hematological and non-hematological cancers there is an urgent need to explore and validate the JAK2 mutation as a novel risk factor for CVD and to establish CHIP-clinics, which in an interdisciplinary collaboration between experts from several disciplines, and ensure timely diagnosis of the undiagnosed MPN patient and associated comorbidities. We envisage studies of the JAK2 mutation in large CVD cohorts to deliver the “Proof of Concept” for the JAK2 mutation to be implemented as a novel, highly important risk factor for CVD. These novel preventive strategies are considered to have the potential of reducing morbidity and mortality in a large population of citizens and patients, carrying the thrombosis- and CVD-promoting JAK2 mutation.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Skov, Vibe","Kjaer, Lasse","Knudsen, Trine Alma","Eickhardt-Dalbøge, Christina Schjellerup","Ellervik, Christina","Cordua, Sabrina","Sørensen, Anders Lindholm","Christensen, Sarah Friis","Kristiansen, Marie Hvelplund","Lindholt, Jes Sanddal","Thomassen, Mads","Kruse, Torben A","Bruun, Niels Eske