{"abstract":"Disease causing variants in the Ryanodine receptor 1 (RYR1) gene are a common cause for congenital myopathy and for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility. We report a 17 year old boy with congenital muscle weakness progressing to a myasthenia like myopathy with muscle weakness, fatigability, ptosis, and ophthalmoplegia. Muscle biopsy showed predominance and atrophy of type 1 fibers. Whole-exome trio sequencing revealed three variants in the RYR1-gene in the patient: c.6721C > T,p.(Arg2241*) and c.2122G > A,p.(Asp708Asn) in cis position, and the c.325C > T,p.(Arg109Trp) variant in trans. Treatment with pyridostigmine improved symptoms. This case supports that a myasthenia like phenotype is part of the phenotypic spectrum of RYR1 related disorders, and that treatment with pyridostigmine can be beneficial for patients with this phenotype.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lester, Emilie Boye","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Laulund, Lone Walentin","Illum, Niels Ove","Dunkhase-Heinl, Ulrike","Schrøder, Henrik Daa","Fagerberg, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-622370"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Fagerberg, Christina"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Humans","Male","Muscle Skeletal pathology","Mutation","Myasthenia","Ophthalmoplegia","Phenotype","Pyridostigmine Bromide therapeutic use","Ryanodine Receptor Calcium Release Channel","Ryanodine Receptor Calcium Release Channel genetics","Therapeutics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ryanodine receptor 000000000001 related myasthenia like myopathy responsive to pyridostigmine","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/223498457/RYR1_accepteret_manuskript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-622370","identifier":[{"id":"36669590","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146700095","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ab9e8c37-831f-47af-82de-1ee76c294fbe"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Humans","Male","Malignant hyperthermia","Muscle Weakness/genetics","Muscle, Skeletal/pathology","Muscular Diseases/genetics","Mutation","Myasthenia","Ophthalmoplegia","Phenotype","Pyridostigmine Bromide/therapeutic use","RYR1 congenital myopathy","Ryanodine Receptor Calcium Release Channel/genetics","Ryanodine receptor calcium release channel","Therapeutics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B1EB563985546D45E9958A066683415A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/223498457/RYR1_accepteret_manuskript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Clinical Genome Center (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie Boye","key":"lesterpau","last":"Lester","locid":"e4b22681-6907-4ebc-812c-55600a0e70ec","name":"Lester, Emilie Boye","orcid":"0000-0002-8343-3084","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Jakob","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7cfc93bc-88f4-48fa-86de-6b0147dc2825","name":"Larsen, Martin Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-4107-8771","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone Walentin","key":"laulundpau","last":"Laulund","locid":"c74cb4fd-f321-40b6-b9ba-73664a198da9","name":"Laulund, Lone Walentin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"illumpau","last":"Illum","locid":"74cadbe0-5f69-40bd-a828-83e795371f86","name":"Illum, Niels Ove","name_org":"Illum, Niels","orcid":"0000-0003-2679-2117","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrike","key":"dunkhaseheinlpau","last":"Dunkhase-Heinl","locid":"462898ec-4b19-4b5e-8c8d-e817c76b641f","name":"Dunkhase-Heinl, Ulrike","orcid":"0000-0002-3712-8871","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Daa","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","locid":"45f34f3c-9832-41b5-813a-585261681c55","name":"Schrøder, Henrik Daa","orcid":"0000-0001-7588-235X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Ringmann","key":"fagerbergpau","last":"Fagerberg","locid":"93aebc29-7681-4e3d-b613-867bd3a7eb65","name":"Fagerberg, Christina","name_org":"Fagerberg, Christina Ringmann","orcid":"0000-0002-5206-4327","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36669590"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejmg.2023.104706","issn":["17697212","18780849"],"issn_org":["17697212"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Medical Genetics","paperid":"104706","publisher":"Elsevier Masson","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Medical Genetics","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146700095"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ab9e8c37-831f-47af-82de-1ee76c294fbe"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ryanodine receptor 1 related myasthenia like myopathy responsive to pyridostigmine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-622370","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Cryogenically cooled magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) coils demonstrate extremely high Q -factors, leading to a very narrow bandwidth. This bandwidth can be increased in a controlled manner using a preamplifier decoupling. In this letter, an MRI coil design procedure is explained, and an example showing over two times bandwidth increase in a cryogenic coil for 13C isotope imaging in 3-Tesla MRI systems is demonstrated. The achieved wider bandwidth preserves the spectral components of magnetic resonance signals and makes coils less susceptive to detuning due to parasitic coupling to surrounding structures. The presented method is also useful in other applications of high- Q coils, for instance, in low-field MRI systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Wang, Wenjun","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669183"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"manipulating bandwidth of cryogenically cooled receive only mri detectors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/318550637/Sensors_Letters_J_BWvsNF_final_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-669183","identifier":[{"id":"85153330065","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-24679033-9c8d-45dd-bb5c-07c3276c4547"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2F7BF0AC11EA7A8411CE83F2B624FB50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/318550637/Sensors_Letters_J_BWvsNF_final_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical univ