en, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-8119","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"grellpau","last":"Grell","name":"Grell, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jonas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"grellpedh","last":"Grell","name":"Grell, Henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"6-18","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","status":"p","title":"Researching and Designing Walking"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-177d6692-c8e7-446b-b018-6d3226c00707"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Introduction, research questions and review","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713226","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Cystic echinococcosis is non-endemic in Denmark and primarily diagnosed in migrants from endemic areas. Here, we report a case of pulmonary cystic echinococcosis in a Danish woman with no history of longer-term stays abroad, only holiday travelling to tourist destinations. This is the first case reported in international literature from Denmark where the causative parasite was identified to species and genotype level. CASE: A 27-year-old pregnant Danish woman was admitted for examination because of haemoptysis for three months.Chest X-ray and computed tomography revealed a cystic structure in the left lung and a left-sided thoracotomy was performed to remove the cyst. Postoperative histopathological examination revealed a hyaline membrane and protoscoleces. Subsequently, infection with Echinococcus granulosus was confirmed by molecular methods. The causative agent was further characterised as E. granulosus sensu stricto G1, which is not known to have an established life cycle in Denmark. It was concluded that the infection was most likely acquired during a tourist travel to an endemic country. The patient was treated with albendazole for four weeks. CONCLUSION: This case of pulmonary cystic echinococcosis in a person who had lived in Denmark and had history of only short-term tourist travelling abroad highlights that the disease may be acquired during tourist travelling. Thus, a diagnosis of cystic echinococcosis should be considered not only in migrants from endemic countries but also in travellers upon incidental findings of a lung or liver cysts. The case also exemplifies the importance of reaching a diagnosis at species and genotype level.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Svensgaard, Siri Nana Halling","Jokelainen, Pikka","Stensvold, Christen Rune","Lausch, Karen Rokkedal","Højsgaard, Anette","Lade-Keller, Johanne","Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","Larsen, Carsten Schade"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718152"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Svensgaard, Siri Nana Halling"],"keyword":["Travel medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pulmonary cystic echinococcosis acquired during a short term tourist travel","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85164495709","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718152","identifier":[{"id":"37448378","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10336687","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85164495709","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e9a82a04-9bc0-46bd-815d-dc382d7d7523"],"keyword":["Cystic echinococcosis","Echinococcus granulosus","Pulmonary cyst","Tourist travel","Travel medicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2D442717C30A1176D8AF9127E09C920"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Siri Nana Halling","key":"svensgaardpau","last":"Svensgaard","locid":"bbbd1ef4-e20c-4