occosis acquired during a short-term tourist travel","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718152","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Biliary tract cancer (BTC) is a rare gastrointestinal cancer with a dismal prognosis. Biomarkers with clinical utility are needed. In this study, we investigated the association between survival and 89 immuno-oncology-related proteins, with the aim of identifying prognostic biomarkers for BTC. The study included patients with BTC ( n = 394) treated at three Danish hospitals. Patients were divided into four cohorts: the first-line discovery cohort ( n = 202), first-line validation cohort ( n = 118), second-line cohort ( n = 56), and surgery cohort ( n = 41). Plasma protein levels were measured using a proximity extension assay (Olink Proteomics). Twenty-seven proteins were associated with overall survival (OS) in a multivariate analysis in the discovery cohort. In the first-line validation cohort, high levels of interleukin (IL)-6, IL-15, mucin 16, hepatocyte growth factor, programmed cell death ligand 1, and placental growth factor were significantly associated with poor OS in univariate Cox regression analyses. When adjusting for performance status, location, and stage, the association was significant only for IL-6 (hazard ratio (HR) = 1.25, 95% confidence interval (CI) 1.08-1.46) and IL-15 (HR = 2.23, 95% CI 1.48-3.35). Receiver operating characteristic analyses confirmed IL-6 and IL-15 as the strongest predictors of survival. Combining several proteins into signatures further improved the ability to distinguish between patients with short (<6 months) and long survival (>18 months). The study identified several circulating proteins as prognostic biomarkers in patients, with BTC, IL-6, and IL-15 being the most promising markers. Combining proteins in a prognostic signature improved prognostic performance, but future studies are needed to determine the optimal combination and thresholds.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Christensen, Troels D","Madsen, Kasper","Maag, Emil","Larsen, Ole","Jensen, Lars Henrik","Hansen, Carsten P","Markussen, Alice","Høgdall, Dan T S","Chen, Inna M","Nielsen, Dorte","Johansen, Julia S"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-698250"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Troels D"],"keyword":["Biliary tract cancer","Cholangiocarcinoma","Gallbladder cancer","Interleukin","Survival prediction","blood protein assay"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["BioXpedia"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protein signatures and individual circulating proteins including il 000000000006 and il 000000000015 associated with prognosis in patients with biliary tract cancer","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers15041062","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-698250","identifier":[{"id":"85149136171","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36831406","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9953893","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-75980676-18ba-46a5-8f76-d9105c1575f2","sdu-a97610dd-300d-44ff-ad1a-232b165725da"],"keyword":["biliary tract cancer","blood protein assay","cholangiocarcinoma","gallbladder cancer","interleukin","prognostic multimarker panel","survival prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F9AC0B95A02844A09227C5EA633C1A8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/228599941/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/374567989/cancers_15_01062_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers15041062","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["BioXpedia"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["BioXpedia A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Lillebaelt University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels D","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Troels D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"maagpau","last":"Maag","name":"Maag, Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5b427622-91b5-4f6e-b14f-2945da9dad8c","name":"Jensen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0020-1537","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten P","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Carsten P","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Alice","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan T S","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","name":"Høgdall, Dan T S","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inna M","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Inna M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"Dorte","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Dorte","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"Julia S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36831406"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers15041062","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"4","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"1062","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149136171"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","bioxpedia a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-75980676-18ba-46a5-8f76-d9105c1575f2","sdu-a97610dd-300d-44ff-ad1a-232b165725da"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Protein Signatures and Individual Circulating Proteins, including IL-6 and IL-15, Associated with Prognosis in Patients with Biliary Tract Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-698250","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The reported hospital length of stay (LOS) following transoral robotic surgery lingual tonsillectomy (TORS-L) is variable, with limited understanding of the factors requiring hospitalization and no evidence-based criteria for discharge. AIMS/OBJECTIVES: This observational cohort study investigated factors hindering discharge following TORS-L in a well-defined postoperative care program. METHODS: Patients were included between August 2020 and October 2022. A discharge scheme was filled out twice daily, specifying the factor(s) for hospitalization among patients undergoing TORS-L. This trial was a sub-investigation of a national multicentre randomized clinical trial (RCT) testing the efficiency of high-dose dexamethasone on postoperative pain control. Participation in the RCT demanded admission to the fourth postoperative day as dexamethasone/placebo was given intravenously in repeated dosages till day 4 postoperatively. RESULTS: Eighteen patients were included in the analysis. The main factor for hospitalization was nutritional difficulties, while pain was a limiting factor for discharge only on the first postoperative 1-3 days. More than half of the patients could have potentially been discharged on postoperative day 2 when omitting the RCT treatment plan in the analysis. CONCLUSION: The study estimates that the majority of patients may be discharged on postoperative day 2 following TORS-L.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Mikkel Hjordt Holm","Channir, Hani Ibrahim","Madsen, Anne Kathrine Østergaard","Rubek, Niclas","O'Leary, Padraig","Kjærgaard, Thomas","Kehlet, Henrik","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-741696"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Dexamethasone","Hospitalization","Hospitals","Humans","Recovery","Robotic Surgical Procedures","Tonsillectomy","Transoral robotic surgery","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"why in hospital following transoral robotic lingual tonsillectomy","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85175046266","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-741696","identifier":[{"id":"85175046266","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37897327","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-173639a8-0b29-45d2-99bd-87cc5e633a3b","ku-7c92c7ce-31c3-499e-b596-0f69f0109495"],"keyword":["Dexamethasone","Hospitals","Humans","Robotic Surgical Procedures","Tonsillectomy","Transoral robotic surgery","Treatment Outcome","hospitalization","recovery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-899C35E07E068CC00E38E0E34C01A8B9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Hjordt Holm","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Mikkel Hjordt Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hani Ibrahim","key":"channirpau","last":"Channir","name":"Channir, Hani Ibrahim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kathrine Østergaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Anne Kathrine Østergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niclas","key":"rubekpau","last":"Rubek","name":"Rubek, Niclas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Padraig","key":"olearypau","last":"O’Leary","name":"O’Leary, Padraig","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"5c2179b1-a9d4-45cf-bf72-8149849d6b5a","name":"Kjærgaard, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37897327"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00016489.2023.2265983","issn":["00016489","16512251"],"issn_org":["00016489"],"issue":"9","journal":"Acta Oto-Laryngologica","pages":"796-800","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Acta Oto-Laryngologica","volume":"143"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175046266"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-173639a8-0b29-45d2-99bd-87cc5e633a3b","ku-7c92c7ce-31c3-499e-b596-0f69f0109495"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Why in hospital following transoral robotic lingual tonsillectomy?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-741696","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Introduction According to a precautionary principle, it is recommended that pregnant women and women trying to conceive abstain from alcohol consumption. In this dose–response meta-analysis, we aimed to examine the association between alcohol consumption and binge drinking and the risk of miscarriage in the first and second trimesters. Material and methods The literature search was conducted in MEDLINE, Embase and the Cochrane Library in May 2022, without any language, geographic or time limitations. Cohort or case–control studies reporting dose-specific effects adjusting for maternal age and using separate risk assessments for first- and second-trimester miscarriages were included. Study quality was assessed using the Newcastle–Ottawa Scale. This study is registered with PROSPERO, registration number CRD42020221070. Results A total of 2124 articles were identified. Five articles met the inclusion criteria. Adjusted data from 153 619 women were included in the first-trimester analysis and data from 458 154 women in the second-trimester analysis. In the first and second trimesters, the risk of miscarriage increased by 7% (odds ratio [OR] 1.07, 95% confidence interval [CI] 0.96–1.20) and 3% (OR 1.03, 95% CI 0.99–1.08) for each additional drink per week, respectively, but not to a statistically significant degree. One article regarding binge drinking and the risk of miscarriage was found, which revealed no association between the variables in either the first or second trimester (OR 0.84 [95% CI 0.62–1.14] and OR 1.04 [95% CI 0.78–1.38]). Conclusions This meta-analysis revealed no dose-dependent association between miscarriage risk and alcohol consumption, but further focused research is recommended. The research gap regarding miscarriage and binge drinking needs further investigation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Saxov, Kristina Rantzau","Strandberg-Larsen, Katrine","Pristed, Sofie Gry","Bruun, Niels Henrik","Kesmodel, Ulrik Schiøler"],"cuid":["S03-094.39-681246"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Saxov, Kristina Rantzau"],"keyword":["Alcohol consumption","Binge drinking","Miscarriage","Pregnancy","Spontaneous abortion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"maternal alcohol consumption and the risk of miscarriage in the first and second trimesters a systematic review and dose response meta analysis","src":["aau","ku","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aogs.14566","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank Conni Skrubbeltrang for supporting the extensive literature search."],"id":"S03-094.39-681246","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10333669","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37221907","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85160070496","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-66921a00-a8e9-4dbf-acc8-3e4b92c5036f","ku-5cb43520-d83a-44ee-b60b-25aafec89251","ucn-3178c28c-6f3f-4716-b7af-63b0b58b7b97"],"keyword":["alcohol consumption","binge drinking","miscarriage","pregnancy","spontaneous abortion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A9D5D60F9437ECA7621CFC1BE40E36A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aogs.14566","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/545832801/Saxov_et_al._2023_Maternal_alcohol_consumption_and_the_risk_of_miscarriage_in_the_first_and_second_trimesters.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa",