{"abstract":"Belysning af hvordan religion sætter en offentlig og politisk dagsorden i nutidens ellers så sekulariserede samfund","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christensen, Henrik Reintoft","Jacobsen, Brian Arly","Larsen, Signe Alma Engelbreth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-162367"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Kristendom","Offentlige rum","Religion","Sekularisering"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"religion i det offentlige rum et dansk perspektiv","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://nota.dk/bibliotek/bogid/656677","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-162367","ids":["au-39ea93ce-6547-4261-a791-219bb6ec956b"],"keyword":["kristendom","offentlige rum","religion","sekularisering"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6515E7DC8E2979821E882CBE7EF68A9E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of the Study of Religion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"reintoftchristensenpau","last":"Reintoft Christensen","locid":"82d3a30c-ceb9-4a89-a156-289e52129599","name":"Christensen, Henrik Reintoft","name_org":"Reintoft Christensen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-4807-4303","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian","key":"arlyjacobsenpau","last":"Arly Jacobsen","locid":"04601664-fa5f-436c-83e6-652d61ef3d03","name":"Jacobsen, Brian Arly","name_org":"Arly Jacobsen, Brian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe","key":"engelbrethlarsenpau","last":"Engelbreth Larsen","locid":"14082606-1054-4844-87ff-6f66941f6603","name":"Larsen, Signe Alma Engelbreth","name_org":"Engelbreth Larsen, Signe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19047762"],"place":"Nakskov","publisher":"Éditions Nota Bene","series":"Sociologiske Studier","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-39ea93ce-6547-4261-a791-219bb6ec956b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Religion i det offentlige rum : et dansk perspektiv","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-162367","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Molecular methods for diagnosing Lyme neuroborreliosis (LNB) have shown suboptimal diagnostic sensitivities. The objective of this study was to improve the clinical sensitivity of PCR detection of Borrelia burgdorferi sensu lato spirochetes by inoculating cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) from patients suspected of LNB directly into culture medium at the time of lumbar puncture, with this pursuing enrichment of Borrelia spirochetes before PCR analysis. Adult patients with symptoms suggestive of LNB were prospectively enrolled at two hospitals in the Region of Southern Denmark. The CSF-culture samples were incubated for at least eight weeks. During this period, culture sample aliquots were analysed for the presence of Borrelia DNA by separate PCR protocols in two independent clinical laboratories. The included patients were diagnosed with definite (n=12) or possible (n=2) LNB, and non-LNB (n=171) based on clinical and paraclinical findings. Patients in the LNB and the non-LNB group had a median duration from symptom onset to lumbar puncture of 40 days (IQR [23–90] days) and 120 days (IQR [32–365] days), respectively. Pre-enrichment growth of Borrelia spirochetes was accomplished from three patients (21 %) in the LNB group. The positive culture samples were confirmed by both the digital droplet PCR and the real-time PCR methods employed. All CSF samples were PCR negative in the non-LNB group. The results of this study do not support the use of Borrelia-specific PCR as a general routine diagnostic tool in adults. Still, they suggest it may prove of additional value in selected patients with a limited time from symptom onset to sample collection.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Leth, Trine Andreasen","Nymark, Anita","Knudtzen, Fredrikke Christie","Larsen, Sanne Løkkegaard","Skov, Marianne Nielsine","Jensen, Thøger Gorm","Bek-Thomsen, Malene","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Hovius, Joppe W.","Skarphéðinsson, Sigurður","Møller, Jens Kjølseth","Andersen, Nanna Skaarup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-643187"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Nanna Skaarup"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Borrelia burgdorferi sensu lato","Cerebrospinal fluid","Culture","Droplet digital PCR","Lyme neuroborreliosis","Real time PCR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detection of borrelia burgdorferi sensu lato dna in cerebrospinal fluid samples following pre enrichment culture","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ttbdis.2023.102138","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["JWH was supported by NorthTick, an Interreg project supported by the North Sea Programme of the European Regional Development Fund of the European Union. This work was supported by the Region of Southern Denmark (J.nr. 18/17830). TAL was supported by the Region of Southern Denmark (J.nr. 17/15139) and by the University of Southern Denmark. This work was supported by the Region of Southern Denmark (J.nr. 18/17830 ). TAL was supported by the Region of Southern Denmark (J.nr. 17/15139 ) and by the University of Southern Denmark."],"id":"S01-000.00-643187","identifier":[{"id":"85147388067","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36746091","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-f468ca59-07fa-4661-984e-0eaea14fe4e1"],"keyword":["Borrelia burgdorferi sensu lato","Cerebrospinal fluid","Culture","Droplet digital PCR","Lyme neuroborreliosis","Real-time PCR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B988483DEAE3A6886D41FF7EC7608A2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ttbdis.2023.102138","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/221070288/1_s2.0_S1877959X23000201_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Clinical Microbiology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Andreasen","key":"lethtrineandreasenpau","last":"Leth","locid":"69eae5a1-9372-4e70-8d5b-a16c1bbc4593","name":"Leth, Trine Andreasen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anita","key":"nymarkanitapau","last":"Nymark","locid":"ad551933-54bf-4baa-9ad6-8996d9fea300","name":"Nymark, Anita","orcid":"0000-0003-0575-0719","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fredrikke Christie","key":"knudtzenfredrikkechristiepau","last":"Knudtzen","locid":"7d403c4d-7658-46ab-9ea1-94da06513969","name":"Knudtzen, Fredrikke Christie","orcid":"0000-0001-8348-7819","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Løkkegaard","key":"larsensanneløkkegaardpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4fb82606-f19e-4298-8205-2530f4416a65","name":"Larsen, Sanne Løkkegaard","orcid":"0000-0003-1923-9890","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne N.","key":"skovmariannenielsinepau","last":"Skov","locid":"5b2553ab-dfde-4995-8c58-7840a16be668","name":"Skov, Marianne Nielsine","name_org":"Skov, Marianne N.","orcid":"0000-0002-2619-0864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thøger Gorm","key":"jensenthøgergormpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5ef769d5-da5b-468a-b80a-75fcc537c166","name":"Jensen, Thøger Gorm","orcid":"0000-0002-3889-0016","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"bekthomsenmalenepau","last":"Bek-Thomsen","locid":"fda1f656-d667-4c35-a0d3-3ca1afffb32f","name":"Bek-Thomsen, Malene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Boye","key":"jensenhenrikboyepau","last":"Jensen","locid":"34f8d097-2b28-40a1-9415-5fe706340c6d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Boye","orcid":"0000-0001-6461-3787","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joppe W.","key":"hoviusjoppewpau","last":"Hovius","name":"Hovius, Joppe W.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigurdur","key":"skarphéðinssonsigurðurpau","last":"Skarphédinsson","locid":"507eb211-4f50-4eda-a660-9e377be7599f","name":"Skarphéðinsson, Sigurður","name_org":"Skarphédinsson, Sigurdur","orcid":"0000-0001-8440-7040","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Kjølseth","key":"møllerjenskjølsethpau","last":"Møller","locid":"f77ab8d6-2472-488f-8251-27288d59f140","name":"Møller, Jens Kjølseth","orcid":"0000-0002-5547-5498","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Skaarup","key":"andersennannaskaaruppau","last":"Andersen","locid":"02206851-f694-4de3-8b85-23bc10a47300","name":"Andersen, Nanna Skaarup","orcid":"0000-0002-3927-9294","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36746091"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ttbdis.2023.102138","issn":["1877959X","18779603"],"issn_org":["1877959X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Ticks and Tick-borne Diseases","paperid":"102138","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ticks and Tick-borne Diseases","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147388067"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f468ca59-07fa-4661-984e-0eaea14fe4e1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Detection of Borrelia burgdorferi sensu lato DNA in cerebrospinal fluid samples following pre-enrichment culture","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-643187","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: The CREB1 gene encodes the cAMP response element binding protein 1 (CREB1), a leucine zipper transcription factor that regulates cellular gene expression in response to elevated levels of intracellular cAMP. When activated by phosphorylation, CREB1 binds to the cAMP response element (CRE) of the promoters of its target genes. CREB1 is an essential component in many physiological processes, and its function is correlated to neurodevelopment, plasticity and cell survival, and learning and memory. The NFATC2 gene codes for the nuclear factor of activated T-cells 2 protein. The NFATC2 protein is a DNA-binding protein that functions as an inducer of gene transcription during immune response. Methods and results: The aim of the present study was to examine the developmental expression of porcine CREB1 and NFACT2 transcripts. The expression of CREB1 and NFACT2 mRNA was examined by quantitative real-time RT-PCR. For the CREB1 transcript, we found significant reduction in transcript levels in the brain stem and basal ganglia during porcine embryo development, determined from day 60 to day 115 of gestation. In contrast, a significant increase in CREB1 mRNA was detected in the lungs during embryo development. No significant changes in the NFATC2 transcript were detected in porcine brain tissue during embryo development. Conclusions: Differential CREB1 mRNA expression was found in pig brain tissues during embryo development.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Knud Erik","Callesen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-668270"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Knud Erik"],"keyword":["Animals","Brain","CREB1","Cell Nucleus metabolism","Embryo","Embryonic Development","Expression","Gene Expression Regulation","Pig","RNA Messenger genetics","Swine genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developmental expression of creb000000000001 and nfatc000000000002 in pig embryos","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85159328132","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-668270","identifier":[{"id":"37171550","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85159328132","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-70f72a89-b420-47bc-af06-6d48e455aa93"],"keyword":["Animals","Brain","CREB1","Cell Nucleus/metabolism","Cyclic AMP Response Element-Binding Protein/genetics","Embryo","Embryonic Development","Expression","Gene Expression Regulation","NFATC2","Pig","RNA, Messenger/genetics","Swine/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-919D98F195C92EA877F2157C9E407E72"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Cellular Health, Intervention, and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46cd3e98-1529-45bf-9054-2978f328044c","name":"Larsen, Knud Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","locid":"7fe33188-4ec4-4b54-bc7a-c922c5ebaa54","name":"Callesen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0185-7300","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37171550"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11033-023-08501-6","issn":["03014851","15734978"],"issn_org":["03014851"],"issue":"7","journal":"Molecular Biology Reports","pages":"6265-6271","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"Molecular Biology Reports","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159328132"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70f72a89-b420-47bc-af06-6d48e455aa93"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Developmental expression of CREB1 and NFATC2 in pig embryos","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-668270","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Power transformers are one of the most costly assets in power grids. Due to increasing electricity demand and levels of distributed generation, they are more and more often loaded above their rated limits. Transformer ratings are traditionally set as static limits, set in a controlled environment with conservative margins. Through dynamic transformer rating, the rating is instead adapted to the actual working conditions of the transformers. This can help distribution system operators (DSOs) to unlock unused capacity and postpone costly grid investments. To this end, real-time information of the transformer operating conditions, and in particular of its hot-spot and oil temperature, is required. This work proposes a grey-box model that can be used for online estimation and forecasting of the transformer temperature. It relies on a limited set of non-intrusive measurements and was developed using experimental data from a DSO in Jutland, Denmark. The thermal model has proven to be able to predict the temperature of the transformers with a high accuracy and low computational time, which is particularly relevant for online applications. With a six-hour prediction horizon the mean average error was 0.4–0.6 °C. By choosing a stochastic data-driven modeling approach we can also provide prediction intervals and account for the uncertainty.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Blomgren, Emma Margareta Viktoria","D'Ettorre, Francesco","Samuelsson, O.","Banaei, Mohsen","Ebrahimy, Razgar","Rasmussen, M. E.","Nielsen, N. H.","Larsen, A. R.","Madsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669319"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Blomgren, Emma Margareta Viktoria"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Data driven modeling","Dynamic transformer rating","Grey box modeling","Thermal model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"grey box modeling for hot spot temperature prediction of oil immersed transformers in power distribution networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.segan.2023.101048","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Flexible Energy Denmark (FED) project funded by Innovation Fund Denmark under Grant No. 8090-00069B and Ebalanceplus project funded by the European Union’s Horizon 2020 under the grant agreement number of 864283 . The authors also would like to thank Claus Schack Urup for technical support and providing the data for this study. This work was supported by the Flexible Energy Denmark (FED) project funded by Innovation Fund Denmark under Grant No. 8090-00069B and Ebalanceplus project funded by the European Union's Horizon 2020 under the grant agreement number of 864283. The authors also would like to thank Claus Schack Urup for technical support and providing the data for this study."],"id":"S01-000.00-669319","identifier":[{"id":"85154554415","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7cddc724-6ea4-41df-874c-e8ecb0816e60"],"keyword":["Data-driven modeling","Distribution grid flexibility","Dynamic transformer rating","Grey-box modeling","Thermal model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1412FDC39EFF8B351781F07320D489CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/320475870/1_s2.0_S2352467723000565_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.segan.2023.101048","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"E. M.V.","key":"blomgrenpau","last":"Blomgren","locid":"08655d8a-6057-47c9-a3d6-3f70e037d85c","name":"Blomgren, Emma Margareta Viktoria","name_org":"Blomgren, E. M.V.","orcid":"0000-0002-3960-1968","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"F.","key":"dettorrepau","last":"D'Ettorre","locid":"6cde3b87-d40a-494b-ae5f-e7dda3acc08a","name":"D'Ettorre, Francesco","name_org":"D'Ettorre, F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"O.","key":"samuelssonpau","last":"Samuelsson","name":"Samuelsson, O.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"banaeipau","last":"Banaei","locid":"c71db5e8-defe-4e32-9e24-6ec8b4551791","name":"Banaei, Mohsen","name_org":"Banaei, M.","orcid":"0000-0003-4429-9422","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R.","key":"ebrahimypau","last":"Ebrahimy","locid":"359fcdf8-1d34-4992-a5a5-bbec0946f40b","name":"Ebrahimy, Razgar","name_org":"Ebrahimy, R.","orcid":"0000-0003-2279-9565","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. E.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, M. E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"N. H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, N. H.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A. R.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, A. R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"458e950b-adfd-4f2d-8d0d-ef39dee24bea","name":"Madsen, Henrik","name_org":"Madsen, H.","orcid":"0000-0003-0690-3713","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.segan.2023.101048","issn":["23524677"],"journal":"Sustainable Energy, Grids and Networks","paperid":"101048","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Sustainable Energy, Grids and Networks","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85154554415"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7cddc724-6ea4-41df-874c-e8ecb0816e60"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Grey-box modeling for hot-spot temperature prediction of oil-immersed transformers in power distribution networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669319","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To describe two cases of severe acute bilateral optic disc edema that occurred in patients with diabetes mellitus shortly after the initiation of intensified antihyperglycemic therapy. Methods: Retrospective observational case report. Case description: Two patients with type 1 diabetes presented for routine retinopathy screening with asymptomatic optic disc edema. One case was bilateral, the other unilateral. Neither patient had visual complaints. Both patients’ glycemia history was characterized by a recent bout of poor regulation and both had optic disc edema consistent with diabetic papillopathy in combination with prominent Optic disc drusen (ODD). The swelling that appeared to constitute the edematous diabetes-related component of the disease resolved within 10–12 weeks during which diabetes therapy was optimized. Visual field deficits were seen early on in both patients and had resolved to some extent in one patient after 9 months but persisted in the one affected eye in the other patient up to at least 30 months. Conclusion: Two cases of ODD-associated diabetic papillopathy were observed: One with classic, bilateral disc edema and minor visual field defects, the other with unilateral disc edema, severe visual field defects and a phenotype that resembled non-arteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy. The cases suggest that ODD may increase the risk of diabetic papillopathy, a condition that is associated with rapid glycemia reduction and crowded optic discs, which may combine to produce nerve fiber swelling and hypoperfusion with venous congestion in a compartment with limited room for expansion.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Becker, Daniel","Larsen, Michael","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Hamann, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690066"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Neuro ophthalmology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diabetic papillopathy in patients with optic disc drusen description of two different phenotypes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-690066","identifier":[{"id":"35570569","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85132612271","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-930febf2-2d1c-4cf7-a67f-76a1cf49dfea"],"keyword":["Diabetic macular edema < RETINA","NEURO OPHTHALMOLOGY","optic neuritis < NEURO OPHTHALMOLOGY","optic neuropathy < NEURO OPHTHALMOLOGY","retinal pathology / research < RETINA","techniques of retinal examination < RETINA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2F34215391ED73D4E5471918A188F1B1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel","key":"beckerpau","last":"Becker","name":"Becker, Daniel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steffen","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","locid":"4e7d48fd-1aa8-4703-94ec-8ae85794b7d7","name":"Hamann, Steffen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35570569"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/11206721221100901","issn":["11206721","17246016"],"issn_org":["11206721"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Ophthalmology","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Ophthalmology","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132612271"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-930febf2-2d1c-4cf7-a67f-76a1cf49dfea"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diabetic papillopathy in patients with optic disc drusen : Description of two different phenotypes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690066","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Data centers are to become a vital part of mobilenetworks when exploring new architectures such as cloud radioaccess network, which is seen as a more energy efficient alternative to today’s mobile network installations. However, the scaleof a data center affects its energy efficiency, with larger datacenters having more resources for energy-saving measures butat the same time different challenges than those faced by datacenters of smaller scale. Hence, this work analyzes and comparesenergy efficiency of small, medium, and large data centers, andexplores the energy minimization opportunities for cloud radioaccess network data centers. When moving processing from theradio access network to a data center to save energy in the radioaccess network, the mobile network operator does not want tomove the energy consumption from the radio access network tothe data center. Hence, energy consumption must be reduced inall segments of the network, and not moved to another segment.In the case study provided, cloud radio access network datacenters are categorized as mid-scale and small-scale dependingon the size of area they cover due to strict latency requirementsof mobile network traffic flow. Thus, even though larger DCsprove to be more energy efficient, other factors, which in thecase of mobile networks will be latency, will impact the size ofthe data center. Hence, this is a major driver to consider howenergy consumption can be minimized in small data centers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Friis, Simon","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","Ruepp, Sarah Renée"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-711734"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"keyword":["C RAN","Cloud","Data center","Energy efficiency","Green RAN"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy consumption minimization in data centers for cloud ran","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/347512293/EXTENDED_Datacenter_CR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-711734","ids":["dtu-988c751f-10d7-49cd-827e-484d8ccde419"],"keyword":["C-RAN","Cloud","Data center","Energy efficiency","Green RAN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-20C90A0A88689348373E460E14B63B38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/347512293/EXTENDED_Datacenter_CR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["TDC NET A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria Pyndt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19422644"],"issue":"3 & 4","journal":"International Journal On Advances in Networks and Services","pages":"75-89","publisher":"IARIA","status":"p","title":"International Journal On Advances in Networks and Services","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","tdc net a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-988c751f-10d7-49cd-827e-484d8ccde419"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Energy Consumption Minimization in Data Centers for Cloud-RAN","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-711734","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Jonas","White, Sofie Ann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713510"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urban walking lab","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98489214/2_The_urban_walking_lab.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713510","ids":["ruc-fe1e4234-0dc9-45f9-a5d1-59507aa325e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3868C25E687AFC92B009460C6237C879"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98489214/2_The_urban_walking_lab.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Mobility, Space, Place and Urban Studies (MOSPUS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1cb27156-b919-462a-9243-4ab2d8f87f26","name":"Larsen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-8119","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Sofie Ann","key":"whitepau","last":"White","locid":"5aa06e0f-1dc8-4faa-b628-27dbfa64a7ba","name":"White, Sofie Ann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jonas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"grellpedh","last":"Grell","name":"Grell, Henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"20-27","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","status":"p","title":"Researching and Designing Walking"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-fe1e4234-0dc9-45f9-a5d1-59507aa325e3"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Urban walking lab","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713510","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This report is the outcome of a research and development project about urban walking (funded by COWIfonden) between Roskilde University (Professor Jonas Larsen and others at the Department of People and Technology) and COWI AS. The research project started in 2019 and was finished in the first half of 2023. A central element of the project was to research the use of streets by pedestrians and implement temporary test designs. The project researched walking practices and made test cases in three Nordic cities: Copenhagen, Gothenburg and Oslo. The report will hopefully inspire urban scholars, planners and designers in understanding walking and researching, planning and designing urban streets attuned to the needs and practices of pedestrians. The authors would like to thank the administration of the three cities in Copenhagen, Gothenburg and Oslo for constructive comments on the research and especially for allowing the test designs to be implemented. Finally, the authors appreciate COWIfonden’s generous financial support and feedback during the project. Without this support, the project would not have been possible","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Jonas","Grell, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713511"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"researching and designing walking","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98481674/_Researching_and_designing_walking.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713511","ids":["ruc-fef181b4-11f9-419e-813b-4815b413f424"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F882302A2353D08E6A0CAD5A8740E45E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98481674/_Researching_and_designing_walking.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S Urban Planning and Transport"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenped","last":"Larsen","locid":"1cb27156-b919-462a-9243-4ab2d8f87f26","name":"Larsen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-8119","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"grellped","last":"Grell","name":"Grell, Henrik","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"pages":"272","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-fef181b4-11f9-419e-813b-4815b413f424"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Researching and designing walking","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713511","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We evaluated the long-term stability of thyroid peroxidase antibody (anti-TPO). In the Danish General Suburban Population Study (GESUS), serum samples were biobanked at -80 °C during 2010-2013. In a paired design with 70 subjects, we compared anti-TPO (30-198 U/mL) measured on fresh serum on Kryptor Classic in 2010-2011 (anti-TPOfresh) with anti-TPO remeasured on frozen serum (anti-TPOfrozen) on Kryptor Compact Plus in 2022. Both instruments used the same reagents and the anti-TPOn automated immunofluorescent assay, which was calibrated against the international standard NIBSC 66/387, based on the Time Resolved Amplified Cryptate Emission (TRACE) technology from BRAHMS. Values greater than 60 U/mL are regarded as positive in Denmark with this assay. Statistical comparisons included Bland-Altman, Passing-Bablok regression, and Kappa statistic. The mean follow-up time was 11.9 years (SD: 0.43). For anti-TPOfrozen vs. anti-TPOfresh, the line of equality was within the confidence interval of the absolute mean difference [5.71 (-0.32; 11.7) U/mL] and the average percentage deviation [+2.22% (-3.89%; +8.34%)]. The average percentage deviation of 2.22% did not exceed analytical variability. Passing-Bablok regression revealed both a statistically significant systematic and proportional difference: Anti-TPOfrozen=-22.6 + 1.22∗(anti-TPOfresh). Frozen samples were correctly classified as positive in 64/70 (91.4%; Kappa=71.8%). Anti-TPO serum samples in the range 30-198 U/mL were stable after 12-years of storage at -80 °C with an estimated nonsignificant average percentage deviation of +2.22%. This comparison is based on Kryptor Classic and Kryptor Compact Plus, which used identical assays, reagents, and calibrator, but for which the agreement in the range 30-198 U/mL is unclarified.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Christian Z.","Nygaard, Birte","Faber, Jens","Pedersen, Palle L.","Larsen, Morten Kranker","Kanters, Jørgen K.","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Kellogg, Mark","Ellervik, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720918"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston Children's Hospital","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Biobank","Fresh samples","Frozen samples","Serum","Stability","Thyroid peroxidase antibody"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term stability of thyroid peroxidase antibody anti tpo in serum in the danish general suburban population study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/cclm-2022-0845","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720918","identifier":[{"id":"85151889543","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36971447","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-82e153c1-ef55-475a-904c-d48d53257854"],"keyword":["anti-TPO autoantibodies","anti-thyroperoxidase autoantibody","biobank","fresh samples","frozen samples","serum","stability","thyroid peroxidase antibody"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7BEBCB761931737D4A2EBAB6DD4F5445"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375207269/10.1515_cclm_2022_0845.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/cclm-2022-0845","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nord