{"abstract":"Siliciclastic and volcaniclastic sediments in a volcanic rifted-margin succession may experience a complex diagenetic history during burial that can have a large impact on sandstone reservoir properties. To understand such changes, variations in initial sediment composition and succeeding diagenetic changes have been studied for a Paleogene outcrop analogue in the Kangerlussuaq area, East Greenland. The nature of the mafic volcanics-bearing succession, which consists of intra-volcanic sandstones, accommodated over quartz-rich pre-volcanic fluvial sandstones, are comparable to the settings of recently discovered hydrocarbon-producing sandstones in the Faroe–Shetland Basin on the conjugate Atlantic margin. Our petrographic and provenance investigations of the pre- and intra-volcanic sandstones are supported by geochemical and X-ray diffraction analyses. The intra-volcanic sandstones were deposited in shallow marine environments with mixed siliciclastic and volcaniclastic input, the latter rich in felsic to mafic volcanic rock fragments and feldspar grains. Similar zircon age distributions of pre- and intra-volcanic sandstones support a continued supply from the same siliciclastic sediment source after the onset of volcanism. Variations in initial detrital grain and pore-fluid (fresh to marine) compositions resulted in different diagenetic changes in the pre- and intra-volcanic sandstones. However, where siliciclastic sandstones were overlain by volcaniclastic rocks rather than massive lava flows, the diagenetic changes resemble those of the intra-volcanic sandstones. The cementing phases are typically quartz, illite (probably illitized kaolinite), and rare anatase in the pre-volcanic sandstones. Chlorite, calcite, zeolite/ feldspar, opal/quartz, and titanite are characteristic authigenic phases in the intra-volcanic sandstones. Precipitation of different minerals in the pre- and intra-volcanic sandstones show that the detrital composition (and to a lesser extent depositional environment) played a major role during early and late diagenesis after deep burial (up to 6–8 km). Inter-eruptive siliciclastic units may prove to form highly valuable reservoirs when they are composed of mixed siliciclastic and volcaniclastic material. In the stratigraphically youngest intra-volcanic sandstones and pre-volcanic sandstones overlain by hyaloclastite or tuff, there is a high potential for preservation of interparticle porosity during burial (, 5 km) due to early chlorite rims and the generation of secondary porosity after the dissolution of early zeolite cement.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Weibel, Rikke","Vosgerau, Henrik","Larsen, Michael","Guarnieri, Pierpaolo","Kokfelt, Thomas Find","Dideriksen, Knud","Balic Zunic, Tonci","Bell, Brian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738867"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INEOS Group (Biz)","University of Glasgow"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagenetic effect on reservoir quality of siliciclastic and volcaniclastic sandstones from a paleogene volcanic rifted margin east greenland","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-738867","identifier":[{"id":"85181119723","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2ad88e7a-ec0b-46de-81d6-1d5a2520ba91"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B469EBC728B91DCE9E9AF556D56C1DAD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"ineos group","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"INEOS Group (Biz)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"weibelpau","last":"Weibel","name":"Weibel, Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"vosgeraupau","last":"Vosgerau","name":"Vosgerau, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pierpaolo","key":"guarnieripau","last":"Guarnieri","name":"Guarnieri, Pierpaolo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Find","key":"kokfeltpau","last":"Kokfelt","name":"Kokfelt, Thomas Find","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Knud","key":"dideriksenpau","last":"Dideriksen","name":"Dideriksen, Knud","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tonci","key":"balićžunićpau","last":"Balić-Žunić","locid":"73e85088-cae0-4517-b2cf-9f339afd3c59","name":"Balic Zunic, Tonci","name_org":"Balić-Žunić, Tonci","orcid":"0000-0003-1687-1233","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Brian","key":"bellpau","last":"Bell","name":"Bell, Brian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2110/jsr.2021.127","issn":["15271404","19383681"],"issn_org":["15271404"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Sedimentary Research","pages":"895-931","status":"p","title":"Journal of Sedimentary Research","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181119723"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2ad88e7a-ec0b-46de-81d6-1d5a2520ba91"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DIAGENETIC EFFECT ON RESERVOIR QUALITY OF SILICICLASTIC AND VOLCANICLASTIC SANDSTONES FROM A PALEOGENE VOLCANIC RIFTED MARGIN, EAST GREENLAND","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738867","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A viruses are RNA viruses that cause epidemics in humans and are enzootic in the pig population globally. In 2009, pig-to-human transmission of a reassortant H1N1 virus (H1N1pdm09) caused the first influenza pandemic of the 21st century. This study investigated the infection dynamics, pathogenesis, and lesions in pigs and ferrets inoculated with natural isolates of swine-adapted, human-adapted, and \"pre-pandemic\" H1N1pdm09 viruses. Additionally, the direct-contact and aerosol transmission properties of the three H1N1pdm09 isolates were assessed in ferrets. In pigs, inoculated ferrets, and ferrets infected by direct contact with inoculated ferrets, the pre-pandemic H1N1pdm09 virus induced an intermediary viral load, caused the most severe lesions, and had the highest clinical impact. The swine-adapted H1N1pdm09 virus induced the highest viral load, caused intermediary lesions, and had the least clinical impact in pigs. The human-adapted H1N1pdm09 virus induced the highest viral load, caused the mildest lesions, and had the least clinical impact in ferrets infected by direct contact. The discrepancy between viral load and clinical impact presumably reflects the importance of viral host adaptation. Interestingly, the swine-adapted H1N1pdm09 virus was transmitted by aerosols to two-thirds of the ferrets. Further work is needed to assess the risk of human-to-human aerosol transmission of swine-adapted H1N1pdm09 viruses.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Kristensen, Charlotte","Glud, Helena Aagaard","Crumpton, Jeri-Carol","Martiny, Karen","Webb, Ashley","Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Trebbien, Ramona","Jensen, Henrik E.","Nissen, Jakob N.","Skovgaard, Kerstin","Webby, Richard J.","Larsen, Lars E."],"cuid":["S02-097.15-716210"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kristensen, Charlotte"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","St. Jude Children’s Research Hospital"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental infection of pigs and ferrets with pre pandemic human adapted and swine adapted variants of the h000000000001n000000000001pdm000000000009 influenza a virus reveals significant differences in viral dynamics and pathological manifestations","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1011838","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.15-716210","identifier":[{"id":"001124345500004","type":"wos"},{"id":"38048355","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85180010480","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10721187","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-221ac87d-3ad7-4536-aec0-298c4f88ac6b","ku-4fa8f00a-b52b-490f-aa4f-a0de70383839"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0E684A6B4320FA6865C6501FC0413500"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1011838","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379169119/journal.ppat.1011838.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376347884/journal.ppat.1011838.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Science and Biotherapeutics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Science and Biotherapeutics, Biotherapeutic Glycoengineering and Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"st jude children s research hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"St. Jude Children’s Research Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helena A.","key":"laybournpau","last":"Laybourn","locid":"8237a5ca-c866-413c-a362-165d58455ea0","name":"Glud, Helena Aagaard","name_org":"Laybourn, Helena A.","orcid":"0000-0002-0477-7584","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeri-Carol","key":"crumptonpau","last":"Crumpton","name":"Crumpton, Jeri-Carol","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"martinypau","last":"Martiny","locid":"2f168c92-c78b-43da-944e-872121b1cc06","name":"Martiny, Karen","orcid":"0000-0002-7948-1067","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashley","key":"webbpau","last":"Webb","name":"Webb, Ashley","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Jakob N.","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"cc63e367-69c4-42e9-b7ab-2f85ed6a2c33","name":"Nissen, Jakob Nybo","name_org":"Nissen, Jakob N.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kerstin","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c3c3868-b5a3-457b-8b97-9645ad03e405","name":"Skovgaard, Kerstin","orcid":"0000-0001-5663-4879","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard J.","key":"webbypau","last":"Webby","name":"Webby, Richard J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38048355"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.ppat.1011838","issn":["15537366","15537374"],"issn_org":["15537366"],"issue":"12","journal":"PLoS Pathogens","paperid":"e1011838","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLoS Pathogens","title_org":"PLOS Pathogens","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180010480"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-221ac87d-3ad7-4536-aec0-298c4f88ac6b","ku-4fa8f00a-b52b-490f-aa4f-a0de70383839"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experimental infection of pigs and ferrets with \"pre-pandemic,\" human-adapted, and swine-adapted variants of the H1N1pdm09 Influenza A virus reveals significant differences in viral dynamics and pathological manifestations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.15-716210","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Staphylococcus aureus is an uncommon cause of community-acquired bacterial meningitis. We aimed to describe patients with this disease. Methods: We evaluated clinical characteristics and outcome of adults with community-acquired S. aureus meningitis from prospective nationwide cohort studies from Denmark (2015-2020) and the Netherlands (2006-2021). Whole genome sequencing of S. aureus isolates was performed to evaluate the potential association between clonal complex and clinical characteristics. Results: We evaluated 111 episodes of community-acquired S. aureus meningitis: 65 from Denmark and 46 from the Netherlands. The median age was 66 years (interquartile range [IQR] 50-74) and 43 of 111 patients were female (39%). Concomitant infectious foci were found in 95 of 107 patients (89%), most commonly endocarditis (53 of 109 [49%]) and spondylodiscitis (43 of 109 [39%]). The triad of neck stiffness, altered mental status (Glasgow Coma Scale score <14), and fever was present in only 18 of 108 patients (17%). Surgery was performed in 14 of 33 patients (42%) with spondylodiscitis and 26 of 52 (50%) with endocarditis. A favorable outcome (Glasgow Outcome Scale score 5) occurred in 26 of 111 patients (23%), while 39 (35%) died. The most common bacterial clonal complexes (CC) were CC30 (16 [17%]), CC45 (16 [17%]), CC5 (12 [13%], and CC15 (10 [11%]); no associations between CCs and concomitant foci or outcome were found. Conclusions: Community-acquired S. aureus meningitis is a severe disease with a high case fatality rate, occurring mainly in patients with concomitant endocarditis or spondylodiscitis.","author_count":12,"contributors":["van Soest, Thijs M.","Søndermølle, Maria Birgitte","Brouwer, Matthijs C.","Chekrouni, Nora","Larsen, Anders Rhod","Petersen, Andreas","van Sorge, Nina M.","Nielsen, Henrik","van de Beek, Diederik","Bodilsen, Jacob","Bodilsen, Jacob","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-097.59-697754"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["DASGIB study group","Danish Study Group of Infections of the Brain (DASGIB)"],"corresponding_author":["Bodilsen, Jacob"],"country":["Netherlands","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","European Society of Clinical Microbiology and Infectious Diseases"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Clinical characteristics","Community acquired bacterial meningitis","Endocarditis","Female","Humans","Male","Meningitis Bacterial epidemiology","Outcome","Prospective Studies","Prospective cohort study","Staphylococcal Infections epidemiology","Staphylococcus aureus","Staphylococcus aureus genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"community acquired staphylococcus aureus meningitis in adults","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85147231884&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.59-697754","identifier":[{"id":"85147231884","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36682629","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-86d23d7e-bdd2-4aaa-a6a9-d95273b14417","sdu-eb59807b-7922-4df2-b0db-61ba112accde"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Clinical characteristics","Community-acquired bacterial meningitis","Discitis/epidemiology","Endocarditis","Female","Humans","Male","Meningitis, Bacterial/epidemiology","Outcome","Prospective Studies","Prospective cohort study","Staphylococcal Infections/epidemiology","Staphylococcus aureus","Staphylococcus aureus/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA4704B73B94EA7664774C49F8FEDBFD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"amsterdam umc","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Amsterdam UMC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"european society of clinical microbiology and infectious diseases","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"European Society of Clinical Microbiology and Infectious Diseases","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Infectious Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":6,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"},{"affno":7,"key":"dasgib study group","name":"DASGIB study group","role":"oau"},{"affno":8,"key":"danish study group of infections of the brain","name":"Danish Study Group of Infections of the Brain (DASGIB)","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thijs M.","key":"vansoestpau","last":"van Soest","name":"van Soest, Thijs M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Birgitte","key":"søndermøllepau","last":"Søndermølle","locid":"c70caf23-68c6-4275-a67d-4cf5f5b7d0ef","name":"Søndermølle, Maria Birgitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthijs C.","key":"brouwerpau","last":"Brouwer","name":"Brouwer, Matthijs C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nora","key":"chekrounipau","last":"Chekrouni","name":"Chekrouni, Nora","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Rhod","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Rhod","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Andreas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina M.","key":"vansorgepau","last":"van Sorge","name":"van Sorge, Nina M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Diederik","key":"vandebeekpau","last":"van de Beek","name":"van de Beek, Diederik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"bodilsenpau","last":"Bodilsen","locid":"260dd517-12cb-4490-b8c0-c69efb455878","name":"Bodilsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-7398-814X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"bodilsenoth","last":"Bodilsen","locid":"260dd517-12cb-4490-b8c0-c69efb455878","name":"Bodilsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-7398-814X","rank":11,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenoth","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":12,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["36682629"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jinf.2023.01.022","issn":["01634453","15322742"],"issn_org":["01634453"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Infection","pages":"239-244","publisher":"WB  Saunders Ltd","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Infection","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147231884"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-86d23d7e-bdd2-4aaa-a6a9-d95273b14417","sdu-eb59807b-7922-4df2-b0db-61ba112accde"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Community-acquired Staphylococcus aureus meningitis in adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.59-697754","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES: Epilepsy in patients with brain abscess is frequent, but risk factors and prognosis remain undetermined. This study examined risk factors of epilepsy among survivors of brain abscess and associated prognosis. METHODS: Nationwide, population-based healthcare registries were used to compute cumulative incidences and cause-specific adjusted hazard rate ratios (adj. HRRs) with 95% CIs for epilepsy among 30-day survivors of brain abscess from 1982 through 2016. Data were enriched with clinical details by medical record review of patients hospitalized from 2007 through 2016. Adjusted mortality rate ratios (adj. MRRs) were examined using epilepsy as a time-dependent variable. RESULTS: The study included 1,179 30-day survivors of brain abscess among whom 323 (27%) developed new-onset epilepsy after a median of 0.76 years (interquartile range [IQR] 0.24-2.41). At admission for brain abscess, the median age was 46 years (IQR 32-59) in patients with epilepsy compared with 52 years (IQR 33-64) in those without epilepsy. The proportion of female individuals was similar in patients with and without epilepsy (37%). Adj. HRRs for epilepsy were 2.44 (95% CI 1.89-3.15) for aspiration or excision of brain abscess, 2.37 (1.56-3.60) for alcohol abuse, 1.75 (1.27-2.40) for previous neurosurgery or head trauma, 1.62 (1.17-2.25) for stroke, and 1.55 (1.04-2.32) for age group 20-39 years. Cumulative incidences were increased in patients with alcohol abuse (52% vs 31%), aspiration or excision of brain abscess (41% vs 20%), previous neurosurgery or head trauma (41% vs 31%), and stroke (46% vs 31%). Analysis using clinical details from medical record review of patients from 2007 through 2016 demonstrated adj. HRRs of 3.70 (2.24-6.13) for seizures at admission for brain abscess and 1.80 (1.04-3.11) for frontal lobe abscess. By contrast, adj. HRR was 0.42 (0.21-0.86) for occipital lobe abscess. Using the entire registry-based cohort, patients with epilepsy had an adj. MRR of 1.26 (1.01-1.57). DISCUSSION: Important risk factors of epilepsy were seizures during admission for brain abscess, neurosurgery, alcoholism, frontal lobe abscess, and stroke. Epilepsy was associated with an increased mortality. Antiepileptic treatment may be guided by individual risk profiles, and a specialized follow-up is highlighted by an increased mortality in survivors with epilepsy.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bodilsen, Jacob","Duerlund, Lærke Storgaard","Mariager, Theis","Brandt, Christian Thomas","Wiese, Lothar","Petersen, Pelle Trier","Larsen, Lykke","Hansen, Birgitte Rønde","Omland, Lars Haukali","Tetens, Malte Mose","Jørgensen, Rasmus Langelund","Leth, Steffen","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-099.59-665825"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["Danish Study Group of Infections of the Brain (DASGIB)"],"corresponding_author":["Bodilsen, Jacob"],"keyword":["Adult","Alcoholism","Brain Abscess epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Epilepsy epidemiology","Female","Humans","Middle Aged","Prognosis","Risk Factors","Seizures","Stroke","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk factors and prognosis of epilepsy following brain abscess a nationwide population based cohort study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/WNL.0000000000206866","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.59-665825","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10103119","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85152165517","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36810235","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-6112daeb-9ab1-47e6-a192-730d7f0b866a","au-9e154419-92a1-4054-b942-2885bb2f646a","sdu-8028e0df-4bdb-43e3-be92-7bcead863720"],"keyword":["Adult","Alcoholism","Brain Abscess/epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Epilepsy/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Middle Aged","Prognosis","Risk Factors","Seizures","Stroke","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-24F89C69035D989F9481C1BD613497C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10103119/pdf/WNL-2022-201658.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/WNL.0000000000206866","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10103119/pdf/WNL-2022-201658.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Infectious Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":