CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Transformative Capacity of Public Sector Organizations in Sustainability Transitions : A Conceptualization","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669058","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The noise figure of a matching network between a receive coil and a preamplifier with low input impedance can be estimated using relationship F ≈ 1 + R11/RC. It is demonstrated how to use this relationship to choose optimal matching-decoupling network topology in terms of signal-to noise ratio (SNR). The formula serves as an efficient tool to estimate noise figure of matching networks and is useful in low-field and high-coil-Q applications, where the noise of the matching network becomes comparable to coil noise.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wang, Wenjun","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-676807"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-08","place":"Toronto, ca","start":"2023-06-03","title":"2023 ISMRM &amp; ISMRT Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Matching","RF Arrays Systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimating noise figure of matching networks for low input impedance preamplifiers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-676807","ids":["dtu-718bcac0-b7e4-4f47-be42-5ae7e5351160"],"keyword":["Matching","RF Arrays & Systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-84431E0A7BD2B1426122B58C8EF361C6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezherediapau","last":"Sanchez Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sanchez Heredia, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15246965"],"publisher":"The International Society for Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","series":"International Society for Magnetic Resonance in Medicine. Scientific Meeting and Exhibition. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2023 ISMRM","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-718bcac0-b7e4-4f47-be42-5ae7e5351160"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Estimating noise figure of matching networks for low-input-impedance preamplifiers","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-676807","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Diagnosing and treatment of diseases in pigs are important to maintain animal welfare, food safety and productivity. At the same time antimicrobial resistance is increasing, and therefore, antibiotic treatment should be reserved for individuals with a bacterial infection. The aim of the study was to investigate gross and histological lesions and related pathogens in pigs that died during the nursery period in five Danish farms. In addition, high throughput, real-time qPCR monitoring of specific porcine pathogens in fecal sock and oral fluid samples were carried out to investigate the between-farm and between-batch variation in the occurrence of pathogens. Results: Twenty-five batches of nursery pigs from five intensive, indoor herds were followed from weaning (approximately four weeks) to the end of nursery (seven to eight weeks post weaning). Gross and histological evaluation of 238 dead and 30 euthanized pigs showed the highest prevalence of lesions in the skin, respiratory system, gastrointestinal tract, and joints. Gross and histological diagnoses of lung and joint lesions agreed in 46.5% and 62.2% of selected pigs, respectively. Bacteriological detection of Escherichia coli, Streptococcus suis or Staphylococcus aureus infections in joints, lungs and livers was confirmed as genuine infection on immunohistochemical staining in 11 out of 70 tissue sections. The real-time qPCR analysis of pooled samples showed that most pathogens detected in feces and in oral fluid in general followed the same shedding patterns in consecutive batches within herds. Conclusions: Gross assessment should be supplemented with a histopathological assessment especially when diagnosing lesions in the lungs and joints. Moreover, microbiological detection of pathogens should optimally be followed up by in situ identification to confirm causality. Furthermore, routine necropsies can reveal gastric lesions that may warrant a change in management. Real-time qPCR testing of fecal sock samples and oral fluid samples may be used to monitor the infections in the individual herd and testing one batch seems to have a good predictive value for subsequent batches within a herd. Overall, optimal diagnostic protocols will provide a more substantiated prescription of antibiotics.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Barington, Kristiane","Eriksen, Esben Østergaard","Kudirkiene, Egle","Pankoke, Karen","Hartmann, Katrine Top","Hansen, Mette Sif","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","Jørgensen, Benjamin Meyer","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Olsen, John Elmerdahl","Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Larsen, Lars Erik","Pedersen, Ken Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-678941"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Herd health management","Histology","Immunohistochemistry","Microbiology","Pathology","Pigs","Real time qPCR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lesions and pathogens found in pigs that died during the nursery period in five danish farms","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-023-00319-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-678941","identifier":[{"id":"85160953154","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10234047","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37264473","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b23fdb45-9fa6-4faf-bbaa-171b053239c0"],"keyword":["Herd health management","Histology","Immunohistochemistry","Microbiology","Pathology","Pigs","Real-time qPCR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4400696ECE2C0D06FA08D3D162AF859A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/356559485/s40813_023_00319_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-023-00319-9","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristiane","key":"baringtonpau","last":"Barington","locid":"0913e657-6538-4dea-a32f-5f97b7acc33c","name":"Barington, Kristiane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Esben Østergaard","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"87d48be8-d777-425b-9366-3d7ed5cfcb59","name":"Eriksen, Esben Østergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9507-8553","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Egle","key":"kudirkienepau","last":"Kudirkiene","locid":"49238462-eac4-44c3-964c-3f16918f3782","name":"Kudirkiene, Egle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"pankokepau","last":"Pankoke","locid":"c59c44ce-f168-448f-82d3-b444274b4fee","name":"Pankoke, Karen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine Top","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"24872909-edcd-41d3-ac0e-6d89e6fef67b","name":"Hartmann, Katrine Top","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Sif","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"cf95e878-fe91-4715-b9f7-05fc972de6c6","name":"Hansen, Mette Sif","orcid":"0000-0002-8132-8475","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie Amalie","key":"blirupplumpau","last":"Blirup-Plum","locid":"54f7ba11-2529-4cf7-adb1-139dfa0e4b53","name":"Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Benjamin Meyer","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7cc4c811-2555-483d-8d2d-c6702903bc93","name":"Jørgensen, Benjamin Meyer","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e550301c-f89e-4a8b-bf34-e6fc3b76ff37","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"ed85c101-c8e6-403b-ba93-39e95e23e68d","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37264473"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40813-023-00319-9","issn":["20555660"],"journal":"Porcine Health Management","paperid":"26","status":"p","title":"Porcine Health Management","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160953154"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b23fdb45-9fa6-4faf-bbaa-171b053239c0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lesions and pathogens found in pigs that died during the nursery period in five Danish farms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-678941","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarization with the dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) technique yields > 10,000-fold signal increases for NMR-active nuclei (e.g. 13C). Hyperpolarized 13C-labeled metabolic tracer molecules thus allow real-time observations of biochemical pathways in living cellular systems without interfering background. This methodology lends itself to the direct observation of altered intracellular reaction chemistry imparted for instance by drug treatment, infections, or other diseases. A reoccurring challenge for longitudinal cell studies of mammalian cells with NMR and dDNP-NMR is maintaining cell viability in the NMR spectrometer. 3D cell culture methods are increasing in popularity because they provide a physiologically more relevant environment compared to 2D cell cultures. Based on such strategies a mobile 3D culture system was devised. The clinical drug etoposide was used to treat cancer cells (HeLa) and the resulting altered metabolism was measured using hyperpolarized [1–13C]pyruvate. We show that sustaining the cell cultivation in cell incubators and only transferring the cells to the NMR spectrometer for the few minutes required for the dDNP-NMR measurements is an attractive alternative to cell maintenance in the NMR tube. High cell viability is sustained, and experimental throughput is many doubled.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Mathiassen, Thomas Benjamin Wareham","Pedersen, Anne Egholm","Karlsson, Magnus","Katsikis, Sotirios","Wang, Ke-Chuan","Pennestri, M.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-688833"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bruker Optics Ltd"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","In cell NMR","Metabolism","Nuclear magnetic resonance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c nmr for longitudinal in cell metabolism using a mobile 000000000003d cell culture system","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmro.2023.100131","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors gratefully acknowledge funding by the Danish National Research Foundation (Grant DNRF124), European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme ERC Synergy grant HyperQ (856432) and dDNP-NMR data were acquired with equipment partially funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF 19OC0055825). The authors gratefully acknowledge funding by the Danish National Research Foundation (Grant DNRF124 ), European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme ERC Synergy grant HyperQ ( 856432 ) and dDNP-NMR data were acquired with equipment partially funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF 19OC0055825 )."],"id":"S01-000.00-688833","identifier":[{"id":"85167821088","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-50a20f35-5939-4721-95c9-dbc465516b38"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","In-Cell NMR","Longitudinal cell studies","Metabolism","Nuclear magnetic resonance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8557822AC970E578E9FEC922E2C3F40D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/335071370/articleMineAugust.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmro.2023.100131","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"bruker optics ltd","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Bruker Optics Ltd","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T. B.W.","key":"mathiassenpau","last":"Mathiassen","locid":"4290ae80-b772-49e6-8afa-17db2574f3ee","name":"Mathiassen, Thomas Benjamin Wareham","name_org":"Mathiassen, T. B.W.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A. E.","key":"høghpau","last":"Høgh","locid":"7143f532-97aa-4771-b1b5-f48c563ae208","name":"Pedersen, Anne Egholm","name_org":"Høgh, A. E.","orcid":"0000-0003-1974-0992","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","name_org":"Karlsson, M.","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"katsikispau","last":"Katsikis","locid":"67eee360-b8b8-4451-958a-ad05e1c70009","name":"Katsikis, Sotirios","name_org":"Katsikis, S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6653-1814","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K.","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"c0762931-9826-44a5-ad31-c2bc1de6b709","name":"Wang, Ke-Chuan","name_org":"Wang, K.","orcid":"0000-0001-7423-7738","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"pennestripau","last":"Pennestri","name":"Pennestri, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","cor