{"abstract":"This chapter explores how, and to what extent, our design interventions helped to create a better walking and cycling environment, where pedestrians and cyclists become more aware and attentive to each other. First, we discuss how the snow during the trial period affected the design. Second, it analyses to what degree the prints guided people’s movement and visual orientation. Third, we discuss how the interviewees evaluated the design","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713425"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"test gothenburg walking in the footprints","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98483211/6-3_Test_Gothenburg.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713425","ids":["ruc-bd3cd9d9-9b9f-4b09-bcf6-c2678d841fe1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EE45E792DA3AE77F3C0C9F3C5A05A7F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98483211/6-3_Test_Gothenburg.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Mobility, Space, Place and Urban Studies (MOSPUS)","Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business, Centre for Tourism Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":