{"abstract":"Antibiotics are widely used in pig farming across the world which has led to concerns about the potential impact on human health through the selection of antibiotic resistant pathogenic bacteria. This worry has resulted in the development of a production scheme known as pigs Raised Without Antibiotics (RWA), in which pigs are produced in commercial farms, but are ear-tagged as RWA until slaughter unless they receive treatment, thus allowing the farmer to sell the pigs either as premium priced RWA or as conventional meat. Development of antibiotic resistance in pig farming has been studied in national surveys of antibiotic usage and resistance, as well as in experimental studies of groups of pigs, but not in individual pigs followed longitudinally in a commercial pig farm. In this study, a cohort of RWA designated pigs were sampled at 10 time points from birth until slaughter along with pen-mates treated with antibiotics at the same farm. From these samples, the microbiome, determined using 16S sequencing, and the resistome, as determined using qPCR for 82 resistance genes, was investigated, allowing us to examine the difference between RWA pigs and antibiotic treated pigs. We furthermore included 176 additional pigs from six different RWA farms which were sampled at the slaughterhouse as an endpoint to substantiate the cohort as well as for evaluation of intra-farm variability. The results showed a clear effect of age in both the microbiome and resistome composition from early life up until slaughter. As a function of antibiotic treatment, however, we observed a small but significant divergence between treated and untreated animals in their microbiome composition immediately following treatment, which disappeared before 8 weeks of age. The effect on the resistome was evident and an effect of treatment could still be detected at week 8. In animals sampled at the slaughterhouse, we observed no difference in the microbiome or the resistome as a result of treatment status but did see a strong effect of farm origin. Network analysis of co-occurrence of microbiome and resistome data suggested that some resistance genes may be transferred through mobile genetic elements, so we used Hi-C metagenomics on a subset of samples to investigate this. We conclude that antibiotic treatment has a differential effect on the microbiome vs. the resistome and that although resistance gene load is increased by antibiotic treatment load, this effect disappears before slaughter. More studies are needed to elucidate the optimal way to rear pigs without antibiotics.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Tams, Katrine Wegener","Larsen, Inge","Hansen, Julie Elvekjær","Spiegelhauer, Henrik","Strøm-Hansen, Alexander Damm","Rasmussen, Sophia","Ingham, Anna Cäcilia","Kalmar, Lajos","Kean, Iain Robert Louis","Angen, Øystein","Holmes, Mark A.","Pedersen, Karl","Jelsbak, Lars","Folkesson, Anders","Larsen, Anders Rhod","Strube, Mikael Lenz"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-686157"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Strube, Mikael Lenz"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Veterinary Institute","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Antibiotic resistance","Metagenomes","Microbiome","Pig farming"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of antibiotic use on the dynamics of the microbiome and resistome in pigs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s42523-023-00258-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-686157","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10440943","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37605221","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85168482114","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cd5f7b11-1657-429d-8a9d-49eb890c3b86","ku-e3ad09b0-1d24-419d-b1e8-50c830826254"],"keyword":["Antibiotic resistance","Metagenomes","Microbiome","Pig farming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-181AD6F4D0B241D10A377F0F7E2C0542"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333146822/s42523_023_00258_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/365824108/s42523_023_00258_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s42523-023-00258-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"national veterinary institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"National Veterinary Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrine Wegener","key":"tamskatrinewegenerpau","last":"Tams","locid":"114e5a13-63a1-438b-9eed-4773937f6b88","name":"Tams, Katrine Wegener","orcid":"0000-0002-8154-6122","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inge","key":"larseningepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"82b09bf9-73d5-4c71-a3c1-01e66b0e9ebe","name":"Larsen, Inge","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-2241","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Julie Elvekjær","key":"hansenjulieelvekjærpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a3e8500a-d9ad-4e89-83d4-3f434670b56f","name":"Hansen, Julie Elvekjær","orcid":"0000-0003-3885-8929","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"spiegelhauerhenrikpau","last":"Spiegelhauer","name":"Spiegelhauer, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Damm","key":"strømhansenalexanderdammpau","last":"Strøm-Hansen","name":"Strøm-Hansen, Alexander Damm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sophia","key":"rasmussensophiapau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ef51a5ef-7b63-460d-bc2b-2d98fd069f3f","name":"Rasmussen, Sophia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Cäcilia","key":"inghamannacäciliapau","last":"Ingham","name":"Ingham, Anna Cäcilia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lajos","key":"kalmarlajospau","last":"Kalmar","name":"Kalmar, Lajos","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Iain Robert Louis","key":"keaniainrobertlouispau","last":"Kean","name":"Kean, Iain Robert Louis","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Øystein","key":"angenøysteinpau","last":"Angen","name":"Angen, Øystein","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark A.","key":"holmesmarkapau","last":"Holmes","name":"Holmes, Mark A.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"pedersenkarlpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Karl","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"jelsbaklarspau","last":"Jelsbak","locid":"0f152051-d6ff-4b86-b98f-2ce118ee9ee1","name":"Jelsbak, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-5759-9769","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"folkessonanderspau","last":"Folkesson","locid":"5a1c007c-1a52-43ec-93c5-b41be27e2e58","name":"Folkesson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-2175-830X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Rhod","key":"larsenandersrhodpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Rhod","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael Lenz","key":"strubemikaellenzpau","last":"Strube","locid":"483fbd14-adb8-4df6-b879-bcbb35737f51","name":"Strube, Mikael Lenz","orcid":"0000-0003-0905-5705","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37605221"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s42523-023-00258-4","issn":["25244671"],"journal":"Animal Microbiome","paperid":"39","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Animal Microbiome","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168482114"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cd5f7b11-1657-429d-8a9d-49eb890c3b86","ku-e3ad09b0-1d24-419d-b1e8-50c830826254"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of antibiotic use on the dynamics of the microbiome and resistome in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-686157","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: It is unknown if patients are relieved of pain after knee arthroplasty revision for unexplained pain. The aim of this cross-sectional case-control study was to compare patient-reported outcome measures (PROMs) and satisfaction 1 to 3 years after revision of total knee arthroplasties (TKAs) for the indications of unexplained pain versus aseptic loosening. METHODS: We included 384 patients undergoing TKA revision for the indications of unexplained pain and aseptic loosening from January 1, 2018 to December 31, 2020 from the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register. A total of 81 patients were revised for unexplained pain and 303 for aseptic loosening. Questionnaires including PROMs (Oxford Knee Score, EQ-5D-5L, and Forgotten Joint Score) and satisfaction with the surgery on a 0-100 scale (100 = not satisfied; 0 = very satisfied) were sent to digitally secured mailboxes. Time from revision to data collection was a median 3.1 years (range, 1.4-4.4 years). RESULTS: Median Oxford Knee Score was 25 (interquartile range [IQR] 15) versus 31 (IQR 18) 1-3 years after revisions for unexplained pain versus aseptic loosening, P = .009. Median EQ-5D-5L was 0.6 (IQR 0.4) versus 0.8 (IQR 0.3) for unexplained pain versus aseptic loosening, P = .009. Median Forgotten Joint Score was 50 (IQR 7) versus 50 (IQR 16) for unexplained pain versus aseptic loosening, P = .905. Satisfaction was 75 (IQR 38) for unexplained pain and 50 (IQR 73) for aseptic loosening, P < .001. CONCLUSION: Patients undergoing TKA revision for the indication of unexplained pain had worse results on PROMs than those revised for aseptic loosening. Likewise, patients revised for unexplained pain were less satisfied compared to patients revised for aseptic loosening. This information is valuable to both surgeons and patients when candidates for revision surgery are selected, to obtain the best possible outcomes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Schrøder, Henrik Morville","Troelsen, Anders","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-692291"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup"],"keyword":["Arthroplasty Replacement Knee methods","Case Control Studies","Cross Sectional Studies","Humans","Knee Joint surgery","Knee Prosthesis adverse effects","Pain","Pain surgery","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Patient Satisfaction","Prosthesis Failure","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Revision","Revision knee arthroplasty","Surveys and Questionnaires","Total knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcomes and satisfaction 000000000001 to 000000000003 years after revisions of total knee arthroplasties for unexplained pain versus aseptic loosening","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2022.10.019","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-692291","identifier":[{"id":"85147010390","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36257505","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-92edcbd9-5922-4586-b994-e4259b1469f3","sdu-6bde409a-c7a0-4da7-8bad-59498af82083"],"keyword":["Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/methods","Case-Control Studies","Cross-Sectional Studies","Humans","Knee Joint/surgery","Knee Prosthesis/adverse effects","Pain/surgery","Patient Satisfaction","Prosthesis Failure","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Surveys and Questionnaires","pain","patient-reported outcome measures","revision","revision knee arthroplasty","total knee arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-58E2BB033F970042BBC41785948C9387"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/221499242/1_s2.0_S0883540322009391_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/369084540/1_s2.0_S0883540322009391_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2022.10.019","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Bollerup","key":"arndtpau","last":"Arndt","locid":"a2513ef2-9214-48ee-b84f-bea6ef1717ac","name":"Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","orcid":"0000-0001-8258-7922","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Morville","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","name":"Schrøder, Henrik Morville","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Anders","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"49cb6bcf-2ff6-41af-a356-a2a09c2ce7ba","name":"Troelsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0132-8182","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36257505"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.arth.2022.10.019","issn":["08835403","15328406"],"issn_org":["08835403"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Arthroplasty","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Arthroplasty","title_org":"The Journal of Arthroplasty","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147010390"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-92edcbd9-5922-4586-b994-e4259b1469f3","sdu-6bde409a-c7a0-4da7-8bad-59498af82083"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patient-Reported Outcomes and Satisfaction 1 to 3 Years After Revisions of Total Knee Arthroplasties for Unexplained Pain Versus Aseptic Loosening","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-692291","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: A characteristic of the retinal circulation is that arterial occlusion is embolic or secondary to vasculitis but rarely or never due to in situ atherosclerosis. Therefore, retinal artery occlusion suggests the presence of cardiac or large-vessel disease outside the eye. This cohort study examined the general risk of macrovascular disease in individuals with diabetes, with or without retinal artery occlusion. Methods: We retrieved data on 992 subjects with incident retinal artery occlusion and preexisting diabetes, registered in Denmark between January 1, 2000, and December 31, 2018. Each retinal artery occlusion subject was matched for age, sex, and diabetes duration, with 5 control subjects with diabetes but without retinal artery occlusion. We performed survival analyses to compare the risk of extraocular macrovascular disease between the 2 groups in a 5-year follow-up. Results: After 1 year, the incidence of macrovascular disease in subjects with retinal artery occlusion was approximately 21 per 100 person-years (95% confidence interval [CI]: 18.11-24.29), compared to 6.25 per 100 patient-years (95% CI: 5.57-7.00) in those without retinal artery occlusion. After 5 years, the cumulative incidences of macrovascular disease were 51.2% (95% CI: 47.9-54.7%) and 29.4% (95% CI: 28.0-30.8%) in patients with diabetes with or without retinal artery occlusion, respectively. Hazard rate ratios were 3.36 (95% CI: 2.79-4.05) after 1 year and 2.27 (95% CI: 2.04-2.53) after 5 years. Conclusion: Among individuals with diabetes, those diagnosed with retinal artery occlusion had a higher general risk of macrovascular complications for at least 5 years after the occlusion event compared with those without retinal artery occlusion.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ørskov, Marie","Vorum, Henrik","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Larsen, Michael","Skjøth, Flemming"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-697803"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ørskov, Marie"],"keyword":["Diabetic complications","Macrovascular complications","Major adverse cardiovascular event","Retinal artery occlusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"retinal artery occlusion as an early indicator of macrovascular complications in diabetes","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85146350197&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-697803","identifier":[{"id":"85146350197","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36170938","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-c1030f5a-4355-4373-bd31-f0df49d9f795","ku-210f7cac-83ec-4019-8c07-274040d9a32b"],"keyword":["Diabetic complications","Macrovascular complications","Major adverse cardiovascular event","Retinal artery occlusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-67B70A5981D53F0EA2511800C6EE6A2B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"aff