"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0c20cef2-6880-4ee2-af4e-21a29ec855bc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Blinded interpretation for the primary and secondary outcomes for the primary endpoint for the NEPNEP trial","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-686437","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Recently, in-feed medicinal zinc has been phased out in pig production in the European Union. This makes updated knowledge about porcine post-weaning diarrhea (PWD) crucial. The objectives of the present study were to investigate (i) the clinical presentation of PWD in pigs housed in Danish herds that did not use medicinal zinc, specifically the prevalence of diarrhea and whether PWD was associated to clinical signs of dehydration or altered body temperature; (ii) which microorganism are associated to PWD; and iii) whether measurements of the fecal pH have a potential to be used diagnostically to differentiate between infectious etiologies in cases of PWD. Results: The prevalence of diarrhea varied considerably between the outbreaks in the nine studied herds (median = 0.58, range = 0.10; 0.94). In a cross-sectional design (n = 923), diarrhea was associated with reduced rectal temperature and alkaline feces. Diarrhea was also associated with observably reduced skin elasticity, possibly indicating dehydration. In both diarrheic case pigs (n = 87) and control pigs (n = 86), the presence of Brachyspira pilosicoli, Clostridium perfringens, Cryptosporidium spp., Cystoisopora suis, enterotoxigenic Escherichia coli, Lawsonia intracellularis, porcine circovirus types 2 and 3, rotavirus A, B, C, and H, Samonella enterica spp. enterica, and Trichuris suis was described. PWD was associated with high levels of enterotoxigenic E. coli shedding (odds ratio versus no E. coli detection = 4.79 [CI 1.14; 12.62]). Diarrhea was associated with high levels of rotavirus A shedding (odds ratio versus no/low rotavirus A = 3.80 [CI 1.33; 7.97]). The association between microbiological findings in diarrheic pigs and fecal pH was negligible. Conclusions: Enterotoxigenic E. coli was confirmed to be a cause of PWD; however, cases of PWD where enterotoxigenic E. coli was not detected in high levels occurred commonly, and this adds to the increasing evidence suggesting that PWD is not necessarily a result of enteric colibacillosis. Rotaviral enteritis might be a differential diagnosis of PWD. pH-measurements cannot be used to differentiate between differential diagnoses for PWD.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Eriksen, Esben Østergaard","Kudirkiene, Egle","Barington, Kristiane","Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Olsen, John Elmerdahl","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Pankoke, Karen","Larsen, Lars Erik","Liu, Gang","Pedersen, Ken Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690515"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Enterotoxigenic Escherichia coli","Pig","Post weaning diarrhoea","Rectal temperature","Rotavirus","pH"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an observational field study of porcine post weaning diarrhea clinical and microbiological findings and fecal ph measurements as a potential diagnostic tool","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-023-00325-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-690515","identifier":[{"id":"85153745673","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37434248","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10334583","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-e08fec70-9d53-411c-97e6-dbd175fac175"],"keyword":["Enterotoxigenic Escherichia coli","Pig","Post-weaning diarrhoea","Rectal temperature","Rotavirus","pH"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30FA8F0D8E78D03903C4405C51EE285E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/362699276/s40813_023_00325_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-023-00325-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Esben Østergaard","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"87d48be8-d777-425b-9366-3d7ed5cfcb59","name":"Eriksen, Esben Østergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9507-8553","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Egle","key":"kudirkienepau","last":"Kudirkiene","locid":"49238462-eac4-44c3-964c-3f16918f3782","name":"Kudirkiene, Egle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristiane","key":"baringtonpau","last":"Barington","locid":"0913e657-6538-4dea-a32f-5f97b7acc33c","name":"Barington, Kristiane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"ed85c101-c8e6-403b-ba93-39e95e23e68d","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie Amalie","key":"blirupplumpau","last":"Blirup-Plum","locid":"54f7ba11-2529-4cf7-adb1-139dfa0e4b53","name":"Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e550301c-f89e-4a8b-bf34-e6fc3b76ff37","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"pankokepau","last":"Pankoke","locid":"c59c44ce-f168-448f-82d3-b444274b4fee","name":"Pankoke, Karen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gang","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"4c43b23c-8aab-4f5b-a9f5-ca65baa6a752","name":"Liu, Gang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37434248"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40813-023-00325-x","issn":["20555660"],"journal":"Porcine Health Management","paperid":"33","status":"p","title":"Porcine Health Management","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153745673"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e08fec70-9d53-411c-97e6-dbd175fac175"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An observational field study of porcine post-weaning diarrhea : clinical and microbiological findings, and fecal pH-measurements as a potential diagnostic tool","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690515","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"I november 2021 afholdt Miljøstyrelsen i samarbejde med DCE – Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, konsensuskonference om vurdering af ikke-hjemmehørende arter i Danmark og deres påvirkning på natur, miljø, økonomi og human sundhed. Nærværende rapport opsummerer det forudgående arbejde med revision af skala og protokol for vurderingen af påvirkningerne, de efterfølgende ekspertvurderinger, samt arbejdet med at skabe konsensus omkring vurderingerne under og efter konsensuskonferencen. Herefter er listerne med vurderinger af ikke-hjemmehørende arter og Horizon-scan arter revideret (Bilag 1 og 2). Desuden er kriteriet, for hvornår en art betragtes som invasiv, revideret. Baseret på konsensusvurderingerne og det reviderede kriterium anses 77 af de 2513 ikke-hjemmehørende arter, der forekommer i Danmark, for at være invasive. Fakta-ark for alle invasive arter er evideret og desuden er udarbejdet fakta-ark for 10 udvalgte Horizon-scan arter. De reviderede fakta-ark findes på Miljøstyrelsens hjemmeside www.mst.dk.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Strandberg, Beate","Andersen, Per","Bruhn, Annette","Buur, Helle","Carl, Henrik","Elmeros, Morten","Fox, Anthony David","Holmstrup, Martin","Kjær, Christian","Kristensen, Hans Viborg","Slotsbo, Stine","Strandberg, Morten Tune","Wiberg-Larsen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-693603"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Naturhistorisk Museum"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"konsensus omkring vurdering af ikke hjemmehørende arter i danmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dce.au.dk/fileadmin/dce.au.dk/Udgivelser/Tekniske_rapporter_250-299/TR271.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-693603","ids":["au-4d88b527-67bd-45c1-b88a-7c3651f5026a"],"keyword":["Ikke-hjemmehørende arter, invasive arter, Danmark, påvirkning på natur, miljø, økonomi og human sundhed"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8D9BCA4A442C225F10591AACC29A9993"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dce.au.dk/fileadmin/dce.au.dk/Udgivelser/Tekniske_rapporter_250-299/TR271.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Statens Naturhistoriske Museum","University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Naturhistorisk Museum"],"nora_code":"DI-OT"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Beate","key":"strandbergbeatepau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"3248f223-fd84-4bdf-a4d3-e823b6b35144","name":"Strandberg, Beate","orcid":"0000-0003-3862-0291","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"andersenperpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"41429ad7-0d97-43aa-aff6-4d466504d665","name":"Andersen, Per","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"bruhnannettepau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"buurhellepau","last":"Buur","locid":"e99df072-1a1e-4f65-9204-18e7f410f286","name":"Buur, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-0828-8374","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"carlhenrikpau","last":"Carl","name":"Carl, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"elmerosmortenpau","last":"Elmeros","locid":"abe67bcb-8575-41d5-b19c-a9edeaedc7b2","name":"Elmeros, Morten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anthony David","key":"foxanthonydavidpau","last":"Fox","locid":"deb15e30-223d-4759-b62b-1df46dcf0d62","name":"Fox, Anthony David","orcid":"0000-0001-8083-7633","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"holmstrupmartinpau","last":"Holmstrup","locid":"e4400a27-9cdc-4b58-a6eb-2868da82f13f","name":"Holmstrup, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8395-6582","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"kjærchristianpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"4417d2d4-6fae-498c-80ee-eeb09c3323ec","name":"Kjær, Christian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Viborg","key":"kristensenhansviborgpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Hans Viborg","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine","key":"slotsbostinepau","last":"Slotsbo","locid":"0cb3bf6d-8fbb-48f1-91a3-52bbc1572a7a","name":"Slotsbo, Stine","orcid":"0000-0001-9974-0014","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Tune","key":"strandbergmortentunepau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"1408a1c4-4357-441c-9f3b-1e823aa69880","name":"Strandberg, Morten Tune","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-2350","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"wiberglarsenpeterpau","last":"Wiberg-Larsen","locid":"71daa3aa-f70d-4a8f-b202-a881d8e0d12c","name":"Wiberg-Larsen, Peter","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771567687"],"issn":["2244999X"],"issue":"217","pages":"48","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Teknisk rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 217","series":"Teknisk rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4d88b527-67bd-45c1-b88a-7c3651f5026a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Konsensus omkring vurdering af ikke-hjemmehørende arter i Danmark","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-693603","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims/hypothesis: These secondary analyses aimed to investigate the effects of different volumes of exercise in adjunct to diet-induced weight loss and standard care on advanced glycation end-products (AGEs) and receptor for AGE (RAGE). We hypothesized that exercise in adjunct to a diet-induced weight loss would dose-dependently increase the soluble decoy receptor for AGE (sRAGE) more than diet-induced weight loss and standard care alone. Secondarily, we expected changes in sRAGE to be associated with improved glycaemic control and inversely associated with low-grade inflammation. Methods: The DOSE-EX study was a 16-week parallel-group, 4-arm, single-centre, assessor-blinded, randomised, controlled trial (NCT03769883). We included persons living with T2D, duration ≤7 years, BMI >27 kg/m2 and <40 kg/m2, without severe diabetic complications. Participants were randomised (1:1:1:1) to either 1) standard care as control (CON), 2) standard care + diet (DCON), 3) standard care + diet + moderate exercise dose (MED) or 4) standard care + diet + high exercise dose (HED). Standard care included algorithm-guided pharmacological treatment. The diet intervention aimed at 25% reduced energy intake. The supervised exercise sessions included two aerobic sessions + one combined (aerobic and resistance training) session per week for the MED group, and four aerobic sessions + two combined sessions per week for the HED group. Primary outcome was the change in sRAGE from baseline to 16-week follow-up. Secondary outcomes encompassed changes in advanced glycation endproducts (AGE), glycaemic control and markers of low-grade inflammation. Results: A total of 80 participants (CON: n = 20, DCON: n = 19, MED: n = 20, HED: n = 21) were included in this secondary analysis. The mean age was 58.3 years (SD 9.9), 53% males, and median T2D duration was 4.1 years (IQR 2.0–5.5). No change in sRAGE was observed in any of the groups from baseline to follow-up (p > 0.05). Conclusion/interpretation: A 16-week intervention with either three or six exercise sessions per week in adjunct to diet-induced weight loss did not change the levels of sRAGE in persons living with well-regulated, short standing T2D.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Legaard, Grit Elster","Lyngbaek, Mark Preben Printz","Almdal, Thomas","Durrer, Cody Garett","Nystrup, Ulrikke","Larsen, Emil List","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Karstoft, Kristian","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Ried-Larsen, Mathias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719443"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of different doses of exercise in adjunct to diet induced weight loss on the age rage axis in patients with short standing type 000000000002 diabetes secondary analysis of the dose ex multi arm parallel group randomised trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-719443","identifier":[{"id":"85166630321","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37532066","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1aacdb21-6020-433b-80cc-1eea6583621b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25E440A913A9A29474E2DCB7E41097AA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Grit Elster","key":"legaardpau","last":"Legaard","name":"Legaard, Grit Elster","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mark Preben Printz","key":"lyngbaekpau","last":"Lyngbaek","name":"Lyngbaek, Mark Preben Printz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thomas Peter","key":"almdalpau","last":"Almdal","locid":"cae595b0-e059-48f9-b1e4-153595fd7455","name":"Almdal, Thomas","name_org":"Almdal, Thomas Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cody Garett","key":"durrerpau","last":"Durrer","name":"Durrer, Cody Garett","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrikke","key":"nystruppau","last":"Nystrup","name":"Nystrup, Ulrikke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Henrik Enghusen","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kristian","key":"karstoftpau","last":"Karstoft","locid":"80f306e9-a560-493c-b7d4-4e18b694660f","name":"Karstoft, Kristian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Bente Klarlund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5d38d54e-e0d1-4397-98ca-6d8c9b78606d","name":"Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias","key":"riedlarsenpau","last":"Ried-Larsen","name":"Ried-Larsen, Mathias","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37532066"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2023.07.031","issn":["08915849","18734596"],"issn_org":["08915849"],"journal":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","pages":"52-61","status":"p","title":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","volume":"208"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166630321"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1aacdb21-6020-433b-80cc-1eea6583621b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of different doses of exercise in adjunct to diet-induced weight loss on the AGE-RAGE axis in patients with short standing type 2 diabetes : Secondary analysis of the DOSE-EX multi-arm, parallel-group, randomised trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719443","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A virus (IAV) is an RNA virus that causes respiratory disease in a wide range of mammals including humans and pigs. Cav1.2 is a specific voltage-dependent calcium channel (VDCC) important for the internalization of IAV and VDCC inhibitors can decrease IAV disease severity in mice. In this paper, the distribution pattern of a range of VDCCs by immunohistochemistry and Cav1.2 by in situ hybridization in the porcine respiratory tract is documented for the first time. Furthermore, we showed co-localization of VDCC-positive and IAV-positive cells in experimentally infected pigs. These findings provide new perspectives on the IAV internalization process and pave the way for further research investigating the effect of VDDC inhibitors on the IAV infection dynamics in pigs, which could have relevance to humans too.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kristensen, Charlotte","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Trebbien, Ramona","Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-722171"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co localization of influenza a virus and voltage dependent calcium channels provides new perspectives on the internalization process in pigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44298-023-00009-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-722171","ids":["ku-e256088e-793e-42b9-9f35-70f0ebef52b4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C01998E44BA9254E0745448BDF72F72B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381842438/Co_localization_of_influenza_A_virus_and_voltage_dependent_calcium_channels_provides_new_perspectives_on_the_internalization_process_in_pigs.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44298-023-00009-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s44298-023-00009-x","issn":["29481767"],"journal":"npj Viruses","paperid":"8","status":"p","title":"npj Viruses","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e256088e-793e-42b9-9f35-70f0ebef52b4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-localization of influenza A virus and voltage-dependent calcium channels provides new perspectives on the internalization process in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722171","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Barents Sea is one of the Polar regions where current climate and ecosystem change is most pronounced. Here we review the current state of knowledge of the physical, chemical and biological systems in the Barents Sea. Physical conditions in this area are characterized by large seasonal contrasts between partial sea-ice cover in winter and spring versus predominantly open water in summer and autumn. Observations over recent decades show that surface air and ocean temperatures have increased, sea-ice extent has decreased, ocean stratification has weakened, and water chemistry and ecosystem components have changed, the latter in a direction often described as “Atlantification” or “borealisation,” with a less “Arctic” appearance. Temporal and spatial changes in the Barents Sea have a wider relevance, both in the context of large-scale climatic (air, water mass and sea-ice) transport processes and in comparison to other Arctic regions. These observed changes also have socioeconomic consequences, including for fisheries and other human activities. While several of the ongoing changes are monitored and quantified, observation and knowledge gaps remain, especially for winter months when field observations and sample collections are still sparse. Knowledge of the interplay of physical and biogeochemical drivers and ecosystem responses, including complex feedback processes, needs further development.","author_count":41,"contributors":["Gerland, Sebastian","Ingvaldsen, Randi B.","Reigstad, Marit","Sundfjord, Arild","Bogstad, Bjarte","Chierici, Melissa","Hop, Haakon","Renaud, Paul E.","Smedsrud, Lars Henrik","Stige, Leif Christian","Arthun, Marius","Berge, Jørgen","Bluhm, Bodil A.","Borgå, Katrine","Bratbak, Gunnar","Divine, Dmitry V.","Eldevik, Tor","Eriksen, Elena","Fer, Ilker","Fransson, Agneta","Gradinger, Rolf","Granskog, Mats A.","Haug, Tore","Husum, Katrine","Johnsen, Geir","Jonassen, Marius O.","Jørgensen, Lis Lindal","Kristiansen, Svein","Larsen, Aud","Lien, Vidar S.","Lind, Sigrid","Lindstrøm, Ulf","Mauritzen, Cecilie","Melsom, Arne","Mernild, Sebastian H.","Müller, Malte","Nilsen, Frank","Primicerio, Raul","Søreide, Janne E.","van der Meeren, Gro I.","Wassmann, Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-723648"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gerland, Sebastian"],"country":["Chile","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bjerknes Centre for Climate Research","Department Tromsø","Ecotoxicology and Risk Assessment","IMR","NORCE Norwegian Research Centre AS","Norsk Polarinstitutt","Norwegian Meteorological Institute","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","The University Centre in Svalbard (UNIS)","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","Universidad de Magallanes","University of Bergen","University of Oslo","Western Norway University of Applied Sciences"],"keyword":["Arctic","Atlantification","Barents Sea","Climate change","Ecosystem","Sea ice"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"still arctic the changing barents sea","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.2022.00088","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was funded by the Norwegian Ministry of Education and Research and the Research Council of Norway (RCN), through the project “The Nansen Legacy” (RCN # 276730) and its pilot study (RCN # 272721), and by the home institutions of all authors."],"id":"S01-000.00-723648","identifier":[{"id":"85180772265","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d3a41319-8fe2-482a-8ad1-a7ef2c44611c"],"keyword":["Arctic","Atlantification","Barents Sea