nding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sidsel Dahl","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f743083c-d5b4-4522-b4c4-6991b8f83397","name":"Andersen, Sidsel Dahl","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid Korning","key":"hvidtpau","last":"Hvidt","name":"Hvidt, Astrid Korning","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Rode","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"ec8117d6-ea18-413d-af91-06dd9564328d","name":"Andreasen, Signe Rode","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva Anna Marianne","key":"baerendspau","last":"Baerends","locid":"c1883c47-7a3c-4bfa-9191-d0e2bc75ef1a","name":"Baerends, Eva Anna Marianne","orcid":"0000-0002-7970-9201","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 7","first":"Jens","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"af310f7a-c49b-4381-bcb4-cf56e3fd80d8","name":"Lundgren, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"fb8358a6-187a-4d5f-8187-06051ed74173","name":"Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","name_org":"Østergaard, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-2459-0511","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"tolstruppau","last":"Tolstrup","locid":"36e9f1d5-608c-46b7-8d41-2505c02086fc","name":"Tolstrup, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7020-5173","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"ruwaldoth","last":"Ruwald","locid":"f66ada42-a498-4f26-97ba-bc9aeae19f84","name":"Juhl, Maria Ruwald","name_org":"Ruwald, M.","rank":29,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"R. K.","key":"thistedoth","last":"Thisted","locid":"9499cebb-fd5b-4b0d-8236-d91752d05f5d","name":"Thisted, Rikke Krog","name_org":"Thisted, R. K.","rank":30,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["37095240"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s43856-023-00277-x","issn":["2730664X"],"journal":"Communications Medicine","paperid":"58","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Communications Medicine","title_org":"Communications medicine","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166405434"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-915ddf15-eb5d-4e5c-bf72-6760594cc6ae","au-79d7b208-f25a-46b5-a2ec-6a8d3b1ffd70","ku-6a9f593a-2599-4952-b712-c682c064807c","sdu-6c6ce684-e95a-46a5-9608-12787604b3a9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of age and comorbidities on SARS-CoV-2 vaccine-induced T cell immunity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-097.22-715722","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Previous studies have reported Blood type O to confer a lower risk of SARS-CoV-2 infection, while secretor status and other blood groups have been suspected to have a similar effect as well. Study design and methods: To determine whether any other blood groups influence testing positive for SARS-CoV-2, COVID-19 severity, or prolonged COVID-19, we used a large cohort of 650,156 Danish blood donors with varying available data for secretor status and blood groups ABO, Rh, Colton, Duffy, Diego, Dombrock, Kell, Kidd, Knops, Lewis, Lutheran, MNS, P1PK, Vel, and Yt. Of these, 36,068 tested positive for SARS-CoV-2 whereas 614,088 tested negative between 2020-02-17 and 2021-08-04. Associations between infection and blood groups were assessed using logistic regression models with sex and age as covariates. Results: The Lewis blood group antigen Le a displayed strongly reduced SARS-CoV-2 susceptibility OR 0.85 CI[0.79–0.93] p <.001. Compared to blood type O, the blood types B, A, and AB were found more susceptible toward infection with ORs 1.1 CI[1.06–1.14] p <.001, 1.17 CI[1.14–1.2] p <.001, and 1.2 CI[1.14–1.26] p <.001, respectively. No susceptibility associations were found for the other 13 blood groups investigated. There was no association between any blood groups and COVID-19 hospitalization or long COVID-19. No secretor status associations were found. Discussion: This study uncovers a new association to reduced SARS-CoV-2 susceptibility for Lewis type Le a and confirms the previous link to blood group O. The new association to Le a could be explained by a link between mucosal microbiome and SARS-CoV-2.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Moslemi, Camous","Sækmose, Susanne","Larsen, Rune","Brodersen, Thorsten","Didriksen, Maria","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Banasik, Karina","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Bruun, Mie T.","Dowsett, Joseph","Kasperen, Kathrine A.","Mikkelsen, Susan","Hansen, Thomas F.","Ullum, Henrik","Erikstrup, Christian","Olsson, Martin L.","Ost