nisations","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bf17e9c0-9cce-4279-91ca-a09ea31ed7f1","au-f012585e-1726-4ba4-b4ce-707410ab267a","ku-91f0a367-ec39-40ab-b139-9d0cdd1657c2","sdu-cda13320-4222-4898-a46b-3e0a739b7bb4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Study protocol for discharge on day of surgery after hip and knee arthroplasty from the Center for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.54-691836","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Kidney transplant recipients receive maintenance immunosuppressive therapy to avoid allograft rejection resulting in increased risk of infections and infection-related morbidity and mortality. Approximately 98% of adults are infected with varicella zoster virus, which upon reactivation causes herpes zoster. The incidence of herpes zoster is higher in kidney transplant recipients than in immunocompetent individuals, and kidney transplant recipients are at increased risk of severe herpes zoster-associated disease. Vaccination with adjuvanted recombinant glycoprotein E subunit herpes zoster vaccine (RZV) prevents herpes zoster in older adults with excellent efficacy (90%), and vaccination of kidney transplant candidates is recommended in Danish and international guidelines. However, the robustness and duration of immune responses after RZV vaccination, as well as the optimal timing of vaccination in relation to transplantation remain unanswered questions. Thus, the aim of this study is to characterize the immune response to RZV vaccination in kidney transplant candidates and recipients at different timepoints before and after transplantation. Methods: The Herpes Virus Infections in Kidney Transplant Patients (HINT) study is a prospective observational cohort study. The study will include kidney transplant candidates on the waiting list for transplantation (n = 375) and kidney transplant recipients transplanted since January 1, 2019 (n = 500) from all Danish kidney transplant centers who are offered a RZV vaccine as routine care. Participants are followed with repeated blood sampling until 12 months after inclusion. In the case of transplantation or herpes zoster disease, additional blood samples will be collected until 12 months after transplantation. The immune response will be characterized by immunophenotyping and functional characterization of varicella zoster virus-specific T cells, by detection of anti-glycoprotein E antibodies, and by measuring cytokine profiles. Discussion: The study will provide new knowledge on the immune response to RZV vaccination in kidney transplant candidates and recipients and the robustness and duration of the response, potentially enhancing preventive strategies against herpes zoster in a population at increased risk. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05604911).","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hamm, Sebastian Rask","Saini, Sunil Kumar","Hald, Annemette","Vaaben, Anna V.","Pedersen, Natasja Wulff","Suarez-Zdunek, Moises Alberto","Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Bruunsgaard, Helle","Johansen, Isik Somuncu","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Bistrup, Claus","Birn, Henrik","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Hadrup, Sine Reker","Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"cuid":["S04-099.94-715949"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"keyword":["Adjuvanted recombinant glycoprotein E subunit herpes zoster vaccine","Aged","Herpes Zoster epidemiology","Herpes zoster","Herpesvirus 3 Human","Humane herpes virus 3","Humans","Immune response","Immunodominant Epitopes","Kidney Transplantation adverse effects","Kidney transplant candidates","Kidney transplant recipients","Prospective Studies","Shingles","Shingrix","T Lymphocytes","Vaccines Synthetic","Varicella zoster virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"herpes virus infections in kidney transplant patients hint a prospective observational cohort study","src":["au","dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12879-023-08663-5","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Royal Library, Copenhagen University Library The study is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF220C0073947), The Augustinus Foundation, The Regions’ Medicine and Treatment Pool, RH and OUH’s Common Research Pool, and Rigshospitalet. SR. Hamm receives grants from the Research Council of Rigshospitalet related to this study. SDN has received unrestricted research grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Lundbeck Foundation, the Independent Research Fund Denmark, and reports advisory board activity for Gilead Sciences and GlaxoSmithKline/ViiV Healthcare, all unrelated to this manuscript. S.R. Hadrup is the cofounder of PokeAcell and coinventor of licensed patents related to T cell detection, but unrelated to this study. H. Birn has participated in advisory board activity for GlaxoSmithKline and has previously received research funding from GlaxoSmithKline unrelated to this study. SKS receives research funding from Lundbeck Foundation, the Danish Research Council, and the Danish Cancer Society for projects, all unrelated to this study. CSL has received honoraria from GlaxoSmithKline for lectures and participation in advisory boards. ZBH has received grants from Independent Research Fund, Lundbeck Foundation, Helen Rudes Foundation, and the Danish Cancer Society, all unrelated to this manuscript. ISJ, SSS, H. Bruunsgaard, AH, MASZ, CB, AVV, and NWP report no competing interests."],"id":"S04-099.94-715949","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10578002","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37845608","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85174285093","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4781b9db-9d99-4ccf-8a24-1f9b62b88695","dtu-b8d614d0-2549-41a0-85df-4da68215ee5d","ku-5ff2efdf-d44c-4c66-9da3-72f9fc16005b","sdu-97c5dc1e-d661-43a1-abd8-1176c5ff322f"],"keyword":["Adjuvanted recombinant glycoprotein E subunit herpes zoster vaccine","Aged","Herpes Zoster Vaccine","Herpes Zoster/epidemiology","Herpes zoster","Herpesvirus 3, Human","Humane herpes virus 3","Humans","Immune response","Immunodominant epitopes","Kidney Transplantation/adverse effects","Kidney transplant candidates","Kidney transplant recipients","Prospective Studies","Shingles","Shingrix","T-Lymphocytes","Vaccines, Synthetic","Varicella zoster virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-E282D157449628FFB30E13919D4D0BF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/374125515/s12879_023_08663_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12879-023-08663-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/346105932/s12879-023-08663-5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/243882796/s12879_023_08663_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunol