rnal":"Journal of Infection","pages":"439-445","publisher":"WB  Saunders Ltd","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Infection","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151491732"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f2e365bc-4a77-43ed-bb76-711703aa4a0e","au-8c16ca24-dd08-459f-b61f-d422e4d8fcf4","ku-1a67b463-abed-438a-a1ca-23d81ee9a730","sdu-dcd21894-0d33-4cc2-ae3d-4ab63109e7c3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Neurosyphilis among people with and without HIV infection : A Danish nationwide prospective, population-based cohort study 2015-2021","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-691878","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Shielded loops have recently attracted keen interest in the design of Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) detector arrays. To prevent unwanted detuning of array elements, preamplifier decoupling is used. So far, the decoupling circuit design was based on intuitive approach of minimizing impedance presented to the terminals of the loop. The approach leads to decent but not optimal results. In this paper a systematic analytical method is used to derive the exact condition for maximum decoupling of shielded loops in array. The condition describes precisely what impedance should be presented to the terminals of the loop for best decoupling. It is shown that the method is valid for single- and multi-gap shielded loops with and without integrated reactive components across the gap. The presented results are useful in the design of MRI receive arrays of shielded loop coils with optimal decoupling.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wang, Wenjun","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343745"],"event":{"end":"2022-11-18","place":"Kharkiv , ua","start":"2022-11-14","title":"2022 IEEE 2nd Ukrainian Microwave Week","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["High impedance coil","Magnetic resonance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"condition for optimal preamplifier decoupling in one turn single and multi gap shielded loop mri detectors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/296892511/preamp_dcpl_condition_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343745","identifier":[{"id":"85149184080","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-832dc06b-b468-467b-bc31-2561b52cb687"],"keyword":["High impedance coil","Magnetic resonance","Radio frequency coil","Shielded loop"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D62D14DCDAC999B7C8ED73A927998A55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/296892511/preamp_dcpl_condition_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ukrmw58013.2022.10037007","isbn":["9798350331523"],"pages":"150-154","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2022 IEEE Ukrainian Microwave Week (UkrMW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149184080"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-832dc06b-b468-467b-bc31-2561b52cb687"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Condition for optimal preamplifier decoupling in one-turn single- and multi-gap shielded loop MRI detectors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343745","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Dette projekt er udført af en gruppe forskere fra Sektion for Landskabsarkitektur og Planlægning, Københavns Universitet, som et pilotprojekt, på foranledning af Gudenåkomitéen. Gudenåkomitéen er et samarbejde mellem de syv kommuner, der deler Gudenåens hovedløb: Hedensted, Horsens, Skanderborg, Silkeborg, Viborg, Favrskov og Randers Kommuner. Komitéen består af ét kommunalt bestyrelsesmedlem fra hver medlemskommune. Formålet med pilotprojektet er at skabe en platform for en kommende implementering af den Helhedsplan for Gudenåen som Gudenåkomitéen enedes om i 2021. De enkelte dele af pilotprojektet omfatter en række analyser af landbrug og landskab langs Gudenåens hovedløb, en identifikation af mulige strategiske projekter, en gennemgang af de gennemførte aktørworkshops og anvendelse af film som planlægnings- og dialogredskab. Resultaterne præsenteres dels i denne rapport, dels i form af en pilotfilm, der anviser mediets muligheder som analyse-, dialog- og kommunikationsredskab i forbindelse med inddragende planlægning. Pilotfilmen kan tilgås direkte via link i kapitel V.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, Erling","Andersen, Peter Stubkjær","Folvig, Sara","Jensen, Miriam","Jessen, Mette Juhl","Larsen, Kristina Cecilie","Løffler, Leah","Munck Petersen, Rikke","Vejre, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471736"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"landskabsanalyse for gudenådalen pilotprojekt i forbindelse med helhedsplan for gudenåen","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341016913/Landskabsanalyse_lr.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471736","ids":["ku-82dc9851-b1de-4cf9-beb8-1588cdb0eb69"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1E8D9A8A29C2C273908320C323819A32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341016913/Landskabsanalyse_lr.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Landscape Architecture and Planning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Spatial Change and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Erling","key":"andersenerlingpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"ee71739a-2c1d-4ebf-93f0-db3419d00da5","name":"Andersen, Erling","orcid":"0000-0002-2178-2772","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Stubkjær","key":"andersenpeterstubkjærpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"bf71bafa-9fb3-41ca-be4c-d426de50e348","name":"Andersen, Peter Stubkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-3795-8939","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sara","key":"folvigsarapau","last":"Folvig","locid":"9e24f183-6cc5-4bda-8807-3db3f9afe4f0","name":"Folvig, Sara","orcid":"0000-0003-3382-7699","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Miriam","key":"jensenmiriampau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Miriam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Juhl","key":"jessenmettejuhlpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"ff71260c-30d5-4e85-a7cf-1c538618f7b3","name":"Jessen, Mette Juhl","orcid":"0009-0007-0316-3189","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Cecilie","key":"larsenkristinaceciliepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"efd93d1f-f798-46cb-9717-8f1f619c6651","name":"Larsen, Kristina Cecilie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leah","key":"løfflerleahpau","last":"Løffler","locid":"0453c5e0-9faf-4dc5-8b0b-4d8fa03a3f20","name":"Løffler, Leah","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"munckpetersenrikkepau","last":"Munck Petersen","locid":"01b63bb6-47bd-48d3-ac0b-3c55663e3473","name":"Munck Petersen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0001-7788-6290","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"vejrehenrikpau","last":"Vejre","locid":"e4073dcd-d8a8-4d8a-b2c6-149ce705394b","name":"Vejre, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-6820-0389","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"marts 2023","pages":"155","publisher":"Institut for Geovidenskab og Naturforvaltning, Københavns Universitet","repno":"IGN Rapport, marts 2023","series":"IGN Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82dc9851-b1de-4cf9-beb8-1588cdb0eb69"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Landskabsanalyse for Gudenådalen : Pilotprojekt i forbindelse med Helhedsplan for Gudenåen","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471736","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Biological features of neoplastic disease affecting mammary gland tissue are shared between canines and humans. Research performed in either species has translational value and early phase clinical trials performed in canines with spontaneous disease could be informative for human trials. The purpose of this study was to investigate the somatic genetic aberrations occurring in canine mammary neoplasia by exome capture and next generation sequencing. Based on 55 tumor-normal pairs we identified the PIK3CA gene as the most commonly mutated gene in canine mammary tumors, with 25% of samples carrying mutations in this gene. A recurrent missense mutation was identified, p.H1047R, which is homologous to the human PIK3CA hotspot mutation found in different types of breast neoplasia. Mutations homologous to other known human mutation hotspots such as the PIK3CA p.E545K and the KRAS p.G12V/D were also identified. We identified copy number aberrations affecting important tumor suppressor and oncogenic pathways including deletions affecting the PTEN tumor suppressor gene. We suggest that activation of the KRAS or PIK3CA oncogenes or loss of the PTEN suppressor gene may be important for mammary tumor development in dogs. This data endorses the conservation of cancer across species and the validity of studying cancer in non-human species.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Arendt, Maja Louise","Sakthikumar, Sharadha","Melin, Malin","Elvers, Ingegerd","Rivera, Patricio","Larsen, Majbritt","Saellström, Sara","Lingaas, Frode","Rönnberg, Henrik","Lindblad-Toh, Kerstin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515171"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Evidensia Equine Specialist Hospital Helsingborg","Harvard University","Karolinska University Hospital","Norwegi