{"abstract":"PURPOSE: This article presents a novel 14-channel receive-only array for 13 C human head imaging at 3 T that explores the SNR gain by operating at cryogenic temperature cooled by liquid nitrogen. METHODS: Cryostats are developed to evaluate single-coil bench SNR performance and cool the 14-channel array with liquid nitrogen while having enough thermal insulation between the coils and the sample. The temperature distribution for the coil array is measured. Circuits are adapted to the -189°C environment and implemented in the 14-channel array. 13 C images are acquired with the array at cryogenic and room temperature in a 3T scanner. RESULTS: Compared with room temperature, the array at cryogenic temperature provides 27%-168% SNR improvement over all voxels and 47% SNR improvement near the image center. The measurements show a decrease of the element noise correlation at cryogenic temperature. CONCLUSION: It is demonstrated that higher SNR can be achieved by cryogenically cooling the 14-channel array. A cryogenic array suitable for clinical imaging can be further developed on the array proposed. The cryogenic coil array is most likely suited for scenarios in which high SNR deep in a head and decent SNR on the periphery are required.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Wang, Wenjun","Sánchez-Heredia, Juan Diego","Olin, Rie Beck","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Laustsen, Christoffer","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-092.14-019024"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy"],"keyword":["Carbon imaging","Cryogenic coil","Head coil","MRI array"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a cryogenic 000000000014 channel sup 000000000013 sup c receiver array for 000000000003t human head imaging","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29508","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.14-019024","identifier":[{"id":"36321576","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10092528","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85141429966","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5758c74d-1ee3-495c-8786-ec779f3bfbbc","dtu-374e8d4e-0d9e-45f0-a032-782fecfe36e6"],"keyword":["MRI array","carbon imaging","cryogenic coil","head coil"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9E27BAE576E4224E083E6CF8A183769D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29508","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/302527911/Magnetic_Resonance_in_Med_2022_Wang_A_cryogenic_14_channel_13C_receiver_array_for_3T_human_head_imaging_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/409575244/Magnetic_Resonance_in_Med_-_2022_-_Wang_-_A_cryogenic_14_channel_13C_receiver_array_for_3T_human_head_imaging.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Juan Diego","key":"sánchezherediapau","last":"Sánchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sánchez-Heredia, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rie Beck","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","name_org":"Olin, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben Søvsø Szocska","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2ea5821e-bbda-4f7e-a18a-0b9eb3b993f0","name":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","name_org":"Hansen, Esben Søvsø Szocska","orcid":"0000-0001-5512-9870","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36321576"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mrm.29508","issn":["07403194","15222594"],"issn_org":["07403194"],"issue":"3","journal":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","pages":"1265-1277","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141429966"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5758c74d-1ee3-495c-8786-ec779f3bfbbc","dtu-374e8d4e-0d9e-45f0-a032-782fecfe36e6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A cryogenic 14-channel 13 C receiver array for 3T human head imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.14-019024","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective To estimate the risk of interval colorectal cancer (CRC) in faecal immunochemical test (FIT) negative screening participants according to socioeconomic status. Design In this register-based study, first round FIT negative (<20 μg hb/g faeces) screening participants (biennial FIT, citizens aged 50-74) were followed to estimate interval CRC risk. Multivariate Cox proportional hazard regression models estimated HRs based on socioeconomic status defined by educational level and income. Models were adjusted for age, sex and FIT concentration. Results We identified 829 (0.7‰) interval CRC in 1 160 902 individuals. Interval CRC was more common in lower socioeconomic strata with 0.7‰ for medium-long higher education compared with 1.0‰ for elementary school and 0.4‰ in the highest income quartile compared with 1.2‰ in the lowest. These differences did not translate into significant differences in HR in the multivariate analysis, as they were explained by FIT concentration and age. HR for interval CRC was 7.09 (95% CI) for FIT concentrations 11.9-19.8 μg hb/g faeces, and 3.37 (95% CI) for FIT between 7.2 and 11.8 compared with those <7.2. The HR rose with increasing age ranging from 2.06 (95% CI 1.45 to 2.93) to 7.60 (95% CI 5.63 to 10.25) compared with those under 55 years. Conclusion Interval CRC risk increased with decreasing income, heavily influenced by lower income individuals more often being older and having increased FIT concentrations. Individualising screening interval based on age and FIT result, may decrease interval CRC rates, reduce the social gradient and thereby increase the screening efficiency.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Deding, Ulrik","Kobaek-Larsen, Morten","Bøggild, Henrik","Kaalby, Lasse","Thygesen, Marianne Kirstine","Baatrup, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-672332"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Deding, Ulrik"],"keyword":["Cancer","Cohort Studies","Colonic Neoplasms","Colorectal Neoplasms diagnosis","Colorectal cancer","Early Detection of Cancer","Epidemiology","Feces chemistry","Hemoglobins analysis","Humans","Screening","Socioeconomic Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic inequalities in interval colorectal cancer are explained by differences in faecal haemoglobin concentration and age a register based cohort study","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjgast-2023-001113","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Odense University Hospital grant number A3610."],"id":"S02-100.00-672332","identifier":[{"id":"37230536","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10230874","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85161050612","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5d9bf952-6472-4cd8-a6d7-8f3785b52297","sdu-15ae01a9-3f16-4953-a828-e45a4cd136da"],"keyword":["CANCER","COLONIC NEOPLASMS","COLORECTAL CANCER","Cohort Studies","Colorectal Neoplasms/diagnosis","EPIDEMIOLOGY","Early Detection of Cancer","Feces/chemistry","Hemoglobins/analysis","Humans","SCREENING","Socioeconomic Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A58EABCC239652F09488010A8ED4BF6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/233565871/e001113.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjgast-2023-001113","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/532227623/e001113.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Public Health and Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"dedingpau","last":"Deding","locid":"ac9881cb-949b-4427-bf3e-8badf8905e2d","name":"Deding, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8263-2989","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"kobaeklarsenpau","last":"Kobaek-Larsen","locid":"0f383fcc-0bd7-4c47-93b8-911d024157d6","name":"Kobaek-Larsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-5097-9283","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"bøggildpau","last":"Bøggild","locid":"f78a6e0b-ac8c-47a0-9b70-8de3cdac496d","name":"Bøggild, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8934-5002","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"kaalbypau","last":"Kaalby","locid":"0c8d2c97-bb94-4040-883e-f9d93c5f4327","name":"Kaalby, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-6721-3604","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Kirstine","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"b71406f7-073f-4c45-920c-5984da19b5c8","name":"Thygesen, Marianne Kirstine","orcid":"0000-0002-1811-7405","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar","key":"baatruppau","last":"Baatrup","locid":"3e62f6ae-0738-4c20-ac2f-3543bb12fa6b","name":"Baatrup, Gunnar","orcid":"0000-0003-0300-5766","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37230536"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjgast-2023-001113","issn":["20544774"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMJ Open Gastroenterology","paperid":"e001113","publisher":"BMJ Group","publisher_org":"B M J Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open Gastroenterology","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161050612"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5d9bf952-6472-4cd8-a6d7-8f3785b52297","sdu-15ae01a9-3f16-4953-a828-e45a4cd136da"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Socioeconomic inequalities in interval colorectal cancer are explained by differences in faecal haemoglobin concentration and age : A register-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-672332","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Current prognostic blood-based biomarkers for pancreatic adenocarcinoma (PDAC) are limited. Recently, promoter hypermethylation of SFRP1 (phSFRP1) has been linked to poor prognosis in patients with gemcitabine-treated stage IV PDAC. This study explores the effects of phSFRP1 in patients with lower stage PDAC. METHODS: Based on a bisulfite treatment process, the promoter region of the SFRP1 gene was analyzed with methylation-specific PCR. Kaplan-Meier curves, log-rank tests, and generalized linear regression analysis were used to assess restricted mean survival time survival at 12 and 24 months. RESULTS: The study included 211 patients with stage I-II PDAC. The median overall survival of patients with phSFRP1 was 13.1 months, compared to 19.6 months in patients with unmethylated SFRP1 (umSFRP1). In adjusted analysis, phSFRP1 was associated with a loss of 1.15 months (95%CI -2.11, -0.20) and 2.71 months (95%CI -2.71, -0.45) of life at 12 and 24 months, respectively. There was no significant effect of phSFRP1 on disease-free or progression-free survival. In stage I-II PDAC, patients with phSFRP1 have worse prognoses than patients with umSFRP1. DISCUSSION: Results could indicate that the poor prognosis may be caused by reduced benefit from adjuvant chemotherapy. SFRP1 may help guide the clinician and be a possible target for epigenetically modifying drugs.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Stubbe, Benjamin","Larsen, Anders Christian","Madsen, Poul Henning","Krarup, Henrik","Pedersen, Inge Søkilde","Lundbye-Christensen, Søren","Hansen, Carsten Palnæs","Hasselby, Jane Preuss","Johansen, Astrid Zedlitz","Thorlacius-Ussing, Ole","Johansen, Julia Sidenius","Henriksen, Stine Dam"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-685685"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Stubbe, Benjamin"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Blood based","DNA methylation","Epigenetic","Pancreatic cancer","Personalized therapy","Survival","cfDNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"promoter hypermethylation of sfrp000000000001 as a prognostic and potentially predictive blood based biomarker in patients with localized pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fonc.2023.1211292","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by two private foundations: The Speciallæge Heinrich Kopps foundation and the Svend Andersen Foundation. Acknowledgments"],"id":"S02-100.00-685685","identifier":[{"id":"37333823","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10272559","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85162043526","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7d8e9f59-fd50-41f9-87be-ef5027311492","ku-01e34c23-5789-4372-8ae7-3ef0612a966c"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","biomarker","blood-based","cfDNA","epigenetic","pancreatic cancer","personalized therapy","survival"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7FC26CAAAE208B3E0EA067712AEE570C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/534462044/Stubbe_et_al._2023_romoter_hypermethylation_of_SFRP1_as_a_prognostic_and_potentially_predictive_blood_based_biomarker_in_patients_with_localized_pancreatic_ductal_adenocarcinoma.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/365590926/Promoter_hypermethylation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fonc.2023.1211292","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Clinical Cancer Research Center","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Gastrointestinal Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"