key":"johansenastridzedlitzpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Astrid Zedlitz","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"thorlaciusussingolepau","last":"Thorlacius-Ussing","locid":"00effb83-33c5-4f0d-97af-5107bd146c4b","name":"Thorlacius-Ussing, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-4963-1551","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Julia Sidenius","key":"johansenjuliaspau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","name_org":"Johansen, Julia Sidenius","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Dam","key":"henriksenstinedampau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"59571ea6-b5de-44f6-ab36-c829af2fdba3","name":"Henriksen, Stine Dam","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37333823"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fonc.2023.1211292","issn":["2234943X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Oncology","paperid":"1211292","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Oncology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162043526"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7d8e9f59-fd50-41f9-87be-ef5027311492","ku-01e34c23-5789-4372-8ae7-3ef0612a966c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Promoter hypermethylation of SFRP1 as a prognostic and potentially predictive blood-based biomarker in patients with localized pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-685685","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND & AIMS: Biliary tract cancer (BTC) is associated with a dismal prognosis, partly because it is typically diagnosed late, highlighting the need for diagnostic biomarkers. The purpose of this project was to identify and validate multiprotein signatures that could differentiate patients with BTC from non-cancer controls. METHODS: In this study, we included treatment-naïve patients with BTC, healthy controls, and patients with benign conditions including benign biliary tract disease. Participants were divided into three non-overlapping cohorts: a case-control-based discovery cohort (BTC = 186, controls = 249); a case-control-based validation cohort (validation cohort 1: BTC = 113, controls = 241); and a cohort study-based validation cohort including participants (BTC = 8, controls = 132) referred for diagnostic work-up for suspected cancer (validation cohort 2). Immuno-Oncology (I-O)-related proteins were measured in serum and plasma using a proximity extension assay (Olink Proteomics). Lasso and Ridge regressions were used to generate protein signatures of I-O-related proteins and carbohydrate antigen 19-9 (CA19-9) in the discovery cohort. RESULTS: Sixteen protein signatures, including 2 to 82 proteins, were generated. All signatures included CA19-9 and chemokine C-C motif ligand 20. Signatures discriminated between patients with BTC vs. controls, with AUCs ranging from 0.95 to 0.99 in the discovery cohort and 0.94 to 0.97 in validation cohort 1. In validation cohort 2, AUCs ranged from 0.84 to 0.94. Nine signatures achieved a specificity of 82% to 84% while keeping a sensitivity of 100% in validation cohort 2. All signatures performed better than CA19-9, and signatures including >15 proteins showed the best performance. CONCLUSION: The study demonstrated that it is possible to generate protein signatures that can successfully differentiate patients with BTC from non-cancer controls. IMPACT AND IMPLICATIONS: We attempted to find blood sample-based protein profiles that could differentiate patients with biliary tract cancer from those without cancer. Several profiles were found and tested in different groups of patients. The profiles were successful at identifying most patients with biliary tract cancer, pointing towards the utility of multiprotein signatures in this context.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Christensen, Troels D.","Maag, Emil","Larsen, Ole","Feltoft, Claus L.","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Jensen, Lars Henrik","Leerhøy, Bonna","Hansen, Carsten P.","M. Chen, Inna","Nielsen, Dorte L.","Johansen, Julia S."],"cuid":["S03-098.82-697814"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Troels D."],"keyword":["Biliary tract cancer","Cholangiocarcinoma","Diagnosis","blood protein assay","gall bladder cancer","multi biomarker signature"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["BioXpedia"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and validation of circulating protein signatures as diagnostic biomarkers for biliary tract cancer","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhepr.2022.100648","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank our colleagues at all the sites for their assistance with inclusion of patients. Likewise, we thank The Danish Cancer Society, Beckett-Fonden, Fonden til fremme af klinisk cancerforskning, The A.P. Moller Foundation, and Tømrermester Holms Mindelegat for their financial contributions to our project. Many thanks to the biomedical laboratory scientists Charlotte Falk, Vibeke H. Holm, Marta Monika Asadi Sohi and Astrid Z. Johansen for their assistance with the blood sample handling. We thank Edwin Stanton Spencer for English language editing. The Danish Cancer Society (grant number R218-A13148) provided salary for TDC. Funding for protein analyses and statistical analyses was provided by Beckett-Fonden, Fonden til fremme af klinisk cancerforskning, The A.P. Moller Foundation, and Tømrermester Holms Mindelegat. The funding sources were not involved in the study design; the collection, analysis, interpretation of the data; or writing of the report."],"id":"S03-098.82-697814","identifier":[{"id":"36699667","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146467400","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9867981","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-cf951faf-a1d9-49e3-ba3e-75c2f296fca8","ku-0a1aaf0d-2ee1-4c59-84cd-d6727da0f722","sdu-a52afb93-804e-45d5-8263-a9080c293913"],"keyword":["biliary tract cancer","blood protein assay","cholangiocarcinoma","diagnosis","gall bladder cancer","multi-biomarker signature"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-240CB06C070007BFC89F53059767EBF0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/370407009/Development_and_validation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/228335590/1_s2.0_S2589555922002208_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/539127058/1-s2.0-S2589555922002208-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhepr.2022.100648","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Bioxpedia A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["BioXpedia"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Immunology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department o