{"abstract":"Background: Despite the wide range of existing performance measures to evaluate functional status of patients with multiple sclerosis, the heterogeneous nature of the disease hinders clinical characterization and monitoring of disease severity. Speckle tracking ultrasonography is a non-invasive technique to assess isolated muscle function by evaluating the contractile properties of muscle tissue, i.e. muscle strain. The aim of this study was to investigate whether muscle strain measured by speckle tracking ultrasonography could be a useful quantitative measure of muscle function in patients with multiple sclerosis. The criterion validity of muscle strain was compared to that of validated performance measures of upper and lower extremity function. Methods: This cross-sectional study used baseline data from an explorative observational cohort study (the MUST study). Participants recruited from a hospital outpatient MS clinic underwent speckle tracking ultrasonography of the biceps brachii, supraspinatus, and soleus muscles of the dominant side according to pre-defined submaximal isometric contractions. Participants also completed the Timed 25-Foot Walk Test, the Six Spot Step Test, the 2-minute walking test, the Nine-Hole Peg Test, the 12-item Multiple Sclerosis Walking Scale, and the Oxford Shoulder Score. Gaussian distribution was investigated by visual inspection of normal probability plots and the Shapiro-Wilk test. The Timed 25-Foot Walk Test and Nine-Hole Peg Test were selected as gold standards for function of the lower and upper extremities, respectively. Criterion validity was assessed using Spearman's rank-order correlation coefficient ρ (rho), comparing the muscle strain and performance measures against predefined gold standards. Differences in criterion validity were estimated using squared correlations on the Fischer's Z-scale, with non-parametric bootstrapping to obtain bias-corrected, accelerated bootstrap confidence intervals (95% BCa). Results: Criterion validity showed good to excellent correlations between the gold standard for lower extremity function and the 2-minute walking test and Six Spot Step Test, and a fair correlation to the 12-item Multiple Sclerosis Walking Scale. No significant correlation was found between the gold standard for upper extremity function and the performance measure. There were no significant correlations between the gold standards and muscle strain. Conclusion: The absence of criterion validity for muscle strain alongside fair to strong criterion validity for the performance measures indicates that speckle tracking ultrasonography assessment of muscle strain is either invalid or evaluates other constructs of multiple sclerosis. Muscle strain assessed by speckle tracking ultrasonography cannot be recommended for the evaluation of treatment effects or disease progression in multiple sclerosis.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Thorning, Maria","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","Skov, Cecilie Dollerup","Frich, Lars Henrik","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-596766"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thorning, Maria"],"keyword":["Criterion validity","Multiple sclerosis","Muscle function","Skeletal muscle"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"criterion validity of muscle strain analyses of skeletal muscle function in patients with multiple sclerosis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.msard.2022.104478","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was funded by the University of Southern Denmark, the Region of Southern Denmark [grant number: 17/33583, 18/51851 ], Lounkaer Foundation, Augustinus’ Foundation [grant number: 18-0217 ], the Danish Multiple Sclerosis Society [grant number: A35607 ], Lily Benthine Lund's Foundation [grant number: 5652 ], the Society of Multiple Sclerosis Patients on Funen, the Chief Physician Committee Research Foundation [grant number: 70-A3228 ], and the Promotion of Medical Science Foundation [grant number: 18-L-0369 ]. The study sponsors have had no involvement in the study or influence on the reporting of the results."],"id":"S01-000.00-596766","identifier":[{"id":"85146013835","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36603294","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-521cbf59-2354-4443-ba93-8b9459e89be9"],"keyword":["Criterion validity","Multiple sclerosis","Muscle function","Skeletal muscle","Speckle tracking ultrasonography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B9CCB97FBB8EB4C49982B142EB64CAC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/219163762/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.msard.2022.104478","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, BRIDGE - Brain Research - Inter Disciplinary Guided Excellence (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurosurgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Neurobiology Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"thorningpau","last":"Thorning","locid":"9cc3883b-fce8-4dc5-865d-03f5cbd05795","name":"Thorning, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kate Lykke","key":"lambertsenpau","last":"Lambertsen","locid":"d867cc02-bda7-455d-8d02-8b602e35e7b3","name":"Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","orcid":"0000-0001-9276-4902","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Dollerup","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"62ddb8a5-b21c-4ec6-8fcc-3923a7a1db0c","name":"Skov, Cecilie Dollerup","orcid":"0000-0002-6063-7113","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"frichpau","last":"Frich","locid":"f5e4ebc5-0851-429f-ae70-b627b21b3d91","name":"Frich, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0147-4211","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Boye","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"34f8d097-2b28-40a1-9415-5fe706340c6d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Boye","orcid":"0000-0001-6461-3787","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Hvilsted","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e1703e06-01b8-4d46-a1d1-4c4d5af99fa5","name":"Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","orcid":"0000-0002-7319-1368","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36603294"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.msard.2022.104478","issn":["22110348","22110356"],"issn_org":["22110348"],"journal":"Multiple Sclerosis and Related Disorders","paperid":"104478","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Multiple Sclerosis and Related Disorders","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146013835"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-521cbf59-2354-4443-ba93-8b9459e89be9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Criterion validity of muscle strain analyses of skeletal muscle function in patients with multiple sclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-596766","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Mobile network traffic is increasing and so is the energy consumption. The Radio Access Network (RAN) part is responsible for the largest share of the mobile network energy consumption, and thus; an important consideration when expanding mobile networks to meet traffic demands. This work analyses how the energy consumption of future mobile networks can be minimised by using the right RAN architecture, share the network with other operators and implementing the most efficient energy minimising technologies in the RAN. It is explored how the different approaches can be realised in real life networks as well as the research state of the art is highlighted. Furthermore, this work provides an overview of future research directions for 6G energy saving potentials. Different energy saving contributions are evaluated by a common methodology for more realistic comparison, based on the potential energy saving of the overall mobile network consumption. Results show that implementing selected technologies and architectures, the mobile network overall energy consumption can be reduced by approximately 30%, corresponding to almost half of the RAN energy consumption. Following this, a set of guidelines towards an energy optimised mobile network is provided, proposing changes to be made initially and in the longer run for brownfield network operators as well as a target network for greenfield network operators.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","Ruepp, Sarah Renée","Berger, Michael Stübert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669226"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"keyword":["5G","6G","AI","C RAN","Green RAN","Network slicing","O RAN","vRAN"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward greener 000000000005g and beyond radio access networks a survey","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/OJCOMS.2023.3257889","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-669226","identifier":[{"id":"85151504122","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3e4ef03c-0eed-4b72-a578-ae8d7b32c836"],"keyword":["5G","6G","AI","C-RAN","Green RAN","MOCN","MORAN","Network slicing","O-RAN","vRAN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5173821682FB0C9AC833261B9E1EEBC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/320476211/Toward_Greener_5G_and_Beyond_Radio_Access_NetworksA_Survey.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/OJCOMS.2023.3257889","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line M.P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Larsen, Line M.P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik L.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"f3aec174-d663-4d97-aaa0-81cd6f4493a9","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","name_org":"Christiansen, Henrik L.","orcid":"0000-0002-9558-3493","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","name_org":"Ruepp, Sarah","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael S.","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","name_org":"Berger, Michael S.","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ojcoms.2023.3257889","issn":["2644125X"],"journal":"IEEE Open Journal of the Communications Society","pages":"768-797","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Open Journal of the Communications Society","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151504122"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3e4ef03c-0eed-4b72-a578-ae8d7b32c836"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Toward Greener 5G and Beyond Radio Access Networks - A Survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669226","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The study investigated the effects of ensiling and brown juice-assisted ensiling of wheat straw and press cake from a green biorefinery plant prior to anaerobic co-digestion (Aco-D) with cattle manure on methane yield and nutrient availability in the digestates. Straw was ensiled with and without brown juice at field-scale and lab-scale levels, followed by Aco-D with manure using continuous stirred-tank reactors (CSTR) and batch tests. The digestates from CSTR were incorporated into the soil to study nitrogen and sulphur dynamics and availability over 80 days. Results show that ensiling of straw increased net inorganic nitrogen release in soil and reduced net inorganic sulphur immobilisation compared to the non-ensiled straw. Brown juice-assisted ensiling of straw at the lab-scale level significantly increased methane production by 14 % and increased hydrolysis and methane production rates compared to non-ensiled straw. These results demonstrate that ensiling of straw has the potential as a pre-treatment technique for enhanced biogas production and higher nutrient availability in digestates for crop production and provides an opportunity to valorise brown juice as an ensiling additive.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nyangáu, Jared Onyango","Møller, Henrik Bjarne","Larsen, Søren Ugilt","Sørensen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674700"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nyangáu, Jared Onyango"],"keyword":["Anaerobic digestion","Methane","Nitrogen mineralisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brown juice assisted ensiling of straw and press cake for enhanced biogas production and nutrient availability in digestates","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eti.2023.103248","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 860127 (FertiCycle project). The authors acknowledge funding from Danish Energy Technology Development and Demonstration programme (EUDP) for StrawSilage project (Project No. 64020–1039 ). The authors acknowledge the technical staff at the Departments of Agroecology and Engineering, Aarhus University, Denmark for their technical assistance, especially Janni Sørensen, Margit Paulsen, Lene Skovmose, Marianne Stevenson and Karin Dyrberg. This project has received funding from the European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 860127 (FertiCycle project). The authors acknowledge funding from Danish Energy Technology Development and Demonstration programme (EUDP) for StrawSilage project (Project No. 64020–1039)."],"id":"S01-000.00-674700","identifier":[{"id":"85163871962","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-292b3080-8748-4745-bb53-7011a8cdeb53"],"keyword":["Anaerobic digestion","Ensilage","Methane","Nitrogen mineralisation","Sulphur mineralisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A098F8ED713FD54089F77719C6438F62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/328744571/Nyang_au_et_al_2023b_Brown_juice_assisted_ensiling_of_straw_and_press_cake_for_enhanced_biogas_production_and_nutrient_availability_in_digestates.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eti.2023.103248","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Soil Fertility"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jared Onyango","key":"nyangáupau","last":"Nyangáu","locid":"aa2c6453-12eb-4977-97a4-5bc39cbd652f","name":"Nyangáu, Jared Onyango","orcid":"0000-0002-1684-1950","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Bjarne","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"a2eda86a-cdac-4996-8db0-3cecfe51be12","name":"Møller, Henrik Bjarne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Ugilt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Søren Ugilt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"02fc3f2d-6c8a-4ed4-af54-ddfa541c1c1b","name":"Sørensen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-3425-3690","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eti.2023.103248","issn":["23521864"],"journal":"Environmental Technology and Innovation","paperid":"103248","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Technology and Innovation","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163871962"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-292b3080-8748-4745-bb53-7011a8cdeb53"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Brown juice assisted ensiling of straw and press cake for enhanced biogas production and nutrient availability in digestates","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674700","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
