 of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3007296e-7585-4a52-8847-9d515e0aaab5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EU-ekspert: Stop med at overfortolke EU’s rolle i den nye udenrigspolitiske strategi – det eneste nye er ordvalget (Kronik i Altinget)","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677864","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Post-weaning diarrhoea (PWD) is a multifactorial condition and the most well documented infectious cause is enterotoxigenic Escherichia coli. The objective of the study was to investigate possible associations between pathological manifestations and pathogens in pigs with and without PWD. The study was conducted as a case–control study and included a total of 173 pigs from 9 different commercial intensive indoor production herds in eastern Denmark. Results: Based on clinical examination, a total of 89 piglets with PWD (cases) and 84 piglets without PWD (controls) were included. Most of the pigs (n = 105/173) presented gastric lesions, which were more frequently observed in the control group. The odds of gastric ulcers were lower among pigs with PWD compared to pigs without PWD with an odds ratio (OR) of 0.2 (0.0; 0.7). Abnormal content in the colon was associated with PWD, with an OR of 6.5 (3.2; 14.3). No apparent association was found between lesions and the various pathogens or a combination of these. The odds of neutrophilic granulocyte infiltration were lower in the jejunum among pigs with PWD (OR 0.3 [0.1; 0.6]) compared to pigs without PWD. The association between neutrophilic granulocyte infiltration in jejunum and PWD differed between the herds (P = 0.03). Furthermore, the associations between PWD and hyperleukocytosis (P = 0.04) or infiltration of eosinophilic granulocytes (P = 0.04) in ileum were also herd dependent. Histopathology revealed several lesions not relatable to PWD. Conclusion: The association between lesions and specific pathogens or PWD is more complex than anticipated.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","Pankoke, Karen","Hansen, Mette Sif","Pedersen, Ken Steen","Eriksen, Esben Østergaard","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Olsen, John Elmerdahl","Kudirkiene, Egle","Larsen, Lars Erik","Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Barington, Kristiane"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683969"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Histopathology","Microbiology","Pigs","Post weaning diarrhoea"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gastro intestinal lesions are not relatable to diarrhoea or specific pathogens in post weaning diarrhoea pwd in pigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-023-00693-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-683969","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10316552","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37400879","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85164028402","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4f5ed508-5041-4ac2-a661-a27a2766d0ca"],"keyword":["Histopathology","Microbiology","Pigs","Post-weaning diarrhoea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C0C01C9C87DE781CEC93F72EC406074"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360984983/Blirup_Plum_Jensen_Jensen_Nielsen_Pankoke_Hansen_Pedersen_Eriksen_Nielsen_Olsen_Kudirkiene_Larsen_Goecke_Barington_2023.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-023-00693-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie Amalie","key":"blirupplumsophieamaliepau","last":"Blirup-Plum","locid":"54f7ba11-2529-4cf7-adb1-139dfa0e4b53","name":"Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenhenrikelvangpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Saxmose","key":"nielsensørensaxmosepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8d00f12a-fe80-48ba-96c2-6769b91281e7","name":"Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","orcid":"0000-0003-2417-0787","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"pankokekarenpau","last":"Pankoke","locid":"c59c44ce-f168-448f-82d3-b444274b4fee","name":"Pankoke, Karen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Sif","key":"hansenmettesifpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"cf95e878-fe91-4715-b9f7-05fc972de6c6","name":"Hansen, Mette Sif","orcid":"0000-0002-8132-8475","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenkensteenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Esben Østergaard","key":"eriksenesbenøstergaardpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"87d48be8-d777-425b-9366-3d7ed5cfcb59","name":"Eriksen, Esben Østergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9507-8553","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenjenspeterpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e550301c-f89e-4a8b-bf34-e6fc3b76ff37","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenjohnelmerdahlpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Egle","key":"kudirkieneeglepau","last":"Kudirkiene","locid":"49238462-eac4-44c3-964c-3f16918f3782","name":"Kudirkiene, Egle","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckenicolebakkegårdpau","last":"Goecke","locid":"ed85c101-c8e6-403b-ba93-39e95e23e68d","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristiane","key":"baringtonkristianepau","last":"Barington","locid":"0913e657-6538-4dea-a32f-5f97b7acc33c","name":"Barington, Kristiane","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37400879"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13028-023-00693-y","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","pages":"1-18","paperid":"30","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164028402"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4f5ed508-5041-4ac2-a661-a27a2766d0ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gastro-intestinal lesions are not relatable to diarrhoea or specific pathogens in post-weaning diarrhoea (PWD) in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-683969","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Animal studies have shown that SGLT2 inhibition decreases oxidative stress, which may explain the cardiovascular protective effects observed following SGLT2 inhibition treatment. Thus, we investigated the effects of two and twelve weeks SGLT2 inhibition on DNA and RNA oxidation. Individuals with type 2 diabetes (n = 31) were randomized to two weeks of treatment with the SGLT2 inhibitor empagliflozin treatment (25 mg once daily) or placebo. The primary outcome was changes in DNA and RNA oxidation measured as urinary excretion of 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2’-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG) and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo), respectively. In another trial, individuals with type 2 diabetes (n = 35) were randomized to twelve weeks of dapagliflozin treatment (10 mg once daily) or placebo in a crossover study. Changes in urinary excretion of 8-oxodG and 8-oxoGuo were investigated as a posthoc analysis. Compared with placebo treatment, two weeks of empagliflozin treatment did not change urinary excretion of 8-oxodG (between-group difference: 0.3 nmol/24-hour (95% CI: −4.2 to 4.8)) or 8-oxoGuo (1.3 nmol/24-hour (95% CI: −4.7 to 7.3)). From a mean baseline 8-oxodG/creatinine urinary excretion of 1.34 nmol/mmol, dapagliflozin-treated individuals changed 8-oxodG/creatinine by −0.17 nmol/mmol (95% CI: −0.29 to −0.04) following twelve weeks of treatment, whereas placebo-treated individuals did not change 8-oxodG/creatinine (within-group effect: 0.10 nmol/mmol (95% CI: −0.02 to 0.22)) resulting in a significant between-group difference (p = 0.01). Urinary excretion of 8-oxoGuo was unaffected by dapagliflozin treatment. In conclusion, two weeks of empagliflozin treatment did not change DNA or RNA oxidation. However, a posthoc analysis revealed that longer-term dapagliflozin treatment decreased DNA oxidation. Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT02890745 and NCT02914691.Highlights Plasma ferritin correlated with DNA and RNA oxidation in individuals with T2D. Twelve weeks dapagliflozin treatment decreased DNA oxidation. Dapagliflozin and empagliflozin treatment did not change RNA oxidation. Lipid peroxidation was unaffected by two weeks empagliflozin treatment.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Larsen, Emil List","Andersen, Andreas","Kjær, Laura K.","Eickhoff, Mie K.","Frimodt-Møller, Marie","Persson, Frederik","Rossing, Peter","Lykkesfeldt, Jens","Knop, Filip K.","Vilsbøll, Tina","Rungby, Jørgen","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690601"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["8 oxoGuo","8 oxodG","Dapagliflozin","Empagliflozin","Oxidative stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of two and twelve weeks sodium glucose cotransporter 000000000002 inhibition on dna and rna oxidation two randomized placebo controlled trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-690601","identifier":[{"id":"85159652939","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000990930700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"37171199","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f01c1feb-e5bd-4417-a164-4578310cdf95"],"keyword":["8-oxoGuo","8-oxodG","dapagliflozin","empagliflozin","oxidative stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6A3455EEF0EECE4AE337A1D371744E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laura K.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Laura K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mie K.","key":"eickhoffpau","last":"Eickhoff","name":"Eickhoff, Mie K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie","key":"frimodtmøllerpau","last":"Frimodt-Møller","name":"Frimodt-Møller, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frederik","key":"perssonpau","last":"Persson","name":"Persson, Frederik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"ca397e2f-e1b3-430b-a537-a047438b44b6","name":"Rossing, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1531-4294","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens","key":"lykkesfeldtpau","last":"Lykkesfeldt","locid":"6e71ebed-c114-42ab-9ae9-6333f14bf8ad","name":"Lykkesfeldt, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6514-8407","rank":8,"rolecode":"p