{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Jonas","Norsk, Anne Kathrine Alexandersen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713412"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"test copenhagen researching a new social infrastructure in istedgade","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98482667/6-1_Test_Copenhagen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713412","ids":["ruc-ad22e8f9-c4a4-43a5-8d8b-ccbb3f0be498"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-282B0954B38AD969A427100BA2B4296A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/98482667/6-1_Test_Copenhagen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Mobility, Space, Place and Urban Studies (MOSPUS)","Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business, Centre for Tourism Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1cb27156-b919-462a-9243-4ab2d8f87f26","name":"Larsen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-8119","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Anne Kathrine Alexandersen","key":"norskpau","last":"Norsk","locid":"d31a3c47-2e64-426c-a424-412731d30a23","name":"Norsk, Anne Kathrine Alexandersen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jonas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"henrik","key":"grellpedh","last":"Grell","name":"Grell, henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"178-196","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","status":"p","title":"Researching and designing walking"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-ad22e8f9-c4a4-43a5-8d8b-ccbb3f0be498"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Test Copenhagen : Researching a new social infrastructure in Istedgade","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713412","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Polyamorphism has been a controversial and highly debated solid-state phenomenon in both material and pharmaceutical communities. Although some evidence of this fascinating phenomenon has been reported for several inorganic systems, and more recently also for a few organic compounds, the occurrence of polyamorphism is poorly understood and the molecular-level organization of polyamorphic forms is still unknown. Here we have investigated the occurrence of polyamorphism and polyamorphic interconversions in hydrochlorothiazide (HCT), using both experimental and computational methods. Three distinct HCT polyamorphs, presenting distinct physical and thermal stabilities as well as distinct relaxation properties, were systematically prepared using spray-drying (SD), quench-cooling (QC) and ball milling (BM) methods. HCT polyamorph II (obtained by QC) was found to be more physically stable than polyamorphs I and III (obtained by SD and BM, respectively). Furthermore, polyamorphs I and III could be converted into polyamorph II after QC, while polyamorph II did not convert to any other polyamorph after SD or BM. Molecular dynamics simulations show that HCT dihedral angle distributions are significantly different for polyamorphs I and II, which is postulated as a possible explanation for their different physicochemical properties.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Martins, Inês C.B.","Larsen, Anders S.","Madsen, Anders Østergaard","Aalling-Frederiksen, Olivia","Correia, Alexandra","Jensen, Kirsten M.Ø.","Jeppesen, Henrik S.","Rades, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719907"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron DESY","University of Helsinki"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unveiling polyamorphism and polyamorphic interconversions in pharmaceuticals the peculiar case of hydrochlorothiazide","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d3sc02802j","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719907","identifier":[{"id":"85174513290","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10599472","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37886102","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3af71432-459e-4a70-83d2-bd56b6e76c63"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC1EFC59D60FD996F6686CF302D45924"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373873883/d3sc02802j.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d3sc02802j","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Solid State Pharmaceutics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"deutsches elektronen synchrotron desy","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron DESY","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Inês C.B.","key":"martinspau","last":"Martins","locid":"f74ce2cf-2009-44cf-aab7-5d1c898666f3","name":"Martins, Inês C.B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"