:"Wedderkopp","locid":"bcfae344-0a75-458d-8ba2-4198ee915d40","name":"Wedderkopp, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-9660-6618","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig","key":"midtibypau","last":"Midtiby","locid":"68dca252-e2e2-40e7-82bc-0832ad90f943","name":"Midtiby, Stig Linnemann","name_org":"Midtiby, Stig","orcid":"0000-0002-4537-3551","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe Jonasson","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Uffe Jonasson","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina","key":"jungepau","last":"Junge","locid":"cfc44ba3-52fb-4ee1-80aa-37d81f46d477","name":"Junge, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-3304-3010","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1f2dc31b-a41a-429b-93b6-442d23833db3","name":"Kjaer, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-5340-8649","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"3","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-31c68639-6c20-4cb9-a7c8-fa61f5996767","ucl-d209893d-fa9e-4ac3-bba0-0cd37dfe6581"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Arbejdspakke 2b: Kvantitativ monitorering og dataanalyser : Rapport resumé","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-704641","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Night and evening work is associated with risk of sickness absence, but little is known about the acute effects of these types of shifts on sickness absence. The aim of the current study is therefore to examine the risk of calling in sick within two days after a night or an evening shift. METHODS: By use of a case-crossover design, odds of calling in sick within two days after a night or an evening shift compared to day shifts were analyzed within the same person. Day-to-day information on shifts and sickness absence were derived from the Danish Working Hour Database on 44 767 cases. Data were analyzed using conditional logistic regression. The analyses were supplemented by extensive testing of methodological choices. RESULTS: Analyses showed higher odds of calling in sick after a night shift [odds ratio (OR) 1.22, 95% confidence intervak (CI) 1.14-1.30] and lower odds after an evening shift (OR 0.89, 95% CI 0.84-0.93) compared to day shifts within the same person. Testing of methodological choices suggested that in particular the duration of case and control periods, time between these periods along with the number of control periods affected the results. CONCLUSION: This large and unique within-person study among Danish hospital employees indicate that the risk of calling in sick is affected by the types of shifts, independently of sex, age, and time-invariant confounding. Extensive testing identified important methodological choices eg, length and number of included periods to consider when choosing the case-crossover design.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Ann Dyreborg","Nielsen, Helena Breth","Kirschheiner-Rasmussen, Jonas","Hansen, Johnni","Hansen, Åse Marie","Kolstad, Henrik Albert","Rugulies, Reiner","Garde, Anne Helene"],"cuid":["S03-087.32-767551"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Ann Dyreborg"],"keyword":["Arbejdstid","Night shift","Register data","Risk Factors","Shift work","Shift worker","Sickness absence","Sygefravær"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"night and evening shifts and risk of calling in sick within the next two days a case crossover study design based on day to day payroll data","src":["au","ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5271/sjweh.4074","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-087.32-767551","identifier":[{"id":"85149054110","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10577016","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36445985","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-704b27df-5dff-4ab1-8f71-c403ebd39380","ku-6507a2ca-e01b-465b-832d-c243c5201bfd","nfa-eb907c4e-1070-43e1-8c0b-909a77343a79"],"keyword":["Key terms hospital staff","arbejdstid","irregular work hour","night shift","register data","risk Factors","shift work","shift worker","sickness absence","sygefravær"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-565D1C189641BE466E2DCC701F7F07B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5271/sjweh.4074","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/337971732/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Psychosocial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Occupational and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann Dyreborg","key":"larsenadpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fa03cd1b-31e4-483a-8ee1-09f917379e33","name":"Larsen, AD","name_org":"Larsen, Ann Dyreborg","orcid":"0000-0002-3587-2998","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena Breth","key":"nielsenhelenabrethpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"47ae35e5-47cc-47ff-b81d-12e2a0f4145d","name":"Nielsen, Helena Breth","orcid":"0000-0001-6409-5166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"kirschheinerrasmussenjonaspau","last":"Kirschheiner-Rasmussen","name":"Kirschheiner-Rasmussen, Jonas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Johnni","key":"hansenjohnnipau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Johnni","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Åse Marie","key":"hansenåsemariepau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5b151ef4-abb8-4673-9522-abc399e62fea","name":"Hansen, Åse Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4075-3918","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Albert","key":"kolstadhenrikapau","last":"Kolstad","locid":"287e6e28-266e-42e8-aa6d-10dffb6dc51e","name":"Kolstad, Henrik A.","name_org":"Kolstad, Henrik Albert","orcid":"0000-0002-6535-4323","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Reiner","key":"ruguliesreinerpau","last":"Rugulies","locid":"88830f3c-e0d6-48c4-8b5e-0f6a8078df69","name":"Rugulies, Reiner","orcid":"0000-0002-7752-131X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","country":"dk","first":"Anne Helene","key":"gardeannehelenepau","last":"Garde","locid":"64b13e21-4e8a-4454-b945-766da6180377","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36445985"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5271/sjweh.4074","issn":["03553140","03566528"],"issn_org":["03553140"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment & Health","pages":"117-125","publisher":"Nordic Association of Occupational Safety and Health","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment & Health","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment and Health","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149054110"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-704b27df-5dff-4ab1-8f71-c403ebd39380","ku-6507a2ca-e01b-465b-832d-c243c5201bfd","nfa-eb907c4e-1070-43e1-8c0b-909a77343a79"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Night and evening shifts and risk of calling in sick within the next two days - a case-crossover study design based on day-to-day payroll data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-087.32-767551","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The aim of this study is to present incidence, histological subtypes, survival rates, and prognostic factors based on a national cohort of patients with salivary gland carcinoma. METHODS: All Danish patients with submandibular gland carcinoma diagnosed from 1990 to 2015 (n = 206) were included and analyzed following histological re-evaluation. Data were collected by the Danish Head and Neck Cancer Group (DAHANCA). Overall, disease-specific and recurrence-free survival were evaluated. Prognostic factors were analyzed with multivariate Cox Hazard Regression. RESULTS: The study population consisted of 109 (53%) men and 97 (47%) women, median age 62 years (range 11-102). Adenoid cystic carcinoma was the most frequent subtype (50%). Tumour classification T1/T2 (75%) and N0 (78%) was most frequent. The mean crude incidence was 0.17/100,000/year. Most patients (n = 194, 94%) were treated with primary surgery, and 130 (67%) received postoperative radiotherapy. The 5- and 10-year survival rates were for overall survival 64% and 41%, disease-specific survival 74% and 61%, and recurrence-free survival 70% and 56%, respectively. Survival rates were higher for adenoid cystic carcinoma compared to other subtypes, but the difference was not significant in multivariate analysis. Recurrence occurred in 69 patients, and 37 (53.6%) of them had recurrence in a distant site. Advanced T-classification and regional lymph-node metastases had significant negative impact on survival rates. CONCLUSION: The incidence of submandibular gland carcinoma in Denmark was 0.17/100,000/year and stable during the time period. The most frequent subtype was adenoid cystic carcinoma. Half of the recurrences presented in a distant site, and multivariate analysis confirmed that advanced stage was independent negative prognostic factor for recurrence and survival.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Westergaard-Nielsen, Marie","Godballe, Christian","Eriksen, Jesper Grau","Larsen, Stine Rosenkilde","Kiss, Katalin","Agander, Tina","Ulhøi, Benedicte Parm","Charabi, Birgitte Wittenborg","Klug, Tejs Ehlers","Jacobsen, Henrik","Johansen, Jørgen","Kristensen, Claus Andrup","Andersen, Elo","Andersen, Maria","Bjørndal, Kristine"],"cuid":["S04-094.00-685629"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Westergaard-Nielsen, Marie"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Child","Female","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Recurrence Local epidemiology","Prognosis","Retrospective Studies","Salivary Gland Neoplasms epidemiology","Salivary gland carcinoma","Submandibular gland","Submandibular gland cancer","Submandibular gland carcinoma","Survival Rate","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epidemiology outcomes and prognostic factors in submandibular gland carcinomas a national dahanca study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00405-023-07940-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-094.00-685629","identifier":[{"id":"85152550275","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37052687","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10219881","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-44803a3b-fa80-4b8d-b9f6-0a978ad8540c","au-95b8f6c9-e92c-4b83-aa93-07baa994c6e9","ku-d4c75388-e478-4351-94b6-607fac95b090","sdu-06657385-42cc-4ef0-acec-3a572de5226c"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Carcinoma, Adenoid