{"abstract":"Er vi som HR-professionelle egentlig opmærksomme på det kæmpe potentiale, der kan være ved at bringe HR-forskning og HR-praksis blot en lille smule tættere på hinanden? Hvad er det, der begrænser dette samspil? Som optakt til årets CRANET-konference 2022 taler vi i denne podcast om samspillet mellem HR-forskning og HR-praksis.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik","Larsen, Alice","Beck Petersen, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-288701"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["NOCA - Network of Corporate Academies"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hr i fokus del 000000000002 hvad skal hr bruge forskningen til cbs executive talks","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/hr-i-fokus-del-2-hvad-skal-hr-bruge-forskningen-til/id1570444522?i=1000549953271","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-288701","ids":["cbs-8c42a600-777e-46cb-9af0-373ff145a979"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FE7E7B445485E010170ABCDDD3D77FEF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/hr-i-fokus-del-2-hvad-skal-hr-bruge-forskningen-til/id1570444522?i=1000549953271","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Chr. Hansen A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["NOCA - Network of Corporate Academies"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Alice","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"beckpetersenppu","last":"Beck Petersen","name":"Beck Petersen, Maria","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"CBS Executive","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-8c42a600-777e-46cb-9af0-373ff145a979"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"HR i fokus del 2. Hvad skal HR bruge forskningen til? : CBS Executive Talks","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-288701","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Purpose There is a limit to the maximum achievable preamplifier decoupling. In many cases, this level is not enough. To overcome this limit, the preamplifier noise figure can be compromised for further decoupling increase. This is useful in flexible MRI arrays where ensuring coil insensitivity to changes in other array elements is a challenge. Methods This work establishes the relation between the preamplifier noise figure and preamplifier decoupling using closed-form equations. These equations allow the evaluation of preamplifier decoupling properties and benchmark different preamplifiers against each other. The method to design the corresponding decoupling networks is described. The derived generalized design equations, which are not limited to 50 omega pre-matched preamplifiers, greatly improve design flexibility and enable use of new amplifiers in MRI detectors. Results Using the method, the decoupling properties of three preamplifiers are studied. For demonstration, the coil decoupling is further increased by 10.8 dB using one of the preamplifiers. The noise figure is sacrificed by 0.5 dB, which is predicted by equations and verified experimentally. Although examples are shown for 3 T systems at 32.13 MHz and 127.7 MHz, the approach and equations apply to any field strength and nucleus. Conclusion Preamplifier decoupling can be improved beyond what is possible by traditional approaches. The derived design equations cover a wide range of cases, including inductive coils and self-resonant low-impedance and high-impedance coils.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wang, Wenjun","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305475"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy"],"keyword":["Matching networks","Noise figure","Preamplifier decoupling","Receiver coil"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trade off between preamplifier noise figure and decoupling in mri detectors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29489","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-305475","identifier":[{"id":"85143088414","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36263582","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000870140200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC10092476","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-02febb53-0645-4f81-83c6-2579e6e92205"],"keyword":["Matching networks","Noise figure","Preamplifier decoupling","Receiver coil"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88634ED96BBF2313218982B841374BB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29489","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/294111643/Magnetic_Resonance_in_Med_2022_Wang_Trade_off_between_preamplifier_noise_figure_and_decoupling_in_MRI_detectors.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezherediapau","last":"Sanchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sanchez-Heredia, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36263582"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mrm.29489","issn":["07403194","15222594"],"issn_org":["07403194"],"issue":"2","journal":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","pages":"859-871","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143088414"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-02febb53-0645-4f81-83c6-2579e6e92205"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Trade-off between preamplifier noise figure and decoupling in MRI detectors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305475","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Parallel imaging can aid hyperpolarized 13C MRI in extracting more information in the limited time window of the hyperpolarized signal. Using a dedicated, flexible 13C receive coil design with coupling coefficients matched for both 13C and 23Na, sensitivity profiles for reconstruction can be acquired at the 23Na frequency. We demonstrate this method in two hyperpolarized in vivo experiments involving pig kidneys and human brain using a two-times accelerated 3D blipped stack-of-spirals sequence with dual-resolution. The results show good SNR, coverage, and resolution. The method is promising for integrating and automating parallel imaging for hyperpolarized 13C MRI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hansen, Rie Beck","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Grist, James T.","Wang, Wenjun","Bøgh, Nikolaj","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Hansen, Esben S.","Schulte, Rolf F.","Tyler, Damian John","Laustsen, Christoffer","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-337984"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-12","place":"London, gb","start":"2022-05-07","title":"2022 ISMRM &amp; SMRT Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Global Research","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parallel imaging of hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c mri using sup 000000000023 sup na sensitivity profiles","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-337984","ids":["dtu-6fefc235-24fe-465f-8add-171b4bf8e322"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-00