"orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaj","key":"bøghpau","last":"Bøgh","name":"Bøgh, Nikolaj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben S.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Esben S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf F.","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, Rolf F.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Damian John","key":"tylerpau","last":"Tyler","name":"Tyler, Damian John","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6fefc235-24fe-465f-8add-171b4bf8e322"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Parallel imaging of hyperpolarized <sup>13</sup>C MRI using <sup>23</sup>Na sensitivity profiles","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-337984","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Self-resonant coils are well suitable for flexible array design. The size of such coils is dictated by the RF signal wavelength, which makes the design challenging at low frequencies. In this work, 13C tuning is achieved by combining distributed and lumped capacitance with the self-inductance of an RG-178 coaxial cable. A 1H trap is moved from the coil to the board of the preamplifier for better coil flexibility. The active 13C decoupling circuit is compact and broadband. The approach is used to develop a flexible 8-channel receive array of parallel-resonance coils for 13C-imaging. The array elements exhibit low noise correlation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Wang, Wenjun","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365782"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-12","place":"London, gb","start":"2022-05-07","title":"2022 ISMRM &amp; SMRT Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flexible receive array of parallel resonance high impedance coaxial coils for 000000000013c imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-365782","ids":["dtu-cd0b4121-9514-4184-9faf-f8234846484a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5DC3BAA28536D01C4236F7C558B9379F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cd0b4121-9514-4184-9faf-f8234846484a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Flexible Receive Array of Parallel-Resonance High-Impedance Coaxial Coils for 13C Imaging","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365782","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The use of hyperpolarised 13C pyruvate for nononcological neurological applications has not been widespread so far, possibly due to delivery issues limiting the visibility of metabolites. First proof-of-concept results have indicated that metabolism can be detected in human brain, and this may supersede the results obtained in preclinical settings. One major difference between the experimental setups is that preclinical MRI/MRS routinely uses anaesthesia, which alters both haemodynamics and metabolism. Here, we used hyperpolarised [1–13C]pyruvate to compare brain metabolism in awake rats and under isoflurane, urethane or medetomidine anaesthesia. Spectroscopic [1–13C]pyruvate time courses measured sequentially showed that pyruvate-to-bicarbonate and pyruvate-to-lactate labelling rates were lower in isoflurane animals than awake animals. An increased bicarbonate-to-lactate ratio was observed in the medetomidine group compared with other groups. The study shows that hyperpolarised [1–13C]pyruvate experiments can be performed in awake rats, thus avoiding anaesthesia-related issues. The results suggest that haemodynamics probably dominate the observed pyruvate-to-metabolite labelling rates and area-under-time course ratios of referenced to pyruvate. On the other hand, the results obtained with medetomidine suggest that the ratios are also modulated by the underlying cerebral metabolism. However, the ratios between intracellular metabolites were unchanged in awake compared with isoflurane-anaesthetised rats.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hyppönen, Viivi","Stenroos, Petteri","Nivajärvi, Riikka","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Gröhn, Olli","Paasonen, Jaakko","Kettunen, Mikko I."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-369315"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kettunen, Mikko I."],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Eastern Finland"],"keyword":["Blood brain barrier","Isoflurane","Medetomidine","Urethane"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metabolism of hyperpolarised 000000000001 sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate in awake and anaesthetised rat brains","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/367859719/16397471431723567133.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-369315","identifier":[{"id":"85117387440","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34672399","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-d89d9ec7-509c-461a-8f7a-9d886f20562c"],"keyword":["Blood–brain barrier","Isoflurane","Medetomidine","Urethane"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E53623CAFEED57900CF3E6A8ECB5809"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/367859719/16397471431723567133.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of eastern finland","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Eastern Finland","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Viivi","key":"hyppönenpau","last":"Hyppönen","name":"Hyppönen, Viivi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petteri","key":"stenroospau","last":"Stenroos","name":"Stenroos, Petteri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Riikka","key":"nivajärvipau","last":"Nivajärvi","name":"Nivajärvi, Riikka","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olli","key":"gröhnpau","last":"Gröhn","name":"Gröhn, Olli","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaakko","key":"paasonenpau","last":"Paasonen","name":"Paasonen, Jaakko","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko I.","key":"kettunenpau","last":"Kettunen","name":"Kettunen, Mikko I.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34672399"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.4635","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"2","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","paperid":"e4635","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117387440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d89d9ec7-509c-461a-8f7a-9d886f20562c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Metabolism of hyperpolarised [1–<sup>13</sup>C]pyruvate in awake and anaesthetised rat brains","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-369315","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Emergence delirium (ED) and postoperative delirium (POD) are associated with increased morbidity and mortality and occur in up to one-third of patients undergoing major non-cardiac surgery, where the underlying pathogenesis is multifactorial, including increased inflammation. We aimed to assess the effect of pre-operative high- versus low-dose glucocorticoid on the occurrence of ED and POD. Methods: This was a substudy from a randomized, double-blinded clinical trial. Patients ≥18 years, undergoing open liver resection were randomized 1:1 to high-dose (HD, 10 mg/kg methylprednisolone) or low-dose (LD, 8 mg dexamethasone) glucocorticoid and assessed for ED and POD for a maximum of 4 days during hospitalization. The 3-min Diagnostic Interview for CAM-defined delirium (3D-CAM) was used for assessment, 15 and 90 min after arrival in the post-anesthesia care unit (PACU), and subsequently once daily in the ward. Results: Fifty-three patients were included in this secondary substudy (26 HD-group and 27 LD-group). ED occurred in n = 5 HD versus n = 6 LD patients 15 min after PACU arrival. At 90 min after PACU arrival, 4 patients had ED, all from LD-group, and resulted in significantly longer PACU admission, 273 versus 178 min in ED versus Non-ED patients. During the first 4 days in the ward, n = 5 patients had at least one occurrence of POD, all from LD-group. Conclusions: The primary finding of the current substudy was a lower occurrence of ED/POD in the PACU 90 min after arrival and during the first four postoperative days in patients receiving high-dose glucocorticoid compared with patients receiving low-dose glucocorticoid. The two study groups were not evenly balanced concerning known explanatory factors, i.e., age and size of surgery, which calls for larger studies to elucidate the matter.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Awada, Hussein Nasser","Steinthorsdottir, Kristin Julia","Schultz, Nicolai A.","Hillingsø, Jens","Larsen, Peter Nørgaard","Jans, Øivind","Kehlet, Henrik","Aasvang, Eske K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408639"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Emergence","Liver resection","Postoperative delirium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high dose preoperative glucocorticoid for prevention of emergence and postoperative delirium in liver resection a double blinded randomized clinical trial substudy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14057","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-408639","identifier":[{"id":"85127737440","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9320957","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35325467","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-196af19f-2483-424c-9a1e-bbae3fb1ce2d"],"keyword":["emergence","liver resection","postoperative delirium","preoperative glucocorticoid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8E903406773303C3739A9238AF3C3F59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14057","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/312625154/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2022_Awada_High_u2010dose_preoperative_glucocorticoid_for_prevention_of_emergence_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hussein Nasser","key":"awadapau","last":"Awada","name":"Awada, Hussein Nasser","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristin Julia","key":"steinthorsdottirpau","last":"Steinthorsdottir","name":"Steinthorsdottir, Kristin Julia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai A.","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","name":"Schultz, Nicolai A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens G.","key":"hillingsøpau","last":"Hillingsø","locid":"6e3f56a3-3e04-4728-872b-b833e9b702df","name":"Hillingsø, Jens","name_org":"Hillingsø, Jens G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Nørgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Peter Nørgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Øivind","key":"janspau","last":"Jans","name":"Jans, Øivind","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eske Kvanner","key":"aasvangpau","last":"Aasvang","locid":"0efc20dd-d2e0-46b8-ae8b-9c67d62079dd","name":"Aasvang, Eske K.","name_org":"Aasvang, Eske Kvanner","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35325467"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14057","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"6","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"696-703","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127737440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-196af19f-2483-424c-9a1e-bbae3fb1ce2d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"High-dose preoperative glucocorticoid for prevention of emergence and postoperative delirium in liver resection : A double-blinded randomized clinical trial substudy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408639","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Survivors of childhood cancer represent a growing population with a long life expectancy but high risks of treatment-induced morbidity and premature mortality. Regular physical activity (PA) may improve their long-term health; however, high-quality empirical knowledge is sparse. Objective: The Physical Activity and Fitness in Childhood Cancer Survivors (PACCS) study comprises 4 work packages (WPs) aiming for the objective determination of PA and self-reported health behavior, fatigue, and quality of life (WP 1); physical fitness determination (WP 2); the evaluation of barriers to and facilitators of PA (WP 1 and 3); and the feasibility testing of an intervention to increase PA and physical fitness (WP 4). Methods: The PACCS study will use a mixed methods design, combining patient-reported outcome measures and objective clinical and physiological assessments with qualitative data gathering methods. A total of 500 survivors of childhood cancer aged 9 to 18 years with ≥1 year after treatment completion will be recruited in follow-up care clinics in Norway, Denmark, Finland, Germany, and Switzerland. All participants will participate in WP 1, of which approximately 150, 40, and 30 will be recruited to WP 2, WP3, and WP 4, respectively. The reference material for WP 1 is available from existing studies, whereas WP 2 will recruit healthy controls. PA levels will be measured using ActiGraph accelerometers and self-reports. Validated questionnaires will be used to assess health behaviors, fatigue, and quality of life. Physical fitness will be measured by a cardiopulmonary exercise test, isometric muscle strength tests, and muscle power and endurance tests. Limiting factors will be identified via neurological, pulmonary, and cardiac evaluations and the assessment of body composition and muscle size. Semistructured, qualitative interviews, analyzed using systematic text condensation, will identify the perceived barriers to and facilitators of PA for survivors of childhood cancer. In WP 4, we will evaluate the feasibility of a 6-month personalized PA intervention with the involvement of local structures. Results: Ethical approvals have been secured at all participating sites (Norwegian Regional Committee for Medical Research Ethics [2016/953 and 2018/739]; the Oslo University Hospital Data Protection Officer; equivalent institutions in Finland, Denmark [file H-19032270], Germany, and Switzerland [Ethics Committee of Northwestern and Central Switzerland, project ID: 2019-00410]). Data collection for WP 1 to 3 is complete. This will be completed by July 2022 for WP 4. Several publications are already in preparation, and 2 have been published. Conclusions: The PACCS study will generate high-quality knowledge that will contribute to the development of an evidence-based PA intervention for young survivors of childhood cancer to improve their long-term care and health. We will identify physiological, psychological, and social barriers to PA that can be targeted in interventions with immediate benefits for young survivors of childhood cancer in need of rehabilitation.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Lie, Hanne C.","Anderssen, Sigmund","Rueegg, Corina Silvia","Raastad, Truls","Grydeland, May","Thorsen, Lene","Stensrud, Trine","Edvardsen, Elisabeth","Larsen, Marie Hamilton","Torsvik, Ingrid Kristin","Bovim, Lars Peder","Götte, Miriam","Lähteenmäki, Päivi Maria","Kriemler, Susi","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","Fridh, Martin Kaj","Ørstavik, Kristin","Brun, Henrik","Matthews, Iren","Hornset, Else","Ruud, Ellen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408698"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Norway","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian Childhood Cancer Society","Norwegian School of Sport Sciences","Oslo University Hospital","University Hospital Essen","University of Bergen","University of Oslo","University of Turku","University of Zurich","Western Norway University of Applied Sciences"],"keyword":["Barriers","Childhood cancer survivor","Fatigue","Intervention","Physical Fitness","Physical activity","Quality of Life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the physical activity and fitness in childhood cancer survivors paccs study protocol for an international mixed methods study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/35838","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-408698","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8941432","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35258456","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85126098109","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-19850542-9441-443c-934b-1ec4d0d1cd36"],"keyword":["Barriers","Childhood cancer survivor","Fatigue","Intervention","Physical activity","Physical fitness","Quality of life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-43D92314C14D33A7D1DB0E10A3EC04F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/310432643/PDF_8_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/35838","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian school of sport sciences","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian School of Sport Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":