{"abstract":"The established view in textbooks and legal commentary is that the Court’s case law should be viewed as a coherent whole. In this article, we ask whether European human rights law is as unified and European as is often presumed. Based on a citation network of all Chamber judgments from 1998–2018, we argue that the practice of the Court is to some extent split in different strands of case law, where the Court reuses particular factual and legal arguments against the same state without applying those as precedent against other states. We quantify this phenomenon and exemplify it qualitatively. Our data also suggests that the trend is declining. We explain this by the introduction of the Pilot Judgement procedure and an increasing bureaucratization of the Registry, aligning the citation practices of the Court’s five sections. The article situates itself within a broader debate about both legal pluralism and the principle of subsidiarity inherent to the European human rights system and proposals to bring the Court “closer” to the contracting states. We introduce a new and more diversified view on the Court’s practice, understanding it as perhaps less homogenous than has hitherto been thought.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Esmark, Magnus","Olsen, Henrik Palmer","Larsen, Mathias Smed","Byrne, William Hamilton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526128"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adjudicating national contexts domestic particularity in the practices of the european court of human rights","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/glj.2022.29","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-526128","identifier":[{"id":"85131625086","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-de20caad-dd3d-4995-9d61-710b1e113a37"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-289F27DAA349020E86D4B57E5F35DBDF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/glj.2022.29","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Full-time Law programs, PhD programme"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Magnus","key":"esmarkpau","last":"Esmark","locid":"a69580dc-379e-417e-b351-eaee105f9193","name":"Esmark, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-5080-2608","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Palmer","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d6151186-5867-4059-bc35-8e82ae4be33e","name":"Olsen, Henrik Palmer","orcid":"0000-0001-8486-8752","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mathias Smed","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Mathias Smed","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"William Hamilton","key":"byrnepau","last":"Byrne","locid":"930d34e1-4a5f-4111-9a05-5b5b35c6f6b0","name":"Byrne, William Hamilton","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/glj.2022.29","issn":["20718322"],"issue":"4","journal":"German Law Journal","pages":"465-492","status":"p","title":"German Law Journal","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131625086"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-de20caad-dd3d-4995-9d61-710b1e113a37"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adjudicating national contexts – Domestic particularity in the practices of the European Court of Human Rights?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526128","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: The principles of enhanced recovery after surgery (ERAS) are being applied to still more advanced procedures. Liver transplantation offers a unique opportunity for a multimodal approach including donor care as well. Our objective was to determine if ERAS was applicable and safe in orthotopic liver transplantation (OLT). Methods: A national single centre retrospective study showing the implementation of ERAS from 2013 to 2019 with the proceeding 2 years serving as baseline. The primary endpoints were mortality, length of stay (LOS) in the ward and intensive care unit stay. Secondary endpoints were complications estimated by Dindo-Clavien classification, comprehensive complication index (CCI®) and re-admissions. Results: A total of 334 patients were included. LOS was significantly reduced from a median of 22.5 days at introduction to 14 days at 2019. Cold ischaemia time was reduced from a mean of 10.7 to 6.0 h and the use of blood products (erythrocytes, plasma and thrombocytes) from a median of 28 to 6 units. Complications were reduced in severity. Mortality and readmission rates were not affected. Conclusion: ERAS principles are safe and recommended in patients undergoing OLT resulting in reduced severity of complications and LOS without affecting re-admissions or mortality.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hillingsø, Jens","Rostved, Andreas A.","Dengsø, Kristine Elberg","Sørensen, Carina L.","Frederiksen, Hans J.","Krohn, Paul S.","Petersen, Christian R.","Larsen, Peter N.","Fukumori, Daisuke","Burgdorff, Stefan K.","Kehlet, Henrik","Schultz, Nicolai A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532345"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced recovery after surgery is feasible and safe in liver transplantation a cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/371551211/HPB_S_22_00166_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532345","identifier":[{"id":"35973930","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85136763079","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e89e086a-f5c9-415b-b877-322a84dd7c89"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50B0F15CE4E8F8C2A2D87EFC14452112"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/371551211/HPB_S_22_00166_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jens G.","key":"hillingsøpau","last":"Hillingsø","locid":"6e3f56a3-3e04-4728-872b-b833e9b702df","name":"Hillingsø, Jens","name_org":"Hillingsø, Jens G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas A.","key":"rostvedpau","last":"Rostved","name":"Rostved, Andreas A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristine E.","key":"dengsøpau","last":"Dengsø","locid":"2ade7ce1-498e-412b-8924-00d586d6bffb","name":"Dengsø, Kristine Elberg","name_org":"Dengsø, Kristine E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Carina L.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Carina L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hans J.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Hans J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paul S.","key":"krohnpau","last":"Krohn","name":"Krohn, Paul S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian R.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Christian R.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter N.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Peter N.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daisuke","key":"fukumoripau","last":"Fukumori","name":"Fukumori, Daisuke","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stefan K.","key":"burgdorffpau","last":"Burgdorff","name":"Burgdorff, Stefan K.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicolai A.","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","name":"Schultz, Nicolai A.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35973930"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.hpb.2022.07.010","issn":["1365182X","14772574"],"issn_org":["1365182X"],"issue":"11","journal":"HPB","pages":"2022-2028","status":"p","title":"HPB","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136763079"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e89e086a-f5c9-415b-b877-322a84dd7c89"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enhanced recovery after surgery is feasible and safe in liver transplantation : a cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532345","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Non-proportional multiaxial stresses in welded structures cause higher fatigue damage than proportional stresses. In this paper, a new approach based on principal component analysis for quantifying the level of non-proportionality in stress signals is developed. The quantifier is developed for large-scale structures (civil and offshore structures), where the influence of mean stresses is negligible. The proposed quantifier is compared and validated with other approaches from literature with the relevant fatigue criteria and experimental data. The results show that the proposed principal component-based quantifier can capture the level of non-proportionality accurately, which can be used for accurate fatigue life estimations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold","Baumgartner, Jörg","Clausen, Henrik Bisgaard","Arora, Vikas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-588511"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fraunhofer LBF"],"keyword":["Multiaxial fatigue","Non proportional fatigue","Notch stress approach","Welded joints"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-RAM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-RAM","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiaxial fatigue assessment of welded joints using a principal component based measure for non proportionality","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijfatigue.2022.106731","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-588511","identifier":[{"id":"85122797856","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-35811aaa-b1dd-4a33-939c-829fa6ec779e"],"ke