{"abstract":"Objectives: Patients with malignant diseases are known to have a high symptom burden including pain, and insufficient treatment of pain in this population has been frequently documented. To promote the integration of specialized palliative care and hematology and oncology, this study investigated disease, treatment, and comorbidity related symptoms as well as functional capacity and health-related quality of life (HQoL) by patient-reported outcome measures (PROMs) and clinician-reported outcome measures (ClinROs) among inpatients in a comprehensive cancer center. Methods: This cross-sectional study was carried out in a large comprehensive cancer centre of both oncological and hematological inpatients. It combined the use of PROMs and ClinROs. Results: A high symptom burden was reported with fatigue and appetite loss as the most frequent symptoms, and role function being the most impaired function. Further, a low HQoL score was associated with a high number of symptoms/impairments. More than half of all patients reported pain in the last 24 h. Out of 95 patients with average pain >0 in the last 24 h, 71% were treated with opioids and 24% were treated with adjuvant analgesic (AA) defined as antiepileptics, antidepressants and prednisolone. Out of 57 patients with average pain >0 in the last 24 h and possible neuropathic pain, 33% were treated with AAs. A high odds ratio for moderate/severe pain in patients with possible neuropathic pain mechanisms was observed. Conclusions and implications: This study did not only emphasize the need for systematic use of PROMs to identify symptoms and needs for inpatients, but also displayed why PROMs supported by ClinROs are a prerequisite to deliver truly individualized and high-quality patient-centered care. This study calls for continuous training of health care professionals to deliver high-quality treatment of pain. Further, it contributes to the growing recognition, that palliative care and standard care must be integrated to strengthen patient-centered care.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sørensen, Jonas","Sjøgren, Per","Stine, Clemmensen","Sørensen, Tanja Vibeke","Heinecke, Katja","Larsen, Henrik","Eidemak, Inge","Kurita, Geana Paula"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669671"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cancer pain","Neuralgia","Pain Measurement","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Quality of Life","Symptom assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcome measures proms and palliative care clinician reported outcomes clinros mutually improve pain and other symptoms assessment of hospitalized cancer patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-669671","identifier":[{"id":"35179007","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85126048145","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0280e298-3728-4d63-afb5-5c7b5e4bb105"],"keyword":["cancer pain","neuralgia","pain measurement","patient reported outcome measures","quality of life","symptom assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF85B14D28BF997C317E5EC4A4499D05"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas","key":"sørensenjonaspau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per","key":"sjøgrenperpau","last":"Sjøgren","locid":"a319b935-f316-4a9c-88b7-8cabd19b1952","name":"Sjøgren, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-3822-2958","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Clemmensen","key":"stineclemmensenpau","last":"Stine","name":"Stine, Clemmensen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tanja Vibeke","key":"sørensentanjavibekepau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Tanja Vibeke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katja","key":"heineckekatjapau","last":"Heinecke","name":"Heinecke, Katja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenhenrikpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge","key":"eidemakingepau","last":"Eidemak","name":"Eidemak, Inge","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Geana Paula","key":"kuritageanapaulapau","last":"Kurita","locid":"479b54ae-f26a-4027-b797-403bcf437ce5","name":"Kurita, Geana Paula","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35179007"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/sjpain-2021-0162","issn":["18778860","18778879"],"issn_org":["18778860"],"issue":"3","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","pages":"569-577","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126048145"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0280e298-3728-4d63-afb5-5c7b5e4bb105"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patient-reported outcome measures (PROMs) and palliative-care clinician reported outcomes (ClinROs) mutually improve pain and other symptoms assessment of hospitalized cancer-patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669671","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The “11 for Health in Denmark” concept aims to enhance 10–12-year-old schoolchildren's physical activity levels and health knowledge through an 11-week football intervention and has been shown to induce positive effects in numerous areas. However, little is known about the implementation facilitation of this concept in schools. This case study therefore aims to gain a deeper understanding of the implementation facilitation of “11 for Health” in a Danish 5 th grade class comprising 22 schoolchildren (12 boys and 10 girls, M age 11.86±) and one teacher. Data were derived from multiple school situations using photographs and videos, observations, and informal interviews. Five themes were identified: (1) environmental and organizational factors impacting on the implementation; (2) familiarization with the concept for the teacher and schoolchildren; (3) previous clique formation; (4) the central role of the teacher; and (5) the importance of how praise partners are allocated. We found high adherence to the “11 for Health” concept, in which the teacher played a key role by applying an autonomy-supportive style of teaching and using the praise partner concept in a suitable manner. A clique of football-playing boys was a resource, as their praising of classmates encouraged adherence. However, familiarization with the “11 for Health” concept was a challenge and the clique's competitive nature occasionally built barriers to other schoolchildren without football experience, potentially leading to a more controlled form of motivation. Based on the results, we encourage teachers to apply autonomy-supportive teaching when applying the “11 for Health” concept.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Madsen, Esben Elholm","Krustrup, Peter","Møller, Trine Kjeldgaard","Hansen, Tina","Larsen, Malte Nejst","Madsen, Mads","Hansen, Henrik Kruse","Elbe, Anne-Marie","Larsen, Carsten Hvid"],"cuid":["S02-095.49-039650"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Esben Elholm"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leipzig University"],"keyword":["11 for Health in Denmark","Case study","Child","Children","Denmark","Female","Football","Humans","Male","Motivation","Physical activity","School setting","Schools","Soccer","Students","children and youth"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the implementation facilitation of the 000000000011 for health in denmark a case study in a danish 000000000005th grade class","src":["kp","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.14069","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.49-039650","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9293193","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34597433","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85116776289","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-fac67ae1-50ca-489d-a25f-d15c4ca73a74","sdu-6302b86e-86ae-4d7e-83cf-b890237e74bb"],"keyword":["11 for Health i Danmark","11 for Health in Denmark","Child","Denmark","Female","Humans","Male","Motivation","Schools","Soccer","Students","case study","children","children and youth","football","physical activity","school setting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-37DFC6D8836952589B748AFA410D9DA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/196596422/Scandinavian_Med_Sci_Sports_2021_Madsen_Implementation_facilitation_of_the_11_for_Health_in_Denmark_A_case_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.14069","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/192615199/The_implementation_facilitation_of_the_11_for_Health_in_Denmark_A_case_study_in_a_Danish_5th_grade_class.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Sport and Health Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["University College Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"leipzig university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leipzig University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Copenhagen University Hospital Amager and Hvidovre, Hvidovre, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben Elholm","key":"madsenesbenelholmpau","last":"M