lackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116776289"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-fac67ae1-50ca-489d-a25f-d15c4ca73a74","sdu-6302b86e-86ae-4d7e-83cf-b890237e74bb"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The implementation facilitation of the \"11 for Health in Denmark\" - A case study in a Danish 5th -grade class","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.49-039650","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Sleep disturbances are increasingly recognized as a major part of chronic pain pathology. Obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) is a common occurrence in patients with chronic pain attending specialized pain clinics, yet its prevalence remains unclear. Using screening tools such as the Berlin and STOP-BANG questionnaires may aid in early identification of OSA and improve clinical care. This study i) examined the frequency of OSA based on objective sleep monitoring in patients with high-impact chronic pain, ii) explored potential differences in self-reported pain and sleep characteristics between patients with and without OSA, and iii) tested the agreement between OSA classification based on objective assessment and two OSA screening questionnaires. METHODS: A consecutive cohort of 90 patients (71 women and 19 men; mean age: 47.1 ± 11.0 years) referred for interdisciplinary pain treatment, underwent one night of sleep monitoring using portable respiratory polygraphy (RP), and suspected OSA was confirmed with polysomnography (PSG). Self-reported data on clinical pain (severity, pain drawings and health-related quality of life), sleep characteristics (sleep quality insomnia, sleepiness), and risk of OSA (Berlin and STOP-BANG questionnaires) were collected the day before RP assessment. RESULTS: Forty-six (51.1%) patients were classified with OSA according to RP and verified with PSG. Twenty-eight patients (31.1%) had moderate or severe OSA (apnea-hypopnea index [AHI] >15). Patients with OSA reported lower sleep quality compared with patients without OSA. Scores on pain severity, disability, quality of life, insomnia and sleepiness were comparable between patients with and without OSA. Sensitivity and specificity were 78.6 and 45.2% respectively for the Berlin questionnaire, and 71.4 and 58.1% respectively for the STOP-BANG questionnaire. The agreement for both questionnaires with objective assessment was poor-to-fair. Both questionnaires had acceptable negative predictive values but low positive predictive values reducing the clinical utility to identify patients with low OSA-risk in this sample. CONCLUSIONS: The current study demonstrates a high prevalence of OSA in patients with high-impact chronic pain referred to specialized pain treatment, however the clinical pain profiles were similar in patients with and without OSA. The Berlin and STOP-BANG questionnaires have poor specificity and low-to-fair agreement with RP/PSG questioning their clinical utility in identifying OSA in this sample.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Dennis Boye","Bendix, Laila","Abeler, Karin","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Sprehn, Michael","Bruun, Karin Due","Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","Vaegter, Henrik Bjarke"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-008423"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Vægter, Henrik Bjarke"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Hospital of North Norway"],"keyword":["Berlin","Chronic pain","OSA","STOP BANG","Sleep","respiratory polygraphy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"obstructive sleep apnea is common in patients with high impact chronic pain an exploratory study from an interdisciplinary pain center","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/201015712/10.1515_sjpain_2021_0112.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-008423","identifier":[{"id":"85117488897","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34643073","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-aed2a72e-8085-4cc2-9628-185633f2d965","sdu-ea017e0b-06fc-4778-8551-d015eeec7915"],"keyword":["Berlin","OSA","STOP-BANG","chronic pain","respiratory polygraphy","sleep"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-33896AC882C5B4C8A9A8C1202A84511A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/464098436/sjpain_2021_0112_R1_Version1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/201015712/10.1515_sjpain_2021_0112.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Pain and Motor System Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"university hospital of north norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital of North Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dennis Boye","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5f965a32-ee12-482a-aa54-95086a33ff2c","name":"Larsen, Dennis Boye","orcid":"0000-0002-2844-7408","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Laila","key":"bendixpau","last":"Bendix","locid":"887b9e45-3627-47ff-b83f-7a2facf19317","name":"Bendix, Laila","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"abelerpau","last":"Abeler","name":"Abeler, Karin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Kjær","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"sprehnpau","last":"Sprehn","locid":"99db7f06-a251-4286-9d83-d51aabd62745","name":"Sprehn, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin Due","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"e276834f-a612-4fb4-9c69-87830182729d","name":"Bruun, Karin Due","orcid":"0000-0002-3106-2461","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Rune","key":"blichfeldteckhardtpau","last":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt","locid":"f603c66f-99ca-4f58-984c-8a37cd15773c","name":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","orcid":"0000-0002-7759-5642","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bjarke","key":"vaegterpau","last":"Vaegter","locid":"b35dd901-cb2f-4f50-a2c5-65e1a4752f02","name":"Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","name_org":"Vaegter, Henrik Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0002-7707-9947","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34643073"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/sjpain-2021-0112","issn":["18778860","18778879"],"issn_org":["18778860"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","pages":"106-117","paperid":"A195","publisher":"De Gruyter Mouton","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117488897"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aed2a72e-8085-4cc2-9628-185633f2d965","sdu-ea017e0b-06fc-4778-8551-d015eeec7915"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Obstructive sleep apnea is common in patients with high-impact chronic pain - an exploratory study from an interdisciplinary pain center","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-008423","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Hyperreflective dots are a common but highly variable feature of optical coherence tomography (OCT) scans of the retina. We studied the spatial characteristics and perfusion of hyperreflective dots using both structural and angiographic OCT B-scans of the macula in 16 eyes in 8 healthy subjects and 8 patients with diabetic retinopathy without macular edema. Hyperreflective dots were manually graded in a 1000 µm parafoveal area by number, diameter, location and perfusion status and traced through adjacent B-scans at 11 µm intervals to determine their length. Thereby, this study defined a procedure to identify granular and elongated hyperreflective elements and differentiate between presumably perfused and occluded capillaries. The latter were only found in the diabetic patients. This classification can potentially be automated to non-invasively identify capillary non-perfusion in vivo.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Torm, Marie Elise Wistrup","Sander, Birgit","Hornum, Mads","Krohn, Paul","Birn, Henrik","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-018214"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Torm, Marie Elise Wistrup"],"keyword":["Diabetic retinopathy","Methodological study","Optical coherence tomography","Optical coherence tomography angiography","hyperreflective dots"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of hyperreflective dots by structural and angiographic optical coherence tomography in patients with diabetic retinopathy and healthy subjects","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm11226646","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-018214","identifier":[{"id":"85142607814","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9697733","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36431121","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4c0b7ac7-217f-4167-ae35-2b2d406e27d9","ku-9d483f2f-2012-4b07-ad31-6bf42598ebc4"],"keyword":["diabetic retinopathy","hyperreflective dots","methodological study","optical coherence tomography","optical coherence tomography angiography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3DF4E0D40DB9622B95C241DD7EC3E081"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm11226646","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/335684955/jcm_11_06646_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Syd","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Medicine and Nephrology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Elise Wistrup","key":"tormpau","last":"Torm","locid":"e472be15-14a7-47af-aa7a-d5defd36b422","name":"Torm, Marie Elise Wistrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birgit","key":"sanderpau","last":"Sander","name":"Sander, Birgit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"hornumpau","last":"Hornum","locid":"6e7135d6-13c5-4f40-a3da-e8adf896bc7d","name":"Hornum, Mads","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paul","key":"krohnpau","last":"Krohn","name":"Krohn, Paul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"birnpau","last":"Birn","locid":"1b3c44f6-5d9b-406d-84a3-700b510fb9ff","name":"Birn, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36431121"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/jcm11226646","issn":["20770383"],"issue":"22","journal":"Journal of Clinical Medicine","paperid":"6646","publisher":"MDPI AG","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Medicine","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142607814"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4c0b7ac7-217f-4167-ae35-2b2d406e27d9","ku-9d483f2f-2012-4b07-ad31-6bf42598ebc4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterization of Hyperreflective Dots by Structural and Angiographic Optical Coherence Tomography in Patients with Diabetic Retinopathy and Healthy Subjects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-018214","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Valid and reliable methods for diagnosing depression are essential. The present study aimed to test the performance of a new diagnostic interview for depression focusing on the core symptoms of depression. Method: We developed a diagnostic interview for depression: the CORE Diagnostic Interview, CORE-DI, which assesses each of the core features of depression on the four dimensions: quality, reactivity, globality, and fluctuations over time. The diagnostic performance of this interview was tested in a clinical study including 83 individuals presenting with various depressive symptoms, who were interviewed independently (1) by means of the CORE-DI and the Mini-International Neuropsychiatric Interview (M.I.N.I.), and (2) by highly skilled specialists in depression representing gold standard diagnoses. Results: We compared the outcome of the CORE-DI, the M.I.N.I., and the diagnosis made by clinicians, respectively, versus the gold standard diagnosis, using diagnostic efficiency statistics. The CORE-DI diagnosed depression with a high specificity (0.91, 95% CI: 0.85-0.97, for International Classification of Diseases [ICD]-10 criteria and 0.88, 95% CI: 0.81-0.95, for Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders [DSM-5] criteria) compared to both M.I.N.I (specificity 0.44, 95% CI: 0.33-0.55) and clinical diagnoses (specificity 0.76, 95% CI: 0.67-0.85). The sensitivity of the CORE-DI was 0.61 (95% CI: 0.55-0.72) for ICD-10 criteria and 0.67 (95% CI: 0.57-0.77) for DSM-5 criteria. Discussion/Conclusion: The CORE-DI increased the specificity of the depression diagnosis substantially compared to clinical diagnoses and the diagnoses obtained by M.I.N.I. The results point to the usefulness of an elaborated and systematic assessment of the core symptoms in the examination of patients with depressive symptoms and thereby indicate a way for further development of specific diagnostic tools for depression in both clinical and research settings. However, it should be noted that the sensitivity of the CORE-DI was modest, and the psychometric properties of the CORE-DI might be different in other settings with higher or lower prevalence or severity of depressive symptoms.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bukh, Jens Drachmann","Fabrazzo, Michele","Christensen, Ellen Margrethe","Mikkelsen, Rie Lambæk","Larsen, Jens Knud","Hageman, Ida","Bendsen, Birgitte Bjerg","Bolwig, Tom","Vinberg, Maj","Bech, Per","Dam, Ole Henrik","Maj, Mario","Kessing, Lars Vedel"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-025593"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bukh, Jens Drachmann"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universita della Campania Vanvitelli","University of Campania Luigi Vanvitelli","University of Naples Federico II"],"keyword":["Affective disorders","Diagnostic criteria","Diagnostic systems","Major depression","Psychiatric Diagnoses","Psychopathology","Validity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"at the core of depression a diagnostic interview of the core features of depression","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85126943079","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-025593","identifier":[{"id":"35279664","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85126943079","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000773285900001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-b14218e7-6c79-4aec-b688-fb4e8cd38118","ku-837f3fc5-b277-4eb9-bfd0-51e5e3b907c8"],"keyword":["Affective disorders","Diagnostic criteria","Diagnostic systems","Major depression","Psychiatric diagnoses","Psychopathology","Validity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C6A53C7548D39BDFFF819726EAB871F9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of campania luigi vanvitelli","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Campania Luigi Vanvitelli","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"universita della campania vanvitelli","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universita della Campania Vanvitelli","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Affective Disorders"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university of naples federico ii","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Naples Federico II","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Drachmann","key":"bukhpau","last":"Bukh","locid":"ed84ce10-678e-4b40-9651-982bf9977abc","name":"Bukh, Jens","name_org":"Bukh, Jens Drachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-7815-4806","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"fabrazzopau","last":"Fabrazzo","name":"Fabrazzo, Michele","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ellen Margrethe","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Ellen Margrethe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rie Lambaek","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Rie Lambaek","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Knud","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0540ac4a-edb8-44cc-b58b-42795de7f31a","name":"Larsen, Jens Knud","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ida","key":"hagemanpau","last":"Hageman","name":"Hageman, Ida","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte Bjerg","key":"bendsenpau","last":"Bendsen","name":"Bendsen, Birgitte Bjerg","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tom","key":"bolwigpau","last":"Bolwig","name":"Bolwig, Tom","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maj","key":"vinbergpau","last":"Vinberg","locid":"c42cfaf1-2554-44d1-bb45-c0fccac79e8c","name":"Vinberg, Maj","orcid":"0000-0002-5982-1335","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"bechpau","last":"Bech","name":"Bech, Per","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole Henrik","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","name":"Dam, Ole Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"majpau","last":"Maj","name":"Maj, Mario","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Vedel","key":"kessingpau","last":"Kessing","locid":"93a97a97-e9d8-464b-8eed-1244a0a9ee56","name":"Kessing, Lars Vedel","orcid":"0000-0001-9377-9436","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35279664"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000522505","issn":["02544962","1423033X"],"issn_org":["02544962"],"issue":"3-4","journal":"Psychopathology","pages":"219-225","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Psychopathology","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126943079"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b14218e7-6c79-4aec-b688-fb4e8cd38118","ku-837f3fc5-b277-4eb9-bfd0-51e5e3b907c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"At the Core of Depression : A Diagnostic Interview of the Core Features of Depression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-025593","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose — Data on application of fasttrack/enhanced recovery protocols in revision hip arthroplasty (R-THA) surgery is scarce. We report length of stay (LOS), risk of LOS > 5 days, and readmission ≤ 90 days after revision hip arthroplasty in centers with a well-established fast-track protocol in both primary and revision procedures. Patients and methods — This is an observational cohort study from the Centre for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement and the Danish Hip Arthroplasty Register. Consecutive elective aseptic major component revision hip arthroplasties from 6 dedicated fast-track centers from 2010 to 2018 were included. Results — 1,345 R-THAs were analyzed, including 23% total revisions, 52% acetabular component revisions, and 25% femoral component revisions. Mean age was 70 years (SD 12) and 61% were female. Median LOS was 3 days (interquartile range [IQR] 2–6), decreasing from median 6 (IQR 3–10) days in 2010 to 2 (IQR 1–4) days in 2018. The 90-day readmission rate was 20%, but showed a fluctuating and increasing trend from 13% in 2010 to 28% in 2018. Risk factors for LOS > 5 days and readmission were use of walking aid, preoperative hemoglobin ≤ 13 g/dL, pharmacological treated psychiatric disorder, age ≥ 80 years, age 70–79 years (only LOS > 5 days), cardiac disease (only LOS > 5 days), pulmonary disease (only readmission), BMI ≥ 35 (only LOS > 5 days) and ≥ 1 previous revision (only LOS > 5 days). Interpretation — LOS decreased to median 2 days at the end of the study period, but the 90 days readmission risk remained high (> 20%). Several risk factors for postoperative complications were identified, suggesting that at-risk patients should be treated using an extended fast-track/ enhanced recovery protocol focusing on preoperative optimization and postoperative monitoring as well as surgical techniques to reduce hip dislocations.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Petersen, Pelle Baggesgaard","Corap, Yasemin","Gromov, Kirill","Jørgensen, Christoffer Calov","Kehlet, Henrik","Hansen, Torben Bæk"],"cuid":["S03-098.46-013466"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["Centre for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement Collaborating Group"],"corresponding_author":["Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arthroplasty Replacement Hip adverse effects","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Elective Surgical Procedures","Female","Humans","Length of Stay","Male","Postoperative Complications epidemiology","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast track revision hip arthroplasty a multicenter cohort study on 000000000001 000000000345 elective aseptic major component revision hip arthroplasties","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2022.2196","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.46-013466","identifier":[{"id":"85125156298","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8865005","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35195270","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0bdc16aa-e196-4636-972f-b573882a5871","ku-04010ba9-6d37-495b-bd74-139616236f4f","sdu-de00d2fa-1840-4a53-9c8e-a531290ef290"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Hip/adverse effects","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Elective Surgical Procedures","Female","Humans","Length of Stay","Male","Postoperative Complications/epidemiology","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A854A5E99DC821057510489AC2750F51"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/199914051/document_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2022.2196","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313044742/document_6_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Ortopædkirurgi, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":6,"key":"centre for fast track hip and knee replacement collaborating group","name":"Centre for Fast-track Hip and Knee Replacement Collaborating Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pelle Baggesgaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Pelle Baggesgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yasemin","key":"corappau","last":"Corap","locid":"4bcb60f3-0627-410c-a844-dffc7f7730a2","name":"Corap, Yasemin","orcid":"0000-0003-3690-6157","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","first":"Kirill","key":"gromovpau","last":"Gromov","locid":"efb84811-45bd-4724-97f5-e10d5b84525f","name":"Gromov, Kirill","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christoffer Calov","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Christoffer Calov","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bæk","key":"hansenoth","last":"Hansen","locid":"2a5b433e-710a-4214-a1f5-a6949dfac7bd","name":"Hansen, Torben Bæk","orcid":"0000-0003-1678-3612","rank":7,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["35195270"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/17453674.2022.2196","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"341-347","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125156298"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0bdc16aa-e196-4636-972f-b573882a5871","ku-04010ba9-6d37-495b-bd74-139616236f4f","sdu-de00d2fa-1840-4a53-9c8e-a531290ef290"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Fast-track revision hip arthroplasty : a multicenter cohort study on 1,345 elective aseptic major component revision hip arthroplasties","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.46-013466","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock (AMICS) comprises a heterogeneous population with high mortality. Insight in timing and cause of death may improve understanding of the condition and aid individualization of treatment. This was assessed in a retrospective, multicenter observational cohort study based on 1,716 patients with AMICS treated during the period of 2010 to 2017, of whom 904 died before hospital discharge. Patients with AMICS were identified through national registries and review of individual patients charts. In 904 patients with AMICS who died before hospital discharge (median age 72 years [interquartile range (IQR) 63 to 79], 70% men), 342 (38%) had suffered out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. The most frequent cause of death was primary cardiac (54%), whereas 24% died of neurologic injury, and 20% of multiorgan failure (MOF). Time to death was 13 hours (IQR 5 to 43) for heart failure; 140 hours (IQR 95 to 209) in neurologic injury; and 137 hours (IQR 59 to 321) in MOF, p <0.001. The causes of death in patients presenting with out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) were: neurologic injury in 57%, as opposed to 4% in patients not presenting with OHCA, p <0.001. In conclusion, in patients with AMICS, cause of death was mainly primary heart failure followed by neurologic injury and MOF. Median time from first medical contact to death was only 13 hours in patients dying from cardiac causes. The risk of dying of neurologic injury was low in patients without OHCA.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Davodian, Lise W","Larsen, Jeppe K P","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Josiassen, Jakob","Helgestad, Ole K L","Udesen, Nanna L J","Hassager, Christian","Schmidt, Henrik","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Holmvang, Lene","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob E"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-021164"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Møller, Jacob E","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"keyword":["Aged","Cause of Death","Cohort Studies","Female","Heart Failure complications","Humans","Male","Myocardial Infarction","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest complications","Retrospective Studies","Shock Cardiogenic therapy","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"timing and causes of death in acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock from the retroshock cohort","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjcard.2022.01.050","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was supported by the Danish Heart Foundation (Benhavn, Denmark), Abiomed (Danvers, Massachusetts), Odense University Hospital (Odense, Denmark) and Rigshospitalets Research Council (Copenhagen, Denmark). Dr. Hassager reports receiving speakers fees from Abiomed. Dr. Henrik Schmidt reports receiving speakers fees from Orion. Drs. Kjaergaard and Holmvang report receiving speakers fees from Abbott, Bayer, and Boston Scientific. Dr. Ravn reports receiving an advisory board fee from Sedana Medical AB. Dr. Møller reports receiving a speakers fee from Abiomed, Orion, Novartis, Abbott, the advisory board of Boehringer Ingelheim (Ingelheim, Denmark), and a research grant from Abiomed. The remaining authors have no conflicts of interest to declare."],"id":"S03-100.00-021164","identifier":[{"id":"85126070413","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35279275","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7436e4de-aa0b-46ed-9542-ced605f9e11c","ku-48a0621f-8d35-4