ng","locid":"7766931c-a3c9-4a38-9d22-e4cc3a2f4607","name":"Kronvang, Brian","orcid":"0000-0003-1165-1354","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"windolfpau","last":"Windolf","locid":"04de6e58-b8ca-4a60-95e7-849dde928efb","name":"Windolf, Jørgen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sofie Gyritia Madsen","key":"vantveenpau","last":"van't Veen","locid":"5b3d9551-ce36-44b1-b7a4-233eb2a38a76","name":"van't Veen, Sofie Gyritia Madsen","orcid":"0000-0003-0867-044X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bering","key":"ovesenpau","last":"Ovesen","locid":"62cfa396-63d2-45a1-b33a-14529d575319","name":"Ovesen, Niels Bering","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"tornbjergpau","last":"Tornbjerg","locid":"673f9989-b651-4f14-8190-b60c45f9cde2","name":"Tornbjerg, Henrik","orcid":"0009-0008-7385-7490","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"thodsenpau","last":"Thodsen","locid":"32bff5cf-3478-427f-a25a-edc45f21b300","name":"Thodsen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0002-6542-4934","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"blichermathiesenpau","last":"Blicher-Mathiesen","locid":"c1194af9-f1ac-4cdb-9312-8696066200b9","name":"Blicher-Mathiesen, Gitte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d7e7c51c-9337-47ca-bf2e-cd18827492ba"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pitfalls and new solutions in water quantity and quality monitoring","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-252615","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Listening programs enable hearing aid (HA) users to change device settings for specific listening situations and thereby personalize their listening experience. However, investigations into real-world use of such listening programs to support clinical decisions and evaluate the success of HA treatment are lacking. OBJECTIVE: We aimed to investigate the provision of listening programs among a large group of in-market HA users and the context in which the programs are typically used. METHODS: First, we analyzed how many and which programs were provided to 32,336 in-market HA users. Second, we explored 332,271 program selections from 1312 selected users to investigate the sound environments in which specific programs were used and whether such environments reflect the listening intent conveyed by the name of the used program. Our analysis was based on real-world longitudinal data logged by smartphone-connected HAs. RESULTS: In our sample, 57.71% (18,663/32,336) of the HA users had programs for specific listening situations, which is a higher proportion than previously reported, most likely because of the inclusion criteria. On the basis of association rule mining, we identified a primary additional listening program, Speech in Noise, which is frequent among users and often provided when other additional programs are also provided. We also identified 2 secondary additional programs (Comfort and Music), which are frequent among users who get ≥3 programs and usually provided in combination with Speech in Noise. In addition, 2 programs (TV and Remote Mic) were related to the use of external accessories and not found to be associated with other programs. On average, users selected Speech in Noise, Comfort, and Music in louder, noisier, and less-modulated (all P<.01) environments compared with the environment in which they selected the default program, General. The difference from the sound environment in which they selected General was significantly larger in the minutes following program selection than in the minutes preceding it. CONCLUSIONS: This study provides a deeper insight into the provision of listening programs on a large scale and demonstrates that additional listening programs are used as intended and according to the sound environment conveyed by the program name.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pasta, Alessandro","Szatmari, Tiberiu-Ioan","Christensen, Jeppe Høy","Jensen, Kasper","Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik","Sun, Kang","Larsen, Jakob Eg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367930"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data logging","Hearing aids","Mobile phone","Personalized medicine","Sound environment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating the provision and context of use of hearing aid listening programs from real world data observational study","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/36671","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367930","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9623464","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36251349","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85140271612","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d406c3aa-4d2b-444e-8189-6cdffba91600"],"keyword":["Data logging","Hearing aids","Listening programs","Mobile phone","Personalized medicine","Sound environment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D3FEC32EA65189BF90BD71742E575689"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/36671","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/293936884/Pasta2022_Investigating_the_Provision_and_Context_of_Use_of_Hearing_Aid_Listening_Programs_From_Real_world_Data_Observational_Study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling, Cognitive Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mathematics, Dynamical systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"oticon","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTI","l3nl":"Oticon A/S","l3nn":"Oticon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oticon","namevar":["Oticon Danmark AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"pastapau","last":"Pasta","locid":"f53ef5d5-4a76-451c-8109-212c835a8f52","name":"Pasta, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0002-9920-6695","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tiberiu Ioan","key":"szatmaripau","last":"Szatmari","locid":"18a19e5f-a6a9-4ea3-b1a6-eecccdd48352","name":"Szatmari, Tiberiu-Ioan","name_org":"Szatmari, Tiberiu Ioan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Høy","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jeppe Høy","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper Juul","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"10b478d2-812b-4196-8c79-c614e2423214","name":"Jensen, Kasper","name_org":"Jensen, Kasper Juul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"pontoppidanpau","last":"Pontoppidan","name":"Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kang","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Kang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Eg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"691c8ae7-9a21-4b98-9b91-5e2d9806a4b9","name":"Larsen, Jakob Eg","orcid":"0000-0002-7461-9901","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36251349"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/36671","issn":["14388871","14394456"],"issn_org":["14394456"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","paperid":"e36671","publisher":"JMIR Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140271612"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Oticon A/S","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d406c3aa-4d2b-444e-8189-6cdffba91600"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Investigating the Provision and Context of Use of Hearing Aid Listening Programs From Real-world Data : Observational Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367930","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The study aims to investigate the effect of stapedotomy on audiology measurements and the disease-specific health-related quality of life for patients with otosclerosis using the Danish Stapesplasty Outcome Test-25 as a quality of life measuring tool. METHODS: In this study, 50 patients who had undergone stapedotomy at our department between September 2017 and December 2020 were included. Data collection was performed by audiometric testing (pure tone and speech audiometry) in the pre-and postoperative settings. Health-related quality of life was assessed pre-and postoperatively in 30 patients using the validated Danish Stapesplasty Outcome Test-25. RESULTS: The mean improvement in air conduction thresholds was 27.7 dB and the mean improvement in air-bone gap was 21.8 dB. Health-related quality of life improved significantly after stapes surgery in all subscores of the Stapesplasty Outcome Test-25 (hearing, mental condition, social restriction, and general), except for “tinnitus.” The improvement in the audiometric data correlated significantly with the improvement in “total score” and “hearing function” but not with “tinnitus,” “social restrictions,” and “mental condition.” CONCLUSION: Stapedotomy leads to significant improvement in hearing and health-related quality of life. The Stapesplasty Outcome Test-25 can be used as a valuable supplement to the hearing test by assessing health-related quality of life.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Mascha","Jensen, Mads Mose","Larsen, Kasper Daugaard","Glad, Henrik","Djurhuus, Bjarki Ditlev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-445809"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Health related quality of life","Otosclerosis","Stapedotomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hearing and disease specific health related quality of life in patients with otosclerosis after stapedotomy a trial of the spot 000000000025 questionnaire","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5152/iao.2022.21479","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-445809","identifier":[{"id":"85134187554","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35894528","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9404310","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-5796ba3d-4602-4026-bd72-bc8cd33bf56e"],"keyword":["Otosclerosis","health-related quality of life","stapedotomy","stapesplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-74EBA120BB72442E2611004787BF45A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5152/iao.2022.21479","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/329570169/Hearing_and_Disease_Specific_Health_Related_Quality.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mascha","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Mascha","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Mose","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Mads Mose","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper Daugaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Kasper Daugaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Henrik","key":"gladpau","last":"Glad","locid":"f2b17ce6-21a5-4377-a125-604c81048ae6","name":"Glad, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Bjarki","key":"djurhuuspau","last":"Djurhuus","locid":"fe999875-a944-44dc-b424-741ba985c2d1","name":"Djurhuus, Bjarki Ditlev","name_org":"Djurhuus, Bjarki","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35894528"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5152/iao.2022.21479","issn":["13087649","21483817"],"issn_org":["13087649"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of International Advanced Otology","pages":"320-326","status":"p","title":"Journal of International Advanced Otology","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134187554"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5796ba3d-4602-4026-bd72-bc8cd33bf56e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hearing and Disease-Specific Health-Related Quality of Life in Patients with Otosclerosis after Stapedotomy-a Trial of the SPOT-25 Questionnaire","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-445809","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"As an example of socio-spatial theorization within the Nordic context, this chapter is written as an autobiographic narrative of my intellectual development from the 1970s to 2021. It is a story involving a steady positioning in the ‘Nordic’ context, but within that a range of shifts in affiliations, as well as a participation in different intellectual networks – both Danish, Nordic and ‘International’ – all of which have influenced my thinking. The chapter is arranged in four parts: First, a presentation of some Nordic predecessors. This is followed by an intellectual history of what I call theoretical approximations to (a) a non-deterministic social ecology, (b) towards a theory of practice, and (c) an engagement with the formulation of a critical phenomenology – all involving issues of the urban question, of everyday life and of modalities of social space.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Simonsen, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557444"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urban space and everyday life a personal theoretical trajectory within nordic social and cultural geography","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-04234-8_15","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-557444","identifier":[{"id":"85134666670","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-15be971a-4bc9-4631-8410-74663a6ffe08"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-75F9007B3D07017EDF86861D0990AC93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-04234-8_15","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-04234-8_15","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/81983646/Urban_Space_and_Everyday_Life._A_Personal_Theoretical_Trajectory_Within_Nordic_Social_and_Cultural_Geography.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Mobility, Space, Place and Urban Studies (MOSPUS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"8192c072-d234-40d8-a980-ea71f9f76ab6","name":"Simonsen, Kirsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Jakobsen","key":"nolastnamepedh","last":"no-lastname","name":"no-lastname, Peter Jakobsen","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik","key":"jönssonpedh","last":"Jönsson","name":"Jönsson, Erik","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"gutzonlarsenpedh","last":"Gutzon Larsen","name":"Gutzon Larsen, Henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-04234-8_15","eisbn":["9783031042348"],"isbn":["9783031042331"],"pages":"253-271","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Intellectual Histories and Critical Interventions","title":"Socio-Spatial Theory in Nordic Geography"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134666670"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-15be971a-4bc9-4631-8410-74663a6ffe08"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Urban Space and everyday life: : A Personal Theoretical Trajectory Within Nordic Social and Cultural Geography","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-557444","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The paper presents a critical and comprehensive analysis of recent developments, trends and challenges of Flexible Query Answering Systems (FQASs). Flexible query answering is a multidisciplinary research field at the crossroad of several disciplines among which Information Retrieval (IR), databases, knowledge based systems, Natural Language Processing (NLP) and the semantic web, which aims to provide powerful means and techniques for better reflecting human preferences and intentions to retrieve relevant information. The analysis follows the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analysis (PRISMA) guidelines characterized by a top-down process, starting with relevant keywords for the topic of interest to retrieve relevant articles from meta-sources, and complementing them with relevant articles from seed sources identified by a bottom-up process. To mine the retrieved publication data a network analysis is performed which allows to present in a synthetic way intrinsic topics of publications by revealing aspects of interest. Issues dealt with are related to both query answering methods, both model-based and data-driven, the latter based on Machine Learning, and to their needs for explainability and fairness, and big data, notably by taking into account data veracity. Conclusions point out trends and challenges to help better shaping the future of the FQAS field.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andreasen, Troels","Bordogna, Gloria","De Tré, Guy","Kacprzyk, Janusz","Larsen, Henrik Legind","Zadrozny, Slawomir"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-565414"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Italy","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ghent University","National Research Council of Italy","Polish Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Legind Technologies"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the power and potentials of flexible query answering systems a critical and comprehensive analysis","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/86348045/Preprint_The_Power_and_Potentials_of_Flexible_Query_Answering_Systems_A_Critical_and_Comprehensive_Analysis.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-565414","ids":["ruc-8c1042ae-03c0-4055-b247-14b0fddd1497"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2832C8D15EE378A89E0C28DA998C84C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4292638","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/86348045/Preprint_The_Power_and_Potentials_of_Flexible_Query_Answering_Systems_A_Critical_and_Comprehensive_Analysis.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"ghent university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pl","key":"polish academy of sciences","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polish Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Legind Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"f31701bc-1bef-45ac-b9fa-3e931672bcd4","name":"Andreasen, Troels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gloria","key":"bordognapau","last":"Bordogna","name":"Bordogna, Gloria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Guy","key":"detrépau","last":"De Tré","name":"De Tré, Guy","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Janusz","key":"kacprzykpau","last":"Kacprzyk","name":"Kacprzyk, Janusz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Henrik Legind","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik Legind","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Slawomir","key":"zadroznypau","last":"Zadrozny","name":"Zadrozny, Slawomir","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"48","publisher":"SSRN","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-8c1042ae-03c0-4055-b247-14b0fddd1497"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The Power and Potentials of Flexible Query Answering Systems : A Critical and Comprehensive Analysis","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-565414","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Estimates of the severity of the emerging Omicron variant are critical to assess the public health impact associated with its rapid global dissemination. We estimated the risk of SARS-CoV-2-related hospitalisations after infection with Omicron compared with Delta in Denmark, a country with high mRNA vaccination coverage and an extensive free-of-charge PCR test capacity. Methods: Observational cohort study of all RT-PCR SARS-CoV-2 positive individuals in Denmark between 21 November and 19 December, 2021, the period Omicron emerged while Delta was still dominant. Individuals were identified in the national COVID-19 surveillance system database which include results of a variant specific RT- PCR detecting Omicron cases, SARS-CoV-2 related hospitalisations (primary outcome of the study). The risk ratio (RR) of hospitalisation after infection with Omicron compared with Delta, overall and stratified by vaccination status, was calculated in a Poisson regression model with robust standard errors, adjusted à priori for reinfection status, sex, age, region, comorbidities, and period. Findings: Among the 188,980 SARS-CoV-2 infected individuals, 38,669 (20.1%) were Omicron vPCR positive. SARS-CoV-2 related hospitalisations and Omicron cases increased during the study period. Overall, 124,313 (65.8 %) were vaccinated and vaccination was associated with a lower risk of hospitalisation (adjusted RR 0.24, 95%CI 0.22-0.26), compared with cases with no or one vaccination. Compared with Delta infection, Omicron was associated with an adjusted RR of hospitalisation of 0.64 (95%CI 0.56-0.75; 222 Omicron and 2,213 Delta hospitalisations). For the similar comparison by vaccination status, the RR of hospitalisation was 0.57 (95%CI 0.44- 0.75) among cases with no or one vaccination, 0.71 (95%CI 0.60-0.86) among two- dose vaccinated, and 0.50 (95%CI 0.32-0.76) among three-dose vaccinated. Interpretation: We found a significantly lower risk of hospitalisation with Omicron infection compared with Delta among both vaccinated and unvaccinated individuals, suggesting an inherent reduced severity of Omicron. Our results can guide modelling of the impact of the ongoing global Omicron wave and thus health care system preparedness.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Bager, Peter","Wohlfahrt, Jan","Bhatt, Samir","Edslev, Sofie Marie","Sieber, Raphael Niklaus","Ingham, Anna Cäcilia","Stegger, Marc","Legarth, Rebecca","Møller, Camilla Holten","Skov, Robert Leo","Valentiner-Branth, Palle","Overvad, Maria","Agermose Gram, Mie","Kristensen Lomholt, Frederikke","Hallundbæk, Louise","Hjorth Espensen, Caroline","Gubbels, Sophie","Voldstedlund, Marianne","Karakis, Marianne","Lauenborg Møller, Karina","Schytte Olsen, Stefan","K. Fischer, Thea","Barrella Harboe, Zitta","Klint Johannesen, Caroline","van Wijhe, Maarten","Gitz Holler, Jon","Simonsen, Lone","Benny Christian Dessau, Ram","Barfred Friis, Martin","Fuglsang-Damgaard, David","Pinholt, Mette","Søren Kirkby, Nikolai","Kragh Thomsen, Marianne","Vognbjerg Sydenham, Thomas","Eugenio Coia, John","Sofie Marmolin, Ea","Fomsgaard, Anders","Fonager, Jannik","Rasmussen, Morten","Spiess, Katja","Marving, Ellinor","Cohen, Arieh","Balle Larsen, Nicolai","Lillebaek, Troels","Ullum, Henrik","Mølbak, Kåre","Grove Krause, Tyra"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-565799"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"re