{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To develop a coil-based method to obtain accurate sensitivity profiles in 13 C MRI at 3T from the endogenous 23 Na. An eight-channel array is designed for 13 C MR acquisitions. As application examples, the array is used for two-fold accelerated acquisitions of both hyperpolarized 13 C metabolic imaging of pig kidneys and the human brain. METHODS: A flexible coil array was tuned optimally for 13 C at 3T (32.1 MHz), with the coil coupling coefficients matched to be nearly identical at the resonance frequency of 23 Na (33.8 MHz). This is done by enforcing a high decoupling (obtained through highly mismatched preamplifiers) and adjusting the coupling frequency response. The SNR performance is compared to reference coils. RESULTS: The measured sensitivity profiles on a phantom showed high spatial similarity for 13 C and 23 Na resonances, with average noise correlation of 9 and 11%, respectively. For acceleration factors 2, 3, and 4, the obtained maximum g-factors were 1.0, 1.1, and 2.6, respectively. The 23 Na profiles obtained in vivo could be used successfully to perform two-fold acceleration of hyperpolarized 13 C 3D acquisitions of both pig kidneys and a healthy human brain. CONCLUSION: A receive array has been developed in such a way that the 13 C sensitivity profiles could be accurately obtained from measurements at the 23 Na frequency. This technique facilitates accelerated acquisitions for hyperpolarized 13 C imaging. The SNR performance obtained at the 13 C frequency, compares well to other state-of-the-art coils for the same purpose, showing slightly better superficial and central SNR.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Sanchez-Heredia, Juan D","Olin, Rie B","Grist, James T","Wang, Wenjun","Bøgh, Nikolaj","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Schulte, Rolf F","Tyler, Damian","Laustsen, Christoffer","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan H"],"cuid":["S02-096.80-013780"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan H","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","University of Birmingham","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Hyperpolarization","MRSI","Parallel imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rf coil design for accurate parallel imaging on sup 000000000013 sup c mrsi using sup 000000000023 sup na sensitivity profiles","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29259","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work has been partly funded by the Danish Council for Independent Research (DFF – 4005‐00531), the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF124), Lundbeck Foundation (R272‐2017‐4023 & R278‐2018‐620), and the European Research Council (ERC‐856432, HyperQ). Dr. James Grist was funded by the Oxford BHF Centre of Research Excellence by grant code (RE/18/3/34214), and by a European Commission grant (858 149, AlternativesToGd). Prof. Damian Tyler was funded by a British Heart Foundation Senior Research Fellowship (FS/19/18/34252). British Heart Foundation, Grant/Award Number: FS/19/18/34252; Danish Council for Independent Research, Grant/Award Number: DFF ‐ 4005‐00531; Danish National Research Foundation, Grant/Award Number: DNRF124; European Comission, Grant/Award Number: 858149; H2020 European Research Council, Grant/Award Number: 856432; Lundbeckfonden, Grant/Award Numbers: R272‐2017‐4023; R278‐2018‐620; Oxford BHF Centre of Research Excellence, Grant/Award Number: RE/18/3/34214 Funding information"],"id":"S02-096.80-013780","identifier":[{"id":"85130968472","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35635156","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9328386","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000802165100001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-105be123-39d7-4dce-9ec3-9ace75a2b5cd","dtu-f75032b8-323e-44b5-b5d3-b2507fa51795"],"keyword":["Hyperpolarization","MRSI","Parallel Imaging","X-Nuclei MRI","flexible RF coil"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-584FF877B8522EFF7BE6CFD1AF75E753"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9328386/pdf/MRM-88-1391.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29259","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/290549928/Magnetic_Resonance_in_Med_2022_Sanchez_Heredia_RF_coil_design_for_accurate_parallel_imaging_on_13C_MRSI_using_23Na.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","lo