{"abstract":"Hvor stærkt står HR-fagområdet lige nu i forhold til at imødekomme fremtidens udfordringer? Og hvor gode er vi egentlig i HR til at omstille os til nye krav og muligheder? Som optakt til årets HR-konference CRANET 2022 tager vi i denne podcast pulsen på HR i Danmark. I podcastafsnittet bliver der bl.a. diskuteret sexchikane, omstilling i forbindelse med Corona og bæredygtig ledelse. Derudover fortæller Alice Larsen om sin erfaring fra praksis og opfordrer til modige og årvågne HR-medarbejdere, som formår at holde fokus og understøtte virksomhedsstrategien.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik","Larsen, Alice","Beck Petersen, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-289198"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["NOCA - Network of Corporate Academies"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hr i fokus del 000000000001 hvordan står det til med hr feltet i danmark cbs executive talks","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/hr-i-fokus-del-1-hvordan-st%C3%A5r-det-til-med-hr-feltet-i-danmark/id1570444522?i=1000548931646","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-289198","ids":["cbs-91697145-4ea6-44df-b0c7-5416840ecfcc"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-464A704A8F786C720FCB586F1BDFEC73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/hr-i-fokus-del-1-hvordan-st%C3%A5r-det-til-med-hr-feltet-i-danmark/id1570444522?i=1000548931646","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Chr. Hansen A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["NOCA - Network of Corporate Academies"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Alice","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"beckpetersenppu","last":"Beck Petersen","name":"Beck Petersen, Maria","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"CBS Executive","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-91697145-4ea6-44df-b0c7-5416840ecfcc"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"HR i fokus del 1. Hvordan står det til med HR-feltet i Danmark? : CBS Executive Talks","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-289198","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Polarisation transfer schemes and indirect detection are central to magnetic resonance. Using the trityl radical OX063 and a pulse electron paramagnetic resonance spectrometer operating in the Q-band (35 GHz, 1.2 T), we show here that it is possible to use pulsed dynamic nuclear polarisation (DNP) to transfer polarisation from electrons to protons and back. The latter is achieved by first saturating the electrons and then simply using a reverse DNP step. A variable mixing time between DNP and reverse DNP allows us to investigate the decay of polarisation on protons in the vicinity of the electrons. We qualitatively investigate the influence of solvent deuteration, temperature, and electron concentration. We expect reverse DNP to be useful in the investigation of nuclear spin diffusion and envisage its use in electron-nuclear double-resonance (ENDOR) experiments.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wili, Nino","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Jeschke, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-376693"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wili, Nino"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reverse dynamic nuclear polarisation for indirect detection of nuclear spins close to unpaired electrons","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/mr-3-161-2022","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Financial support. This research has been supported by the Eid-genössische Technische Hochschule Zürich (grant no. ETH-48 16-1)."],"id":"S01-000.00-376693","identifier":[{"id":"85136931866","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f0f77929-085b-4375-ace3-4a805d164b69"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A471BACCDD0DC353A7F49770F54B15B2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/290175015/mr_3_161_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/mr-3-161-2022","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nino","key":"wilipau","last":"Wili","name":"Wili, Nino","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar","key":"jeschkepau","last":"Jeschke","name":"Jeschke, Gunnar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/mr-3-161-2022","issn":["26990016"],"issue":"2","journal":"Magnetic Resonance","pages":"161-168","publisher":"Copernicus Publications","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136931866"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f0f77929-085b-4375-ace3-4a805d164b69"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Reverse dynamic nuclear polarisation for indirect detection of nuclear spins close to unpaired electrons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-376693","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: The present case contributes to the limited literature on central nervous system involvement of blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm (BPDCN). Case presentation : A 63-year-old male presented to the department of neurology with a three-day history of rapidly progressing headache, fatigue, and confusion. Physical examination revealed multiple bruise-like skin lesions. Initial laboratory workup raised suspicion of acute leukemia, and a brain computer tomography identified several hyperdense processes. A bone marrow biopsy gave the diagnosis BPDCN, a rare and aggressive hematologic malignancy derived from plasmacytoid dendritic cells with a poor prognosis. Lumbar puncture showed not only signs of BPDCN, but also cerebral toxoplasmosis, thus providing a differential diagnosis. Despite intensive systemic and intrathecal chemotherapy, the patient died 25 days later due to multi-organ failure. Discussion: The exact incidence of BPDCN is unknown and perhaps underestimated but may account for 0.5 – 1% of all hematological malignancies. The median age at onset is 60 to 70 years, and most patients are men. Cutaneous lesions are the most frequent clinical manifestation at diagnosis. Other symptoms present at time of diagnosis or during disease progression include lymphadenopathy, splenomegaly and cytopenia caused by bone marrow involvement. Although the majority of BPDCN patients have no symptoms or signs of central nervous system involvement, plasmacytoid dendritic cells have been detected in the cerebrospinal fluid in more than 50%. Conclusions: This case highlights the importance of considering hematological malignancies as a differential diagnosis in patients developing acute neurological symptoms and raises suspicion of a possible association between toxoplasmosis and hematological malignancies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Florescu, Anna Maria","Sørensen, Anne Louise Tølbøll","Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","Tolnai, Daniel","Sjö, Lene Dissing","Larsen, Katja Lohmann","Al-Karagholi, Mohammad Al-Mahdi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-393642"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute leukemia","Cerebral toxoplasmosis","Confusion","Headache","Hematologic malignancy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm and cerebral toxoplasmosis a case report","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12883-022-02748-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-393642","identifier":[{"id":"35751052","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9229753","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85132892857","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0048aed7-50fa-4759-a5c5-6c41e1ce1b77"],"keyword":["Acute Leukemia","Cerebral toxoplasmosis","Confusion","Headache","Hematologic malignancy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4DF594D6774B4169909F2696A6B214B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321479376/s12883_022_02748_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12883-022-02748-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Maria","key":"florescupau","last":"Florescu","name":"Florescu, Anna Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Louise Tølbøll","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Anne Louise Tølbøll","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik Vedel","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel","key":"tolnaipau","last":"Tolnai","name":"Tolnai, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lene Dissing","key":"sjöpau","last":"Sjö","locid":"5f179427-1ae6-4519-a858-32ca986f7db8","name":"Sjö, Lene Dissing","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katja Lohmann","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Katja Lohmann","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mohammad Al-Mahdi","key":"alkaragholipau","last":"Al-Karagholi","name":"Al-Karagholi, Mohammad Al-Mahdi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35751052"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12883-022-02748-5","issn":["14712377"],"journal":"BMC Neurology","paperid":"233","status":"p","title":"BMC Neurology","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132892857"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0048aed7-50fa-4759-a5c5-6c41e1ce1b77"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm and cerebral toxoplasmosis : a case report","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-393642","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To compare retinal function assessed by full-field electroretinography (ffERG) and multifocal electroretinography (mfERG) in diabetes without retinopathy, diabetes with moderate non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy (NPDR) and in the absence of diabetes. Methods: Scotopic and photopic ffERG and mfERG was made in non-fasting volunteers, including 26 diabetic participants without retinopathy, 22 diabetic participants with moderate NPDR and 22 participants without diabetes using full International Society for Clinical Electrophysiology of Vision protocols. Results: Of the ffERG responses, significant deviation (p ≤ 0.05, corrected for multiple sampling and other relevant confounders) from the non-diabetic participants was seen in the diabetic participants only for the OP1-OP3 oscillatory amplitudes and the OP2 implicit time. This finding was independent of whether retinopathy was present or not. For the mfERG, minor amplitude or implicit time deviations were found for a small number of rings (R2, R4 and R5). Receiver of operating characteristic analysis showed that the single most prominent abnormality of the ffERG in diabetes, regardless of whether retinopathy was present or not, was the OP2 implicit time (area under the curve ≥ 0.80). Conclusion: This bi-modal study of electroretinographic characteristics found that the most prominent anomaly associated with diabetes was a prolongation of the implicit time of the OP2 of the scotopic ffERG, while the most prominent added effect of non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy was a further prolongation of the OP2 implicit time. Although the variation in ERG characteristics is far too large for diagnostic purposes, the close association of the oscillatory potentials with the amacrine cells of the retina indicate that their function is particularly sensitive to diabetes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ba-Ali, Shakoor","Larsen, Michael","Andersen, Henrik Ullits","Lund-Andersen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394639"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diabetic retinopathy","ERG","Multifocal ERG","cones"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"full field and multifocal electroretinogram in non diabetic controls and diabetics with and without retinopathy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.15184","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394639","identifier":[{"id":"35661609","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85131151292","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9795888","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-01ed229e-5568-4802-8941-aa1e78c5ee00"],"keyword":["ERG","cones","diabetic retinopathy","full-field ERG","multifocal ERG","rods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59897B9EE9B7ADDDF2380D8BB101B420"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/334007403/Acta_Ophthalmologica_2022_Ba_Ali_Full_field_and_multifocal_electroretinogram_in_non_diabetic_controls_and_diabetics.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.15184","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Shakoor","key":"baalipau","last":"Ba-Ali","name":"Ba-Ali, Shakoor","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Henrik Ullits","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Henrik Ullits","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35661609"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.15184","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"100"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131151292"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-01ed229e-5568-4802-8941-aa1e78c5ee00"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Full-field and multifocal electroretinogram in non-diabetic controls and diabetics with and without retinopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394639","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Atrial fibrillation (AF) management in primary care often requires a referral to cardiology clinics, which can be strenuous for frail patients. We developed \"cardio-share\" (CS), a new cross-sector collaboration model, to ease this process. General practitioners (GPs) can use a compact Holter monitor (C3 from Cortrium) to receive remote advice from the cardiologist. Objective: To test the feasibility and acceptability of the CS model to manage suspected AF in frail elderly patients. Methods: We used a mixed methods design, including the preparation of qualitative semistructured interviews of GPs and nurses. Results: Between MAR-2019 and FEB-2020, 54 patients were consulted through the CS model, of whom 35 underwent C3 Holter monitoring. The time from referral to a final Holter report was shortened from a mean (SD) of 117 (45) days in usual care to 30 days (13) with the CS model. Furthermore, 90% of the patients did not need to attend visits at the cardiology clinic. The GPs and nurses highlighted the ease of using the C3 monitor. Their perception was that patients were confident in the GPs' collaboration with cardiologists. Conclusions: The CS model using a C3 monitor for AF is both feasible and seems acceptable to GPs. The elapsed time from referral to the Holter report performed for the diagnosis was significantly reduced.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Ladegaard, Caroline Thorup","Bamberg, Carsten","Aalling, Mathias","Jensen, Dorthea Marie","Kamstrup-Larsen, Nina","Madsen, Christoffer Valdorff","Kamil, Sadaf","Gudbergsen, Henrik","Saxild, Thomas","Schiotz, Michaela Louise","Grew, Julie","Castillo, Luana Sandoval","Frolich, Anne","Dominguez, Helena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-436085"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aortic valve replacement","Atrial fibrillation","Community","Cross sector collaboration","Health professionals","Qualitative content analysis","Risk","Stroke","Surgery","Warfarin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["VihTek Res Ctr Welf Technol Reg"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reaching frail elderly patients to optimize diagnosis and management of atrial fibrillation reafel a feasibility study of a cross sectoral shared care model","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19127383","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-436085","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9223795","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000816146900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35742632","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85132014305","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-47745cf9-545b-4770-a5a9-d4975d956caf"],"keyword":["AORTIC-VALVE-REPLACEMENT","COMMUNITY","QUALITATIVE CONTENT-ANALYSIS","RISK","STROKE","SURGERY","WARFARIN","atrial fibrillation","cross-sector collaboration","frail elderly patients","health professionals","sensor Holter monitoring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E45DAD1E6923101730551C6D0F0F9423"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19127383","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/312466071/Reaching.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["VihTek Res Ctr Welf Technol Reg"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline Thorup","key":"ladegaardpau","last":"Ladegaard","name":"Ladegaard, Caroline Thorup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"bambergpau","last":"Bamberg","name":"Bamberg, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mathias","key":"aallingpau","last":"Aalling","name":"Aalling, Mathias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dorthea Marie","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Dorthea Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Nina","key":"kamstruplarsenpau","last":"Kamstrup-Larsen","locid":"f6ea5afe-b591-447e-a6f7-26d177e74d46","name":"Kamstrup-Larsen, Nina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer Valdorff","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Christoffer Valdorff","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sadaf","key":"kamilpau","last":"Kamil","name":"Kamil, Sadaf","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"gudbergsenpau","last":"Gudbergsen","name":"Gudbergsen, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"saxildpau","last":"Saxild","name":"Saxild, Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michaela Louise","key":"schiotzpau","last":"Schiotz","name":"Schiotz, Michaela Louise","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie","key":"grewpau","last":"Grew","name":"Grew, Julie","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Luana Sandoval","key":"castillopau","last":"Castillo","name":"Castillo, Luana Sandoval","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Anne","key":"frolichpau","last":"Frolich","name":"Frolich, Anne","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Helena","key":"dominguezpau","last":"Dominguez","locid":"70411448-5bf8-4954-84c6-5512cb480021","name":"Dominguez, Helena","orcid":"0000-0002-7089-2636","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35742632"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijerph19127383","issn":["16604601","16617827"],"issn_org":["16617827"],"issue":"12","journal":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","paperid":"7383","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132014305"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-47745cf9-545b-4770-a5a9-d4975d956caf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reaching Frail Elderly Patients to Optimize Diagnosis and Management of Atrial Fibrillation (REAFEL) : A Feasibility Study of a Cross-Sectoral Shared-Care Model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-436085","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Both amino acid positron emission tomography (PET) and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) blood volume (BV) measurements are used in suspected recurrent high-grade gliomas. We compared the separate and combined diagnostic yield of simultaneously acquired dynamic contrast-enhanced (DCE) perfusion MRI and O-(2-[18F]-fluoroethyl)-L-tyrosine ([18F]FET) PET in patients with anaplastic astrocytoma and glioblastoma following standard therapy. Methods: A total of 76 lesions in 60 hybrid [18F]FET PET/MRI scans with DCE MRI from patients with suspected recurrence of anaplastic astrocytoma and glioblastoma were included retrospectively. BV was measured from DCE MRI employing a 2-compartment exchange model (2CXM). Diagnostic performances of maximal tumour-to-background [18F]FET uptake (TBRmax), maximal BV (BVmax) and normalised BVmax (nBVmax) were determined by ROC analysis using 6-month histopathological (n = 28) or clinical/radiographical follow-up (n = 48) as reference. Sensitivity and specificity at optimal cut-offs were determined separately for enhancing and non-enhancing lesions. Results: In progressive lesions, all BV and [18F]FET metrics were higher than in non-progressive lesions. ROC analyses showed higher overall ROC AUCs for TBRmax than both BVmax and nBVmax in both lesion-wise (all lesions, p = 0.04) and in patient-wise analysis (p < 0.01). Combining TBRmax with BV metrics did not increase ROC AUC. Lesion-wise positive fraction/sensitivity/specificity at optimal cut-offs were 55%/91%/84% for TBRmax, 45%/77%/84% for BVmax and 59%/84%/72% for nBVmax. Combining TBRmax and best-performing BV cut-offs yielded lesion-wise sensitivity/specificity of 75/97%. The fraction of progressive lesions was 11% in concordant negative lesions, 33% in lesions only BV positive, 64% in lesions only [18F]FET positive and 97% in concordant positive lesions. Conclusion: The overall diagnostic accuracy of DCE BV imaging is good, but lower than that of [18F]FET PET. Adding DCE BV imaging did not improve the overall diagnostic accuracy of [18F]FET PET, but may improve specificity and allow better lesion-wise risk stratification than [18F]FET PET alone.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Henriksen, Otto M.","Hansen, Adam Espe","Muhic, Aida","Marner, Lisbeth","Madsen, Karine","Møller, Søren","Hasselbalch, Benedikte","Lundemann, Michael J.","Scheie, David","Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","Poulsen, Hans Skovgaard","Larsen, Vibeke A.","Larsson, Henrik B W","Law, Ian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455726"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blood Volume","Glioma","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Perfusion Imaging","Positron Emission Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic yield of simultaneous dynamic contrast enhanced magnetic resonance perfusion measurements and sup 000000000018 sup f fet pet in patients with suspected recurrent anaplastic astrocytoma and glioblastoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00259-022-05917-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-455726","identifier":[{"id":"35907033","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9605929","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85135274150","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6854fb24-c8e8-4c71-9db8-3d813bf2272c"],"keyword":["Amino acid tracers","Blood volume","Glioma","Magnetic resonance imaging","Perfusion imaging","Positron emission tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-107562030C772B23829C872635682F2B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00259-022-05917-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/328550536/s00259_022_05917_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Otto M.","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Otto M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Aida","key":"muhicpau","last":"Muhic","name":"Muhic, Aida","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lisbeth","key":"marnerpau","last":"Marner","locid":"bdc32ba4-8b70-4cae-807b-c3c8cfce3258","name":"Marner, Lisbeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karine","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Karine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"a4bee617-45cc-4a85-a58a-817fb06a5525","name":"Møller, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Benedikte","key":"hasselbalchpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Benedikte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael J.","key":"lundemannpau","last":"Lundemann","name":"Lundemann, Michael J.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"David","key":"scheiepau","last":"Scheie","locid":"88f5350d-9e09-4c54-933e-a854bd33b9a5","name":"Scheie, David","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jane","key":"skjøthrasmussenpau","last":"Skjøth-Rasmussen","locid":"549d7d96-8a0c-4f6e-8a8e-2f9697a2aedc","name":"Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hans S.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"318d653c-4a69-4344-a913-f8a2073c75f8","name":"Poulsen, Hans Skovgaard","name_org":"Poulsen, Hans S.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke A.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke A.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik B. W.","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","locid":"3c09e175-dfd1-4df5-9132-536a42c19373","name":"Larsson, Henrik B W","name_org":"Larsson, Henrik B. W.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ian","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","locid":"fa2c54ee-d725-4edb-9918-8c6cbebfc84a","name":"Law, Ian","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35907033"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00259-022-05917-3","issn":["16197070","16197089"],"issn_org":["16197070"],"issue":"13","journal":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"4677-4691","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135274150"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6854fb24-c8e8-4c71-9db8-3d813bf2272c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diagnostic yield of simultaneous dynamic contrast-enhanced magnetic resonance perfusion measurements and [<sup>18</sup>F]FET PET in patients with suspected recurrent anaplastic astrocytoma and glioblastoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455726","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Drusen are hallmarks of early and intermediate age-related macular degeneration (AMD) but their quantification remains a challenge. We compared automated drusen volume measurements between different OCT devices. We included 380 eyes from 200 individuals with bilateral intermediate (iAMD, n = 126), early (eAMD, n = 25) or no AMD (n = 49) from the MACUSTAR study. We assessed OCT scans from Cirrus (200 × 200 macular cube, 6 × 6 mm; Zeiss Meditec, CA) and Spectralis (20° × 20°, 25 B-scans; 30° × 25°, 241 B-scans; Heidelberg Engineering, Germany) devices. Sensitivity and specificity for drusen detection and differences between modalities were assessed with intra-class correlation coefficients (ICCs) and mean difference in a 5 mm diameter fovea-centered circle. Specificity was > 90% in the three modalities. In eAMD, we observed highest sensitivity in the denser Spectralis scan (68.1). The two different Spectralis modalities showed a significantly higher agreement in quantifying drusen volume in iAMD (ICC 0.993 [0.991–0.994]) than the dense Spectralis with Cirrus scan (ICC 0.807 [0.757–0.847]). Formulae for drusen volume conversion in iAMD between the two devices are provided. Automated drusen volume measures are not interchangeable between devices and softwares and need to be interpreted with the used imaging devices and software in mind. Accounting for systematic difference between methods increases comparability and conversion formulae are provided. Less dense scans did not affect drusen volume measurements in iAMD but decreased sensitivity for medium drusen in eAMD. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT03349801. Registered on 22 November 2017.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Garzone, Davide","Terheyden, Jan Henrik","Morelle, Olivier","Wintergerst, Maximilian W.M.","Saßmannshausen, Marlene","Schmitz-Valckenberg, Steffen","Pfau, Maximilian","Thiele, Sarah","Poor, Stephen","Leal, Sergio","Holz, Frank G.","Finger, Robert P.","Agostini, H.","Altay, L.","Atia, R.","Bandello, F.","Basile, P. G.","Behning, C.","Belmouhand, Mohamed","Berger, M.","Binns, A.","Boon, C. J.F.","Böttger, M.","Bouchet, C.","Brazier, J. E.","Butt, T.","Carapezzi, C.","Carlton, J.","Carneiro, A.","Charil, A.","Coimbra, R.","Cozzi, M.","Crabb, D. P.","Cunha-Vaz, J.","Dahlke, C.","de Sisternes, L.","Dunbar, H.","Fletcher, E.","Francisco, C.","Gutfleisch, M.","Hogg, R.","Hoyng, C. B.","Kilani, A.","Krätzschmar, J.","Kühlewein, L.","Larsen, Michael","Lechanteur, Y. T.E.","Luhmann, U. F.O.","Lüning, A.","Schmid, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-499625"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["MACUSTAR Consortium"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Portugal","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AIBILI Association for Innovation and Biomedical Research on Light and Image (AIBILI)","All Global Affiliations","Bayer AG","Belfast Health and Social Care Trust","Carl Zeiss SMT AG","Centre hospitalier national d'ophtalmologie des Quinze-Vingts","City, University of London","F. Hoffmann-La Roche","Fondation Voir et Etendre","German Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases","Gloucestershire Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Hospital Center São João","Leiden University","Novartis","Novartis USA","Radboud University Nijmegen","St. Franziskus-Hospital Münster","Ulm University","University College London","University of Bonn","University of Cologne","University of Freiburg","University of Milan","University of Sheffield","University of Tübingen","University of Utah","Vita-Salute San Raffaele University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparability of automated drusen volume measurements in age related macula