{"abstract":"Offshore structures are exposed to cyclic loading and thereby at risk of fatigue failure, especially at the welded joints between trusses in offshore jacket foundations. In this paper, an optimization framework for welded joints considering fatigue damages is presented. The framework can be used to optimize the orientation and location of welds connecting the joint in a welded K-node in offshore jacket structures considering fatigue damage. It is known that longer welds are at higher risk of fatigue failure compared to shorter welds. To account for this, the statistical size effect is modelled using the Karhunen-Loéve expansion which can be used to take into account the effect of longer welds in the damage assessment. The approach is included in the optimization framework and it is shown that using this method it is possible to simulate the effect of having a good welding quality and a poor welding quality using the correlation length and coefficient of variation. The proposed optimization framework is validated on a simple plate structure and the effect of the statistical input parameters in the statistical size effect is examined. The results show that the proposed optimization approach is robust in predicting the expected tendencies for a simple plate structure. Furthermore, a full-scale welded K-node in an offshore jacket structure manufactured using cast steel is optimized with respect to mass. The optimization is performed considering a good quality weld and a poor-quality weld by including the statistical size effect. The results show that using high quality welds will result in lower mass of the K-node.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold","Arora, Vikas","Adhikari, S.","Clausen, Henrik Bisgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-603600"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Arora, Vikas"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Glasgow"],"keyword":["Cast steel","Fatigue strength","Karhunen Loéve expansion","Size effect","Stochastic finite element method"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-RAM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-RAM","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimization of welded k node in offshore jacket structure including the stochastic size effect","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marstruc.2021.103128","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-603600","identifier":[{"id":"85121259867","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6a5bf1d0-f1f6-4ca9-87e6-6d7536acad5b"],"keyword":["Cast steel","Fatigue strength","Karhunen-Loéve expansion","Size effect","Stochastic finite element method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B7BAF99636C95B3154363038291CD8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marstruc.2021.103128","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/197601007/Optimization_of_welded_K_node_in_offshore_jacket_structure_including_the_stochastic_size_effect_Elsevier_Enhanced_Reader.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, SDU Mechanical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ramboll group","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-RAM","l3nl":"Rambøll Group","l3nn":"Ramboll Group","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ramboll Group","namevar":["Ramboll Group A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-RAM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Løvenskjold","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1e448908-ddff-4e12-811d-0e9d88a3dff9","name":"Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold","orcid":"0000-0003-2853-6563","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vikas","key":"arorapau","last":"Arora","locid":"825c3f36-eeab-4635-980b-01218adb6f82","name":"Arora, Vikas","orcid":"0000-0002-4369-7851","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"adhikaripau","last":"Adhikari","name":"Adhikari, S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bisgaard","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Henrik Bisgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marstruc.2021.103128","issn":["09518339","18734170"],"issn_org":["09518339"],"journal":"Marine Structures","paperid":"103128","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Marine Structures","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121259867"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Rambøll Group","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6a5bf1d0-f1f6-4ca9-87e6-6d7536acad5b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Optimization of welded K-node in offshore jacket structure including the stochastic size effect","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-603600","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Fampridine has shown to improve walking speed, motor control, and balance in patients with multiple sclerosis. However, potential fampridine-induced changes in gait quality and underlying mechanisms, evaluated by three-dimensional gait analysis, are poorly examined. The aim was to examine if two weeks of fampridine treatment would improve gait quality (using Gait Profile Score and Gait Variable Scores from three-dimensional gait analysis) and gait function (using performance-based tests, spatiotemporal parameters, and self-perceived gait function). METHODS: 14 participants with multiple sclerosis were included (9 women and 5 men, age 53.6 ± 12.8 years, disease duration 21 ± 9.1 years) in this cohort study. Tests were completed prior to fampridine and after 14 (± 1) days of treatment. Three-dimensional gait analyses were completed, and kinematic measures were calculated for overall gait quality using Gait Profile Score, and for joint-specific variables, Gait Variable Scores. Gait function was assessed using spatiotemporal parameters, performance-based tests, and a patient-reported outcome measure. Student's paired t-test/Wilcoxon signed rank test were used to compare baseline and follow-up variables. Sample size calculation for Gait Profile Score required at least 9 participants. FINDINGS: No fampridine-induced improvements in gait quality were demonstrated. For gait function, improvements were found in performance-based tests (Timed 25-Foot Walk: -11.5%; Six Spot Step Test: -13.9%; 2-Minute Walk Test: 18.2%) and self-perceived gait function (12-itemMS Walking Scale: -35.2%). INTERPRETATION: Although two weeks of fampridine treatment in patients with multiple sclerosis improved gait function, there was no change in overall kinematic quality of gait. TRIAL REGISTRATION: This work was collected as a part of a registered clinical trial (MUST): ClinicalTrials.govNCT03847545.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thorning, Maria","Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","Frich, Lars Henrik","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-646209"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thorning, Maria"],"keyword":["Fampridine","Gait function","Gait quality","Multiple sclerosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gait quality and function after fampridine treatment in patients with multiple sclerosis a prospective cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2022.105826","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-646209","identifier":[{"id":"36436320","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85142451276","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-fef5b826-dd47-4414-9e5d-e33b477e0c09"],"keyword":["Fampridine","Gait function","Gait quality","Multiple sclerosis","Three-dimensional gait analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-10C41B47FDCDEBEC8826623954688C92"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2022.105826","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/213960697/1_s2.0_S026800332200256X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar