omech.2022.105826","issn":["02680033","18791271"],"issn_org":["02680033"],"journal":"Clinical Biomechanics","paperid":"105826","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Clinical Biomechanics","volume":"100"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142451276"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fef5b826-dd47-4414-9e5d-e33b477e0c09"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Gait quality and function after fampridine treatment in patients with multiple sclerosis - A prospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-646209","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Børns Vilkår har netop udsendt en rapport, der viser, at kun hver anden pige i 8. klasse er glad for den, hun er, og at en tredjedel har lav livstilfredshed.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Køster-Rasmussen, Rasmus","Meyer, Lene","Christiansen, Lene Bull","Kristensen, Johanne Stubbe T","Bols, Inger","Larsen, Lars Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-679922"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Børn","Trivsel","Tykhed"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unknown external organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sundhedspersoner mere vægtfokus giver ikke flere børn i trivsel","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://politiken.dk/debat/debatindlaeg/art9029261/Mere-v%C3%A6gtfokus-giver-ikke-flere-b%C3%B8rn-i-trivsel","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-679922","ids":["ruc-b9443947-2469-45e4-87ec-7819107c87cd"],"keyword":["Børn","Tykhed","trivsel"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A6CE4E423A2ACEB45B817AF648AFD2A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unknown external organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Communication and Arts","Roskilde University, Department of Communication and Arts, Audiences & Mediated life","Roskilde University, Department of Communication and Arts, Centre for Digital Citizenship","Roskilde University, Department of Communication and Arts, Intercultural studies","Roskilde University, Department of Communication and Arts, Media and Culture","Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business, Centre for Gender, Power and Diversity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"køsterrasmussenpau","last":"Køster-Rasmussen","name":"Køster-Rasmussen, Rasmus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Lene Bull","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"5b325cf8-16c6-4cdd-a1a8-bf155e2985c1","name":"Christiansen, Lene Bull","orcid":"0000-0001-6019-9670","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johanne Stubbe T","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Johanne Stubbe T","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inger","key":"bolspau","last":"Bols","name":"Bols, Inger","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Lars Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09071814"],"newspaper":"Politiken","status":"p","title":"Politiken"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-b9443947-2469-45e4-87ec-7819107c87cd"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Sundhedspersoner : Mere vægtfokus giver ikke flere børn i trivsel","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-679922","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Greenland has had political autonomy in some form for more than 40 years. Formally, it has been divided by the first 30 year of Home Rule and the present period of Self-Government. The paper asks what the drivers of the development Greenlandic autonomy have been. It also asks whether there is continuity or change between these two autonomy regimes and, if so, what the reason for this state of affairs is. The idea in the paper is that historical institutionalism (HI) is fruitful for answering these questions with its focus on concepts such as critical junctures, path dependency and interests of political actors. HI has not been drawn on in analyses of Greenlandic autonomy in the existing literature so in a broader sense the paper also examines whether HI is helpful in analyzing a phenomenon in this geographical area with an indigenous population. The paper inquires into whether the development of Greenland’s autonomy over the years can be understood as a case of path dependency, or whether it has rather been marked by critical junctures whereby Greenlandic autonomy can be seen as a series of changing equilibriums. This is not least interesting with regard to the change to Self-Government in 2009, but also subsequent initiatives such as the setting up of a Greenlandic constitutional committee in 2017 and an increasing focus on a stronger Greenlandic profile in foreign and security policy. Can these developments be understood as path dependency interrupted by critical junctures - along the lines of classical HI. Or should they rather be understood as negative feedback to, or endogenous contestation of, the path dependency of the self-government structures - the newer focus in HI? Answers to these questions will be helpful to provide concepts for talking about the drivers of change and continuity in Greenlandic Self-Government and for comparisons with political autonomies within other Arctic states. The paper first presents the main elements of historical institutionalism drawing on Pierson, Steinmo and Thélen, Pollack and Cappocia and Kelemen and Mahoney. It then goes on to present the basic dimensions of Greenlandic Self-Government drawing on Trinn and Schulte’s dimensions for assessing regional autonomy. It concludes that Greenland’s Self-Government can be seen as extensive. In the main part of the paper which follows, the development of Greenland autonomy since the 1970s is analyzed drawing on key concepts from HI. It is concluded that HI is a fruitful theoretical framework for analyzing the development of political autonomy in Greenland, but also that the concepts of classical HI has difficulties in explaining some elements in the development of Greenland Self-Government after 2009. This is the case for political initiatives such as the preparation of a constitution.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik","Jakobsen, Uffe"],"cuid":["S02-085.14-673118"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-16","start":"2022-08-16","title":"Annual Meeting of the Danish Political Science Organisation","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenland s self government within the danish realm a historical institutionalist outcome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-085.14-673118","ids":["ku-6dea0fae-7f28-464f-8bed-1057ef387547","ku-87a10704-b891-4bc7-8d2d-dce780b845a1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-7DFD31503BB9051614585BEF85F016D3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, International Relations"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Uffe","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"3253599b-6c78-4522-a1c6-87f06fe37df7","name":"Jakobsen, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0002-7114-1981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6dea0fae-7f28-464f-8bed-1057ef387547","ku-87a10704-b891-4bc7-8d2d-dce780b845a1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Greenland's Self-Government within the Danish Realm : a Historical Institutionalist Outcome?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.14-673118","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Müller, Maja","Larsen, Jørgen Elm"],"cuid":["S02-091.00-006032"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"marginalisering og coping","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://samfundslitteratur.dk/bog/social-ulighed-og-socialt-arbejde","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.00-006032","ids":["aau-7c22666b-209d-47c5-af02-36b7b280ff38","ku-d02b2b66-51b1-4db0-8e23-35009ff7557c"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-EF11C88C3D74AF2441B34544A6B4E5E9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work, Practice Research and Service User Perspectives"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","locid":"a6ffbdef-2cc5-47c8-8239-592d3d2b1d6f","name":"Müller, Maja","orcid":"0000-0002-1403-6114","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Elm","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"12398e5f-f494-4e0a-9022-51e159113fec","name":"Larsen, Jørgen Elm","orcid":"0000-0002-8604-7509","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn Henrik","key":"enevoldsenpedh","last":"Enevoldsen","name":"Enevoldsen, Jørn Henrik","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Samuel","key":"pjonespedh","last":"P. Jones","name":"P. Jones, Samuel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Samuel","key":"pedersenjonespedh","last":"Pedersen Jones","name":"Pedersen Jones, Samuel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788759341476"],"isbn":["9788759338766"],"pages":"111-129","place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Samfundslitteratur","status":"p","title":"Social ulighed og socialt arbejde"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7c22666b-209d-47c5-af02-36b7b280ff38","ku-d02b2b66-51b1-4db0-8e23-35009ff7557c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Marginalisering og coping","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.00-006032","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Temporal variation in eDNA signals is increasingly explored for understanding community ecology in aquatic habitats. Seasonal changes have been addressed using eDNA sampling, but very little is known regarding short-term temporal variation that spans hours to days. To address this, we filtered marine water samples from a single coastal site in Denmark every hour for 32 h. We used metabarcoding to target both fish and broader eukaryote diversity and evaluated temporal changes in this marine community. Results revealed variation in fish species richness (15–27) and eukaryote class richness (35–64) across the 32 h of sampling, and we further evaluated sampling efforts needed to reach different levels of diversity saturation. Relative read frequency data for both fish and eukaryotes indicated a clear diel change in community composition, with different communities detected during daylight versus dark hours. The abundance signals in our data reflected biological variation rather than stochastic variation, since replicates taken at the same hour were more similar to each other than those taken at different hours. Our compositional results indicated a dynamic community, rather than a static pool of eDNA—even across a few hours. The fish data showed a daily pattern of relative species abundances, and the uncoupling of fish and broader eukaryote data suggest that variation in eDNA profiles across a single day can provide valuable information reflecting diel changes, at least for highly mobile organism groups. However, our results also point to several pitfalls in current eDNA experimental design, in which samples are taken over large areas without relative time-consistency or short-term replication. Our findings shed new light on short-term variation in coastal eDNA and have wide implications for experimental study design and for incorporating temporality into project conceptualization for future aquatic biodiversity monitoring.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jensen, Mads Reinholdt","Sigsgaard, Eva Egelyng","de Paula Avila, Marcelo","Agersnap, Sune","Larsen, William Brenner","Sengupta, Mita Eva","Xing, Yingchun","Krag, Marcus Anders","Knudsen, Steen Wilhelm","Carl, Henrik","Moller, Peter Rask","Thomsen, Philip Francis"],"cuid":["S02-095.11-017891"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Mads Reinholdt"],"country":["China","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Fishery Sciences","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["NIVA Denmark Water Research"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short term temporal variation of coastal marine edna","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/edn3.285","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.11-017891","identifier":[{"id":"85125073546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-47ecad89-7d3c-4a9e-a62a-98e96e207ada","ku-07a3f571-10d9-4bed-a5f4-a17f7b1d60f4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8B7D87C61D1F61A61476E85871000144"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/edn3.285","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/316749255/Environmental_DNA_2022_Jensen_Short_u2010term_temporal_variation_of_coastal_marine_eDNA.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022",