{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Risk factors for retinal vein occlusion have been extensively studied, with varying population sizes. Smaller populations result in less certain measures of associations. The present review included studies with a relevant population size to identify clinically relevant risk factors for retinal vein occlusion. Understanding the risk factors of retinal vein occlusion is important for the management of these patients. AREAS COVERED: A comprehensive literature review was conducted through a systematic literature search in PubMed and Embase. Additional studies were selected from cross references in the assessed studies. Weighted effect measures were calculated for all included risk factors.Risk factors associated with retinal vein occlusion included cardiovascular diseases, eye diseases, systemic diseases, medical interventions, and sociodemographic factors. EXPERT OPINION: This review provided an extensive overview of a wide variety of risk factors increasing the risk of developing retinal vein occlusion. The severity of the identified risk factors indicated that these patients have been in contact with the health care system before their retinal vein occlusion event. Therefore, the clinical course for patients with retinal vein occlusion may benefit from a multidisciplinary collaboration between ophthalmologists and especially cardiologists.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ørskov, Marie","Vorum, Henrik","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Vestergaard, Nanna","Lip, Gregory Y H","Bek, Toke","Skjøth, Flemming"],"cuid":["S02-099.90-007969"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ørskov, Marie"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Etiology","Retinal vein occlusion","Review","Risk Factors","Systematic literature search"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a review of risk factors for retinal vein occlusions","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85136454648&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.90-007969","identifier":[{"id":"35972726","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85136454648","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a4e9c92a-2d4e-48d4-a288-fd5082ae56c7","au-dfcba293-457b-4680-a27a-df07d65a4dbf"],"keyword":["etiology","retinal vein occlusion","review","risk factors","systematic literature search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BA820B599B2EF760C089C7310790D048"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"liverpool heart and chest hospital nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"ørskovpau","last":"Ørskov","locid":"98e0db01-70c1-4f44-821d-849ca9a135eb","name":"Ørskov, Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"vorumpau","last":"Vorum","locid":"60554352-1557-4c7b-905d-e4b7c7f8c94a","name":"Vorum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-7600-0731","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"bjerregaardlarsenpau","last":"Bjerregaard Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","name_org":"Bjerregaard Larsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"2613db29-1c02-4522-8bc1-8d0bf478d93f","name":"Vestergaard, Nanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y. H.","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y. H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","locid":"ffc6d181-f10a-40f1-9446-0a5680b91ab8","name":"Bek, Toke","orcid":"0000-0002-0409-2534","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"skjøthpau","last":"Skjøth","locid":"6166e832-f5f5-47be-82bb-07962be7c943","name":"Skjøth, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0003-2975-647X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35972726"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/14779072.2022.2112667","issn":["14779072","17448344"],"issn_org":["14779072"],"issue":"9","journal":"Expert Review of Cardiovascular Therapy","pages":"761-772","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Expert Review of Cardiovascular Therapy","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136454648"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a4e9c92a-2d4e-48d4-a288-fd5082ae56c7","au-dfcba293-457b-4680-a27a-df07d65a4dbf"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A review of risk factors for retinal vein occlusions","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.90-007969","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The objective of this systematic review was to test the hypothesis of no difference in recovery following surgical removal of mandibular third molars with the application of advanced platelet-rich fibrin (A-PRF) in the extraction socket compared with alternative biomaterials or natural wound healing. A search of MEDLINE (PubMed), Embase, Cochrane Library, and Scopus was conducted. Human randomized controlled trials published in English up until December 31, 2020 were included. Outcome measures were pain, facial swelling, trismus, soft tissue healing, alveolar osteitis, and quality of life; these were evaluated by descriptive statistics and meta-analysis including 95% confidence intervals (CI). Four studies with a low or moderate risk of bias fulfilled the inclusion criteria. A-PRF resulted in significantly lower pain scores when compared with leucocyte platelet-rich fibrin or natural wound healing after 2 days (-16.8, 95% CI -18.9 to -14.7), 3 days (-12.1, 95% CI -13.4 to -10.7), and 7 days (-1.9, 95% CI -2.9 to -0.9). A-PRF seems to have a negligible effect on facial swelling and trismus and some beneficial effect on soft tissue healing. Alveolar osteitis and quality of life were not assessed. The included studies were characterized by considerable heterogeneity and confounding variables. Thus, the level of evidence appears to be inadequate for clinical recommendations according to the focused question.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vitenson, Julie","Starch-Jensen, Thomas","Bruun, Niels Henrik","Larsen, Marie Kjærgaard"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-010731"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Vitenson, Julie"],"keyword":["Dry Socket prevention control","Edema","Humans","Molar Third surgery","Pain","Platelet Rich Fibrin","Quality of Life","Third molar","Tooth Extraction methods","Trismus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the use of advanced platelet rich fibrin after surgical removal of mandibular third molars a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85123099495&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-010731","identifier":[{"id":"85123099495","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35033409","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e0c4a69f-aa62-4fd0-bfa7-1c16a9e6a68b","ku-4f8f3d7c-0f96-4623-9aed-e53356b1b315"],"keyword":["Dry Socket/prevention & control","Humans","Molar, Third/surgery","Tooth Extraction/methods","Tooth, Impacted/surgery","edema","pain","platelet-rich fibrin","quality of life","third molar","trismus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-11AFCE0B3F1DA904B85733FB0C2292DB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 03 - Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"vitensonpau","last":"Vitenson","locid":"c380f9ab-8770-4c59-8e23-fe9ade71fc12","name":"Vitenson, Julie","name_org":"Vitenson, J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"T.","key":"starchjensenpau","last":"Starch-Jensen","locid":"3886ebbc-a26a-4733-8fd5-78be54b0273e","name":"Starch-Jensen, Thomas","name_org":"Starch-Jensen, T.","orcid":"0000-0002-3726-4267","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"N. H.","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"c46a199e-22d6-4140-807a-33564453684f","name":"Bruun, Niels Henrik","name_org":"Bruun, N. H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"M. K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"18554167-358e-4c61-bae8-802171b440c1","name":"Larsen, Marie Kjærgaard","name_org":"Larsen, M. K.","orcid":"0000-0002-7024-3089","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35033409"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijom.2021.11.014","issn":["09015027","13974203"],"issn_org":["09015027"],"issue":"7","journal":"International Journal of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery","pages":"962-974","publisher":"Churchill Livingstone","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123099495"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e0c4a69f-aa62-4fd0-bfa7-1c16a9e6a68b","ku-4f8f3d7c-0f96-4623-9aed-e53356b1b315"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The use of advanced platelet-rich fibrin after surgical removal of mandibular third molars : a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-010731","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Cytokine-specific autoantibodies (c-aAb) represent a novel type of immune dysfunction. Though they have been detected in both patient cohorts and healthy individuals, and have immunomodulatory properties, the full extent of their influence remains unknown. Based on the critical role of several cytokines in thrombopoiesis, we investigated if there is an association between c-aAb and platelet variables in healthy individuals, with a specific focus on c-aAb against a known thrombopoietic cytokine, IL-6. Using platelet count and mean platelet volume in 3,569 healthy participants of the Danish Blood Donor Study as dependent variables, we performed a series of multivariate regression analyses using five cytokine autoantibodies, including IL-6 c-aAb, as independent variables. In men, high titers of IL-6 c-aAb were negatively associated with platelet counts (β = −24 *109/l (95% confidence interval −43 to −6), p = 0.008) and positively associated with mean platelet volume (β = 0.4 fL (95% confidence interval 0.0–0.7) p = 0.043). These associations were exacerbated when adjusting for undetectable C-reactive protein levels, which we used as a proxy for c-aAb mediated IL-6 inhibition in vivo. Furthermore, in a smaller subgroup, individuals with high vs. low titer IL-6 c-aAb had different profiles of plasma IL-6, IL-10, TNFα and TPO, further suggesting a functional inhibition of IL-6 by high titers of circulating IL-6 c-aAb. We therefore speculate that in addition to their immunomodulatory potential IL-6 c-aAb may interfere with thrombopoiesis – directly or indirectly – under normal physiological conditions. This study is the first to suggest an influence of c-aAb on platelets in healthy individuals, beyond their apparent effects on immune competence.","author_count":11,"contributors":["von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Erikstrup, Christian","Ullum, Henrik","Dowsett, Joseph","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Sørensen, Erik","Hansen, Morten Bagge","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029824"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth"],"keyword":["Autoimmunity","Blood Donors","Cytokines","Epidemiology","IL 6","Platelets","Thrombopoiesis","cytokine autoantibodies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"il 000000000006 autoantibodies predict lower platelet counts and altered plasma cytokine profiles in healthy blood donors results from the danish blood donor study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2022.914262","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-029824","identifier":[{"id":"85134042648","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000822554800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9263719","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35814772","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ec94121d-610d-425f-b04e-5cdb5f1ebac9","ku-0588f2da-e104-4193-9248-d71010ec136e"],"keyword":["IL-6","autoimmunity","blood donors","cytokine autoantibodies","cytokines","epidemiology","platelets","thrombopoiesis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D41FDDB20BAC1F5BB1D2D849890A6EC4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/322195421/fmed_09_914262.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2022.914262","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Hjorth","key":"vonstemannpau","last":"von Stemann","name":"von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Ole Birger Vesterager","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0d43956a-6e43-42d7-8b29-4505d03ea5c8","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4 5","first":"Henrik","key":"hjalgrimpau","last":"Hjalgrim","locid":"ae40e66a-f263-444f-877f-838370aec64a","name":"Hjalgrim, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","locid":"523ae417-65a9-46aa-b665-0d88271dc0b9","name":"Erikstrup, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6551-6647","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","name":"Ullum, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joseph","key":"dowsettpau","last":"Dowsett","name":"Dowsett, Joseph","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise Wegner","key":"thørnerpau","last":"Thørner","name":"Thørner, Lise Wegner","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Margit Anita Hørup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Erik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten Bagge","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"31f07839-f4e2-44f2-8668-3bd6d1a24b2f","name":"Hansen, Morten Bagge","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35814772"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmed.2022.914262","issn":["2296858X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Medicine","paperid":"914262","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Medicine","title_org":"Frontiers in medicine","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134042648"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ec94121d-610d-425f-b04e-5cdb5f1ebac9","ku-0588f2da-e104-4193-9248-d71010ec136e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"IL-6 Autoantibodies Predict Lower Platelet Counts and Altered Plasma Cytokine Profiles in Healthy Blood Donors : Results From the Danish Blood Donor Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-029824","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background The cause of atrioventricular block (AVB) remains unknown in approximately half of young patients with the diagnosis. Although variants in several genes associated with cardiac conduction diseases have been identified, the contribution of genetic variants in younger patients with AVB is unknown. Methods and Results Using the Danish Pacemaker and Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillator (ICD) Registry, we identified all patients younger than 50 years receiving a pacemaker because of AVB in Denmark in the period from January 1, 1996 to December 31, 2015. From medical records, we identified patients with unknown cause of AVB at time of pacemaker implantation. These patients were invited to a genetic screening using a panel of 102 genes associated with inherited cardiac diseases. We identified 471 living patients with AVB of unknown cause, of whom 226 (48%) accepted participation. Median age at the time of pacemaker implantation was 39 years (interquartile range, 32-45 years), and 123 (54%) were men. We found pathogenic or likely pathogenic variants in genes associated with or possibly associated with AVB in 12 patients (5%). Most variants were found in the LMNA gene (n=5). LMNA variant carriers all had a family history of either AVB and/or sudden cardiac death. Conclusions In young patients with AVB of unknown cause, we found a possible genetic cause in 1 out of 20 participating patients. Variants in the LMNA gene were most common and associated with a family history of AVB and/or sudden cardiac death, suggesting that genetic testing should be a part of the diagnostic workup in these patients to stratify risk and screen family members.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Resdal Dyssekilde, Johnni","Frederiksen, Tanja Charlotte","Christiansen, Morten Krogh","Hasle Sørensen, Rikke","Pedersen, Lisbeth Nørum","Loof Møller, Peter","Christensen, Lene Svendstrup","Larsen, Jacob Moesgaard","Thomsen, Kristian Korsgaard","Lindhardt, Tommi Bo","Böttcher, Morten","Molsted, Stig","Havndrup, Ole","Fischer, Thomas","Møller, Dorthe Svenstrup","Henriksen, Finn Lund","Johansen, Jens Brock","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Bundgaard, Henning","Nyegaard, Mette","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf"],"cuid":["S04-097.37-011825"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Tanja Charlotte"],"keyword":["Atrioventricular Block diagnosis","Conduction","Death Sudden Cardiac etiology","Diagnostic testing","Female","Genetic Testing","Humans","LMNA","Male","Pacemaker Artificial adverse effects","Risk Factors","inherited heart diseases"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic yield of genetic testing in young patients with atrioventricular block of unknown cause","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.121.025643","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by unrestricted research grants from Skibsreder Per Henriksen, Roghustrus Foundation, Danish Heart Foundation (16-R107-A6707-22988), the A. P. Møller Foundation for the Advancement of Medical Science, and the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF18OC0031258 to Jensen). This work was supported by unrestricted research grants from Skibsreder Per Henriksen, R. og hustrus Foundation, Danish Heart Foundation (16-R107-A6707-22988), the A. P. Møller Foundation for the Advancement of Medical Science, and the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF18OC0031258 to Jensen). Dr Böttcher discloses advisory board participation for NOVO Nordisk, Astra-Zeneca, Bayer, Sanofi, and Acarix. Dr Nielsen received grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF16OC0018658 and NNF17OC0029148) outside the current work. Dr Bundgaard received lecture fees from Amgen. Dr Jensen is supported by grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Denmark (NNF18OC0031258 and NNF20OC0065151), and received lecture fees from Abbott Denmark and Biosense Webster, Europe. The remaining authors have no disclosures to report."],"id":"S04-097.37-011825","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9238593","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85129781151","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35470684","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f796d2e5-6959-4c63-9b04-ffaf0c07642d","au-d96ac6b5-de65-4453-a8e1-3056e1d02a71","ku-a338c51c-593f-4ce3-9941-f5e80ef76a6b","sdu-10ed91c8-08bf-4dff-9d3f-2badfabc4647"],"keyword":["Atrioventricular Block/diagnosis","Death, Sudden, Cardiac/etiology","Female","Genetic Testing","Humans","LMNA","Male","Pacemaker, Artificial/adverse effects","Risk Factors","conduction","diagnostic testing","inherited heart diseases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-32ED7760DF35F449A24802AB6A3CF68E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/469813369/Dyssekilde_et_al._2022_._Diagnostic_Yield_of_Genetic_Testing_in_Young_Patients_With_Atrioventricular_Block_of_Unknown_Cause.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/308333691/JAHA.121.025643.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.121.025643","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/202682146/JAHA.121.025643.pdf"