{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Søren Erik","Tornbjerg, Henrik","Kronvang, Brian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-160947"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udvikling af en korrektionsformel for kvælstofkoncentrationer analyseret i naturvandløb i perioden 000000002009 000000002015","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dce.au.dk/fileadmin/dce.au.dk/Udgivelser/Notater_2022/N2022_64.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-160947","ids":["au-3752d757-c364-447b-b15f-1c9dbdab0848"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AE6E13180D13D40535043BC677F7C2FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dce.au.dk/fileadmin/dce.au.dk/Udgivelser/Notater_2022/N2022_64.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Catchment Science and Environmental Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"tornbjergpau","last":"Tornbjerg","locid":"673f9989-b651-4f14-8190-b60c45f9cde2","name":"Tornbjerg, Henrik","orcid":"0009-0008-7385-7490","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian","key":"kronvangpau","last":"Kronvang","locid":"7766931c-a3c9-4a38-9d22-e4cc3a2f4607","name":"Kronvang, Brian","orcid":"0000-0003-1165-1354","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3752d757-c364-447b-b15f-1c9dbdab0848"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Udvikling af en korrektionsformel for kvælstofkoncentrationer analyseret i naturvandløb i perioden 2009-2015","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-160947","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The network is organized by three partners but interacts with the entire fishing sector. The organizers are the two trade organizations, The Danish Fisheries Association Producer Organization (DFPO) and the Danish Pelagic Producers Organization (DPPO) as well as the National Institute of Aquatic Resources at the Technical University of Denmark (DTU Aqua). The European Maritime and Fisheries Fund (EMFF) and the Danish Fisheries Agency finance the project. The purpose of the project is to support networking activities that bring the executive Danish fishing industry and operational fisheries research closer together through fisher-researcher alliances. The idea is to target research against the practical challenges in the fishing industry and to streamline the development of business and ease of generational succession through the synergy arising from dialogue, common problem formulation and resolution. The project also aims at streamlining and professionalizing the work of the various Thematic and Regional Advisory Councils with Danish interests in collaboration between the fishing industry and DTU Aqua experts before and during the meetings. The fishing industry is faced with ever-increasing challenges in terms of regulatory requirements in the context of the Common Fisheries Policy and its national implementation, consumer requirements for fishing activities and environmental impact, as well as an ecosystem in dynamic transformation that offers changing fishing opportunities. In order to continue the development of profitable and sustainable fisheries, workshops and dialog meetings have been conducted to exchange experiences about fisheries and management, identify problems, elaborate ideas for solutions and formulate projects for testing ideas. Since solutions require knowledge from many areas, networking between fisheries, research and management has been in focus with results from collaboration and announcement of new initiatives being regularly communicated via a dedicated platform www.fisker-forsker.dk through a wide range of articles, reports, interviews and videos on this and other media. In order to ensure an effective generational succession in modern Danish fishery, the project has also invested in the field of teaching the next generation fishers on topics of fish and ecosystem biology, oceanography, aquaculture, fishing technology, stock assessment and the advisory process behind fisheries management as well as basic fisheries economics. Further, along these lines the project has facilitated knowledge sharing between businesses as well as courses and internship in fishery for students in Aquatic Science and Technology (AST) at DTU. It has been the goal to form fisherman-researcher alliances on concrete collaborative projects for the development of Danish fisheries. Through screening of a large number of ideas from the fishing industry, 17 concrete collaborative project-ideas have been established with submitted proposals for support by the EMFF for seven of these, ranging from improving knowledge basis on fisheries and elucidating fisheries management questions to collaboration on novel approaches for data collection. The primary contact for dialogue and knowledge sharing between fishermen and researchers has been through targeted workshops and dialogue meetings at DTU as well as in local fisheries organizations. The project has been the second phase of hopefully three network initiatives involving workshops, working groups, experience exchange, idea gathering, knowledge sharing, courses, web dissemination and advisory council work in collaboration between fishermen and apprentices, industry associations, as well as researchers and students.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mosegaard, Henrik","Pedersen, Eva Maria","Christensen, Linda Stuhr","Reedtz Sparrevohn, Claus","Larsen, Ole Lundberg","Fischer, Kenn Skau"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-333117"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mosegaard, Henrik"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Pelagic Producers Organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dansk fisker forsker netværk fase 000000000002","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/268995635/396_2022_Dansk_Fisker_Forsker_Netvaerk_Fase2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-333117","ids":["dtu-5fdbf818-f459-4057-ae95-20fa64d19326"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-114E5AE84114D3C247B34271EF206E46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aqua.dtu.dk/-/media/institutter/aqua/publikationer/rapporter-352-400/396-2022_dansk-fisker-forsker-netvaerk-fase2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/268995635/396_2022_Dansk_Fisker_Forsker_Netvaerk_Fase2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Marine Living Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Pelagic Producers Organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"mosegaardpau","last":"Mosegaard","locid":"01482533-590c-4ffd-b236-9baf6fe84c8d","name":"Mosegaard, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7045-9456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva Maria","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"1e48fb0a-018a-4f02-bb25-946ee7b7ff28","name":"Pedersen, Eva Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0298-2648","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linda Stuhr","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"07910e0a-0cc4-4a20-93c0-df167bb57413","name":"Christensen, Linda Stuhr","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"reedtzsparrevohnpau","last":"Reedtz Sparrevohn","name":"Reedtz Sparrevohn, Claus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Lundberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Ole Lundberg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenn Skau","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Kenn Skau","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13958216"],"issue":"396-2022","pages":"30","place":"Kgs. Lyngby, Denmark","publisher":"DTU Aqua","repno":"DTU Aqua-rapport, 396-2022","series":"DTU Aqua-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5fdbf818-f459-4057-ae95-20fa64d19326"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dansk Fisker-Forsker Netværk. Fase 2","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-333117","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We demonstrate the transfer and immobilization of active antibodies from a low surface- energy mold surface to thermoplastic replica surfaces using injection molding, and we investigate the process at molecular scale. The transfer process is highly efficient, as verified by atomic force microscopy (AFM) and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS) of the mold and replica surfaces. AFM analysis reveals partial nanometer-scale embedding of the protein into the polymer matrix as a possible mechanism of permanent immobilization. Replicas with rabbit anti-mouse IgG immobilized as capture antibody at the hot polymer melt surface during injection molding show similar affinity for their antigen (mouse IgG) in sandwich enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) as capture antibodies deposited by passive adsorption onto a bare thermoplastic replica. The transferred antibodies retain their functionality after incubation in serum-containing cell medium for >1 week. A mold coating time of 10 min prior to injection molding is sufficient for producing highly sensitive ELISA assays, thus enabling the short processing cycle times required for mass production of single-use biodevices relying on active immobilized antibodies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hobæk, Thor Christian","Pranov, Henrik J.","Larsen, Niels Bent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357440"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Niels Bent"],"keyword":["AFM","Antibody","ELISA","Injection molding","XPS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immobilization of active antibodies at polymer melt surfaces during injection molding","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/polym14204426","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We gratefully acknowledge funding support from the Danish Council for Strategic Research through the Strategic Research Center PolyNano (grant no 10-092322/DSF)."],"id":"S01-000.00-357440","identifier":[{"id":"85140872946","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36298004","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9606872","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-b0fa0e42-8e21-424f-af54-d3797e30af8f"],"keyword":["AFM","Antibody","ELISA","Injection molding","Protein transfer","Thermoplastic polymers","XPS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D8F9B65000D0B92A018199AF7A160C0B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/296218720/polymers_14_04426.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/polym14204426","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Inmold A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thor Christian","key":"hobækpau","last":"Hobæk","locid":"466cc5d8-a472-4572-85ad-6e645e49eab4","name":"Hobæk, Thor Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik J.","key":"pranovpau","last":"Pranov","name":"Pranov, Henrik J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels B.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7a727b09-e209-47ab-80f7-9df731c2178f","name":"Larsen, Niels Bent","name_org":"Larsen, Niels B.","orcid":"0000-0001-6506-3991","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36298004"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/polym14204426","issn":["20734360"],"issue":"20","journal":"Polymers","paperid":"4426","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Polymers","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140872946"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","inmold a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b0fa0e42-8e21-424f-af54-d3797e30af8f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Immobilization of Active Antibodies at Polymer Melt Surfaces during Injection Molding","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357440","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: To evaluate the association of urinary oxidized guanine/guanosine (OxGuo) levels with incident type 2 diabetes (T2D) among older adults. Methods: A nested case-control design was applied with 440 cases of incident T2D and 440 controls, randomly sampled from all 65-75 year-old study participants of the ESTHER study, which is a population-based German cohort study with 14 years of follow-up. Analyses of 8-hydroxy-2′-deoxyguanosine (8-oxo-dGuo; DNA oxidation product) and 8-hydroxyguanosine (8-oxo-Guo; RNA oxidation product) were measured by ultra-performance liquid chromatography tandem-mass spectrometry (UPLC-MS/MS). The sum of the two OxGuo molecule concentrations was calculated and called OxGuo-UPLC-MS/MS. The corresponding OxGuo-ELISA levels were measured by Cayman's DNA/RNA oxidative damage ELISA, which detects a mix of 8-oxo-dGuo, 8-oxo-Guo and one other OxGuo molecule. Logistic regression was applied and models were adjusted for age, sex, BMI, HbA1c, and C-reactive protein levels. Results: 8-oxo-dGuo and 8-oxo-Guo were highly correlated with each other (r = 0.642) and weakly correlated with OxGuo-ELISA (r = 0.22 and r = 0.14, respectively). OxGuo-ELISA levels were statistically significant associated with T2D incidence (odds ratio (OR) and 95% confidence interval [95%CI] for comparison of top and bottom quartile: 1.77 [1.14; 2.76]). In contrast, the ORs did not increase stepwise from quartile 2 to 4 for neither 8-oxo-Guo, 8-oxo-dGuo levels nor OxGuo-UPLC-MS/MS and comparisons of top and bottom quartile were not statistically significant. In a post-hoc analysis comparing bottom quartile 1 with a combined group of quartile 2–4, the association of OxGuo-UPLC-MS/MS with T2D incidence reached statistical significance (OR [95%CI]: 0.66 [0.46; 0.96]) and was very similar with the one obtained for OxGuo-ELISA (OR [95%CI]: 0.66 [0.45; 0.95]). Conclusions: Although only the measurements of the DNA/RNA oxidative damage ELISA kit of Cayman were statistically significantly associated with T2D incidence in the main analysis, confidence intervals overlapped and the post-hoc analysis showed that results for OxGuo-UPLC-MS/MS were quite comparable.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Schöttker, Ben","Larsen, Emil L.","Weimann, Allan","Henriksen, Trine","Brenner, Hermann","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-396582"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center","Heidelberg University "],"keyword":["8 Hydroxy 2 Deoxyguanosine","Cohort study","Diabetes mellitus","Free radicals","Oxidative stress","Type 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations of urinary metabolites of oxidized dna and rna with the incidence of diabetes mellitus using uplc ms ms and elisa methods","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-396582","identifier":[{"id":"35307553","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85126514877","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-052ee5ba-8fe7-4ffa-98b3-03ff062fa42b"],"keyword":["8-Hydroxy-2′-deoxyguanosine","Cohort study","Diabetes mellitus","Free radicals","Oxidative stress","Type 2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8BF6285A01E606711DE15137D4532EBE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"german cancer research center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Cancer Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"heidelberg university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University ","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ben","key":"schöttkerpau","last":"Schöttker","name":"Schöttker, Ben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Emil L.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Allan","key":"weimannpau","last":"Weimann","name":"Weimann, Allan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Trine","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Trine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Hermann","key":"brennerpau","last":"Brenner","name":"Brenner, Hermann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Henrik E.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","name_org":"Poulsen, Henrik E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35307553"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2022.03.007","issn":["08915849","18734596"],"issn_org":["08915849"],"journal":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","pages":"51-59","status":"p","title":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","volume":"183"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126514877"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-052ee5ba-8fe7-4ffa-98b3-03ff062fa42b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Associations of urinary metabolites of oxidized DNA and RNA with the incidence of diabetes mellitus using UPLC-MS/MS and ELISA methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-396582","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Naturen har brug for plads, både i form af øget areal og øget mulighed for at lade naturen gå sin gang. Det kan to redskaber, naturzone og naturpligt, være med til at sikre, skriver medlemmer af forskernetværk ved Københavns Universitet.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Baaner, Lasse","Bruun, Hans Henrik","Vejre, Henrik","Møller, Peter Rask","Båstrup-Spohr, Lars","Krøijer, Stine","Larsen, Kristina C.","Kjøller, Rasmus","Strange, Niels","Jepsen, Martin Rudbeck","Heilmann-Clausen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-420376"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"naturpligt skal sikre mere og vildere natur i danmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.altinget.dk/miljoe/artikel/forskere-naturpligt-skal-sikre-mere-og-vildere-natur-i-danmark","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-420376","ids":["ku-2d301a9a-4b4f-46e1-a711-91070a087365"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8B4E01492E294C8CED0BE3C7BAFC3ACF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.altinget.dk/miljoe/artikel/forskere-naturpligt-skal-sikre-mere-og-vildere-natur-i-danmark","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Consumption, Bioethics and Governance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affn