{"abstract":"Objective: To examine the Multiple Sclerosis Impairment Scale (MSIS) in secondary progressive MS (SPMS) in relation to the Expanded Disability Status Scale (EDSS), magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) outcomes, and mobility. Methods: In this observational single-center study, 68 secondary progressive multiple sclerosis (SPMS) patients were examined by MSIS, EDSS, functional mobility tests of upper/lower extremities, and multimodal MRI. Participants had EDSS ≥3.5, a decline in daily activities over the last year unrelated to relapses, and/or 6-month confirmed disability progression. Results: Mean disease duration was 23.1 ± 8.3 years and mean age 54.4 ± 8.1 years. MSIS, EDSS, and their corresponding motor, cerebellar, and sensory subscores correlated (p <.0001). Motor subscores of MSIS correlated stronger with Timed-25-Foot-Walk (T25FW) than pyramidal functional system score (FSS) (p =.03), but EDSS had a stronger correlation to T25FW than the total MSIS score (p =.01). MSIS cerebellar subscore correlated stronger with 9-Hole Peg Test (9-HPT) than cerebellar FSS (p =.04). The sensory MSIS subscore also showed correlation with 9-HPT in contrast to sensory FSS (p =.006). MSIS subscores had stronger correlations with MRI volumetry measures than FSS scores (lesion volume and putamen, thalamus, corpus callosum volumetry, p =.0001–0.0017). Conclusion: In patients with SPMS, MSIS correlated with functional motor tests. MSIS showed stronger correlations with atrophy of central nervous system areas, and may be more sensitive to scale cerebellar and sensory function than EDSS.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Theódórsdóttir, Ásta","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","Illes, Zsolt","Ravnborg, Mads Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-610978"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Theódórsdóttir, Ásta"],"keyword":["Brain diagnostic imaging","Disability Evaluation","Humans","MRI","MSIS","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Middle Aged","Multiple Sclerosis Chronic Progressive diagnostic imaging","Multiple sclerosis","Observational Study","Secondary progressive","Walking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-FILA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-FILA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiple sclerosis impairment scale and brain mri in secondary progressive multiple sclerosis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195733336/ane.13554_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["AT has served on a scientific advisory board for Roche, has received research grant from Novartis Healthcare, and support for congress participation from Roche, Biogen, Novartis Healthcare, Merck, and Sanofi Genzyme. PVL and MHR have nothing to disclose. HHN has received financial compensation for travels and consultations from Novartis Healthcare, Biogen, Teva, Sanofi‐Genzyme, and Roche, has received a research grant from the Danish MS society, and served as a board member on the MS Society Research Council. ZI has received speakers’ honoraria and/or research grants from Biogen, Roche, Sanofi, Novartis, Merck, Lundbeckfonden, and Scleroseforeningen, has been member of advisory boards at Alexion, Biogen, Sanofi, Merck, Roche, and Novartis, was member of the adjudication relapse committee in the SAKuraStar and SakuraSky trials, and has been principal investigator in studies sponsored by Biogen, Merck, and Sanofi."],"id":"S01-000.00-610978","identifier":[{"id":"85119426178","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34799851","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-83f47819-02c8-4efa-9a4c-bb40738a544b"],"keyword":["9HPT","Brain/diagnostic imaging","Disability Evaluation","Humans","MRI","MSIS","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Middle Aged","Multiple Sclerosis, Chronic Progressive/diagnostic imaging","T25FW","Walking","multiple sclerosis","observational study","scale properties","secondary progressive"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B4166E657C3D99249EBC44C0BDD5711"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195733336/ane.13554_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"filadelfia danish epilepsy hospital","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-FILA","l3nn":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","namevar":["Epilepsihospitalet Filadelfia"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-FILA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asta","key":"theodorsdottirpau","last":"Theodorsdottir","locid":"7b24fc83-23dc-461d-a339-d2b16d2b4d8e","name":"Theódórsdóttir, Ásta","name_org":"Theodorsdottir, Asta","orcid":"0000-0001-7894-611X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Veldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Hvilsted","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e1703e06-01b8-4d46-a1d1-4c4d5af99fa5","name":"Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","orcid":"0000-0002-7319-1368","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zsolt","key":"illespau","last":"Illes","locid":"3e0aeebb-ee40-4c3d-9cee-47e786e6f12e","name":"Illes, Zsolt","orcid":"0000-0001-9655-0450","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Henrik","key":"ravnborgpau","last":"Ravnborg","name":"Ravnborg, Mads Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34799851"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ane.13554","issn":["00016314","16000404"],"issn_org":["00016314"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Neurologica Scandinavica","pages":"332-347","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Neurologica Scandinavica","volume":"145"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119426178"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-83f47819-02c8-4efa-9a4c-bb40738a544b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Multiple sclerosis impairment scale and brain MRI in secondary progressive multiple sclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-610978","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Funding Acknowledgements Type of funding sources: Private grant(s) and/or Sponsorship. Main funding source(s): The Danish Heart Foundation Odense University Hospital and Rigshospitalets Research Council. Background Acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock (AMICS) comprises a heterogenous population with high mortality. Insight in timing and cause of death may improve understanding of the condition and aid individualization of treatment. Purpose To determine the cause and timing of death in patients admitted with AMICS. Methods This was a retrospective, multi-center observational cohort study based on 1716 AMICS patients treated during the period of 2010-2017, of whom 904 died prior to hospital discharge from either of two tertiary cardiac centers in Denmark providing advanced care for cardiogenic shock for 3.9 million inhabitants. Patients admitted with AMICS were identified through national registries and review of individual patient charts. Only patients dying during hospitalization were eligible. Cause of death was categorized as caused by progressive cardiac failure, multi organ failure or due to neurological damage. Time to death was calculated in hours from first medical contact to death. Results Among 904 patients with AMICS who died prior to hospital discharge (median age 72 years [IQR: 63 - 79], 70% men), 342 (38%) patients had suffered an out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). The most frequent cause of death was primary cardiac (54%), whereas 24% died of neurologic injury and 20% of multi-organ failure. Time to death was 13 hours [IQR: 5, 43] for cardiac failure; 140 hours [IQR: 95, 209] in neurological injury; and 137 hours [IQR: 59, 321] in multi-organ failure, p","author_count":13,"contributors":["Witten Davodian, L","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Josiassen, J","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Hassager, C","Schmidt, Henrik","Kjaergaard, J","Holmvang, L","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Moeller, JE"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-626136"],"event":{"end":"2022-03-19","start":"2022-03-18","title":"ESC Acute CardioVascular Care 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"timing and causes of death in acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjacc/zuac041.042","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-626136","ids":["sdu-b88bf35e-016e-4c43-8dbf-2b65b5ec8c53"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-06B550FD0106F034C91157FF6F78DFA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjacc/zuac041.042","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":"wittendavodianpau","last":"Witten Davodian","name":"Witten Davodian, L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"JKP","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c1f7b9d-9e43-45ec-aa4d-310cdce6686a","name":"Larsen, Jeppe P.","name_org":"Larsen, JKP","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"AL","key":"povlsenpau","last":"Povlsen","locid":"085efe15-36a1-434b-9b9e-b4341cd84a0d","name":"Povlsen, Amalie Ling","name_org":"Povlsen, AL","orcid":"0000-0001-6044-8841","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","name":"Josiassen, J","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"OKL","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, OKL","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"NLJ","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"f71f56f5-4f36-4de5-a7ae-e5e51f101a83","name":"Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","name_org":"Udesen, NLJ","orcid":"0000-0003-1542-3260","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","name":"Hassager, C","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"H","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","name_org":"Schmidt, H","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, J","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, L","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"LO","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, LO","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"HB","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, HB","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"JE","key":"moellerpau","last":"Moeller","name":"Moeller, JE","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjacc/zuac041.042","issn":["20488726","20488734"],"issn_org":["20488734"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"European Heart Journal: Acute Cardiovascular Care","paperid":"20074","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal: Acute Cardiovascular Care","title_org":"European Heart Journal - Acute Cardiovascular Care","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b88bf35e-016e-4c43-8dbf-2b65b5ec8c53"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Timing and causes of death in acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-626136","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Baggrund: Patienter med kroniske smerter kan have behov for at arbejde med livsstilsforbedringer som en del af den tværfaglige rehabilitering. Tidligere studier har vist ergoterapiens potentiale i en livsstilsorienteret tilgang til smertebehandling, men der er behov for yderligere forskning i dansk kontekst. Formål: Som forberedelse til et randomiseret kontrolleret studie, blev den ergoterapeutiske intervention REVEAL(OT) [Redesign your EVEryday Activities and Lifestyle with Occupational Therapy] pilotafprøvet som et tillæg til det nuværende tværfaglige behandlingstilbud på et regionalt smertecenter i Region Sjælland. Metoder: Ambulante patienter med kroniske smerter (n=40) mellem 18 og 65 år (85% kvinder) henvist til Tværfagligt Smertecenter på Næstved sygehus deltog i undersøgelsen. Ergoterapeuter har samarbejdet med deltagerne omkring deres personlige mål i relation til daglige aktiviteter, regelmæssig bevægelse og spisevaner. Primære effektmål for studiet var prædefinerede progressionskriterier (ift. progression til det randomiserede studie) for rekruttering, accept af undersøgelsesprocedurer, retention, deltagelsesprocent, uønskede hændelser og planmæssig levering af programmet. Sekundære effektmål var helbredsrelateret livskvalitet, aktivitetsudførelse, aktivitetsbalance, kroppens antropometri og smertesensitisering. Tendenser blev monitoreret ved at sammenligne før- og eftermålingerne. Fokusgruppeinterviews med 8 patienter og 4 klinikere blev gennemført for en dybere indsigt i, hvordan REVEAL(OT) blev oplevet. Resultater: Foreløbige analyser af data fra deltagere (n=30) som har afsluttet programmet, demonstrerede acceptabelt-til-godt niveau i opfyldelsen af de primære effektmål, samt en tendens til signifikant forbedring i de sekundære mål: aktivitetsudførelse (1.76 [95% CI 1.22; 2.29]) og tilfredsheden med aktivitetsudførelsen (1.88 [95% CI 1.01; 2.75]). REVEAL(OT) medvirkede til øget accept af livet med kroniske smerter hos patienterne og deres empowerment for livsstilsændringer. Patienter og klinikere foreslog en række forbedringer i interventionen. Konklusioner: Pilotafprøvningen af det ergoterapeutiske program REVEAL(OT) har givet et indblik i, hvordan der kan arbejdes med daglige aktiviteter og livsstil som led i den tværfaglige smertebehandling. Et randomiseret studie skal afdække effekten af det ergoterapeutiske livsstilsorienterede program for kroniske smertepatienter.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard","Skou, Søren Thorgaard","Larsen, Anette Enemark","Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","Polianskis, Romanes","Simonÿ, Charlotte","Søndergaard, Jens","Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-641716"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-02","place":"Nyborg, dk","start":"2022-06-01","title":"Ergo22: Styrket forskning - styrket praksis","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ergoterapi i den tværfaglige behandling af kroniske smerter erfaringer fra en pilotafprøvning occupational therapy in multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment experiences from a feasibility study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-641716","ids":["sdu-ef351d1f-ed95-43bf-bf28-09b4e5a38ad8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AE4978FAD2C9C3AE808B2F8AFE57A529"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, User Perspectives and Community-based Interventions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["UCC Metropol"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Svetlana Solgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8af11fa7-c3b5-4b92-b8c7-54cc4889b827","name":"Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-3694-4236","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Thorgaard","key":"skoupau","last":"Skou","locid":"656a59cf-32bc-4190-b072-4adf47d954c1","name":"Skou, Søren Thorgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-7059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette Enemark","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anette Enemark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bjarke","key":"vægterpau","last":"Vægter","locid":"b35dd901-cb2f-4f50-a2c5-65e1a4752f02","name":"Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0002-7707-9947","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Romanes","key":"polianskispau","last":"Polianskis","name":"Polianskis, Romanes","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"simonÿpau","last":"Simonÿ","locid":"6c2dbf49-1a55-4aa3-a990-1549e39274dd","name":"Simonÿ, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1189-2967","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette Reffstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7b0b955e-4090-479a-8bef-6fd6ad983680","name":"Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2412-5989","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Region Zealand","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ef351d1f-ed95-43bf-bf28-09b4e5a38ad8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ergoterapi i den tværfaglige behandling af kroniske smerter– erfaringer fra en pilotafprøvning [Occupational therapy in multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment - experiences from a feasibility study]","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-641716","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background:  Essential thrombocythemia (ET), along with polycythemia vera (PV) and primary myelofibrosis (PMF), belongs to the Philadelphia chromosome negative myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPNs). Chronic inflammation is considered a hallmark in the pathogenesis and progression of the MPNs. The human gut microbiota helps regulate and mature the immune system, digest food, protect against pathogens and induce hematopoiesis. As our immune system constantly interacts with our gut microbiota any change to the microbiota could have significant impact on the overall health of the patient. This influence of the gut microbiota on the patient has been described as being involved in the pathogenesis of several diseases, such as obesity and diabetes mellitus. We recently added to this list by showing that the gut microbiota in patients with PV differs significantly from that of healthy controls (HCs), however the composition of the gut microbiota in patients with ET remains unknown. Thus, we hypothesized that patients with ET have a distinct gut microbiota signature compared with that of HCs. This study is the first to explore the gut microbiota in patients with ET specifically and compared with that of HCs. Methods: We included patients with ET, diagnosed according to the 2016 WHO classification. Included patients had not received antibiotics within the last 2 months and no change in cytoreductive treatment had occurred within the last 3 months. Comorbidities were assessed using the Charlson Comorbidity Index score (CCI). The gut microbiota was characterized using amplicon-based next generation sequencing of the V3-V4 region of the 16S ribosomal unit while dada2 was used for taxonomic classification. Alpha diversity, beta diversity and linear discriminant analysis effect size (LEfSe), were used to assess the microbiota between and within the patient groups. Alpha diversity describes the richness and evenness within a sample and beta diversity the difference in composition between the samples, while LEfSe is used for differential abundance analysis. Results: In total, 54 patients with ET (median age 68, range 38-83) and 42 HCs (median age 71, range 66-74), fulfilled the inclusion criteria. Patients with ET had a higher CCI score (p=0.038) compared with the HCs. Thirty-six patients had the JAK2V617F mutation. Seven were positive for calreticulin (CALR), three for myeloproliferative leukemia virus gene (MPL), two for CALR+JAK2V617F mutations, and 6 were triple negative. The treatments were: no cytoreductive treatment (n=15), PEG-interferon-α2 (n=11), anagrelide (ANG)(n=3), hydroxyurea (HU)(n=23) and HU+ANG(n=2). Patients with ET had a significantly higher observed richness (number of different bacteria present) compared with HCs (median, 283.5 vs 191.5; p<0.001), however, no significant difference was found in alpha diversity. The bacterial composition differed significantly between ET and HCs (p=0.004 and R=0.063). Eight taxa, with a relative abundance >1%, differed between ET and HCs. Patients with ET had a lower relative abundance of the phylum Firmicutes (p=0.03), class Clostridia (p=0.001), order Oscillospirales (p<0.01), and family Ruminococcaceae (p<0.001) compared with HCs. On genus level, patients with ET had a lower relative abundance of Faecalibacterium (p <0.001). While all mutations were associated with a significantly different microbiota in ET compared with HCs, ET patients who only had the JAK2V617F differed to a larger degree. Conclusion: The gut microbiota in patients with ET differed significantly from that of HCs, both in regard to richness and bacterial composition. The relative abundance of several taxa within the phylum Firmicutes differed significantly, with ET patients having a lower relative abundance in general. These differences appear to be more pronounced in patients who have the JAK2V617F mutation. Thus, it needs to be elucidated if the change of the microbiota is the cause or the consequence of the disease. Is it the increased inflammatory response which changes the microbiota or is it the change in microbiota which aggravates the inflammatory effects of the JAK2V617F mutation?","author_count":16,"contributors":["Eickhardt-Dalboge, Christina Schjellerup Schjellerup","Ingham, Anna Cacilia","Andersen, Lee O'Brien","Nielsen, Henrik V.","Fuursted, Kurt","Stensvold, Christen Rune","Larsen, Morten Kranker","Kjaer, Lasse","Christensen, Sarah F.","Knudsen, Trine A.","Skov, Vibe","Ellervik, Christina","Olsen, Lars Rønn","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","Elmer Christensen, Jens Jorgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-676481"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patients with essential thrombocythemia have a gut microbiota that differs from healthy controls","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-676481","identifier":[{"id":"000893230305099","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-1545b4bc-30bd-4512-b95c-28c9dbb65ca9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6B8F4A8FD437A885F4517BD2CBC54E07"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Bioinformatics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Bioinformatics, Single Cell Omics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Schjellerup Schjellerup","key":"eickhardtdalbogechristinaschjellerupschjelleruppau","last":"Eickhardt-Dalboge","name":"Eickhardt-Dalboge, Christina Schjellerup Schjellerup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Cacilia","key":"inghamannacaciliapau","last":"Ingham","name":"Ingham, Anna Cacilia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lee O'Brien","key":"andersenleeobrienpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lee O'Brien","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik V.","key":"nielsenhenrikvpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik V.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kurt","key":"fuurstedkurtpau","last":"Fuursted","name":"Fuursted, Kurt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christen Rune","key":"stensvoldchristenrunepau","last":"Stensvold","name":"Stensvold, Christen Rune","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Kranker","key":"larsenmortenkrankerpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Morten Kranker","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"kjaerlassepau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Lasse","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah F.","key":"christensensarahfpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Sarah F.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine A.","key":"knudsentrineapau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Trine A.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibe","key":"skovvibepau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Vibe","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"ellervikchristinapau","last":"Ellervik","name":"Ellervik, Christina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Ronn","key":"olsenlarsrønnpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"90ca0980-3661-4875-a116-e47082f82351","name":"Olsen, Lars Rønn","name_org":"Olsen, Lars Ronn","orcid":"0000-0002-6725-7850","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Carl","key":"hasselbalchhanscarlpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaohui Chen","key":"nielsenxiaohuichenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Jorgen","key":"elmerchristensenjensjorgenpau","last":"Elmer Christensen","name":"Elmer Christensen, Jens Jorgen","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1182/blood-2022-166031","issn":["00064971","15280020"],"issn_org":["00064971"],"issue":"Issue Supplement 1","journal":"Blood","pages":"12178-12179","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Blood","volume":"140"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1545b4bc-30bd-4512-b95c-28c9dbb65ca9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Patients with Essential Thrombocythemia Have a Gut Microbiota That Differs from Healthy Controls","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-676481","year":"2022","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The myeloproliferative neoplasms are associated with chronic kidney disease but whether clonal haematopoiesis of indeterminate potential (CHIP) is associated with impaired kidney function is unknown. In the Danish General Suburban Population Study (N = 19 958) from 2010 to 2013, 645 individuals were positive for JAK2V617F (N = 613) or CALR (N = 32) mutations. Mutation-positive individuals without haematological malignancy were defined as having CHIP (N = 629). We used multiple and inverse probability weighted (IPW)-adjusted linear regression analysis to estimate adjusted mean (95% confidence interval) differences in estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR; ml/min/1.73 m2) by mutation status, variant allele frequency (VAF%), blood cell counts, and neutrophil-to-lymphocyte ratio (NLR). We performed 11-year longitudinal follow-up of eGFR in all individuals. Compared to CHIP-negative individuals, the mean differences in eGFR were −5.6 (−10.3, −0.8, p =.02) for CALR, −11.9 (−21.4, −2.4, p = 0.01) for CALR type 2, and −10.1 (−18.1, −2.2, p =.01) for CALR with VAF ≥ 1%. The IPW-adjusted linear regression analyses showed similar results. NLR was negatively associated with eGFR. Individuals with CALR type 2 had a worse 11-year longitudinal follow-up on eGFR compared to CHIP-negative individuals (p =.004). In conclusion, individuals with CALR mutations, especially CALR type 2, had impaired kidney function compared to CHIP-negative individuals as measured by a lower eGFR at baseline and during 11-year follow-up.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Larsen, Morten Kranker","Skov, Vibe","Kjær, Lasse","Møller-Palacino, Natascha A.","Pedersen, Rasmus K.","Andersen, Morten","Ottesen, Johnny T.","Cordua, Sabrina","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Dahl, Morten","Knudsen, Trine A.","Eickhardt-Dalbøge, Christina Schjellerup","Koschmieder, Steffen","Pedersen, Kasper M.","Çolak, Yunus","Bojesen, Stig E","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Stiehl, Thomas","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Ellervik, Christina"],"cuid":["S02-087.50-040422"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard Medical School","RWTH Aachen University"],"keyword":["CALR","CHIP","Clonal haematopoiesis of indeterminate potential","EGFR","Epidemiology","JAK2V617F","Population Studies","impaired kidney function"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clonal haematopoiesis of indeterminate potential and impaired kidney function a danish general population study with 000000000011 years follow up","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ejh.13845","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.50-040422","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9804367","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36054308","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85136518495","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-15c1d4d4-7b83-492f-8342-285edd345be9","ruc-9a54dcba-1bab-496b-953f-8101d3fbc4d8"],"keyword":["CALR","CHIP","JAK2V617F","clonal haematopoiesis of indeterminate potential","eGFR","epidemiology","impaired kidney function","population studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-093124F9FAF7DAA86B0FA32E3EACAEBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/323846769/European_J_of_Haematology_2022_Larsen_Clonal_haematopoiesis_of_indeterminate_potential_and_impaired_kidney_function_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ejh.13845","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/82471288/European_J_of_Haematology_2022_Larsen_Clonal_haematopoiesis_of_indeterminate_potential_and_impaired_kidney_function_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"rwth aachen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"RWTH Aachen University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten K.","key":"larsenmortenkrankerpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"c40e7114-22be-4f3d-a2d1-a5ea65fc1ec6","name":"Larsen, Morten Kranker","name_org":"Larsen, Morten K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vibe","key":"skovvibepau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Vibe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lasse","key":"kjærlassepau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Lasse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Natascha A.","key":"møllerpalacinonataschaapau","last":"Møller-Palacino","name":"Møller-Palacino, Natascha A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Rasmus K.","key":"pedersenrasmuskristofferpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"2de16c98-24b3-4f5d-a6ab-cef1902ad008","name":"Pedersen, Rasmus Kristoffer","name_org":"Pedersen, Rasmus K.","orcid":"0000-0001-5946-8220","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"andersenmortenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"c3e27de5-fa0e-4dde-9dd5-249374492239","name":"Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7582-0685","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Johnny T.","key":"ottesenjohnnytpau","last":"Ottesen","locid":"bed8426a-9bf1-481a-ad64-cf70b31b0d16","name":"Ottesen, Johnny T.","orcid":"0000-0002-9786-0300","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Sabrina","key":"corduasabrinapau","last":"Cordua","name":"Cordua, Sabrina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"poulsenhenrikenghusenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","name_org":"Poulsen, Henrik E.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"dahlmortenpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"f5409642-33da-4a45-8f34-725572c574fb","name":"Dahl, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-6686-312X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Trine A.","key":"knudsentrineapau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Kn