stpau","last":"Frost","locid":"26ef8020-923a-483f-bd05-7f0c9d47d99c","name":"Frost, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-5608-1589","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Moustapha","key":"kassempau","last":"Kassem","locid":"49b7ae18-6230-4bbd-a8e2-7ddd247dfe50","name":"Kassem, Moustapha","orcid":"0000-0003-1557-0869","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lilian B.","key":"ousagerpau","last":"Ousager","locid":"58559d8d-61ee-42b3-aeac-cfd62bdf9b70","name":"Ousager, Lilian Bomme","name_org":"Ousager, Lilian B.","orcid":"0000-0001-9936-2201","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja L.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"548bce44-5f6e-4762-af76-57862429f292","name":"Frederiksen, Anja Lisbeth","name_org":"Frederiksen, Anja L.","orcid":"0000-0002-7944-8910","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10184813","14765438"],"issn_org":["10184813"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"European Journal of Human Genetics","pages":"205","paperid":"P06.014.C","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Human Genetics","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dcefa044-262f-4669-a1ce-50815bb25fef","sdu-77414ac0-72b5-480b-b973-15320381598c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Familial Multiple Lipomatosis - analyses of genetic etiology by whole genome sequencing and delineation of the clinical phenotype","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.83-010519","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose — Patients having a knee arthroplasty revision for the indication “pain without loos-ening” may have a higher risk of re-revisions than patients revised for other indications. The primary aim of this study was to compare the survival of knee arthroplasties revised for “pain without loosening” compared with “aseptic loos-ening.” The second was to investigate the prosthesis survival rates in 3 surgical subgroups (total knee arthroplasty (TKA)–TKA; partial revision (revision of tibial or femoral component); unicompartmental knee arthroplasty–TKA) and to compare the prosthesis survival rates for 1997–2009 and 2010–2018. Patients and methods — 4,299 revisions were identified in the period 1997–2018 from the Danish Knee Arthro-plasty Register. Of these, 1,111 (26%) were performed due to “pain without loosening” without any other indications, 674 (16%) due to “pain without loosening” combined with other indications, and 2,514 (59%) due to “aseptic loosen-ing”. Survival analysis was performed by a Cox multivariate analysis and Kaplan–Meier curves were presented. Results — The cumulated proportions of re-revision after 2, 5, and 20 years were 12% (95% CI 10–14), 18% (CI 16–20), and 23% (CI 20–25) for “pain without loosen-ing” versus 11% (CI 9.3–12), 16% (CI 14–17), and 19% (CI 18–21) for “aseptic loosening.” There were no statistically significant differences between the 2 indications in repeated analyses for each of the surgical subgroups. The hazard ratio for re-revision comparing “pain without loosening” with “aseptic loosening” was 1.03 (CI 0.87–1.2). The 8-year risk of re-revision for “pain without loosening” was 22% (CI 19–26) versus 22% (CI 20–25) for “aseptic loosening” in the period from 1997–2009, and 18% (CI 15–22) versus 14% (CI 13–16) in the period from 2010–2018. Interpretation — The risk of re-revision was similar for patients having a knee arthroplasty revision for the indication “pain without loosening” compared with “aseptic loos-ening.” However, we observed a slight improvement of prosthesis survival rates after revisions for both indications from 1997–2009 to 2010–2018. We cannot recommend for or against revision in cases with “pain without loosening” based on these data alone.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Schrøder, Henrik M.","Troelsen, Anders","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S02-099.59-045214"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prosthesis survival after revision knee arthroplasty for pain without loosening versus aseptic loosening a danish nationwide study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17453674.2021.1999069","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was approved by the Danish Data Protection Agency (Journal no. 19/14416). Ethical approval was not needed as the study was non-interventional. The study was conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki. The study was funded by the Danish Rheumatism Association. The authors have no competing interests to declare. The authors acknowledge Odense Patient data Explorative Network for their help and advice on this study. Furthermore, they thank Odense University Hospital and the University of Southern Denmark for their financial support."],"id":"S02-099.59-045214","identifier":[{"id":"85121498388","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34906032","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8815427","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-aaee3dcc-59ca-4f91-b3f2-34ac1f26782f","sdu-e8eb8131-6afb-4657-bfe8-679e88c857f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A9A84CAC7C70AEBB40E68C8F5FB748A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/312770539/document_3_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/197564913/16._15641_ARNDT_D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17453674.2021.1999069","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Bollerup","key":"arndtpau","last":"Arndt","locid":"a2513ef2-9214-48ee-b84f-bea6ef1717ac","name":"Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","orcid":"0000-0001-8258-7922","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik M.","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","locid":"e123aeda-8b2e-44a9-b78f-34d1a4c942af","name":"Schrøder, Henrik Morville","name_org":"Schrøder, Henrik M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Anders","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"49cb6bcf-2ff6-41af-a356-a2a09c2ce7ba","name":"Troelsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0132-8182","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34906032"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17453674.2021.1999069","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"103-110","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121498388"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-aaee3dcc-59ca-4f91-b3f2-34ac1f26782f","sdu-e8eb8131-6afb-4657-bfe8-679e88c857f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prosthesis survival after revision knee arthroplasty for “pain without loosening” versus “aseptic loosening” : a Danish nationwide study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.59-045214","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: The majority of persons who die by suicide have a mental disorder. Preventive strategies should include addressing social and psychological factors and the treatment of the mental disorder. Aim: We aimed to identify breaches in clinical care and identify areas for quality improvement initiatives. Method: An aggregate analysis of suicides reported as adverse events during 2012-2016 to Psychiatry, North Denmark Region was carried out. We developed an audit chart and identified items through (a) medical chart review and (b) consensus meetings in an expert panel. Results: A total of 35 cases were analyzed. Suicide risk assessments were adequately documented in the medial chart in six of 35 cases. Risk assessments emphasized suicidal ideation rather than well-known risk factors such as previous suicide attempts, substance abuse, physical illness, or job loss. Relatives were involved in four of 35 of the risk assessments. The panel suggested nine areas for quality improvement. Limitations: Most people who die by suicide are not seen in mental health facilities prior to suicide, and hence conclusions can only be generalized to these patients. Information on the gap between \"Work-as-Done\"and \"Work-As-Imagined\"was not recognized. Conclusion: Most of the risk assessments among suicides reported as adverse events to our mental health facilities were insufficient. Quality improvement initiatives focusing on training, documentation, involving relatives, communication, and data sharing must be planned to improve clinical care.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mackenhauer, Julie","Winsløv, Jan-Henrik","Holmskov, Jens","Brødsgaard, Inger","Larsen, Tina Gram","Mainz, Jan"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-009869"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mackenhauer, Julie"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Haifa"],"keyword":["Adverse event","Audit","Humans","Psychiatry","Quality Improvement","Risk Factors","Suicidal Ideation","Suicide","Suicide Attempted prevention control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of suicides reported as adverse events in psychiatry resulted in nine quality improvement initiatives","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85106174314&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-009869","identifier":[{"id":"85106174314","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34003020","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-cdc99c3f-1711-4d2b-a200-6e252e66e2eb","sdu-49bc8e96-449c-4da2-a003-03c97592378f"],"keyword":["Humans","Psychiatry","Risk Factors","Suicidal Ideation","Suicide, Attempted/prevention & control","adverse event","audit","quality improvement","suicide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E603067676C6255DA55B34B62B81E3CC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Psychiatry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Danish Center for Clinical Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"il","key":"university of haifa","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"University of Haifa","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie","key":"mackenhauerpau","last":"Mackenhauer","locid":"a2416ac8-315b-4cb0-91a6-a962890a59c6","name":"Mackenhauer, Julie","orcid":"0000-0001-7155-4105","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"winsløvpau","last":"Winsløv","locid":"9e8a97e8-3b61-4afc-86b4-733cdd740bf5","name":"Winsløv, Jan-Henrik","name_org":"Winsløv, Jan Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"holmskovpau","last":"Holmskov","locid":"e5818293-317d-42c4-aef1-2a12a22f2259","name":"Holmskov, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Inger","key":"brødsgaardpau","last":"Brødsgaard","locid":"d67ca41f-eddd-4cb5-bf95-30d012fbe0b6","name":"Brødsgaard, Inger","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Gram","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2fb0d668-bdb6-4d83-8285-0466d253adbc","name":"Larsen, Tina Gram","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"mainzpau","last":"Mainz","locid":"fadbea42-81be-48a2-afb2-c868f9dfa4f5","name":"Mainz, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-0242-9233","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34003020"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1027/0227-5910/a000787","issn":["02275910","21512396"],"issn_org":["02275910"],"issue":"4","journal":"Crisis: The Journal of Crisis Intervention and Suicide Prevention","pages":"307-314","publisher":"Hogrefe Publishing","status":"p","title":"Crisis: The Journal of Crisis Intervention and Suicide Prevention","title_org":"Crisis","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106174314"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cdc99c3f-1711-4d2b-a200-6e252e66e2eb","sdu-49bc8e96-449c-4da2-a003-03c97592378f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Analysis of Suicides Reported as Adverse Events in Psychiatry Resulted in Nine Quality Improvement Initiatives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-009869","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"High numbers of harbor porpoises (Phocoena phocoena) end up as bycatch in gillnets every year. Acoustic alarms (pingers) have been demonstrated to be an efficient mitigation tool to prevent bycatch of this species; however, little is known about the behavioral reactions of wild porpoises to pingers. This knowledge is important for optimizing the design and use of pingers. We tracked 16 wild porpoises with a drone and recorded their behavior before and during exposure to pinger sounds. Range from the pinger to the porpoise was 158–797 m when the pinger was first activated. In four of the exposures, with pinger-to-porpoise ranges of 199–521 m, reaction to the pinger was strong avoidance behavior with increased swimming speed heading away from the pinger. Average number of surfacings decreased from 3.4 surfacings/min before pinging to 2.8 surfacings/min during pinging. Eight animals were lost from the drone’s field of view as soon as the pinger playback started, indicating that they were either diving deep or speeding away from the area very rapidly. Four animals did not respond to pinger sounds, demonstrating a diversity in the behavioral response. Neither the behavior of porpoises (i.e., foraging, socializing and traveling) before sound exposure, the animal’s initial direction in relation to the sound source, nor the porpoise-to-pinger range affected their reaction in relation to the pinger. Pingers can cause very strong aversive reactions in harbor porpoises, which explains their efficiency in reducing bycatch. The strong aversive reactions may suggest that pinger use should be limited to critical time periods and regions, or that more focus needs to be put on developing acoustic devices which cause less severe behavioral reactions. At the same time, this study shows that 25 % of animals may not react to pinger sounds, indicating a great diversity in behavioral responses.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Brennecke, Dennis","Siebert, Ursula","Kindt-Larsen, Lotte","Midtiby, Henrik Skov","Egemose, Henrik Dyrberg","Ortiz, Sara Torres","Knickmeier, Katrin","Wahlberg, Magnus"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-037536"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wahlberg, Magnus"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Institute for Science and Mathematics Education","Max Planck Institute","University of Veterinary Medicine Hannover","University of Veterinary Medicine Hannover, Foundation"],"keyword":["Acoustic deterrent","Bycatch","Drone","Phocoena phocoena","Pinger"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the fine scale behavior of harbor porpoises towards pingers","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fishres.2022.106437","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Field work was conducted within the project “Reduction of harbor porpoise bycatch in protected areas”, funded by European Maritime and Fisheries Fund (EMFF), granted to LKL."],"id":"S02-100.00-037536","identifier":[{"id":"85135100952","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-dc16a130-3c17-4045-bbba-b2004cd40ff9","sdu-f3b526d8-192e-474d-aa0c-74f11f8b80f6"],"keyword":["Acoustic deterrent","Bycatch","Drone","Phocoena phocoena","Pinger"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4E82AFE8F60248ED4A3FE8D81E33054E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/205392611/The_fine_scale_behavior_of_harbor_porpo...pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/282110927/1_s2.0_S0165783622002144_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fishres.2022.106437","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of veterinary medicine hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Veterinary Medicine Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for science and mathematics education","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Institute for Science and Mathematics Education","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of veterinary medicine hannover foundation","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Veterinary Medicine Hannover, Foundation","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Ecosystem based Marine Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"max planck institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis","key":"brenneckepau","last":"Brennecke","locid":"8ed0b1ab-aa1d-468a-9fae-675655e9bade","name":"Brennecke, Dennis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ursula","key":"siebertpau","last":"Siebert","name":"Siebert, Ursula","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte","key":"kindtlarsenpau","last":"Kindt-Larsen","locid":"3f77db7c-02d7-4abf-af1c-253ce0a508aa","name":"Kindt-Larsen, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4696-5943","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Skov","key":"midtibypau","last":"Midtiby","locid":"ef2c97e9-dc8e-4765-b064-a5c07e2c66b3","name":"Midtiby, Henrik Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-3310-5680","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Dyrberg","key":"egemosepau","last":"Egemose","locid":"a5f582ab-443e-4f57-9105-601763fe5a40","name":"Egemose, Henrik Dyrberg","orcid":"0000-0002-6765-8216","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Torres","key":"ortizpau","last":"Ortiz","locid":"9a99be93-409c-4c17-a5e5-36b20b8f450d","name":"Ortiz, Sara Torres","orcid":"0000-0003-1065-9194","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrin","key":"knickmeierpau","last":"Knickmeier","name":"Knickmeier, Katrin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","locid":"753afa47-2a49-47fc-b23a-30f6b0a2bdb6","name":"Wahlberg, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0002-8239-5485","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fishres.2022.106437","issn":["01657836","18726763"],"issn_org":["01657836"],"journal":"Fisheries Research","paperid":"106437","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fisheries Research","volume":"255"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135100952"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-dc16a130-3c17-4045-bbba-b2004cd40ff9","sdu-f3b526d8-192e-474d-aa0c-74f11f8b80f6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The fine-scale behavior of harbor porpoises towards pingers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-037536","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: It is uncertain if patients undergoing revision knee arthroplasty for “pain without loosening” are relieved of pain. This study aimed to compare pre- and postoperative analgesic consumption by patients undergoing revision for “pain without loosening” versus “aseptic loosening” and to determine predictors for postoperative long-term opioid use. Methods: A retrospective nationwide study of 1,037 revisions for “pain without loosening” and 2,317 revisions for “aseptic loosening” during 1997-2018 from the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register was carried out. Analgesic use was defined by prescription reimbursement, and long-term opioid use by prescription reimbursement in 4 consecutive quarters. Results: In the preoperative year, 37% and 29% of patients revised for “pain without loosening” and “aseptic loosening” were opioid users compared to 32% and 30% in the postoperative year. Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) use was significantly lower postoperatively for both indications (35% versus 28% for “pain without loosening” and 33% versus 25% for “aseptic loosening”). Use of other analgesics was unchanged. Long-term opioid use increased postoperatively by 4% for patients with “pain without loosening” (P = .029) and by 3% for “aseptic loosening” (P = .003). New long-term opioid users (without preoperative long-term use) were 9% for “pain without loosening” and 8% for “aseptic loosening“. Predictors of new long-term opioid use were other opioid-requiring diagnoses or procedures within the first postoperative year, Charlson Comorbidity Index (CCI) ≥3, and preoperative long-term NSAID use. Conclusion: The consumption of opioids decreased slightly after knee arthroplasty revision for the indication “pain without loosening”, but not for “aseptic loosening”. The amount of new long-term opioid users increased for both indications.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Schrøder, Henrik M.","Troelsen, Anders","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-040455"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup"],"keyword":["Analgesic","Analgesics Opioid therapeutic use","Anti Inflammatory Agents Non Steroidal","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee methods","Denmark","Humans","Opioid","Pain","Prosthesis Failure","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Revision","Revision knee arthroplasty","Total knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opioid and analgesic use before and after revision knee arthroplasty for the indications pain without loosening versus aseptic loosening a danish nationwide study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2022.03.077","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-040455","identifier":[{"id":"85129019748","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35378235","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-16995c80-5dd2-4b13-8189-6b0bfabd5d17","sdu-7611bd56-5f35-4dfe-8a08-293181dc9071"],"keyword":["Analgesics, Opioid/therapeutic use","Anti-Inflammatory Agents, Non-Steroidal","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/methods","Denmark","Humans","Prosthesis Failure","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","analgesic","opioid","pain","revision","revision knee arthroplasty","total knee arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6C4C5A8694340E2D4C0857759C62FDFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2022.03.077","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type"