"SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Occupational therapy lifestyle intervention added to multidisciplinary treatment for adults living with chronic pain : A feasibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.21-025041","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The clinical benefit of implementing the quick Sepsis-related Organ Failure Assessment (qSOFA) instead of early warning scores (EWS) to screen all hospitalised patients for critical illness has yet to be investigated in a large, multicentre study. METHODS: We conducted a cohort study including all hospitalised patients ≥18 years with EWS recorded at hospitals in the Central Denmark Region during the year 2016. The primary outcome was intensive care unit (ICU) admission and/or death within 2 days following an initial EWS. Prognostic accuracy was examined using sensitivity, specificity, negative predictive value (NPV) and positive predictive value (PPV). Discriminative accuracy was examined by the area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC). RESULTS: Among 97 332 evaluated patients, 1714 (1.8%) experienced the primary outcome. The qSOFA ≥2 was less sensitive (11.7% (95% CI: 10.2% to 13.3%) vs 25.1% (95% CI: 23.1% to 27.3%)) and more specific (99.3% (95% CI: 99.2% to 99.3%) vs 97.5% (95% CI: 97.4% to 97.6%)) than EWS ≥5. The NPV was similar for the two scores (EWS ≥5, 98.6% (95% CI: 98.6% to 98.7%) and qSOFA ≥2, 98.4% (95% CI: 98.3% to 98.5%)), while the PPV was 15.1% (95% CI: 13.8% to 16.5%) for EWS ≥5 and 22.4% (95% CI: 19.7% to 25.3%) for qSOFA ≥2. The AUROC was 0.72 (95% CI: 0.70 to 0.73) for EWS and 0.66 (95% CI: 0.65 to 0.67) for qSOFA. CONCLUSION: The qSOFA was less sensitive (qSOFA ≥2 vs EWS ≥5) and discriminatively accurate than the EWS for predicting ICU admission and/or death within 2 days after an initial EWS. This study did not support replacing EWS with qSOFA in all hospitalised patients.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Svingel, Lise Skovgaard","Storgaard, Merete","Esen, Buket Öztürk","Ebdrup, Lotte","Ahrensberg, Jette Møller","Larsen, Kim Michael","Nørgaard, Mette","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-166594"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Svingel, Lise Skovgaard"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Acute care","Assessment","Epidemiology","Intensive care","Systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic and discriminative accuracy of the quick sepsis related organ failure assessment compared with an early warning score a danish cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85137124188","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-166594","identifier":[{"id":"000721837500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85137124188","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34725109","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4178173e-14d5-4170-b3aa-a47762e24027"],"keyword":["acute care","assessment","epidemiology","intensive care","systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26AB6CCD26B7662E34E5E358D3BA94B1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Skovgaard","key":"svingelpau","last":"Svingel","locid":"f5bcee60-2dd4-4605-8a72-5321c72b1210","name":"Svingel, Lise Skovgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merete","key":"storgaardpau","last":"Storgaard","locid":"2c2b23fe-581a-47b7-9194-ab66b60773d3","name":"Storgaard, Merete","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5963","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Buket Öztürk","key":"esenpau","last":"Esen","locid":"980125df-a4d5-47da-af44-b07cb30b69ea","name":"Esen, Buket Öztürk","orcid":"0000-0003-2957-7797","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte","key":"ebdruppau","last":"Ebdrup","locid":"240c9044-c0f2-4a19-ac18-95805422d7d4","name":"Ebdrup, Lotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jette","key":"ahrensbergpau","last":"Ahrensberg","locid":"27985bde-d467-4277-9997-e094df4fac89","name":"Ahrensberg, Jette Møller","name_org":"Ahrensberg, Jette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim M","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09d620e0-681c-44dd-b366-3f39a74e9ac9","name":"Larsen, Kim Michael","name_org":"Larsen, Kim M","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"3cb2ae19-c1b9-4dad-9928-adbd1c51b4b7","name":"Nørgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5891","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Fynbo","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"b1104ec4-1322-428f-af8f-7771361930bb","name":"Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","orcid":"0000-0002-0727-953X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34725109"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/emermed-2020-209746","issn":["14720205","14720213"],"issn_org":["14720205"],"issue":"9","journal":"Emergency Medicine Journal","pages":"697-700","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Emergency Medicine Journal","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137124188"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4178173e-14d5-4170-b3aa-a47762e24027"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prognostic and discriminative accuracy of the quick Sepsis-related Organ Failure Assessment compared with an early warning score : a Danish cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-166594","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Persistent cardiac symptoms are an increasingly reported phenomenon following COVID-19. However, the underlying cause of cardiac symptoms is unknown. This study aimed to identify the underlying causes, if any, of these symptoms 1 year following acute COVID-19 infection. Methods and Results: 22 individuals with persistent cardiac symptoms were prospectively investigated using echocardiography, cardiovascular magnetic resonance (CMR), 6-min walking test, cardio-pulmonary exercise testing and electrocardiography. A median of 382 days (IQR 368, 442) passed between diagnosis of COVID-19 and investigation. As a cohort their echocardiography, CMR, 6-min walking test and exercise testing results were within the normal ranges. There were no differences in left ventricular ejection fraction (61.45 ± 6.59 %), global longitudinal strain (19.80 ± 3.12 %) or tricuspid annular plane systolic excursion (24.96 ± 5.55 mm) as measured by echocardiography compared to a healthy control group. VO2 max (2045.00 ± 658.40 ml/min), % expected VO2 max (114.80 ± 23.08 %) and 6-minute distance walked (608.90 ± 54.51 m) exceeded that expected for the patient cohort, whilst Troponin I (5.59 ± 6.59 ng/l) and Nt-proBNP (88.18 ± 54.27 ng/l) were normal. Conclusion: Among a cohort of 22 patients with self-reported persistent cardiac symptoms, we identified no underlying cardiac disease or reduced cardiopulmonary fitness 1 year following COVID-19.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Wood, Gregory","Kirkevang, Therese Stegeager","Agergaard, Jane","Leth, Steffen","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Laustsen, Christoffer","Larsen, Anders Hostrup","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","Kim, Won Yong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-173530"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiac performance and cardiopulmonary fitness after infection with sars cov 000000000002","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85138521353","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-173530","identifier":[{"id":"35647079","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138521353","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9136046","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-4d9d3eed-ebd1-4aba-9110-6f8e92d1c3da"],"keyword":["Covid-19"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4BEAB3B7BB348A01DC5CB7506D732E32"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Gødstrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory","key":"woodpau","last":"Wood","locid":"a0519ae0-8c5b-47c5-890e-b99319da202b","name":"Wood, Gregory","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Therese Stegeager","key":"kirkevangpau","last":"Kirkevang","locid":"8c2502be-729f-46f6-a9cd-25768e6aebb6"