{"abstract":"This work considers the latency boundaries for Ultra Reliable Low Latency (URLLC) applications in 5G mobile networks using a Cloud-Radio Access Network (C-RAN) architecture. We present a use case for drone control, where the 5G network provides connectivity between the drone and the Ground Control Station (GCS). The 5G C-RAN architecture under investigation is the virtualised URLLC scenario proposed by Open-RAN (O-RAN) Alliance where radio processing is divided into three units, connected by an xhaul network. Hence, this work analyses opportunities for using the O-RAN virtualised URLLC scenario for drone control in two states; autonomous and under manual real-time control. The 5G network consists of different segments, each with different latency requirements, and this work outlines the deployment and dimensioning options in each segment. This work explores an Ethernet xhaul network, and thus the impact of queuing latency since the traffic link can be shared by different sources. The segments in the xhaul network must transport data that has not yet been through all radio processing layers, and thus, it is interesting to investigate how this affects the use case. Results illustrate how the maximum distance between the drone and GCS is limited by various xhaul parameters, while the maximum number of supported drones is not. This distance depends on both the xhaul network topology and link rates. This work shows the impact different message sizes has on the distance between drone and GCS, for example an Ethernet xhaul network with 4 hops requires at least 10 Gbps xhaul link rate to reach an xhaul length of 10 km. Hence, over-provisioning of xhaul bandwidth is a good solution seen from a latency perspective.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Pruski, Aleksander","Christiansen, Henrik L.","Ruepp, Sarah Renée","Berger, Michael Stübert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-317239"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-24","place":"Dubrovnik, hr","start":"2022-06-21","title":"2022 International Conference on Unmanned Aircraft Systems","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Crosshaul","Delay","Drones","Functional split","Latency","ORAN","UAV","Xhaul"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"xhaul latency dimensioning of 000000000005g drone control","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85136135262","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-317239","identifier":[{"id":"85136135262","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2a8d782c-2072-43fc-8ddb-2663db5c45a6"],"keyword":["Crosshaul","Delay","Drones","Functional split","Latency","ORAN","UAV","Xhaul"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C797DBB411562BC0A9B678AB645E524B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["TDC NET A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line M. P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Larsen, Line M. P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aleksander","key":"pruskipau","last":"Pruski","locid":"529e71e1-bd1e-469e-9b0e-579168499c12","name":"Pruski, Aleksander","orcid":"0000-0002-7354-7280","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik L.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Henrik L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","name_org":"Ruepp, Sarah","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael S.","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","name_org":"Berger, Michael S.","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icuas54217.2022.9836059","isbn":["9781665405942"],"pages":"762-771","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2022 International Conference on Unmanned Aircraft Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136135262"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","tdc net a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2a8d782c-2072-43fc-8ddb-2663db5c45a6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Xhaul Latency Dimensioning of 5G Drone Control","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-317239","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The feasibility of integrating a whole-body X-nucleus birdcage in a wide-bore clinical 3T MR scanner is evaluated. The challenge is that this extension coil has to be tightly fit into the scanner bore, having a diameter just 16 mm smaller than the concentric 1H coil. Different configurations are proposed and evaluated with the purpose of minimizing interaction between the X-nucleus coil and the native 1H body coil of the scanner. Experimental results are in agreement with simulations and demonstrate a 1H coil detuning of 0.4 MHz due to cointegration with X-nucleus birdcage.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sanchez, Juan Diego","Wang, Wenjun","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-322068"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-12","place":"London, gb","start":"2022-05-07","title":"2022 ISMRM &amp; SMRT Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coupling study between two concentric whole body mri birdcage coils towards a whole body x nucleus coil","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-322068","ids":["dtu-3ad50f99-2e25-45cb-9de4-5bc0594f93ea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-89780B307FB4F7DE207782D876C682D2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denm