Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f7b24c45-5905-4d6f-bc36-5fcf7dbc668e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“Greenland's Self-Government within the Danish Realm: a Historical Institutionalist Outcome?” Paper Presented at the Annual Meeting of the Danish Political Science Organisation, Hotel Nyborg Strand, 27-28 October 2022 (med Uffe Jakobsen)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732890","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate the effects of one and two doses of intravenous dexamethasone in patients after total knee arthroplasty. DESIGN: Randomised, blinded, placebo controlled trial with follow-up at 90 days. SETTING: Five Danish hospitals, September 2018 to March 2020. PARTICIPANTS: 485 adult participants undergoing total knee arthroplasty. INTERVENTION: A computer generated randomised sequence stratified for site was used to allocate participants to one of three groups: DX1 (dexamethasone (24 mg)+placebo); DX2 (dexamethasone (24 mg)+dexamethasone (24 mg)); or placebo (placebo+placebo). The intervention was given preoperatively and after 24 hours. Participants, investigators, and outcome assessors were blinded. All participants received paracetamol, ibuprofen, and local infiltration analgesia. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: The primary outcome was total intravenous morphine consumption 0 to 48 hours postoperatively. Multiplicity adjusted threshold for statistical significance was P<0.017 and minimal important difference was 10 mg morphine. Secondary outcomes included postoperative pain. RESULTS: 485 participants were randomised: 161 to DX1, 162 to DX2, and 162 to placebo. Data from 472 participants (97.3%) were included in the primary outcome analysis. The median (interquartile range) morphine consumptions at 0-48 hours were: DX1 37.9 mg (20.7 to 56.7); DX2 35.0 mg (20.6 to 52.0); and placebo 43.0 mg (28.7 to 64.0). Hodges-Lehmann median differences between groups were: -2.7 mg (98.3% confidence interval -9.3 to 3.7), P=0.30 between DX1 and DX2; 7.8 mg (0.7 to 14.7), P=0.008 between DX1 and placebo; and 10.7 mg (4.0 to 17.3), P<0.001 between DX2 and placebo. Postoperative pain was reduced at 24 hours with one dose, and at 48 hours with two doses, of dexamethasone. CONCLUSION: Two doses of dexamethasone reduced morphine consumption during 48 hours after total knee arthroplasty and reduced postoperative pain. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinicaltrials.gov NCT03506789.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Gasbjerg, Kasper Smidt","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Lunn, Troels Haxholdt","Laursen, Christina Cleveland","Holmqvist, Majken","Vinstrup, Louise Ørts","Ammitzboell, Mette","Jakobsen, Karina","Jensen, Mette Skov","Pallesen, Marie Jøhnk","Bagger, Jens","Lindholm, Peter","Pedersen, Niels Anker","Schrøder, Henrik Morville","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Nørskov, Anders Kehlet","Thybo, Kasper Højgaard","Brorson, Stig","Overgaard, Søren","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Mathiesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-085.15-046862"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Mathiesen, Ole"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of dexamethasone as an analgesic adjuvant to multimodal pain treatment after total knee arthroplasty randomised clinical trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2021-067325","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-085.15-046862","identifier":[{"id":"85122885365","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8724786","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34983775","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e2618727-3e2b-4708-813d-6e5ce4441da2","sdu-02cfe2f3-c0ca-4e58-ab35-5f4fb6743539"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-79E0B1292FB6BD369CF3C9AD9E4412D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/289325484/bmj_2021_067325.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/