{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Torsten Bjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ophavsretlig beskyttelse af tøj og sko","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-616601","ids":["sdu-978bfe66-9582-413a-9aa3-1d27bda64125"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7FCB96D64889348DFB4667DF4AD61D77"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Law","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Law, Private Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Bjørn","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"092fc245-1036-4233-ae53-c73806d7f132","name":"Larsen, Torsten Bjørn","orcid":"0000-0003-1784-8801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"rosenmeierpedh","last":"Rosenmeier","name":"Rosenmeier, Morten","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"riispedh","last":"Riis","name":"Riis, Thomas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"schovsbopedh","last":"Schovsbo","name":"Schovsbo, Jens","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"udsenpedh","last":"Udsen","name":"Udsen, Henrik","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788742000410"],"pages":"345-368","publisher":"Ex Tuto Publishing","status":"p","title":"Festskrift til Jørgen Blomqvist"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-978bfe66-9582-413a-9aa3-1d27bda64125"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ophavsretlig beskyttelse af tøj og sko","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-616601","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Cerebral hypoxia may occur during surgery but currently used cerebral oxygenation saturation (rSO2) monitors remain controversial with respect to improving clinical outcome. Novel neuroprotein biomarkers are potentially released into systemic circulation and combined with near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) could clarify the presence of per-operative cerebral hypoxia. We investigated changes to serum-neuroprotein concentrations post-surgically, paired with NIRS and cognitive outcome, in patients operated in the beach chair position (BCP). Methods: A prospective cohort in 28 shoulder surgery patients placed in the BCP. Blood samples were collected before induction of anaesthesia, and 2 hours and 3-5 days post-operatively. We analysed blood levels of biomarkers including tau and neurofilament light (NFL). We post hoc assessed the cross-wise relationship between biomarker levels and post-surgical changes in cognitive function and intraoperatively monitored rSO2 from NIRS. Results: Serum-NFL decreased from 24.2 pg/mL to 21.5 (P =.02) 2 hours post-operatively, then increased to 27.7 pg/mL on day 3-5 (P =.03). Conversely, s-tau increased from 0.77 pg/mL to 0.98 (2 h), then decreased to 0.81 on day 3-5 (P =.08). In 14/28 patients, episodic rSO2 below 55% occurred, and the duration < 55% was correlated to change in s-tau (P <.05). The cognitive function z-score at 1 week and 3 mo. correlated to the change in tau (P =.01), but not to NFL. Conclusion: Some biomarkers were significantly changed with surgery in the beach chair position. The change was at some points associated to post-operative cognitive decline, and to intraoperative low rSO2. (237).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Jens Rolighed","Kobborg, Tina","Shahim, Pashtun","Blennow, Kaj","Rasmussen, Lars S","Zetterberg, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-085.37-030105"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jens Rolighed"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Near infrared spectroscopy","Neurofilament light chain","Tau protein"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"serum neuroproteins near infrared spectroscopy and cognitive outcome after beach chair shoulder surgery observational cohort study analyses","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/312771571/Serum_neuroproteins_near_infrared_spectroscopy_and_cognitive_outcome_after_beach_chair_shoulder_surgery....pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-085.37-030105","identifier":[{"id":"85091004096","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32812646","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000570618100001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-f0d30cb7-b5d9-43e9-af23-09713a4dd352","ku-47fef0bf-13ac-44df-8472-da737d45aa4e"],"keyword":["beach chair position","cerebral hypoxia","near-infrared spectroscopy","neurofilament light chain","post-operative cognitive dysfunction","tau protein"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EB5E3EA4F4A7717586605ECD1D9AAE27"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/312771571/Serum_neuroproteins_near_infrared_spectroscopy_and_cognitive_outcome_after_beach_chair_shoulder_surgery....pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anæstesiologisk afdeling, Silkeborg","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - University Clinic for Interdisciplinary Orthopaedic Pathways (UCOP)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Rolighed","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"485143af-239d-407f-96e4-f045733fa8c8","name":"Larsen, Jens Rolighed","orcid":"0000-0003-0694-0135","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina","key":"kobborgpau","last":"Kobborg","locid":"3c9b8b53-8837-44f1-87a1-a46ee3f326f4","name":"Kobborg, Tina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pashtun","key":"shahimpau","last":"Shahim","name":"Shahim, Pashtun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaj","key":"blennowpau","last":"Blennow","name":"Blennow, Kaj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lars S.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37e36b99-34dd-471f-b09b-d93e72940ec0","name":"Rasmussen, Lars S","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lars S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"zetterbergpau","last":"Zetterberg","name":"Zetterberg, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32812646"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.13691","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"26-33","paperid":"AAS13691","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091004096"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f0d30cb7-b5d9-43e9-af23-09713a4dd352","ku-47fef0bf-13ac-44df-8472-da737d45aa4e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Serum‐neuroproteins, near‐infrared spectroscopy, and cognitive outcome after beach‐chair shoulder surgery : Observational cohort study analyses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.37-030105","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Cancer has a multitude of phenotypic expressions and identifying these are important for correct diagnosis and treatment selection. Clinical molecular imaging such as positron emission tomography can access several of these hallmarks of cancer non-invasively. Recently, hyperpolarized magnetic resonance spectroscopy with [1-13C] pyruvate has shown great potential to probe metabolic pathways. Here, we investigate simultaneous dual modality clinical molecular imaging of angiogenesis and deregulated energy metabolism in canine cancer patients. Methods: Canine cancer patients (n = 11) underwent simultaneous [68Ga]Ga-NODAGA-E[(cRGDyK)]2 (RGD) PET and hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate-MRSI (hyperPET). Standardized uptake values and [1-13C]lactate to total 13C ratio were quantified and compared generally and voxel-wise. Results: Ten out of 11 patients showed clear tumor uptake of [68Ga]Ga-NODAGA-RGD at both 20 and 60 min after injection, with an average SUVmean of 1.36 ± 0.23 g/mL and 1.13 ± 0.21 g/mL, respectively. A similar pattern was seen for SUVmax values, which were 2.74 ± 0.41 g/mL and 2.37 ± 0.45 g/mL. The [1-13C]lactate generation followed patterns previously reported. We found no obvious pattern or consistent correlation between the two modalities. Voxel-wise tumor values of RGD uptake and lactate generation analysis revealed a tendency for each canine cancer patient to cluster in separated groups. Conclusion: We demonstrated combined imaging of [68Ga]Ga-NODAGA-RGD-PET for angiogenesis and hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate-MRSI for probing energy metabolism. The results suggest that [68Ga]Ga-NODAGA-RGD-PET and [1-13C]pyruvate-MRSI may provide complementary information, indicating that hyperPET imaging of angiogenesis and energy metabolism is able to aid in cancer phenotyping, leading to improved therapy planning.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Clemmensen, Andreas","Hansen, Adam E.","Holst, Pernille","Schøier, Christina","Bisgaard, Sissel","Johannesen, Helle H.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Kristensen, Annemarie T.","Kjaer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S02-096.23-032941"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kjaer, Andreas"],"keyword":["1 C pyruvate","Cancer","Glycolysis","Positron Emission Tomography","hyperPET"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sup 000000000068 sup ga ga nodaga e crgdyk sub 000000000002 sub pet and hyperpolarized 000000000001 sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate mrsi hyperpet in canine cancer patients simultaneous imaging of angiogenesis and the warburg effect","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00259-020-04881-0","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under grant agreements no. 670261 (ERC Advanced Grant) and 668532 (Click-It), the Lundbeck Foundation, the Novo Nordisk Foundation, the Innovation Fund Denmark, the Danish Cancer Society, Arvid Nilsson Foundation, Svend Andersen Foundation, the Neye Foundation, the Research Foundation of Rigshospitalet, the Danish National Research Foundation (grant 126), the Research Council of the Capital Region of Denmark, the Danish Health Authority, and Research Council for Independent Research."],"id":"S02-096.23-032941","identifier":[{"id":"32621132","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85087505777","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7835292","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-10584c7b-fbf3-4404-87c7-ff529b018974","ku-88367889-1dc4-4d33-ae5b-5b172d8c1f23"],"keyword":["Angiogenesis-PET","Cancer","Ga-RDG","Glycolysis","Hyperpolarized magnetic resonance spectroscopy imaging","Positron emission tomography","[1-C]pyruvate","hyperPET"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-33E9620821E8A58AF81C2E7E9118AA00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/256574578/Open_access_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00259-020-04881-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/255476714/Clemmensen2021_Article_68Ga_Ga_NODAGA_E_CRGDyK_2PETA.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"5f1471f7-ae5b-4864-bdab-f57d5e4b8566","n