}],"pmid":["33976571"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/jpr.s306504","issn":["11787090"],"journal":"Journal of Pain Research","pages":"1215-1230","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","publisher_org":"Dove Medical Press Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pain Research","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106160407"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","capio privathospital","capio privathospitaler","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk","private hospital mølholm","the private pain clinic, herlev."],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0d8885d3-2042-401a-9d1c-9372c4e53dd1","au-f47c8755-a2e0-4889-a57d-0e46c6532164","ku-90804613-9af4-4a88-8e42-47c4e11f7f58","sdu-d57f6701-be3e-4d71-a2a9-210961cb456b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Socio-Demographics, Pain Characteristics, Quality of Life and Treatment Values Before and After Specialized Interdisciplinary Pain Treatment : Results from the Danish Clinical Pain Registry (PainData)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-098.50-000713","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Salivary gland carcinoma is a rare disease and studies on epidemiology and outcome require data collection over many years. The aim of this study is to present an update of incidence rates, anatomical sites, histological subtypes, and survival rates based on the Danish national cohort of salivary gland carcinoma patients. Methods: Data from all Danish patients with salivary gland carcinoma diagnosed from 1990 to 2015 (n = 1601) were included and analyzed following histological reevaluation and reclassification. Overall, disease-specific, and recurrence-free survival were evaluated. Prognostic factors were analyzed with multivariate Cox Hazard Regression. Results: The study population consisted of 769 men and 832 women, median age 62 years (range 6–102). The most frequent anatomic site was the parotid gland (51.8%). Adenoid cystic carcinoma was the most common subtype (24.7%). The majority had tumor classification T1/T2 (65.3%). The mean crude incidence was 1.2/100.000/year with an increase of 1.5% per year. There was no increase in age-adjusted incidence. The 5-, 10-, and 20-year survival rates were for overall survival 68, 52, and 35%, for disease-specific survival, 77, 69, and 64%, and for recurrence-free survival, 75, 64, and 51%, respectively. Age, high-grade histological subtype, advanced T-classification, cervical lymph node metastases, vascular invasion, and involved surgical margins had significantly negative impact on survival rates. Conclusion: The age-adjusted incidence has been stable for a period of 26 years. Multivariate analysis confirmed that histological grade, advanced stage, involved surgical margins and vascular invasion are independent negative prognostic factors. Survival rates were stationary compared to earlier reports.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Westergaard-Nielsen, Marie","Godballe, Christian","Eriksen, Jesper Grau","Larsen, Stine Rosenkilde","Kiss, Katalin","Agander, Tina","Ulhøi, Benedicte Parm","Charabi, Birgitte","Klug, Tejs Ehlers","Jacobsen, Henrik","Johansen, Jørgen","Kristensen, Claus Andrup","Andersen, Elo","Andersen, Maria","Andreasen, Simon","Bjørndal, Kristine"],"cuid":["S04-099.19-011985"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Westergaard-Nielsen, Marie"],"keyword":["Adenoid cystic carcinoma","Cancer","DANISH HEAD","Histological subtypes","Incidence","Management","Neck","Parotid Gland","Prognostic factors","Salivary gland carcinoma","Survival","Survival rates"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"salivary gland carcinoma in denmark a national update and follow up on incidence histology and outcome","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85088248430&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was conducted as part of PhD funded by grants from University of Southern Denmark, Region of Southern Denmark, Danish Cancer Research Fund, and Danish Cancer Society. Funding for the histological reevaluation process was provided by Odense University Hospital Research Fund, Sigvald and Edith Rasmussen b. Poulsens Fund, and Aase and Ejnar Danielsens Fund. The study was supported by the Danish Head and Neck Cancer Group (DAHANCA) and by OPEN, Odense Patient data Explorative Network, Odense University Hospital, Denmark."],"id":"S04-099.19-011985","identifier":[{"id":"85088248430","type":"scopus"},{