Tornby","key":"stendermogenstornbypau","last":"Stender","locid":"28ece5ea-1fc2-476b-bfc2-c02cbb0f759b","name":"Stender, Mogens Tornby","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"storkholmjanhenrikpau","last":"Storkholm","name":"Storkholm, Jan Henrik","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"gyllenborgjpau","last":"Gyllenborg","name":"Gyllenborg, J.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"hillingsøjpau","last":"Hillingsø","name":"Hillingsø, J.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"164","status":"p","subtitle":"Abstract Book","title":"Danske Kræftforskningsdage"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a61c2364-98a5-4074-9653-06ef293f0ed8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Beskrivelse af den nationale MDT konference for pancreascancer : deltagelse og tilbud om operation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-098208","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Uremic myopathy is a condition seen in end-stage renal disease (ESRD), characterized by muscle weakness and muscle fatigue, in which the pathophysiology is uncertain. The aim of this study was to assess the role of abnormal serum constituents in ESRD patients by relating them to the excitability properties of the tibialis anterior muscle, at rest and during electrically induced muscle activation, by recording muscle velocity recovery cycles (MVRC) and frequency ramp responses. Methods: Eighteen ESRD patients undergoing hemodialysis were evaluated by blood sample, MVRC, and frequency ramp (before and near the end of dialysis treatment), quantitative electromyography, and nerve conduction studies. Patients were compared to 24 control subjects. Results: In patients, muscle relative refractory period, early supernormality, late supernormality after 5 conditioning stimuli, and latency of the last of 15 and 30 frequency ramp pulses were strongly associated with potassium levels (p < 0.01), showing depolarization before and normalization in the end of hemodialysis. Conclusions: In ESRD patients, the muscle membrane is depolarized, mainly due to hyperkalemia. Significance: Since normal muscle fatigue has been attributed to potassium-induced depolarization, it seems likely that this mechanism is also a major cause of the exaggerated muscle fatigue and weakness in ESRD patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Lotte Hardbo","Z'Graggen, Werner J.","Bostock, Hugh","Tan, S. Veronica","Buus, Niels Henrik","Tankisi, Hatice"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-161069"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tankisi, Hatice"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London","University College London Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","University of Bern"],"keyword":["Electromyography","End stage renal disease","Frequency ramp","Hemodialysis","Hyperkalemia","Muscle velocity recovery cycles"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of potassium in muscle membrane dysfunction in end stage renal disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinph.2021.09.012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-161069","identifier":[{"id":"85118495363","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34740043","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3793d6c3-0b2f-4b64-a7bd-3d6dce0f7dd4"],"keyword":["Electromyography","End-stage renal disease","Frequency ramp","Hemodialysis","Hyperkalemia","Muscle velocity recovery cycles","Uremic myopathy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E30DC200FFD34217B9FE2568B68F122B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273845304/1_s2.0_S1388245721007458_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinph.2021.09.012","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Neurophysiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university college london hospitals nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Hardbo","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3b0c9475-c45f-449f-8cbb-6a158124ee5f","name":"Larsen, Lotte Hardbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Werner J.","key":"zgraggenpau","last":"Z'Graggen","name":"Z'Graggen, Werner J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugh","key":"bostockpau","last":"Bostock","name":"Bostock, Hugh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"S. Veronica","key":"tanpau","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, S. Veronica","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Henrik","key":"buuspau","last":"Buus","locid":"cb682ed6-2fe3-4664-90d6-0690462e8f80","name":"Buus, Niels Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hatice","key":"tankisipau","last":"Tankisi","locid":"2b3f7bfd-71e0-4e1e-9a63-62cf6d26d1ea","name":"Tankisi, Hatice","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34740043"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clinph.2021.09.012","issn":["13882457"],"issue":"12","journal":"Clinical Neurophysiology","pages":"3125-3135","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Neurophysiology","volume":"132"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118495363"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3793d6c3-0b2f-4b64-a7bd-3d6dce0f7dd4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The role of potassium in muscle membrane dysfunction in