{"abstract":"Digital twins are digital representations of cyber-physical systems, allowing bi-directional data and control flow between them. In this paper, we introduce the digital twin concept in self-integrating and self-improving systems. Specifically, we highlight the usage of digital twin models for autonomous systems spontaneously interacting with each other and aiming to improve collaboration and mutual safety. We present the main challenges and an initial architecture to enable autonomous cyber-physical systems to collaborate, self-integrate, and self-improve during run-time.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Esterle, Lukas","Gomes, Cláudio","Frasheri, Mirgita","Ejersbo, Henrik","Tomforde, Sven","Larsen, Peter Gorm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-161402"],"event":{"end":"2021-10-01","place":"Virtual, Washington DC","start":"2021-09-27","title":"2021 IEEE International Conference on Autonomic Computing and Self-Organizing Systems Companion (ACSOS-C)","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ejersbo, Henrik","Esterle, Lukas","Frasheri, Mirgita","Gomes, Cláudio","Larsen, Peter Gorm","Tomforde, Sven"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kiel University"],"keyword":["Autonomy","Cyber physical systems","Digital twins","System of systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital twins for collaboration and self integration","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85123445667","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-161402","identifier":[{"id":"85123445667","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-38311258-16db-4881-a354-cd73a