Peter Gorm","orcid":"0000-0002-4589-1500","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Esam","key":"elarabypedh","last":"El-Araby","name":"El-Araby, Esam","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Vana","key":"kalogerakipedh","last":"Kalogeraki","name":"Kalogeraki, Vana","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Danilo","key":"pianinipedh","last":"Pianini","name":"Pianini, Danilo","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Frederic","key":"lassabepedh","last":"Lassabe","name":"Lassabe, Frederic","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Barry","key":"porterpedh","last":"Porter","name":"Porter, Barry","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sona","key":"ghahremanipedh","last":"Ghahremani","name":"Ghahremani, Sona","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingrid","key":"nunespedh","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Ingrid","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohamed","key":"bakhouyapedh","last":"Bakhouya","name":"Bakhouya, Mohamed","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sven","key":"tomfordepedh","last":"Tomforde","name":"Tomforde, Sven","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/acsos-c52956.2021.00040","eisbn":["9781665443937"],"pages":"172-177","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2021 IEEE International Conference on Autonomic Computing and Self-Organizing Systems Companion, ACSOS-C 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123445667"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-38311258-16db-4881-a354-cd73add793a3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Digital twins for collaboration and self-integration","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-161402","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The need for renovation and energy retrofitting of Danish social housing from the 1960s and 1970s is substantial. Such energy retrofits often include the installation of mechanical ventilation systems with heat recovery to fulfil the current standards for energy efficiency. These systems typically ensure a more constant and higher ventilation rate than previous systems. Therefore, there is potential for residents to perceive a higher air quality and a reduction in problems due to condensation on cold surfaces and mould growth after retrofits. The purpose of the present study was to evaluate if this potential is realised for residents in social housing complexes. A questionnaire survey was performed among residents in dwellings with ventilation categorised within one of the five ventilation principles: natural ventilation, bathroom fan, exhaust fans in the kitchen and bath, decentralized balanced mechanical ventilation and centralized balanced mechanical ventilation. Compared with residents without balanced mechanical ventilation, residents having such systems perceived less often problems with unpleasant odour from their own apartment and less visible mould, but more often perceived the air as dry. Residents with decentralized mechanical ventilation tended to experience more often problems with noise from their ventilation system. However, results show that nuisance are avoidable with correctly designed decentralized ventilation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Knudsen, Henrik N.","Bekö, Gabriel","Larsen, Tine Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-306012"],"event":{"end":"2021-06-23","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2021-06-21","title":"Healthy Buildings Europe 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Knudsen, Henrik N."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perceived indoor environment in social housing with different ventilation principles","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-306012","ids":["dtu-04b44776-9bbf-4d98-93e2-3195c8151c39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8F2894D2C1A6AA04723883F747442B8D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Indoor Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik N.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Henrik N.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriel","key":"beköpau","last":"Bekö","locid":"c4ad7184-0df3-48b9-8ef0-fc51d4cadfaf","name":"Bekö, Gabriel","orcid":"0000-0001-6107-8336","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Tine Steen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-04b44776-9bbf-4d98-93e2-3195c8151c39"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Perceived indoor environment in social housing with different ventilation principles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-306012","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarized 13C isotope resolved spectroscopy boosts NMR signal intensity, which improves signal detection and allows metabolic fluxes to be analyzed. Such hyperpolarized flux data may offer new approaches to tissue classification and biomarker identification that could be translated in vivo. Here we used hyperpolarized stable isotope resolved analysis (SIRA) to measure metabolite specific 13C isotopic enrichments in the central carbon metabolism of mouse prostate. Prostate and tumor tissue samples were acquired from transgenic adenocarcinomas of the mouse prostate (TRAMP) mice. Before euthanasia, mice were injected with [U–13C]glucose intraperitoneally (i.p.). Polar metabolite extracts were prepared, and hyperpolarized 1D-13C NMR spectra were obtained from normal prostate (n = 19) and cancer tissue (n = 19) samples. Binary classification and feature analysis was performed to make a separation model and to investigate differences between samples originating from normal and cancerous prostate tissue, respectively. Hyperpolarized experiments were carried out according to a standardized protocol, which showed a high repeatability (CV = 15%) and an average linewidth in the 1D-13C NMR spectra of 2 ± 0.5 Hz. The resolution of the hyperpolarized 1D-13C spectra was high with little signal overlap in the carbonyl region and metabolite identification was easily accomplished. A discrimination with 95% success rate could be made between samples originating from TRAMP mice prostate and tumor tissue based on isotopomers from uniquely identified metabolites. Hyperpolarized 13C-SIRA allowed detailed metabolic information to be obtained from tissue specimens. The positional information of 13C isotopic enrichments lead to easily interpreted features responsible for high predictive classification of tissue types. This analytical approach has matured, and the robust experimental protocols currently available allow systematic tracking of metabolite flux ex vivo.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Frahm, Anne Birk","Hill, Deborah","Katsikis, Sotirios","Andreassen, Trygve","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Bathen, Tone Frost","Moestue, Siver Andreas","Jensen, Pernille Rose","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-314733"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lerche, Mathilde Hauge"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","Isotopic fingerprinting","Prostate cancer","Random forest","Support vector machines"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"classification and biomarker identification of prostate tissue from tramp mice with hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c sira","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256584395/Talanta_140821.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors gratefully acknowledge funding by the Danish National Research Foundation (Grant DNRF124 ). TRAMP mice breeding, housing, and genotyping was provided by the Comparative medicine Core Facility (CoMed), Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU). CoMed is funded by the Faculty of Medicine at NTNU and Central Norway Regional Health Authority . Anne B. Frahm was supported by a travel and study grant from the Danish Cancer Society for a visiting stay at NTNU (Grant R235-A14222-19-S44 ). The tissue extraction procedures and 1 H -NMR experiments were performed at the MR Core Facility, Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU). MR core facility is funded by the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences at NTNU and Central Norway Regional Health Authority . Hyperpolarized 1D- 13 C NMR data in this study was acquired with equipment partially funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF19OC0055825 ). The authors gratefully acknowledge funding by the Danish National Research Foundation (Grant DNRF124). Hyperpolarized 1D-13C NMR data in this study was acquired with equipment partially funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF19OC0055825). The tissue extraction procedures and 1H -NMR experiments were performed at the MR Core Facility, Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU). MR core facility is funded by the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences at NTNU and Central Norway Regional Health Authority. TRAMP mice breeding, housing, and genotyping was provided by the Comparative medicine Core Facility (CoMed), Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU). CoMed is funded by the Faculty of Medicine at NTNU and Central Norway Regional Health Authority. The NMR center at DTU is acknowledged for the high-resolution 1H?13C HSQC and HMBC Spectrum acquired on their 800 MHz Avance II NMR spectrometer. Anne B. Frahm was supported by a travel and study grant from the Danish Cancer Society for a visiting stay at NTNU (Grant R235-A14222-19-S44)."],"id":"S01-000.00-314733","identifier":[{"id":"34517669","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85113278526","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-22273302-ad48-4d90-ac84-30c2b83198ae"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","Isotopic fingerprinting","Prostate cancer","Random forest","Stable isotope resolved analysis","Support vector machines"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBAF565342B40E4DA09F7FC413142820"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256584395/Talanta_140821.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne B.","key":"frahmpau","last":"Frahm","locid":"e1c57a75-5e33-408f-b05d-077262dafeb4","name":"Frahm, Anne Birk","name_org":"Frahm, Anne B.","orcid":"0000-0001-6909-9369","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Deborah","key":"hillpau","last":"Hill","name":"Hill, Deborah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sotirios","key":"katsikispau","last":"Katsikis","locid":"67eee360-b8b8-4451-958a-ad05e1c70009","name":"Katsikis, Sotirios","orcid":"0000-0001-6653-1814","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Trygve","key":"andreassenpau","last":"Andreassen","name":"Andreassen, Trygve","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tone Frost","key":"bathenpau","last":"Bathen","name":"Bathen, Tone Frost","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siver Andreas","key":"moestuepau","last":"Moestue","name":