{"abstract":"Magnetic Resonance Imaging combined with hyperpolarized 13C-labelled metabolic contrast agents produced via dissolution Dynamic Nuclear Polarization can, non-invasively and in real-time, report on tissue specific aberrant metabolism. However, hyperpolarization equipment is expensive, technically demanding and needs to be installed on-site for the end-user. In this work, we provide a robust methodology that allows remote production of the hyperpolarized 13C-labelled metabolic contrast agents. The methodology, built on photo-induced thermally labile radicals, allows solid sample extraction from the hyperpolarization equipment and several hours' lifetime of the 13C-labelled metabolic contrast agents at appropriate storage/transport conditions. Exemplified with [U-13C, d7]-D-glucose, we remotely produce hyperpolarized 13C-labelled metabolic contrast agents and generate above 10,000-fold liquid-state Magnetic Resonance signal enhancement at 9.4 T, keeping on-site only a simple dissolution device. Hyperpolarized metabolic contrast agents for magnetic resonance imaging can provide non-invasive and realtime information on tissue specific aberrant metabolism, but producing and handling them is highly demanding because of their short lifetime. Here a solid sample extraction, storage, and transport technique allows disconnecting production from end-user sites handling, as well as hour-long lifetimes of the agents.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Capozzi, Andrea","Kilund, Jan","Karlsson, Magnus","Patel, Saket","Pinon, Arthur César","Vibert, Francois","Ouari, Olivier","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360459"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Capozzi, Andrea"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille Université","All Global Affiliations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metabolic contrast agents produced from transported solid sup 000000000013 sup c glucose hyperpolarized via dynamic nuclear polarization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42004-021-00536-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360459","identifier":[{"id":"000665018300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85108858262","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-baf0b926-929a-4307-be8f-406b2b194d4c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7003D5D33EF4A3E3DD07D8780FC4EDBA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256271899/s42004_021_00536_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42004-021-00536-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"aix marseille université","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aix-Marseille Université","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"capozzipau","last":"Capozzi","