ordogna, Gloria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sławomir","key":"zadrożnypau","last":"Zadrożny","name":"Zadrożny, Sławomir","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Troels","key":"andreasenpedh","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Troels","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guy","key":"detrépedh","last":"De Tré","name":"De Tré, Guy","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Janusz","key":"kacprzykpedh","last":"Kacprzyk","name":"Kacprzyk, Janusz","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"legindlarsenpedh","last":"Legind Larsen","name":"Legind Larsen, Henrik","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gloria","key":"bordognapedh","last":"Bordogna","name":"Bordogna, Gloria","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sławomir","key":"zadrożnypedh","last":"Zadrożny","name":"Zadrożny, Sławomir","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-86967-0_1","isbn":["9783030869663"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"3-14","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Flexible Query Answering Systems - 14th International Conference, FQAS 2021, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115844823"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-87ba2cee-1392-4fd8-a61c-f10a1d934ab1"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Perspectives and Views of Flexible Query Answering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-565107","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objectives To correlate the level of fibrocytes in peripheral blood, synovial tissue and in vitro culture in rheumatoid arthritis (RA) with changes in disease activity, imaging and pulmonary function. Methods Twenty patients with early RA (ERA) and 20 patients with long-standing RA (LRA) were enrolled in a 6-month prospective study. Sixteen patients undergoing wrist arthroscopy were healthy controls. Patients with RA underwent pulmonary function tests, ultrasound and synovial ultrasound-guided needle biopsy of the same wrist at baseline and 6 months. Wrist MRI was performed at baseline (all) and 6 months (ERA). Circulating fibrocytes were measured by flow cytometry, in vitro by the number of monocytes that were differentiated to fibrocytes and in synovial biopsies by counting in histological sections. Results Fibrocytes were primarily located around vessels and in the subintimal area in the synovium. Fibrocyte levels did not decline during the trial despite effective RA treatment. In the ERA group, increased synovitis assessed by ultrasound was moderate and strongly correlated with an increase in circulating and synovial fibrocyte levels, respectively. Increased synovitis assessed by MRI during the trial in the ERA group was moderately correlated with both increased numbers of circulating and cultured fibrocytes. Absolute diffusion capacity level was overall weakly negatively correlated with the level of circulating and synovial fibrocytes. The decline in diffusion capacity during the trial was moderately correlated with increased levels of synovial fibrocytes. Conclusion Our findings suggest that fibrocytes are involved in RA pathogenesis, both in the synovium and the reduction in lung function seen in a part of patients with RA.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Just, Søren Andreas","Nielsen, Christian","Werlinrud, Jens Christian","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Hejbøl, Eva Kildall","Tenstad, Helene Broch","Schrøder, Henrik Daa","Barington, Torben","Torfing, Trine","Humby, Frances","Lindegaard, Hanne Merete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-625956"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Just, Søren Andreas"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Barts and London Nhs Trust"],"keyword":["Arthritis","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Pulmonary fibrosis","Rheumatoid","Ultrasonography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fibrocytes in early and long standing rheumatoid arthritis a 000000000006 month trial with repeated synovial biopsy imaging and lung function test","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2020-001494","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-625956","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7938972","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85102180972","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33674419","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b7e58b8b-ef95-4308-ace8-e6e35ce7c9d3"],"keyword":["Arthritis","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Pulmonary fibrosis","Rheumatoid","Ultrasonography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB41878F08BEA0FC6E633269E2E5C5E7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2020-001494","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180443580/10.1136_rmdopen_2020_001494.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U",