{"abstract":"Solid-state, natural-abundance 95Mo NMR experiments of four different MoS2 materials have been performed on a magnet at B0 = 19.6 T and on a new series-connected hybrid magnet at 35.2 T. Employing two different 2H-MoS2 (2H phase) materials, a \"pseudo-amorphous\"MoS2 nanomaterial and a MoS2 layer on an Al2O3 support of a hydrodesulfurization (HDS) catalyst, has enabled the introduction of solid-state 95Mo NMR as an important analytical tool in the study of MoS2 nanomaterials. 95Mo spin-lattice relaxation time (T1) studies of 160- and 4-layer 2H-MoS2 samples at 19.6 and 35.2 T show their relaxation rate (1/T1) increase in proportion to B02. This is in accord with chemical shift anisotropy (CSA) relaxation, which is the dominant T1(95Mo) mechanism, with a large 95Mo CSA of 1025 ppm determined for all four MoS2 nanomaterials. The dominant CSA mechanism suggests that the MoS2 band gap electrons are delocalized throughout the lattice-layer structures, thereby acting as a fast modulation source (ωoτc ≈ 1) for 95Mo CSA in 2H-MoS2. A decrease in T1(95Mo) is observed for an increase in the B0 field and for a decrease in the number of 2H-MoS2 layers. All four nanomaterials exhibit identical 95Mo electric-field gradient (EFG) parameters. The T1 results account for the several failures in retrieving the 95Mo spectral EFG and CSA parameters for multilayer 2H-MoS2 samples in the pioneering solid-state 95Mo NMR studies performed during the past 2 decades (1990-2010) because of the extremely long T1(95Mo) = ∼200-250 s observed at a low B0 (∼9.4 T) used at that time. Much shorter T1(95Mo) values are observed even at 19.6 T for the \"pseudo-amorphous\"and the HDS catalyst (MoS2-Al2O3 support) MoS2 nanomaterials. These allowed obtaining useful solid-state 95Mo NMR spectra for these two samples at 19.6 T in a few to <24 h. Most importantly, this research led to the observation of an impressive 95Mo MAS spectrum for an average of 1-4 layer thick MoS2 on an Al2O3 support, that is, the first MAS NMR spectrum of a low-natural-abundance, low-γquadrupole-nucleus species layered on a catalyst support. While a huge gain in NMR sensitivity, by a factor of ∼60, is observed for the 95Mo MAS spectrum of the 160-layer sample at 35.2 T as compared to 14.1 T, the MAS spectrum of the 4-layer sample is almost completely wiped out at 35.2 T. This unusual observation for the 4-layer sample (crumpled, rose-like, and defective Mo-edge structures) is due to an increased distribution of the isotropic 95Mo shifts in the 95Mo MAS spectra at B0 up to 35.2 T upon reduction of the number of sample layers.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Hans Jørgen","Bildsøe, Henrik K.","Bondesgaard, Martin","Iversen, Bo Brummerstedt","Brorson, Michael","Larsen, Flemming H.","Gan, Zhehong","Hung, Ivan"],"cuid":["S02-096.45-030248"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jakobsen, Hans Jørgen"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Florida State University"],"keyword":["Catalysts","QUADRUPOLAR NUCLEI","Spectroscopy","TERM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-HLT"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-HLT","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exciting opportunities for solid state sup 000000000095 sup mo nmr studies of mos sub 000000000002 sub nanostructures in materials research from a low to an ultrahigh magnetic field 000000000035 000000000002 t","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313053265/nihms_1706497.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-096.45-030248","identifier":[{"id":"000641307100030","type":"wos"},{"id":"34262634","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85104927554","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8276973","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f33144ce-d6bb-4a33-b04d-4ede825b3703","ku-8fea3dda-7eeb-40aa-97b1-691aa3fc8e48"],"keyword":["CATALYSTS","QCPMG-MAS NMR","QUADRUPOLAR NUCLEI","SPECTROSCOPY","TERM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DC68286A1BF3F18D4B6DDB11B3D8DDD9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8276973/pdf/nihms-1706497.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313053265/nihms_1706497.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"topsoe","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-HLT","l3nl":"Haldor Topsoe","l3nn":"Topsoe","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Topsoe","namevar":["Haldor Topsøe A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-HLT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Analytics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"florida state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Florida State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans J.","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"2c14e457-bc3a-4fe9-a952-c67daf60ffb8","name":"Jakobsen, Hans Jørgen","name_org":"Jakobsen, Hans J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bildsøepau","last":"Bildsøe","locid":"ed9b2cea-ee92-4c02-8372-b5c7e65be24b","name":"Bildsøe, Henrik K.","name_org":"Bildsøe, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"bondesgaardpau","last":"Bondesgaard","locid":"a81f50c0-3253-4944-9cf6-626e09941601","name":"Bondesgaard, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bo B.","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"17abd7bf-2bbb-4ff3-9405-a140882a86b2","name":"Iversen, Bo Brummerstedt","name_org":"Iversen, Bo B.","orcid":"0000-0002-4632-1024","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"brorsonpau","last":"Brorson","name":"Brorson, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Flemming H.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"eda11dab-a7a0-43f1-91cc-0087bd5538b5","name":"Larsen, Flemming Hofmann","name_org":"Larsen, Flemming H.","orcid":"0000-0001-5180-6870","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhehong","key":"ganpau","last":"Gan","name":"Gan, Zhehong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"hungpau","last":"Hung","name":"Hung, Ivan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34262634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpcc.0c10522","issn":["19327447","19327455"],"issn_org":["19327447"],"issue":"14","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","pages":"7824-7838","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","volume":"125"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104927554"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Haldor Topsoe","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f33144ce-d6bb-4a33-b04d-4ede825b3703","ku-8fea3dda-7eeb-40aa-97b1-691aa3fc8e48"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exciting Opportunities for Solid-State <sup>95</sup>Mo NMR Studies of MoS<sub>2 </sub>Nanostructures in Materials Research from a Low to an Ultrahigh Magnetic Field (35.2 T)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.45-030248","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To determine the incidence of hospital admissions and associated mortality rates for non-covid medical conditions during the covid-19 pandemic. Design: Nationwide, population based cohort study. Setting: Denmark from 13 March 2019 to 27 January 2021. Participants: All Danish residents >1 year of age. Main outcomes measures: Population based healthcare registries that encompass the entire Danish population were used to compare hospital admission and mortality rates during the covid-19 pandemic (from 11 March 2020 to 27 January 2021) with the prepandemic baseline data (from 13 March 2019 to 10 March 2020). Hospital admissions were categorised as covid-19 when patients were assigned a diagnosis code for covid-19 within five days of admission. All patients were followed until migration, death, or end of follow-up, whichever came first. Rate ratios for hospital admissions were computed using Poisson regression and were directly standardised using the Danish population on 1 January 2019 as reference. 30 day mortality rate ratios were examined by Cox regression, adjusted for age and sex, and covid-19 diagnosis was used as a competing risk. Results: 5 753 179 residents were identified during 567.8 million person weeks of observation, with 1 113 705 hospital admissions among 675 447 people. Compared with the prepandemic baseline period (mean hospital admission rate 204.1 per 100 000/week), the overall hospital admission rate for non-covid-19 conditions decreased to 142.8 per 100 000/week (rate ratio 0.70, 95% confidence interval 0.66 to 0.74) after the first national lockdown, followed by a gradual return to baseline levels until the second national lockdown when it decreased to 158.3 per 100 000/week (0.78, 0.73 to 0.82). This pattern was mirrored for most major diagnosis groups except for non-covid-19 respiratory diseases, nervous system diseases, cancer, heart failure, sepsis, and non-covid-19 respiratory infections, which remained lower throughout the study period. Overall 30 day mortality rates were higher during the first national lockdown (mortality rate ratio 1.28, 95% confidence interval 1.23 to 1.32) and the second national lockdown (1.20, 1.16 to 1.24), and these results were similar across most major diagnosis groups. For non-covid-19 respiratory diseases, cancer, pneumonia, and sepsis, the 30 day mortality rate ratios were also higher between lockdown periods. Conclusions: Hospital admissions for all major non-covid-19 disease groups decreased during national lockdowns compared with the prepandemic baseline period. Additionally, mortality rates were higher overall and for patients admitted to hospital with conditions such as respiratory diseases, cancer, pneumonia, and sepsis. Increased attention towards management of serious non-covid-19 medical conditions is warranted.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bodilsen, Jacob","Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","Søgaard, Mette","Dalager-Pedersen, Michael","Speiser, Lasse Ole Zacho","Yndigegn, Troels","Nielsen, Henrik","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Skjøth, Flemming"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-012061"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bodilsen, Jacob"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["SYSTEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hospital admission and mortality rates for non covid diseases in denmark during covid 000000000019 pandemic nationwide population based cohort study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.n1135","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-012061","identifier":[{"id":"34035000","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85106931194","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8142604","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000656562600003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-fd96d8e4-786e-45e6-bdee-2f5cbf9a5eda","au-877fd36b-4337-40d6-84c8-59ea8a160a0e"],"keyword":["SYSTEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-42D83792041BB8F08CCB43DD62D9EC3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.n1135","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/412828228/Bodilsen_et_al_2021_Hospital_admission_and_mortality_rates_for_non_covid_diseases_in_Denmark_during_covid_19_pandemic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/277774959/bmj.n1135.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Infectious Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"bodilsenjacobpau","last":"Bodilsen","locid":"260dd517-12cb-4490-b8c0-c69efb455878","name":"Bodilsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-7398-814X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brønnum","key":"nielsenpeterbrønnumpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ce5c24a-cc41-4e4c-a071-9a41f036faf8","name":"Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","orcid":"0000-0003-2922-6970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"søgaardmettepau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5ce4f246-03bc-4e72-b36a-eb5f76e5e5cb","name":"Søgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-2830-4968","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"dalagerpedersenmichaelpau","last":"Dalager-Pedersen","locid":"4f3b7227-33bc-4eab-b0c7-19920797c015","name":"Dalager-Pedersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-3220-2526","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse Ole Zacho","key":"speiserlassepau","last":"Speiser","locid":"2d6cbdc3-0357-4142-83ce-d1f764ada0c7","name":"Speiser, Lasse","name_org":"Speiser, Lasse Ole Zacho","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Ole Zacho","key":"speiserlasseolezachopau","last":"Speiser","name":"Speiser, Lasse Ole Zacho","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels","key":"yndigegntroelspau","last":"Yndigegn","name":"Yndigegn, Troels","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenhenrikpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsentorbenbjerregaardpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"skjøthflemmingpau","last":"Skjøth","locid":"6166e832-f5f5-47be-82bb-07962be7c943","name":"Skjøth, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0003-2975-647X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34035000"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmj.n1135","issn":["09598146","17561833"],"issn_org":["09598146"],"journal":"BMJ","paperid":"n1135","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ","title_org":"The BMJ","volume":"373"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106931194"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fd96d8e4-786e-45e6-bdee-2f5cbf9a5eda","au-877fd36b-4337-40d6-84c8-59ea8a160a0e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hospital admission and mortality rates for non-covid diseases in Denmark during covid-19 pandemic: Nationwide population based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-012061","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Dysregulation of interleukin 33 (IL-33) has been implicated in the pathogenesis of several autoimmune and inflammatory diseases, but few studies have examined transcriptional regulation of the IL33 gene. In the intestines, gene regulation is controlled by a transcription factor network of which the intestinal-specific transcription factor CDX2 is a key component. In this study, we investigated whether CDX2 regulates IL33 mRNA expression. We examined IL33 mRNA expression in primary colonic epithelial cells from healthy humans and epithelial cell lines, revealing high expression levels in primary colonic and LS174T cells. Combining genomics data (ChIP-Seq, RNA-Seq) and IL33 promoter analyses in LS174T cells revealed intronic enhancer activity in the IL33 gene that is dependent on CDX2 expression. Western blotting and qRT-PCR confirmed that IL33 expression is upregulated in a CDX2 concentration-dependent manner, thereby providing the first evidence that CDX2 regulates the expression of IL33.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Sylvester","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Davidsen, Johanne","Dahlgaard, Katja","Nielsen, Claus Henrik","Bennett, Eric P","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Coskun, Mehmet","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045994"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Gene regulation","Inflammatory bowel disease","Interleukin 33","transcriptional control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cdx000000000002 regulates interleukin 000000000033 gene expression in intestinal epithelial cells ls000000000174t","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2211-5463.13161","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-045994","identifier":[{"id":"85104865410","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8167865","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33838073","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c3ab6e3a-c765-4d4f-80ca-d1dbe9458023","ruc-ec415210-fc06-4263-8c89-11b765a72d8e"],"keyword":["Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2","gene regulation","inflammatory bowel disease","interleukin-33","intestinal regulation","transcriptional control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E87C42FF75451E4463E2F83B02087DEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273587073/2211_5463.13161.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2211-5463.13161","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/78158996/2211_5463.13161.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved, Slagelse, Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Gastroenterology and Hepatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Sylvester","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ec07d30c-2417-4f63-a00a-af298dda69bd","name":"Larsen, Sylvester","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jakob Benedict","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","locid":"e31587ea-e362-4ce5-942d-bc27c0f0d340","name":"Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","orcid":"0000-0003-3230-7966","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Johanne","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"5f273e10-a1e5-4ba7-ba9d-7ab1c51636d5","name":"Davidsen, Johanne","orcid":"0000-0003-4655-1513","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Katja","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"bd84257d-f62e-4de3-b1f4-aa6253e79f76","name":"Dahlgaard, Katja","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Claus Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8caf59ab-44ff-4d9a-a722-8dd317bbd8b9","name":"Nielsen, Claus Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7543-9016","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Eric Paul","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","locid":"985ebfda-1253-424b-8e7d-d5918fa165bf","name":"Bennett, Eric P","name_org":"Bennett, Eric Paul","orcid":"0000-0002-4976-0647","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ole Birger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Thorvald","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"3b39117d-6f4e-47c7-a61d-5192c15b00a9","name":"Troelsen, Jesper","name_org":"Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33838073"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/2211-5463.13161","issn":["22115463"],"issue":"6","journal":"FEBS Open Bio","pages":"1638-1644","status":"p","title":"FEBS Open Bio","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104865410"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c3ab6e3a-c765-4d4f-80ca-d1dbe9458023","ruc-ec415210-fc06-4263-8c89-11b765a72d8e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"CDX2 regulates interleukin-33 gene expression in intestinal epithelial cells (LS174T)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045994","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Whole-body oxidative stress can be estimated by the urine excretion of oxidized guanosine species, 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo) and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2'-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG), derived from RNA and DNA, respectively. These oxidative stress markers are not well explored in thyroid disorders. OBJECTIVE: We aimed to determine whether treatment of hyperthyroid patients affects the levels of these oxidative stress markers. METHODS: Urinary excretion of 8-oxoGuo and 8-oxodG was measured in 51 hyperthyroid patients (toxic nodular goiter [TNG], n = 30; Graves disease [GD], n = 21) before or shortly after initiation of therapy and when stable euthyroidism had been achieved for at least 12 months. RESULTS: Adjusting for age, the baseline urinary excretion of oxidative stress markers correlated positively with plasma thyroxine (8-oxoGuo, P = 0.002; 8-oxodG, P = 0.021) and was significantly higher in GD than in TNG patients (P = 0.001 for both oxidative stress markers). Restoration of euthyroidism significantly affected the excretion of the oxidative stress markers. In TNG, 8-oxoGuo decreased from geometric mean 2.11 nmol/mmol creatinine (95% CI, 1.85-2.39) to 1.91 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.67-2.19; P = 0.001), while 8-oxodG decreased from 1.65 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.41-1.93) to 1.48 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.27-1.74; P = 0.026). In GD, 8-oxoGuo decreased from 2.25 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.95-2.59) to 1.79 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.63-1.97; P = 0.0003), while 8-oxodG decreased from 2.02 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.73-2.38) to 1.54 nmol/mmol (95% CI, 1.31-1.81; P = 0.001). In the euthyroid state, there were no differences between groups. CONCLUSION: Restoration of euthyroidism in patients with hyperthyroidism significantly decreased the systemic oxidative stress load by 10% to 25%. Our findings may help to explain the higher morbidity and mortality linked to hyperthyroid diseases, as shown in observational studies.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Larsen, Camilla B.","Riis, Kamilla Ryom","Winther, Kristian Hillert","Larsen, Emil List","Ellervik, Christina","Hegedüs, Laszlo","Brix, Thomas Heiberg","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Bonnema, Steen Joop"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-047307"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Camilla Bøgelund"],"keyword":["8 Oxo 7 8 dihydro 2 deoxyguanosine","8 oxo 7 8 dihydroguanosine","Graves disease","Hyperthyroidism","Oxidative stress","Toxic nodular goiter"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Ukendt"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"treatment of hyperthyroidism reduces systemic oxidative stress as measured by markers of rna and dna damage","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/202354415/JCEM_144_21.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-047307","identifier":[{"id":"33901280","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85108386758","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f0e23df2-c6e3-473a-aef7-eb1002ee3636","sdu-a8ea9017-d6d0-4f4c-962d-439cd5eb0381"],"keyword":["8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2’-deoxyguanosine","8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine","Graves disease","hyperthyroidism","oxidative stress","toxic nodular goiter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-44D60787D98B0304FFEADB230AF5B460"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/334007113/JCEM_144_21_2_28.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/202354415/JCEM_144_21.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Re