ical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C.B.","key":"larsencamillabøgelundpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7e82cf5f-1769-47b6-9ce4-fce0b54a0dd3","name":"Larsen, Camilla Bøgelund","name_org":"Larsen, C.B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7342-8660","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K.R.","key":"riiskamillaryompau","last":"Riis","locid":"deadd2ee-d2d3-4279-afe0-0cb0603aa074","name":"Riis, Kamilla Ryom","name_org":"Riis, K.R.","orcid":"0000-0003-2679-7153","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristian Hillert","key":"wintherkristianhillertpau","last":"Winther","name":"Winther, Kristian Hillert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"K.H.","key":"wintherkhpau","last":"Winther","name":"Winther, K.H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenemillistpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil L,","key":"larsenemillpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil L,","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Christina","key":"ellervikchristinapau","last":"Ellervik","locid":"f08e5172-d3cf-4e0a-a733-6a450b16075a","name":"Ellervik, Christina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"hegedüslaszlopau","last":"Hegedüs","locid":"68214bbe-c02e-40e1-bc7b-49fedd3d5723","name":"Hegedüs, Laszlo","name_org":"Hegedüs, L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T.H.","key":"brixthomasheibergpau","last":"Brix","locid":"8fe88cb1-b1bb-496a-81bf-6dec7d3a2d0c","name":"Brix, Thomas Heiberg","name_org":"Brix, T.H.","orcid":"0000-0002-2327-531X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Henrik Enghusen","key":"poulsenhenrikenghusenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"H.E.","key":"poulsenhepau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, H.E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.J.","key":"bonnemasteenjooppau","last":"Bonnema","locid":"6a7e6a38-b12e-4b13-bfdb-0bea96f3b1e1","name":"Bonnema, Steen Joop","name_org":"Bonnema, S.J.","orcid":"0000-0002-6898-1752","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33901280"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgab273","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","publisher":"Endocrine Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism","volume":"106"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108386758"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f0e23df2-c6e3-473a-aef7-eb1002ee3636","sdu-a8ea9017-d6d0-4f4c-962d-439cd5eb0381"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Treatment of Hyperthyroidism Reduces Systemic Oxidative Stress, as Measured by Markers of RNA and DNA Damage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-047307","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Lifestyle intervention, i.e. diet and physical activity, forms the basis for care of type 2 diabetes (T2D). The current physical activity recommendation for T2D is aerobic training for 150 min/week of moderate to vigorous intensity, supplemented with resistance training 2–3 days/week, with no more than two consecutive days without physical activity. The rationale for the recommendations is based on studies showing a reduction in glycated haemoglobin (HbA1c). This reduction is supposed to be caused by increased insulin sensitivity in muscle and adipose tissue, whereas knowledge about effects on abnormalities in the liver and pancreas are scarce, with the majority of evidence stemming from in vitro and animal studies. The aim of this study is to investigate the role of the volume of exercise training as an adjunct to dietary therapy in order to improve the pancreatic β-cell function in T2D patients less than 7 years from diagnosis. The objective of this protocol for the DOSE-EX trial is to describe the scientific rationale in detail and to provide explicit information about study procedures and planned analyses. Methods/design: In a parallel-group, 4-arm assessor-blinded randomised clinical trial, 80 patients with T2D will be randomly allocated (1:1:1:1, stratified by sex) to 16 weeks in either of the following groups: (1) no intervention (CON), (2) dietary intervention (DCON), (3) dietary intervention and supervised moderate volume exercise (MED), or (4) dietary intervention and supervised high volume exercise (HED). Enrolment was initiated December 15th, 2018, and will continue until N = 80 or December 1st, 2021. Primary outcome is pancreatic beta-cell function assessed as change in late-phase disposition index (DI) from baseline to follow-up assessed by hyperglycaemic clamp. Secondary outcomes include measures of cardiometabolic risk factors and the effect on subsequent complications related to T2D. The study was approved by The Scientific Ethical Committee at the Capital Region of Denmark (H-18038298). Trial registration: The Effects of Different Doses of Exercise on Pancreatic β-cell Function in Patients With Newly Diagnosed Type 2 Diabetes (DOSE-EX), NCT03769883, registered 10 December 2018 https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT03769883). Any modification to the protocol, study design, and changes in written participant information will be approved by The Scientific Ethical Committee at the Capital Region of Denmark before effectuation. Discussion: The data from this study will add knowledge to which volume of exercise training in combination with a dietary intervention is needed to improve β-cell function in T2D. Secondarily, our results will elucidate mechanisms of physical activity mitigating the development of micro- and macrovascular complications correlated with T2D.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Lyngbæk, Mark","Legård, Grit Elster","Bennetsen, Sebastian L.","Feineis, Camilla S.","Rasmussen, Villads","Moegelberg, Nana","Brinkløv, Cecilie F.","Nielsen, Anette B.","Kofoed, Katja S.","Lauridsen, Carsten A.","Ewertsen, Caroline","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Christensen, Robin","van Hall, Gerrit","Karstoft, Kristian","Solomon, Thomas P.J.","Ellingsgaard, Helga","Almdal, Thomas","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Ried-Larsen, Mathias"],"cuid":["S03-097.87-039250"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ried-Larsen, Mathias"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Blazon Scientific"],"keyword":["Exercise","Inflammation","Insulin Resistance","Lifestyle intervention","Oxidative stress","Randomised clinical trial","Randomised controlled trial","Type 2 diabetes mellitus","disease health science and nursing","β cell Function"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-KEN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-KEN","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of different doses of exercise on pancreatic β cell function in patients with newly diagnosed type 000000000002 diabetes study protocol for and rationale behind the dose ex multi arm parallel group randomised clinical trial","src":["kp","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-021-05207-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The Centre for Physical Activity Research (CFAS) is supported by TrygFonden (info@trygfonden.dk). The DOSE-EX study is supported by an additional grant from TrygFonden (ID: 124708) and Svend Andersen Fonden. Robin Christensen from the Parker Institute, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospital is supported by a core grant from the Oak Foundation (OCAY-18-774-OFIL). MPPL is funded by The Danish Diabetes Academy."],"id":"S03-097.87-039250","identifier":[{"id":"85103806997","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33794975","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8017660","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["kp-a6939140-4ca1-42ba-8e73-0f672ac33f40","ku-f176d9f8-3456-4448-972c-4ad9454ec250","sdu-cfe5df44-35c5-41d4-99ae-eb230e21a62d"],"keyword":["Exercise","Inflammation","Insulin resistance","Lifestyle intervention","Oxidative stress","Randomised clinical trial","Randomised controlled trial","Type 2 diabetes mellitus","disease, health science and nursing","β-cell function"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B36DBB65967A35C24D283F8B3459E412"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/181755877/s13063_021_05207_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa