","name":"Noe-Nygaard, Nanna","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefan","key":"piaseckipau","last":"Piasecki","locid":"aaa85f29-e235-4ecb-aca1-7a0bfc967f9e","name":"Piasecki, Stefan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jens","key":"therkelsenpau","last":"Therkelsen","name":"Therkelsen, Jens","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"vosgeraupau","last":"Vosgerau","name":"Vosgerau, Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34194/geusb.v46.6521","issn":["16048156","19044666"],"issn_org":["16048156"],"journal":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland (GEUS) Bulletin","paperid":"6521","status":"p","title":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland (GEUS) Bulletin","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111712498"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","moe a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-01afd723-1774-4066-b593-c6620b38f417"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Jurassic stratigraphy of East Greenland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394498","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The effect of oral glutathione (GSH) supplementation was studied in obese subjects with and without type 2 diabetes (T2DM) on measures of glucose homeostasis and markers of oxidative stress. Twenty subjects (10 patients with T2DM and 10 obese subjects) were recruited for the study, and randomized in a double-blinded placebo-controlled manner to consume either 1000 mg GSH per day or placebo for 3 weeks. Before and after the 3 weeks insulin sensitivity was measured with the hyperinsulinemic-euglycemic clamp and a muscle biopsy was obtained to measure GSH and skeletal muscle mitochondrial hydrogen peroxide (H2O2) emission rate. Whole body insulin sensitivity increased significantly in the GSH group. Skeletal muscle GSH was numerically increased (∼19%) in the GSH group; no change was seen in GSH to glutathione disulfide ratio. Skeletal muscle mitochondrial H2O2 emission rate did not change in response to the intervention and neither did the urinary excretion of the RNA oxidation product 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine or the DNA oxidation product 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2'-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG), although 8-oxodG decreased as a main effect of time. Oral GSH supplementation improves insulin sensitivity in obese subjects with and without T2DM, although it does not alter markers of oxidative stress. The study has been registered in clinicaltrials.gov (NCT02948673). Novelty: Reduced glutathione supplementation increases insulin sensitivity in obese subjects with and without T2DM. H2O2 emission rate from skeletal muscle mitochondria was not affected by GSH supplementation.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Søndergård, Stine D","Cintin, Ida","Kuhlman, Anja Birk","Morville, Thomas","Bergmann, Marie Louise","Kjær, Laura K","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Giustarini, Daniela","Rossi, Ranieri","Dela, Flemming","Helge, Jørn Wulff","Larsen, Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425924"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Siena"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of 000000000003 weeks of oral glutathione supplementation on whole body insulin sensitivity in obese males with and without type 000000000002 diabetes a randomized trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-425924","identifier":[{"id":"85114730165","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000695418000016","type":"wos"},{"id":"33740389","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-36ab5eb4-9331-4cee-b4c9-8ed3421591a3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-97AF1EC27BB89243DAD167ED19B66D55"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Torekov Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of siena","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Siena","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine D","key":"søndergårdpau","last":"Søndergård","locid":"bf638db0-41ca-454d-8e99-9f033742738c","name":"Søndergård, Stine D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida","key":"cintinpau","last":"Cintin","name":"Cintin, Ida","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja B","key":"kuhlmanpau","last":"Kuhlman","locid":"d1607964-8f7c-4ccb-a105-73c17ff3b8bd","name":"Kuhlman, Anja Birk","name_org":"Kuhlman, Anja B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas H","key":"morvillepau","last":"Morville","locid":"1b840aa6-720e-4e1e-a199-265170bc9147","name":"Morville, Thomas","name_org":"Morville, Thomas H","orcid":"0000-0002-9039-2591","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise","key":"bergmannpau","last":"Bergmann","name":"Bergmann, Marie Louise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Laura K","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Laura K","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","name_org":"Poulsen, Henrik E","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Daniela","key":"giustarinipau","last":"Giustarini","name":"Giustarini, Daniela","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ranieri","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","name":"Rossi, Ranieri","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"delapau","last":"Dela","locid":"5d84458e-34c1-4874-a128-7fc3cb13f7f2","name":"Dela, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-9970-9535","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørn W","key":"helgepau","last":"Helge","locid":"a5560afa-4f31-4278-8ae9-0c49fb0027c1","name":"Helge, Jørn Wulff","name_org":"Helge, Jørn W","orcid":"0000-0001-9724-5423","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7a869b1b-85f0-4d92-a44f-cbd16750054b","name":"Larsen, Steen","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33740389"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1139/apnm-2020-1099","issn":["17155312","17155320"],"issn_org":["17155312"],"issue":"9","journal":"Applied Physiology, Nutrition and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"Applied Physiology, Nutrition and Metabolism","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114730165"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-36ab5eb4-9331-4cee-b4c9-8ed3421591a3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of 3 weeks of oral glutathione supplementation on whole body insulin sensitivity in obese males with and without type 2 diabetes : a randomized trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425924","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor agonists have shown cardioprotective effects which have been suggested to be mediated through inhibition of oxidative stress. We investigated the effect of treatment with a glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor agonist (liraglutide) on oxidative stress measured as urinary nucleic acid oxidation in persons with type 2 diabetes. Post-hoc analysis of two independent, randomised, placebo-controlled and double-blinded clinical trials. In a cross-over study where persons with type 2 diabetes and microalbuminuria (LIRALBU, n = 32) received liraglutide (1.8 mg/day) or placebo for 12 weeks in random order, separated by 4 weeks of wash-out. In a parallel-grouped study where obese persons with type 2 diabetes (SAFEGUARD, n = 56) received liraglutide (1.8 mg/day), sitagliptin (100 mg/day) or placebo for 12 weeks. Endpoints were changes in the urinary markers of DNA oxidation (8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2′-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG)) and RNA oxidation [8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo)]. In LIRALBU, we observed no significant differences between treatment periods in urinary excretion of 8-oxodG [0.028 (standard error (SE): 0.17] nmol/mmol creatinine, p = 0.87) or of 8-oxoGuo [0.12 (0.12) nmol/mmol creatinine, p = 0.31]. In SAFEGUARD, excretion of 8-oxodG was not changed in the liraglutide group [2.8 (− 8.51; 15.49) %, p = 0.62] but a significant decline was demonstrated in the placebo group [12.6 (− 21.3; 3.1) %, p = 0.02], resulting in a relative increase in the liraglutide group compared to placebo (0.16 nmol/mmol creatinine, SE 0.07, p = 0.02). Treatment with sitagliptin compared to placebo demonstrated no significant difference (0.07 (0.07) nmol/mmol creatinine, p = 0.34). Nor were any significant differences for urinary excretion of 8-oxoGuo liraglutide vs placebo [0.09 (SE: 0.07) nmol/mmol creatinine, p = 0.19] or sitagliptin vs placebo [0.07 (SE: 0.07) nmol/mmol creatinine, p = 0.35] observed. This post-hoc analysis could not demonstrate a beneficial effect of 12 weeks of treatment with liraglutide or sitagliptin on oxidatively generated modifications of nucleic acid in persons with type 2 diabetes.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Sivalingam, Suvanjaa","Larsen, Emil List","van Raalte, Daniel H.","Muskiet, Marcel H.A.","Smits, Mark M.","Tonneijck, Lennart","Joles, Jaap A.","von Scholten, Bernt Johan","Zobel, Emilie Hein","Persson, Frederik","Henriksen, Trine","Diaz, Lars Jorge","Hansen, Tine W.","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Rossing, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429041"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of liraglutide and sitagliptin on oxidative stress in persons with type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-90191-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-429041","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8134438","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34012064","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85106049038","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3ba1b4c5-e2be-4226-bc94-6ff3320cee0e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A8AA518D4A42CEBFFE3ED990F45062B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/272027373/s41598_021_90191_w.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-90191-w","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Suvanjaa","key":"sivalingampau","last":"Sivalingam","locid":"8f249ed7-e923-4ae3-be3d-3cb9bce929e0","name":"Sivalingam, Suvanjaa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel H.","key":"vanraaltepau","last":"van Raalte","name":"van Raalte, Daniel H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcel H.A.","key":"muskietpau","last":"Muskiet","name":"Muskiet, Marcel H.A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark M.","key":"smitspau","last":"Smits","name":"Smits, Mark M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lennart","key":"tonneijckpau","last":"Tonneijck","name":"Tonneijck, Lennart","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jaap A.","key":"jolespau","last":"Joles","name":"Joles, Jaap A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bernt Johan","key":"vonscholtenpau","last":"von Scholten","name":"von Scholten, Bernt Johan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emilie Hein","key":"zobelpau","last":"Zobel","name":"Zobel, Emilie Hein","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frederik","key":"perssonpau","last":"Persson","name":"Persson, Frederik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Trine","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Trine","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars Jorge","key":"diazpau","last":"Diaz","name":"Diaz, Lars Jorge","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tine W.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Tine W.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Enghusen","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"ca397e2f-e1b3-430b-a537-a047438b44b6","name":"Rossing, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1531-4294","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34012064"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-021-90191-w","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"10624","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106049038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3ba1b4c5-e2be-4226-bc94-6ff3320cee0e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effect of liraglutide and sitagliptin on oxidative stress in persons with type 2 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-429041","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Biotin (or Vitamin B7) is a vitamin where deficiency can be caused by inadequate intake. Biotin deficiency is rare, as most people get enough biotin from diet, since many foods contain biotin. In addition to biotin from food, intestinal bacteria can synthesize biotin, which can then be absorbed by the body. Supplementation with biotin has been advocated, mainly due to proposed beneficial effects on skin, nail and hair growth. There is no evidence that high biotin intakes are toxic, but a high intake may interfere with diagnostic assays that use biotin-streptavidin technology. These tests are commonly used to measure plasma concentrations of a wide range of hormones. Erroneous results may lead to misdiagnosis of various endocrine disorders. Supplementation with high-dose biotin has been used experimental for the treatment of diseases (e.g. multiple sclerosis) and high doses are used to obtain effect on nail and hair growth. On this background a demand for tests to determine if there is a risk of obtaining false test results when using biotin-streptavidin based tests have appeared. In this paper we present a method based on column switching liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry for the quantification of biotin in plasma and serum and explore the effects of biotin on an immunoassay based on biotin strept(avidin) chemistry.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Weimann, Allan","Plomgaard, Peter","Hilsted, Linda M.","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Larsen, Emil L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429561"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantification of biotin in plasma samples by column switching liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-429561","identifier":[{"id":"85099590371","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33461365","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3c720431-992b-4627-8f90-f7e9f5fa9f7b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E130CC69902845A633DEFA60DFFB838"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"weimannpau","last":"Weimann","name":"Weimann, Allan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"plomgaardpau","last":"Plomgaard","locid":"876d799c-45f9-4296-8dc4-455c10728a8a","name":"Plomgaard, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda M.","key":"hilstedpau","last":"Hilsted","name":"Hilsted, Linda M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","name_org":"Poulsen, Henrik E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emil L.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33461365"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365513.2020.1871504","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"127-136","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical and Laboratory Investigation","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099590371"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3c720431-992b-4627-8f90-f7e9f5fa9f7b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quantification of biotin in plasma samples by column switching liquid chromatography – tandem mass spectrometry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-429561","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: In hospitalized patients, abnormal plasma electrolyte concentrations are frequent and have been linked to poor outcomes following acute surgery. The aim of this study was to assess whether preoperative plasma levels of potassium, sodium, and creatinine at the time of admission were associated with 30-day mortality in patients following open abdominal surgery. Methods: This was a single-center register-based retrospective study. By means of electronic search in a maintained surgery database, all patients (n = 4177) aged ≥ 60 years old undergoing open surgery in our department from January 2000 to May 2013 were identified. Plasma was assessed within 30 days prior to surgery. The primary endpoint was 30-day postoperative mortality. The association between mortality and plasma levels of potassium, sodium, and creatinine were examined using Cox proportional hazard models. Results: A total of 3690 patients were included in the study cohort. The rates of abnormal preoperative plasma levels were 36, 41, and 38% for potassium, sodium, and creatinine, respectively. The overall 30 day mortality was 20%. A predictive algorithm for 30 day mortality following abdominal surgery was constructed by means of logistic regression showing excellent distinction between patients with and without a fatal postoperative outcome. Conclusion: Apart from demographic factors (age, sex, and emergency surgery), preoperative imbalance in potassium, sodium and creatinine levels were significant independent predictors of early mortality following open abdominal surgery.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ebrahim, Mohamed","Larsen, Pia Bükmann","Hannani, Damoun","Liest, Sara","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-432027"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithm","Creatinine","Electrolytes","Frailty","Mortality","Surgery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preoperative risk factors including serum levels of potassium sodium and creatinine for early mortality after open abdominal surgery a retrospective cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12893-021-01070-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-432027","identifier":[{"id":"33499844","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85099923097","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7836189","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4085259b-061f-4c14-b0b3-8a67271abede"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Creatinine","Electrolytes","Frailty","Mortality","Surgery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4A7A7C7478A50970FED12D1D30CD883F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12893-021-01070-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/256627269/s12893_021_01070_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mohamed","key":"ebrahimmohamedpau","last":"Ebrahim","name":"Ebrahim, Mohamed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pia Bükmann","key":"larsenpiabükmannpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Pia Bükmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Damoun","key":"hannanidamounpau","last":"Hannani","name":"Hannani, Damoun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sara","key":"liestsarapau","last":"Liest","name":"Liest, Sara","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Nannestad","key":"jørgensenlarsnannestadpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Løvendahl","key":"jørgensenhenrikløvendahlpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cf84c34a-16a5-4a24-9667-bc1c2481e1a5","name":"Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33499844"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12893-021-01070-0","issn":["14712482"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Surgery","paperid":"62","status":"p","title":"BMC Surgery","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099923097"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4085259b-061f-4c14-b0b3-8a67271abede"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preoperative risk factors including serum levels of potassium, sodium, and creatinine for early mortality after open abdominal surgery : a retrospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432027","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to investigate the characteristics of patients co-infected with Chlamydia trachomatis and Neisseria gonorrhoea. A retrospective case-control study was performed, which included 399 co-infected patients seen at a sexually transmitted infection clinic in Copenhagen, Denmark. Case-control groups included 300 patients who tested positive only for N. gonorrhoea, 300 who tested positive only for C. trachomatis, and 300 who tested negative for both N. gonorrhoea and C. trachomatis in the same study period. For men, non-Danish origin (odds ratio (OR) 2.3, 95% confidence interval (Cl) 1.34–4.12), previous sexually transmitted infections with C. trachomatis (OR 3.3, 95% CI 1.94–5.92) and N. gonorrhoea (OR 10.6, 95% CI 6.36-17.76), and higher number of sex partners (OR 1.7, 95% Cl 1.40-2.28) were significantly associated with diagnosis of co-infection. For women, previous sexually transmitted infections with C. trachomatis (OR 6.7, 95% CI 3.89-11.78) and N. gonorrhoea (OR 10.4, 95% CI 4.99-21.71), and higher number of sex partners (OR 1.8, 95% CI 1.28-2.56) were significantly associated with a diagnosis of co-infection, whereas being of non-Danish origin was, in some cases, a protective factor (OR 0.3, 95% CI 0.17-0.69). Furthermore, this study demonstrated sex-associated characteristics that should raise concern about coinfection, including: for men, being of non-Danish origin, men who have sex with men status, and higher age, and, for women, young age, in particular, and previous sexually transmitted infections.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Barati Sedeh, Farnam","Thomsen, Simon Francis","Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Westh, Henrik","Saladorasmussen, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-513998"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chlamydia","Co infection","Gonorrhoea"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex associated risk factors for co infection with i chlamydia trachomatis i and i neisseria gonorrhoea i among patients presenting to a sexually transmitted infection clinic","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/00015555-3721","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-513998","identifier":[{"id":"85099326320","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9309828","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33320275","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c9deeb24-4e54-4289-96fc-80bc090774b8"],"keyword":["Chlamydia","Co-infection","Gonorrhoea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66035EFD91FDC7B8AA783F9BBCF2CFBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/00015555-3721","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/256939780/5967.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Inflammation, Metabolism and Oxidation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Farnam","key":"baratisedehpau","last":"Barati Sedeh","name":"Barati Sedeh, Farnam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Simon Francis","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"045de28d-7e61-4908-8fa9-afd09ac8234a","name":"Thomsen, Simon Francis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle Kiellberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cff32a53-c07d-466a-9bf3-cc621c1e2cb6","name":"Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"saladorasmussenpau","last":"Saladorasmussen","name":"Saladorasmussen, Kirsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33320275"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/00015555-3721","issn":["00015555","16512057"],"issn_org":["00015555"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Dermato-Venereologica","pages":"1-7","paperid":"adv00356","status":"p","title":"Acta Dermato-Venereologica","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099326320"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c9deeb24-4e54-4289-96fc-80bc090774b8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sex-associated risk factors for co-infection with <i>chlamydia trachomatis</i> and <i>neisseria gonorrhoea</i> among patients presenting to a sexually transmitted infection clinic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-513998","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Two siblings were diagnosed with adult metachromatic leukodystrophy (MLD) and treated with hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT). While the older sibling was symptomatic at the time of diagnosis, her younger brother was diagnosed and transplanted at the presymptomatic state. We describe patients' clinical, biochemical, and genetic features, as well as neuropsychological and neurophysiological test results, and brain magnetic resonance imaging from pretransplantation and posttransplantation assessments. Both patients converted to complete donor chimerism and arylsulfatase A levels normalized 3 months posttransplantation. Twelve months posttransplantation, neurological and neuropsychological assessment for both patients showed stabilization, and they remained stable for the 38 months long observation period. To assess the effect of HSCT used as treatment for the rare, adult MLD subtype on survival and stabilization, we performed a systematic literature review and included 7 studies with a total of 26 cases. Of these 26 cases, 6 patients died of HSCT-related complications and 2 patients had graft rejection. Of the remaining 18 patients, 2 patients improved after HSCT, 13 patients stabilized, and 3 patients progressed, suggesting that HSCT potentially benefits adult MLD patients. Larger studies focusing on this subtype are needed and recommendations on criteria for HSCT in adult MLD need to be evolved.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Videbæk, Cecilie","Stokholm, Jette","Sengeløv, Henrik","Fjeldborg, Lone U.","Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","Krarup, Christian","Nielsen, Jørgen Erik","Grønborg, Sabine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-544951"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Den Sociale Virksomhed"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"allogenic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation in two siblings with adult metachromatic leukodystrophy and a systematic literature review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jmd2.12221","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-544951","identifier":[{"id":"85121691783","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34258145","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8260480","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-fdee320a-f25c-4108-81d4-ef06cc7194db"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-372CE6A051123235550DB7749410C688"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jmd2.12221","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290601928/Allogenic_hematopoietic_stem_cell_transplantation_in_two_siblings_with_adult_metachromatic_leukodystrophy_and_a_systematic_literature_review.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Haematology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Den Sociale Virksomhed"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie","key":"videbækpau","last":"Videbæk","name":"Videbæk, Cecilie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","name":"Stokholm, Jette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"sengeløvpau","last":"Sengeløv","locid":"ff0cb82b-deb8-4d4e-b871-8f70d359af15","name":"Sengeløv, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lone U.","key":"fjeldborgpau","last":"Fjeldborg","name":"Fjeldborg, Lone U.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke Andrée","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"kraruppau","last":"Krarup","locid":"bd59f25a-fa63-4ea7-b6ce-1b8fe1b11c12","name":"Krarup, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-4903-9681","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jørgen E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"eefef282-eb8c-4a7f-a85e-4b77dd779a3c","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Erik","name_org":"Nielsen, Jørgen E.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sabine","key":"grønborgpau","last":"Grønborg","name":"Grønborg, Sabine","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34258145"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jmd2.12221","issn":["21928304","21928312"],"issn_org":["21928304"],"issue":"1","journal":"JIMD Reports","pages":"96-104","status":"p","title":"JIMD Reports","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121691783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fdee320a-f25c-4108-81d4-ef06cc7194db"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Allogenic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation in two siblings with adult metachromatic leukodystrophy and a systematic literature review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-544951","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Dynamically loaded structures are generally in risk of fatigue damage. The fatigue lives of such structures can be improved using traditional methods like producing a better weld or using post-weld treatment. Another method is to improve the overall design of the structure by using the finite element method in combination with shape optimization. In this paper, a framework for finite element shape optimization has been developed, considering the fatigue life of welded joints. Simplicity and the possibility of including different fatigue estimation methods have been in focus for the framework. The framework has been used on a simple plate structure, where the weld orientation has been optimized based on four different fatigue criteria. The results show that the criteria from governing guidelines predict the same optimized weld orientation. However, the critical plane approaches cannot produce optimized weld orientations, when using the nominal stress approach as it does not account for increased stresses from the weld.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold","Arora, Vikas","Clausen, Henrik Bisgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-618890"],"event":{"end":"2020-09-18","place":"Dubrovnik, hr","start":"2020-09-15","title":"4th International Conference on Structural Integrity and Durability","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-RAM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-RAM","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"finite element shape optimization of weld orientation in simple plate structure considering different fatigue estimation methods","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.prostr.2021.03.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-618890","identifier":[{"id":"85121280294","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-9f859dc3-e57b-4e9b-9d7f-0cf9937121ec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC235A647EEAF4A8CDBFD475CE98F5FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.prostr.2021.03.011","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/197442205/1_s2.0_S2452321621000135_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, SDU Mechanical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ramboll group","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-RAM","l3nl":"Rambøll Group","l3nn":"Ramboll Group","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ramboll Group","namevar":["Ramboll Offshore Wind"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-RAM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Løvenskjold","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1e448908-ddff-4e12-811d-0e9d88a3dff9","name":"Larsen, Mikkel Løvenskjold","orcid":"0000-0003-2853-6563","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vikas","key":"arorapau","last":"Arora","locid":"825c3f36-eeab-4635-980b-01218adb6f82","name":"Arora, Vikas","orcid":"0000-0002-4369-7851","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bisgaard","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Henrik Bisgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.prostr.2021.03.011","issn":["24523216"],"journal":"Procedia Structural Integrity","pages":"70-74","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Procedia Structural Integrity","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121280294"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Rambøll Group","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9f859dc3-e57b-4e9b-9d7f-0cf9937121ec"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Finite element shape optimization of weld orientation in simple plate structure considering different fatigue estimation methods","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-618890","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
