 of Emergency Medicine","pages":"11-18","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Annals of Emergency Medicine","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088927296"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-62753239-20e1-4c2f-b58d-ba53e4a803c6","au-5132f752-cf6a-49e5-91c6-e20a1084394f","ku-9d1dbd70-8a64-413b-ac30-197dbcb06334","sdu-eb7c6de4-421b-4630-9822-aa4945abdeb5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Normocellular Community-Acquired Bacterial Meningitis in Adults : A Nationwide Population-Based Case Series","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-004791","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of the present study was, among other things, to evaluate how tenants perceived the indoor environment in renovated and energy-retrofitted social housing erected in the 1960s. Tenants answered a questionnaire to quantify problems and satisfaction with the indoor environment before and after the renovation work. A majority of tenants perceived the indoor environment improved for all parameters: temperature, draught, air quality, noise and daylight, after the renovation work. In particular, the tenants experienced fewer problems with too low temperature and draught during the winter, noise from outside and too little daylight. The evaluation shows that it is possible to achieve a win-win situation, with both energy savings and improved perceived indoor environment. The evaluation also reveals that careful attention is needed to avoid introducing annoying noise from new technical installations.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","Bekö, Gabriel","Larsen, Tine Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064641"],"event":{"acronym":"HB","end":"2021-06-23","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2021-06-21","title":"Healthy Buildings Europe 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Almene boliger","Brugeroplevelse","Building renovation","Energirenovering","Energy savings","Indeklima","Indoor climate","Indoor environment","Occupant satisfaction","Oplevet indeklima","Perceived indoor climate","Questionnaire survey","Renovering","Tenant s satisfaction","Tilfredshed","Ventilation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perceived indoor environment in social housing with different ventilation principles","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/461307714/Perceived_indoor_environment_in_social_housing_with_different_ventilation_principles.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064641","ids":["aau-3263219a-9647-4e90-98a2-5503a35faa4a"],"keyword":["Almene boliger","Brugeroplevelse","Building renovation","Energirenovering","Energy savings","Indeklima","Indoor environment","Occupant satisfaction","Oplevet indeklima","Perceived indoor climate","Questionnaire survey","Renovering","Tenant’s satisfaction","Tilfredshed","Ventilation","indoor climate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E0DE6ACD6D71AAAD390B5FF73F509159"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/461307714/Perceived_indoor_environment_in_social_housing_with_different_ventilation_principles.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Energy and Sustainability in Buildings","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Indoor Environmental Quality and Building Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Nellemose","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7f5e707b-235a-4e71-ae71-e9278e7aa2ba","name":"Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","orcid":"0000-0002-3196-7279","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gabriel","key":"beköpau","last":"Bekö","name":"Bekö, Gabriel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6f4c1acc-34db-423a-9567-359fc381a0c4","name":"Larsen, Tine Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-4704-6503","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guangyu","key":"caopedh","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Guangyu","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sverre B.","key":"holøspedh","last":"Holøs","name":"Holøs, Sverre B.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Moon Keun","key":"kimpedh","last":"Kim","name":"Kim, Moon Keun","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter G.","key":"schildpedh","last":"Schild","name":"Schild, Peter G.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788253617282 (Pdf)"],"issn":["23874295"],"issue":"9","pages":"468-477","publisher":"SINTEF Academic Press","series":"SINTEF proceedings","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 17th International Healthy Buildings Conference 21–23 June 2021","title":"Healthy Buildings 2021 – Europe"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3263219a-9647-4e90-98a2-5503a35faa4a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Perceived indoor environment in social housing with different ventilation principles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064641","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE To ascertain the association and coaggregation of eating disorders and childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in families. RESEARCH DESIGN AND METHODS Using population samples from national registers in Sweden (n 5 2,517,277) and Demark (n 5 1,825,920), we investigated the within-individual association between type 1 diabetes and eating disorders and their familial coaggregation among full siblings, half siblings, full cousins, and half cousins. On the basis of clinical diagnoses, we classified eating disorders into any eating disorder (AED), anorexia nervosa (AN) and atypical AN, and other eating disorder (OED). Associations were determined with hazard ratios (HRs) with 95% CIs from Cox regressions. RESULTS Swedish and Danish individuals with a type 1 diabetes diagnosis had a greater risk of receiving an eating disorder diagnosis (HR [95% CI] Sweden: AED 2.02 [1.80–2.27], AN 1.63 [1.36–1.96], OED 2.34 [2.07–2.63]; Denmark: AED 2.19 [1.84–2.61], AN 1.78 [1.36–2.33], OED 2.65 [2.20–3.21]). We also meta-analyzed the results: AED 2.07 (1.88–2.28), AN 1.68 (1.44–1.95), OED 2.44 (2.17–2.72). There was an increased risk of receiving an eating disorder diagnosis in full siblings in the Swedish cohort (AED 1.25 [1.07–1.46], AN 1.28 [1.04–1.57], OED 1.28 [1.07–1.52]); these results were nonsignificant in the Danish cohort. CONCLUSIONS Patients with type 1 diabetes are at a higher risk of subsequent eating disorders; however, there is conflicting support for the relationship between having a sibling with type 1 diabetes and an eating disorder diagnosis. Diabetes health care teams should be vigilant about disordered eating behaviors in children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Tate, Ashley E.","Liu, Shengxin","Zhang, Ruyue","Yilmaz, Zeynep","Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","Petersen, Liselotte","Bulik, Cynthia M.","Svensson, Ann Marie","Gudbjörnsdottir, Soffia","Larsson, Henrik","Butwicka, Agnieszka","Kuja-Halkola, Ralf"],"cuid