{"abstract":"An 8-Channel flexible array is proposed for hyperpolarized 13C, where the coil coupling coefficients are matched to be nearly identical at the 13C (32.1 MHz) and 23Na (33.8 MHz) frequencies. This way, the 23Na present in biological tissue can be used to obtain accurate 13C profiles.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sanchez, Juan Diego","Wang, Wenjun","Grist, James T.","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Laustsen, Christoffer","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334730"],"event":{"end":"2021-05-20","place":"Online","start":"2021-05-15","title":"2021 ISMRM &amp; SMRT Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flexible 000000000008 channel array for hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c at 000000000003t 000000000032 000000000001 mhz with nearly identical sup 000000000023 sup na 000000000033 000000000008 mhz sensitivity pro","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265179396/ISMRM2021_JD.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334730","ids":["dtu-6525e58a-ae40-4684-8653-bbe008207295"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2BFA64908DF03246468ED0830206C77D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265179396/ISMRM2021_JD.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"James T.","key":"gristpau","last":"Grist","name":"Grist, James T.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"søvsøszocskahansenpau","last":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen","name":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6525e58a-ae40-4684-8653-bbe008207295"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Flexible 8-Channel Array for Hyperpolarized <sup>13</sup>C at 3T (32.1 MHz), with Nearly Identical <sup>23</sup>Na (33.8 MHz) Sensitivity Pro","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334730","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The basic principles of dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) will be described with the aim to hyperpolarize nuclear spins for in vivo magnetic resonance imaging and its applications. Hyperpolarization signifies a strong, nonequilibrium nuclear spin polarization, and as a consequence, a strong enhancement of the available magnetic resonance signal. dDNP is one of several methods to hyperpolarize nuclear spins in the liquid state, and the most general. However, hyperpolarization and dDNP have some limitations that will be discussed. It requires a device, the polarizer, to create the solution of hyperpolarized nuclear spins. The device and pharmaceutical requirements for clinical translation are presented. We will discuss the implications of imaging strong, nonequilibrium nuclear spin polarization from a pulse sequence and scanner perspective. 13C-labeled pyruvate is the first agent to be introduced clinically and progress toward the application of hyperpolarized 13C metabolic imaging in oncology, cardiology, and neurology are reviewed.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340308"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized magnetic resonance with dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization principles and applications","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85129106968","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340308","identifier":[{"id":"85129106968","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-77b0994a-6f20-4cea-b09e-8905d62fee06"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-752D1EA06C6FB25B403CC3A0DDC3D50E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan H.","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/b978-0-12-816386-3.00036-3","edition":"2","eisbn":["9780128163863"],"isbn":["9780128163870"],"pages":"563-581","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","subtitle":"Principles and Practice","title":"Molecular Imaging"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129106968"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-77b0994a-6f20-4cea-b09e-8905d62fee06"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Hyperpolarized Magnetic Resonance With Dissolution Dynamic Nuclear Polarization : Principles and Applications","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340308","year":"2021","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Loads from storm waves can in some cases be dimensioning for offshore wind turbine substructures. Accurate determination of nonlinear wave loads is therefore important for a safe, yet economic design. In this paper, the fully nonlinear waves, realized by a fully nonlinear potential wave solver OceanWave3D, are incorporated into coupled aero-servo-hydro-elastic simulations for a reduced set of wave-sensitive design load cases, in comparison with the widely used linear and constrained waves. The coupled aero-elastic simulations are performed for the DTU 10 MW reference wind turbine on a large monopile at 33 m water depth using the aero-elastic code HAWC2. Effect of the wave nonlinearity is investigated in terms of the ultimate sectional moments at tower bottom and monopile mudline. Higher ultimate moments, 5% at tower bottom and 13% at monopile mudline as maximum, are predicated when the nonlinear waves are used. It could be explained by the fact that the extreme nonlinear waves, that are close to the breaking limit, can induce resonant ringing-type responses, and hereby dominate the ultimate load responses. However, the constrained wave approach shows marginal difference compared to the standard linear wave approach. It can be concluded at least for the present configuration that the industry standard approaches (linear and constrained wave approach) underestimate the ultimate load responses on offshore wind turbines in severe sea states.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wang, Shaofeng","Larsen, Torben Juul","Bredmose, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346042"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Wang, Shaofeng"],"keyword":["Ultimate load"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultimate load analysis of a 000000000010 mw offshore monopile wind turbine incorporating fully nonlinear irregular wave kinematics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277178708/MASTR_D_20_00175_Revised_ShaofengWang2020.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-346042","identifier":[{"id":"85098457360","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8b128210-11df-4a41-9136-19aed5ef40e8"],"keyword":["Fully nonlinear wave kinematics","Offshore monopile wind turbine","Ultimate load"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B1A2A7E592C39667F55C55A25159478"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277178708/MASTR_D_20_00175_Revised_ShaofengWang2020.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shaofeng","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"17f49d6a-2ba8-4205-88f0-ec4c7246de62","name":"Wang, Shaofeng","orcid":"0000-0003-3113-0468","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Juul","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Torben Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bredmosepau","last":"Bredmose","locid":"a46a2dd1-d040-4240-8dfb-bdb22c646a47","name":"Bredmose, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-0753","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marstruc.2020.102922","issn":["09518339","18734170"],"issn_org":["09518339"],"journal":"Marine Structures","paperid":"102922","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Marine Structures","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098457360"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8b128210-11df-4a41-9136-19aed5ef40e8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Ultimate load analysis of a 10 MW offshore monopile wind turbine incorporating fully nonlinear irregular wave kinematics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-346042","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarized 13C magnetic resonance (MR) is a promising technique for the noninvasive assessment of the regional cardiac metabolism since it permits heart physiology studies in pig and mouse models. The main objective of the present study is to resume the work carried out at our electromagnetic laboratory in the field of radio frequency (RF) coil design, building, and testing. In this paper, first, we review the principles of RF coils, coil performance parameters, and estimation methods by using simulations, workbench, and MR imaging experiments. Then, we describe the simulation, design, and testing of different 13C coil configurations and acquisition settings for hyperpolarized studies on pig and mouse heart with a clinical 3T MRI scanner. The coil simulation is performed by developing a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) model in terms of coil resistance, sample-induced resistance, and magnetic field pattern. Coil resistance was calculated from Ohm’s law and sample-induced resistances were estimated with a finite-difference time-domain (FDTD) algorithm. In contrast, the magnetic field per unit current was calculated by magnetostatic theory and a FDTD algorithm. The information could be of interest to graduate students and researchers working on the design and development of an MR coil to be used in 13C studies.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Giovannetti, Giulio","Flori, Alessandra","Santarelli, Maria Filomena","Positano, Vincenzo","Martini, Nicola","Francischello, Roberto","Schulte, Rolf F.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Menichetti, Luca","Aquaro, Giovanni Donato","Barison, Andrea","Frijia, Francesca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347536"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Giovannetti, Giulio"],"country":["Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","National Research Council of Italy"],"keyword":["Magnetic resonance","Simulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"radio frequency coils for hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c magnetic resonance experiments with a 000000000003t mr clinical scanner experience from a cardiovascular lab","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics10040366","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This research was funded by a grant from the Italian Ministry of Health and Tuscany Region Myocardial perfusion imaging with cardiovascular magnetic resonance and hyperpolarized contrast media (GR-2016-02361586)."],"id":"S01-000.00-347536","identifier":[{"id":"85100541159","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-900a98df-0405-4710-9631-6f84ac3caa74"],"keyword":["Magnetic resonance","Radio frequency coils","Simulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACB566D63C9A65A5615F3403CB7C4AAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics10040366","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/263880221/electronics_10_00366_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"ge healthcare","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GE Healthcare","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giulio","key":"giovannettipau","last":"Giovannetti","name":"Giovannetti, Giulio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandra","key":"floripau","last":"Flori","name":"Flori, Alessandra","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Filomena","key":"santarellipau","last":"Santarelli","name":"Santarelli, Maria Filomena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo","key":"positanopau","last":"Positano","name":"Positano, Vincenzo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"martinipau","last":"Martini","name":"Martini, Nicola","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"francischellopau","last":"Francischello","name":"Francischello, Roberto","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf F.","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, Rolf F.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"menichettipau","last":"Menichetti","name":"Menichetti, Luca","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni Donato","key":"aquaropau","last":"Aquaro","name":"Aquaro, Giovanni Donato","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"barisonpau","last":"Barison","name":"Barison, Andrea","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"frijiapau","last":"Frijia","name":"Frijia, Francesca","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/electronics10040366","issn":["20799292"],"issue":"4","journal":"Electronics","paperid":"366","publisher":"MDPI AG","status":"p","title":"Electronics","title_org":"Electronics (Switzerland)","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100541159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-900a98df-0405-4710-9631-6f84ac3caa74"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Radio frequency coils for hyperpolarized <sup>13</sup>C magnetic resonance experiments with a 3T mr clinical scanner : Experience from a cardiovascular lab","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347536","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Oral delivery is a highly preferred method for drug administration due to high patient compliance. However, oral administration is intrinsically challenging for pharmacologically interesting drug classes, in particular pharmaceutical peptides, due to the biological barriers associated with the gastrointestinal tract. In this review, we start by summarizing the pharmacological performance of several clinically relevant orally administrated therapeutic peptides, highlighting their low bioavailabilities. Thus, there is a strong need to increase the transport of peptide drugs across the intestinal barrier to realize future treatment needs and further development in the field. Currently, progress is hampered by a lack of understanding of transport mechanisms that govern intestinal absorption and transport of peptide drugs, including the effects of the permeability enhancers commonly used to mediate uptake. We describe how, for the past decades, mechanistic insights have predominantly been gained using functional assays with end-point read-out capabilities, which only allow indirect study of peptide transport mechanisms. We then focus on fluorescence imaging that, on the other hand, provides opportunities to directly visualize and thus follow peptide transport at high spatiotemporal resolution. Consequently, it may provide new and detailed mechanistic understanding of the interplay between the physicochemical properties of peptides and cellular processes; an interplay that determines the efficiency of transport. We review current methodology and state of the art in the field of fluorescence imaging to study intestinal barrier transport of peptides, and provide a comprehensive overview of the imaging-compatible in vitro, ex vivo, and in vivo platforms that currently are being developed to accelerate this emerging field of research. This journal is","author_count":16,"contributors":["Larsen, Jannik B.","Taebnia, Nayere","Dolatshahi-Pirouz, Alireza","Eriksen, Anne Zebitz","Hjørringgaard, Claudia","Kristensen, Kasper","Larsen, Nanna Wichmann","Larsen, Niels Bent","Marie, Rodolphe","Mündler, Ann Kathrin","Parhamifar, Ladan","Urquhart, Andrew J.","Weller, Arjen","Mortensen, Kim I.","Flyvbjerg, Henrik","Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347672"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imaging therapeutic peptide transport across intestinal barriers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d1cb00024a","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (Grant No. NNF16OC0022166)."],"id":"S01-000.00-347672","identifier":[{"id":"85112166684","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8341777","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34458827","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-9085cd7f-5b8d-480e-979e-160ce8209504"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3CE594199C25C9D316CEC335A50FD41"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d1cb00024a","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/264652801/d1cb00024a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["