esen, Thomas Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-1048-127X","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34458827"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d1cb00024a","issn":["26330679"],"issue":"4","journal":"RSC Chemical Biology","pages":"1115-1143","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"RSC Chemical Biology","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112166684"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9085cd7f-5b8d-480e-979e-160ce8209504"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Imaging therapeutic peptide transport across intestinal barriers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347672","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Magnetic Resonance is a powerful imaging modality which relies on arrays of detector coils to collect weak RF signals. Parasitic coupling between array elements degrades imaging system performance and greatly complicates array design process. In this work we show how to significantly reduce interaction between array elements by employing a modified high-impedance coil structure and combining it with a noise-matched low-input-impedance LNA.The approach is verified experimentally by designing a two element array for Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) of carbon-13. The fabricated detector demonstrates over 35 dB decoupling between array elements. Imaging experiments in a 3 tesla MRI scanner showed very low variation of noise correlation between channels in the array. The coils utilize flexible conductors and suitable for construction of flexible arrays conformal to different patient sizes.The presented approach is useful in the design of antenna arrays and RF detector arrays where channel-to-channel interaction creates a significant problem.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Wang, Wenjun","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-369103"],"event":{"end":"2021-01-14","place":"Utrecht, nl","start":"2021-01-12","title":"50<sup>th</sup> European Microwave Conference","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Zhurbenko, Vitaliy"],"keyword":["Biomedical electronics","Detectors","Low noise amplifiers","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Mutual coupling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flexible self resonant detector coil for magnetic resonance imaging of carbon 000000000013","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/241044821/EuMW2020_HIC_final_PID6489701.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-369103","identifier":[{"id":"85100947257","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d7fb747a-011f-4e25-a29e-a372de3a5252"],"keyword":["Air coils","Biomedical electronics","Detectors","Low-noise amplifiers","Magnetic resonance imaging","Mutual coupling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1BABCF22EB4F6826F39D2DB72590A922"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/241044821/EuMW2020_HIC_final_PID6489701.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electromagnetic Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan D.","key":"sanchezherediapau","last":"Sanchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sanchez-Heredia, Juan D.","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"21310cb6-dd90-4add-b43a-5ada0e7d9da9","name":"Wang, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-7781-9856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan H.","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/eumc48046.2021.9338182","isbn":["9781728170398"],"pages":"112-115","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2020 European Microwave Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100947257"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d7fb747a-011f-4e25-a29e-a372de3a5252"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Flexible Self-Resonant Detector Coil for Magnetic Resonance Imaging of Carbon-13","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-369103","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"A previous study of the effect of Gadolinium doping on the dynamic polarization (DNP) of 13C using trityls showed that the rate at which the polarization builds up is almost independent of the Gadolinium concentration, while the electron spin–lattice relaxation rate varies over an order of magnitude. In this paper we analyze the polarization build-up in detail and show that in this case DNP is due to the cross-effect (CE) and that the build-up rate can be quantitatively interpreted as the rate of the triple spin flips responsible for the CE. Thus this build-up rate presents a direct measurement of this triple spin flip rate.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wenckebach, W. Th","Capozzi, Andrea","Patel, Saket","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373497"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wenckebach, W. Th"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paul Scherrer Institute"],"keyword":["Cross Effect","Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"direct measurement of the triple spin flip rate in dynamic nuclear polarization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85105696919","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The research leading to these results has received funding from the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF124), the Swiss National Fund under the SPARK grant agreement No. CRSK-2_190547 and Ambizione grant agreement No. PZ00P2_193276 and the European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 713683 (COFUNDfellowsDTU). The research leading to these results has received funding from the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF124), the Swiss National Fund under the SPARK grant agreement No. CRSK-2_190547 and Ambizione grant agreement No. PZ00P2_193276 and the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 713683 (COFUNDfellowsDTU)."],"id":"S01-000.00-373497","identifier":[{"id":"33932911","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85105696919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e68b35d5-556b-4ec2-abfb-c83b1886aed7"],"keyword":["Cross effect","Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarization","Thermal mixing","Triple spin flip rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4A9C333D0B69AF56A39382149D2C2866"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"paul scherrer institute","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Paul Scherrer Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance, Hyperpolarization & Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"W. Th","key":"wenckebachpau","last":"Wenckebach","name":"Wenckebach, W. Th","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"capozzipau","last":"Capozzi","locid":"b0cf62b2-059b-44b4-b