{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","Larsen, Lars Erik","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Kvisgaard, Lise K"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398548"],"event":{"end":"2021-04-16","start":"2021-04-14","title":"ESPHM 2020+1","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"histological examination of testes and epididymides from boars naturally infected with porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus prrsv","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-398548","ids":["ku-08773d5b-f1d8-4f70-881b-fac87f49dbdf"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C4D8C907F8676D11323DDD2555977580"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie Amalie","key":"blirupplumpau","last":"Blirup-Plum","locid":"54f7ba11-2529-4cf7-adb1-139dfa0e4b53","name":"Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lise K","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise K","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-08773d5b-f1d8-4f70-881b-fac87f49dbdf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Histological examination of testes and epididymides from boars naturally infected with porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus (PRRSV)","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-398548","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Glucocorticoids modulate the surgical stress response. Previous studies showed that high-dose preoperative glucocorticoids reduce levels of postoperative inflammatory markers and specific biomarkers of liver damage compared with placebo, and suggested a reduced complication rate and shorter hospital stay after liver surgery. However, there are no studies with a clinical primary outcome or of early recovery outcomes. The aim of this study was to investigate whether a single high dose of preoperative glucocorticoid reduces complications in the immediate postoperative phase after liver surgery. METHODS: This was a single-centre, double-blinded, parallel-group RCT investigating preoperative methylprednisolone 10 mg/kg (high dose) versus dexamethasone 8 mg (standard-dose postoperative nausea prophylaxis) in patients scheduled for open liver resection. The primary outcome was number of patients with a complication in the postanaesthesia care unit; secondary outcomes included duration of hospital stay, pain and nausea during admission, and 30-day morbidity. RESULTS: A total of 174 patients (88 in high-dose group, 86 in standard-dose group) were randomized and analysed (mean(s.d.) age 65(12) years, 67.2 per cent men); 31.6 per cent had no serious co-morbidities and 25.3 per cent underwent major liver resection. Complications occurred in the postanaesthesia care unit in 51 patients (58 per cent) in the high-dose group and 58 (67 per cent) in the standard-dose group (risk ratio 0.86, 95 per cent c.i. 0.68 to 1.08; P = 0.213). Median duration of hospital stay was 4 days in both groups (P = 0.160). Thirty-day morbidity and mortality rates were similar in the two groups. CONCLUSION: A high dose of preoperative glucocorticoids did not reduce acute postoperative complications after open liver resection compared with a standard dose. Registration number: NCT03403517 (http://www.clinicaltrials.gov); EudraCT 2017-002652-81 (https://eudract.ema.europa.eu/).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Steinthorsdottir, Kristin Julia","Awada, H. N.","Schultz, N. A.","Larsen, P. N.","Hillingsø, Jens","Jans, no-firstname","Kehlet, Henrik","Aasvang, Eske K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434708"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preoperative high dose glucocorticoids for early recovery after liver resection randomized double blinded trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bjsopen/zrab063","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434708","identifier":[{"id":"85115906521","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34480563","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8418207","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-451c3bf9-f2d8-4573-ae25-279183395820"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E61CEF7EAC6867B0B2D7CC9468D48F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bjsopen/zrab063","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/303580929/zrab063.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"K. J.","key":"steinthorsdottirpau","last":"Steinthorsdottir","locid":"d26915dc-4247-4e32-8ed0-cde5e0471fdb","name":"Steinthorsdottir, Kristin Julia","name_org":"Steinthorsdottir, K. J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"H. N.","key":"awadapau","last":"Awada","name":"Awada, H. N.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"N. A.","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","name":"Schultz, N. A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"P. N.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, P. N.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. G.","key":"hillingsøpau","last":"Hillingsø","locid":"6e3f56a3-3e04-4728-872b-b833e9b702df","name":"Hillingsø, Jens","name_org":"Hillingsø, J. G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"no-firstname","key":"janspau","last":"Jans","name":"Jans, no-firstname","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H.","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","name_org":"Kehlet, H.","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"E. K.","key":"aasvangpau","last":"Aasvang","locid":"0efc20dd-d2e0-46b8-ae8b-9c67d62079dd","name":"Aasvang, Eske K.","name_org":"Aasvang, E. K.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34480563"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/bjsopen/zrab063","issn":["24749842"],"issue":"5","journal":"BJS open","paperid":"zrab063","status":"p","title":"BJS open","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115906521"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-451c3bf9-f2d8-4573-ae25-279183395820"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preoperative high-dose glucocorticoids for early recovery after liver resection : randomized double-blinded trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-434708","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Major abdominal surgery in older and frail patients is associated with considerable morbidity and mortality. Plasma albumin is routinely measured in the clinic and has been proposed as an indicator of frailty. This study aimed to investigate if plasma albumin is a predictor of mortality in older patients undergoing open abdominal surgery. Materials and methods: We conducted a single-center, register-based retrospective study of patients, aged ⩾60 years who underwent one of 81 open abdominal surgical procedures. Patients operated on during the period from January 1st, 2000 to May 31st, 2013 were consecutively identified in the Danish National Patient Registry. Plasma albumin was measured within 30 days prior to surgery and the primary endpoint was 30-day postoperative mortality. Results: 3,639 patients were included of whom 68.2% underwent emergency surgery. The rate of severe hypoalbuminemia (plasma albumin < 28 g/L) was 43.4%. Preoperative plasma albumin was lower in patients with a fatal 30-day outcome (mean 20.6 g/L vs 30.1 g/L in survivors, p < 0.0001). Other independent predictive parameters of 30-day mortality were age, male sex, and emergency surgery. We present an algorithm including these four variables for the prediction of 30-day mortality for patients aged ⩾60 years undergoing open abdominal surgery. Conclusion: Preoperative plasma albumin is a predictor of 30-day mortality in patients above 60 years of age following open abdominal surgery. Assessment of plasma albumin in conjunction with other risk factors such as age, sex, and surgical priority may improve preoperative decision-making.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, P. B.","Liest, S.","Hannani, D.","Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl","Sørensen, Lars Tue","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443788"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Abdominal surgery","Albumin","Algorithm","Frailty","Gastrointestinal surgery","Hypoalbuminemia","Mortality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preoperative hypoalbuminemia predicts early mortality following open abdominal surgery in patients above 000000000060 years of age","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/333474600/1457496919888598.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-443788","identifier":[{"id":"31769347","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075648561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5453833d-4c78-490e-99d1-6fa0845be40f"],"keyword":["Albumin","abdominal surgery","algorithm","frailty","gastrointestinal surgery","hypoalbuminemia","mortality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ED91B9BD28452285718C1D189C6C7ABA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/333474600/1457496919888598.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"P. B.","key":"larsenpbpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, P. B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"S.","key":"liestspau","last":"Liest","name":"Liest, S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"D.","key":"hannanidpau","last":"Hannani","name":"Hannani, D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H. L.","key":"jørgensenhenrikløvendahlpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cf84c34a-16a5-4a24-9667-bc1c2481e1a5","name":"Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl","name_org":"Jørgensen, H. L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L. T.","key":"sørensenlarstuepau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0a5b4403-2e6f-437b-a477-98d38aecaae0","name":"Sørensen, Lars Tue","name_org":"Sørensen, L. T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L. N.","key":"jørgensenlarsnannestadpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","name_org":"Jørgensen, L. N.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31769347"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1457496919888598","issn":["14574969","17997267"],"issn_org":["14574969"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Surgery","pages":"29-36","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Surgery","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075648561"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5453833d-4c78-490e-99d1-6fa0845be40f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preoperative Hypoalbuminemia Predicts Early Mortality Following Open Abdominal Surgery in Patients Above 60 Years of Age","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443788","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In situ forming implants are exposed to an extracellular matrix resembling a gel rather than aqueous solution upon subcutaneous administration. The aim of study was to develop a gel-based release testing system for characterizing the long-term in vitro behavior of in situ forming implants. The gel-based system consisted of an agarose gel mimicking the subcutaneous injection site and a receiver layer comprising phosphate buffer. Poly(D,L-lactide-co-glycolide) in situ forming implants containing leuprolide acetate as the model peptide and N-methyl-2-pyrrolidone (NMP), dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO) or triacetin as co-solvent were investigated. The gel-based release testing system discriminated between the formulations. Accelerated release data obtained at elevated temperatures were able to predict real-time release applying the Arrhenius equation. Monitoring of the microenvironmental pH of the implants was performed by UV–Vis imaging in the gel-based system at 50 °C. A pH drop (from pH 7.4 to 6.7 for the NMP and DMSO implants, to pH 5.5 for the triacetin implants) within the first day was observed, followed by an increase to pH ∼7.4. The gel-based system coupled with UV imaging offered opportunity for detailed evaluation and prediction of the in vitro performance of long-acting injectables, facilitating future development of in situ depot forming delivery systems.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Li, Zhuoxuan","Mu, Huiling","Larsen, Susan Weng","Jensen, Henrik","Østergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-466950"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Microenvironmental pH","UV Vis imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an i in vitro i gel based system for characterizing and predicting the long term performance of plga i in situ i forming implants","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpharm.2021.121183","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-466950","identifier":[{"id":"85117611761","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34653562","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7ac748db-2520-4556-9c53-58ad41ebcc11"],"keyword":["Accelerated release","In situ forming implants","In vitro release testing model","Solvent induced phase inversion","UV–Vis imaging","microenvironmental pH"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6DD3F1238F238F6547B29C55294183A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/283011709/1_s2.0_S0378517321009893_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpharm.2021.121183","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Physical and Analytical Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zhuoxuan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"1b9299d7-bca7-499b-8e06-734921531509","name":"Li, Zhuoxuan","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-888X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Huiling","key":"mupau","last":"Mu","locid":"f112da1b-f1ab-4891-bf6a-3c799d71d4cc","name":"Mu, Huiling","orcid":"0000-0001-9246-3931","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susan","key":"wenglarsenpau","last":"Weng Larsen","locid":"f6980004-978f-4940-b71f-de426f2a084a","name":"Larsen, Susan Weng","name_org":"Weng Larsen, Susan","orcid":"0000-0002-3818-7275","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"88cd8faf-69c6-46de-a355-03f93d52eeb1","name":"Jensen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34653562"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijpharm.2021.121183","issn":["03785173","18733476"],"issn_org":["03785173"],"journal":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","paperid":"121183","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","volume":"609"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117611761"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7ac748db-2520-4556-9c53-58ad41ebcc11"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An <i>in vitro</i> gel-based system for characterizing and predicting the long-term performance of PLGA<i> in situ</i> forming implants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466950","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Angioedema is a rare but potentially life-threatening adverse reaction associated with angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors. Identification of potential genetic factors related to this adverse event may help identify at-risk patients. Objectives: The aim of this study was to identify genetic factors associated with ACE inhibitor–associated angioedema. Methods: A genomewide association study involving patients of European descent, all taking ACE inhibitors, was conducted in a discovery cohort (Copenhagen Hospital Biobank), and associations were confirmed in a replication cohort (Swedegene). Cases were defined as subjects with angioedema events and filled prescriptions for ACE inhibitors ≤180 days before the events. Control subjects were defined as those with continuous treatment with ACE inhibitors without any history of angioedema. Odds ratios (ORs) and 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were computed for angioedema risk using logistic mixed model regression analysis. Summary statistics from the discovery and replication cohorts were analyzed using a fixed-effects meta-analysis model. Results: The discovery cohort consisted of 462 cases and 53,391 ACE inhibitor–treated control subjects. The replication cohort consisted of 142 cases and 1,345 ACE inhibitor–treated control subjects. In the discovery cohort, 1 locus, residing at chromosome 14q32.2, was identified that associated with angioedema at the genomewide significance level of P <5 × 10–8. The lead variant at this locus, rs34485356, is an intergenic variant located 60 kb upstream of BDKRB2 (OR: 1.62; 95% CI: 1.38 to 1.90; P = 4.3 × 10−9). This variant was validated in our replication cohort with a similar direction and effect size (OR: 1.60; 95% CI: 1.13 to 2.25; P = 7.2 × 10−3). We found that carriers of the risk allele had significantly lower systolic (−0.46 mm Hg per T allele; 95% CI: −0.83 to −0.10; P = 0.013) and diastolic (−0.26 mm Hg per T allele; 95% CI: −0.46 to −0.05; P = 0.013) blood pressure. Conclusions: In this genomewide association study involving individuals treated with ACE inhibitors, we found that common variants located in close proximity to the bradykinin receptor B2 gene were associated with increased risk for ACE inhibitor–related angioedema.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Ghouse, Jonas","Ahlberg, Gustav","Andreasen, Laura","Banasik, Karina","Brunak, Søren","Schwinn, Michael","Larsen, Ina Holst","Petersen, Oscar","Sørensen, Erik","Ullum, Henrik","Rasmussen, Eva Rye","Eriksson, Niclas","Hallberg, Pär","Wadelius, Mia","Bundgaard, Henning","Olesen, Morten S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-497081"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["ACE inhibitors","ADR","Adverse drug reaction","Angioedema","Bradykinin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of variants near the bradykinin receptor b sub 000000000002 sub gene with angioedema in patients taking ace inhibitors","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-497081","identifier":[{"id":"34384552","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111331289","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000684836000008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-ad7b193e-3ba2-47bc-948c-0c412f8b66ac"],"keyword":["ACE inhibitors","ADR","adverse drug reaction","angioedema","bradykinin","bradykinin receptor B"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-437D26E6A7EF7BB3BF572ECDD93BD522"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"o