{"abstract":"Among markers for oxidative stress urinary excretion 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2′-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodGuo) and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-guanosine (8-oxoGuo) have been widely used in controlled and epidemiological studies, and are considered to represent intracellular markers of oxidation of DNA and RNA in the entire organism, respectively. Although being non-invasive, urinary methods have shortcomings. There is no established method for analysis of 8-oxodGuo and 8-oxoGuo in plasma and the few plasma values presented in the literature vary greatly. We here present a liquid chromatography mass spectrometry method with full validation for analysis of 8-oxodGuo and 8-oxoGuo in plasma. Further, we investigated the basis for our previously physiological model and show that a single plasma sample can be used to estimate the 24-h production of 8-oxoGuo, whereas we challenge the use of urinary 8-oxodGuo/creatinine ratio or plasma 8-oxodGuo as measures of oxidative stress.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Henriksen, Trine","Weimann, Allan","Larsen, Emil List","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-523019"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DNA oxidation","Mass spectroscopy","Oxidative stress","Plasma","RNA oxidation","Urine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantification of 000000000008 oxo 000000000007 000000000008 dihydro 000000000002 deoxyguanosine and 000000000008 oxo 000000000007 000000000008 dihydro guanosine concentrations in urine and plasma for estimating 000000000024 h urinary output","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-523019","identifier":[{"id":"85108819798","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34166769","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d8ef71b4-c3d0-48d7-8d55-ab9e0c8513d9"],"keyword":["DNA oxidation","Mass spectroscopy","Oxidative stress","Plasma","RNA oxidation","Urine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE994E5B48E62013349CCBED865A7BC0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Trine","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Trine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"weimannpau","last":"Weimann","name":"Weimann, Allan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Enghusen","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34166769"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2021.06.014","issn":["08915849","18734596"],"issn_org":["08915849"],"journal":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","pages":"350-357","status":"p","title":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","volume":"172"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108819798"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d8ef71b4-c3d0-48d7-8d55-ab9e0c8513d9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quantification of 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2′-deoxyguanosine and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-guanosine concentrations in urine and plasma for estimating 24-h urinary output","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523019","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Pietras, Jens Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-555888"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Læring pædagogik og undervisning"],"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"åben skole","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-555888","ids":["pha-f6785721-8ff1-438f-8674-ca047c054a74"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-53AC4F92BD42C5F7AF9AA7F702542BE0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Læreruddannelsen - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Flemming","key":"pietraspau","last":"Pietras","locid":"3e6b6e55-6609-4812-8425-765ee702094d","name":"Pietras, Jens Flemming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Aage","key":"poulsenpedh","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Jens Aage","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sten","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Sten","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"juulpedh","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788741279367"],"pages":"155-167","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"en fagmetodik","title":"Historieundervisning"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-f6785721-8ff1-438f-8674-ca047c054a74"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Åben skole","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-555888","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Esophageal atresia (EA) is a congenital malformation affecting 1:3000-4500 newborns. Approximately 15% have a long-gap EA (LGEA), in which case a primary anastomosis is often impossible to achieve. To create continuity of the esophagus patients instead have to undergo lengthening procedures or organ interpositions; methods associated with high morbidity and poor functional outcomes. Esophageal injections of Botulinum Toxin Type A (BTX-A) could enable primary anastomosis and mitigate stricture formation through decreased tissue tension. Methods and Analysis: In this randomized controlled blinded animal trial, 24 pigs are divided into a long- or short-gap EA group (LGEA and SGEA, respectively) and randomized to receive BTX-A or isotonic saline injections. In the LGEA group, injections are given endoscopically in the esophageal musculature. After seven days, a 3 cm esophageal resection and primary anastomosis is performed. In the SGEA group, a 1 cm esophageal resection and primary anastomosis is performed, followed by intraoperative injections of BTX-A or isotonic saline. After 14 days, stricture formation, presence of leakage, and esophageal compliance is assessed using endoscopic and manometric techniques, and in vivo and ex vivo contrast radiography. Tissue elongation is evaluated in a stretch-tension test, and the esophagus is assessed histologically to evaluate anastomotic healing. Ethics and Dissemination: The study complies with the ARRIVE guidelines for animal studies and has been approved by the Danish Animal Experimentation Council. Results will be published in peer-reviewed journals and presented at national and international conferences. Highlights: The optimal management of long-gap esophageal atresia remains controversial Primary anastomosis could improve functional outcomes and reduce complications Botulinum Toxin Type A decreases tissue tension and could facilitate anastomosis Reduced tension could further abate the risk for anastomotic stricture and leakage We present a model to evaluate the method in long- and short-gap esophageal atresia","author_count":14,"contributors":["Svensson, Emma","Zvara, Peter","Qvist, Niels","Hagander, Lars","Möller, Sören","Rasmussen, Lars","Schrøder, Henrik Daa","Hejbøl, Eva Kildall","Jørgen, Niels Bjørn","Petersen, Súsanna","Larsen, Kristine Cederstrøm","Krhut, Jan","Muensterer, Oliver J.","Ellebæk, Mark Bremholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-576979"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Svensson, Emma"],"country":["Czechia","Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig-Maximilian University of Munich","Lund University","University Hospital Ostrava","University of Ostrava"],"keyword":["Botulinum toxin","oesophageal atresia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of botulinum toxin type a injections on stricture formation leakage rates esophageal elongation and anastomotic healing following primary anastomosis in a longand short gap esophageal atresia model a protocol for a randomized controlled blinded trial in pigs","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.29337/ijsp.156","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-576979","identifier":[{"id":"34435166","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8362621","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139146905","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-0d40f2b9-4607-4635-a88e-af0022f4405e"],"keyword":["anastomotic stricture","botulinum toxin","oesophageal atresia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-841C106B