Epidemiology","pages":"1847-1855","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100358342"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a6047389-c115-4da5-8423-c971128c658b","ku-e23d111f-ea67-4ddc-a846-724650f6825b","nfa-c243d64c-f835-4477-b651-0a0ca09ce702"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Maternal life and work stressors during pregnancy and asthma in offspring","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.69-767737","year":"2021","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The glucose-lowering drug metformin has recently been shown to reduce myocardial oxygen consumption and increase myocardial efficiency in chronic heart failure (HF) patients without diabetes. However, it remains to be established whether these beneficial myocardial effects are associated with metformin-induced alterations in whole-body insulin sensitivity and substrate metabolism. METHODS: Eighteen HF patients with reduced ejection fraction and without diabetes (median age, 65 (interquartile range 55-68); ejection fraction 39 ± 6%; HbA1c 5.5 to 6.4%) were randomized to receive metformin (n = 10) or placebo (n = 8) for 3 months. We studied the effects of metformin on whole-body insulin sensitivity using a two-step hyperinsulinemic euglycemic clamp incorporating isotope-labeled tracers of glucose, palmitate, and urea. Substrate metabolism and skeletal muscle mitochondrial respiratory capacity were determined by indirect calorimetry and high-resolution respirometry, and body composition was assessed by bioelectrical impedance analysis. The primary outcome measure was change in insulin sensitivity. RESULTS: Compared with placebo, metformin treatment lowered mean glycated hemoglobin levels (absolute mean difference, - 0.2%; 95% CI - 0.3 to 0.0; p = 0.03), reduced body weight (- 2.8 kg; 95% CI - 5.0 to - 0.6; p = 0.02), and increased fasting glucagon levels (3.2 pmol L-1; 95% CI 0.4 to 6.0; p = 0.03). No changes were observed in whole-body insulin sensitivity, endogenous glucose production, and peripheral glucose disposal or oxidation with metformin. Equally, resting energy expenditure, lipid and urea turnover, and skeletal muscle mitochondrial respiratory capacity remained unaltered. CONCLUSION: Increased myocardial efficiency during metformin treatment is not mediated through improvements in insulin action in HF patients without diabetes. CLINICAL TRIAL REGISTRATION: URL: https://clinicaltrials.gov . Unique identifier: NCT02810132. Date of registration: June 22, 2016.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Larsen, Anders Hostrup","Wiggers, Henrik","Dollerup, Ole L","Jespersen, Nichlas Riise","Hansson, Nils Henrik","Frøkiær, Jørgen","Brøsen, Kim","Nørrelund, Helene","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Møller, Niels","Jessen, Niels"],"cuid":["S03-097.17-030171"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Jessen, Niels"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Hepatic glucose production","Homeostasis","Hyperinsulinemic euglycemic clamp","Inhibition","Insulin sensitivity","Mechanism","Metformin","Obese","Resistance","Rosiglitazone","Skeletal muscle","Substrate metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metformin lowers body weight but fails to increase insulin sensitivity in chronic heart failure patients without diabetes a randomized double blind placebo controlled study","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175382924/Larsen_et_al_CVDT_2020_accepted_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-097.17-030171","identifier":[{"id":"000557339100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85089256114","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32770520","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f1f17d60-8ceb-40df-81a8-7ca365547093","ku-ad5aa7d8-47e6-4661-b441-683a9867c615","sdu-ce578c1a-d450-412b-a8e1-209fdfce2f6f"],"keyword":["HEPATIC GLUCOSE-PRODUCTION","HOMEOSTASIS","Heart failure","Hyperinsulinemic euglycemic clamp","INHIBITION","Insulin sensitivity","MECHANISM","Metformin","OBESE","RESISTANCE","ROSIGLITAZONE","SKELETAL-MUSCLE","SUBSTRATE METABOLISM","TROGLITAZONE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-0C980E444FD00CCE6E932330A30F5669"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175382924/Larsen_et_al_CVDT_2020_accepted_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/317200347/Metformin_Lowers_Body_Weight_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Hostrup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f340dab7-a57a-4893-aa30-fca3f929a280","name":"Larsen, Anders Hostrup","orcid":"0000-0003-1127-6910","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"wiggerspau","last":"Wiggers","locid":"aef6a13e-8c07-474c-a4f6-bc35236a6eda","name":"Wiggers, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Lindgård","key":"dolleruppau","last":"Dollerup","locid":"571b3fca-42a9-44aa-853b-054665af5b80","name":"Dollerup, Ole L","name_org":"Dollerup, Ole Lindgård","orcid":"0000-0001-6924-7114","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nichlas Riise","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"dc7856f9-39e7-497a-a291-eab166abe2ef","name":"Jespersen, Nichlas Riise","orcid":"0000-0003-2502-2102","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils Henrik","key":"hanssonpau","last":"Hansson","locid":"660859d2-6c38-4b6e-bab8-507d364ecce1","name":"Hansson, Nils Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"frøkiærpau","last":"Frøkiær","locid":"49d24192-9cad-4d32-88ee-cf46bb315b72","name":"Frøkiær, Jørgen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jorgen","key":"frokiaerpau","last":"Frokiaer","name":"Frokiaer, Jorgen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"brøsenpau","last":"Brøsen","locid":"8c6b2aeb-e594-4852-89a1-285b9a944557","name":"Brøsen, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-8444-7835","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helene","key":"nørrelundpau","last":"Nørrelund","locid":"678afca5-0464-4e97-9b74-8ad8138ae73c","name":"Nørrelund, Helene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helene","key":"norrelundpau","last":"Norrelund","name":"Norrelund, Helene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"2e0d8e2a-2da1-4d55-b2da-0a25c0375b1e","name":"Møller, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5627-7322","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"f0d20e5e-d5b5-44da-980e-3e052af18b46","name":"Jessen, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5613-7274","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32770520"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10557-020-07050-5","issn":["09203206","15737241"],"issn_org":["09203206"],"issue":"3","journal":"Cardiovascular Drugs and Therapy","pages":"491-503","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Drugs and Therapy","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089256114"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f1f17d60-8ceb-40df-81a8-7ca365547093","ku-ad5aa7d8-47e6-4661-b441-683a9867c615","sdu-ce578c1a-d450-412b-a8e1-209fdfce2f6f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Metformin Lowers Body Weight But Fails to Increase Insulin Sensitivity in Chronic Heart Failure Patients without Diabetes: a Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.17-030171","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Patient-reported outcome measures (PROMs) may predict poor clinical outcome in patients with heart failure (HF). It remains unclear whether PROMs are associated with subsequent adherence to HF medication. We aimed to determine whether health-related quality of life, anxiety and depression were associated with long-term medication adherence in these patients. METHODS AND RESULTS: A national cohort study of Danish patients with HF with three-year follow-up (n = 1,464). PROMs included the EuroQol five-dimensional, five-level questionnaire (EQ-5D-5L), the HeartQoL and the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS). Patient-reported outcomes (PRO) data were linked to demographic and clinical data at baseline, and data on all redeemed prescriptions for angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors/angiotensin II receptor blockers/angiotensin receptor neprilysin inhibitors (ACEI/ARB/ARNI), β-blockers and mineralocorticoid receptor antagonists (MRAs) during follow-up. Medication non-adherence was defined as < 80% of proportion of days covered (PDC). In adjusted regression analyses, lower health-related quality of life (EQ-5D and HeartQoL) and symptoms of depression (HADS-D) at discharge were associated with non-adherence. After three years of follow-up, lower health-related quality of life (EQ-5D) was associated with non-adherence for ACEI/ARB/ARNI (adjusted OR 2.78, 95% CI:1.19-6.49), β-blockers (adjusted OR 2.35, 95% CI:1.04-5.29), whereas HADS-D was associated with non-adherence for ACEI/ARB/ARNI (adjusted OR 1.07, 95% CI:1.03-1.11) and β-blockers (adjusted OR 1.06, 95% CI:1.02-1.10). CONCLUSION: Lower health-related quality of life and symptoms of depression were associated with non-adherence across HF medications at one- and three years of follow-up. Person-centred care using PROMs may carry a potential for identifying patients at increased risk of future medication non-adherence.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anne Ankerstjerne","Wiggers, Henrik","Jensen, Martin","Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","Rasmussen, Trine Bernholdt","Borregaard, Britt","Thrysoee, Lars","Thorup, Charlotte Brun","Mols, Rikke Elmose","Larsen, Signe Holm","Johnsen, Søren Paaske"],"cuid":["S04-090.72-011051"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Anne Ankerstjerne"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Medication Adherence","Patient reported outcomes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcomes and medication adherence in patients with heart failure","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85100779832","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-090.72-011051","identifier":[{"id":"85100779832","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32761093","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e7485fb4-5297-41e7-b111-5aff46866c53","au-c6773a07-d930-4030-a014-32f1405042a4","ku-6257bc1e-4491-437c-9602-c9771c4c7e1e","sdu-dcc3031d-6c18-4459-bd93-371c7abd9ff7"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Medication adherence","Patient-reported outcomes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-252169A96C0D0B991C364FDBD894A548"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus