Henrik","key":"ullumhenrikpau","last":"Ullum","locid":"ef594d49-5aeb-4d32-80b4-4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32758438"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s1473-3099(20)30589-2","issn":["14733099","14744457"],"issn_org":["14733099"],"issue":"12","journal":"The Lancet Infectious Diseases","pages":"1401-1408","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Infectious Diseases","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089980210"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c234fef5-ea5b-4743-8fcf-bd1715a35d6b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of COVID-19 in health-care workers in Denmark : an observational cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509369","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The long-term consequences of transient neonatal hypoglycemia are sparsely studied. We performed a follow-up of a cohort of neonates with blood glucose recordings < 1.7 mmol/L (< 30 mg/dL), treated with > 2.5 mmol/L (> 45 mg/dL), compared with healthy siblings. Exclusion criteria were gestational age < 35 weeks, severe asphyxia, head injury, and other cerebral diseases. In 71 children with neonatal hypoglycemia and 32 control siblings, Wechsler IV cognitive test, Movement ABC-2 test, and Child Behavior Checklist were performed at mean age 7.75 and 9.17 years, respectively. No significant changes were detected for cognitive function by using Wechsler IV or for behavior by using Child Behavior Checklist. In univariate analysis, the hypoglycemia group had lower age-adjusted fine motor scores by using the Movement ABC-2 test compared with control siblings, 42.6 ± 31.2 vs. 57.2 ± 30.8 percentile (p = 0.03). In the sibling-paired analysis, the decrease in total motor score was highly significant, p = 0.009, driven by a decrease in fine motor score, p = 0.008. In the hypoglycemia group, adjusted analysis showed a lower fine motor function for boys, β = − 16.4, p = 0.048. Conclusion: Neonatal hypoglycemia treated with > 2.5 mmol/L was associated with lower fine motor scores within the normal range, particularly in boys. No associations with cognitive function or behavior were detected.What is Known:• Transient neonatal hypoglycemia is associated with acute neurologic dysfunction and long-term neurodevelopment impairment in 18 months of age.What is New:• Neonatal hypoglycemia treated with > 2.5 mmol/L is associated with lower fine motor function within the normal range, particularly in boys, but not to changes in cognitive function or behavior.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov","Wehberg, Sonja","Portner, Fani Juel","Larsen, Anna Marie","Filipsen, Karen","Christesen, Henrik Thybo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-634599"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov"],"keyword":["Follow up","Neonatal hypoglycemia","Risk groups"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neurodevelopmental outcomes after moderate to severe neonatal hypoglycemia","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00431-020-03729-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-634599","identifier":[{"id":"32666280","type":"pmid"},{"id":"32794121","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7666672","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85087874699","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85089356862","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7852896","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-d64d1e46-db91-447c-b604-8ad902233a1e"],"keyword":["Cerebral impairment","Follow-up","Neonatal hypoglycemia","Risk groups"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E312B21112E375DA2003BC3953D442CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171456270/Helleskov2020_Article_NeurodevelopmentalOutcomesAfte.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00431-020-03729-x","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annett","key":"helleskovrasmussenpau","last":"Helleskov Rasmussen","locid":"5e6d18d0-56bd-4173-808e-7be947059c9f","name":"Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov","name_org":"Helleskov Rasmussen, Annett","orcid":"0000-0001-7122-4114","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sonja","key":"wehbergpau","last":"Wehberg","locid":"2a11b516-c573-4a93-88f1-4a86a858b664","name":"Wehberg, Sonja","orcid":"0000-0003-1503-2649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fani","key":"pørtnerpau","last":"Pørtner","locid":"b7d41fc4-a537-438d-9fde-ca7724e330e4","name":"Portner, Fani Juel","name_org":"Pørtner, Fani","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Marie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"99ee0494-b5ab-4375-85b0-5898a75acadf","name":"Larsen, Anna Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"filipsenpau","last":"Filipsen","locid":"9b300892-e301-4ae3-89b0-b50f137bfed1","name":"Filipsen, Karen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Thybo","key":"christesenpau","last":"Christesen","locid":"c8317e72-7a09-4c80-81e9-b69855b68e8f","name":"Christesen, Henrik Thybo","orcid":"0000-0001-5330-6853","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32666280","32794121"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00431-020-03729-x","issn":["03406199","09439676"],"issn_org":["14321076"],"issue":"12","journal":"European Journal of Pediatrics","pages":"1981-1991","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pediatrics","volume":"179"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087874699"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d64d1e46-db91-447c-b604-8ad902233a1