 University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Colon Capsule Endoscopy vs. CT Colonography Following Incomplete Colonoscopy : A Systematic Review with Meta-Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.83-009605","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To develop an autonomous, in-bore, MR-compatible cryostat cooled with liquid nitrogen that provides full-day operation, and to demonstrate that the theoretical signal-to-noise benefit can be achieved for 13 C imaging at 3 T (32.13 MHz). METHODS: The cryogenic setup uses a vacuum-insulated fiberglass cryostat, which indirectly cools a cold finger where the RF coil is attached. The cryostat was evacuated before use and had a reservoir of liquid nitrogen for full-day operation. A 30 × 40 mm2 copper coil was mounted inside the cryostat with a 3-mm distance to the sample. Two examples of in vivo experiments of rat brain metabolism after a hyperpolarized [1-13 C]pyruvate injection are reported. RESULTS: A coil Q-factor ratio of Q88K /Q290K = 550/280 was obtained, and the theoretical SNR enhancement was verified with MR measurements. We achieved a coil temperature of 88 K and a preamplifier temperature of 77 K. A 2-fold overall SNR enhancement was achieved, compared with the best case at room temperature. The thermal performance of the coil was adequate for in vivo experiments, with an autonomy of 5 hours consuming 6 L of LN2 , extendable to over 12 hours by LN2 refilling. CONCLUSION: Cryogenic surface coils can be highly beneficial for 13 C imaging, provided that the coil-to-sample distance remains short. An autonomous, in-bore cryostat was developed that achieved the theoretical improvement in SNR.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sánchez-Heredia, Juan Diego","Baron, Rafael","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Laustsen, Christoffer","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-096.48-021908"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Sanchez, Juan Diego"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare"],"keyword":["13C MRI","C 13 MRI","C MRI","Copper","Cryogenic","Design","Hyperpolarization","MRI","Mouse","Performance","RF coil","SNR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomous cryogenic rf receive coil for sup 000000000013 sup c imaging of rodents at 000000000003 t","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/200568707/MRM_19_20209.R1_Proof_hi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-096.48-021908","identifier":[{"id":"000499278700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85075713671","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31782552","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7e8281a3-2228-49d3-a4e4-7aed99ccfeb2","dtu-d8f76552-94b4-4f70-ae1b-768e8d884083"],"keyword":["13C MRI","C MRI","C-13 MRI","COPPER","DESIGN","MOUSE","MRI","NMR PROBE","NOISE RATIO","PERFORMANCE","RF coil","SNR","SURFACE COIL","cryogenic","hyperpolarization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-09AE00028984C6D29BC3EB71E3632E59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/200568707/MRM_19_20209.R1_Proof_hi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","ke