7403194"],"issue":"1","journal":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","pages":"497-508","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","volume":"84"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075713671"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7e8281a3-2228-49d3-a4e4-7aed99ccfeb2","dtu-d8f76552-94b4-4f70-ae1b-768e8d884083"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Autonomous cryogenic RF receive coil for <sup>13</sup>C imaging of rodents at 3 T","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.48-021908","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aims To investigate the effect of adding the short-acting glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor agonist (GLP-1RA) exenatide to insulin treatment on markers of cardiovascular risk in type 1 diabetes. Materials and methods In a randomized, double-blind, parallel-group trial, 108 individuals with type 1 diabetes aged >= 18 years on multiple daily injection therapy with a body mass index >22.0 kg/m(2)and glycated haemoglobin concentration of 59 to 88 mmol/mol (7.5%-10.0%) were randomized (1:1) to preprandial subcutaneous injection of 10 mu g exenatide (Byetta (R)) or placebo three times daily over 26 weeks as add-on treatment to existing insulin therapy. Reported markers of cardiovascular risk were secondary endpoints and were analyzed in a baseline-adjusted linear mixed model in the intention-to-treat population. The primary results of this study, the MAG1C (Meal-time Administration of exenatide for Glycaemic control in type 1 diabetes Cases) trial, were previously reported. Results Exenatide changed total fat mass by -2.6 kg (95% confidence interval [CI] -3.6; -1.6;P < 0.0001) and lean body mass by -1.1 kg (95% CI -1.9; -0.4;P= 0.01) compared with placebo, as assessed by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Fat mass reductions were similar for central and peripheral fat mass. Exenatide did not change levels of interleukin-2 or -6; tumour necrosis factor-alpha; C-reactive protein; N-terminal prohormone of brain natriuretic peptide; or 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (RNA oxidation marker) and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2 '-deoxyguanosine (DNA oxidation marker). Conclusions Exenatide added to insulin therapy in type 1 diabetes for 26 weeks resulted in body weight loss primarily from fat mass reduction, but had no effect on biomarkers of cardiovascular disease risk.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Johansen, Nicklas J.","Dejgaard, Thomas F.","Lund, Asger","Schlüntz, Camilla","Larsen, Emil L.","Poulsen, Henrik E.","Goetze, Jens P.","Møller, Holger Jon","Vilsbøll, Tina","Andersen, Henrik U.","Knop, Filip K."],"cuid":["S02-097.71-020457"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Knop, Filip K."],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of short acting exenatide administered three times daily on markers of cardiovascular disease in type 000000000001 diabetes a randomized double blind placebo controlled trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85089238177","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.71-020457","identifier":[{"id":"000540290300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85089238177","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32543021","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6aeab27d-5dc1-44ea-b5dc-a2854d55babf","ku-9c64ea40-f2eb-452e-8fc0-a94fd4f36a81"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-56DD2A8FF3C1349535DF6E701C30722E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of clinical biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Nicklas J.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Nicklas J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas F.","key":"dejgaardpau","last":"Dejgaard","name":"Dejgaard, Thomas F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Asger","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Asger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla","key":"schluentzpau","last":"Schluentz","name":"Schluentz, Camilla","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emil L.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","name_org":"Poulsen, Henrik E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens P.","key":"goetzepau","last":"Goetze","locid":"980bceaf-dbf3-4f7a-a8d7-0a8e81b638b2","name":"Goetze, Jens P.","orcid":"0000-0001-6356-3829","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger J.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"b08dc9ce-d595-49c6-833a-4ec9b4223a05","name":"Møller, Holger Jon","name_org":"Møller, Holger J.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tina","key":"vilsbøllpau","last":"Vilsbøll","locid":"76773372-af8c-45a0-9447-a509cbf6d466","name":"Vilsbøll, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-0456-6787","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Henrik U.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"645c4d33-e15a-4c7e-af45-04f71aa4f63b","name":"Andersen, Henrik Ullits","name_org":"Andersen, Henrik U.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Filip K.","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32543021"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/dom.14078","issn":["14628902","14631326"],"issn_org":["14628902"],"issue":"9","journal":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","pages":"1639-1647","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089238177"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6aeab27d-5dc1-44ea-b5dc-a2854d55babf","ku-9c64ea40-f2eb-452e-8fc0-a94fd4f36a81"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of short-acting exenatide administered three times daily on markers of cardiovascular disease in type 1 diabetes : A randomized double-blind placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.71-020457","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The development of a new tool (IEQCompass) for holistic evaluation of indoor environmental quality (IEQ) is presented. The purpose of the new tool is to facilitate a broader understanding of IEQ, its importance for comfort, health and well-being, and to help and guide the building design process regarding IEQ. The tool evaluates the potential indoor air quality (IAQ), thermal, visual and acoustic IEQ, without considering user influence. The evaluation uses 16 parameters, four for each of the four areas of IEQ (IAQ, thermal, visual and acoustic IEQ). These are evaluated based on relevant criteria assessed from blueprints, existing building information modelling data or observations during building inspection. The criteria and parameters are weighted to obtain an overall IEQ label for the building, as well as partial labels for the four areas. The labelling scheme uses letter ranking and colour code similar to that used in energy performance certification. The results are also communicated through the newly developed “IEQ Design Compass”, which is a detailed graphical visualisation at criteria level and helps identify potential IEQ problems that warrant attention.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Tine Steen","Rohde, Lasse","Jønsson, Kim Trangbæk","Rasmussen, Birgit","Jensen, Rasmus Lund","Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","Witterseh, Thomas","Bekö, Gabriel"],"cuid":["S02-099.75-003610"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Tine Steen"],"keyword":["Acoustic environment","Building certification","Building renovation","Indoor air quality","Residential buildings","Thermal environment","Visual environment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ieq compass a tool for holistic evaluation of potential indoor environmental quality","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.buildenv.2020.106707","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work presented in this paper is part of the REBUS project (Renovating Buildings Sustainably). The authors would like to thank Innovation Fund Denmark [grant number 5151-00002B ], Realdania, Denmark [grant number PRJ-2015-00481 ] and The Landowners' Investment Foundation (Grundejernes Investeringsfond), Denmark [grant number 9025410 ], who funded the project. The authors would also like to thank the individuals who tested the tool during its development and provided valuable feedback, and the 67 Danish professionals and experts who filled in the questionnaire used to determine the weighting of the criteria and parameters in the tool. Finally, the authors would like to thank Martin Vraa Nielsen (Henning Larsen Architechts), Lone Hedegaard Mortensen and Per Haugaard (Niras), Anne Iversen (Realdania), Eva Hellgren and Delphine Bard (Saint Gobain), Anna Heebøll, Birger Bech Jessen and Amanda Bonderup (Danish Technological Institute), Ásta Logadóttir and Jesper Kragh (Aalborg University) for their cooperation and contribution to the development of the tool."],"id":"S02-099.75-003610","identifier":[{"id":"85079341404","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4a20e2fc-a33b-4271-aff3-0196f79d3e50","dtu-ccc6182c-897c-467d-a44a-531b7ab9dfa2"],"keyword":["Acoustic environment","Building certification","Building renovation","Indoor air quality","Residential buildings","Thermal environment","Visual environment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E33C98C1E50A1A91B3901C9BF1CC429D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/329328134/IEQ_Compass_A_tool_for_holistic_evaluation_of_potential_indoor_environmental_quality.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/211179277/S0360132320300652.html","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.buildenv.2020.106707","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Energy in Buildings Research Group (Civil)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Indoor Environment and Sustainable Buildings Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Architectural Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Indoor Environmental Quality and Building Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Indoor Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6f4c1acc-34db-423a-9567-359fc381a0c4","name":"Larsen, Tine Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-4704-6503","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse","key":"rohdepau","last":"Rohde","locid":"13b11fd5-f00b-4ba4-af43-fd85676b67d8","name":"Rohde, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-1075-1874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Trangbæk","key":"jønssonpau","last":"Jønsson","locid":"c97a6ce8-80f2-4c02-a539-70e695fcdd5a","name":"Jønsson, Kim Trangbæk","orcid":"0000-0002-7882-7900","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"b9de7fa2-9ee2-4dc7-9fe6-696d2a6a7e3a","name":"Rasmussen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-9567-2680","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Lund","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"423b54bd-019f-4c14-9dfc-3808e1985566","name":"Jensen, Rasmus Lund","orcid":"0000-0001-7008-2601","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik N.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7f5e707b-235a-4e71-ae71-e9278e7aa2ba","name":"Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","name_org":"Knudsen, Henrik N.","orcid":"0000-0002-3196-7279","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"wittersehpau","last":"Witterseh","name":"Witterseh, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriel","key":"beköpau","last":"Bekö","locid":"c4ad7184-0df3-48b9-8ef0-fc51d4cadfaf","name":"Bekö, Gabriel","orcid":"0000-0001-6107-8336","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.buildenv.2020.106707","issn":["03601323"],"journal":"Building and Environment","paperid":"106707","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Building and Environment","volume":"172"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079341404"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4a20e2fc-a33b-4271-aff3-0196f79d3e50","dtu-ccc6182c-897c-467d-a44a-531b7ab9dfa2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"IEQ-Compass – A tool for holistic evaluation of potential indoor environmental quality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.75-003610","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To evaluate response rates for volunteer first responders (VFRs) activated by use of a smartphone GPS-tracking system and to compare response times of VFRs with those of emergency medical services (EMS). Furthermore, to evaluate 30-day-survival after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) on a rural island. METHODS: Since 2012 a GPS-tracking system has been used on a rural island to activate VFRs during all emergency calls requesting an EMS. When activated, three VFRs were recruited and given distinct roles, including collection of the nearest automatic external defibrillator (AED). We retrospectively investigated EMS response data from April 2012 to December 2017. These were matched with VFR response times from the GPS-tracking system. The 30-day survival in OHCA patients was also assessed. RESULTS: In 2266 of 2662 emergency calls (85%) at least one VFR arrived to the site before EMS. Median response times for VFRs (n = 2662) was 4:46 min:sec (IQR 3:16-6:52) compared with 10:13 min:sec (6:14-13:41) for EMS (p < 0.0001). A total of 17 OHCAs took place in public locations and 65 in residential areas. Thirty-day survival in these were 24% and 15%, respectively. CONCLUSION: Use of a smartphone GPS-tracking system to dispatch VFRs ensures that in more than four of five cases, a VFR arrives to the site before EMS. Response times for VFRs were also found to be lower than EMS response times. Finally, the 30-day survival of OHCA patients in a rural area, based on these results, surpass our expectations.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sarkisian, Laura","Mickley, Hans","Schakow, Henrik","Gerke, Oke","Jørgensen, Gitte","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Henriksen, Finn Lund"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-006742"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["AED","App","Application","Automated external defibrillator","Bystander","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","First responder","GPS","OHCA","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Smartphone","Survival","Volunteer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"global positioning system alerted volunteer first responders arrive before emergency medical services in more than four out of five emergency calls","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180053618/Original_article_to_Resuscitation_revised_without_changes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-006742","identifier":[{"id":"85077757974","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31923531","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8b1050b5-4d40-4180-9321-bb02bc52454c","sdu-9fb01f71-1092-425c-bd4d-5b61d19d807b"],"keyword":["AED","App","Application","Automated external defibrillator","Bystander","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","First responder","GPS","OHCA","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Smartphone","Survival","Volunteer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B50814904C957CC6DD10F77F265C4107"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/431644704/Original_article_to_Resuscitation_revised_without_changes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180053618/Original_article_to_Resuscitation_revised_without_changes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Univ