{"abstract":"Circular DNA can arise from all parts of eukaryotic chromosomes. In yeast, circular ribosomal DNA (rDNA) accumulates dramatically as cells age, however little is known about the accumulation of other chromosome-derived circles or the contribution of such circles to genetic variation in aged cells. We profiled circular DNA in Saccharomyces cerevisiae populations sampled when young and after extensive aging. Young cells possessed highly diverse circular DNA populations but 94% of the circular DNA were lost after ∼15 divisions, whereas rDNA circles underwent massive accumulation to >95% of circular DNA. Circles present in both young and old cells were characterized by replication origins including circles from unique regions of the genome and repetitive regions: rDNA and telomeric Y' regions. We further observed that circles can have flexible inheritance patterns: [HXT6/7circle] normally segregates to mother cells but in low glucose is present in up to 50% of cells, the majority of which must have inherited this circle from their mother. Interestingly, [HXT6/7circle] cells are eventually replaced by cells carrying stable chromosomal HXT6 HXT6/7 HXT7 amplifications, suggesting circular DNAs are intermediates in chromosomal amplifications. In conclusion, the heterogeneity of circular DNA offers flexibility in adaptation, but this heterogeneity is remarkably diminished with age.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Prada-Luengo, Iñigo","Møller, Henrik D.","Henriksen, Rasmus A.","Gao, Qian","Larsen, Camilla Eggert","Alizadeh, Sefa","Maretty, Lasse","Houseley, Jonathan","Regenberg, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-015635"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Regenberg, Birgitte"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Babraham Institute","ETH Zürich"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"replicative aging is associated with loss of genetic heterogeneity from extrachromosomal circular dna in i saccharomyces cerevisiae i","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkaa545","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-015635","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7430651","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85089709269","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32609810","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-29c537be-23b2-4f19-a8c6-a5e9c8c038e9","ku-1a402ef5-97a1-4b9f-8ab0-d69b12adf73c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4D3370FFBD604F82DA0EEA0799A5ED93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkaa545","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248190047/Replicative_aging_is_associated_with_loss_of_genetic_heterogeneity_from_extrachromosomal_circular_DNA_in_Saccharomyces_cerevisiae.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"babraham institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Babraham Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Iñigo","key":"pradaluengopau","last":"Prada-Luengo","locid":"c34d1714-3cf4-4a0f-9452-234271a00e9b","name":"Prada-Luengo, Iñigo","orcid":"0000-0002-4392-0726","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik D.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"da78c156-98ea-4521-ba25-1f80f9845b1e","name":"Møller, Henrik D.","orcid":"0000-0002-1886-3053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus A.","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"1d8a08e9-d213-4af9-88dc-cbfe87e9f27b","name":"Henriksen, Rasmus Amund","name_org":"Henriksen, Rasmus A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Qian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Eggert","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3084a3e3-0e04-4d37-9a4b-544294d733d9","name":"Larsen, Camilla Eggert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Sefa","key":"alizadehpau","last":"Alizadeh","locid":"39137b64-1c63-4ff0-8d8e-e7f276c86787","name":"Alizadeh, Sefa","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse","key":"marettypau","last":"Maretty","locid":"52f9d323-920a-409b-8f2d-20edf9ee7465","name":"Maretty, Lasse","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan","key":"houseleypau","last":"Houseley","name":"Houseley, Jonathan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"regenbergpau","last":"Regenberg","locid":"75f0527b-218d-48ef-96f9-6b790772e2a8","name":"Regenberg, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0003-4996-7012","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32609810"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkaa545","issn":["03051048","13624962"],"issn_org":["03051048"],"issue":"14","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","pages":"7883-7898","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nucleic Acids Research","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089709269"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-29c537be-23b2-4f19-a8c6-a5e9c8c038e9","ku-1a402ef5-97a1-4b9f-8ab0-d69b12adf73c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Replicative aging is associated with loss of genetic heterogeneity from extrachromosomal circular DNA in <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-015635","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Ischemia reperfusion (IR) injury may be attenuated through succinate dehydrogenase (SDH) inhibition by dimethyl malonate (DiMAL). Whether SDH inhibition yields protection in diabetic individuals and translates into human cardiac tissue remain unknown. In isolated perfused hearts from 24 weeks old male Zucker diabetic fatty (ZDF) and age matched non-diabetic control rats and atrial trabeculae from patients with and without diabetes, we compared infarct size, contractile force recovery and mitochondrial function. The cardioprotective effect of a 10 minutes DiMAL administration prior to global ischemia and ischemic preconditioning (IPC) was evaluated. In non-diabetic hearts exposed to IR, DiMAL 0.1 mM reduced infarct size compared to IR (55 ± 7% vs. 69 ± 6%, p < 0.05). Mitochondrial respiration was reduced by DiMAL 0.6 mM compared to sham and DiMAL 0.1 mM (p < 0.05). In diabetic hearts an increased concentration of DiMAL (0.6 mM) was required for protection compared to IR (64 ± 13% vs. 79 ± 8%, p < 0.05). Mitochondrial function remained unchanged. In trabeculae from humans without diabetes, IPC and DiMAL improved contractile force recovery compared to IR (43 ± 12% and 43 ± 13% vs. 23 ± 13%, p < 0.05) but in patients with diabetes only IPC provided protection compared to IR (51 ± 15% vs. 21 ± 8%, p < 0.05). Neither IPC nor DiMAL modulated mitochondrial respiration in patients. Cardioprotection by SDH inhibition is possible in human tissue, but depends on diabetes status. The narrow therapeutic range and discrepancy in respiration between experimental and human studies may limit clinical translation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jespersen, Nichlas Riise","Hjortbak, Marie Vognstoft","Lassen, Thomas Ravn","Støttrup, Nicolaj Brejnholt","Johnsen, Jacob","Tonnesen, Pernille Tilma","Larsen, Steen","Kimose, Hans-Henrik","Bøtker, Hans Erik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-021227"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Medical University of Bialystok"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardioprotective effect of succinate dehydrogenase inhibition in rat hearts and human myocardium with and without diabetes mellitus","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-67247-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-021227","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7316713","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85086858839","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32587298","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-74f6750b-cbe7-4026-957a-1b4ae067ee40","ku-17104ae9-e4af-4883-abdb-7cfbf06a06a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0D0010328FBAFA584074002E8E705315"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-67247-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/246866516/OA_Cardioprotective_efect_of_succinate.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing, Web Track 3: Individualized health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing, Web: Center for Healthy Aging","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nichlas Riise","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"dc7856f9-39e7-497a-a291-eab166abe2ef","name":"Jespersen, Nichlas Riise","orcid":"0000-0003-2502-2102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Vognstoft","key":"hjortbakpau","last":"Hjortbak","locid":"5a6d757d-6979-4b18-9019-a415ff01a423","name":"Hjortbak, Marie Vognstoft","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Ravn","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"7627977a-3461-4cd1-b356-d2aa4161a9e8","name":"Lassen, Thomas Ravn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicolaj Brejnholt","key":"støttruppau","last":"Støttrup","locid":"73ad5a61-0765-4d5c-8cbb-41362eeb666c","name":"Støttrup, Nicolaj Brejnholt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"9d617d37-f691-4de9-947d-932d42fa5db0","name":"Johnsen, Jacob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Tilma","key":"tonnesenpau","last":"Tonnesen","locid":"45e24a32-6d83-4150-86b3-a4e2b9e7ce61","name":"Tonnesen, Pernille Tilma","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d4c64c4e-1edf-41cf-890e-aba81d9e35f7","name":"Larsen, Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-5170-4337","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans-Henrik","key":"kimosepau","last":"Kimose","locid":"b56d5fdf-32d4-4e67-abb1-41d820ba642f","name":"Kimose, Hans-Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32587298"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-67247-4","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"10344","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086858839"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-74f6750b-cbe7-4026-957a-1b4ae067ee40","ku-17104ae9-e4af-4883-abdb-7cfbf06a06a1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cardioprotective effect of succinate dehydrogenase inhibition in rat hearts and human myocardium with and without diabetes mellitus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-021227","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) has recently been implicated in the pathogenesis of post-traumatic headache (PTH), which raises the prospect for therapeutic use of monoclonal antibodies targeting CGRP or its receptor. Therefore, we decided to assess the efficacy, tolerability, and safety of erenumab for prevention of persistent PTH attributed to mild traumatic brain injury. Methods: A single-center, non-randomized, single-arm, open-label study of erenumab for adults aged 18-65 years with persistent PTH. Patients were assigned to receive 140-mg erenumab monthly by two subcutaneous 1-mL injections, given every 4 weeks for 12 weeks. The primary outcome measure was the mean change in number of monthly headache days of moderate to severe intensity from baseline (4-week pretreatment period) to week 9 through 12. Tolerability and safety endpoints were adverse events (i.e. number and type). Results: Eighty-nine of 100 patients completed the open-label trial. At baseline, the mean monthly number of headache days of moderate to severe intensity was 15.7. By week 9 through 12, the number was reduced by 2.8 days. The most common adverse events were constipation (n = 30) and injection-site reactions (n = 15). Of 100 patients who received at least one dose of erenumab, two patients discontinued the treatment regimen due to adverse events. Conclusions: Among patients with persistent PTH, erenumab resulted in a lower frequency of moderate to severe headache days in this 12-week open-label trial. In addition, erenumab was well-tolerated as discontinuations due to adverse events were low. Placebo-controlled randomized clinical trials are needed to adequately evaluate the efficacy and safety of erenumab in patients with persistent PTH. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.Gov, NCT03974360. Registered on April 17, 2019-Retrospectively registered","author_count":15,"contributors":["Ashina, Håkan","Iljazi, Afrim","Al-Khazali, Haidar Muhsen","Eigenbrodt, Anna Kristina","Larsen, Eigil Lindekilde","Andersen, Amalie Middelboe","Hansen, Kevin John","Braüner, Karoline Bendix","Mørch-Jessen, Thomas","Chaudhry, Basit","Antic, Sonja","Christensen, Casper Emil","Ashina, Messoud","Amin, Faisal Mohammad","Schytz, Henrik Winther"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Schytz, Henrik Winther"],"keyword":["Clinical management","Concussion","Head injury","Head trauma","Secondary headache"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy tolerability and safety of erenumab for the preventive treatment of persistent post traumatic headache attributed to mild traumatic brain injury an open label study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s10194-020-01136-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026686","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7271543","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85086007958","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32493206","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c0f5d303-d6b2-4e04-ba15-0b6fbbf7441c","ku-2e61e23a-734c-47e5-9102-c065d472ea38"],"keyword":["Clinical management","Concussion","Head injury","Head trauma","Secondary headache"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8A74AB21E208B2590B461C9B46249CA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250207141/s10194_020_01136_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s10194-020-01136-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Håkan","key":"ashinahåkanpau","last":"Ashina","name":"Ashina, Håkan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Afrim","key":"iljaziafrimpau","last":"Iljazi","name":"Iljazi, Afrim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Haidar Muhsen","key":"alkhazalihaidarmuhsenpau","last":"Al-Khazali","name":"Al-Khazali, Haidar Muhsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna Kristina","key":"eigenbrodtannakristinapau","last":"Eigenbrodt","name":"Eigenbrodt, Anna Kristina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eigil Lindekilde","key":"larseneigillindekildepau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Eigil Lindekilde","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amalie Middelboe","key":"andersenamaliemiddelboepau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Amalie Middelboe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kevin John","key":"hansenkevinjohnpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kevin John","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karoline Bendix","key":"braünerkarolinebendixpau","last":"Braüner","name":"Braüner, Karoline Bendix","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"mørchjessenthomaspau","last":"Mørch-Jessen","name":"Mørch-Jessen, Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Basit","key":"chaudhrybasitpau","last":"Chaudhry","name":"Chaudhry, Basit","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonja","key":"anticsonjapau","last":"Antic","locid":"c4e6974d-31b5-4f28-a03f-ecc14ff997b8","name":"Antic, Sonja","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Casper Emil","key":"christensencasperemilpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Casper Emil","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Messoud","key":"ashinamessoudpau","last":"Ashina","locid":"0e941844-26c5-4777-a66a-64a163c19cd2","name":"Ashina, Messoud","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Faisal Mohammad","key":"aminfaisalmohammadpau","last":"Amin","locid":"5cea7989-5872-4bc7-bc2d-220a5536f5fb","name":"Amin, Faisal Mohammad","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik Winther","key":"schytzhenrikwintherpau","last":"Schytz","locid":"825ca3a5-a8f5-4f5b-95af-ed64c48207f9","name":"Schytz, Henrik Winther","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32493206"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s10194-020-01136-z","issn":["11292369","11292377"],"issn_org":["11292369"],"journal":"Journal of Headache and Pain","paperid":"62","publisher":"Springer-Verlag Italia s.r.l.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Headache and Pain","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086007958"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c0f5d303-d6b2-4e04-ba15-0b6fbbf7441c","ku-2e61e23a-734c-47e5-9102-c065d472ea38"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Efficacy, tolerability, and safety of erenumab for the preventive treatment of persistent post-traumatic headache attributed to mild traumatic brain injury : An open-label study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026686","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Children with cancer experience impaired cardiorespiratory fitness and physical function during and after treatment restricting their possibilities to engage in social activities including sport, leisure activities, and school. The objectives were to determine the effects of classmate-supported, controlled, supervised, in-hospital, physical activity program to preserve cardiorespiratory fitness and physical function from time of diagnosis in children with cancer. METHODS: National non-randomized controlled trial including schoolchildren aged 6-18 years at diagnosis treated with chemo-/radiotherapy. We included 120 of 128 eligible patients (94%) in the intervention group (62.5% boys, 11.2 ± 3.1 years) from East Denmark and 58 patients in the control group (57% boys, 11.0 ± 3.2 years) from West Denmark. Eight children from the control group withdrew from participation. The groups were comparable in anthropometrics and cancer diagnoses (p > 0.05). The intervention consisted of (i) supervised in-hospital physical activity from diagnosis and throughout intensive treatment, (ii) 90-min general educational session on cancer and therapy in the child's school class, and (iii) selection of two classmates as ambassadors who took turns to support the child's physical training during the daytime. The primary outcome was cardiorespiratory fitness (VO2peak, mL/min/kg) at 6 months after diagnosis (sex, age, diagnosis adjusted). Secondary outcomes were sit-to-stand, timed-up-and-go, handgrip strength, and balance test scores. RESULTS: Ambassadors were identified for all, and 2542 individual and 621 group training sessions were held. VO2peak deteriorated over time in the control group (- 0.17 [95% CI - 0.32 to - 0.02] per week, p = 0.02), but not in the intervention group (p = 0.14). At 6 months from diagnosis, VO2peak was higher in the intervention group (29.6 ± 5.6 mL/kg/min) than in the control group (22.1 ± 5.6 mL/kg/min) (p = 0.01), and the intervention group had a better physical function at 3 and 6 months (p < 0.0001). CONCLUSIONS: Peer-supported, supervised, in-hospital, physical activity is safe and feasible in children with cancer during treatment. Further, the results suggest that the intervention might mitigate impairments in cardiorespiratory fitness during treatment in children with cancer. TRIAL REGISTRATION: The study was prospectively registered on the 11 January 2013. Clinicaltrial.gov NCT01772849 and NCT01772862 .","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Martin Kaj Fridh","Christensen, Jesper Frank","Frandsen, Thomas Leth","Thorsteinsson, Troels","Andersen, Lars Bo","Christensen, Karl Bang","Wehner, Peder Skov","Hasle, Henrik","Adamsen, Lis Ørgaard","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard"],"cuid":["S03-099.67-018163"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian School of Sport Sciences","Oslo University Hospital","Western Norway University of Applied Sciences"],"keyword":["Cardiorespiratory fitness","Childhood cancer","Exercise","Exercise program","Intervention","Motor performance","Muscle Strength","Pediatric cancer","Quality of Life","Social outcomes","functional mobility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of a physical activity program from diagnosis on cardiorespiratory fitness in children with cancer a national non randomized controlled trial","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12916-020-01634-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study received funding from the Novo Nordic Foundation, The Danish Child Cancer Foundation, Trygfonden, Danish Cancer Society, Lundbeckfonden, Arvid Nilssons Foundation, Aase and Ejnar Danielsen’s Foundation, Familien Hede Nielsens Foundations, ML Jørgensen & Gunnar Hansen Foundation, and Toyota Foundation."],"id":"S03-099.67-018163","identifier":[{"id":"000548785300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7336676","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85087473575","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32624004","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4b728506-9c76-4827-bd6c-1c27d828f219","ku-ebe66510-72a3-4b56-a962-b576111582ce","sdu-fa1d9383-91ba-4616-8f9d-20e884d48119"],"keyword":["Cardiorespiratory fitness","Childhood cancer","EXERCISE PROGRAM","Exercise","FUNCTIONAL MOBILITY","INTERVENTION","MOTOR-PERFORMANCE","MUSCLE STRENGTH","PEDIATRIC CANCER","PEER VICTIMIZATION","QUALITY-OF-LIFE","SOCIAL OUTCOMES"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DEEDEFCF60BAFF764284228D6FC61B9E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/246671596/Effects_of_a_physical_activity_program_from_diagnosis_on_cardiorespiratory_fitness_in_children_with_cancer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171801839/s12916_020_01634_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12916-020-01634-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"norwegian school of sport sciences","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian School of Sport Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"western norway university of applied sciences","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Western Norway University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"no","key":"oslo university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Martin Kaj Fridh","key":"nielsenmartinkajfridhpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0ed7e4c8-3698-4429-b293-06b6978844cc","name":"Nielsen, Martin Kaj Fridh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Frank","key":"christensenjesperfrankpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jesper Frank","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Leth","key":"frandsenthomaslethpau","last":"Frandsen","name":"Frandsen, Thomas Leth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Troels","key":"thorsteinssontroelspau","last":"Thorsteinsson","name":"Thorsteinsson, Troels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Bo","key":"andersenlarsbopau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lars Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karl Bang","key":"christensenkarlbangpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"850a805f-c580-4858-822c-8e5c72ac780c","name":"Christensen, Karl Bang","orcid":"0000-0003-4518-5187","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Peder Skov","key":"wehnerpederskovpau","last":"Wehner","locid":"62f49153-9438-4065-af6b-0f5bb33297d0","name":"Wehner, Peder Skov","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"haslehenrikpau","last":"Hasle","locid":"bde24b22-8663-440f-ae65-37d61f0a8975","name":"Hasle, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lis Orgaard","key":"adamsenlispau","last":"Adamsen","locid":"e2dd2ae3-e721-4895-8f98-a857c3a88e6a","name":"Adamsen, Lis","name_org":"Adamsen, Lis Orgaard","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowkjeldpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Hanne Bækgaard","key":"larsenhannebækgaardpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"88b48e37-454f-41e8-a110-a385dce66a6e","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32624004"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12916-020-01634-6","issn":["17417015"],"journal":"BMC Medicine","pages":"175","paperid":"175","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Medicine","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087473575"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4b728506-9c76-4827-bd6c-1c27d828f219","ku-ebe66510-72a3-4b56-a962-b576111582ce","sdu-fa1d9383-91ba-4616-8f9d-20e884d48119"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effects of a physical activity program from diagnosis on cardiorespiratory fitness in children with cancer : a national non-randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.67-018163","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"A quality assurance protocol for RF coils is proposed, which can be used for volume (Tx/Rx) and surface (Rx) coils. Following this protocol, a benchmarking of seven coils (from three different MR sites) dedicated to 13C MRI at 3T is reported. Coil performance is particularly important for 3T MRI at the 13C frequency, since the coil-to-sample noise ratio is typically high. The coils are evaluated experimentally using the proposed protocol based on MR spectroscopic imaging performed with two different phantoms: one head-shaped, and one with cylindrical shape and nearly twice the volume of the first one. To achieve an unbiased SNR comparison of volume and array coils, coil combination was done using sensitivity profiles extracted from the data. SNR, noise correlation matrices and example g-factor maps are reported. For globally calibrated, equal excitation angles, the measured SNR shows large differences for the volume coils of up to 115% at the phantom center for a head phantom. The arrays show lower differences in superficial SNR. The sample surface depth at which the volume coils outperform the arrays is estimated to 7 cm, and SNR furthest away from the coil surface is 28% lower for the best array compared to the best volume coil. A broad set of coils for 13C at 3T have been benchmarked. The results reported, and the method used to benchmark them, should guide the 13C community to choose the most suitable coil for a given experiment.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sánchez-Heredia, Juan Diego","Olin, Rie B","McLean, Mary A","Laustsen, Christoffer","Hansen, Adam E","Hanson, Lars G","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-026604"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["13C MRI","C MRI","Hyperpolarization","Parallel imaging","Quality assurance","RF coil","SNR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi site benchmarking of clinical sup 000000000013 sup c rf coils at 000000000003t","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmr.2020.106798","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-026604","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7501735","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85088888089","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32755748","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bfde1dfd-4a15-403c-b4eb-b05dc5b13500","dtu-d1b7be99-b891-4d7e-96a8-5cf07ee80e45","ku-3f277583-7fb3-43d8-96e8-881fd6d13dcf"],"keyword":["13C MRI","C MRI","Hyperpolarization","Parallel imaging","Quality assurance","RF coil","SNR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DDCD6DCB9C023FE655253E405BAED706"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/220038462/1_s2.0_S1090780720301166_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmr.2020.106798","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/217956757/1_s2.0_S1090780720301166_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260600096/1_s2.0_S1090780720301166_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sánchezherediapau","last":"Sánchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sánchez-Heredia, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rie Beck","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","name_org":"Olin, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mary A","key":"mcleanpau","last":"McLean","name":"McLean, Mary A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars G.","key":"hansonpau","last":"Hanson","locid":"6c7cc6f9-5b6a-47dc-bb02-efe208e52f16","name":"Hanson, Lars G.","orcid":"0000-0002-8204-6912","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32755748"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2020.106798","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","paperid":"106798","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"318"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088888089"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bfde1dfd-4a15-403c-b4eb-b05dc5b13500","dtu-d1b7be99-b891-4d7e-96a8-5cf07ee80e45","ku-3f277583-7fb3-43d8-96e8-881fd6d13dcf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-site benchmarking of clinical <sup>13</sup>C RF coils at 3T","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-026604","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Checkpoint blockade therapies that reactivate tumour-associated T cells can induce durable tumour control and result in the long-term survival of patients with advanced cancers1. Current predictive biomarkers for therapy response include high levels of intratumour immunological activity, a high tumour mutational burden and specific characteristics of the gut microbiota2,3. Although the role of T cells in antitumour responses has thoroughly been studied, other immune cells remain insufficiently explored. Here we use clinical samples of metastatic melanomas to investigate the role of B cells in antitumour responses, and find that the co-occurrence of tumour-associated CD8+ T cells and CD20+ B cells is associated with improved survival, independently of other clinical variables. Immunofluorescence staining of CXCR5 and CXCL13 in combination with CD20 reveals the formation of tertiary lymphoid structures in these CD8+CD20+ tumours. We derived a gene signature associated with tertiary lymphoid structures, which predicted clinical outcomes in cohorts of patients treated with immune checkpoint blockade. Furthermore, B-cell-rich tumours were accompanied by increased levels of TCF7+ naive and/or memory T cells. This was corroborated by digital spatial-profiling data, in which T cells in tumours without tertiary lymphoid structures had a dysfunctional molecular phenotype. Our results indicate that tertiary lymphoid structures have a key role in the immune microenvironment in melanoma, by conferring distinct T cell phenotypes. Therapeutic strategies to induce the formation of tertiary lymphoid structures should be explored to improve responses to cancer immunotherapy.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Cabrita, Rita","Lauss, Martin","Sanna, Adriana","Donia, Marco","Skaarup Larsen, Mathilde","Mitra, Shamik","Johansson, Iva","Phung, Bengt","Harbst, Katja","Vallon-Christersson, Johan","van Schoiack, Alison","Lövgren, Kristina","Warren, Sarah","Jirström, Karin","Olsson, Håkan","Pietras, Kristian","Ingvar, Christian","Isaksson, Karolin","Schadendorf, Dirk","Schmidt, Henrik","Bastholt, Lars","Carneiro, Ana","Wargo, Jennifer A.","Svane, Inge Marie","Jönsson, Göran"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-029827"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jönsson, Göran"],"country":["Germany","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Essen University Hospital","Lund University","NanoString Technologies","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center"],"keyword":["CELLS","Dynamics","Expression"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tertiary lymphoid structures improve immunotherapy and survival in melanoma","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85078123517","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Acknowledgements The study was supported by the Swedish Cancer Society, the Swedish Research Council, BioCARE, the Berta Kamprad Foundation, the King Gustaf V Jubilee foundation, Mats Paulsson’s foundation, Stefan Paulsson’s foundation and governmental funding for healthcare research (ALF). The Danish Cancer Society, the Aase and Einar Danielsen’s Fund and the Capital Region of Denmark Research Foundation. The research leading to these results has received funding from the European Community’s Horizon 2020 Framework Programme for Research and Innovation (H2020-MSCA-ITN-2014) under Grant Agreement no. 247634."],"id":"S03-100.00-029827","identifier":[{"id":"85078123517","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31942071","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000509200100023","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-ec9be655-fddd-4de0-b0d3-b174605fb96e","ku-6fb71d04-63bd-4f2b-8e71-7fa6f58537b6","sdu-aaa8449e-ca7a-47c4-a1ed-8980f482d894"],"keyword":["CELLS","DYNAMICS","EXPRESSION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-0929D2D4C32116B4855FDCD5A4D8F5E8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"nanostring technologies","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"n