{"abstract":"Talent bor i de mennesker, der er ansat i organisationen. Og når mennesker forlader en organisation, tager de den unikke kompetence med sig, og så bliver organisationen svækket. Talentudviklingsprogrammer skal sikre de bedste talenter. Men der er nogle iboende dilemmaer, som du kan læse om her.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-290218"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["MUS","Personale","Talentudvikling"],"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000010 etiske dilemmaer i talentudvikling","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/10-etiske-dilemmaer-i-talentudvikling/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-290218","ids":["cbs-9b722f35-1470-4b6a-b1bf-44f9f028f3cb"],"keyword":["MUS","Personale","Talentudvikling"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9C864AD08123600A75943A3EDDE7093F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/10-etiske-dilemmaer-i-talentudvikling/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-9b722f35-1470-4b6a-b1bf-44f9f028f3cb"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"10 etiske dilemmaer i talentudvikling","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-290218","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The global number of people living with hearing loss continues to grow, while the clinical resources are limited. To address this we describe a scalable goal oriented system. We outline a method on creating an audiological vocabulary, which can be mapped to intents. We create a shared audiological parameter space, with inspiration from clinical workflows. Matching of the intents and the audiological space, results in hearing aid fitting parameters, which then receive feedback from the user. We discuss how to train embedding and recurrent neural network models implementing attention mechanisms, to predict the optimal settings based on learned sequences of dialogue states and device fitting outcomes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Johansen, Benjamin","Larsen, Jakob Eg","Petersen, Michael Kai","Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356433"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-09","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2019-05-04","title":"Chi Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling user utterances as intents in an audiological design space","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85128542047","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356433","identifier":[{"id":"85128542047","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ad9ec3f7-18ca-4d67-b0c0-f875421cb190"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D7BE10DFED767608C70E72B240DC76F1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"oticon","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTI","l3nl":"Oticon A/S","l3nn":"Oticon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oticon","namevar":["Eriksholm Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"3c721ddf-2426-4b69-ac27-00a5847c25fd","name":"Johansen, Benjamin","orcid":"0000-0002-6516-4757","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Eg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"691c8ae7-9a21-4b98-9b91-5e2d9806a4b9","name":"Larsen, Jakob Eg","orcid":"0000-0002-7461-9901","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Kai","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Michael Kai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"pontoppidanpau","last":"Pontoppidan","name":"Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/1122445.1122456","isbn":["9781450399999"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The ACM CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing System 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Oticon A/S","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ad9ec3f7-18ca-4d67-b0c0-f875421cb190"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Modeling User Utterances as Intents in an Audiological Design Space","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356433","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Although multinational enterprises (MNEs) from advanced economies have increasingly internationalised their innovation activities, including R&D, into emerging economies, we have an incomplete understanding of how subsidiaries in these contexts create the technological capabilities to innovate. Based on a single-case qualitative study of a Brazilian subsidiary of a large biotechnology MNE (1989-2016), we found that: (1) the subsidiary's technological capability-building, from production-based to advanced levels (including R&D for applied research), reflects the effectiveness with which it implemented interactive learning strategies through the use of ‘science, technology and innovation’ (STI) and ‘doing, using and interacting’ (DUI) learning mechanisms to tap into three types of knowledge sources: within the subsidiary, the MNE corporate network, and other host sectoral system organisations; (2) the effectiveness of these strategies related to the combined and complementary use of various STI/DUI learning mechanisms over time, which supported the technological capability-building process and, ultimately, the implementation of innovation activities with increased value and novelty. By using a comprehensive and integrative approach to interactive learning, examining how such learning affects the subsidiary's accumulation of innovation capability ‘levels’ and adopting a micro-level perspective in a host emerging economy, we contribute to furthering the understanding of knowledge-seeking strategies and innovation in MNE-subsidiaries, from the standpoint of biotechnology. We also provide a basis for deepening the analysis of interactive learning in subsidiaries in other industries and other emerging economies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Figueiredo, Paulo N.","Larsen, Henrik","Hansen, Ulrich Elmer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379105"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brazilian School of Public and Business Administration","Imperial College London"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of interactive learning in innovation capability building in multinational subsidiaries a micro level study of biotechnology in brazil","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85084956232","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379105","identifier":[{"id":"85084956232","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000540272800010","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-f91a1cd4-9c01-45b1-8302-0de11ae27216"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-91311C8C4DA2E8464A1148DE76591B32"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"brazilian school of public and business administration","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Brazilian School of Public and Business Administration","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, UNEP DTU Partnership","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, UNEP DTU Partnership, Technology - Transitions and System Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paulo N.","key":"figueiredopau","last":"Figueiredo","name":"Figueiredo, Paulo N.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrich Elmer","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b3b4964a-0c31-4c39-8877-d298f9ada8b3","name":"Hansen, Ulrich Elmer","orcid":"0000-0002-8997-6717","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.respol.2020.103995","issn":["00487333"],"issue":"6","journal":"Research Policy","paperid":"103995","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Research Policy","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084956232"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f91a1cd4-9c01-45b1-8302-0de11ae27216"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The role of interactive learning in innovation capability building in multinational subsidiaries: A micro-level study of biotechnology in Brazil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379105","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
