en","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Dorthe","key":"zwisleranndortheolsenpau","last":"Zwisler","locid":"6e2c85c0-d456-45f2-a017-7942ea7eb12a","name":"Zwisler, Ann Dorthe Olsen","name_org":"Zwisler, Ann-Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-9241-2090","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Dorthe","key":"zwisleranndorthepau","last":"Zwisler","name":"Zwisler, Ann-Dorthe","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32380928"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1089/jpm.2019.0566","issn":["10966218","15577740"],"issn_org":["10966218"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Palliative Medicine","pages":"1159-1166","publisher":"Mary Ann Liebert Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Palliative Medicine","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090274147"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","the danish knowledge centre for rehabilitation and palliative care"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e0b3a3ac-32da-4612-adea-5581d04906ee","au-2d224133-31f0-452b-93f9-d6bfc3e62b12","ku-4258cb53-3a22-4e60-86fa-e38987474a8f","sdu-f12557a5-27c4-46e3-a1c3-80d64c9ac7f7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The First Steps Taken to Implement Palliative Care in Advanced Heart Disease : A Position Statement from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-010724","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Detective stories in games have long been a heavily used inspiration source and setting for games, and it is indeed a fitting genre at first glance with its clearly defined set of expectations, rules, and type of storytelling relying on uncovering the past. It is curious then, that until recently, most detective games have followed a more traditional adventure game structure, with little emphasis on actual investigation in the player’s actions, but where the player more acts as a proxy for the plot to follow its course. However, in recent years, a number of games have shown a tendency to shift this balance, and push the bulk of the detective work onto the players themselves, to leave them with an inscrutable mystery to slowly uncover over the course of the game, to decipher the story of the crime in their mind. This paper will investigate a few of these games as well as compare with literature on traditional detective stories to understand how detective games have typically been a different type of detective story all together, which is crucial to understanding how we can make the player the detective instead of an observer of a detective.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","Schoenau-Fog, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-103010"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","end":"2020-09-18","place":"Bugibba, mt","start":"2020-09-15","title":"FDG '20: International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Crime","Detective Fiction","Environmental Storytelling","Mystery"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"making the player the detective","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85092304361&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-103010","identifier":[{"id":"85092304361","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b663029d-955f-4380-b7b2-429855ed2f31"],"keyword":["Crime","Detective Fiction","Detective games","Environmental Storytelling","Mystery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F88F2C17F2454C21759E76D905C5630"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarke Alexander","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b20b35fc-c929-4058-a942-903b3772a4b1","name":"Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schoenaufogpau","last":"Schoenau-Fog","locid":"34a35708-1cbb-4d3b-9b7c-53080126b5ef","name":"Schoenau-Fog, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-157X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Georgios N.","key":"yannakakispedh","last":"Yannakakis","name":"Yannakakis, Georgios N.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonios","key":"liapispedh","last":"Liapis","name":"Liapis, Anton