{"abstract":"The most common genetic cause of neonatal diabetes and hyperinsulinism is pathogenic variants in ABCC8 and KCNJ11. These genes encode the subunits of the β-cell ATP-sensitive potassium channel, a key component of the glucose-stimulated insulin secretion pathway. Mutations in the two genes cause dysregulated insulin secretion; inactivating mutations cause an oversecretion of insulin, leading to congenital hyperinsulinism, whereas activating mutations cause the opposing phenotype, diabetes. This review focuses on variants identified in ABCC8 and KCNJ11, the phenotypic spectrum and the treatment implications for individuals with pathogenic variants.","author_count":20,"contributors":["De Franco, Elisa","Saint-Martin, Cécile","Brusgaard, Klaus","Knight Johnson, Amy E.","Aguilar-Bryan, Lydia","Bowman, Pamela","Arnoux, Jean Baptiste","Larsen, Annette Rønholt","May, Sanyoura","Greeley, Siri Atma W.","Calzada-León, Raúl","Harman, Bradley","Houghton, Jayne A.L.","Nishimura-Meguro, Elisa","Laver, Thomas W.","Ellard, Sian","del Gaudio, Daniela","Christesen, Henrik Thybo","Bellanné-Chantelot, Christine","Flanagan, Sarah E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586229"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Flanagan, Sarah E."],"country":["France","Mexico","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AP-HP)","All Global Affiliations","Instituto Mexicano del Seguro Social","National Institute for Pediatrics","Necker Enfants Malades Hospital","Pacific Northwest Research Institute","Royal Devon & Exeter NHS Foundation Trust","University of Chicago","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["ABCC8","Congenital hyperinsulinism","K ATP channel","Neonatal diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"update of variants identified in the pancreatic β cell k sub atp sub channel genes kcnj000000000011 and abcc000000000008 in individuals with congenital hyperinsulinism and diabetes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/humu.23995","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586229","identifier":[{"id":"32027066","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85079703035","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7187370","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-2d7feb57-070e-48c4-a329-bab2ccf25b99"],"keyword":["ABCC8","K-ATP channel","KCNJ11","congenital hyperinsulinism","neonatal diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7A01902B2FAA1C42E82BDBB1BC3CB244"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/humu.23995","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/169018444/humu.23995.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"ap hp","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"AP-HP)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of chicago","loc":[