University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Creating a clinical platform for carbon-13 studies using the sodium-23 and proton resonances","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.94-027932","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The aim of this study was to compare the acute effects of isometric versus dynamic resistance exercise on pain during a pain-provoking activity, and exercise-induced hypoalgesia in participants with patellar tendinopathy. DESIGN: This study was a pre-registered randomised crossover study. Participants were blinded to the study hypothesis. METHODS: Participants (N = 21) performed a single session of high load isometric resistance exercise or dynamic resistance exercise, in a randomised order separated by a 7-day washout period. Outcomes were assessed before, immediately after, and 45 min post-exercise. The primary outcome was pain intensity scored on a numeric pain rating scale (NRS; 0-10) during a pain-provoking single leg decline squat (SLDS). Secondary outcomes were pressure pain thresholds (PPTs) locally, distally and remotely, as well as tendon thickness. RESULTS: There was a significant decrease in pain NRS scores (mean reduction 0.9, NRS 95%CI 0.1-1.7; p = 0.028), and increase in PPTs at the tibialis anterior muscle (mean increase 34 kPa 95%CI 9.5-58.5; p = 0.009) immediately post-exercise. These were not sustained 45 min post-exercise for pain (NRS) or PPTs (p > 0.05). There were no differences between exercise on any outcome. CONCLUSIONS: While patients with patellar tendinopathy decreased pain during SLDS in response to resistance training, but the magnitude was small. Contraction mode may not be the most important factor in determining the magnitude of pain relieving effects. Similarly, there were only small increases in PPTs at the tibialis anterior which were not superior for isometric exercise.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holden, Sinead","Lyng, Kristian Damgaard","Graven-Nielsen, Thomas","Riel, Henrik","Olesen, Jens Lykkegaard","Larsen, Lars Henrik","Rathleff, Michael Skovdal"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-010411"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Athletes","Exercise induced hypoalgesia","Pain Measurement","Pain Threshold","Pain relief","Psychophysiology","Resistance exercise","Tendon"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"isometric exercise and pain in patellar tendinopathy a randomized crossover trial","src":["aau","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsams.2019.09.015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-010411","identifier":[{"id":"31735531","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075437780","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-da0bbb76-271c-461a-aad8-5513b3a523a5","ucn-b3ef37cc-01b9-465a-8217-5ad5cf0ceff5"],"keyword":["Athletes","Exercise induced hypoalgesia","Pain measurement","Pain relief","Pain threshold","Psychophysiology","Resistance exercise","Tendon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-78AA735D88ACD4B1644D4BE5BF52DED8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsams.2019.09.015","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/402719184/AM_Isometric_exercise_and_pain_in_patellar_tendinopathy._A_randomized_crossover.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for General Practice at Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Musculoskeletal Health and Implementation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sinéad","key":"holdenpau","last":"Holden","locid":"8cd76341-9177-4b45-b939-3c487530e766","name":"Holden, Sinead","name_org":"Holden, Sinéad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"lyngpau","last":"Lyng","locid":"6e9c1959-3cf2-4ccc-8941-9b82c7f0c9a5","name":"Lyng, Kristian Damgaard","name_org":"Lyng, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0001-8668-691X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"gravennielsenpau","last":"Graven-Nielsen","locid":"474a635b-4e83-4b02-a90b-80d417d37e52","name":"Graven-Nielsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7787-4860","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"rielpau","last":"Riel","locid":"8ebfac40-1730-494c-83ee-d4ca459c1fbc","name":"Riel, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-6293","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Lykkegaard","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"73e90fa7-9139-4759-8fed-aac470f54696","name":"Olesen, Jens Lykkegaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a997ad4d-e8d1-47b2-8b96-d5b9b748e4c5","name":"Larsen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7830-1186","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Skovdal","key":"rathleffpau","last":"Rathleff","locid":"90c1260f-4cd4-497f-88ca-a98f412bbe7b","name":"Rathleff, Michael Skovdal","orcid":"0000-0003-1173-0335","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31735531"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jsams.2019.09.015","issn":["14402440","18781861"],"issn_org":["14402440"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Science and Medicine in Sport","pages":"208-214","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Science and Medicine in Sport","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075437780"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-da0bbb76-271c-461a-aad8-5513b3a523a5","ucn-b3ef37cc-01b9-465a-8217-5ad5cf0ceff5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Isometric exercise and pain in patellar tendinopathy : A randomized crossover trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-010411","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The present study tested the hypothesis that metformin treatment may increase myocardial efficiency (stroke work/myocardial oxygen consumption) in insulin-resistant patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF) without diabetes. METHODS AND RESULTS: Thirty-six HFrEF patients (ejection fraction 37 ± 8%; median age 66 years) were randomised to metformin (n = 19) or placebo (n = 17) for 3 months in addition to standard heart failure therapy. The primary endpoint was change in myocardial efficiency expressed as the work metabolic index (WMI), assessed by 11 C-acetate positron emission tomography and transthoracic echocardiography. Compared with placebo, metformin treatment (1450 ± 550 mg/day) increased WMI [absolute mean difference, 1.0 mmHg·mL·m-2 ·106 ; 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.1 to 1.8; P = 0.03], equivalent to a 20% relative efficiency increase. Patients with above-median plasma metformin levels displayed greater WMI increase (25% vs. -4%; P = 0.02). Metformin reduced myocardial oxygen consumption (-1.6 mL O2 ·100 g-1 ·min-1 ; P = 0.014). Cardiac stroke work was preserved (-2 J; 95% CI -11 to 7; P = 0.69). Metformin reduced body weight (-2.2 kg; 95% CI -3.6 to -0.8; P = 0.003) and glycated haemoglobin levels (-0.2%; 95% CI -0.3 to 0.0; P = 0.02). Changes in resting and exercise ejection fraction, global longitudinal strain, and exercise capacity did not differ between groups. CONCLUSION: Metformin treatment in non-diabetic HFrEF patients improved myocardial efficiency by reducing myocardial oxygen consumption. Measurement of circulating metformin levels differentiated responders from non-responders. These energy-sparing effects of metformin encourage further large-scale investigations in heart failure patients without diabetes.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Larsen, Anders Hostrup","Jessen, Niels","Nørrelund, Helene","Tolbod, Lars Poulsen","Harms, Hendrik Johannes","Feddersen, Søren","Nielsen, Flemming","Brøsen, Kim","Hansson, Nils Henrik","Frøkiær, Jørgen","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","Sørensen, Jens","Wiggers, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024347"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Anders Hostrup"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Insulin Resistance","Metformin","Mitochondrial function","Myocardial efficiency","Myocardial oxygen consumption"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a randomised double blind placebo controlled trial of metformin on myocardial efficiency in insulin resistant chronic heart failure patients without diabetes","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171355540/ejhf.1656.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024347","identifier":[{"id":"85076914044","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31863557","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9f8dd9e3-e889-4a26-981f-22aa50d2f2e9","sdu-6114a1c4-a4b0-479e-85c1-0583c5949068"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Insulin resistance","Metformin","Mitochondrial function","Myocardial efficiency","Myocardial oxygen consumption"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D8DFB50E331E417160636CAAFBD249F1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171355540/ejhf.1656.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","