ensen","locid":"cab278f0-6db5-48a8-8764-b7da319d7818","name":"Sørensen, Jens","name_org":"Sörensen, Jens","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"wiggerspau","last":"Wiggers","locid":"aef6a13e-8c07-474c-a4f6-bc35236a6eda","name":"Wiggers, Henrik","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31863557"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejhf.1656","issn":["13889842","18790844"],"issn_org":["13889842"],"issue":"9","journal":"European Journal of Heart Failure","pages":"1628-1637","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Heart Failure","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076914044"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9f8dd9e3-e889-4a26-981f-22aa50d2f2e9","sdu-6114a1c4-a4b0-479e-85c1-0583c5949068"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of metformin on myocardial efficiency in insulin-resistant chronic heart failure patients without diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024347","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to acquire the transient MRI signal of hyperpolarized tracers and their metabolites efficiently, for which specialized imaging sequences are required. In this work, a multi-echo balanced steady-state free precession (me-bSSFP) sequence with Iterative Decomposition with Echo Asymmetry and Least squares estimation (IDEAL) reconstruction was implemented on a clinical 3 T positron-emission tomography/MRI system for fast 2D and 3D metabolic imaging. Simulations were conducted to obtain signal-efficient sequence protocols for the metabolic imaging of hyperpolarized biomolecules. The sequence was applied in vitro and in vivo for probing the enzymatic exchange of hyperpolarized [1–13C]pyruvate and [1–13C]lactate. Chemical shift resolution was achieved using a least-square, iterative chemical species separation algorithm in the reconstruction. In vitro, metabolic conversion rate measurements from me-bSSFP were compared with NMR spectroscopy and free induction decay-chemical shift imaging (FID-CSI). In vivo, a rat MAT-B-III tumor model was imaged with me-bSSFP and FID-CSI. 2D metabolite maps of [1–13C]pyruvate and [1–13C]lactate acquired with me-bSSFP showed the same spatial distributions as FID-CSI. The pyruvate-lactate conversion kinetics measured with me-bSSFP and NMR corresponded well. Dynamic 2D metabolite mapping with me-bSSFP enabled the acquisition of up to 420 time frames (scan time: 180-350 ms/frame) before the hyperpolarized [1–13C]pyruvate was relaxed below noise level. 3D metabolite mapping with a large field of view (180 × 180 × 48 mm3) and high spatial resolution (5.6 × 5.6 × 2 mm3) was conducted with me-bSSFP in a scan time of 8.2 seconds. It was concluded that Me-bSSFP improves the spatial and temporal resolution for metabolic imaging of hyperpolarized [1–13C]pyruvate and [1–13C]lactate compared with either of the FID-CSI or EPSI methods reported at 3 T, providing new possibilities for clinical and preclinical applications.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Müller, Christoph A.","Hundshammer, Christian","Braeuer, Miriam","Skinner, Jason G.","Berner, Stephan","Leupold, Jochen","Düwel, Stephan","Nekolla, Stephan G.","Månsson, Sven","Hansen, Adam E.","von Elverfeldt, Dominik","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Schilling, Franz","Schwaiger, Markus","Hennig, Jürgen","Hövener, Jan Bernd"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038120"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Müller, Christoph A."],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center","Kiel University","Lund University","Technical University of Munich","University of Freiburg"],"keyword":["Balanced steady state free precession","Carbon 13","Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarization","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Metabolite mapping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic 000000000002d and 000000000003d mapping of hyperpolarized pyruvate to lactate conversion in vivo with efficient multi echo balanced steady state free precession at 000000000003 t","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.4291","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Support by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG) (SFB 824, 391523415, 68647618), the Emmy Noether Program (HO‐4604/2‐1, HO‐4604/2‐2), Cluster of Excellence funding (EXC 306, PMI 1267) and the DFG Major Instrumentation Initiative PET/MR, is gratefully acknowledged. We thank the European Commission for the European Regional Development Fund (122‐09‐053), the Horizon 2020 Marie Skłodowska Curie grant (642773) and the ERC Advanced Grant (294582). We thank the German Consortium for Translational Cancer Research (DKTK)."],"id":"S02-100.00-038120","identifier":[{"id":"85081218147","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32154970","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-f963aff4-c439-4565-9806-ca31a3496180","ku-11bfce40-7763-4c76-bcb5-5b95ade689d9"],"keyword":["Balanced steady-state free precession","Carbon-13","Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarization","Magnetic resonance imaging","Metabolite mapping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C37346D78F9BDE36D0E0517B63876476"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.4291","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/209278779/nbm.4291.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346953197/NMR_in_Biomedicine_2020_M_ller_Dynamic_2D_and_3D_mapping_of_hyperpolarized_pyruvate_to_lactate_conversion_in_vivo.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"german cancer research center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Cancer Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU Universit