{"abstract":"Corona har på få dage ført til en massiv udbredelse af hjemmearbejde. Det giver mere autonomi til medarbejderne, men også en risiko for konstant dårlig samvittighed og ensomhed. Desuden opstår der lettere misforståelser og sårede følelser, når kommunikationen primært sker via mail. Læs om distancearbejde og -ledelse, og hvad du og dine medarbejdere skal være særligt opmærksomme på.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-295519"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nærværende corona ledelse på afstand","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/naervaerende-corona-ledelse-paa-distancen/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-295519","ids":["cbs-d397ac72-655a-4c1c-853e-d2cbf1513111"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1DC63FADC1BF5B166100B494A0C11B41"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/naervaerende-corona-ledelse-paa-distancen/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-d397ac72-655a-4c1c-853e-d2cbf1513111"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Nærværende corona-ledelse på afstand","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-295519","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Life cycle impact assessment (LCIA) is a lively field of research, and data and models are continuously improved in terms of impact pathways covered, reliability, and spatial detail. However, many of these advancements are scattered throughout the scientific literature, making it difficult for practitioners to apply the new models. Here, we present the LC‐IMPACT method that provides characterization factors at the damage level for 11 impact categories related to three areas of protection (human health, ecosystem quality, natural resources). Human health damage is quantified as disability adjusted life years, damage to ecosystem quality as global species extinction equivalents (based on potentially disappeared fraction of species), and damage to mineral resources as kilogram of extra ore extracted. Seven of the impact categories include spatial differentiation at various levels of spatial scale. The influence of value choices related to the time horizon and the level of scientific evidence of the impacts considered is quantified with four distinct sets of characterization factors. We demonstrate the applicability of the proposed method with an illustrative life cycle assessment example of different fuel options in Europe (petrol or biofuel). Differences between generic and regionalized impacts vary up to two orders of magnitude for some of the selected impact categories, highlighting the importance of spatial detail in LCIA.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Verones, Francesca","Hellweg, Stefanie","Antón, Assumpció","Azevedo, Ligia B.","Chaudhary, Abhishek","Cosme, Nuno Miguel Dias","Cucurachi, Stefano","Baan, Laura","Dong, Yan","Fantke, Peter","Golsteijn, Laura","Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","Heijungs, Reinout","Jolliet, Olivier","Juraske, Ronnie","Larsen, Henrik","Laurent, Alexis","Mutel, Christopher L.","Margni, Manuele","Núñez, Montserrat","Owsianiak, Mikolaj","Pfister, Stephan","Ponsioen, Tommie","Preiss, Philipp","Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","Roy, Pierre‐Olivier","Sala, Serenella","Steinmann, Zoran","Zelm, Rosalie","Van Dingenen, Rita","Vieira, Marisa","Huijbregts, Mark A. J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311047"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DG Joint Research Centre","Institute of Agrifood Research and Technology","Leiden University","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","PRé Sustainability B.V.","Paul Scherrer Institute","Pforzheim University of Applied Sciences","Polytechnique Montreal","Radboud University Nijmegen","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","University of Michigan"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lc impact a regionalized life cycle damage assessment method","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jiec.13018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311047","identifier":[{"id":"85084996216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1573f16f-df1b-46c2-91e6-6d6e0840da40"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C016AC01CA390B0D3C9C15FA407C5D13"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235400390/jiec.13018.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jiec.13018","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/216215255/Verones_2020a.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"