"name":"Rouse, Nicholas","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Prasoon","key":"agarwalpau","last":"Agarwal","name":"Agarwal, Prasoon","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Vernon W","key":"dolinskypau","last":"Dolinsky","name":"Dolinsky, Vernon W","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marica","key":"bakovicpau","last":"Bakovic","name":"Bakovic, Marica","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31855247"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/brain/awz376","issn":["00068950","14602156"],"issn_org":["00068950"],"issue":"1","journal":"Brain","pages":"94-111","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Brain","volume":"143"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077349906"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2b492459-14ce-4617-8524-e4b239aa39c7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Choline transporter-like 1 deficiency causes a new type of childhood-onset neurodegeneration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-585592","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Unexplained or idiopathic ketotic hypoglycemia (KH) is the most common type of hypoglycemia in children. The diagnosis is based on the exclusion of routine hormonal and metabolic causes of hypoglycemia. We aimed to identify novel genes that cause KH, as this may lead to a more targeted treatment. Deep phenotyping of ten preschool age at onset KH patients (boys, n = 5; girls, n = 5) was performed followed by trio exome sequencing and comprehensive bioinformatics analysis. Data analysis revealed four novel candidate genes: (1) NCOR1 in a patient with KH, iron deficiency and loose stools; (2) IGF2BP1 in a proband with KH, short stature and delayed bone age; (3) SLC5A2 in a proband with KH, intermittent glucosuria and extremely elevated p-GLP-1; and (4) NEK11 in a proband with ketotic hypoglycemia and liver affliction. These genes are associated with different metabolic processes, such as gluconeogenesis, translational regulation, and glucose transport. In conclusion, WES identified DNA variants in four different genes as potential novel causes of IKH, suggesting that IKH is a heterogeneous disorder that can be split into several novel diseases: NCOR1-KH, IGF2BP1-KH, SGLT2-KH or familial renal glucosuria KH, and NEK11-KH. Precision medicine treatment based on exome sequencing may lead to advances in the management of IKH.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Alhaidan, Yazeid","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Schou, Anders Jørgen","Stenlid, Maria H","Al Balwi, Mohammed A","Christesen, Henrik Thybo","Brusgaard, Klaus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627946"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Saudi Arabia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Paediatric Endocrinology, Uppsala University Children's Hospital, Uppsala, Sweden.","King Abdullah International Medical Research Center","King Saud Bin Abdulaziz University for Health Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exome sequencing revealed dna variants in ncor000000000001 igf000000000002bp000000000001 sglt000000000002 and nek000000000011 as potential novel causes of ketotic hypoglycemia in children","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-58845-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627946","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7005888","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32034166","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85079080922","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bef03409-e696-4951-a268-770b3126fda3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D607832BAAF5C8BCC26ABBD823CE19FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-58845-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170150963/s41598_020_58845_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sa","key":"king abdullah international medical research center","loc":["Saudi Arabia","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"King Abdullah International Medical Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"sa","key":"king