,"rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788757134056"],"pages":"130-149","publisher":"Praxis","status":"p","subtitle":"Pædagogisk videnskabsteori for erhvervsskolelærere","title":"Sandheder og menneskesyn"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-f9effdfe-e4cf-4b68-9418-920974379dc7"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Læring og lærebaner","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-652704","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background and Aim: Based on advances in the diagnosis, classification, and management of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL), a number of new prognostic models have been proposed. The aim of this study was to review and compare different prognostic models of DLBCL based on the statistical methods used to evaluate the performance of each model, as well as to analyze the possible limitations of the methods. Methods and Results: A literature search identified 46 articles that proposed 55 different prognostic models for DLBCL by combining different clinical, laboratory, and other para-meters of prognostic significance. In addition, six studies used nomograms, which avoid risk categorization, to create prognostic models. Only a minority of studies assessed discrimination and/or calibration to compare existing models built upon different statistical methods in the process of development of a new prognostic model. All models based on nomograms reported the c-index as a measure of discrimination. There was no uniform evaluation of the performance in other prognostic models. We compared these models of DLBCL by calculat-ing differences and ratios of 3-year overall survival probabilities between the high-and the low-risk groups. We found that the highest and lowest ratio between low-and high-risk groups was 6 and 1.31, respectively, while the difference between these groups was 18.9% and 100%, respectively. However, these studies had limited duration of follow-up and the number of patients ranged from 71 to 335. Conclusion: There is no universal statistical instrument that could facilitate a comparison of prognostic models in DLBCL. However, when developing a prognostic model, it is recom-mended to report its discrimination and calibration in order to facilitate comparisons between different models. Furthermore, prognostic models based on nomograms are becoming more appealing owing to individualized disease-related risk estimations. However, they have not been validated yet in other study populations.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jelicic, Jelena","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","Frederiksen, Henrik","Andjelic, Bosko","Maksimovic, Milos","Bukumiric, Zoran"],"cuid":["S02-096.08-006626"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Thomas Stauffer"],"country":["Serbia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Blackpool Victoria Hospital","University of Belgrade"],"keyword":["Calibration","Diffuse large B cell lymphoma","Discrimination","MODELS","Nomograms","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Blackpool Victoria Hospital, Lancashire Haematology Centre, Blackpool, UK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statistical challenges in development of prognostic models in diffuse large b cell lymphoma comparison between existing models a systematic review","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S244294","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.08-006626","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7266947","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32581596","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085881277","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-88ee9e21-ddd9-42c4-976a-182067444c6a","sdu-5d79d322-82ff-4fda-afec-99440d4a81ce"],"keyword":["Calibration","Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma","Discrimination","Models","Nomograms","Prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-78F660DC61EA2432AD233841F2AF413E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/344113962/Jelicic_et_al_2020_Statistical_challenges_in_development_of_prognostic_models_in_diffuse_large_B_cell_lymphoma.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170403249/clep_244294_statistical_challenges_in_development_of_prognostic_models_i.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S244294","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Haematology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Blackpool Victoria Hospital, Lancashire Haematology Centre, Blackpool, UK"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"blackpool victoria hospital","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Blackpool Victoria Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Ophthalmology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"rs","key":"university of belgrade","loc":["Serbia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"University of Belgrade","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jelena","key":"jelicicpau","last":"Jelicic","locid":"096a2a0c-5198-4740-9e4f-c3e3073ee4fc","name":"Jelicic, Jelena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Stauffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dd2de49b-c3d9-49cb-bb8d-e92119e0b2d1","name":"Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"6e4bf33a-3b75-42c4-b830-43e26dcea675","name":"Frederiksen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8905-0220","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bosko","key":"andjelicpau","last":"Andjelic","name":"Andjelic, Bosko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Milos","key":"maksimovicpau","last":"Maksimovic","locid":"9ad67ff5-685e-4242-a591-1160a9904038","name":"Maksimovic, Milos","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Zoran","key":"bukumiricpau","last":"Bukumiric","name":"Bukumiric, Zoran","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32581596"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s244294","issn":["11791349"],"journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"537-555","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","publisher_org":"Dove Medical Press Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085881277"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-88ee9e21-ddd9-42c4-976a-182067444c6a","sdu-5d79d322-82ff-4fda-afec-99440d4a81ce"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Statistical challenges in development of prognostic models in diffuse large B-cell lymphoma : Comparison between existing models – A systematic review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.08-006626","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Pancreatic beta-cells become irreversibly damaged by long-term exposure to excessive glucose concentrations and lose their ability to carry out glucose stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) upon damage. The beta-cells are not able to control glucose uptake and they are therefore left vulnerable for endogenous toxicity from metabolites produced in excess amounts upon increased glucose availability. In order to handle excess fuel, the beta-cells possess specific metabolic pathways, but little is known about these pathways. We present a study of beta-cell metabolism under increased fuel pressure using a stable isotope resolved NMR approach to investigate early metabolic events leading up to beta-cell dysfunction. The approach is based on a recently described combination of C-13 metabolomics combined with signal enhanced NMR via dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP). Glucose-responsive INS-1 beta-cells were incubated with increasing concentrations of [U-C-13] glucose under conditions where GSIS was not affected (2-8 h). We find that pyruvate and DHAP were the metabolites that responded most strongly to increasing fuel pressure. The two major divergence pathways for fuel excess, the glycerolipid/fatty acid metabolism and the polyol pathway, were found not only to operate at unchanged rate but also with similar quantity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Malinowski, Ronja Maja","Ghiasi, Seyed M.","Mandrup-Poulsen, Thomas","Meier, Sebastian","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"cuid":["S02-096.24-785326"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"keyword":["13C NMR","Beta cells","DNP","Excess","Glucose","LINE","Metabolomics","Pathway"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pancreatic beta cells respond to fuel pressure with an early metabolic switch","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-72348-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.24-785326","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7508987","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85091287516","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32963286","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000577217800002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-4acb2800-5297-43d8-af31-c2197204312a","ku-be4a9b5c-28b0-4b9c-9c54-0f5f27fe9ab2"],"keyword":["13C NMR","Beta cells","DNP","EXCESS","Excess-fuel handling","GLUCOSE","ISOTOPE-RESOLVED METABOLOMICS","LINE","Metabolomics","PATHWAY","STIMULATED INSULIN-SECRETION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CCCDD436437831BDCC990BA45823F784"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-72348-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/222263088/s41598_020_72348_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251644445/OA_Pancreatic_cells_respond_to_fuel.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of cop