{"abstract":"Background âThe ABO locus has been associated with increased risk of myocardial infarction (MI) in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD), but the underlying mechanisms are unknown. As altered fibrin clot structure has been demonstrated to predict MI in CAD patients, we examined the association between the ABO risk variant and fibrin clot properties, and investigated the effects of other CAD-associated risk variants. Methods âWe included 773 stable CAD patients. Patients were genotyped for 45 genome-wide CAD risk variants, including rs495828 at the ABO locus. We used a genetic risk score (GRS) for CAD calculated as the weighted sum of the number of risk alleles based on all 45 variants. Fibrin clot properties were evaluated using a turbidimetric assay. We studied clot maximum absorbance, a measure of clot density and fiber thickness, together with clot lysis time, an indicator of fibrinolysis potential. Results âThe rs495828 risk allele was present in 13.2% of patients and associated with higher clot maximum absorbance (adjusted effect size per risk allele: 1.05 [1.01-1.09], p = 0.01) but not with clot lysis time (p = 0.97). The rs12936587 (p = 0.04), rs4773144 (p = 0.02), and rs501120 (p = 0.04) were associated with clot lysis time; however, after Bonferroni correction, no significant associations were found between any of the remaining 44 CAD-associated variants and fibrin clot properties. The GRS was not associated with fibrin clot properties (p-values > 0.05). Conclusion âThe ABO risk allele was associated with a more compact fibrin network in stable CAD patients, which may represent a mechanism for increased MI risk in ABO risk variant carriers.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Winther-Larsen, Anne","Christiansen, Morten Krogh","Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","Nyegaard, Mette","Neergaard-Petersen, Søs","Ajjan, Ramzi A","Würtz, Morten","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Kristensen, Steen Dalby","Hvas, Anne-Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-180452"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hvas, Anne-Mette"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Leeds"],"keyword":["ABO Blood Group System","Blood Coagulation","Coronary artery disease","Fibrin clot","Fibrinolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the abo locus is associated with increased fibrin network formation in patients with stable coronary artery disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090231454","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-180452","identifier":[{"id":"32604426","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090231454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-59ae9f19-7ccd-475d-a5af-3428a6e854c6"],"keyword":["ABO blood-group system","blood coagulation","coronary artery disease","fibrin clot","fibrinolysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8FB2DE4D28F3638521CD7B7BFCC47F68"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of clinical biochemistry","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Viborg Regional Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of leeds","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Leeds","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"wintherlarsenpau","last":"Winther-Larsen","locid":"162faab4-e6ad-4fce-8149-eafe733901ec","name":"Winther-Larsen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-2763-595X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Krogh","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"bf2444c5-3e70-45d3-b035-850325ff2f6e","name":"Christiansen, Morten Krogh","orcid":"0000-0002-3894-888X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Bøjet","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"15c7c979-5236-47ec-b92e-a4a5992b2d1e","name":"Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardpau","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"a34df7ff-0fb5-44b0-8255-6dc2c9b962f3","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søs","key":"neergaardpetersenpau","last":"Neergaard-Petersen","locid":"7c75329a-0cef-4da3-959b-2bf6b326aaf5","name":"Neergaard-Petersen, Søs","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramzi A","key":"ajjanpau","last":"Ajjan","name":"Ajjan, Ramzi A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"würtzpau","last":"Würtz","locid":"b5e070b9-ecf1-43ae-83c2-164d5eeccfc5","name":"Würtz, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7150-7704","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Lerkevang","key":"grovepau","last":"Grove","locid":"f527f99e-8eed-433e-923e-afc0686af8b7","name":"Grove, Erik Lerkevang","orcid":"0000-0002-1466-0865","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Dalby","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"6d64271d-8a2c-41ea-891d-e85555bbd47a","name":"Kristensen, Steen Dalby","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne-Mette","key":"hvaspau","last":"Hvas","locid":"b4362b49-6deb-4c2c-9027-48dc6cdbd5e6","name":"Hvas, Anne-Mette","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32604426"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1055/s-0040-1713753","issn":["03406245","03447618"],"issn_org":["03406245"],"issue":"9","journal":"Thrombosis and Haemostasis","pages":"1248-1256","publisher":"Georg Thieme Verlag","status":"p","title":"Thrombosis and Haemostasis","volume":"120"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090231454"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-59ae9f19-7ccd-475d-a5af-3428a6e854c6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The ABO Locus is Associated with Increased Fibrin Network Formation in Patients with Stable Coronary Artery Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-180452","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Monitoring of agricultural mini-catchments (AMC) has been part of the Danish national monitoring programme (National Monitoring Programme for Water and Nature) since 1989. Thus, nitrogen (N) concentrations and loads have been monitored in soil water, tile drains, and streams within five AMC. Moreover, extensive monitoring of N concentrations and loads in streams draining 46 mini-catchments has been conducted every year since 1989. This has resulted in two national datasets on trends in flow-weighted N concentrations relative to factors such as groundwater age and management history. We analyzed these datasets and found that the intensively monitored micro-catchments generally showed a strong signal with significant downward trends in flow-weighted N concentrations in monitored soil water (-22% to -68%), tile drains (-38% to -59%), and streams (-19% to -53%). The 46 micro-catchments monitored for N in streams also exhibited downward trends in flow-weighted N concentrations, which can mainly be ascribed to the introduction of mandatory national regulation of N in agriculture in Denmark in the mid-1980s. However, classification of the mini-catchments according to the age of the oxidized groundwater revealed significant differences in N trends between the groups of mini-catchments. Thus, the strongest downward trend in flow-weighted N concentrations was as follows: <1 year (-52%), 1-3 years (-44%), and >3 years (-38%).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Blicher-Mathiesen, Gitte","Windolf, Jørgen","Larsen, Søren Erik","Rolighed, Jonas","Carstensen, Mette Vodder","Højberg, A. L.","Tornbjerg, Henrik","Kronvang, Brian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-202947"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Blicher-Mathiesen, Gitte"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"keyword":["Agriculture","Groundwater age","Nitrogen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of nitrogen mitigation measures evaluated by monitoring of nitrogen concentrations and loadings in danish mini catchments 000000001990 000000002015","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/ws.2020.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-202947","identifier":[{"id":"85082738359","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-80cb7d1d-a4ac-421b-9c86-a76888227ba9"],"keyword":["Agriculture","Groundwater age","Mini-catchments","Nitrogen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DB86A9D9C2FD88E19A2FD76098ECFEE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/ws.2020.002","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Catchment Science and Environmental Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"G.","key":"blichermathiesenpau","last":"Blicher-Mathiesen","locid":"c1194af9-f1ac-4cdb-9312-8696066200b9","name":"Blicher-Mathiesen, Gitte","name_org":"Blicher-Mathiesen, G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"windolfpau","last":"Windolf","locid":"04de6e58-b8ca-4a60-95e7-849dde928efb","name":"Windolf, Jørgen","name_org":"Windolf, J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S. E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","name_org":"Larsen, S. E.","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rolighedpau","last":"Rolighed","locid":"bdaf0e47-f2a1-4a23-a1da-d30cee160e19","name":"Rolighed, Jonas","name_org":"Rolighed, J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M. V.","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","locid":"142356a9-6bec-4f9d-a05d-2e144e4a792e","name":"Carstensen, Mette Vodder","name_org":"Carstensen, M. V.","orcid":"0000-0003-4882-9945","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A. L.","key":"højbergpau","last":"Højberg","name":"Højberg, A. L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H.","key":"tornbjergpau","last":"Tornbjerg","locid":"673f9989-b651-4f14-8190-b60c45f9cde2","name":"Tornbjerg, Henrik","name_org":"Tornbjerg, H.","orcid":"0009-0008-7385-7490","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"B.","key":"kronvangpau","last":"Kronvang","locid":"7766931c-a3c9-4a38-9d22-e4cc3a2f4607","name":"Kronvang, Brian","name_org":"Kronvang, B.","orcid":"0000-0003-1165-1354","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2166/ws.2020.002","issn":["16069749","16070798"],"issn_org":["16069749"],"issue":"2","journal":"Water Science and Technology: Water Supply","pages":"586-593","publisher":"IWA Publishing","publisher_org":"I W A Publishing","status":"p","title":"Water Science and Technology: Water Supply","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082738359"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-80cb7d1d-a4ac-421b-9c86-a76888227ba9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effect of nitrogen mitigation measures evaluated by monitoring of nitrogen concentrations and loadings in Danish mini-catchments - 1990-2015","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-202947","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Shigella, one of the most important foodborne pathogens, cause bacillary dysentery in humans. During the process, bacterial invasion and the subsequent proliferation in the cytosol of intestinal epithelium are necessary for the progress of infection. Recently, the glucose has been reported as the major nutrient for facilitating its intracellular proliferation, and the excretion of acetate was the main metabolite during the metabolism. However, the extensive analysis of the intracellular glucose utilization still needs to be established. 1H-NMR was used for analyzing 13C-glucose-derived metabolites from the mid-log cultured Shigella, non-infected HeLa, and Shigella-infected HeLa cells. Then, the effects of the three major metabolites from our analysis, acetate, lactate, and formate on Shigella infection have been evaluated. Our 1H-NMR spectra showed that 13C-EtOH, 13C-acetate, and 13C-formate were the main metabolites from the mid-log cultured Shigella. Also in the infection assay, these metabolites dominated the carbon flux from glucose together with 13C-lactate generated by the HeLa cells. However, the 13C-formate and 13C-EtOH production were terminated when Shigella invaded into HeLa cells whereas 13C-acetate production continued. We tested the ability of acetate, lactate, and formate to attenuate infection. A significant decrease in infection rate was obtained when HeLa cells were pretreated with formate. Contrarily, acetate pretreatment on HeLa cells resulted in an increased infection rate. Our data firstly described that the main metabolites, acetate, EtOH and formate are potential good biomarkers for intracellular Shigella metabolism since HeLa cells essentially do not produce these. Observed changes in the ratio between these metabolites indicate that the fermentation pathway used by Shigella during intracellular proliferation compared to ex vivo conditions changed. Especially formate production was found to be sensitive to the environment of the Shigella proliferation. While formate has been shown in literature to increase Shigella virulence we additionally observed that it also increases the ability of HeLa cells to withstand infection. Formate metabolism thus candidate for further investigations to understand it’s complex role in pathogenesis. We think that detailed understanding of the intracellular lifestyle of bacterial pathogens is an alternative way for developing new therapeutic strategies adressing the increasing issue of antibiotics resistance of Shigella infection.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Ke-Chuan","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Yigit, Demet","Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-304649"],"event":{"end":"2020-08-17","place":"Chicago, us","start":"2020-06-22","title":"ASM Microbe 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the analysis of the glucose derived metabolites from i shigella i and its host cells by sup 000000000001 sup h nmr for resolving the metabolic riddles during the infectious process","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/236588736/Abstract_for_ASM_2020_Chicago_conference.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-304649","ids":["dtu-0074395c-808a-48d3-8d7b-4f29e272a31c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B316D9FE6F3A7639418C20BA760E1CB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/236588736/Abstract_for_ASM_2020_Chicago_conference.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ke-Chuan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"c0762931-9826-44a5-ad31-c2bc1de6b709","name":"Wang, Ke-Chuan","orcid":"0000-0001-7423-7738","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Demet","key":"yigitpau","last":"Yigit","locid":"a0ba8b00-22cd-430d-9d01-9358364c663f","name":"Yigit, Demet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Rose","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"945cf0b9-5a16-4e82-a927-c9c42c2467b2","name":"Jensen, Pernille Rose","orcid":"0000-0003-4359-848X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0074395c-808a-48d3-8d7b-4f29e272a31c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The analysis of the glucose-derived metabolites from <i>Shigella </i>and its host cells by <sup>1</sup>H-NMR for resolving the metabolic riddles during the infectious process","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-304649","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Metabolic fingerprinting is a strong tool for characterization of biological phenotypes. Classification with machine learning is a critical component in the discrimination of molecular determinants. Cellular activity can be traced using stable isotope labelling of metabolites from which information on cellular pathways may be obtained. Nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy is, due to its ability to trace labelling in specific atom positions, a method of choice for such metabolic activity measurements. In this study, we used hyperpolarization in the form of dissolution Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (dDNP) NMR to measure signal enhanced isotope labelled metabolites reporting on pathway activity from four different prostate cancer cell lines. The spectra have a high signal-to-noise, with less than 30 signals reporting on 10 metabolic reactions. This allows easy extraction and straightforward interpretation of spectral data. Four metabolite signals selected using a Random Forest algorithm allowed a classification with Support Vector Machines between aggressive and indolent cancer cells with 96.9% accuracy, -corresponding to 31 out of 32 samples. This demonstrates that the information contained in the few features measured with dDNP NMR, is sufficient and robust for performing binary classification based on the metabolic activity of cultured prostate cancer cells.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Frahm, Anne Birk","Jensen, Pernille Rose","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Yigit, Demet","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319849"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lerche, Mathilde Hauge"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","Nuclear magnetic resonance","Random forest","Support vector machine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stable isotope resolved metabolomics classification of prostate cancer cells using hyperpolarized nmr data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/221998008/Frahm_test.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors gratefully acknowledge funding by the Danish National Research Foundation (Grant DNRF124 ) and the work of Emma Lundsgaard and Amalia Matei in the initial part of the statistical analysis for selection of relevant tools. The NMR center at DTU is acknowledged for the 1 H 1D Spectra acquired on their 800 MHz Avance II NMR spectrometer."],"id":"S01-000.00-319849","identifier":[{"id":"32480236","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085274957","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-334f6611-c133-405c-b3c0-f5b82b50b967"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","Nuclear magnetic resonance","Random forest","Stable isotope resolved metabolomics","Support vector machine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB0A959F4F4C4063F364C2160D899351"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/221998008/Frahm_test.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Birk","key":"frahmpau","last":"Frahm","locid":"e1c57a75-5e33-408f-b05d-077262dafeb4","name":"Frahm, Anne Birk","orcid":"0000-0001-6909-9369","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Rose","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"945cf0b9-5a16-4e82-a927-c9c42c2467b2","name":"Jensen, Pernille Rose","orcid":"0000-0003-4359-848X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Demet","key":"yigitpau","last":"Yigit","locid":"a0ba8b00-22cd-430d-9d01-9358364c663f","name":"Yigit, Demet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32480236"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2020.106750","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","paperid":"106750","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"316"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085274957"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-334f6611-c133-405c-b3c0-f5b82b50b967"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Stable isotope resolved metabolomics classification of prostate cancer cells using hyperpolarized NMR data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319849","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Communication networks are not only important to society, they also consume a lot of energy. Recent years research has focused on Cloud-Radio Access Network (C-RAN) to decrease the energy consumption of mobile networks. Hence, this work investigates how to lower the energy consumption in the fronthaul network by choosing the right C-RAN functional split and the right type of fronthaul network. Different functional splits assign different loads to the fronthaul network, and this work considers how much impact the data load has on the fronthaul network’s energy consumption. At the same time different types of fronthaul network impact the energy consumption in different ways. The paper provides models to be used for calculating the energy consumption in different network types and for the choice of different functional splits. Results show huge differences in energy consumption between especially wired and wireless technologies. Considering the same functional split, the difference between the most energy consuming transport technology and the least energy consuming is 99.5% for LTE and 99.6% for 5G. For the Ethernet overlay alone, the difference in energy consumption between the, with regard to energy consumption, best and worst case scenario is 99.3% per switch.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Berger, Michael Stübert","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-369778"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["5G","C RAN","Energy consumption","Ethernet","Fronthaul","Functional split","Green networking","PON","PTP"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy aware technology comparisons for 000000000005g mobile fronthaul networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/255196631/IARIA_journal_v5_camera_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-369778","ids":["dtu-da111d33-9dd0-4d42-aa3b-2de64944e8b3"],"keyword":["5G","C-RAN","CWDM","Energy consumption","Ethernet","Fronthaul","Functional split","Green networking","PON","PtP"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-04F197C49DA3665398BB48FF0865C6B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/255196631/IARIA_journal_v5_camera_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria Pyndt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"f3aec174-d663-4d97-aaa0-81cd6f4493a9","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9558-3493","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19422644"],"issue":"1&2","journal":"International Journal On Advances in Networks and Services","pages":"21-32","publisher":"IARIA","status":"p","title":"International Journal On Advances in Networks and Services","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-da111d33-9dd0-4d42-aa3b-2de64944e8b3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Energy-Aware Technology Comparisons for 5G Mobile Fronthaul Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-369778","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The inconsistent link observed between salivary amylase gene copy number (AMY1 CN) and weight management is likely modified by diet and microbiome. Objective: Based on analysis of a previously published study, we investigated the hypothesis that interaction between diet, Prevotella-to-Bacteriodes ratio (P/B ratio), and AMY1 CN influence weight change. Methods: Sixty-two people with increased waist circumference were randomly assigned to receive an ad libitum New Nordic Diet (NND) high in dietary fiber, whole grain, intrinsic sugars, and starch or an Average Danish (Western) Diet (ADD) for 26 weeks. All foods were provided free of charge. Before subjects were randomly assigned to receive the NND or ADD diet, blood and fecal samples were collected, from which AMY1 CN and P/B ratio, respectively, were determined. Body weight change was described by using linear mixed models, including biomarker [log10(P/B ratio) and/or AMY1 CN] diet-group interactions. Results: Baseline means ± SDs of log10(P/B ratio) and AMY1 CN were -2.1 ± 1.8 and 6.6 ± 2.4, respectively. Baseline P/B ratio predicted a 0.99-kg/unit (95% CI: 0.40, 1.57; n = 54; P < 0.001) higher weight loss for those subjects on the NND compared with those on the ADD diet, whereas AMY1 CN was not found to predict weight loss differences between the NND and ADD groups [0.05 kg/CN (95% CI: -0.40, 0.51; n = 54; P = 0.83)]. However, among subjects with low AMY1 CN (<6.5 copies), baseline P/B ratio predicted a 2.12-kg/unit (95% CI: 1.37, 2.88; n = 30; P < 0.001) higher weight loss for the NND group than the ADD group. No such differences in weight loss were found among subjects in both groups with high AMY1 CN [-0.17 kg/unit (95% CI: -1.01, 0.66; n = 24; P = 0.68)]. Conclusions: The combined use of low AMY1 CN and pretreatment P/B ratio for weight loss prediction led to highly individualized weight loss results with the introduction of more fiber, whole grain, intrinsic sugars, and starch in the diet. These preliminary observations suggest that more undigested starch reaches the colon in individuals with low AMY1 CN, and that the fate of this starch depends on the gut microbiota composition. This trial was registered at clinicaltrials.gov as NCT01195610.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Christensen, Lars","Larsen, Thomas Meinert","Roager, Henrik Munch","Krych, Lukasz","Kot, Witold","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Ritz, Christian","Astrup, Arne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Amylase","Enterotypes","Faculty of Science","GENES","Health","Microbiota","Prevotella","WEIGHT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pretreatment i prevotella i to i bacteroides i ratio and salivary amylase gene copy number as prognostic markers for dietary weight loss","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-412735","identifier":[{"id":"85087434784","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32034403","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-205ed5ce-5ca4-4b68-894f-a6546dae5c86"],"keyword":["Amylase","Enterotypes","Faculty of Science","Genes","Health","Microbiota","Prevotella","Weight"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF21148B454236BE7B4FEE55FF3CFB1A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Fiil","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"00918fa0-7b1e-4128-919e-a0af9497026b","name":"Hjorth, Mads Fiil","orcid":"0000-0001-9440-2737","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"d87ec11e-b7a7-481a-a376-8e7a1c56dc81","name":"Christensen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-2251-6713","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Meinert","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"be620f10-2a0e-430c-94d1-5246c8ef122a","name":"Larsen, Thomas Meinert","orcid":"0000-0001-7621-3131","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Munch","key":"roagerpau","last":"Roager","locid":"14e7430e-c904-4824-a35f-4b142c67dae4","name":"Roager, Henrik Munch","orcid":"0000-0002-2504-8313","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lukasz","key":"krychpau","last":"Krych","locid":"a9463259-048d-4fd6-8218-dde9fb94c96b","name":"Krych, Lukasz","orcid":"0000-0003-3224-1346","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Witold","key":"kotpau","last":"Kot","locid":"89d6e892-d0a3-40c3-a7f5-7052029eeb1b","name":"Kot, Witold","orcid":"0000-0002-0188-4587","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","locid":"c881424f-d529-443e-b60e-bc2edb674ede","name":"Ritz, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5095-0624","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32034403"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ajcn/nqaa007","issn":["00029165","19383207"],"issn_org":["00029165"],"issue":"5","journal":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","pages":"1079-1086","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087434784"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-205ed5ce-5ca4-4b68-894f-a6546dae5c86"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pretreatment <i>Prevotella</i>-to-<i>Bacteroides</i> ratio and salivary amylase gene copy number as prognostic markers for dietary weight loss","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412735","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The article argues that the view of theories as constitutive of their object of study is usefulfor reflecting on the role of theories in the analysis of European foreign policy. A key concept used to study the constitutive role of theories is performativity (Derrida, 1988). The article illustrates its relevance through a study of the use of the concept “Capability-Expectations Gap”. On the basis of this study, the article also makes the point that, contrary to Cebeci´s (2012) argument, research on European foreign policy does not unambiguously construct the EU as an `Ideal Power Europe’ (of which Normative Power Europe is a part) as the use of the Capability-Expectations Gap concept does not draw on the ”Ideal Power Europe” discourse. The concept is mainly used as a critical label to describe EU foreign policy and applications of the concept end up by concluding that the EU is an international actor with quasi-permanent shortcomings.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477049"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"normative power europe or capability expectations gap the performativity of concepts in the study of european foreign policy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/285718553/JCMS_12998.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-477049","identifier":[{"id":"85078732768","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8bdb30bb-8388-4290-bedb-ccfd545dd38a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FF4CD7FB9301C05ED1642E326649085"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/285718553/JCMS_12998.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, International Relations"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jcms.12998","issn":["00219886","14685965"],"issn_org":["00219886"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Common Market Studies","pages":"962-977","status":"p","title":"Journal of Common Market Studies","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078732768"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8bdb30bb-8388-4290-bedb-ccfd545dd38a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Normative Power Europe or Capability-Expectations Gap? : The Performativity of Concepts in the Study of European Foreign Policy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477049","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Libraries, archives and museums have traditionally been a part of the public sphere's infrastructure. They have been so by providing public access to culture and knowledge, by being agents for enlightenment and by being public meeting places in their communities. Digitization and globalization poses new challenges in relation to upholding a sustainable public sphere. Can libraries, archives and museums contribute in meeting these challenges?","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jochumsen, Henrik","Audunson, Ragnar","Andresen, Herbjørn","Fagerlid, Cicilie","Henningsen, Erik","Hobohm, Hans-Christoph","Larsen, Håkon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-484350"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oslo Metropolitan University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physical places and virtual spaces libraries archives and museums in a digital age","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-484350","ids":["ku-9819ecc3-a2b3-4715-b399-955a7f3243f8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-08DD4257AB76E4696EF12DFB2395645F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"oslo metropolitan university","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo Metropolitan Univer