{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate sex differences in associations between attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) and a spectrum of comorbid disorders. METHOD: The study population included all children born in Denmark between 1981 and 2013 (N=1,665,729). We merged data from Danish registers and obtained information on birth characteristics, socioeconomic status, familial psychiatric history, and diagnoses of ADHD (n=32,308) and comorbid disorders. In order to estimate absolute and relative risks of comorbid disorders, incidence rates (IRs) and adjusted hazard ratios (HRs) with 95% CIs were calculated for females and males. We also examined interactions between ADHD and sex in association with comorbid disorders - estimated as ratios of the hazard ratios (HRRs) in females and males (95% CIs). RESULTS: Individuals diagnosed with ADHD had significantly increased absolute and relative risks of all 12 comorbid psychiatric disorders investigated. For some comorbid disorders, we found ADHD-sex interactions. Compared to males, ADHD in females showed a stronger association with autism spectrum disorder (HRR=1.86; 95%CI 1.62-2.14), oppositional defiant/conduct disorder (HRR=1.97; 95%CI 1.68-2.30), intellectual disability (HRR=1.79; 95%CI 1.54-2.09), personality disorders (HRR=1.23; 95%CI 1.06-1.43), schizophrenia (HRR=1.21; 95%CI 1.02-1.43), substance use disorders (HRR=1.21; 95%CI 1.07-1.38), and suicidal behavior (1.28; 95%CI 1.12-1.47). The remaining disorders showed no significant sex differences in association with ADHD. CONCLUSION: This study indicates that the association between ADHD and several comorbid disorders is stronger in females than in males. These important findings add to the literature on sex differences in ADHD and suggest that females diagnosed with ADHD are a more vulnerable group of patients.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ottosen, Cæcilie","Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","Faraone, Stephen V","Chen, Qi","Hartman, Catharina","Larsson, Henrik","Petersen, Liselotte","Dalsgaard, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-191523"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","SUNY Upstate Medical University","Telemark Hospital Trust","University of Groningen","Örebro University"],"keyword":["ADHD","Comorbid disorders","Sex differences"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex differences in comorbidity patterns of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85063339757","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-191523","identifier":[{"id":"85063339757","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30768399","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6d0bb177-5d5f-4248-8b01-2f8379afa3ad"],"keyword":["ADHD","comorbid disorders","sex differences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E3F9F77C522B0A7C5305B745F4DA57D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - CIRRAU - Centre for Integrated Register-based Research","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - National Centre for Register-based Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-LUND","l3nn":"Lundbeck Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck Foundation","namevar":["iPSYCH -The Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-LUND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"suny upstate medical university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"SUNY Upstate Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"örebro university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Örebro University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"no","key":"telemark hospital trust","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Telemark Hospital Trust","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie","key":"ottosenpau","last":"Ottosen","locid":"08323744-03fa-4499-9eb7-f8e857d6c67e","name":"Ottosen, Cæcilie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janne Tidselbak","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5e35426b-5cd7-438a-a11a-bfd44f63fbdf","name":"Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","orcid":"0000-0002-0385-1017","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephen V","key":"faraonepau","last":"Faraone","name":"Faraone, Stephen V","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Qi","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Qi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Catharina","key":"hartmanpau","last":"Hartman","name":"Hartman, Catharina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","name":"Larsson, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liselotte","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ba9cb39d-0fd4-4e02-94fc-ce861a4b6d62","name":"Petersen, Liselotte","orcid":"0000-0002-0479-5379","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"9da04734-659f-4d4e-bae8-a6ca57c22f05","name":"Dalsgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-4659-0969","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30768399"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jaac.2018.07.910","issn":["08908567","15275418"],"issn_org":["08908567"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of the American Academy of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Academy of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063339757"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6d0bb177-5d5f-4248-8b01-2f8379afa3ad"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Sex Differences in Comorbidity Patterns of Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-191523","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Hverdagens superhelte, som leverer sublime arbejdspræstationer, bliver forbigået på grund af myter og misforståelser om talentudvikling. Læs, hvad du skal være opmærksom på for at undgå at falde i en af de fem faldgruber.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mogensen, Lilian","Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-278739"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000005 faldgruber i talentudvikling","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/5-faldgruber-i-talentudvikling-og-5-maader-du-kan-undgaa-dem/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-278739","ids":["cbs-2388b8a2-3f32-47ab-9f81-4ea47f88e880"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-77EB5B46D3B46467CEFD24F8D545F58F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/5-faldgruber-i-talentudvikling-og-5-maader-du-kan-undgaa-dem/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lilian","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","name":"Mogensen, Lilian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-2388b8a2-3f32-47ab-9f81-4ea47f88e880"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"5 faldgruber i talentudvikling","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-278739","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We show that the trityl electron spin resonance (ESR) features, crucial for an efficient dynamic nuclear polarization (DNP) process, are sample-composition-dependent. Working at 6.7 T and 1.1 K with a generally applicable DNP sample solvent mixture such as water/glycerol plus trityl, the addition of Gd3+ leads to a dramatic increase in [U-13C] glucose polarization from 37 ± 4% to 69 ± 3%. This is the highest value reported to date and is comparable to what can be achieved on pyruvic acid. Moreover, performing ESR measurements under actual DNP conditions, we provide experimental evidence that gadolinium doping not only shortens the trityl electron spin-lattice relaxation time but also modifies the radical g-tensor. The latter yielded a considerable narrowing of the ESR spectrum line width. Finally, in the frame of the spin temperature theory, we discuss how these two phenomena affect the DNP performance.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Capozzi, Andrea","Patel, Saket","Wenckebach, W. Thomas","Karlsson, Magnus","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-328076"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Capozzi, Andrea"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paul Scherrer Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gadolinium effect at high magnetic field dnp 000000000070 sup 000000000013 sup c polarization of u sup 000000000013 sup c glucose using trityl","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/181971877/JPCL_Gd_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-328076","identifier":[{"id":"85067641811","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31181932","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-4f069433-31f2-4b78-9181-d7c98140e1af"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83ACB91F41ABFE0DD8A27BDA65DA7305"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/181971877/JPCL_Gd_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"paul scherrer institute","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Paul Scherrer Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"capozzipau","last":"Capozzi","locid":"b0cf62b2-059b-44b4-bcf7-c10bdbeda7b9","name":"Capozzi, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-2306-9049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saket","key":"patelpau","last":"Patel","locid":"d95a24de-cc76-438a-8227-491bb521eb4c","name":"Patel, Saket","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-3326","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"W. Thomas","key":"wenckebachpau","last":"Wenckebach","name":"Wenckebach, W. Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde H.","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","name_org":"Lerche, Mathilde H.","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31181932"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01306","issn":["19487185"],"journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry Letters","pages":"3420-3425","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry Letters","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067641811"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4f069433-31f2-4b78-9181-d7c98140e1af"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Gadolinium Effect at High-Magnetic-Field DNP: 70% <sup>13</sup>C Polarization of [U-<sup>13</sup>C] Glucose Using Trityl","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-328076","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Transmembrane flux of Cs+ (a K+ congener) was measured in human red blood cells (RBCs; erythrocytes) on the 10-s time scale. This is the first report on dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy with this nuclide in mammalian cells. Four technical developments regularized sample delivery and led to high quality NMR spectra. Cation-free media with the Piezo1 (mechanosensitive cation channel) activator yoda1 maximized the extent of membrane transport. First-order rate constants describing the fluxes were estimated using a combination of statistical methods in Mathematica, including the Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm. Fluxes were in the range 4–70 μmol Cs+ (L RBC)−1 s−1; these are smaller than for urea, but comparable to glucose. Methodology and analytical procedures developed will be applicable to transmembrane cation transport studies in the presence of additional Piezo1 effectors, to other cellular systems, and potentially in vivo.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kuchel, Philip William","Karlsson, Magnus","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Shishmarev, Dmitry","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340252"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Kuchel, Philip William"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rapid zero trans kinetics of cs exchange in human erythrocytes quantified by dissolution hyperpolarized sup 000000000133 sup cs nmr spectroscopy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-56250-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340252","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6928147","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31873230","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85077038758","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-777fcec0-fc74-4500-b6e8-6ff41ebdad4e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-98AE2DEB9B3DB11A70D05FB5E0F40735"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/205590914/s41598_019_56250_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-56250-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"australian national university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Australian National University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip William","key":"kuchelpau","last":"Kuchel","locid":"22791846-af6f-46cb-b5ae-97c7924b03d9","name":"Kuchel, Philip William","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dmitry","key":"shishmarevpau","last":"Shishmarev","name":"Shishmarev, Dmitry","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31873230"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-019-56250-z","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"19726","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077038758"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-777fcec0-fc74-4500-b6e8-6ff41ebdad4e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Rapid zero-trans kinetics of Cs+ exchange in human erythrocytes quantified by dissolution hyperpolarized <sup>133</sup>Cs+ NMR spectroscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340252","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Dissolution DNP has emerged as a technique to improve SNR in an NMR experiment with inherent limitation of polarization retention in solution ranging, in general, from 30 to 100 s for the interesting bio-molecules. The limitation in sensitivity and available time window can be, however, improved by a better SNR of the RF receivers. At 3 T the Larmor frequency of the 13C nuclei is 32.13 MHz, which is still in the electronics noise dominated regime for smaller coils. A High-Temperature Superconducting (HTS) receiver coil with high-Q, remotely tunable, detunable and compatible to standard electronics Tin soldering has been developed for MRI 13C applications.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Baron, Rafael Antonio","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341052"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-16","place":"Montréal, ca","start":"2019-05-11","title":"ISMRM 27th Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high q tunable high temperature superconducting receiver coil for sup 000000000013 sup c applications","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/181826706/ISMRM2019_1487.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-341052","ids":["dtu-7a3a3be4-9d87-46d2-897a-c6d5eed3c6bb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FE9F65488A6F940682DAA1856989E301"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/181826706/ISMRM2019_1487.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rafael Antonio","key":"baronpau","last":"Baron","locid":"16ea55c1-2461-438e-abbe-a63d4b3144b6","name":"Baron, Rafael Antonio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7a3a3be4-9d87-46d2-897a-c6d5eed3c6bb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"High-Q, tunable High Temperature Superconducting receiver coil for <sup>13</sup>C applications","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-341052","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The hydrogenation of alkynes and alkenes using a Shrock-Osborn catalysts was followed in-situ with dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) NMR. Natural abundance and 13C labeled dimethyl acetylenedicarboxylate was hyperpolarized prior to hydrogenation using (1,4-bis{diphenylphosphino}butane)(2,5-norbornadiene) rhodium(I) perchlorate, [Rh(NBD)(DPPB)]ClO4. The increased signal-to-noise ratio of dDNP compared to conventional 13C NMR allowed real-time detection of substrate and products as well as the modeling of the hydrogenation kinetics. The build-up of an intermediate was observed during interruption in hydrogen flow, substantiating the current view of the reaction mechanism. Selective inversion of the carbonyl NMR signal of the substrate was applied to demonstrate unequivocally that the new peak appearing in the spectrum originates from a reaction intermediate. The scope of the dDNP method for following reaction dynamics in real time was further demonstrated by substrate competition experiments.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Boeg, Peter Andreas","Duus, Jens Øllgaard","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Karlsson, Magnus","Mossin, Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352723"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mossin, Susanne"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real time detection of intermediates in rhodium catalyzed hydrogenation of alkynes and alkenes by dissolution dnp","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/171226888/acs.jpcc.9b01376.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352723","identifier":[{"id":"85064701389","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a1561329-401c-4779-8999-1ceec81e81fe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F977424CDE4413A7371F12394B03A8C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/171226888/acs.jpcc.9b01376.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Andreas","key":"boegpau","last":"Boeg","locid":"b4f910e2-ca25-4263-918a-b2890a1f8432","name":"Boeg, Peter Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-6696-5281","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Øllgaard","key":"duuspau","last":"Duus","locid":"4317dfee-5351-4137-a6e2-c82bd6a3d0bf","name":"Duus, Jens Øllgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3625-1250","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne","key":"mossinpau","last":"Mossin","locid":"0eb59f32-26b3-4799-a810-07608783b9cb","name":"Mossin, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0001-7763-9660","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpcc.9b01376","issn":["19327447","19327455"],"issn_org":["19327447"],"issue":"15","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","pages":"9949-9956","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","title_org":"The Journal of Physical Chemistry Part C","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064701389"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a1561329-401c-4779-8999-1ceec81e81fe"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Real-Time Detection of Intermediates in Rhodium Catalyzed Hydrogenation of Alkynes and Alkenes by Dissolution DNP","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352723","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The aim of this study was to compare the efficacy and tolerability of BP-C1 vs equallooking placebo in metastatic breast cancer. Materials and methods: A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled multi-center study with a semicross-over design was performed. Sixteen patients received daily intramuscular injection of 0.035 mg/kg bodyweight of BP-C1 and 15 patients received equal-looking placebo for 32 days. After 32 days, the placebo patients crossed to BP-C1 with the last observation in the placebo period as baseline. The status of receptors including estrogen receptor (ER), progesterone receptor (PtR), and human EGF receptor 2 (HER2) was analyzed prior to inclusion in the study. Thoracoabdominal CT scan was blindly analyzed by the same independent radiologist in accordance with the RECIST criteria 1.1. Toxicity was assessed according to the NCI Bethesda Version 2.0 (CTC-NCI), and the quality of life (QOL) was assessed according to European Organization for the Research and Treatment of Cancer QOL-C30 and QOL-BR23. Results: The sum of target lesion diameters (sum lesions) after 32 days of treatment increased by 8.9% (P=0.08) in the BP-C1 arm compared to 37.6% (P<0.001) in placebo patients. Twelve of the 15 placebo patients subsequently had BP-C1 treatment. The increase in sum lesions was 3.5% in these patients. The sum of CTC-NCI was increased 18.7% in the BP-C1 arm (P=0.38) compared to 50.9% (P=0.04) in placebo patients. Four mild/moderate adverse events (AEs) present in BP-C1. Two mild/moderate AEs and one severe AE present in placebo. The QOL benchmarks “breast cancer problems last week”, “sexual interest and activity last 4 weeks”, and “breast cancer-related pain and discomfort last week” were stable in the BP-C1 arm but deteriorated in placebo patients. The sum lesions increased significantly in ER+ (P=0.02) and PtR+ (P=0.03) but not in HER2+. The increase in sum lesions significantly decreased (P=0.02) with an increasing number of negative receptors. Conclusion: A total of 32 days of BP-C1 treatment inhibited cancer growth and was well tolerated with few and mainly mild AEs. The efficacy of BP-C1 was superior in receptor-negative patients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Butthongkomvong, Kritiya","Raunroadroong, Nilubol","Sorrarichingchai, Sirikul","Sangsaikae, Isaraporn","Srimuninnimit, Vichien","Harling, Henrik","Larsen, Stig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417719"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Thailand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lampang Cancer Hospital","Mahidol University","Norwegian University of Life Sciences","Ubon Ratchathani Cancer Hospital","Udonthani Cancer Hospital"],"keyword":["Breast cancer","Hormone receptors","Stage IV"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy and tolerability of bp c000000000001 in metastatic breast cancer a phase ii randomized double blind and placebo controlled thai multi center study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/BCTT.S174298","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-417719","identifier":[{"id":"85072815144","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6336026","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30666153","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-28a01a0d-4092-4094-b906-8e8885e8b34b"],"keyword":["BP-C1","Benzene-polycarboxylic acid complex","Breast cancer","Hormone receptors","Low-dose cisplatin","Randomized double-blind","Stage IV"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-452F42C8DED4FE0F825E0446617C7732"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://d