{"abstract":"This study highlights the potential benefits of applying physico-mental strategies from the Japanese martial art Ki-aikido in the general approach to teaching and playing percussion instruments. Two groups of percussion students played an exercise on marimba before and after either a Ki-aikido or a control instruction. Between-group Fourier analyses were robust and showed a significant effect of the Ki-aikido intervention, indicated by a change in the harmonic distribution in the instrument’s timbre. By contrast, subjective ratings by marimba experts were less consistent and showed no effect of the intervention on any parameter. More research into the field is encouraged.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Knarborg Larsen, Henrik","Heggli, Ole Adrian","Petersen, Bjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-265732"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Sound quality","Spectral analysis","Timbre"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDAM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDAM","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"marimba mallet and mind enhancing the marimba sound by ki aikido approach","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85071316841","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-265732","identifier":[{"id":"85071316841","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000484633200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-eefdacfc-e457-4cf2-84ba-6da298e348ef"],"keyword":["Ki-aikido","Marimba","Marimba, Ki-aikido, timbre, sound quality, spectral analysis","sound quality","spectral analysis","timbre"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E4C617858A4B85B585B7B5166AB747AF"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"rdam the royal danish academy of music","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDAM","l3nn":"RDAM The Royal Danish Academy of Music","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RDAM The Royal Danish Academy of Music","namevar":["Royal Academy of Music"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDAM","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center for Music In the Brain"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"knarborglarsenpau","last":"Knarborg Larsen","name":"Knarborg Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Adrian","key":"hegglipau","last":"Heggli","locid":"7426c89c-fe52-4677-808f-b2c553878a1d","name":"Heggli, Ole Adrian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjørn","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"f659916d-2c46-4493-a63d-105d78541fb9","name":"Petersen, Bjørn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09298215.2019.1657465","issn":["09298215","17445027"],"issn_org":["09298215"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of New Music Research","pages":"469-478","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of New Music Research","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071316841"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eefdacfc-e457-4cf2-84ba-6da298e348ef"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Marimba, mallet and mind – enhancing the marimba sound by Ki-aikido approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-265732","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarized MR by dissolution Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (dDNP) appeared on the scene in 2003. Since then, it has been translated to the clinic and several sites are now conducting human studies. This has happened at record pace despite all its complexities. The method has reached a pivotal point, and the coming years will be critical in realizing its full potential. Though the field has been characterized by strong collaboration between academia, government and industry, the key message of this perspective paper is that accelerated consensus building is of the essence in fulfilling the original vision for the method and ensuring widespread adoption. The challenge is to gain acceptance among clinicians based on strong indications and clear evidence. The future appears bright; initial clinical data looks promising and the scope for improvement is significant.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305498"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"keyword":["Dissolution DNP","Hyperpolarization","hyperpolarized MR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized mr what s up doc","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/214119642/JMR_19_195.Rev.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-305498","identifier":[{"id":"85068790578","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31307893","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-03122675-6f5d-4929-8f81-ab3a1fa7c235"],"keyword":["Dissolution-DNP","Hyperpolarization","Hyperpolarized MR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39A97043148FCF6B77D522644A92B0B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/214119642/JMR_19_195.Rev.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan H.","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31307893"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2019.07.017","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","pages":"124-127","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"306"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068790578"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-03122675-6f5d-4929-8f81-ab3a1fa7c235"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Hyperpolarized MR – What's up Doc?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305498","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Designing custom coils for magnetic resonance systems, such as nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectrometers and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scanners, often entails using non-standard configurations of the transmit-receive (T/R) switch and Q-spoiling circuits. The built-in drivers of commercial NMR and MRI systems are, typically, only reconfigurable within a narrow application range (if at all). Thus, the built-in driver may not be able to properly control the custom T/R switches and Q-spoiling circuits when using custom built coils. We present a PIN diode driver which functions in both an MRI scanner and NMR spectrometer. The PIN diode driver is based on readily available discrete components and achieves switching times for the reverse and forward bias states (transmit on and off) of 2 Î¼s and 0.4 Î¼s respectively. Hence, this work enables a higher degree of customization of the RF switching circuits in an MR system and is potentially of interest for designers of custom coils for both NMR spectrometers and MRI scanners.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Albannay, Mohammed M.","Petersen, Jan Raagaard","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335944"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup"],"keyword":["Driver","MRI","NMR","Switch"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pin diode driver for nmr and mri","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/169037158/PIN_driver_manuscript_v2_0.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Danish National Research Foundation [ DNRF124 ]."],"id":"S01-000.00-335944","identifier":[{"id":"85061058683","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30738272","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-691caf0e-0e84-4e01-b31e-6b2a5c9f5522"],"keyword":["Active decoupling","Driver","MRI","NMR","PIN diode","Q-spoiling","Switch","TR switching"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A21D97F205AAED1D3F4FD6A59C0125EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/169037158/PIN_driver_manuscript_v2_0.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammed M.","key":"albannaypau","last":"Albannay","locid":"2cb48487-30c9-4d3e-81d8-52475a08025e","name":"Albannay, Mohammed M.","orcid":"0000-0002-6635-8844","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J. R.","key":"petersenpau","la