,"first":"Martin","key":"tholstrupmartinpau","last":"Tholstrup","name":"Tholstrup, Martin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Martin L.","key":"petersenmartinlpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Martin L.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Anders","key":"vestergaardjensenanderspau","last":"Vestergaard-Jensen","name":"Vestergaard-Jensen, Anders","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Simon Auken","key":"becksimonaukenpau","last":"Beck","name":"Beck, Simon Auken","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Rygg","key":"klaumannjakobryggpau","last":"Klaumann","name":"Klaumann, Jakob Rygg","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Peder","key":"fynholmpederpau","last":"Fynholm","name":"Fynholm, Peder","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01056220"],"newspaper":"Ingenioeren","status":"p","title":"Ingenioeren","title_org":"Ingeniøren"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","GTS Institutes","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","c.f. møller a/s (biz)","dansk træforening (biz)","moe rådgivende ingeniører","rambøll","tegnestuen vandkunsten","træinformation"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-250929aa-0517-4806-aca0-a9c155992024"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Kronik : Hvem uddanner ingeniører til at bygge med træ?","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415546","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Staphylococcus argenteus and Staphylococcus schweitzeri, previously known as divergent Staphylococcus aureus clonal lineages, have been recently established as novel, difficult-to-delimit, coagulase-positive species within the S. aureus complex. Methicillin-resistant strains of S. argenteus are known from Australia and the UK. Knowledge of their epidemiology, medical significance and transmission risk is limited and partly contradictory, hampering definitive recommendations. There is mounting evidence that the pathogenicity of S. argenteus is similar to that of ‘classical’ S. aureus, while as yet no S. schweitzeri infections have been reported. Aim: To provide decision support on whether and how to distinguish and report both species. Sources: PubMed, searched for S. argenteus and S. schweitzeri. Content: This position paper reviews the main characteristics of both species and draws conclusions for microbiological diagnostics and surveillance as well as infection prevention and control measures. Implications: We propose not distinguishing within the S. aureus complex for routine reporting purposes until there is evidence that pathogenicity or clinical outcome differ markedly between the different species. Primarily for research purposes, suitably equipped laboratories are encouraged to differentiate between S. argenteus and S. schweitzeri. Caution is urged if these novel species are explicitly reported. In such cases, a specific comment should be added (i.e. ‘member of the S.aureus complex’) to prevent confusion with less- or non-pathogenic staphylococci. Prioritizing aspects of patient safety, methicillin-resistant isolates should be handled as recommended for methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA). In these cases, the clinician responsible should be directly contacted and informed by the diagnosing microbiological laboratory, as they would be for MRSA. Research is warranted to clarify the epidemiology, clinical impact and implications for infection control of such isolates.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Becker, K.","Schaumburg, F.","Kearns, A.","Larsen, A. R.","Lindsay, J. A.","Skov, R. L.","Westh, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527078"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Public Health England","St. George's University of London","University of Münster"],"keyword":["Diagnostics","Epidemiology","Infection control","MRSA","Pathogenicity","Prevention","Recommendation","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implications of identifying the recently defined members of the i staphylococcus aureus i complex i s argenteus i and i s schweitzeri i a position paper of members of the escmid study group for staphylococci and staphylococcal diseases esgs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-527078","identifier":[{"id":"85063439443","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30872103","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-dfb306fb-56b7-4972-8ac7-5116b7058ff3"],"keyword":["Diagnostics","Epidemiology","Infection control","MRSA","Pathogenicity","Prevention","Recommendation","Staphylococcus argenteus","Staphylococcus aureus","Staphylococcus schweitzeri"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6BD376926D5CCB658F7DF6D02C32A425"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of münster","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Münster","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"public health england","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Public Health England","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"st george s university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"St. George's University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Microbiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"K.","key":"beckerpau","last":"Becker","name":"Becker, K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"F.","key":"schaumburgpau","last":"Schaumburg","name":"Schaumburg, F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A.","key":"kearnspau","last":"Kearns","name":"Kearns, A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A. R.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, A. R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"J. A.","key":"lindsaypau","last":"Lindsay","name":"Lindsay, J. A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"R. L.","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, R. L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"H.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, H.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30872103"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cmi.2019.02.028","issn":["1198743X","14690691"],"issn_org":["1198743X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Clinical Microbiology and Infection","pages":"1064-1070","status":"p","title":"Clinical Microbiology and Infection","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063439443"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dfb306fb-56b7-4972-8ac7-5116b7058ff3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Implications of identifying the recently defined members of the <i>Staphylococcus aureus</i> complex <i>S. argenteus</i> and <i>S. schweitzeri</i> : a position paper of members of the ESCMID Study Group for Staphylococci and Staphylococcal Diseases (ESGS)","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527078","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Cationic polyplexes and lipoplexes are widely used as artificial systems for nucleic acid delivery into the cells, but they can also induce cell death. Mechanistic understanding of cell toxicity and biological side effects of these cationic entities is essential for optimization strategies and design of safe and efficient nucleic acid delivery systems. Numerous methods are presently available to detect and delineate cytotoxicity and cell death-mediated signals in cell cultures. Activation of caspases is part of the classical apoptosis program and increased caspase activity is therefore a well-established hallmark of programmed cell death. Additional methods to monitor cell-death related signals must, however, also be carried out to fully define the type of cell toxicity in play. These may include methods that detect plasma membrane damage, loss of mitochondrial membrane potential, phosphatidylserine exposure, and cell morphological changes (e.g., membrane blebbing, nuclear changes, cytoplasmic swelling, cell rounding). Here we describe a 96-well format protocol for detection of caspase-3/7 activity in cell lysates, based on a fluorescent caspase-3 assay, combined with a method to simultaneously determine relative protein contents in the individual wells.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Anna K","Hall, Arnaldur","Lundsgart, Henrik","Moghimi, S Moein"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530496"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Newcastle"],"keyword":["Apoptosis drug effects","Caspase 3 metabolism","Fluorescent Dyes chemistry","Fluorometry methods","Humans","Jurkat Cells","Nucleic Acids genetics","Polyamines toxicity","Toxicity Tests methods","Transfection methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combined fluorimetric caspase 000000000003 000000000007 assay and bradford protein determination for assessment of polycation mediated cytotoxicity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-530496","identifier":[{"id":"30838624","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85062603114","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e584e343-f800-49fb-9c42-0742a11fc62c"],"keyword":["Apoptosis/drug effects","Caspase 3/metabolism","Caspase 7/metabolism","Fluorescent Dyes/chemistry","Fluorometry/methods","Humans","Jurkat Cells","Nucleic Acids/genetics","Polyamines/toxicity","Toxicity Tests/methods","Transfection/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-4-468A5EBBD4CE46A382E5A7246B8BE68A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of newcastle","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Newcastle","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna K","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"af9425e1-1c4f-4a75-845c-aec8e3d1d60f","name":"Larsen, Anna K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Arnaldur","key":"hallpau","last":"Hall","name":"Hall, Arnaldur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"lundsgartpau","last":"Lundsgart","name":"Lundsgart, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"S Moein","key":"moghimipau","last":"Moghimi","name":"Moghimi, S Moein","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30838624"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-4939-9092-4_19","isbn":["9781493990917"],"issn":["10643745"],"pages":"301-311","series":"Methods in molecular biology","status":"p","title":"Nanotechnology for Nucleic Acid Delivery","volume":"1943"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062603114"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e584e343-f800-49fb-9c42-0742a11fc62c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combined Fluorimetric Caspase-3/7 Assay and Bradford Protein Determination for Assessment of Polycation-Mediated Cytotoxicity","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-530496","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This book constitutes the refereed proceedings of the 13th International Conference on Flexible Query Answering Systems, FQAS 2019, held in Amantea, Italy, in July 2019. The 27 full papers and 10 short papers presented were carefully reviewed and selected from 43 submissions. The papers present emerging research trends with a special focus on flexible querying and analytics for smart cities and smart societies in the age of big data. They are organized in the following topical sections: flexible database management and querying; ontologies and knowledge bases; social networks and social media; argumentation-based query answering; data mining and knowledge discovery; advanced flexible query answering methodologies and techniques; flexible query answering methods and techniques; flexible intelligent information-oriented and network-oriented approaches; big data veracity and soft computing; flexibility in tools; and systems and miscellanea.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Cuzzocrea, Alfredo","Greco, Sergio","Legind Larsen, Henrik","Sacca, Domenico","Andreasen, Troels","Christiansen, Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-572513"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Mediterranea of Reggio Calabria"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flexible query answering systems 000000000013th international conference fqas 000000002019 amantea italy july 000000000002 000000000005 000000002019 proceedings","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-572513","ids":["ruc-f5640bb0-9dda-46da-81f1-0c13e84dd927"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-87B8B13152BC1416DE8689D90D75E22F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university mediterranea of reggio calabria","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Mediterranea of Reggio Calabria","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Communication and Arts, Experience Lab","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Programming, Logic and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alfredo","key":"cuzzocreaped","last":"Cuzzocrea","name":"Cuzzocrea, Alfredo","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sergio","key":"grecoped","last":"Greco","name":"Greco, Sergio","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"legindlarsenped","last":"Legind Larsen","name":"Legind Larsen, Henrik","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","first":"Domenico","key":"saccaped","last":"Sacca","name":"Sacca, Domenico","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"andreasenped","last":"Andreasen","locid":"f31701bc-1bef-45ac-b9fa-3e931672bcd4","name":"Andreasen, Troels","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"christiansenped","last":"Christiansen","locid":"d1d3d938-5986-4368-a6db-1e282e894268","name":"Christiansen, Henning","orcid":"0000-0003-4731-9927","rank":6,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-27629-4","isbn":["9783030276287"],"issn":["03029743"],"issue":"11529","pages":"414","publisher":"Springer","repno":"Lecture notes in artificial intelligence, No. 11529","series":"Lecture notes in artificial intelligence","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-f5640bb0-9dda-46da-81f1-0c13e84dd927"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Flexible Query Answering Systems : 13th International Conference, FQAS 2019, Amantea, Italy, July 2-5, 2019, Proceedings","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-572513","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Diseased, injured, or dysfunctional skeletal muscles may demonstrate abnormal function and contractility. Currently, only few in vivo imaging techniques are able to characterize the contractile properties of muscle tissue. This study aimed to test the hypothesis that muscle strain can be tracked in two upper extremity skeletal muscles by speckle-tracking ultrasonography (STU) and correlates with isometric muscle contractions. Methods: A convenience sample of 10 healthy, adult volunteers with normal shoulder function were tested. The 5 women and 5 men had a mean age of 45 years (range: 39-59 years) and BMI < 30. STU was applied to the supraspinatus (SS) and biceps brachii (BB) muscles using a M11 L-MHz linear transducer (frequency 8-15 MHz) hooked to a Vivid E 9TM ultrasound machine. Strain validation was performed by correlating peak strain against standardized sub-maximal, isometric load conditions of the two muscles (20-80% of maximal voluntary contraction) using a custom-built muscle dynamometer based on strain-gauge technique. Data were analyzed offline using the EchoPac speckle-tracking software and were blinded to the examiner. Results: Intramuscular strain measured by STU in the SS and BB muscles showed moderate to strong correlations with external muscle load (SS: r = - 0.76, p < 0.0001 and BB: r = - 0.60, p < 0.0001). We found strain to vary from approximately 10-20% during increasing submaximal, isometric conditions. Conclusions: We demonstrate that STU can be applied on healthy skeletal musculature (SS and BB muscles). The observed correlations between strain and isometric contractions suggest a valid technique. However, the concept of measuring muscle strain non-invasively needs further investigation for validity, accuracy, responsiveness, and reliability before its therapeutic and research potential can be realized.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Frich, Lars Henrik","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","Hjarbæk, John","Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-589542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frich, Lars Henrik"],"keyword":["Non invasive","Skeletal muscle","Speckle tracking","Strain","Ultrasonography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"musculoskeletal application and validation of speckle tracking ultrasonography","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-019-2562-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-589542","identifier":[{"id":"85065248964","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6499961","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31054565","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-391ec7c1-9476-4138-9522-5a0e6820ee31"],"keyword":["Non-invasive","Skeletal muscle","Speckle tracking","Strain","Ultrasonography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BFD13EE961398BEB2EB74E987FD6239E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-019-2562-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/150135957/Musculoskeletal_application_and_validation.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Henrik","key":"frichpau","last":"Frich","locid":"f5e4ebc5-0851-429f-ae70-b627b21b3d91","name":"Frich, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0147-4211","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kate Lykke","key":"lambertsenpau","last":"Lambertsen","locid":"d867cc02-bda7-455d-8d02-8b602e35e7b3","name":"Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","orcid":"0000-0001-9276-4902","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"hjarbækpau","last":"Hjarbæk","locid":"980308bb-c86b-484f-bafe-2d117034b9d6","name":"Hjarbæk, John","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jordi","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"fa82ce60-e408-4c0f-b013-151f87c6998c","name":"Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","name_org":"Dahl, Jordi","orcid":"0000-0002-8345-204X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Holsgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","name_org":"Larsen, Anders Holsgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31054565"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12891-019-2562-8","issn":["14712474"],"journal":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","paperid":"192","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065248964"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-391ec7c1-9476-4138-9522-5a0e6820ee31"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Musculoskeletal application and va