{"abstract":"Purpose: A novel dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) polarizer platform is presented. The polarizer meets a number of key requirements for in vitro, preclinical, and clinical applications. Method: It uses no liquid cryogens, operates in continuous mode, accommodates a wide range of sample sizes up to and including those required for human studies, and is fully automated. Results: It offers a wide operational window both in terms of magnetic field, up to 10.1 T, and temperature, from room temperature down to 1.3 K. The polarizer delivers a 13C liquid state polarization for [1-13C]pyruvate of 70%. The build-up time constant in the solid state is approximately 1200 s (20 minutes), allowing a sample throughput of at least one sample per hour including sample loading and dissolution. Conclusion: We confirm the previously reported strong field dependence in the range 3.35 to 6.7 T, but see no further increase in polarization when increasing the magnetic field strength to 10.1 T for [1-13C]pyruvate and trityl. Using a custom dry magnet, cold head and recondensing, closed-cycle cooling system, combined with a modular DNP probe, and automation and fluid handling systems, we have designed a unique dDNP system with unrivalled flexibility and performance.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Bowen, Sean","Petersen, Jan Raagaard","Rybalko, Oleksandr","Vinding, Mads Sloth","Ullisch, Marcus Görge","Nielsen, Niels Chr"],"cuid":["S02-099.48-027241"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","Merck"],"keyword":["Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","Dry magnet","Hyperpolarization","Polarizer","Resonance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cryogen free dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization polarizer operating at 000000000003 000000000035 t 000000000006 000000000070 t and 000000000010 000000000001 t","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/169040115/Cryogen_free_dissolution_dynamic_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Danish Council for Independent Research (1323‐00331B/00331A) and the Danish National Research Foundation (grant number DNRF124)"],"id":"S02-099.48-027241","identifier":[{"id":"000462091200059","type":"wos"},{"id":"85055416410","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30357898","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c8f2c373-9596-4dba-a535-f4af93b68ae5","dtu-a08d1489-1d4b-4266-b3c3-cb64db13e8fe"],"keyword":["RESONANCE","dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","dry magnet","hyperpolarization","polarizer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9D5356F69546D7F49D4282899B871808"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/158809932/arXiv.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/ftp/arxiv/papers/1808/1808.04870.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/169040115/Cryogen_free_dissolution_dynamic_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Center for Functionally Integrative Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sean","key":"bowenpau","last":"Bowen","locid":"77cc622d-d330-44a7-8947-f1463e9c8cef","name":"Bowen, Sean","orcid":"0000-0003-1047-4325","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Raagaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"bbaeda22-d4b8-4371-b87c-e76f77d54014","name":"Petersen, Jan Raagaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3194-5798","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oleksandr","key":"rybalkopau","last":"Rybalko","locid":"35007e3c-be65-457f-99ea-073043576468","name":"Rybalko, Oleksandr","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-6868","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Sloth","key":"vindingpau","last":"Vinding","locid":"79d8bdf1-5ea8-421e-a9b7-86f6a55b0b7f","name":"Vinding, Mads Sloth","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"ullischpau","last":"Ullisch","locid":"4250ce34-89f2-4a4c-8e20-da9b9a699c86","name":"Ullisch, Marcus Görge","name_org":"Ullisch, Marcus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Chr","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0d054b51-d357-4971-b459-6fa1d0d608f0","name":"Nielsen, Niels Chr","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30357898"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mrm.27537","issn":["07403194","15222594"],"issn_org":["07403194"],"issue":"3","journal":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","pages":"2184-2194","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance in Medicine","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055416410"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c8f2c373-9596-4dba-a535-f4af93b68ae5","dtu-a08d1489-1d4b-4266-b3c3-cb64db13e8fe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Cryogen-free dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization polarizer operating at 3.35 T, 6.70 T, and 10.1 T","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.48-027241","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Climate change may significantly impact the large number of households in developing countries depending on agricultural production, not least through changes in the frequency and/or magnitude of climatic hazards resulting in household income shocks. This paper analyses rural householdsâ€™ responses to past experiences of and future expectations to substantial and unexpected negative and positive agricultural income shocks. Empirical data is derived from an environmentally-augmented structured household (n = 112) survey in the high mountains of central Nepal. Multinomial logit regression, using data on rural household demographics, assets (agricultural land, livestock), value of other assets such as furniture, bicycles, and agricultural implements, and income sources showed that household coping choices are determined by opportunities to generate cash. We argue that public policies should enhance the ability of rural household to generate cash income, including through environmental products.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Møller, Lea Ravnkilde","Smith-Hall, Carsten","Meilby, Henrik","Rayamajhi, Santosh","Herslund, Lise Byskov","Larsen, Helle Overgaard","Nielsen, Øystein Juul","Byg, Anja"],"cuid":["S02-099.75-033629"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Smith-Hall, Carsten"],"country":["Nepal","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The James Hutton Institute","Tribhuvan University"],"keyword":["Coping","Development","Former LIFE faculty","Geography Planning and Development","Global and Planetary Change","Livelihoods","Nepal","Vulnerability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"empirically based analysis of households coping with unexpected shocks in the central himalayas","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85053518154","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.75-033629","identifier":[{"id":"85053518154","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2f22d387-71f4-45de-bd23-7445ffebc7c9","ku-e4984236-ac6a-4c41-b8f7-d1814eea0fdc"],"keyword":["Coping","Development","Former LIFE faculty","Geography, Planning and Development","Global and Planetary Change","Nepal","livelihoods","vulnerability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-94DBDEC4ACC5FB0B898A667F453F9CB2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Global Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"np","key":"tribhuvan university","loc":["Nepal","Asia, South"],"name":"Tribhuvan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":