 shifts and risk of injury among Danish hospital workers: A register-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.80-767660","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Current guidelines on the use of β-blockers in post-acute myocardial infarction (MI) patients without reduced left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) are based on studies before the implementation of modern reperfusion and secondary prevention therapies. It remains unknown whether β-blockers will reduce mortality and recurrent MI in contemporary revascularized post-MI patients without reduced LVEF. DESIGN: BETAMI is a prospective, randomized, open, blinded end point multicenter study in 10,000 MI patients designed to test the superiority of oral β-blocker therapy compared to no β-blocker therapy. Patients with LVEF ≥40% following treatment with percutaneous coronary intervention or thrombolysis and/or no clinical signs of heart failure are eligible to participate. The primary end point is a composite of all-cause mortality or recurrent MI obtained from national registries over a mean follow-up period of 3 years. Safety end points include rates of nonfatal MI, all-cause mortality, ventricular arrhythmias, and hospitalizations for heart failure obtained from hospital medical records 30 days after randomization, and from national registries after 6 and 18 months. Key secondary end points include recurrent MI, heart failure, cardiovascular and all-cause mortality, and clinical outcomes linked to β-blocker therapy including drug adherence, adverse effects, cardiovascular risk factors, psychosocial factors, and health economy. Statistical analyses will be conducted according to the intention-to-treat principle. A prespecified per-protocol analysis (patients truly on β-blockers or not) will also be conducted. CONCLUSIONS: The results from the BETAMI trial may have the potential of changing current clinical practice for treatment with β-blockers following MI in patients without reduced LVEF. EudraCT number 2018-000590-75.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Munkhaugen, John","Ruddox, Vidar","Halvorsen, Sigrun","Dammen, Toril","Fagerland, Morten W","Hernæs, Kjersti H","Vethe, Nils Tore","Prescott, Eva","Jensen, Svend Eggert","Rødevand, Olaf","Jortveit, Jarle","Bendz, Bjørn","Schirmer, Henrik","Køber, Lars","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Larsen, Alf Inge","Vikenes, Kjell","Steigen, Terje","Wiseth, Rune","Pedersen, Terje","Edvardsen, Thor","Otterstad, Jan Erik","Atar, Dan"],"cuid":["S03-099.81-009190"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hospital of Southern Norway","Oslo University Hospital","St. Olavs University Hospital (Trondheim)","Stavanger University Hospital","University Hospital of North Norway","University of Bergen","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"betablocker treatment after acute myocardial infarction in revascularized patients without reduced left ventricular ejection fraction betami rationale and design of a prospective randomized open blinded end point study","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ahj.2018.10.005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.81-009190","identifier":[{"id":"85057808059","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30530121","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-be70513e-9e81-44b3-8957-78e83d0904a2","au-c0cf0609-7990-4556-a93f-f3346fe7fecb","ku-721b6cf2-25ad-41ec-b440-9c6f0b2a8d63"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-1C18CB31A62BA2C72FF80BE8D9A9377F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files