{"abstract":"The field of Emergent Narrative in digital narrative studies has seen a lot of research since its inception in 1999, and a lot of it is helpful, but also there has been confusion in terms and a lack of focus on the specifics of how the narrative is shaped in the mind of the player. The term itself has been used to both describe the ensuing field, the concept, the process, and the resulting narrative experience. This paper aims to clarify these misunderstandings by investigating the field and defining the term “afterstory” to help solidify the relationship between the differing aspects of Emergent Narrative. Afterstory is specifically defined as the virtual, mental story that exists in the player’s mind after play and informed by the interactions and their perspective on them. Then, using previous work on retellings, the paper will relate afterstory to how people retell their afterstories, and what we can use those retellings for in relation to the system that helped form them. In conclusion, some examples will be brought forth that showcase the difficult nature of extrapolating a retelling’s quality to its interactive narrative system’s quality, but how it can still be done with careful, purposeful analysis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","Bruni, Luis Emilio","Schoenau-Fog, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102118"],"event":{"acronym":"ICIDS","end":"2019-11-23","place":"us","start":"2019-10-19","title":"International Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Bjarke Alexander"],"keyword":["Emergent narrative","Storyworld"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the story we cannot see on how a retelling relates to its afterstory","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85077715495&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-102118","identifier":[{"id":"85077715495","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b358d07d-be9a-49a1-b52a-b2bfb4a3b7dc"],"keyword":["Afterstory","Emergent Narrative","Emergent storytelling","Interactive Digital Narrative","Retelling","Storyworld"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-600B3A58843B21922F74F0B6B710F9E0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarke Alexander","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b20b35fc-c929-4058-a942-903b3772a4b1","name":"Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis Emilio","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"c7095325-82f2-4f1a-8e0e-703e01500273","name":"Bruni, Luis Emilio","orcid":"0000-0002-3019-5043","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schoenaufogpau","last":"Schoenau-Fog","locid":"34a35708-1cbb-4d3b-9b7c-53080126b5ef","name":"Schoenau-Fog, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-157X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rogelio E.","key":"cardonariverapedh","last":"Cardona-Rivera","name":"Cardona-Rivera, Rogelio E.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"R. Michael","key":"youngpedh","last":"Young","name":"Young, R. Michael","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"sullivanpedh","last":"Sullivan","name":"Sullivan, Anne","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-33894-7_21","eisbn":["9783030338947"],"isbn":["9783030338930"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"190-203","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"12th International Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling, ICIDS 2019, Little Cottonwood Canyon, UT, USA, November 19–22, 2019, Proceedings","title":"Interactive Storytelling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077715495"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b358d07d-be9a-49a1-b52a-b2bfb4a3b7dc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Story We Cannot See : On How a Retelling Relates to its Afterstory","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102118","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
