{"abstract":"We explore a new design approach for low frequency RF coils, where a transmit and receive array are built together in a totally rigid frame, and therefore their B and B distributions can be accurately mapped and used as prior information for SNR-optimal combination of signals from different coil elements. Using this principle, a coil is designed for C MRS of a pig at 3T (32.13 MHz). We show that at this frequency, the effect of sample loading is minimal, and the prior information obtained in phantoms benefits in-vivo experiments. This one-time calibration allows for optimal combination of coil signals, which is also expected to improve parallel imaging performance.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sanchez, Juan Diego","Hansen, Rie Beck","Baron, Rafael Antonio","Hansen, Esben S. Szocska","Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Laustsen, Christoffer","Hanson, Lars G.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309860"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-16","place":"Montréal, ca","start":"2019-05-11","title":"ISMRM 27th Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calibrated coil combination for fixed geometry low frequency coils with application to hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c measurements","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/179425204/1450_19.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309860","ids":["dtu-117c2d32-96b9-41bf-952c-c3feba88d672"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F21BBEA40AA7A737E6A96B2B5CE588E1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/179425204/1450_19.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezjuandiegopau","last":"Sánchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sánchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rie Beck","key":"hansenriebeckpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rafael Antonio","key":"baronrafaelantoniopau","last":"Baron","locid":"16ea55c1-2461-438e-abbe-a63d4b3144b6","name":"Baron, Rafael Antonio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben S. Szocska","key":"hansenesbensszocskapau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Esben S. Szocska","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansendanielhøjruppau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkovitaliypau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenchristofferpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars G.","key":"hansonlarsgpau","last":"Hanson","locid":"6c7cc6f9-5b6a-47dc-bb02-efe208e52f16","name":"Hanson, Lars G.","orcid":"0000-0002-8204-6912","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenjanhenrikpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-117c2d32-96b9-41bf-952c-c3feba88d672"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Calibrated Coil Combination for Fixed-Geometry, Low-Frequency Coils with Application to Hyperpolarized <sup>13</sup>C Measurements","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309860","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Several recent reports encourage targeting bacterial central metabolic pathways as a new strategy for antimicrobial drug discovery based on lessons learned from oncology and virus infection. The hitherto limited experimental evidence for the metabolic interference by intracellular bacteria in their host emphasizes the urgent need for enabling methodologies to study the metabolism of the bacterial pathogens in their target cells. Stable Isotope Resolved Analysis with Hyperpolarized NMR (SIRAH-NMR) is a new method providing metabolic fingerprint with few features and high contrast to noise. Here we use SIRAH-NMR to gain information on metabolic pathway utilization when the intracellular bacterial pathogen Shigella flexneri adapt to the intracellular lifestyle of the infected host cell. Distinct differences are observed from the host cell (HeLa) and the bacteria alone when [U-13C]glucose is used as substrate and the metabolic fingerprint is analyzed with SIRAH-NMR. Lactate and pyruvate are observed from the host cell whereas Shigella produces acetate and formate as main metabolites. Since there is no overlap between the metabolic fingerprint produced by HeLa and Shigella we use this method to investigate the metabolic cross-talk when HeLa cells are infected with Shigella (MOI=6). Under these conditions three of the four metabolites are observed. Lactate is unchanged which corresponds to unchanged flux through glycolysis of the HeLa cells while pyruvate is decreased and replaced by a similar amount of acetate -a metabolic product from Shigella. Formate is not observed in the infected cells. This indicates a different use of metabolic pathways in the bacteria when inside the host. SIRAH-NMR provides sensitivity and specificity to study and untangle the metabolic cross-talk between host cells and intra cellular pathogens in vivo.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Ke-Chuan","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Yigit, Demet","Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-321144"],"event":{"end":"2019-07-13","place":"Heidelberg, de","start":"2019-07-10","title":"EMBO New Approaches and Concepts in Microbiology 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"untangling metabolism between infected mammalian host cells and intracellular pathogen","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-321144","ids":["dtu-37bab559-a234-4e03-9d16-f3f6186b1558"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D7B2FB7C653311F122C785302075B9E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K.","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"c0762931-9826-44a5-ad31-c2bc1de6b709","name":"Wang, Ke-Chuan","name_org":"Wang, K.","orcid":"0000-0001-7423-7738","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.H.","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","name_org":"Lerche, M.H.","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.H.","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, J.H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"D.","key":"yigitpau","last":"Yigit","locid":"a0ba8b00-22cd-430d-9d01-9358364c663f","name":"Yigit, Demet","name_org":"Yigit, D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"P.R.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"945cf0b9-5a16-4e82-a927-c9c42c2467b2","name":"Jensen, Pernille Rose","name_org":"Jensen, P.R.","orcid":"0000-0003-4359-848X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-37bab559-a234-4e03-9d16-f3f6186b1558"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Untangling metabolism between infected mammalian host cells and intracellular pathogen","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-321144","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Shigellosis caused by Shigella is the one of the most important foodborne illness in global health, and the intracellular proliferation within the host cells is the most necessary step for inducing shigellosis. The known knowledge indicated that acetate was generated by the intracellular Shigella flexneri within the infected HeLa. It meant that Shigella can utilize the cytosolic glucose as the energy source for its cytosolic proliferation. So, metabolites switching in cytosolic Shigella is a notable issue for preventing Shigella infection. In this study, we analyzed the turnover of 13C-glucose-derived metabolites among the mid-log phase Shigella, non-infected HeLa, and its Shigella-infected cells. Briefly, the HeLa cells provided with uniformly-labeled [U-13C] glucose were infected with mid-log phase Shigella flexneri based on the gentamicin protection assay for 6-h. Meanwhile, each medium was collected every hour for following 1H- nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) analysis. In addition, the intracellular bacteria within HeLa infected with either formate pre-treated Shigella or non-treated Shigella were counted for identifying the effect of formate on Shigella infection. Our results showed that the 13C-acetate and 13C-formate were the two of the major products in mid-log Shigella. Otherwise, 13C-latctate and 13C-pyruvate were abundant in non-infected HeLa. However, when Shigella entered into HeLa the 13C-formate was gradually decreased after 2-h postinfection. In further, the intracellular bacterial number within HeLa after infection with formate pre-treated Shigella showed that formate can increase Shigella colonization in HeLa. Our findings indicated that the intracellular Shigella cannot continually produce formate after invasion, and was also involved in regulation of Shigella infection. Our findings support that the glycolysis is important for Shigella infection, and one of the metabolites, formate, may play also an important role in pathogenesis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Ke-Chuan","Yigit, Demet","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352571"],"event":{"end":"2019-07-13","place":"Heidelberg, de","start":"2019-07-10","title":"EMBO New Approaches and Concepts in Microbiology 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of formate in shigella flexneri after invading into hela cells","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-352571","ids":["dtu-a0d79a22-4625-40df-8a74-0d5352e64a1e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-490A703A30ADDAD6A326743F1A4A7F7B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K.","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"c0762931-9826-44a5-ad31-c2bc1de6b709","name":"Wang, Ke-Chuan","name_org":"Wang, K.","orcid":"0000-0001-7423-7738","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"D.","key":"yigitpau","last":"Yigit","locid":"a0ba8b00-22cd-430d-9d01-9358364c663f","name":"Yigit, Demet","name_org":"Yigit, D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.H.","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, J.H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.H.","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","name_org":"Lerche, M.H.","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"P.R.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"945cf0b9-5a16-4e82-a927-c9c42c2467b2","name":"Jensen, Pernille Rose","name_org":"Jensen, P.R.","orcid":"0000-0003-4359-848X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a0d79a22-4625-40df-8a74-0d5352e64a1e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The impact of formate in Shigella flexneri after invading into HeLa cells","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352571","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Metabolic differences among and within tumors can be an important determinant in cancer treatment outcome. However, methods for determining these differences non-invasively in vivo is lacking. Using pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma as a model, we demonstrate that tumor xenografts with a similar genetic background can be distinguished by their differing rates of the metabolism of 13C labeled glucose tracers, which can be imaged without hyperpolarization by using newly developed techniques for noise suppression. Using this method, cancer subtypes that appeared to have similar metabolic profiles based on steady state metabolic measurement can be distinguished from each other. The metabolic maps from 13C-glucose imaging localized lactate production and overall glucose metabolism to different regions of some tumors. Such tumor heterogeneity would not be not detectable in FDG-PET.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Kishimoto, Shun","Brender, Jeffrey R.","Crooks, Daniel R.","Matsumoto, Shingo","Seki, Tomohiro","Oshima, Nobu","Merkle, Hellmut","Lin, Penghui","Reed, Galen","Chen, Albert P.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Munasinghe, Jeeva","Saito, Keita","Yamamoto, Kazutoshi","Choyke, Peter L.","Mitchell, James","Lane, Andrew N.","Fan, Teresa Wm","Linehan, W. Marston","Krishna, Murali C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-361148"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","Hokkaido University","National Institutes of Health","University of Kentucky"],"keyword":["Cancer biology","Imaging","MRI","Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy","Metabolism","Metabolomics","Mouse","Tumor microenvironment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imaging of glucose metabolism by 000000000013c mri distinguishes pancreatic cancer subtypes in mice","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.46312","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-361148","identifier":[{"id":"31408004","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6706239","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85071705931","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-bd491e25-d414-4bab-9dc0-db0eec6cf163"],"keyword":["Cancer biology","Imaging","MRI","Magnetic resonance spectroscopy","Metabolism","Metabolomics","Mouse","Tumor microenvironment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-233A0C669161F0AC8FED366186DB519F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.46312","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/194761304/elife_46312_v1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"national institutes of health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Institutes of Health","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"hokkaido university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Hokkaido University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of kentucky","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Kentucky","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"ge healthcare","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GE Healthcare","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","nameva