{"abstract":"BackgroundRecurrence in glioblastoma patients often occur close to the original tumour and indicates that the current treatment is inadequate for local tumour control. In this study, we explored the feasibility of using multi-modality imaging at the time of radiotherapy planning. Specifically, we aimed to identify parameters from pre-treatment PET and MRI with potential to predict tumour recurrence.Materials and methodsSixteen patients were prospectively recruited and treated according to established guidelines. Multi-parametric imaging with F-18-FET PET/CT and F-18-FDG PET/MR including diffusion and dynamic contrast enhanced perfusion MRI were performed before radiotherapy. Correlations between imaging parameters were calculated. Imaging was related to the voxel-wise outcome at the time of tumour recurrence. Within the radiotherapy target, median differences of imaging parameters in recurring and non-recurring voxels were calculated for contrast-enhancing lesion (CEL), non-enhancing lesion (NEL), and normal appearing grey and white matter. Logistic regression models were created to predict the patient-specific probability of recurrence. The most important parameters were identified using standardized model coefficients.ResultsSignificant median differences between recurring and non-recurring voxels were observed for FDG, FET, fractional anisotropy, mean diffusivity, mean transit time, extra-vascular, extra-cellular blood volume and permeability derived from scans prior to chemo-radiotherapy. Tissue-specific patterns of voxel-wise correlations were observed. The most pronounced correlations were observed for F-18-FDG- and F-18-FET-uptake in CEL and NEL. Voxel-wise modelling of recurrence probability resulted in area under the receiver operating characteristic curve of 0.77 from scans prior to therapy. Overall, FET proved to be the most important parameter for recurrence prediction.ConclusionMulti-parametric imaging before radiotherapy is feasible and significant differences in imaging parameters between recurring and non-recurring voxels were observed. Combining parameters in a logistic regression model enabled patient-specific maps of recurrence probability, where F-18-FET proved to be most important. This strategy could enable risk-adapted radiotherapy planning.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Lundemann, Michael Juncker","af Rosenschold, Per Munck","Muhic, Aida","Larsen, Vibeke A.","Poulsen, Hans Skovgaard","Engelholm, Svend-Aage","Andersen, Flemming Littrup","Kjaer, Andreas","Larsson, Henrik B W","Law, Ian","Hansen, Adam Espe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-497853"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["FET","Glioblastoma","MRI","PET","Radiotherapy","Response prediction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of multi parametric pet and mri for prediction of tumour recurrence in patients with glioblastoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-497853","identifier":[{"id":"30276440","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000457151600008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85054329340","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-aed22b3c-8ac7-4e80-864a-c127843ef621"],"keyword":["FET","Glioblastoma","MRI","PET","Radiotherapy","Response prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EDF2FFAAC7DF3D3E67992B5DABCFB78"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Xray and Neutron Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"lundemannpau","last":"Lundemann","locid":"40a336a2-bcbc-465a-9a57-3646b127fce9","name":"Lundemann, Michael Juncker","name_org":"Lundemann, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per Munck","key":"afrosenscholdpau","last":"af Rosenschold","locid":"93f3270f-ab95-4929-9778-0e4c06c8b7cf","name":"af Rosenschold, Per Munck","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Aida","key":"muhicpau","last":"Muhic","locid":"1a60a121-e7d4-4b37-8799-0a5ba78bdb5d","name":"Muhic, Aida","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vibeke A.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans S.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"318d653c-4a69-4344-a913-f8a2073c75f8","name":"Poulsen, Hans Skovgaard","name_org":"Poulsen, Hans S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Svend-Aage","key":"engelholmpau","last":"Engelholm","name":"Engelholm, Svend-Aage","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming L.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"abbdc93c-3b5b-4a18-a96f-3be1e9e7da09","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","name_org":"Andersen, Flemming L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik B. W.","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","locid":"3c09e175-dfd1-4df5-9132-536a42c19373","name":"Larsson, Henrik B W","name_org":"Larsson, Henrik B. W.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ian","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","locid":"fa2c54ee-d725-4edb-9918-8c6cbebfc84a","name":"Law, Ian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30276440"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00259-018-4180-3","issn":["16197070","16197089"],"issn_org":["16197070"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"603-613","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054329340"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-aed22b3c-8ac7-4e80-864a-c127843ef621"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Feasibility of multi-parametric PET and MRI for prediction of tumour recurrence in patients with glioblastoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-497853","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH) signified by hepatic steatosis, inflammation, hepatocellular injury, and fibrosis is a growing cause of chronic liver disease, cirrhosis, and hepatocellular carcinoma. Hepatic fibrosis resulting from accumulation of extracellular matrix proteins secreted by hepatic myofibroblasts plays an important role in disease progression. Activated hepatic stellate cells (HSCs) have been identified as the primary source of myofibroblasts in animal models of hepatotoxic liver injury; however, so far HSC activation and plasticity have not been thoroughly investigated in the context of NASH-related fibrogenesis. Here we have determined the time-resolved changes in the HSC transcriptome during development of Western diet- and fructose-induced NASH in mice, a NASH model recapitulating human disease. Intriguingly, HSC transcriptional dynamics are highly similar across disease models pointing to HSC activation as a point of convergence in the development of fibrotic liver disease. Bioinformatic interrogation of the promoter sequences of activated genes combined with loss-of-function experiments indicates that the transcriptional regulators ETS1 and RUNX1 act as drivers of NASH-associated HSC plasticity. Taken together, our results implicate HSC activation and transcriptional plasticity as key aspects of NASH pathophysiology.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Marcher, Ann-Britt","Bendixen, Sofie Marchsteiner","Terkelsen, Mike Krogh","Hohmann, Sonja","Hansen, Maria Høj","Larsen, Bjørk Ditlev","Mandrup, Susanne","Dimke, Henrik","Detlefsen, Sönke","Ravnskjaer, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-585777"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcriptional regulation of hepatic stellate cell activation in nash","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-39112-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-585777","identifier":[{"id":"30787418","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6382845","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85061797951","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-2bf397fa-2598-4568-81b0-73f3d137fbd3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9EC3AB214BB03A07804C4BF843C9B910"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146617357/s41598_019_39112_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-39112-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, ATLAS - Center for Functional Genomics and Tissue Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Britt","key":"marcherpau","last":"Marcher","locid":"11d5c9d9-4b44-4171-bd3b-7b1312bef200","name":"Marcher, Ann-Britt","orcid":"0000-0002-4799-8870","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie M","key":"bendixenpau","last":"Bendixen","locid":"cf0a7f61-1f94-4e99-9239-cfaec0fbb083","name":"Bendixen, Sofie Marchsteiner","name_org":"Bendixen, Sofie M","orcid":"0000-0001-9510-941X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike K","key":"terkelsenpau","last":"Terkelsen","locid":"90bb746f-730a-4ae1-9001-1ff65f21bb00","name":"Terkelsen, Mike Krogh","name_org":"Terkelsen, Mike K","orcid":"0000-0002-5478-7895","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonja S","key":"hohmannpau","last":"Hohmann","locid":"fbc816a6-cda3-4210-9367-a7a3c4cceef6","name":"Hohmann, Sonja","name_org":"Hohmann, Sonja S","orcid":"0009-0006-0403-0583","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria H","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c83ff06d-f443-4199-9e15-8f4a16deb2a2","name":"Hansen, Maria Høj","name_org":"Hansen, Maria H","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørk D","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b5604438-a5c4-48e6-bfe1-323596b91e52","name":"Larsen, Bjørk Ditlev","name_org":"Larsen, Bjørk D","orcid":"0000-0003-1754-770X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne","key":"mandruppau","last":"Mandrup","locid":"6e8c29d6-da8a-4ef0-ab1a-03efe2e3d9e5","name":"Mandrup, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-0961-5787","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"dimkepau","last":"Dimke","locid":"77b413c1-0598-49ab-b29d-68b9b723c33a","name":"Dimke, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9170-2168","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sönke","key":"detlefsenpau","last":"Detlefsen","locid":"6bbd570e-0f99-4ee0-a239-7433591decbd","name":"Detlefsen, Sönke","orcid":"0000-0002-9466-2333","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"ravnskjaerpau","last":"Ravnskjaer","locid":"1842e135-4b37-4106-a274-f936925e391e","name":"Ravnskjaer, Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-5322-3887","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30787418"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-019-39112-6","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"2324","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061797951"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2bf397fa-2598-4568-81b0-73f3d137fbd3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Transcriptional regulation of Hepatic Stellate Cell activation in NASH","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-585777","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Neoadjuvant chemotherapy may represent a shift in the treatment of locally advanced colon cancer. The angiogenic couple has-microRNA-126 (miRNA-126) and epidermal growth factor-like domain 7 (EGFL7) are transcribed from the same gene and regulates all aspects of angiogenesis and may influence the ability of tumor cells to disseminate. The aim was to analyze the relationship between miRNA-126 and EGFL7 and disease recurrence in patients with locally advanced colon cancer treated with neoadjuvant chemotherapy. Methods: This study included 71 patients from a phase II study all planned for three cycles of capecitabine and oxaliplatin before surgery. Blood was sampled at baseline and right before and after the operation. Circulating miRNA-126 was analysed by RT-qPCR and a quantitative immunoassay was used for the analyses of EGFL7. Results: The rates of 5-year disease-free survival (DFS) and overall survival (OS) were 80% and 85%, respectively. The level of circulating miRNA-126 before the operation predicts recurrence, P = 0.035. In patients with values below and above the median the recurrence rate was 31% and 4%, respectively. Similar results applied to EGFL7. A www.cdrjournal.com combined estimate identified a subgroup of patients (25 of 71) with no recurrence and a 5-year DFS and OS rate of 100%, respectively. Conclusion: MicroRNA-126 and EGFL7 are predictors for disease recurrence in patients with locally advanced colon cancer treated with neoadjuvant chemotherapy and may assist in selection of adjuvant chemotherapy.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Torben Frøstrup","Carlsen, Anting Liu","Tanassi, Julia Tanas","Larsen, Ole","Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","Jensen, Lars Henrik","Jakobsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-587478"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Torben Frøstrup"],"keyword":["Chemotherapy","Colon cancer","Epidermal growth factor like domain 7","microRNA 126"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microrna 000000000126 and epidermal growth factor like domain 000000000007 predict recurrence in patients with colon cancer treated with neoadjuvant chemotherapy","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20517/cdr.2019.08","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-587478","identifier":[{"id":"85107456326","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35582589","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8992522","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-31dc22d3-8a83-4f34-88f6-9fbbb936bada"],"keyword":["Chemotherapy","Colon cancer","Epidermal growth factor-like domain 7","MicroRNA-126"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86327E4FAAD78EE1CB2175CC07F5B70A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/169363294/3140.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20517/cdr.2019.08","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of sou