ype":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-624909","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The senescence response to oncogenes is believed to be a barrier to oncogenic transformation in premalignant lesions, and describing the mechanisms by which tumor cells evade this response is important for early diagnosis and treatment. The male germ cell-associated protein SSX2 is ectopically expressed in many types of cancer and is functionally involved in regulating chromatin structure and supporting cell proliferation. Similar to many well-characterized oncogenes, SSX2 has the ability to induce senescence in cells. In this study, we performed a functional genetic screen to identify proteins implicated in SSX2-induced senescence and identified several subunits of the Mediator complex, which is central in regulating RNA polymerase-mediated transcription. Further experiments showed that reduced levels of MED1, MED4, and MED14 perturbed the development of senescence in SSX2-expressing cells. In contrast, knockdown of MED1 did not prevent development of B-Raf- and Epirubicin-induced senescence, suggesting that Mediator may be specifically linked to the cellular functions of SSX2 that may lead to development of senescence or be central in a SSX2-specific senescence response. Indeed, immunostaining of melanoma tumors, which often express SSX proteins, exhibited altered levels of MED1 compared to benign nevi. Similarly, RNA-seq analysis suggested that MED1, MED4, and MED14 were downregulated in some tumors, while upregulated in others. In conclusion, our study reveals the Mediator complex as essential for SSX2-induced senescence and suggests that changes in Mediator activity could be instrumental for tumorigenesis.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Brückmann, Nadine Heidi","Bennedsen, Sofie N","Duijf, Pascal H G","Terp, Mikkel Green","Thomassen, Mads","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Pedersen, Christina Bøg","Kruse, Torben A","Alcaraz, Nicolas","Ditzel, Henrik","Gjerstorff, Morten Frier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Gjerstorff, Morten Frier"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queensland University of Technology","The University of Queensland"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a functional genetic screen identifies the mediator complex as essential for ssx000000000002 induced senescence","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41419-019-2068-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-638991","identifier":[{"id":"85074712963","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6834653","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31695025","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e5c090ff-c2d3-49cc-84a5-779a2f342152"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBD817E583062851E34A68B2A87496A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41419-019-2068-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/156242690/A_functional_genetic_screen_identifies_the_Mediator.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Department of Cancer and Inflammation Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"