{"abstract":"Objective: In this study, we describe a method to improve preamplifier decoupling in low frequency MRI receive coil arrays, where sample loading is low and coils exhibit a high Q-factor. Methods: The method relies on the higher decoupling obtained when coils are matched to an impedance higher than 50 . Preamplifiers with inductive and low resistive input impedance further increase the effectiveness of the method. Results: We show that for coils with poor sample loading, coupling to other elements in an array is a major source of SNR degradation due to a reduction in the coil Q-factor. An eight-channel 13C array at 32 MHz for imaging the human head has been designed following this strategy. The improved decoupling even allowed the construction of the array without the overlapping of neighboring coils. Parallel imaging performance is also evaluated, demonstrating better spatial encoding of the array due to its non-overlapped geometry. Conclusion: The proposed design strategy for coil arrays is beneficial for low frequency coils where the coil thermal noise is dominant. The method has been demonstrated on an eight-channel array for the human head for 13C MRI at 3 T (32 MHz), with almost twofold SNR enhancement when compared with a traditional array of similar size and number of elements. Significance: The proposed method is of relevance for low frequency arrays, where sample loading is low and noise correlation is high due to insufficient coil decoupling.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sanchez-Heredia, Juan D","Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Hansen, Rie B","Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Laustsen, Christoffer","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan H"],"cuid":["S02-086.42-030245"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"keyword":["13C MRI","C 13 MRI","Coil","Couplings","Design","Hyperpolarization","Impedance","Loading","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Preamplifiers","Q factor","RF coil","SNR","Sense","Signal to noise ratio"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved decoupling for low frequency mri arrays using non conventional preamplifier impedance","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/160471071/08533360.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-086.42-030245","identifier":[{"id":"85056598105","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000473175400012","type":"wos"},{"id":"30442598","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f3288b05-c246-412c-8965-8d6da892b294","dtu-162852c9-e001-4d68-90fd-42e51aef9925"],"keyword":["13C MRI","C-13 MRI","COIL","Couplings","DESIGN","Hyperpolarization","Impedance","Loading","Magnetic resonance imaging","PARALLEL MRI","Preamplifiers","Q-factor","RF coil","SENSE","SNR","Signal to noise ratio"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4283BFE6F4E968AC03ED42592F94206B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/160471071/08533360.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezjuandiegopau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansendanielhøjruppau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rie Beck","key":"hansenriebeckpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben S","key":"søvsøszocskahansenesbenpau","last":"Szocska Hansen","locid":"2ea5821e-bbda-4f7e-a18a-0b9eb3b993f0","name":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","name_org":"Szocska Hansen, Esben S","orcid":"0000-0001-5512-9870","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenchristofferpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkovitaliypau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenjanhenrikpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30442598"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tbme.2018.2881203","issn":["00189294","15582531"],"issn_org":["00189294"],"issue":"7","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering","pages":"1940-1948","paperid":"8533360","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering","title_org":"IEEE transactions on bio-medical engineering","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056598105"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f3288b05-c246-412c-8965-8d6da892b294","dtu-162852c9-e001-4d68-90fd-42e51aef9925"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved Decoupling for Low Frequency MRI Arrays using Non-conventional Preamplifier Impedance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.42-030245","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Myocardial deformation assessed by speckle tracking echocardiography (STE) is increasingly used for diagnosis, monitoring and prognosis in patients with clinical and pre-clinical cardiovascular diseases. Feature tracking cardiac magnetic resonance (FT-CMR) also allows myocardial deformation analysis. To clarify whether the two modalities can be used interchangeably, we compared myocardial deformation analysis by FT-CMR with STE in patients with a variety of cardiovascular diseases and healthy subjects. We included 40 patients and 10 healthy subjects undergoing cardiac magnetic resonance and echocardiographic examination for left ventricular volumetric assessment. We studied patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction (n = 10), acute perimyocarditis (n = 10), aortic valve stenosis (n = 10), and previous heart transplantation (n = 10) by global longitudinal (GLS), radial (GRS) and circumferential strain (GCS). Myocardial deformation analysis by FT-CMR was feasible in all but one participant. While GLS, GRS and GCS measured by FT-CMR correlated overall with STE (r = 0.74 and p < 0.001, r = 0.58 and p < 0.001, and r = 0.76 and p < 0.001), the correlations were not consistent within subgroups. GLS was systematically lower, whereas GRS and GCS were higher by FT-CMR compared to STE (p = 0.04 and p < 0.0001). Inter- and intra-observer reproducibility were comparable for FT-CMR and STE overall and across subgroups. In conclusion, myocardial deformation can be evaluated using FT-CMR applied to routine cine-CMR images in patients with a variety of cardiovascular diseases. However, correlation between FT-CMR and STE was modest and agreement was not optimal due to systematic bias regarding GLS and GCS. Consequently, FT-CMR and STE should not be used interchangeably for myocardial strain evaluation.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Pryds, Kasper","Larsen, Anders Hostrup","Hansen, Mona Sahlholdt","Grøndal, Anne Yoon Krogh","Tougaard, Rasmus Stilling","Hansson, Nils Henrik","Clemmensen, Tor Skibsted","Løgstrup, Brian Bridal","Wiggers, Henrik","Kim, Won Yong","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Nielsen, Roni Ranghøj"],"cuid":["S02-094.22-004464"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Pryds, Kasper"],"keyword":["Dysfunction","Ejection fraction","Global longitudinal strain","Heart","Left ventricular volumes","Mechanics","Speckle tracking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"myocardial strain assessed by feature tracking cardiac magnetic resonance in patients with a variety of cardiovascular diseases a comparison with echocardiography","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-47775-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.22-004464","identifier":[{"id":"85071161529","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000478743700008","type":"wos"},{"id":"31383914","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6683180","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-5bb8903c-07d7-402a-95b7-397610e1df11","au-6fdd5e57-2ad5-47aa-b7e3-23a5e66a5de7"],"keyword":["2-DIMENSIONAL ECHOCARDIOGRAPHY","DYSFUNCTION","EJECTION FRACTION","GLOBAL LONGITUDINAL STRAIN","HEART","LEFT-VENTRICULAR VOLUMES","MECHANICS","SPECKLE-TRACKING","TISSUE TRACKING"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-ACCA94D701797C6000CDE599E3912501"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-47775-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309391111/Open_Access_Article.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"o