{"abstract":"Samfundspartnerskabet Rebus har i tre år arbejdet intenst på at udvikle en række nye værktøjer og guidelines. Et centralt mål er at øge fokus på et godt indeklima, når beslutningerne skal træffes. Løsningerne er målrettet renovering, men perspektiverne rækker også til brug i nybyggeri.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Tine Steen","Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068624"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Guidelines","Indeklima","Nybyggeri","Renovering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pakkeløsning til et godt indeklima danvak dagen 000000002019","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ipaper.ipapercms.dk/TechMedia/HVACMagasinet/2019/4/?page=18","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-068624","ids":["aau-402e9735-d018-490e-ae6c-e0c75726fafa"],"keyword":["Guidelines","Indeklima","Nybyggeri","Renovering"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7AAB359CF6E207B997C5B823E74101D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ipaper.ipapercms.dk/TechMedia/HVACMagasinet/2019/4/?page=18","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Architectural Engineering (CIVIL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Energy in Buildings Research Group (Civil)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Indoor Environment and Sustainable Buildings Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Energy and Sustainability in Buildings","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Indoor Environmental Quality and Building Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6f4c1acc-34db-423a-9567-359fc381a0c4","name":"Larsen, Tine Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-4704-6503","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik N.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7f5e707b-235a-4e71-ae71-e9278e7aa2ba","name":"Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","name_org":"Knudsen, Henrik N.","orcid":"0000-0002-3196-7279","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16036913"],"issn_org":["22456511"],"issue":"4","journal":"HVAC Magasinet","pages":"18-23","publisher":"TechMedia AS","publisher_org":"TechMedia A/S","status":"p","title":"HVAC Magasinet","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-402e9735-d018-490e-ae6c-e0c75726fafa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Pakkeløsning til et godt indeklima : Danvak Dagen 2019","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-068624","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Litter size and other conventional measures in rodents are common end-points in the assessment of xenobiotics for reprotoxic effects. However, since litter size may be normal despite reduced semen quality, we established and tested a mouse in vitro fertilization/in vitro culture (IVF/IVC) system to assess other aspects of reprotoxicity of xenobiotic exposure. Two pesticides, vinclozolin (V) and chlormequat (C), were added to feed in low (40 and 900 ppm, respectively) and high (300 and 2700 ppm, respectively) doses and compared to control (nil pesticide). Exposed males were used for natural mating to evaluate litter size and then used for IVF/IVC and sperm evaluation. The IVF/IVC system detected significant adverse effect of high dose of vinclozolin on blastocyst formation, which was not detected by conventional measures such as litter size or sperm motility and viability. We conclude that assessment based on IVF/IVC measures may complement litter size and other conventional end-points.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Liu, Ying","Pedersen, Hanne Skovsgaard","Larsen, Knud Erik","Kristensen, Kaja Kjær","Foldager, Leslie","Callesen, Henrik","Sørensen, Martin Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146280"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Mouse","Pesticides","Reproductive toxicity","Sperm fertilizing capacity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combined i in vitro i fertilization and culture ivf ivc in mouse for reprotoxicity assessment of xenobiotic exposure","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85069560049","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-146280","identifier":[{"id":"85069560049","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31301413","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1d9b0217-c3e7-4006-833a-ed4d41c5b485"],"keyword":["Mouse","Pesticides","Reproductive toxicity","Sperm fertilizing capacity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1E31FCD1BEC2411BBE83F75240061985"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Molecular nutrition and reproduction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"4d0cfc77-a33e-41e0-b0e6-5bc7f148222a","name":"Liu, Ying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Skovsgaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dbbbd39e-77dc-4209-b35f-089ac5d2159a","name":"Pedersen, Hanne Skovsgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46cd3e98-1529-45bf-9054-2978f328044c","name":"Larsen, Knud Erik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaja","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"4f25f09d-05c1-40d9-8ebf-31aa6ee5ffbe","name":"Kristensen, Kaja Kjær","name_org":"Kristensen, Kaja","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leslie","key":"foldagerpau","last":"Foldager","locid":"a815b9b5-4778-40b7-9686-3020f664195f","name":"Foldager, Leslie","orcid":"0000-0002-2639-826X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","locid":"7fe33188-4ec4-4b54-bc7a-c922c5ebaa54","name":"Callesen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0185-7300","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Tang","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fefc1862-587c-4b1f-9e20-694246b18221","name":"Sørensen, Martin Tang","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-4282","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31301413"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.reprotox.2019.07.006","issn":["08906238","18731708"],"issn_org":["08906238"],"issue":"October","journal":"Reproductive Toxicology","pages":"115-123","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Reproductive Toxicology","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069560049"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1d9b0217-c3e7-4006-833a-ed4d41c5b485"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Combined <i>in vitro</i> fertilization and culture (IVF/IVC) in mouse for reprotoxicity assessment of xenobiotic exposure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146280","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper examines territorial functioning in collaborative writing through a mixed methods study involving interviews and analysis of collaboratively authored documents. Our findings have implications for the way we think about collaborative writing as a design problem, in that current conceptualizations of collaborative writing emphasize the work context rather than the work itself, at the cost of understanding interpersonal dynamics that are central to the common process. The findings come from 23 interviews with 32 university researchers and students regarding their experiences with collaborative writing of academic texts. The analysis of these interviews is supplemented with visualizations of the revision histories of documents written by a subset of the study participants. We discuss our findings in terms of fragmented exchanges in common information spaces and consider the shared document as a mediator for the simultaneous accomplishment and negotiation of work.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen-Ledet, Ida","Korsgaard, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-220693"],"event":{"acronym":"ECSCW","end":"2019-06-12","place":"Salzburg, at","start":"2019-06-08","title":"European Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative writing","Empirical study","Interview","Territoriality","Visual analysis","Visualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"territorial functioning in collaborative writing fragmented exchanges and common outcomes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/193690913/TerritorialFunctioningInCollaborativeWriting_ECSCW2019.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-220693","identifier":[{"id":"000473162800005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85065640930","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a057036f-5c28-4905-8fa6-280634026ff2"],"keyword":["Collaborative writing","Empirical study","Group writing","Interview","Territoriality","Visual analysis","Visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-481423B9E285B1A48E38712C023399DF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/193690913/TerritorialFunctioningInCollaborativeWriting_ECSCW2019.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida","key":"larsenledetpau","last":"Larsen-Ledet","locid":"81887b35-ffb8-40da-af5e-290504107b38","name":"Larsen-Ledet, Ida","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"korsgaardpau","last":"Korsgaard","locid":"8d0ec8d8-aa95-47a0-966a-0a9a8ad968ed","name":"Korsgaard, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10606-019-09359-8","issn":["09259724","15737551"],"issn_org":["09259724"],"issue":"3-4","journal":"Computer Supported Cooperative Work","pages":"391-433","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Computer Supported Cooperative Work","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065640930"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a057036f-5c28-4905-8fa6-280634026ff2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Territorial Functioning in Collaborative Writing : Fragmented Exchanges and Common Outcomes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220693","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
