{"abstract":"I dit lederjob går du fra det ene ledelsesdilemma til det næste. Det er netop i mødet med dilemmaer, at der er brug for ledelse. Her får du et værktøj til at se, indkredse og definere dilemmaer: Hvad er de unikke kendetegn ved dilemmaer, og hvordan får du dem til at træde ud af kompleksitetens tåge, så du kan arbejde med dem?","author_count":2,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik","Mogensen, Lilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-296571"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000012 spørgsmål du skal kunne svare på for at lede dilemmaer","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/12-spoergsmaal-du-skal-kunne-svare-paa-for-at-lede-dilemmaer/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-296571","ids":["cbs-def8d1c5-801e-455e-9515-977959d366e8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-28CE5E2AF5EAC3A4F7693216DBC25F59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lederweb.dk/artikler/12-spoergsmaal-du-skal-kunne-svare-paa-for-at-lede-dilemmaer/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lilian","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","name":"Mogensen, Lilian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-def8d1c5-801e-455e-9515-977959d366e8"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"12 spørgsmål du skal kunne svare på for at lede dilemmaer","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-296571","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) has permitted the production of highly polarized liquid-state samples enabling real-time imaging of metabolic processes non-invasively in vivo. The desire for higher magnetic resonance sensitivity has led to the development of multiple home-built and commercial dDNP polarizers employing solid-state microwave sources. Providing efficient microwave delivery that avoids unwanted heating of the sample is a crucial step to achieve high nuclear polarization. Consequently, a process is described to reduce waveguide attenuation due to resistive loss thereby doubling the delivered power. A mirror and reflector are designed and tested to increase the microwave field density across the sample volume resulting in a 2.3 dB increase of delivered power. Thermal considerations with regards to waveguide geometry and dDNP probe design are discussed. A thermal model of the dDNP probe is computed and experimentally verified.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Albannay, Mohammed M.","Vinther, Joachim M.","Capozzi, Andrea","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-312901"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"keyword":["Electromagnetic simulation","Microwave","Solid state NMR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized microwave delivery in ddnp","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/182109798/1_s2.0_S1090780719301119_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-312901","identifier":[{"id":"85067304583","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31220776","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1be9d662-f795-4919-b55b-8568ec2dab36"],"keyword":["Disssolution-DNP","Electromagnetic simulation","Microwave","Solid-state NMR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7FACB62F5BB61C3E05569C1E4492DCFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/182109798/1_s2.0_S1090780719301119_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammed M.","key":"albannaypau","last":"Albannay","locid":"2cb48487-30c9-4d3e-81d8-52475a08025e","name":"Albannay, Mohammed M.","orcid":"0000-0002-6635-8844","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"movintherpau","last":"M.O. Vinther","locid":"ea849433-5b54-41be-8972-8948a094d660","name":"Vinther, Joachim M.","name_org":"M.O. Vinther, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0003-4930-3179","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"capozzipau","last":"Capozzi","locid":"b0cf62b2-059b-44b4-bcf7-c10bdbeda7b9","name":"Capozzi, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-2306-9049","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31220776"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2019.06.004","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","pages":"58-65","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"305"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067304583"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1be9d662-f795-4919-b55b-8568ec2dab36"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Optimized microwave delivery in dDNP","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-312901","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Dynamic nuclear polarization (DNP) build-up times at low temperature for low-gamma heteronuclei can be unfavorably long and can be accelerated by transfer of polarization from protons. The efficiency of the cross polarization (CP) depends on the B1-field strengths, the pulse sequence chosen for cross polarization and the sample composition. CP experiments rely on high B1-fields, which typically lead to electrical discharge and breakdown in the circuit. This problem is particularly severe in the low pressure helium atmosphere due to easily ionized helium atoms. The purpose of this study is to identify strategies to minimize voltages across components in a tuning and matching circuit of the coil to avoid electrical discharge during CP experiments. Design equations for three tuning and matching network configurations are derived. The results of the study are then used in the design of a single coil double resonance DNP probe operating at 71.8 MHz (13C frequency) and 285.5 MHz (1H frequency). In the current setup we achieve 28% polarization on 13C in urea with a build-up time of 11.6 min with CP compared to 14% and 53 min by direct polarization using TEMPOL as the radical. Different cross polarization sequences are compared.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vinther, Joachim M.","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Albannay, Mohammed M.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327862"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"keyword":["CP","DNP probe","Electrical discharge","Helium"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design of a local quasi distributed tuning and matching circuit for dissolution dnp cross polarization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/177200711/SSNMR_CP_probe.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327862","identifier":[{"id":"31220747","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065084393","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4e3a4e3c-be5b-41ce-9a3a-2738adb90f67"],"keyword":["CP","Cross-polarisation","DNP probe","Electrical discharge","Helium","Matching circuit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F0389CC30A2F417B585DA142CA4AD4A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/177200711/SSNMR_CP_probe.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim Møllesøe","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","locid":"ea849433-5b54-41be-8972-8948a094d660","name":"Vinther, Joachim M.","name_org":"Vinther, Joachim Møllesøe","orcid":"0000-0003-4930-3179","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammed M.","key":"albannaypau","last":"Albannay","locid":"2cb48487-30c9-4d3e-81d8-52475a08025e","name":"Albannay, Mohammed M.","orcid":"0000-0002-6635-8844","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31220747"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ssnmr.2019.04.006","issn":["09262040","15273326"],"issn_org":["09262040"],"journal":"Solid State Nuclear Magnetic Resonance","pages":"12-20","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Solid State Nuclear Magnetic Resonance","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065084393"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4e3a4e3c-be5b-41ce-9a3a-2738adb90f67"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Design of a local quasi-distributed tuning and matching circuit for dissolution DNP cross polarization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327862","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We report the performance of a cryogenic RF receive-only coil for 13C imaging of small animals. It is experimentally demonstrated 2-fold SNR improvement in comparison to a room temperature coil in immediate vicinity of the sample. The self-developed cryostat employed for coil cooling shows thermal stability within 5 h of use for 6 L of LN2 , which can be extended up to 12 h if more LN is added. The Q88K /Q290K ratio of the unloaded coil is 550/285","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sanchez, Juan Diego","Baron, Rafael Antonio","Hansen, Esben S. Szocska","Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Laustsen, Christoffer","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334236"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-16","place":"Montréal, ca","start":"2019-05-11","title":"ISMRM 27th Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a robust cryogenic rf coil 000000000088k for in vivo hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c mri of rats","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/181826465/ISMRM2019_0434.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334236","ids":["dtu-6398f9d4-0396-45cd-96c7-a028542ede1b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4749621BC45CDC85AAC34F95D6AD42D3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/181826465/ISMRM2019_0434.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rafael Antonio","key":"baronpau","last":"Baron","locid":"16ea55c1-2461-438e-abbe-a63d4b3144b6","name":"Baron, Rafael Antonio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben S. Szocska","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Esben S. Szocska","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk