{"abstract":"Oxidative stress is associated with the development and progression of numerous diseases. However, targeting oxidative stress has not been established in the clinical management of any disease. Several methods and markers are available to measure oxidative stress, including direct measurement of free radicals, antioxidants, redox balance, and oxidative modifications of cellular macromolecules. Oxidatively generated nucleic acid modifications have attracted much interest due to the pre-mutagenic oxidative modification of DNA into 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2′-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG), associated with cancer development. During the last decade, the perception of RNA has changed from that of a ‘silent messenger’ to an ‘active contributor’, and, parallelly oxidatively generated RNA modifications measured as 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-guanosine (8-oxoGuo), has been demonstrated as a prognostic factor for all-caused and cardiovascular related mortality in patients with type 2 diabetes. Several attempts have been made to modify the amount of oxidative nucleic acid modifications. Thus, this review aims to introduce researchers to the measurement of oxidatively generated nucleic acid modifications as well as critically review previous attempts and provide future directions for targeting oxidatively generated nucleic acid modifications.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Emil List","Weimann, Allan","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524083"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["8 Oxo 7 8 dihydro 2 deoxyguanosine","8 oxo 7 8 dihydro guanosine","Clinical trials","Intervention","Oxidative Nucleic Acid Modifications","Oxidative stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interventions targeted at oxidatively generated modifications of nucleic acids focused on urine and plasma markers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-524083","identifier":[{"id":"31563634","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85072804227","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-dabebfca-b45c-4f1d-8bac-02225fb6b9d7"],"keyword":["8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2′-deoxyguanosine","8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-guanosine","Clinical trials","Intervention","Oxidative nucleic acid modifications","Oxidative stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E4BA13D0EAC01EE9B02FAABF272C0559"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"weimannpau","last":"Weimann","name":"Weimann, Allan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik Enghusen","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31563634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2019.09.030","issn":["08915849","18734596"],"issn_org":["08915849"],"journal":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","pages":"256-283","status":"p","title":"Free Radical Biology and Medicine","volume":"145"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072804227"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dabebfca-b45c-4f1d-8bac-02225fb6b9d7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interventions targeted at oxidatively generated modifications of nucleic acids focused on urine and plasma markers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524083","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Investigations into the possible associations between early in life motor function and later in life musculoskeletal health, will require easily obtainable, valid, and reliable measures of gross motor function and kinematics. Marker-based motion capture systems provide reasonably valid and reliable measures, but recordings are restricted to expensive lab environments. Markerless motion capture systems can provide measures of gross motor function and kinematics outside of lab environments and with minimal interference to the subjects being investigated. It is, however, unknown if these measures are sufficiently valid and reliable in young children to warrant further use. This study aims to document the concurrent validity of a markerless motion capture system: \"The Captury.\" Method: Measures of gross motor function and lower extremity kinematics from 14 preschool children (age between three and 6 years) performing a series of squats and standing broad jumps were recorded by a marker-based (Vicon) and a markerless (The Captury) motion capture system simultaneously, in December 2015. Measurement differences between the two systems were examined for the following variables: jump length, jump height, hip flexion, knee flexion, ankle dorsi flexion, knee varus, knee to hip separation distance ratio (KHR), ankle to hip separation distance ratio (AHR), frontal plane projection angle, frontal plane knee angle (FPKA), and frontal plane knee deviation (FPKD). Measurement differences between the systems were expressed in terms of root mean square errors, mean differences, limits of agreement (LOA), and intraclass correlations of absolute agreement (ICC (2,1) A) and consistency of agreement. Results: Measurement differences between the two systems varied depending on the variables. Agreement and reliability ranged from acceptable for e.g. jump height [LOA: - 3.8 cm to 2.2 cm; ICC (2,1) A: 0.91] to unacceptable for knee varus [LOA: - 33° to 19°; ICC (2,1) A: 0.29]. Conclusions: The measurements by the markerless motion capture system \"The Captury\" cannot be considered interchangeable with the Vicon measures, but our results suggest that this system can produce estimates of jump length, jump height, KHR, AHR, knee flexion, FPKA, and FPKD, with acceptable levels of agreement and reliability. These variables are promising for use in future research but require further investigation of their clinimetric properties.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Harsted, Steen","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","Hestbæk, Lise","Boyle, Eleanor","Lauridsen, Henrik Hein"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614077"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Concurrent validity","Markerless motion capture"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"concurrent validity of lower extremity kinematics and jump characteristics captured in pre school children by a markerless 000000000003d motion capture system","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12998-019-0261-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-614077","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6689331","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85070561128","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31417672","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-8e9c75d6-5d74-407a-9fcf-bccf14fc7719"],"keyword":["Concurrent validity","Markerless motion capture"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2931699EAF2139A1C11C0D58DBC6EE97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/153079140/s12998_019_0261_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12998-019-0261-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Nordic Institute of Chiropractic and Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"harstedpau","last":"Harsted","locid":"ff230edf-3d7c-4d44-b496-51c32c6c8a4f","name":"Harsted, Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-1879-2224","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise","key":"hestbækpau","last":"Hestbæk","locid":"033861d4-b80b-485c-90d5-2f1f6b9f686b","name":"Hestbæk, Lise","orcid":"0000-0002-1620-4556","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleanor","key":"boylepau","last":"Boyle","locid":"79e9e639-9ded-45fe-bc17-4677eb6c95e3","name":"Boyle, Eleanor","orcid":"0000-0002-9012-9128","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Hein","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"f7e4b9ef-9405-42c2-9a11-7a982af019c5","name":"Lauridsen, Henrik Hein","orcid":"0000-0001-5198-5215","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31417672"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12998-019-0261-z","issn":["2045709X"],"journal":"Chiropractic & Manual Therapies","paperid":"39","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Chiropractic & Manual Therapies","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070561128"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","nordic institute of chiropractic and clinical biomechanics"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8e9c75d6-5d74-407a-9fcf-bccf14fc7719"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Concurrent validity of lower extremity kinematics and jump characteristics captured in pre-school children by a markerless 3D motion capture system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614077","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
