last":"Kolstad","name":"Kolstad, Henrik A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"AD","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fa03cd1b-31e4-483a-8ee1-09f917379e33","name":"Larsen, AD","orcid":"0000-0002-3587-2998","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisa A","key":"pompeiipau","last":"Pompeii","name":"Pompeii, Lisa A","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"AH","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"8e894baf-467c-45d3-8abe-41a805b30b22","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","name_org":"Garde, AH","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-2f061b3d-63a0-4b58-92b0-a11e1e0372b5"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Cohort study of short time between shifts and risk of injury","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-780270","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The magnetic properties of spinel ferrites (MFe 2 O 4 , M = Mn, Fe, Co, Ni, Zn, etc.) are largely determined by the type of divalent cation, M 2+ and cation distribution between the tetrahedral and octahedral sites in the structure. Partial substitution of Zn 2+ into the thermodynamically preferred tetrahedral coordination in ferrites produces an increase in magnetic saturation at room temperature. However, nanosized crystallites are known to adopt different structures compared to their bulk equivalents. Consequently, reliable characterization of the atomic structure of nanosized ferrites is essential for understanding and tailoring their magnetic properties. Here, we present a meticulous study of the crystal-, magnetic- and micro-structures of mixed Zn x Co 1-x Fe 2 O 4 spinel ferrite nanocrystallites in the entire composition range (x = 0.0-1.0 in steps of 0.1). Gram-scale nanoparticle preparation was performed via the widely used hydrothermal method. Eight compositions were selected to study the effect of 4 hours vacuum annealing at 823 K. Combined Rietveld refinement of powder X-ray and neutron diffraction data along with Mössbauer analysis reveal how the as-synthesized nanocrystallites adopt metastable cation inversions, different from the well-established and thermodynamically stable inversions of the bulk equivalents. The annealing treatment causes the structure of the crystallites to relax towards a more bulk-like cation distribution. For all compositions, the smaller as-synthesized nanocrystallites with metastable cation inversion exhibit a higher saturation magnetization compared to the annealed samples. The demonstrated control over the spinel ferrite cation distribution is a key step on the way to designing cheap magnetic materials with tunable properties optimized for specific applications.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andersen, Henrik Lyder","Granados-Miralles, Cecilia","Saura-Múzquiz, Matilde","Stingaciu, Marian","Larsen, Jacob","Søndergaard-Pedersen, Frederik M","Ahlburg, Jakob","Keller, Lukas","Frandsen, Cathrine","Christensen, Mogens"],"cuid":["S02-080.17-024639"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Mogens"],"country":["Norway","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute for Energy Technology","Paul Scherrer Institute"],"keyword":["CO","Functionalization","MRI CONTRAST","Magnetism","Neutron","SCHERRER","SIZE","X ray diffraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced intrinsic saturation magnetization of zn sub x sub co sub 000000000001 x sub fe sub 000000000002 sub o sub 000000000004 sub nanocrystallites with metastable spinel inversion","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85063596353","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was financially supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (Center for Materials Crystallography, DNRF93), Innovation Fund Denmark (Green Chemistry for Advanced Materials, GCAM-4107-00008B), Independent Research Fund Denmark (Small and Smart Magnet Design) and the Danish Center for Synchrotron and Neutron Science (DanScatt). Affiliation with the Center for Integrated Materials Research (iMAT) at Aarhus University is gratefully acknowledged. The authors are grateful for the obtained beamtime at the DMC beamline, SINQ, PSI, Villigen, Switzerland."],"id":"S02-080.17-024639","identifier":[{"id":"85063596353","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000467884100014","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-a3752429-9cda-4bde-9724-0a9633b3a7d2","dtu-dfa0d54c-6364-41a8-8fc6-500b0576d5e6"],"keyword":["CO","COFE2O4 NANOPARTICLES","FERRITE NANOPARTICLES","FUNCTIONALIZATION","MAGNETISM","MRI CONTRAST","NEUTRON","SCHERRER","SIZE","X-RAY-DIFFRACTION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FC26E769C43A2D3A448058F18A237965"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Centre for Materials Crystallography (CMC)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, Langelandsgade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"institute for energy technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Institute for Energy Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"paul scherrer institute","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Paul Scherrer Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Lyder","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"c8507bba-0089-4559-a2de-76c5c7f0aca7","name":"Andersen, Henrik Lyder","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilia","key":"granadosmirallespau","last":"Granados-Miralles","locid":"e09b2206-b559-450c-be3d-496d76d99e5b","name":"Granados-Miralles, Cecilia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matilde","key":"sauramúzquizpau","last":"Saura-Múzquiz","locid":"725d982d-9da7-42cc-8c4f-6817cb5e07f8","name":"Saura-Múzquiz, Matilde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marian","key":"stingaciupau","last":"Stingaciu","locid":"8c07f678-e2e0-45a6-a306-3d838de8f7a0","name":"Stingaciu, Marian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"18ec921a-3295-467a-981e-656d9a23377c","name":"Larsen, Jacob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"søndergaardpedersenpau","last":"Søndergaard-Pedersen","locid":"2ca78f28-86b6-4a54-8fc2-bd854c296eac","name":"Søndergaard-Pedersen, Frederik M","name_org":"Søndergaard-Pedersen, Frederik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Voldum","key":"ahlburgpau","last":"Ahlburg","locid":"490ea9ff-a403-46f3-ac03-61b06341688a","name":"Ahlburg, Jakob","name_org":"Ahlburg, Jakob Voldum","orcid":"0000-0003-3215-3506","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lukas","key":"kellerpau","last":"Keller","name":"Keller, Lukas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cathrine","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"e2abec6d-ca8d-4391-b9da-53d1399942fc","name":"Frandsen, Cathrine","orcid":"0000-0001-5006-924X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"95104029-b560-4ada-ba4c-0eaab3ed18f4","name":"Christensen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0001-6805-1232","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c9qm00012g","issn":["20521537"],"issue":"4","journal":"Materials Chemistry Frontiers","pages":"668-679","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Materials Chemistry Frontiers","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063596353"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a3752429-9cda-4bde-9724-0a9633b3a7d2","dtu-dfa0d54c-6364-41a8-8fc6-500b0576d5e6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Enhanced intrinsic saturation magnetization of Zn <sub>x</sub> Co <sub>1-x</sub> Fe <sub>2</sub> O <sub>4</sub> nanocrystallites with metastable spinel inversion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.17-024639","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Toxoplasma gondii is an important foodborne zoonotic parasite. Meat of infected animals is presumed to constitute a major source of human infection and may be a driver of geographical variation in the prevalence of anti-T. gondii antibodies in humans, which is substantial in the Nordic-Baltic region in northern Europe. However, data on seroprevalence of T. gondii in different animal species used for human consumption are scattered. Methods: We conducted a systematic review of seroprevalence studies and meta-analysis to estimate the seroprevalence of T. gondii in five animal species that are raised or hunted for human consumption in the Nordic-Baltic region: domestic pigs (Sus scrofa domesticus), sheep (Ovis aries), cattle (Bos taurus), wild boars (Sus scrofa), and moose (Alces alces). We searched for studies that were conducted between January 1990 and June 2018, and reported in articles, theses, conference abstracts and proceedings, and manuscripts. Subgroup analyses were performed to identify variables influencing the seroprevalence. Findings: From a total of 271 studies identified in the systematic review, 32 were included in the meta-analysis. These comprised of 13 studies on domestic pigs, six on sheep, three on cattle, six on wild boars, and four on moose. The estimated pooled seroprevalence of T. gondii was 6% in domestic pigs (CI 95% : 3–10%), 23% in sheep (CI 95% : 12–36%), 7% in cattle (CI 95% : 1–21%), 33% in wild boars (CI 95% : 26–41%), and 16% in moose (CI 95% : 10–23%). High heterogeneity was observed in the seroprevalence data within each species. In all host species except wild boars, the pooled seroprevalence estimates were significantly higher in animals >1 year of age than in younger animals. Not all studies provided information on animal age, sensitivity and specificity of the serological method employed, and the cut-off values used for defining an animal seropositive. Conclusions: A substantial proportion of animals raised or hunted for human consumption in the region had tested positive for T. gondii. This indicates widespread exposure to T. gondii among animals raised or hunted for human consumption in the region. Large variations were observed in the seroprevalence estimates between the studies in the region; however, studies were too few to identify spatial patterns at country-level.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Olsen, Abbey","Berg, Rebecca","Tagel, Maarja","Must, Kärt","Deksne, Gunita","Enemark, Heidi Larsen","Alban, Lis","Johansen, Maria Vang","Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","Sandberg, Marianne","Lundén, Anna","Stensvold, Christen Rune","Pires, Sara Monteiro","Jokelainen, Pikka"],"cuid":["S02-093.39-036119"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Olsen, Abbey"],"country":["Estonia","Finland","Latvia","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Estonian University of Life Sciences","Institute of Food Safety Animal Health and Environment","Latvia University of Agriculture","National Veterinary Institute","Norwegian Veterinary Institute","University of Helsinki","University of Latvia"],"keyword":["Europe","Food borne","Seroepidemiology","Toxoplasmosis","Zoonosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["National Veterinary Institute , Uppsala , Sweden."],"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-AAF","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"seroprevalence of i toxoplasma gondii i in domestic pigs sheep cattle wild boars and moose in the nordic baltic region a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.parepi.2019.e00100","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the other members of the Burden of Disease of Toxoplasmosis in Denmark Working Group and the Nordic Source Attribution of Toxoplasmosis Working Group for discussions during the preparation of this work. The Nordic Source Attribution of Toxoplasmosis Working Group has been financially supported by The Nordic Council of Ministers . In addition, this work was partly supported by the Innovation Fund Denmark ( 7038-00129B ), SEGES pig research center, the European Regional Development Fund “Post-doctoral research aid” project “One Health multidisciplinary approaches for epidemiology and prevention of selected parasitic zoonosis”(OMEPPAZ) ( 1.1.1.2/VIAA/1/16/204 ), and COST Action FA1408 “A European Network for Foodborne Parasites: Euro-FBP”. We also thank all who helped in identifying unpublished studies and provided other relevant information. Additionally, Tariq Halasa, from Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Copenhagen University, is thanked for his input to the statistical analyses."],"id":"S02-093.39-036119","identifier":[{"id":"30906889","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85062647036","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6411595","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-9affdaaf-0656-44b6-b8cc-d9cf0fe74c1f","ku-a759f832-a5a0-4dfe-aff5-e21d0877ef57"],"keyword":["Europe","Food-borne","Meat-borne","Seroepidemiology","Toxoplasmosis","Zoonosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1B7452EA8742138F5E7CD802C90F73C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/215135675/1_s2.0_S2405673119300157_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.parepi.2019.e00100","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"o