s","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-086616","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper proposes an investigation into interactive storyworld adaptivity, which is adapting the world in ways that do not necessarily alter the plot or narrative management of the story, but rather, purely change the world around the player. Using the game “Red Dead Redemption 2” as a case study, the paper discusses the possibilities of these kinds of adaptations and looks ahead to the future possibilities and what an interactive storyworld design might need to consider if it could change the entire world in real time, while letting the player roam free. It considers the types of interactions we should focus for more natural adaptations and what technology might help implement such a future, and why we would want to do so in the first place.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","Schoenau-Fog, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095020"],"event":{"acronym":"ICIDS","end":"2019-11-23","place":"us","start":"2019-10-19","title":"International Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adaptivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"well that was quick towards storyworld adaptivity that reacts to players as people","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85077684295&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-095020","identifier":[{"id":"85077684295","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9b0fcdd5-16d9-4021-924b-7e172d8f4162"],"keyword":["Adaptivity","Interactive storyworlds","Red Dead Redemption 2","Storyworlds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D99DEE1B1CFC8D750861B4920CA0EA98"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarke Alexander","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b20b35fc-c929-4058-a942-903b3772a4b1","name":"Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schoenaufogpau","last":"Schoenau-Fog","locid":"34a35708-1cbb-4d3b-9b7c-53080126b5ef","name":"Schoenau-Fog, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-157X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rogelio E.","key":"cardonariverapedh","last":"Cardona-Rivera","name":"Cardona-Rivera, Rogelio E.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"R. Michael","key":"youngpedh","last":"Young","name":"Young, R. Michael","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"sullivanpedh","last":"Sullivan","name":"Sullivan, Anne","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-33894-7_22","eisbn":["9783030338947"],"isbn":["9783030338930"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"204-213","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"12th International Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling, ICIDS 2019, Little Cottonwood Canyon, UT, USA, November 19–22, 2019, Proceedings","title":"Interactive Storytelling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077684295"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9b0fcdd5-16d9-4021-924b-7e172d8f4162"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"\"Well, That was Quick\" - Towards Storyworld Adaptivity That Reacts To Players as People","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-095020","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Genome-wide association studies of patients with coronary artery disease (CAD) suggest that several risk loci increase the risk of CAD and myocardial infarction (MI) equally. In contrast, the ABO locus is stronger associated with MI than with CAD, but the underlying mechanisms are unknown. PURPOSE: To investigate the association between the ABO risk variant and platelet activation and aggregation. Moreover, to explore the effects of other CAD-associated risk variants. METHODS: We included 879 stable CAD patients receiving low-dose aspirin. All patients were genotyped for 45 genome-wide significant CAD risk variants, including rs495828 at the ABO locus. A genetic risk score (GRS) was calculated to assess the combined risk of all genetic variants. Serum soluble P-selectin (sP-selectin) and thromboxane B2 were used as measures of platelet activation, and platelet aggregation was assessed by multiple electrode aggregometry (MEA) using arachidonic acid and collagen as agonists and VerifyNow. RESULTS: The rs495828 CAD risk allele was associated with higher MEA platelet aggregation; arachidonic acid: 14.9% (6.7-23.7%, p = 0.0002) higher AUC (Area Under aggregation Curve) per risk allele, and collagen: 13.1% (5.8%-20.9%, p = 0.0003). Conversely, sP-selectin levels were 7.5% (3.1%-11.7%, p = 0.001) lower per risk allele. Rs495828 genotypes were not associated with aggregation assessed by VerifyNow (p = 0.30) or S-thromboxane B2 levels (p = 0.98). None of the remaining variants or the GRS were associated with platelet activation or aggregation. CONCLUSIONS: The ABO risk allele was associated with increased platelet aggregation as assessed by MEA. This finding may contribute to explain the increased MI risk in ABO risk variant carriers.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christiansen, Morten Krogh","Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","Nyegaard, Mette","Neergaard-Petersen, Søs","Würtz, Morten","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Hvas, Anne-Mette","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Kristensen, Steen Dalby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137696"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ABO Blood Group System","Coronary artery disease","Genetics","Myocardial Infarction","Platelet Activation","Platelet Aggregation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the abo locus is associated with increased platelet aggregation in patients with stable coronary artery disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85062270985","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137696","identifier":[{"id":"85062270985","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30837090","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0e953b9b-df7d-4f7c-a3c0-c48193e7d4d0"],"keyword":["ABO blood-group system","Coronary artery disease","Genetics","Myocardial infarction","Platelet activation","Platelet aggregation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FCDF037C3A3DFE7FD997CBA48D432C48"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Krogh","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"bf2444c5-3e70-45d3-b035-850325ff2f6e","name":"Christiansen, Morten Krogh","orcid":"0000-0002-3894-888X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Bøjet","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"15c7c979-5236-47ec-b92e-a4a5992b2d1e","name":"Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardpau","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"a34df7ff-0fb5-44b0-8255-6dc2c9b962f3","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søs","key":"neergaardpetersenpau","last":"Neergaard-Petersen","locid":"7c75329a-0cef-4da3-959b-2bf6b326aaf5","name":"Neergaard-Petersen, Søs","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"würtzpau","last":"Würtz","locid":"b5e070b9-ecf1-43ae-83c2-164d5eeccfc5","name":"Würtz, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7150-7704","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Lerkevang","key":"grovepau","last":"Grove","locid":"f527f99e-8eed-433e-923e-afc0686af8b7","name":"Grove, Erik Lerkevang","orcid":"0000-0002-1466-0865","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne-Mette","key":"hvaspau","last":"Hvas","locid":"b4362b49-6deb-4c2c-9027-48dc6cdbd5e6","name":"Hvas, Anne-Mette","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Dalby","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"6d64271d-8a2c-41ea-891d-e85555bbd47a","name":"Kristensen, Steen Dalby","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30837090"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2019.01.090","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"issue":"July","journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"152-158","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"286"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062270985"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0e953b9b-df7d-4f7c-a3c0-c48193e7d4d0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The ABO locus is associated with increased platelet aggregation in patients with stable coronary artery disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-137696","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
