{"abstract":"Xenobiotics, such as chemicals and pesticides, may result in adverse effects on reproduction in human and animals. Using in-vitro embryo production as a testing system reveals details of fertilization (IVF) and early embryonic development (IVC). The aim of our study was to perform a systematical calibration of sperm concentration in an IVF/IVC system, using an outbred mouse strain, and further determine the sperm concentration that furnishes a sensitive assessment of sperm fertilizing capacity in relation to reprotoxic evaluations. By performing breakpoint analysis, the results revealed a maximum two-cell percentage (51%, 95% CI: 38 to 69%) at 3.6 × 10 4 sperm/ml (95% CI: 2.1 × 10 4 to 6.1 × 10 4). For future application of the IVF/IVC system, a sperm concentration lower than this breakpoint concentration is required to be within the responsive range for determining sperm fertilizing capacity. We conclude that a relatively low sperm concentration (2.5 × 10 4 sperm/ml) is a precondition in a mouse IVF/IVC system in order to detect potential reprotoxic effects on sperm fertilizing capacity. Our study illustrates that a systematic approach is necessary for validation and appropriate use of such in-vitro system used for reproductive toxicity testing.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pedersen, Hanne Skovsgaard","Liu, Ying","Foldager, Leslie","Callesen, Henrik","Larsen, Knud Erik","Sørensen, Martin Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-234392"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["In vitro embryo production","Mouse","Reproductive toxicity","Sperm concentration","Sperm fertilizing capacity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calibration of sperm concentration for in vitro fertilization in a mouse reprotoxicity model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tiv.2018.11.009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-234392","identifier":[{"id":"30476541","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85057779797","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b819fb4b-e413-43ce-9fc7-4f0b6035065c"],"keyword":["In vitro embryo production","Mouse","Reproductive toxicity","Sperm concentration","Sperm fertilizing capacity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC62F4D2867DB3A6A283A202D506233B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tiv.2018.11.009","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Molecular nutrition and reproduction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Skovsgaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dbbbd39e-77dc-4209-b35f-089ac5d2159a","name":"Pedersen, Hanne Skovsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"4d0cfc77-a33e-41e0-b0e6-5bc7f148222a","name":"Liu, Ying","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leslie","key":"foldagerpau","last":"Foldager","locid":"a815b9b5-4778-40b7-9686-3020f664195f","name":"Foldager, Leslie","orcid":"0000-0002-2639-826X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","locid":"7fe33188-4ec4-4b54-bc7a-c922c5ebaa54","name":"Callesen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0185-7300","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46cd3e98-1529-45bf-9054-2978f328044c","name":"Larsen, Knud Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Tang","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fefc1862-587c-4b1f-9e20-694246b18221","name":"Sørensen, Martin Tang","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-4282","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30476541"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tiv.2018.11.009","issn":["08872333","18793177"],"issn_org":["08872333"],"journal":"Toxicology in Vitro","pages":"58-61","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Toxicology in Vitro","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057779797"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b819fb4b-e413-43ce-9fc7-4f0b6035065c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Calibration of sperm concentration for in vitro fertilization in a mouse reprotoxicity model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-234392","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objectives Lifestyle may affect observed associations between glucocorticoid use and adverse events. This study aimed to investigate whether lifestyle differ according to use of systemic glucocorticoids. Design Population-based cross-sectional study. Setting The Central Denmark Region. Participants 30 245 adults (≥25 years of age) who participated in a questionnaire-based public health survey in 2010. Outcome measures Systemic glucocorticoid use was categorised as never use, current use (prescription redemption ≤90 days before completing the questionnaire), recent use (prescription redemption 91-365 days before completing the questionnaire), former use (prescription redemption >365 days before completing the questionnaire) and according to cumulative dose expressed in prednisolone equivalents (<100, 100-499, 500-999, 1000-1999, 2000-4999, ≥5000 mg). We computed the prevalence of lifestyle factors (body mass index, smoking, alcohol intake, physical activity and dietary habits) according to glucocorticoid use. We then estimated age-adjusted prevalence ratios (aPRs) and 95% CIs, comparing the categories of glucocorticoid users versus never users. All analyses were stratified by sex. Results Of the 30 245 participants (53% women, median age 53 years), 563 (1.9%) were current users, 885 (2.9%) were recent users, 3054 (10%) were former users and 25 743 (85%) were never users. Ever users of glucocorticoids had a slightly higher prevalence of obesity than never users (18% vs 14%, aPR=1.4, 95% CI 1.2 to 1.5 in women and 17% vs 15%, aPR=1.2, 95% CI 1.1 to 1.4 in men). In women, ever users of glucocorticoids had a slightly lower prevalence of high-risk alcohol consumption compared with never users (17% vs 20%, aPR=0.8, 95% CI 0.7 to 1.0). Smoking, diet and physical activity did not differ substantially according to use of glucocorticoids. Conclusion Our study provides a framework for quantifying potential uncontrolled confounding by lifestyle factors in studies of systemic glucocorticoids.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Laugesen, Kristina","Petersen, Irene","Pedersen, Lars","Larsen, Finn Breinholt","Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-260850"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Laugesen, Kristina"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London"],"keyword":["Alcohol Drinking","Body Mass Index","Diet","Exercise","Glucocorticoids","Smoking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of lifestyle characteristics in glucocorticoid users and non users a danish population based cross sectional study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-030780","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-260850","identifier":[{"id":"31662378","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6830647","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85074274764","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e65abd16-ca5f-4d85-8118-e72ede5ec7ad"],"keyword":["alcohol drinking","body mass index","diet","exercise","glucocorticoids","smoking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F8E043135BA005F19671F0361583675D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-030780","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"laugesenpau","last":"Laugesen","locid":"ab62af11-21a5-4b44-a8ec-6c6d2afc742d","name":"Laugesen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0001-7971-8223","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irene","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"379db212-1e10-49ad-89d3-435afad9c9cc","name":"Petersen, Irene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Finn","key":"breinholtlarsenpau","last":"Breinholt Larsen","locid":"bee6772d-1940-4d39-b53b-dc3a5cf79d98","name":"Larsen, Finn Breinholt","name_org":"Breinholt Larsen, Finn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Otto Lunde","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"303ebe86-6861-4b19-b4d7-6bda0526b27e","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-1526","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik T.Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","name_org":"Sørensen, Henrik T.Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31662378"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2019-030780","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"10","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e030780","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074274764"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e65abd16-ca5f-4d85-8118-e72ede5ec7ad"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prevalence of lifestyle characteristics in glucocorticoid users and non-users : A Danish population-based cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-260850","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Bundgaard Larsen, Mads","Rothe, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-282125"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000026 sø og handelsretssager","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-282125","ids":["cbs-472240a9-349f-4ac8-9e44-8888eb4aa96e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-09C6FE69E71B7985462ADD681AB90DF4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Business Humanities and Law, CBS LAW"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"bundgaardlarsenpau","last":"Bundgaard Larsen","name":"Bundgaard Larsen, Mads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"rothepau","last":"Rothe","locid":"40dd3ff2-b8e3-430b-bf41-904458692533","name":"Rothe, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pernille","key":"backhausenpedh","last":"Backhausen","name":"Backhausen, Pernille","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Håkun","key":"djurhuuspedh","last":"Djurhuus","name":"Djurhuus, Håkun","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"lundbladpedh","last":"Lundblad","name":"Lundblad, Christian","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"4.","isbn":["9788757431865"],"pages":"559-575","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p","title":"Proceduren"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-472240a9-349f-4ac8-9e44-8888eb4aa96e"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"§ 26, Sø- og Handelsretssager","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-282125","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The Danish Fisher-Researcher-Network is organized by the trade organizations: The Danish Fisheries Association Producer Organization and the Danish Pelagic Producers Organization as well as the research institute, DTU Aqua. The European Maritime and Fisheries Fund and the Fisheries Agency finance the project. The purpose of the project is to support networking activities that bring the executive Danish fisheries industry and operational fisheries research closer together through fisher-researcher alliances. The idea is to target research against the practical challenges in the fishing industry and to streamline the development of business and ease of generation through the synergy arising from dialogue, common problem formulation and resolution. The project will also streamline and professionalize the work of the various Thematic and Regional Advisory Councils with Danish interests in collaboration between the fishing industry and DTU Aqua experts before and during the meetings. The fishing industry is faced with ever-increasing challenges in terms of regulatory requirements in the context of the Common Fisheries Policy and its national implementation, consumer requirements for fishing activities and environmental impact, as well as an ecosystem in dynamic transformation that offers changing fishing opportunities. In order to continue the development of profitable and sustainable fisheries, it is necessary to exchange experiences about fisheries and management, identify problems, elaborate ideas for solutions and formulate projects for testing ideas. Since solutions require knowledge from many areas, networking between fisheries, research and management is necessary. In order to ensure the change of generations in modern Danish fishing, the project will also work in the field of teaching apprenticeships and knowledge sharing between businesses as well as course and internship in fishery for students in Aquatic Science and Technology (AST). The project has been the first phase of so far two network initiatives involving workshops, working groups, experience exchange, idea gathering, knowledge sharing, courses, web dissemination and advisory council work in collaboration between fishermen and apprentices, industry associations, as well as researchers and students. The network has established a platform for knowledge sharing www.fisker-forsker.dk. The network's events and results have been regularly communicated to the fishermen through a wide range of articles, reports, interviews and videos on this and other media. The primary contact for dialogue and knowledge sharing between fishermen and researchers has been through more than 20 targeted workshops and dialogue meetings at DTU as well as in local fisheries organizations. In addition, 3 completed teaching initiatives for students at the Fisheries School as well as courses for AST masters students with project practice on fishing boats during the studies contributed to the transfer of knowledge at generational change. It has been the goal to form fisherman-researcher alliances on concrete collaborative projects for the development of Danish fisheries. Through screening of more than 30 ideas from the fishing industry, 9 concrete collaborative projects have been established with proposals for support by the EMFF. The projects have ranged from development self-management in brown shrimp fisheries over analyzes of cod shedding for cod for exploitation of fish-gathered data in mackerel and poached fish The primary contact for dialogue and knowledge sharing between fishermen and researchers has been through more than 20 targeted workshops and dialogue meetings at DTU as well as in local fisheries organizations. In addition, 3 completed courses for students at the Fisheries School in Thyborøn as well as courses for Aquatic Technology and Science students at DTU with project practice on fishing boats during the studies contributed to the transfer of knowledge at generational change. Finally, the network has supported work in the Thematic and Regional Advisory Boards.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mosegaard, Henrik","Pedersen, Eva Maria","Christensen, Linda Stuhr","Sparrevohn, Claus Reedtz","Larsen, Ole Lundberg","Fischer, Kenn Skau"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-315820"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Pelagic Producers Organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dansk fisker forsker netværk fase 000000000001 slutrapport","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/184370657/344_2019_Dansk_Fisker_Forsker_Netvaerk_Fase1_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-315820","ids":["dtu-25ea0e7d-7b98-44e3-9ac6-9935f4a8ec41"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B9B7F540F3C7E44F2FE149AF4DDF71FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/184370657/344_2019_Dansk_Fisker_Forsker_Netvaerk_Fase1_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Marine Living Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Pelagic Producers Organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"mosegaardpau","last":"Mosegaard","locid":"01482533-590c-4ffd-b236-9baf6fe84c8d","name":"Mosegaard, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7045-9456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva Maria","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"1e48fb0a-018a-4f02-bb25-946ee7b7ff28","name":"Pedersen, Eva Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0298-2648","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linda Stuhr","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"07910e0a-0cc4-4a20-93c0-df167bb57413","name":"Christensen, Linda Stuhr","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Reedtz","key":"sparrevohnpau","last":"Sparrevohn","name":"Sparrevohn, Claus Reedtz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Lundberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Ole Lundberg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenn Skau","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Kenn Skau","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"344-2019","pages":"39","place":"Kgl. Lyngby","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","repno":"DTU Aqua-rapport, 344-2019","series":"DTU Aqua-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-25ea0e7d-7b98-44e3-9ac6-9935f4a8ec41"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dansk Fisker-Forsker Netværk. Fase 1 : Slutrapport","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsport