:"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Merete","key":"lindegaardpau","last":"Lindegaard","locid":"84162349-4120-418e-8358-3c416b6107a1","name":"Lindegaard, Hanne Merete","orcid":"0000-0002-5675-3859","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/annrheumdis-2019-eular.3626","issn":["00034967","14682060"],"issn_org":["00034967"],"issue":"Suppl. 2","journal":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","pages":"1017-1018","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","volume":"78"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4da2e70a-908e-4432-8172-cc95a3a5b883"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comparing Disease Activity in the Wrist by Repeat Synovial Biopsies, Ramris Magnetic Resonance Score and Eular-Omeract Ultrasound Score: A 6-month Prospective Trial in Early and Longstanding Rheumatoid Arthritis","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-595478","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Compromised cerebral energy metabolism is common in patients with bacterial meningitis. In this study, simultaneous measurements of cerebral oxygen tension and lactate/pyruvate ratio were compared to explore whether disturbed energy metabolism was usually caused by insufficient tissue oxygenation or compromised oxidative metabolism of pyruvate indicating mitochondrial dysfunction. Subject and Methods: Ten consecutive patients with severe streptococcus meningitis were included in this prospective cohort study. Intracranial pressure, brain tissue oxygen tension (PbtO 2 ), and energy metabolism (intracerebral microdialysis) were continuously monitored in nine patients. A cerebral lactate/pyruvate (LP) ratio <30 was considered indicating normal oxidative metabolism, LP ratio >30 simultaneously with pyruvate below lower normal level (70 µmol/L) was interpreted as biochemical indication of ischemia, and LP ratio >30 simultaneously with a normal or increased level of pyruvate was interpreted as mitochondrial dysfunction. The biochemical variables were compared with PbtO 2 simultaneously monitored within the same cerebral region. Results: In two cases, the LP ratio was normal during the whole study period and the simultaneously monitored PbtO 2 was 18 ± 6 mm Hg. In six cases, interpreted as mitochondrial dysfunction, the simultaneously monitored PbtO 2 was 20 ± 6 mm Hg and without correlation with the LP ratio. In one patient, exhibiting a pattern interpreted as ischemia, PbtO 2 decreased below 10 mm Hg and a correlation between LP and PbtO 2 was observed. Conclusion: This study demonstrated that compromised cerebral energy metabolism, evidenced by increased LP ratio, was common in patients with severe bacterial meningitis while not related to insufficient tissue oxygenation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Lykke","Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","Nordström, Carl-Henrik","Andersen, Åse Bengård","Schierbeck, Jens","Schulz, Mette Katrine","Poulsen, Frantz Rom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-617570"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bacterial meningitis","Cerebral tissue oxygenation","Mitochondrial dysfunction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patterns of cerebral tissue oxygen tension and cytoplasmic redox state in bacterial meningitis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170610771/aas.13278.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-617570","identifier":[{"id":"30328110","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85055029376","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-9add767c-7740-4207-bade-8a94a7cc49dc"],"keyword":["bacterial meningitis","cerebral tissue oxygenation","intracerebral microdialysis","intracranial pressure, ischemia","mitochondrial dysfunction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B6599CBC6B788343E7F9E4FE182B6C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170610771/aas.13278.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lykke","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f4fd0451-0508-4d78-8726-1e63c7620925","name":"Larsen, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0002-4113-4182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels Halfeld","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"18f40b9c-d8d6-4d6b-b3af-374f6221676a","name":"Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3943-8128","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl-Henrik","key":"nordströmpau","last":"Nordström","locid":"832530b4-9bf3-4eb3-bbda-ad9fad3cae33","name":"Nordström, Carl-Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Åse Bengård","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a8872eef-ddea-4708-acdb-b238eaef934c","name":"Andersen, Åse Bengård","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"schierbeckpau","last":"Schierbeck","locid":"166d4f2f-d76e-4dee-bf5f-7cefc440807e","name":"Schierbeck, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Katrine","key":"schulzpau","last":"Schulz","locid":"7b7927f3-4205-4c14-81d7-cda980a06d20","name":"Schulz, Mette Katrine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frantz","key":"rompoulsenpau","last":"Rom Poulsen","locid":"b50645f6-f0c4-4356-9f63-d44290b0dfd9","name":"Poulsen, Frantz Rom","name_org":"Rom Poulsen, Frantz","orcid":"0000-0001-5715-6901","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30328110"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.13278","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"329-336","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055029376"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9add767c-7740-4207-bade-8a94a7cc49dc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patterns of cerebral tissue oxygen tension and cytoplasmic redox state in bacterial meningitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-617570","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Standardised scoring systems for rheumatoid arthritis (RA) joint disease activity include Larsen score for radiographs, rheumatoid arthritis magnetic resonance imaging score (RAMRIS) for MRI and using the European League Against Rheumatisms-Outcome Measures in Rheumatology (EULAR-OMERACT) score for ultrasound (US) images. The aim of this prospective study was to investigate the relationship between histological synovitis and radiological synovitis, assessed by conventional X-ray, US and MRI of the wrist radiocarpal joint. Methods 20 patients with treatment naive early RA (ERA) and 20 with long-standing RA (LRA) were enrolled in a 6-month prospective study. Patients with RA underwent US-guided synovial biopsy, X-ray and US of the wrist at enrolment and 6 months. MRI at baseline and also at 6 months for the ERA group, and scored with the RAMRIS system. X-ray was scored by Larsen score and US by the EULAR-OMERACT system. Synovial biopsy inflammation was determined by the Krenn score. Results In the ERA group at baseline, Krenn score was correlated strongly with both US combined score (r = 0.77 p < 0.001) and MRI synovitis score (r = 0.85 p < 0.001), while uncorrelated at 6 months. In the LRA group at baseline, these scores correlated strongly (r = 0.83, p < 0.001) to moderately (r = 0.61, p = 0.002), and persisted at 6 months for US score (r = 0.81 p < 0.001). For all patients with RA, change in Krenn score between baseline and 6 months was correlated with both change in US combined score (r = 0.65, p < 0.001) and change in MRI synovitis score (r = 0.50, p = 0.03). Conclusion The MRI RAMRIS synovitis score and EULAR-OMERACT US scoring system are sensitive measures of histological synovitis in LRA and ERA. After 6 months, this correlation persists in the established RA group, but not in the ERA group. Overall, decreases in MRI/US synovitis are associated with reductions in histological synovitis. The study validates the use of MRI RAMRIS and EULAR-OMERACT US scores as surrogate markers of histological synovitis in established RA and early untreated RA.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Just, Søren Andreas","Nielsen, Christian","Werlinrud, Jens Christian","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Klinkby, Camilla Schufri","Schrøder, Henrik Daa","Humby, Fran","Torfing, Trine","Lindegaard, Hanne Merete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635382"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Just, Søren Andreas"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London"],"keyword":["Imaging","RAMRIS","Rheumatoid arthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"six month prospective trial in early and long standing rheumatoid arthritis evaluating disease activity in the wrist through sequential synovial histopathological analysis ramris magnetic resonance score and eular omeract ultrasound score","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2019-000951","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding SaJ is supported by grants from the Danish rheumatism association and Odense University Hospital PhD Fund and Fund for clinical research."],"id":"S01-000.00-635382","identifier":[{"id":"31413866","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6667976","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85068843152","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d90f9a74-63ae-4c98-b391-8092e7833d2f"],"keyword":["EULAR-OMERACT ultrasound score","RAMRIS","imaging","rheumatoid arthritis","synovial pathotypes","ultrasound-guided synovial biopsies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1BE