{"abstract":"We report a radio-frequency-to-optical converter based on an electro-optomechanical transduction scheme where the electrical, optical, and mechanical interface was integrated on a chip and operated with a fiber-coupled optical setup. The device was designed for field tests in a magnetic resonance scanner where its small form-factor and simple operation is paramount. For the appurtenant magnetic resonance detection circuit at 32 MHz, we demonstrate transduction with an intrinsic magnetic field sensitivity of 8 fT/√Hz, noise figure 2.3 dB, noise temperature 210 K, voltage noise 99 pV/√Hz, and current noise e 113 pA/√Hz, all in a 3 dB-bandwidth of 12 kHz. Such sensitivity and bandwidth make the transducer a valuable alternative to conventional electronic preamplifiers that additionally is directly compatible with fiber communication networks.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Simonsen, Anders","Saarinen, Sampo Antero","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Schliesser, Albert","Polzik, Eugene Simon"],"cuid":["S02-096.43-033438"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Simonsen, Anders"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sensitive optomechanical transduction of electric and magnetic signals to the optical domain","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1364/OE.27.018561","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.43-033438","identifier":[{"id":"31252797","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068031870","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000472621000095","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-26327588-0d24-4ea6-942e-7c26057a9a44","ku-98831084-0c7a-4cc9-a742-1f0cf337f408"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DCDE85A87CA0489E700A2BBD3B757E35"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/197285791/oe_27_13_18561.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250387843/oe_27_13_18561.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1364/OE.27.018561","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Quantop"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"4ea51723-e2c9-4d71-be50-f1c56d2e391d","name":"Simonsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-2521-5986","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sampo Antero","key":"saarinenpau","last":"Saarinen","locid":"c141b453-a0f6-4c51-b9cb-d1f1d068198a","name":"Saarinen, Sampo Antero","orcid":