erpau","last":"Moser","locid":"c253e3b6-b6c2-4633-9c44-2ccfcef5d5e8","name":"Moser, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-7664-8570","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30883059"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1056/nejmc1902096","issn":["00284793","15334406"],"issn_org":["00284793"],"issue":"14","journal":"The New England Journal of Medicine","pages":"1373-1374","publisher":"Massachussetts Medical Society","status":"p","title":"The New England Journal of Medicine","title_org":"New England Journal of Medicine","volume":"380"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063948340"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-19b97db1-39d3-4ccd-9ef5-1b6974566a72","au-2af10d65-8582-44d8-a84d-423d0603bab8","ku-b6236c3f-5255-4ed0-bc80-c06dcc44fe81","sdu-467ae8d0-ecca-49ac-bcb9-edbfe1b4d5d7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-Term Outcomes of Partial Oral Treatment of Endocarditis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-096.82-001321","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background Patients with infective endocarditis on the left side of the heart are typically treated with intravenous antibiotic agents for up to 6 weeks. Whether a shift from intravenous to oral antibiotics once the patient is in stable condition would result in efficacy and safety similar to those with continued intravenous treatment is unknown. Methods In a randomized, noninferiority, multicenter trial, we assigned 400 adults in stable condition who had endocarditis on the left side of the heart caused by streptococcus, Enterococcus faecalis, Staphylococcus aureus, or coagulase-negative staphylococci and who were being treated with intravenous antibiotics to continue intravenous treatment (199 patients) or to switch to oral antibiotic treatment (201 patients). In all patients, antibiotic treatment was administered intravenously for at least 10 days. If feasible, patients in the orally treated group were discharged to outpatient treatment. The primary outcome was a composite of all-cause mortality, unplanned cardiac surgery, embolic events, or relapse of bacteremia with the primary pathogen, from the time of randomization until 6 months after antibiotic treatment was completed. Results After randomization, antibiotic treatment was completed after a median of 19 days (interquartile range, 14 to 25) in the intravenously treated group and 17 days (interquartile range, 14 to 25) in the orally treated group (P=0.48). The primary composite outcome occurred in 24 patients (12.1%) in the intravenously treated group and in 18 (9.0%) in the orally treated group (between-group difference, 3.1 percentage points; 95% confidence interval, -3.4 to 9.6; P=0.40), which met noninferiority criteria. Conclusions In patients with endocarditis on the left side of the heart who were in stable condition, changing to oral antibiotic treatment was noninferior to continued intravenous antibiotic treatment. (Funded by the Danish Heart Foundation and others; POET ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT01375257 .).","author_count":21,"contributors":["Iversen, Kasper","Ihlemann, Nikolaj","Gill, Sabine U","Madsen, Trine","Elming, Hanne","Jensen, Kaare T","Bruun, Niels E","Høfsten, Dan E","Fursted, Kurt","Christensen, Jens J","Schultz, Martin","Klein, Christine F","Fosbøll, Emil L","Rosenvinge, Flemming","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Køber, Lars","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Helweg-Larsen, Jannik","Tønder, Niels","Moser, Claus","Bundgaard, Henning"],"cuid":["S04-099.68-000182"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Administration Intravenous","Administration Oral","Aged","Anti Bacterial Agents administration dosage","Antimicrobial therapy","Bacteremia drug therapy","Criteria","Diagnosis","Drug Users","Endocarditis Bacterial drug therapy","Female","Functional decline","Guidelines","Heart Valve Prosthesis microbiology","Humans","In hospital mortality","Infective endocarditis","Intention to Treat Analysis","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Length of Stay","Male","Management","Middle Aged","Recurrence","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"partial oral versus intravenous antibiotic treatment of endocarditis","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/209028339/Partial_Oral_versus_Intravenous_Antibiotic_Treatment.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.68-000182","identifier":[{"id":"000457135700005","type":"wos"},{"id