{"abstract":"Pacing the way towards 5G has lead researchers and industry in the direction of centralized processing known from Cloud-Radio Access Networks (C-RAN). In C-RAN research, a variety of different functional splits is presented by different names and focusing on different directions. The functional split determines how many Base Station (BS) functions to leave locally, close to the user, with the benefit of relaxing fronthaul network bitrate and delay requirements, and how many functions to centralize with the possibility of achieving greater processing benefits. This work presents for the first time a comprehensive overview systematizing the different work directions for both research and industry, while providing a detailed description of each functional split option and an assessment of the advantages and disadvantages. This work gives an overview of where the most effort has been directed in terms of functional splits, and where there is room for further studies. The standardization currently taking place is also considered and mapped into the research directions. It is investigated how the fronthaul network will be affected by the choice of functional split, both in terms of bitrates and latency, and as the different functional splits provide different advantages and disadvantages, the option of flexible functional splits is also looked into.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Checko, Aleksandra","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316423"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"keyword":["C RAN","Crosshaul","Fronthaul","Functional split","Industry","Network architecture","Standardization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a survey of the functional splits proposed for 000000000005g mobile crosshaul networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/COMST.2018.2868805","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316423","identifier":[{"id":"85053421589","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-27dc6285-f04b-46fa-bb34-855a9db84d3d"],"keyword":["C-RAN","Crosshaul","Fronthaul","Functional Split","Industry","Network architecture.","Standardization","X-haul"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D1558BB98EACFFEF2FDE0BDEC2EB1A01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/COMST.2018.2868805","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/158484230/hkkr_08479363.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/204172085/08479363.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Radiocomp ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria","key":"pyndtlarsenpau","last":"Pyndt Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Pyndt Larsen, Line Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandra","key":"checkopau","last":"Checko","name":"Checko, Aleksandra","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"f3aec174-d663-4d97-aaa0-81cd6f4493a9","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9558-3493","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/comst.2018.2868805","issn":["1553877X"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Communications Surveys and Tutorials","pages":"146-172","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Communications Surveys and Tutorials","title_org":"I E E E Communications Surveys and Tutorials","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053421589"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","radiocomp aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-27dc6285-f04b-46fa-bb34-855a9db84d3d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Survey of the Functional Splits Proposed for 5G Mobile Crosshaul Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316423","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The benchmark workshop on sprat (WKSPRAT) was held in ICES headquarters in Copenhagen from 5–9 November 2018. The benchmark process started in June 2017 with a 3 day data compilation meeting, also held at ICES. Three stocks were benchmarked: North Sea sprat, 3.a sprat and the Channel sprat. During the benchmark process, several arguments were put forward on the connection between the North Sea stock and the 3.a stock in Kattegat-Skagerrak. It was therefore agreed to merge the two stocks and assess them as one stock assessment unit. Sprat in area 4 and 3a During the 2018 benchmark, enough evidence were presented to merge the sprat stocks in the Skagerrak-Kattegak and in the North Sea. The catch data and the indices of abundance from 3.a were included in the data from area 4. Three surveys are carried out in the area (IBTS in Q1 and Q3 and HERAS survey) and were all used as tuning indices in the model. The IBTS indices were standardized using a delta-GAM approach: the inclusion of 3.a data increased the internal consistency between all age classes for all indices. The SMS model, previously used to assess the North Sea component, was used to assess the new combined stock. The model year is resolved into 4 seasons, where season 1 corresponds to quarter 3 of the calender year. The term ‘season’ is hence used here to identify the model year, while the term ‘quarter’ refers to the calendar year. The final model formulation includes a power function for the age 0 catchability of IBTS Q1, a constant maturity ogive and the inclusion of the very few catches reported for season 4 (Q2) into season 1 (Q3) of the following year. The new stock assessment shows a considerable improvement in the retrospective pattern, as well a better fitting to some ages of the IBTS surveys and catches (as indicated by survey and catch CVs). The stock reference points were revised following ICES standard guidelines. Blim was estimated as the breakpoint of the segmented stock recruitment relationship and Bpa was derived from Blim. Short-term forecast settings were updated. The Management Strategy Evaluation (MSE) settings for the estimation of the Fcap were presented and discussed. Several scenarios were proposed to be tested and results will be evaluated during an ad-hoc MSE workshop that will take place on 11–12 December 2018. Sprat in area 7d,e Not enough evidences were available to change the boundaries of the English Channel stock. The stock is a category 3, and the data available are still scarce. An acoustic survey (PELTIC) is carried out in the English part of area 7.e since 2013. In 2017, the survey has been extended to include also the French part of 7.e and in 2018 the Eastern Channel was surveyed as well. Also, an IBTS index in Q1 is available for the Eastern Channel from 2007 onwards. The time series from the PELTIC survey has been used since 2017 to provide advice. At the benchmark, the updated time series was presented: the method used to produce the acoustic index was revised compared to previous years and it was changed to StoX (StoX, 2015). Concerns were raised because of the uncertainty in the stock distribution, and the fact that the acoustic survey covers only the Western part of the English Channel. No analytical assessment seems to work so far: both a seasonal and non-seasonal SPiCt were attempted during the benchmark workshop, but the short time series in the acoustic index and the lack of any contrast in the data still does not allow the model to converge. The group agreed to provide a seasonal advice based on an empirical method, i.e. to use both indices for trends, but only the acoustic survey for provision of advice. Two advice rules were proposed: the 1 over 2 rule, and a fixed F rule. Both options will be tested in an MSE framework and presented during the ad-hoc MSE workshop that will take place on 11–12 December 2018.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Carpi, Piera","Pekcan-Hekim, Zeynep","Silva, Alexandra","Ibaibarriaga, Leire","Rindorf, Anna","Cooper, Anne","Kvamme, Cecilie","Sparrevohn, Claus Reedtz","Bekkevold, Dorte","Morello, Elisabetta Betulla","Berg, Florian","Lund, Henrik S.","Juul Larsen, Jesper","Carleton, Liese","Sanchez, Maria Quintela","Lindegren, Martin","van Deurs, Mikael","Brooks, Mollie Elizabeth","Nash, Richard D.M.","Rodriguez-Climent, Silvia","Pedersen, Søren Anker","Bartolino, Valerio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316937"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Portugal","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AZTI","All Global Affiliations","Centre for the Environment Fisheries and Aquaculture Science","Institute of Marine Research","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","The Portuguese Institute for Sea and Atmosphere","University of Bergen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["International Council for the Exploration of the Sea"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"benchmark workshop on sprat wksprat 000000002018 000000000005 000000000009 november 000000002018 ices hq copenhagen denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/199139770/WKSPRAT_2018_Report.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316937","ids":["dtu-299ba2e3-fac3-4bf9-9af7-03a51f087917"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B843ED06D7874EC1743E8DF290750B59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/199139770/WKSPRAT_2018_Report.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"centre for the environment fisheries and aquaculture science","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Centre for the Environment Fisheries and Aquaculture Science","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"swedish university of agricultural sciences","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"the portuguese institute for sea and atmosphere","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The Portuguese Institute for Sea and Atmosphere","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"azti","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"AZTI","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Ecosystem based Marine Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["International Council for the Exploration of the Sea"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"no","key":"institute of marine research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Marine Research","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Piera","key":"carpipau","last":"Carpi","name":"Carpi, Piera","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zeynep","key":"pekcanhekimpau","last":"Pekcan-Hekim","name":"Pekcan-Hekim, Zeynep","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandra","key":"silvapau","last":"Silva","name":"Silva, Alexandra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Leire","key":"ibaibarriagapau","last":"Ibaibarriaga","name":"Ibaibarriaga, Leire","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna","key":"rindorfpau","last":"Rindorf","locid":"2c2410ed-7de6-4b0f-aa4f-eff51aa20d68","name":"Rindorf, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4290-3983","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"cooperpau","last":"Cooper","name":"Cooper, Anne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie","key":"kvammepau","last":"Kvamme","name":"Kvamme, Cecilie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Reedtz","key":"sparrevohnpau","last":"Sparrevohn","name":"Sparrevohn, Claus Reedtz","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte","key":"bekkevoldpau","last":"Bekkevold","locid":"0ee61284-08a6-47d0-84ab-60406ba617b0","name":"Bekkevold, Dorte","orcid":"0000-0002-5297-032X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabetta Betulla","key":"morellopau","last":"Morello","name":"Morello, Elisabetta Betulla","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Florian","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","name":"Berg, Florian","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik S.","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Henrik S.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"juullarsenpau","last":"Juul Larsen","name":"Juul Larsen, Jesper","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Liese","key":"carletonpau","last":"Carleton","name":"Carleton, Liese","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Quintela","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","name":"Sanchez, Maria Quintela","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"lindegrenpau","last":"Lindegren","locid":"7147d50b-a973-4f66-a5ab-be3b8827719b","name":"Lindegren, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-9185-951X","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael","key":"vandeurspau","last":"van Deurs","locid":"b53d99e4-6f18-4cd2-add1-c6582f37bd84","name":"van Deurs, Mikael","orcid":"0000-0003-2368-2502","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mollie Elizabeth","key":"brookspau","last":"Brooks","locid":"6c5a7a04-2684-4608-b38d-d8e5117f93f5","name":"Brooks, Mollie Elizabeth","orcid":"0000-0001-6963-8326","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard D.M.","key":"nashpau","last":"Nash","name":"Nash, Richard D.M.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"rodriguezclimentpau","last":"Rodriguez-Climent","name":"Rodriguez-Climent, Silvia","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Anker","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Søren Anker","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Valerio","key":"bartolinopau","last":"Bartolino","name":"Bartolino, Valerio","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"35","pages":"60","publisher":"International Council for the Exploration of the Sea (ICES)","repno":"ACOM, No. 35","series":"ACOM","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-299ba2e3-fac3-4bf9-9af7-03a51f087917"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Benchmark Workshop on Sprat (WKSPRAT 2018) : 5 – 9 November 2018, ICES HQ, Copenhagen, Denmark","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316937","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This work considers how network slicing can use the network architecture Cloud-Radio Access Network (C-RAN) as an enabler for the required prerequisite network virtualization. Specifically this work looks at a segment of the C-RAN architecture called the fronthaul network. The fronthaul network required for network slicing needs to be able to dynamically assign capacity where it is needed. Deploying a fronthaul network faces a trade-off between fronthaul bitrate, flexibility, and complexity of the local equipment close to the user. This work relates the challenges currently faced in C-RAN research to the network requirements in network slicing. It also shows how using a packet-switched fronthaul for network slicing will bring great advantages and enable the use of different functional splits, while the price to pay is a minor decrease in fronthaul length due to latency constraints.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Berger, Michael Stübert","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324795"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fronthaul for cloud ran enabling network slicing in 000000000005g mobile networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/4860212","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324795","identifier":[{"id":"85053421228","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-43fd12f7-7cfc-4dd4-baca-a137f67e57a2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC5B20298F375BFC0A0CA6BABEF6A258"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152923275/4860212.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/4860212","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line M. P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Larsen, Line M. P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"f3aec174-d663-4d97-aaa0-81cd6f4493a9","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9558-3493","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2018/4860212","issn":["15308669","15308677"],"issn_org":["15308669"],"journal":"Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing","paperid":"4860212","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053421228"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-43fd12f7-7cfc-4dd4-baca-a137f67e57a2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fronthaul for Cloud-RAN Enabling Network Slicing in 5G Mobile Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324795","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Pursuing the ultimate limit of detection in magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) requires cryogenics to decrease the thermal noise of the electronic circuits. As cryogenic coils for MRI are slowly emerging cryogenic preamplifiers are required to fully exploit their potential. A cryogenic preamplifier operated at 77 K is designed and implemented for C imaging at 3 T (32.13 MHz), using off-the-shelves components. The design is based on a high electron mobility transistor (ATF54143) in a common source configuration. Required auxiliary circuitry for optimal cryogenic preamplifier performance is also presented consisting of a voltage regulator (noise free supply voltage and optimal power consumption), switch, and trigger (for active detuning during transmission to protect the preamplifier). A gain of 18 dB with a noise temperature of 13.7 K is achieved. Performing imaging experiments in a 3 T scanner showed an 8% increased signal-to-noise ratio from 365 to 399 when lowering the temperature of the preamplifier from 296 to 77 K while keeping the coil at room temperature. This paper thus enables the merger of cryogenic coils and preamplifiers in the hopes of reaching the ultimate limit of detection for MRI.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Petersen, Jan Raagaard","Johansen, Tom Keinicke","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-330924"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"keyword":["Biomedical electronics","Hyperpolarization","Low noise amplifier","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Preamplifiers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cryogenic preamplifiers for magnetic resonance imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/170360214/FINAL_VERSION.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Manuscript received July 4, 2017; revised October 23, 2017; accepted November 15, 2017. Date of publication December 21, 2017; date of current version January 26, 2018. This work was supported in part by the Danish National Research Foundation under Grant DNRF124. This paper was recommended by Associate Editor V. Gruev. (Corresponding author: Jan H. Ardenkjær-Larsen.) D. H. Johansen and V. Zhurbenko are with the Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance, the Electromagnetic Systems Group, the Department of Electrical Engineering, Technical University of Denmark, Kongens Lyngby 2800, Denmark (e-mail: dhjo@elektro.dtu.dk; vz@elektro.dtu.dk)."],"id":"S01-000.00-330924","identifier":[{"id":"29377808","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85039775952","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-58a8a649-c98f-40c2-b5d7-3c1247925772"],"keyword":["Biomedical electronics","Cryogenic electronics","Hyperpolarization","Low noise amplifier","Magnetic resonance imaging","preamplifiers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-093317A8F6C4F2C122D76DCC6F535C5D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/170360214/FINAL_VERSION.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel H.","key":"johansendanielhøjruppau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","name_org":"Johansen, Daniel H.","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan D.","key":"sanchezjuandiegopau","last":"Sanchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sanchez-Heredia, Juan D.","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan R.","key":"petersenjanraagaardpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"bbaeda22-d4b8-4371-b87c-e76f77d54014","name":"Petersen, Jan Raagaard","name_org":"Petersen, Jan R.","orcid":"0000-0003-3194-5798","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tom K.","key":"johansentomkeinickepau","last":"Johansen","locid":"7b44a94d-ae22-4678-87e4-8024f351462c","name":"Johansen, Tom Keinicke","name_org":"Johansen, Tom K.","orcid":"0000-0001-8182-1051","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkovitaliypau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan H.","key":"ardenkjærlarsenjanhenrikpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29377808"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tbcas.2017.2776256","issn":["19324545","19409990"],"issn_org":["19324545"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Circuits and Systems","pages":"202-210","paperid":"8233404","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Circuits and Systems","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039775952"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-58a8a649-c98f-40c2-b5d7-3c1247925772"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Cryogenic Preamplifiers for Magnetic Resonance Imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-330924","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This work presents the method of achieving ideal decoupling between elements in a receive coil array. Generally, preamplifier decoupling is limited by nonidealities of the implemented components. It is shown analytically and numerically, that for the ideal (lossless) matching circuits the input resistance of the preamplifier should be zero, while for the realistic lossy case a small negative resistance can be used to achieve ideal decoupling. Here we use a negative input resistance preamplifier (NIRP) to compensate for the loss of the circuit. The analysis is verified experimentally showing a decoupling of -62 dB when a NIRP with an input resistance of -0.023 ? is used.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357969"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-21","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2018-06-16","title":"Joint Annual Meeting ISMRM-ESMRMB 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ideal coil decoupling in receive arrays using negative resistance preamplifiers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/151960058/ISMRM18_1711_Decoupling.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357969","ids":["dtu-b2b87159-dd4e-4721-96c0-8388cd2d8025"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BBDF93A64DDD48F191BB7C1C3E4E54B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/151960058/ISMRM18_1711_Decoupling.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"