{"abstract":"Various experimental animal models are used in haemophilia research, however, little is known about how well the different species predict pharmacokinetic (PK) profiles in haemophilia patients. The aim of the current study was to describe the plasma concentration-time profile of recombinant activated factor VII (rFVIIa) and recombinant factor VIII (rFVIII) in several experimental animal models using population PK modelling, and apply a simulation-based approach to evaluate how well the developed animal population PK models predict human PK. PK models were developed for rFVIIa and rFVIII in mice, rats, monkeys, and dogs using nonlinear mixed-effects modelling, accounting for inter-individual variability, nonlinear kinetics and covariate effects. Three scaling principles were applied to predict human PK: proportional scaling to body weight from single species, scaling with fixed theory-based allometric exponents from single species, and allometric interspecies scaling with estimated allometric coefficients and exponents. The plasma concentration-time profile of rFVIIa and rFVIII in mice, rats, monkeys and dogs were accurately described by the developed species-specific PK models, accounting for nonlinear kinetics and gender-specific difference in clearance for rFVIII. The predictive performance of the animal population PK models of rFVIIa and rFVIII revealed significant species-variation. The developed PK models of rFVIIa and rFVIII in monkeys and dogs along with allometric interspecies scaling revealed high predictive performance for human PK, and may promote rational decision-making in future first-in-human trials for rFVIIa and rFVIII variants.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Malte Selch","Juul, Rasmus Vestergaard","Groth, Andreas Velsing","Simonsson, Ulrika S.H.","Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","Knudsen, Tom","Agersø, Henrik","Kreilgaard, Mads"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-397892"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Allometric scaling","Coagulation factors","Pharmacokinetic modelling","Prediction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prediction of human pharmacokinetics of activated recombinant factor vii and b domain truncated factor viii from animal population pharmacokinetic models of haemophilia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-397892","identifier":[{"id":"29369801","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85040966899","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-07660d33-5a3f-4971-a413-e5804e64a23b"],"keyword":["Allometric scaling","Coagulation factors","Interspecies","Pharmacokinetic modelling","Prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88F390198CFC82C79D3B4AA8FE71B9DC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Internal Medicine, Clinical Oncology and Veterinary Clinical Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Malte Selch","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8c2a5af4-5d44-4dce-b426-1dbf0eb3cfc1","name":"Larsen, Malte Selch","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus Vestergaard","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Rasmus Vestergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas Velsing","key":"grothpau","last":"Groth","name":"Groth, Andreas Velsing","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ulrika S.H.","key":"simonssonpau","last":"Simonsson","name":"Simonsson, Ulrika S.H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Annemarie T.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a7007b3a-f743-46be-8a05-6473fd440756","name":"Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","name_org":"Kristensen, Annemarie T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tom","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Tom","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"agersøpau","last":"Agersø","name":"Agersø, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mads","key":"kreilgaardpau","last":"Kreilgaard","name":"Kreilgaard, Mads","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29369801"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejps.2018.01.035","issn":["09280987","18790720"],"issn_org":["09280987"],"journal":"European Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","pages":"196-203","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","volume":"115"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040966899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-07660d33-5a3f-4971-a413-e5804e64a23b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prediction of human pharmacokinetics of activated recombinant factor VII and B-domain truncated factor VIII from animal population pharmacokinetic models of haemophilia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-397892","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Precise gene editing technologies are providing new opportunities to stably engineer host cells for recombinant production of therapeutic glycoproteins with different glycan structures. The glycosylation of recombinant therapeutics has long been a focus for both quality and consistency of products and for optimizing and improving pharmacokinetic properties as well as bioactivity. Structures of glycans on therapeutic glycoproteins are important for circulation, biodistribution and bioactivity. In particular, the latter has been demonstrated for therapeutic IgG1 antibodies where the core α1,6Fucose on the conserved N-glycan at Asn297 have remarkable dampening effect on Fc effector functions. We previously explored precise gene engineering and design options for N-glycosylation in CHO cells, and here we focus on engineering options possible for N-glycans on human IgG1. We demonstrate stable precise gene engineering of rather homogenous biantennary N-glycans with and without galactose (G0F, G2F) as well as the α2,6-linked monosialylated (G2FS1) glycoform. We were unable to introduce substantial disialylated glycoforms. Instead we engineered a novel monoantennary homogeneous N-glycan design with complete α2,6-linked sialic acid capping. All N-glycoforms may be engineered with and without core α1,6Fucose. The stably engineered design options enable production of human IgG antibodies with an array of distinct glycoforms for testing and selection of optimal design for different therapeutic applications.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Schulz, Morten Alder","Tian, Weihua","Mao, Yang","Van Coillie, Julie","Sun, Lingbo","Larsen, Joachim Steen","Chen, Yen-Hsi","Kristensen, Claus","Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","Clausen, Henrik","Yang, Zhang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425563"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glycoengineering design options for igg000000000001 in cho cells using precise gene editing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-425563","identifier":[{"id":"85049115510","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29596681","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-36097379-d048-468e-bf0d-13474cd97168"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9ECC6A397F15B0CFA20EB2CF8AB5BA74"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["GlycoDisplay ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten A","key":"schulzpau","last":"Schulz","locid":"2bc935b8-6d66-4e6c-872a-4d5b41a96c04","name":"Schulz, Morten Alder","name_org":"Schulz, Morten A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Weihua","key":"tianpau","last":"Tian","locid":"9c94707a-e04c-4c99-b4b6-3adce8a13103","name":"Tian, Weihua","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yang","key":"maopau","last":"Mao","locid":"d9dc26d0-d85f-41b0-828e-4971b57b796d","name":"Mao, Yang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie","key":"vancoillie