ls","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"428f2151-f2aa-4a5e-bdee-4184c0586467","name":"Thomassen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-0078-1217","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Carl","key":"hasselbalchpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"EHA Learning Center","paperid":"PF620","status":"p","title":"EHA Learning Center","volume":"2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2db0db94-e2db-432a-af41-55c2a60892be","sdu-36166198-59af-4e85-b714-eccf6cff2e89"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Safety And Efficacy Of Combination Therapy Of Interferon Αlpha-2 And Ruxolitinib In Polycythemia Vera And Low-/Intermediate-1-Risk Myelofibrosis – A One Year Follow-Up Update Of A Phase II Study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.66-048731","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Based on the abundance of specific bacterial genera, the human gut microbiota can be divided into two relatively stable groups that might play a role in personalized nutrition. We studied these simplified enterotypes as prognostic markers for successful body fat loss on two different diets. A total of 62 participants with increased waist circumference were randomly assigned to receive an ad libitum New Nordic Diet (NND) high in fiber/wholegrain or an Average Danish Diet (ADD) for 26 weeks. Participants were grouped into two discrete enterotypes by their relative abundance of Prevotella spp. divided by Bacteroides spp. (P/B ratio) obtained by quantitative PCR analysis. Modifications of dietary effects of pre-treatment P/B group were examined by linear mixed models. Among individuals with high P/B the NND resulted in a 3.15 kg (95%CI 1.55;4.76, P<0.001) larger body fat loss compared to ADD whereas no differences was observed among individuals with low P/B (0.88 kg [95% CI -0.61;2.37, P=0.25]). Consequently, a 2.27 kg (95%CI 0.09;4.45, P=0.041) difference in responsiveness to the diets were found between the two groups. In summary, subjects with high P/B-ratio appeared more susceptible to lose body fat on diets high in fiber and wholegrain than subjects with a low P/B-ratio.International Journal of Obesity accepted article preview online, 08 September 2017. doi:10.1038/ijo.2017.220.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hjorth, M F","Roager, Henrik Munch","Larsen, T. M.","Poulsen, S K","Licht, Tine Rask","Bahl, Martin Iain","Zohar, Y","Astrup, A."],"cuid":["S02-090.43-037270"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hjorth, M F"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Gelesis Inc.","Gelesis, Inc. (Biz)"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pre treatment microbial i prevotella i to i bacteroides i ratio determines body fat loss success during a 000000000006 month randomized controlled diet intervention","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ijo.2017.220","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.43-037270","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5880576","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28883543","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044620123","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cf745868-a66a-4ba1-8c2e-af48e9bb5e71","ku-af04ae71-4494-40c8-a850-9a94028866f0"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-88CD772E88591A990E8AB9A19F7C174D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/194533377/Hjorth_et_al_International_Journal_of_Obesity_2018_Vol_42_580_583.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ijo.2017.220","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ijo.2018.1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/137910719/14_Hjorth_et_al._2017_IJO_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Un