{"abstract":"Staphylococcus aureus is a major agent of nosocomial infections. Especially in methicillin-resistant strains, conventional treatment options are limited and expensive, which has fueled a growing interest in phage therapy approaches. We have tested the susceptibility of 207 clinical S. aureus strains to 12 (nine monovalent) different therapeutic phage preparations and subsequently employed linear regression models to estimate the influence of individual host gene families on resistance to phages. Specifically, we used a two-step regression model setup with a preselection step based on gene family enrichment. We show that our models are robust and capture the data’s underlying signal by comparing their performance to that of models build on randomized data. In doing so, we have identified 167 gene families that govern phage resistance in our strain set and performed functional analysis on them. This revealed genes of possible prophage or mobile genetic element origin, along with genes involved in restriction-modification and transcription regulators, though the majority were genes of unknown function. This study is a step in the direction of understanding the intricate host-phage relationship in this important pathogen with the outlook to targeted phage therapy applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zschach, Henrike","Larsen, Mette Voldby","Hasman, Henrik","Westh, Henrik","Nielsen, Morten","Międzybrodzki, Ryszard","Jończyk-Matysiak, Ewa","Weber-Dąbrowska, Beata","Górski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352459"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zschach, Henrike"],"country":["Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polish Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Bacterial phage resistance","MRSA","Phage therapy","RM1 950","Regression modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of a regression model to study host genomic determinants of phage susceptibility in mrsa","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/antibiotics7010009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352459","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5872120","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85041359959","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29382143","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-a07fb2f5-e729-4350-b822-859b238ab70e"],"keyword":["Bacterial phage resistance","MRSA","Phage therapy","RM1-950","Regression modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-06A7725A42169F5DA2BC6F27280C0EA1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/antibiotics7010009","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/146551942/antibiotics_07_00009_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics, Immunoinformatics and Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["GoSeqIt ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Hvidovre Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"pl","key":"polish academy of sciences","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polish Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrike","key":"zschachpau","last":"Zschach","locid":"a14db70e-7eeb-4dfd-922a-5d4569be078e","name":"Zschach, Henrike","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Voldby","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Mette Voldby","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"hasmanpau","last":"Hasman","name":"Hasman, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","name":"Westh, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"70ba2d95-32b6-4c85-a05e-dfe3788bef7a","name":"Nielsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7885-4311","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ryszard","key":"międzybrodzkipau","last":"Międzybrodzki","name":"Międzybrodzki, Ryszard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ewa","key":"jończykmatysiakpau","last":"Jończyk-Matysiak","name":"Jończyk-Matysiak, Ewa","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Beata","key":"weberdąbrowskapau","last":"Weber-Dąbrowska","name":"Weber-Dąbrowska, Beata","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"górskipau","last":"Górski","name":"Górski, Andrzej","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29382143"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/antibiotics7010009","issn":["00218820","03682781"],"issn_org":["00218820"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Journal of Antibiotics","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Antibiotics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041359959"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","goseqit aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a07fb2f5-e729-4350-b822-859b238ab70e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Use of a Regression Model to Study Host-Genomic Determinants of Phage Susceptibility in MRSA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352459","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Today's river systems have been extensively modified, requiring us to rethink how we approach the management of these important ecosystems. We evaluated the effects of removing 6 weirs in River Villestrup (Jutland, Denmark) on the smolt run of brown trout (Salmo trutta) over the course of 12 years. During 5 of these years, we evaluated the number, size, and timing of smolts during their downstream migration. We found an increase in smolt output following the weir removals, along with a decrease in average length and indications of an earlier peak migration. Our results suggest that barrier removal has led to an increase in spawning success by adults, fry survival, recruitment, and smolt migration success. Weir removal is therefore a viable management approach to restore connectivity in freshwater streams and rivers, which promotes the passage of smolts as they migrate to marine environment","author_count":6,"contributors":["Birnie-Gauvin, Kim","Candee, Martin Milton","Baktoft, Henrik","Larsen, Martin Hage","Koed, Anders","Aarestrup, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353709"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Birnie-Gauvin, Kim"],"keyword":["Barriers","Freshwater ecosystems","Migration","Removal","River restoration","Salmo trutta","Smolt"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"river connectivity reestablished effects and implications of six weir removals on brown trout smolt migration","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/rra.3271","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353709","identifier":[{"id":"85049593681","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a49d96d7-4769-41ea-a2bc-97ed53720b21"],"keyword":["Barriers","Freshwater ecosystems","Migration","Removal","River restoration","Salmo trutta","Smolt"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-6-1A5BB1103974B201180DF3F80EA00520"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149274528/Postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/rra.3271","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Freshwater Fisheries Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"birniegauvinpau","last":"Birnie-Gauvin","locid":"d54ccfbf-3d3c-463d-8dd0-e2481ba6f572","name":"Birnie-Gauvin, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-9242-0560","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Milton","key":"candeepau","last":"Candee","locid":"896bc83d-76ec-443f-b7cb-2252b3d28700","name":"Candee, Martin Milton","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"baktoftpau","last":"Baktoft","locid":"642a7cea-4ecc-4866-97f3-0d86f3e47ec0","name":"Baktoft, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3644-4960","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Hage","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"df4c70da-87a0-45c4-883d-9f9d64e2ffd6","name":"Larsen, Martin Hage","orcid":"0000-0001-9521-835X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"koedpau","last":"Koed","locid":"70851536-6d9b-439b-b100-58a92830a28f","name":"Koed, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-2163-0955","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"aarestruppau","last":"Aarestrup","locid":"60987b6f-7027-4bd5-91bc-d2f10390aa63","name":"Aarestrup, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-8521-6270","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/rra.3271","issn":["15351459","15351467"],"issn_org":["15351459"],"issue":"6","journal":"River Research and Applications","pages":"548-554","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"River Research and Applications","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049593681"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","15. Life on Land","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a49d96d7-4769-41ea-a2bc-97ed53720b21"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"River connectivity reestablished: effects and implications of six weir removals on brown trout smolt migration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-353709","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we describe the basic principles of dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP). Hyperpolarization is a technique to enhance the nuclear polarization and thereby increase the available signal in magnetic resonance (MR). We will discuss the consequences of strong non‐equilibrium nuclear spin polarization acquisition of the MR signal. The hardware requirements for clinical translation of this technology are presented. For studies that allow the use of externally administered agents, hyperpolarization offers a way to overcome normal MR sensitivity limitations, at least for a brief T 1‐dependent observation window. A 10 000 to 100 000‐fold signal‐to‐noise advantage provides an avenue for real‐time measurement of perfusion, metabolite transport, exchange, and metabolism. The principles behind these measurements, as well as the choice of agent, and progress toward the application of hyperpolarized 13C metabolic imaging in oncology, cardiology, and neurology are reviewed.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-354065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarization","Magnetic resonance","Magnetic resonance spectroscopic imaging","dDNP"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction to dissolution dnp overview instrumentation and human applications","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/259282496/emrstm1549_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-354065","identifier":[{"id":"85065709506","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a5cd3d32-e576-4d6b-84b5-6682aaf18e7f"],"keyword":["Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarization","Magnetic resonance","Magnetic resonance spectroscopic imaging","dDNP"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3B5C64E3E13092D7A49943C88CE9C689"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/259282496/emrstm1549_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/9780470034590.emrstm1549","issn":["20556101"],"issue":"4","journal":"eMagRes","pages":"63-78","publisher":"Blackwell Publishing","status":"p","title":"eMagRes","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065709506"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a5cd3d32-e576-4d6b-84b5-6682aaf18e7f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Introduction to dissolution DNP: Overview, instrumentation, and human applications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-354065","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This article investigates whether regime-based asset allocation can effectively respond to changes in financial regimes at the portfolio level in an effort to provide better long-term results when compared to a static 60/40 benchmark. The potential benefit from taking large positions in a few assets at a time comes at the cost of reduced diversification. The authors analyze this trade-off in a multi-asset universe with great potential for static diversification. The regime-based approach is centered around a regime-switching model with time-varying parameters that can match financial markets’ behavior and a new, more intuitive way of inferring the hidden market regimes. The empirical results show that regime-based asset allocation is profitable, even when compared to a diversified benchmark portfolio. The results are robust because they are based on available market data with no assumptions about forecasting skills.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nystrup, Peter","Hansen, Bo William","Larsen, Henrik Olejasz","Madsen, Henrik","Lindström, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-359241"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nystrup, Peter"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic allocation or diversification a regime based approach to multiple assets","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85041288600","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-359241","identifier":[{"id":"85041288600","type":"scopus"}],"i