{"abstract":"Background Patient acceptance is an important factor when implementing imaging methods in clinical practice in line with availability, diagnostic accuracy, and cost-effectiveness. Purpose To investigate patient experience and acceptance regarding18F-sodium fluoride (NaF) positron emission tomography/computed tomography (PET/CT), 11 C-choline-PET/CT, whole-body magnetic resonance imaging (WB-MRI), and 99mTc-hydroxymethane diphosphonate (HDP) single photon emission/computed tomography (SPECT/CT). Material and Methods One hundred and forty-nine patients with prostate cancer filled in a questionnaire regarding their experience of the imaging procedures they had been undergoing as part of a diagnostic accuracy study. Each patient had been undergoing a NaF-PET/CT, a WB-MRI, and either a SPECT/CT (group A) or a choline-PET/CT (group B). Results All four imaging methods received overall experience ratings at the favorable end of a 5-point Likert scale with the two PET/CT scans receiving marginally better average ratings (2.0) compared to SPECT/CT (2.2) and WB-MRI (2.3). The arm positioning above the head was the most uncomfortable part of the three nuclear medicine scans, whereas the acoustic noise was the most unpleasant part of the WB-MRI. The experience of staff instruction was relatively strongly correlated to the overall scanning experience of all four imaging modalities. Overall, the patients were willing to repeat the four imaging methods and NaF-PET/CT was the method most preferred in both groups. Conclusion Four imaging procedures were evaluated from the perspective of a selected group of prostate cancer patients. NaF-PET/CT, choline-PET/CT, WB-MRI, and bone SPECT/CT are well accepted imaging methods, and most patients prefer NaF-PET/CT.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dyrberg, Eva","Larsen, Emil L","Hendel, Helle Westergren","Thomsen, Henrik S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-454388"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms diagnostic imaging","Choline","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Acceptance of Health Care","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Prostatic Neoplasms pathology","Radiopharmaceuticals","Single Photon Emission Computed Tomography Computed Tomography","Sodium Fluoride","Surveys and Questionnaires","Whole Body Imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic bone imaging in patients with prostate cancer patient experience and acceptance of naf pet ct choline pet ct whole body mri and bone spect ct","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-454388","identifier":[{"id":"29313360","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044303125","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6608b498-80d3-4b48-b975-c8d4ce74c7a2"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms/diagnostic imaging","Choline","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Acceptance of Health Care","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Prostatic Neoplasms/pathology","Radiopharmaceuticals","Single Photon Emission Computed Tomography Computed Tomography","Sodium Fluoride","Surveys and Questionnaires","Technetium Tc 99m Medronate/analogs & derivatives","Whole Body Imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E320FD7C643A61D16CBB57957055173C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"dyrbergpau","last":"Dyrberg","name":"Dyrberg, Eva","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emil L","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle W","key":"hendelpau","last":"Hendel","locid":"0ed6dd56-8353-40da-a0d8-b1bd06e37567","name":"Hendel, Helle Westergren","name_org":"Hendel, Helle W","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik S","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c1b9dc28-6145-43cc-a1e7-c8a93ab22ec7","name":"Thomsen, Henrik S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29313360"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0284185117751280","issn":["02841851","16000455"],"issn_org":["02841851"],"issue":"9","journal":"Acta Radiologica","pages":"1119-1125","status":"p","title":"Acta Radiologica","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044303125"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6608b498-80d3-4b48-b975-c8d4ce74c7a2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diagnostic bone imaging in patients with prostate cancer : patient experience and acceptance of NaF-PET/CT, choline-PET/CT, whole-body MRI, and bone SPECT/CT","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-454388","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Elevated levels of oxidative nucleic acid modifications have been proposed to be associated with some of the clinical characteristics of Down syndrome. Oral intake of coenzyme Q10 improves oxidative status and shows a tendency toward protective effect on DNA oxidation in certain age groups of children with Down syndrome. Here, we demonstrate that long-term (i.e., 4 years) treatment with coenzyme Q10 (ubiquinone) at the dosage of 4 mg/kg/d does not affect whole body DNA and RNA oxidation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Emil List","Padella, Lucia","Bergholdt, Helle Kirstine Mørup","Henriksen, Trine","Santoro, Lucia","Gabrielli, Orazio","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","Littarru, Gian Paolo","Orlando, Patrick","Tiano, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-456857"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Administration Oral","Biomarkers urine","Child","DNA metabolism","Humans","Oxidative Stress drug effects","RNA metabolism","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of long term treatment with coenzyme q000000000010 on nucleic acid modifications by oxidation in children with down syndrome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-456857","identifier":[{"id":"85045396977","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29665577","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6a32658c-2d29-4166-8695-d6b7b39b35a5"],"keyword":["Administration, Oral","Biomarkers/urine","Child","DNA/metabolism","Deoxyadenosines/urine","Down Syndrome/drug therapy","Guanine/analogs & derivatives","Humans","Oxidation-Reduction/drug effects","Oxidative Stress/drug effects","RNA/metabolism","Time Factors","Ubiquinone/administration & dosage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"