/local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-299823","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The main purpose of wastewater treatment is to protect humans against waterborne diseases and to safeguard aquatic bio-resources like fish. The dominating environmental concerns within this domain are indeed still potential aquatic eutrophication/oxygen depletion due to nutrient/organic matter emissions and potential health impacts due to spreading of pathogens. Anyway, the use of treatment for micro-pollutants is increasing and a paradigm shift is ongoing — wastewater is more and more considered as a resource of, e.g. energy, nutrients and even polymers, in the innovations going on. The focus of LCA studies addressing wastewater treatment have from the very first published cases, been on energy and resource consumption. In recent time, the use of characterisation has increased and besides global warming potential, especially eutrophication is in focus. Even the toxicity-related impact categories are nowadays included more often. Application of LCA for comparing avoided against induced impacts, and hereby identifying trade-offs when introducing new technology, is increasingly used. A typical functional unit is the treatment of one cubic metre of wastewater which should be well defined regarding composition. Depending on the goal and scope of the study, all life cycle stages have the potential of being significant, though disposal of infrastructure seems to be the least important for the impact profile in many cases. No inventory data and none of the conventional impact categories (except stratospheric ozone depletion if emission of N2O is excluded) should be ruled out; but eutrophication and ecotoxicity are in many cases among the dominating ones.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Fred","Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","Olsen, Stig Irving"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-328748"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Road Directorate"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lca of wastewater treatment","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85037638796","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-328748","identifier":[{"id":"85037638796","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5157e5aa-6c13-40d4-a0bf-90be0c201c98"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7AD3064C7CD557A6BB11C2E8BB728DB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Road Directorate"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Zwicky","key":"hauschildped","last":"Hauschild","locid":"5c85fd08-0c76-4c6c-90c3-431093cff94b","name":"Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","orcid":"0000-0002-8331-7390","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph K.","key":"rosenbaumped","last":"Rosenbaum","locid":"c09ddfbe-dc02-4fd1-9962-f27ae586db0e","name":"Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig Irving","key":"olsenped","last":"Olsen","locid":"a9ecdd67-d38d-45d2-8dee-463cc9f1e05c","name":"Olsen, Stig Irving","orcid":"0000-0003-4599-7660","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-56475-3_34","edition":"1","eisbn":["9783319564753"],"isbn":["9783319564746"],"pages":"861-886","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Life Cycle Assessment: Theory and Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85037638796"],"sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5157e5aa-6c13-40d4-a0bf-90be0c201c98"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"LCA of Wastewater Treatment","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-328748","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Typing of methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) is important in infection control and surveillance. The current nomenclature of MRSA includes the genetic background of the S. aureus strain determined by multilocus sequence typing (MLST) or equivalent methods like spa typing and typing of the mobile genetic element staphylococcal cassette chromosome mec (SCCmec), which carries the mecA or mecC gene. Whereas MLST and spa typing are relatively simple, typing of SCCmec is less trivial because of its heterogeneity. Whole-genome sequencing (WGS) provides the essential data for typing of the genetic background and SCCmec, but so far, no bioinformatic tools for SCCmec typing have been available. Here, we report the development and evaluation of SCCmecFinder for characterization of the SCCmec element from S. aureus WGS data. SCCmecFinder is able to identify all SCCmec element types, designated I to XIII, with subtyping of SCCmec types IV (2B) and V (5C2). SCCmec elements are characterized by two different gene prediction approaches to achieve correct annotation, a Basic Local Alignment Search Tool (BLAST)-based approach and a k-mer-based approach. Evaluation of SCCmecFinder by using a diverse collection of clinical isolates (n = 93) showed a high typeability level of 96.7%, which increased to 98.9% upon modification of the default settings. In conclusion, SCCmecFinder can be an alternative to more laborious SCCmec typing methods and is freely available at https://cge.cbs.dtu.dk/services/SCCmecFinder. IMPORTANCE SCCmec in MRSA is acknowledged to be of importance not only because it contains the mecA or mecC gene but also for staphylococcal adaptation to different environments, e.g., in hospitals, the community, and livestock. Typing of SCCmec by PCR techniques has, because of its heterogeneity, been challenging, and whole-genome sequencing has only partially solved this since no good bioinformatic tools have been available. In this article, we describe the development of a new bioinformatic tool, SCCmecFinder, that includes most of the needs for infection control professionals and researchers regarding the interpretation of SCCmec elements. The software detects all of the SCCmec elements accepted by the International Working Group on the Classification of Staphylococcal Cassette Chromosome Elements, and users will be prompted if diverging and potential new elements are uploaded. Furthermore, SCCmecFinder will be curated and updated as new elements are found and it is easy to use and freely accessible.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kaya, Hülya","Hasman, Henrik","Larsen, Jesper","Stegger, Marc","Johannesen, Thor Bech","Allesøe, Rosa Lundbye","Lemvigh, Camilla K.","Aarestrup, Frank Møller","Lund, Ole","Larsen, Anders Rhod"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-332758"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Anders Rhod"],"keyword":["Bioinformatics","MRSA","SCCmec","Typing","mecA","mecC"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sccmecfinder a web based tool for typing of staphylococcal cassette chromosome mec in staphylococcus aureus using whole genome sequence data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mSphere.00612-17","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-332758","identifier":[{"id":"85048105171","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29468193","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5812897","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-5ea786e9-84f9-4e38-a668-dbf783291e5e"],"keyword":["MRSA","SCCmec","bioinformatics","mecA","mecC","typing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B59080B337BFB58772D86C2D8FC7C05D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/144522541/e00612_17.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mSphere.00612-17","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Genomic Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hülya","key":"kayahülyapau","last":"Kaya","locid":"5de68879-f6a0-4cc7-8f42-afc38236864d","name":"Kaya, Hülya","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"hasmanhenrikpau","last":"Hasman","name":"Hasman, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenjesperpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"steggermarcpau","last":"Stegger","name":"Stegger, Marc","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thor Bech","key":"johannesenthorbechpau","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Thor Bech","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rosa Lundbye","key":"allesøerosalundbyepau","last":"Allesøe","locid":"157d48b0-57be-4940-b247-ec2931222ce6","name":"Allesøe, Rosa Lundbye","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla Koldbæk","key":"lemvighcamillakpau","last":"Lemvigh","locid":"630d862f-926c-49c5-b9bd-72ff1c91eca5","name":"Lemvigh, Camilla K.","name_org":"Lemvigh, Camilla Koldbæk","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank Møller","key":"aarestrupfrankmøllerpau","last":"Aarestrup","locid":"8a1eb030-2c37-4557-bce1-7bc6d5c75aaa","name":"Aarestrup, Frank Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-7116-2723","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"lundolepau","last":"Lund","locid":"d2f5060c-0c9a-4875-820f-91180f3bb685","name":"Lund, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-1108-0491","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Rhod","key":"larsenandersrhodpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Rhod","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29468193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/msphere.00612-17","issn":["23795042"],"issn_org":["15359786"],"issue":"1","journal":"mSphere","paperid":"e00612-17","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"mSphere","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048105171"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5ea786e9-84f9-4e38-a668-dbf783291e5e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"SCCmecFinder, a Web-Based Tool for Typing of Staphylococcal Cassette Chromosome mec in Staphylococcus aureus Using Whole-Genome Sequence Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-332758","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Free radicals generated by UV-light irradiation of a frozen solution containing a fraction of pyruvic acid (PA) have demonstrated their dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dDNP) potential, providing up to 30 % [1-13C]PA liquid-state polarization. Moreover, their labile nature has proven to pave a way to nuclear polarization storage and transport. Herein, differently from the case of PA, the issue of providing dDNP UV-radical precursors (trimethylpyruvic acid and its methyl-deuterated form) not involved in any metabolic pathway was investigated. The 13C dDNP performance was evaluated for hyperpolarization of [U-13 C6 ,1,2,3,4,5,6,6-d7 ]-d-glucose. The generated UV-radicals proved to be versatile and highly efficient polarizing agents, providing, after dissolution and transfer (10 s), a 13 C liquid-state polarization of up to 32 %.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Capozzi, Andrea","Patel, Saket","Gunnarsson, Christine Pepke","Marco-Rius, Irene","Comment, Arnaud","Karlsson, Magnus","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ouari, Olivier","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335328"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Capozzi, Andrea"],"country":["France","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille Université","All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Glucose","Hyperpolarization","NMR spectroscopy","Radicals"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient hyperpolarization of u 000000000013 c glucose using narrow line uv generated labile free radicals","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/170614271/MANUSCRIPT.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335328","identifier":[{"id":"85058841775","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6531289","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30515929","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-66f92d9a-8236-406f-9029-4de0ff9aed84"],"keyword":["Glucose","Hyperpolarization","NMR spectroscopy","Radicals"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C458A7ED4015AC9066C65AD0796587D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/170614271/MANUSCRIPT.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"aix marseille université","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aix-Marseille Université","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"capozzipau","last":"Capozzi","locid":"b0cf62b2-059b-44b4-bcf7-c10bdbeda7b9","name":"Capozzi, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-2306-9049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Saket","key":"patelpau","last":"Patel","name":"Patel, Saket","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christine Pepke","key":"gunnarssonpau","last":"Gunnarsson","locid":"5835867c-bfa7-4bff-b60e-67aa921e9d93","name":"Gunnarsson, Christine Pepke","orcid":"0000-0002-8483-8024","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"marcoriuspau","last":"Marco-Rius","name":"Marco-Rius, Irene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Arnaud","key":"commentpau","last":"Comment","name":"Comment, Arnaud","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivier","key":"ouaripau","last":"Ouari","name":"Ouari, Olivier","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30515929"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/anie.201810522","issn":["14337851","15213773"],"issn_org":["14337851"],"journal":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","title_org":"ANGEWANDTE CHEMIE","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058841775"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-66f92d9a-8236-406f-9029-4de0ff9aed84"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Efficient Hyperpolarization of U-13 C-Glucose Using Narrow-Line UV-Generated Labile Free Radicals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335328","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Despite the technological advancement of modern hearing aids, many users leave their devices unused due to little perceived benefit. This problem arises from the limitations of the current fitting procedure that rarely takes into account 1) the perceptual differences between users not explained by measurable hearing loss characteristics and 2) the variation in context-specific preferences within individuals. However, the recent emergence of smartphoneconnected hearings aids opens the door to a new level of context awareness that can facilitate dynamic adaptation of settings to users' changing needs. In this position paper, we discuss how user auditory intents could be modeled as context collected via mobile devices and suggest what kinds of contextual information are relevant when learning situation-specific intents and the corresponding preferences of hearing impaired users. Finally, we illustrate our ideas with several examples of real-life situations experienced by subjects from our study.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Korzepa, Maciej Jan","Johansen, Benjamin","Petersen, Michael Kai","Larsen, Jan","Larsen, Jakob Eg","Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343988"],"event":{"end":"2018-07-11","place":"Singapore, sg","start":"2018-07-08","title":"26<sup>th</sup> Conference on User Modeling, Adaptation and Personalization","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Context awareness","User adaptation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling user intents as context in smartphone connected hearing aids","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85051485164","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343988","identifier":[{"id":"85051485164","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-83f6b42d-e67a-44c6-b84a-adb3f81b00a3"],"keyword":["Augmented hearing","Context awareness","User adaptation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0810B344BD751A5A4660B18A313A7A21"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"oticon","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTI","l3nl":"Oticon A/S","l3nn":"Oticon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oticon","namevar":["Oticon Danmark AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maciej Jan","key":"korzepamaciejjanpau","last":"Korzepa","locid":"33872b3c-235a-453a-80d5-e82faec48916","name":"Korzepa, Maciej Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benjamin","key":"johansenbenjaminpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"3c721ddf-2426-4b69-ac27-00a5847c25fd","name":"Johansen, Benjamin","orcid":"0000-0002-6516-4757","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Kai","key":"petersenmichaelkaipau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0184dad5-da00-4ca8-b00a-53165ce84766","name":"Petersen, Michael Kai","orcid":"0000-0002-2156-9226","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"larsenjanpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"172b79ba-ccb1-4bea-8cd3-30dfd62f4624","name":"Larsen, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-1880-1810","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Eg","key":"larsenjakobegpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"691c8ae7-9a21-4b98-9b91-5e2d9806a4b9","name":"Larsen, Jakob Eg","orcid":"0000-0002-7461-9901","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"pontoppidannielshenrikpau","last":"Pontoppidan","name":"Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3213586.3226211","isbn":["9781450357845"],"pages":"151-155","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 26th Conference on User Modeling, Adaptation and Personalization"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051485164"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Oticon A/S","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-83f6b42d-e67a-44c6-b84a-adb3f81b00a3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Modeling user intents as context in smartphone-connected hearing AIDS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343988","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarization via dissolutiondynamic nuclear polarization(dDNP) is crucial to significantly increasing the magnetic resonanceimaging (MRI) sensitivity, opening up in vivo real-time MRI using 13C-labeled substrates. The range of applications, however,is limited by the relatively fast decay of the nuclear spin polarizationtogether with the constraint of having to polarize the spins nearthe MRI magnet. As recently demonstrated, the employment of UV-inducednonpersistent radicals represents an elegant solution to tacklingthese drawbacks. Nevertheless, since its introduction, the spreadof the technique has been prevented by the relatively low achievablepolarization, slow buildup time, and time-consuming sample preparation.In the present work, thanks to a thorough investigation of the radicalgeneration step, we provide a robust protocol to enhance the efficiencyand performance of the UV-radical technique. Under optimal conditions,it was possible to produce up to 60 mM radical in less than 5 minand reach maximum DNP enhancement with a buildup time constant ofapproximately 25 min at 6.7 T and 1 K, resulting in 30% 13C liquid-state polarization.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Capozzi, Andrea","Karlsson, Magnus","Petersen, Jan Raagaard","Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360081"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Capozzi, Andrea"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liquid state sup 000000000013 sup c polarization of 000000000030 through photoinduced nonpersistent radicals","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/176486808/JPCC_optimized_UV_PA_Capozzi_et_al_revision1_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360081","identifier":[{"id":"85045077157","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b9ab4bc8-a5f9-4961-9f58-5cbcbfb00eec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E5D0BBB8327A0E0C4400EF98BB93993B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/176486808/JPCC_optimized_UV_PA_Capozzi_et_al_revision1_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"capozzipau","last":"Capozzi","locid":"b0cf62b2-059b-44b4-bcf7-c10bdbeda7b9","name":"Capozzi, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-2306-9049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"b36d1ae3-33f2-4b98-9112-fbe3e155be82","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-1700","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Raagaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"bbaeda22-d4b8-4371-b87c-e76f77d54014","name":"Petersen, Jan Raagaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3194-5798","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","locid":"bf55c4cb-8ebc-4c00-a107-f90c312e6e76","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","orcid":"0000-0002-5899-2781","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpcc.8b01482","issn":["19327447","19327455"],"issn_org":["19327447"],"issue":"13","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","pages":"7432-7443","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","volume":"122"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045077157"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b9ab4bc8-a5f9-4961-9f58-5cbcbfb00eec"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Liquid-State <sup>13</sup>C Polarization of 30% through Photoinduced Nonpersistent Radicals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-360081","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Advancing Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) technology requires integration of the MRI scanners with sensors and systems for monitoring various non-MRI signals. In this paper, we present design and integration of a low power AM radio transmitter into a 3T MRI scanner, which can be used for efficient collection of data from non-MRI sensors. The transmitter consumes only 1.3mW while transmitting 2.7µW at 120MHz with high frequency stability. The presented design is useful in low power applications requiring high frequency stability and is intended for wireless transmission of non-MR signal recordings during MRI scanning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Petersen, Jan Raagaard","Pedersen, Jan Ole","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Hanson, Lars G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365991"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-21","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2018-06-16","title":"Joint Annual Meeting ISMRM-ESMRMB 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultra low power transmitter for encoding non mr signals in magnetic resonance mr recordings","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149166407/ISMRM18_1736_JanOscillator.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365991","ids":["dtu-cdc70938-ba34-49c1-b8ff-b53433c081e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-11FEE6E903AFC33DBF9D1C5519570350"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149166407/ISMRM18_1736_JanOscillator.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical univer