{"abstract":"This chapter discusses how practice theory can help us to connect running and tourism, and explains how, and why, what it might term 'running tourism'. It argues that practice theory and tourism studies can enrich each other, as everyday practices and tourism practices increasingly overlap. The chapter focuses on developing a practice approach to running and running events in three-fold of research questions. First, it discusses how can we understand running as a differentiated practice? Second, why does running now attract so many practitioners? Thirdly, how do practices of running connect with practices of tourism? The chapter draws together marathons and tourism by discussing the literature on sport/running tourism and by briefly discussing the ongoing tourism research on the two running events: the Berlin Marathon and Etape Bornholm. Practice theory is yet to make a sustained impact on tourist studies where economic models and cultural theories about representation, discourses and gazing prevail","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-569988"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"running and tourism a practice approach","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-569988","identifier":[{"id":"85060002254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-d09a6a49-3c85-40cf-aeef-9a8d4f0afb41"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E5334691CAC67E753415A73E98EB62AE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Space, Place, Mobility and Urban Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1cb27156-b919-462a-9243-4ab2d8f87f26","name":"Larsen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-8119","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Laura","key":"jamespedh","last":"James","name":"James, Laura","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Canria","key":"renpedh","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Canria","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"halkierpedh","last":"Halkier","name":"Halkier, Henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9781315162171-4","eisbn":["9781315162171"],"isbn":["9781138061705"],"pages":"41-57","place":"Abingdon","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Theories of Practice in Tourism"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-d09a6a49-3c85-40cf-aeef-9a8d4f0afb41"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Running and tourism : A practice approach","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-569988","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Ship’s ballast water has been a vector for the spreading of nonindigenous invasive species (NIS) around the globe for more than a century and has had devastating impact on aquatic ecosystems in many regions. Due to the harsh climate, shipping activities in Arctic waters have been limited compared to many parts of the world but will increase in the coming years due to climate changes. This will potentially affect the pristine Arctic marine ecosystems by introduction of NIS. In this chapter, we present the international ballast water regulations that have entered into force and the specific challenges of ballast water management in relation to the Arctic environment and marine ecosystems. We discuss the risk of NIS affecting the Arctic marine ecosystems including the impact of increased shipping activity, changes in living conditions of marine organisms because of climate changes and lack of knowledge of the eco-physiological boundaries and distributions of Arctic marine species. It is concluded that at present only a few marine NIS have been recorded in the Arctic area. Despite the existing and planned ballast water regulations, NIS establishment in the region will increase with an unknown magnitude due to lack of biological data.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Holbech, Henrik","Pedersen, Knud Ladegaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-607254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Arctic marine ecosystems","Climate changes","IMO"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ballast water and invasive species in the arctic","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85056986885","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-607254","identifier":[{"id":"85056986885","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-76de4809-434b-43dd-93d3-aea5c97c533d"],"keyword":["Arctic marine ecosystems","Ballast water regulations","Climate changes","HELCOM/OSPAR","IMO","Nonindigenous invasive species","Ship’s ballast water","US Coast Guard"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78C91A384AF6BA895671EDF54841301E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holbechpau","last":"Holbech","locid":"8aa38e7d-ae8b-422b-abb7-06cd6c20ffd8","name":"Holbech, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-5174-9458","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud Ladegaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bdfc62ce-6d8a-4479-aa2d-63ca4fe70568","name":"Pedersen, Knud Ladegaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels","key":"vestergaardpedh","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Niels","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brooks","key":"akaiserpedh","last":"A. Kaiser","name":"A. Kaiser, Brooks","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"fernandezpedh","last":"Fernandez","name":"Fernandez, Linda","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joan Nymand","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Joan Nymand","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-67365-3_7","eisbn":["9783319673653"],"isbn":["9783319673646"],"pages":"115-137","publisher":"Springer","series":"Springer Polar Sciences","status":"p","title":"Arctic Marine Resource Governance and Development"},"review":"Undetermined","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056986885"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-76de4809-434b-43dd-93d3-aea5c97c533d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ballast Water and Invasive Species in the Arctic","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-607254","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
