","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdóttirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Maria Gunnleivsdottir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdottirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdottir","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771563306"],"pages":"876","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus University","repno":"Scientific Report from DCE – Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","series":"Scientific Report from DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6c6d485a-9300-4e45-8e1c-76f9e9f90f8b","ku-2d036f65-725d-46ba-82af-da6007945f7a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denmark's National Inventory Report 2018 : Emission Inventories 1990-2016 - Submitted under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Kyoto Protocol","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.89-020588","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Integrated buffer zones (IBZs) represent a novel form of edge-of-field technology in Northwest Europe. Contrary to the common riparian buffer strips, IBZs collect tile drainage water from agricultural fields by combining a ditch-like pond (POND), where soil particles can settle, and a flow-through filter bed (FILTERBED) planted with Alnus glutinosa (L.), a European alder (black alder). The first experimental IBZ facility was constructed and thoroughly tested in Denmark for its capability to retain various nitrogen (N) and phosphorus (P) species within the first three years after construction. We calculated the water and nutrient budget for the total IBZ and for the two compartments, POND and FILTERBED, separately. Furthermore, a tracer experiment using sodium bromide was conducted in order to trace the water flow and estimate the hydraulic residence time in the FILTERBEDs. The monthly average removal efficiency amounted to 10-67% for total N and 31-69% for total P, with performance being highest during the warm season. Accordingly, we suggest that IBZs may be a valuable modification of dry buffer strips in order to mitigate the adverse impacts of high nutrient loading from agricultural fields on the aquatic environment.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Zak, Dominik Henrik","Kronvang, Brian","Carstensen, Mette Vodder","Hoffmann, Carl Christian","Kjeldgaard, Ane","Larsen, Soren E.","Audet, Joachim","Egemose, Sara","Jorgensen, Charlotte A.","Feuerbach, Peter","Gertz, Flemming","Jensen, Henning S."],"cuid":["S02-095.05-028051"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zak, Dominik Henrik"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz-Institute of Freshwater Ecology and Inland Fisheries","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences"],"keyword":["Constructed wetlands","Denitrification","Eutrophication","Fresh Water","Harmful algal blooms","Nitrate","Organic carbon","Release","Riparian zones","Water quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nitrogen and phosphorus removal from agricultural runoff in integrated buffer zones","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/143271017/Nitrogen_and_phosphorus_removal_from_agricultural_runoff_in_integrated_buffer_zones.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-095.05-028051","identifier":[{"id":"29733209","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85046711812","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000434892900046","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-d48099bb-51b6-47ba-a489-c93c70613fff","sdu-75ceea45-1fab-41f5-9668-c24a5a2d89bd"],"keyword":["CONSTRUCTED WETLANDS","DENITRIFICATION","EUTROPHICATION","FRESH-WATER","HARMFUL ALGAL BLOOMS","NITRATE","ORGANIC-CARBON","RELEASE","RIPARIAN ZONES","WATER-QUALITY"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-618FFF145CB8E520A45423C705BDDB8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/143271017/Nitrogen_and_phosphorus_removal_from_agricultural_runoff_in_integrated_buffer_zones.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences