{"abstract":"This paper presents two tools for evaluation of the indoor environment in social housing, developed as part of the REBUS project. The main aim of the paper is to present the tool, a questionnaire for evaluation of tenants’ perceived problems and satisfaction with the indoor environment. Based on the experience gained from a previous study that applied a similar questionnaire, a procedure for evaluation of the perceived indoor environment in social housing before and after a renovation work is proposed. The procedure includes a questionnaire and a distribution procedure of the questionnaire to the tenants to ensure the highest possible response rate. The questionnaire is intended to be used before the renovation work to identify the initially most pronounced indoor environment problems, thus allowing for a targeted problem solving adding the most value for the tenants. After the renovation work the questionnaire may be applied to document whether the defined goals for the indoor environment have been reached. The usefulness as well as some challenges in applying a questionnaire is exemplified by the results of an evaluation of the perceived indoor environment of a renovated social housing settlement.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","Larsen, Tine Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120753"],"event":{"acronym":"Indoor Air","end":"2018-07-27","place":"Philadelphia, us","start":"2018-07-22","title":"Indoor Air 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Building renovation","Energy savings","Indoor climate","Indoor environment","Questionnaire survey","Social housing","Tenant s satisfaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of the perceived indoor environment before and after renovation of social housing","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.indoorair2018.org/images/IA2018-Paper-List.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-120753","ids":["aau-f329bbf5-329f-4e93-a96b-3eeb7dd0a24b"],"keyword":["Building renovation","Energy savings","Indoor environment","Social housing","Tenant’s satisfaction","evaluation tools","indoor climate","questionnaire survey","tenant’s experience and satisfaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9C1E11FBB80ADF0B7E05C6F5B5EFD19F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Department of Energy Performance, Indoor Environment and Sustainability of Buildings (EIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Energy Efficiency Research Group (SBi)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Energy and Buildings Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Indoor Environmental Quality and Building Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Nellemose","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"7f5e707b-235a-4e71-ae71-e9278e7aa2ba","name":"Knudsen, Henrik Nellemose","orcid":"0000-0002-3196-7279","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},