{"abstract":"Et meget vigtigt aspekt af moderne ledelse er håndtering af ledelsesdilemmaer, det vil sige beslutningssituationer, hvor der til de forskellige handlemulighedermknytter sig en vifte af fordele og ulemper. Dilemmaer kanikke som sådan \"løses\" og lægges til side, men man kan blive bedre til at navigere i den skærgård, som dilemmaerne udgør.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-277193"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dilemmaledelse baner vej","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.e-pages.dk/lederne/2016493452/4/?query=copenhagen+business+school","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-277193","ids":["cbs-1318e2a6-2d8d-4294-a31f-71bdba1b91ec"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EE46FFDD359364BE3A2E4CE4D22FC659"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.e-pages.dk/lederne/2016493452/4/?query=copenhagen+business+school","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pia Funch","key":"braskhøjpedh","last":"Braskhøj","name":"Braskhøj, Pia Funch","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Dahlgaard","key":"pøhlerpedh","last":"Pøhler","name":"Pøhler, Jesper Dahlgaard","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788790313951"],"issn":["09058966"],"issue":"Special edition 2018-2019","pages":"66-72","place":"København","publisher":"Lederne","series":"Ledelse i Dag","status":"p","title":"Paradokser i ledelse"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-1318e2a6-2d8d-4294-a31f-71bdba1b91ec"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Dilemmaledelse baner vej","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-277193","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"For magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) receive coil arrays, an ideal low-noise amplifier (LNA) is noise matched while exhibiting a high-input reflection coefficient of unity or slightly higher. For this purpose, we present a design approach allowing to manipulate the optimal noise impedance and input impedance. The method is based on noise and S-parameters, hence technology independent. As an example, the method is used to design an LNA for MRI receive coil arrays operating at 32.1 MHz. The design demonstrates the highest coil decoupling published so far of 54 dB. The measured noise figure of 0.44 dB is also better than other published designs. The measured gain is 22 dB with a 1-dB compression point of -14.5 dBm. The power consumption is 81 mW. We expect this method to enable better MRI receive coil array designs resulting in lower examination time and cost due to higher quality images.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305309"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup"],"keyword":["Biomedical imaging","Design methodology","Gain","Impedance matching","Magnetic resonance","Noise figure","Scattering parameters"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association and dissociation of optimal noise and input impedance for low noise amplifiers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/158484684/hkkr_08475031.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-305309","identifier":[{"id":"85054367221","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-027e966c-d386-4c46-b5c8-f31cf1bdfb38"],"keyword":["Biomedical imaging","Design methodology","Gain","Impedance matching","Low-noise amplifiers (LNAs)","Magnetic resonance","Noise figure","Optimized circuit design","Scattering parameters"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-814F01B4BF4BD7430C13CA966175E8CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/170360438/FINAL_VERSION_002_.PDF","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/158484684/hkkr_08475031.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan D.","key":"sanchezherediapau","last":"Sanchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sanchez-Heredia, Juan D.","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tmtt.2018.2869603","issn":["00189480","15579670"],"issn_org":["00189480"],"issue":"12","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Microwave Theory and Techniques","pages":"5290-5299","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Microwave Theory and Techniques","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054367221"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-027e966c-d386-4c46-b5c8-f31cf1bdfb38"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Association and Dissociation of Optimal Noise and Input Impedance for Low-Noise Amplifiers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305309","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Near-infrared photoimmunotherapy (NIR PIT) employs the photoabsorbing dye IR700 conjugated to antibodies specific for cell surface epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR). NIR PIT has shown highly selective cytotoxicity in vitro and in vivo. Cell necrosis is thought to be the main mode of cytotoxicity based mainly on in vitro studies. To better understand the acute effects of NIR PIT, molecular imaging studies were performed to assess its cellular and vascular effects.In addition to in vitro studies for cytotoxicity of NIR PIT, the in vivo tumoricidal effects and hemodynamic changes induced by NIR PIT were evaluated by C-13 MRI using hyperpolarized [1,4-C-13(2)] fumarate, R-2* mapping from T-2*-weighted MRI, and photoacoustic imaging. In vitro studies confirmed that NIR PIT resulted in rapid cell death via membrane damage, with evidence for rapid cell expansion followed by membrane rupture. Following NIR PIT, metabolic MRI using hyperpolarized fumarate showed the production of malate in EGFR-expressing A431 tumor xenografts, providing direct evidence for photosensitized tumor necrosis induced by NIR PIT. R2* mapping studies showed temporal changes in oxygenation, with an accompanying increase of deoxyhemoglobin at the start of light exposure followed by a sustained decrease after cessation of light exposure. This result suggests a rapid decrease of blood flow in EGFR-expressing A431 tumor xenografts, which is supported by the results of the photoacoustic imaging experiments. Our findings suggest NIR PIT mediates necrosis and hemodynamic changes in tumors by photosensitized oxidation pathways and that these imaging modalities, once translated, may be useful in monitoring clinical treatment response.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kishimoto, Shun","Oshima, Nobu","Yamamoto, Kazutoshi","Munasinghe, Jeeva","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Mitchell, James B.","Choyke, Peter L.","Krishna, Murali C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316504"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Krishna, Murali C."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Cancer Institute United States","National Institute of Neurological Disease and Stroke"],"keyword":["C 13 MRI","Photoacoustic imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular imaging of tumor photoimmunotherapy evidence of photosensitized tumor necrosis and hemodynamic changes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/190884153/nihms933296.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316504","identifier":[{"id":"85039796372","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29289705","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5963721","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-28223d61-f8af-42ee-af3c-eb976a643d0f"],"keyword":["C-13 MRI","Hemodynamic change","Photoacoustic imaging","Photoimmunotherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F0982408807CADF79ADA7A8D513AE04B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/190884153/nihms933296.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"national cancer institute united states","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Cancer Institute United States","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"national institute of neurological disease and stroke","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Institute of Neurological Disea