{"abstract":"MRI with hyperpolarized tracers has enabled new diagnostic applications, e.g. metabolic imaging in cancer research. However, the acquisition of the transient, hyperpolarized signal with spatial and frequency resolution requires dedicated imaging methods. Here, we compare three promising candidates for 2D MR spectroscopic imaging (MRSI): (i) multi-echo balanced steady-state free precession (me-bSSFP), 1,2 (ii) echo planar spectroscopic imaging (EPSI) sequence and (iii) phase-encoded, pulseacquisition chemical-shift imaging (CSI)","author_count":9,"contributors":["Müller, C. A.","Hansen, Rie Beck","Skinner, J. G.","Eldirdiri, A.","Leupold, J.","Hennig, J.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Hansen, A.E.","Hövener, J. - B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-329346"],"event":{"end":"2018-03-23","place":"San Sebastián, es","start":"2018-03-20","title":"13th European Molecular Imaging Meeting","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kiel University","University of Freiburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"signal to noise comparison of metabolic imaging methods on a clinical 000000000003t mri","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/143090307/2017_11_EMIM_ABSTRACT_CM_FINAL.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-329346","ids":["dtu-535eb97f-b379-4452-959d-0d8603d4600c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8280AABA28A0815ED7AE5DE94EE1C845"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/143090307/2017_11_EMIM_ABSTRACT_CM_FINAL.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"kiel university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Kiel University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C. A.","key":"müllercapau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, C. A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rie Beck","key":"hansenriebeckpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J. G.","key":"skinnerjgpau","last":"Skinner","name":"Skinner, J. G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"eldirdiriapau","last":"Eldirdiri","name":"Eldirdiri, A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"leupoldjpau","last":"Leupold","name":"Leupold, J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"hennigjpau","last":"Hennig","name":"Hennig, J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenjanhenrikpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A.E.","key":"hansenaepau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, A.E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"J. - B.","key":"hövenerjbpau","last":"Hövener","name":"Hövener, J. - B.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-535eb97f-b379-4452-959d-0d8603d4600c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Signal to noise comparison of metabolic imaging methods on a clinical 3T MRI","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-329346","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Metabolite profiles and their isotopomer distributions can be studied non-invasively in complex mixtures with NMR. The advent of dissolution Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (dDNP) and isotope enrichment add sensitivity and resolution to such met-abolic studies. Metabolic pathways and networks can be mapped and quantified if protocols that control and exploit the ex situ sig-nal enhancement are created. We present a sample preparation method, including cell incubation, extraction and signal enhance-ment, to facilitate reproducible and quantitative dDNP (qdDNP) NMR-based isotope tracer analysis. We further illustrate how qdDNP was applied to gain systematic and novel metabolic phenotypic insights into aggressive cancer cells.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Yigit, Demet","Frahm, Anne Birk","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Malinowski, Ronja Maja","Jensen, Pernille Rose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331873"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stable isotope resolved analysis with quantitative dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/140500319/acs.analchem.7b02779.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331873","identifier":[{"id":"85040183673","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29200272","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-5be1958f-222b-4ef7-8868-3f9b04d1d887"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-795B1FAC4D1AAEC90478D4CE72DBEF7C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/140500319/acs.analchem.7b02779.pdf","ve