nsen","locid":"945cf0b9-5a16-4e82-a927-c9c42c2467b2","name":"Jensen, Pernille Rose","orcid":"0000-0003-4359-848X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29200272"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.7b02779","issn":["00032700","15204782"],"issn_org":["00032700"],"issue":"1","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","pages":"674-678","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Analytical Chemistry","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040183673"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5be1958f-222b-4ef7-8868-3f9b04d1d887"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Stable isotope-resolved analysis with quantitative dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-331873","year":"2018","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Microwave sample irradiation is essential to perform DNP. Waveguides provide an effective way of coupling the output of a microwave source to the electron spins. Indivertibly, the waveguide introduces a significant thermal heat load into the sample space of our dDNP probe. The use of a circular stainless steel waveguide with an internally electroplated layer of copper offers an effective, economical solution to address this problem.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Albannay, Mohammed M.","Vinther, Joachim M.","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364577"],"event":{"end":"2018-09-05","place":"Southampton , gb","start":"2018-09-02","title":"International Conference on Nuclear Hyperpolarization 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low microwave attenuation and low thermal loss waveguides for ddnp probes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164879226/Poster_Low_loss_low_thermal_loading_microwave_structures_for_dDNP_probes.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364577","ids":["dtu-c8f56618-f547-442b-afc6-232dffaa86d7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F2DDBAD25313BEB4B3791D8E52E5BE77"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164879226/Poster_Low_loss_low_thermal_loading_microwave_structures_for_dDNP_probes.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammed M.","key":"albannaypau","last":"Albannay","locid":"2cb48487-30c9-4d3e-81d8-52475a08025e","name":"Albannay, Mohammed M.","orcid":"0000-0002-6635-8844","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim M.","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","locid":"ea849433-5b54-41be-8972-8948a094d660","name":"Vinther, Joachim M.","orcid":"0000-0003-4930-3179","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan H.","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c8f56618-f547-442b-afc6-232dffaa86d7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Low microwave attenuation and low thermal loss waveguides for dDNP probes","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-364577","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The experimentation with a movable outdoor electroluminescence (EL) testbed is performed in this work. For EL inspections of PV power plants, the fastest scenario will include the use of unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) performing image acquisition in continuous motion. With this motivation, we investigate the EL image quality of an acquisition in motion and the extent of image processing required to correct scene displacement. The results show processed EL images with a high level of information even when acquired at 1 m/s camera speed and at frame rate of 120 fps.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Benatto, Gisele Alves dos Reis","Mantel, Claire","Riedel, Nicholas","Santamaria Lancia, Adrian Alejo","Thorsteinsson, Sune","Poulsen, Peter Behrensdorff","Forchhammer, Søren","Thorseth, Anders","Dam-Hansen, Carsten","Kenn H. B., Frederiksen","Vedde, Jan","Larsen, Michael","Voss, Henrik","Parikh, Harsh","Spataru, Sergiu","Sera, Dezso"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-368997"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-15","place":"Waikoloa, us","start":"2018-06-10","title":"7th World Conference on Photovoltaic Energy Conversion","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Electroluminescence","PV inspections","PV reliability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["SiCon"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outdoor electroluminescence acquisition using a movable testbed","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150160600/Paper_Moving_EL.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-368997","identifier":[{"id":"85059918133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-