{"abstract":"Background: Low foetal vitamin D status may be associated with higher blood pressure (BP) in later life. Objective: To examine whether serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D 2+3 (s-25OHD) in cord and pregnancy associates with systolic and diastolic BP (SBP; DBP) in children up to 3 years of age. Design: Prospective, population-based cohort study. Methods: We included 1594 singletons from the Odense Child Cohort with available cord s-25OHD and BP data at median age 3.7 months (48% girls), 18.9 months (44% girls) or 3 years (48% girls). Maternal s-25OHD was also assessed at gestational ages 12 and 29 weeks. Multiple regression models were stratified by sex a priori and adjusted for maternal educational level, season of birth and child height, weight and age. Results: In 3-year-old girls, SBP decreased with −0.7 mmHg (95% CI −1.1; −0.3, P = 0.001) and DBP with −0.4 mmHg (95% CI −0.7; −0.1, P = 0.016) for every 10 nmol/L increase in cord s-25OHD in adjusted analyses. Moreover, the adjusted odds of having SBP >90th percentile were reduced by 30% for every 10 nmol/L increase in cord s-25OHD (P = 0.004) and by 64% for cord s-25OHD above the median 45.1 nmol/L (P = 0.02). Similar findings were observed between pregnancy s-25OHD and 3-year SBP, cord s-25OHD and SBP at 18.9 months, and cord s-25OHD and DBP at 3 years. No consistent associations were observed between s-25OHD and BP in boys. Conclusion: Cord s-25OHD was inversely associated with SBP and DBP in young girls, but not in boys. Higher vitamin D status in foetal life may modulate BP in young girls. The sex difference remains unexplained.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Søs Dragsbæk","Dalgård, Christine","Christensen, Mathilde Egelund","Lykkedegn, Sine","Andersen, Louise Bjørkholt","Andersen, Marianne","Glintborg, Dorte","Christesen, Henrik Thybo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-622751"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Søs Dragsbæk"],"keyword":["Blood Pressure","Children","Sex dimorphism","Vitamin D"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blood pressure in 000000000003 year old girls associates inversely with umbilical cord serum 000000000025 hydroxyvitamin d an odense child cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-18-0308","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-622751","identifier":[{"id":"30533001","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6240151","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30352408","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065073036","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-acfc5696-64fd-4f2e-bca4-76a9687d365f"],"keyword":["Blood pressure","Children","Sex-dimorphism","Vitamin D"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46123CC3288DF3EF79AB3C6A253D8238"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-18-0308","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/144362452/Blood_pressure_in_3_year_old_girls_associates.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søs Drags