{"abstract":"13C Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy (MRS) using hyperpolarized 13C-labeled pyruvate as a substrate offers a measure of pyruvate-lactate interconversion and is thereby a marker of the elevated aerobic glycolysis (Warburg effect) generally exhibited by cancer cells. Here, we aim to compare hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate MRS with simultaneous 18F-2-fluoro-2-deoxy-D-glucose (FDG) PET in a cross-sectional study of canine cancer patients. Methods: Canine cancer patients underwent integrated PET/MRI using a clinical whole-body system. Hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate was obtained using dissolution-DNP. 18F-FDG PET, dynamic 13C MRS, 13C MRS Imaging (MRSI) and anatomical 1 H MRI was acquired from 17 patients. Apparent pyruvate-to-lactate rate constants were estimated from dynamic 13C MRS. 18F-FDG Standard Uptake Values and maximum [1-13C]lactate-to-total-13C ratios were obtained from tumor regions of interest. Following inspection of data, patients were grouped according to main cancer type and linear regression between measures of lactate generation and 18FFDG uptake were tested within groups. Between groups, the same measures were tested for group differences. Results: The main cancer types of the 17 patients were sarcoma (n = 11), carcinoma (n = 5) and mastocytoma (n = 1). Significant correlations between pyruvate-to-lactate rate constants and 18F-FDG uptake were found for sarcoma patients, whereas no significant correlations appeared for carcinoma patients. The sarcoma patients showed a non-significant trend towards lower 18F-FDG uptake and higher lactate generation than carcinoma patients. However, the ratio of lactate generation to 18F-FDG uptake was found to be significantly higher in sarcoma as compared to carcinoma. The results were found both when lactate generation was estimated as an apparent pyruvate-to-lactate rate constant from dynamic 13C MRS and as an [1-13C]lactate to total 13C ratio from 13C MRSI. Conclusions: A comparison of hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate MRS with simultaneous 18F-FDG PET indicate that lactate generation and 18F-FDG uptake in cancers can be related and that their relation depend on cancer type. This finding could be important for the interpretation and eventual clinical implementation of hyperpolarized 13C. In addition, the differences between the two modalities may allow for better metabolic phenotyping performing hybrid imaging in the form of hyperPET","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hansen, Adam E.","Gutte, Henrik","Holst, Pernille","Johannesen, Helle H.","Rahbek, Sofie","Clemmensen, Andreas E.","Larsen, Majbritt M.E.","Schøier, Christina","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Klausen, Thomas L.","Kristensen, Annemarie T.","Kjær, Andreas"],"cuid":["S02-086.10-032835"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Adam E."],"keyword":["FDG PET","Glycolysis","Hyperpolarization","MRS","PET MRI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combined hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate mrs and sup 000000000018 sup f fdg pet hyperpet estimates of glycolysis in canine cancer patients","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejrad.2018.02.028","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.10-032835","identifier":[{"id":"000433201500002","type":"wos"},{"id":"85044577188","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29803387","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-0b0b26f8-9054-4b42-9969-93d158adbe31","ku-b3fc3574-5366-47de-9593-0754a6a2505e"],"keyword":["FDG-PET","Glycolysis","Hyperpolarization","MRS","PET/MRI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9DF2551281F52D47C1F1DE47E79D49F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejrad.2018.02.028","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/145858533/PIIS0720048X18300755.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"guttepau","last":"Gutte","locid":"c7c7ba68-3373-4d28-9c52-1df481849fb7","name":"Borgwardt, Henrik Gutte","name_org":"Gutte, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"acec9b26-a223-482f-8b9f-7622cd704e67","name":"Holst, Pernille","orcid":"0000-0002-3037-7349","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle H.","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Helle H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie","key":"rahbekpau","last":"Rahbek","name":"Rahbek, Sofie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas E.","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"5f1471f7-ae5b-4864-bdab-f57d5e4b8566","name":"Clemmensen, Andreas","name_org":"Clemmensen, Andreas E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Majbritt M. E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0b9341a0-27ca-4d8d-bdee-d5ce50c02956","name":"Larsen, Majbritt M. E.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"schoierpau","last":"Schoier","locid":"c334c96e-ffcf-441f-b4c3-3b9ac5a53876","name":"Schoier, Christina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas L.","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","locid":"1119807a-9526-4fb5-9f8f-16e4e4624514","name":"Levin Andersen, Thomas","name_org":"Klausen, Thomas L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6981-7276","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Annemarie T.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a7007b3a-f743-46be-8a05-6473fd440756","name":"Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","name_org":"Kristensen, Annemarie T.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29803387"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejrad.2018.02.028","issn":["0720048X","18727727"],"issn_org":["0720048X"],"journal":"European Journal of Radiology","pages":"6-12","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Radiology","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044577188"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0b0b26f8-9054-4b42-9969-93d158adbe31","ku-b3fc3574-5366-47de-9593-0754a6a2505e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combined Hyperpolarized <sup>13</sup>C-pyruvate MRS and <sup>18</sup>F-FDG PET (HyperPET) Estimates of Glycolysis in Canine Cancer Patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.10-032835","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To evaluate the positive predictive value (PPV) of ICD-10 diagnosis codes for brain abscess in the Danish National Patient Registry (DNPR). Patients and methods: We examined medical records of all patients with a first-time diagnosis code of brain abscess in the DNPR from 2007 to 2016. Patients were categorized with either confirmed or disproved brain abscess using a priori defined criteria. We computed the PPV as the proportion of confirmed diagnoses. Results: We identified 709 patients, of whom the medical records could not be retrieved for 15 patients, leaving 694 for further analyses. Of these, 444 had a confirmed brain abscess and 250 had another proven diagnosis, including 47 cases of intracranial empyema. The overall PPV was 64% (95% CI: 60–68) ranging from 24% to 96% among the different codes evaluated. By including only patients with either 1) both a diagnosis and surgical procedure code for brain abscess or 2) patients admitted to hospital with certain primary diagnosis codes (DG060[C,E,F] or DG079B) without newly diagnosed central nervous system (CNS) cancer, spondylodiscitis/intraspinal abscess, or procedure codes for evacuation of intracranial empyema, the PPV increased to 84% (95% CI 80–87) and 89% (395/444) of all confirmed cases were identified. Conclusion: The overall PPV of diagnosis codes for brain abscess in the DNPR was moderate. However, by exclusion of newly diagnosed CNS tumors, spondylodiscitis/intraspinal abscess, and intracranial empyemas, the PPV was high and therefore suitable for future registry-based studies of brain abscess.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bodilsen, Jacob","Dalager-Pedersen, Michael","Kjærgaard, Nicolai","van de Beek, Diederik","Brouwer, Matthijs C","Nielsen, Henrik","Bodilsen, Jacob","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-087.23-001527"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["DASGIB study group","Danish Study Group of Infections of the Brain (DASGIB)"],"keyword":["Cerebral abscess","Epidemiology","Intracranial abscess","PPV","Register"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"positive predictive value of icd 000000000010 diagnosis codes for brain abscess in the danish national patient registry","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S176072","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.23-001527","identifier":[{"id":"30349397","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6190620","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000447346200003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85057762163","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1e54c0e1-1425-4bcf-9371-a2b2b57ee397","sdu-0ab3a41f-8f52-4a7c-9a76-9b24e4d90b65"],"keyword":["Cerebral abscess","Epidemiology","Intracranial abscess","PPV","Register"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B5619ACE11FD81F18F4ACFB5A15522FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/294335570/clep_176072_positive_predictive_value_of_icd_10_diagnosis_codes_for_brai_101118_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S176072","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/156143739/Positive_predictive_value_of_ICD_10_diagnosis_codes_for_brain_abscess_in_the_Danish_National_Patient_Registry.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3n