 B.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"31f07839-f4e2-44f2-8668-3bd6d1a24b2f","name":"Hansen, Morten Bagge","name_org":"Hansen, M. B.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29023768"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/vox.12607","issn":["00429007","02580330"],"issn_org":["00429007"],"issue":"1","journal":"Vox Sanguinis","pages":"76-79","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Vox Sanguinis","volume":"113"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031101490"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d952b6fa-e9ce-45f0-a1b7-c28402057ddc","sdu-24672e66-5b5b-4fa6-bd87-59afd615d932"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Changes in circulating inflammatory markers following febrile non-haemolytic transfusion reactions to leucoreduced red cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.50-046603","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"To compare the effect of a conventional to an intensive blood pressure monitoring regimen on blood pressure in hypertensive patients in the general practice setting. Randomized controlled parallel group trial with 12-month follow-up. One hundred and ten general practices in all regions of Denmark. One thousand forty-eight patients with essential hypertension. Conventional blood pressure monitoring ('usual group') continued usual ad hoc blood pressure monitoring by office blood pressure measurements, while intensive blood pressure monitoring ('intensive group') supplemented this with frequent home blood pressure monitoring and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring. Mean day- and night-time systolic and diastolic 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure. Change in systolic and diastolic office blood pressure and change in cardiovascular risk profile. Of the patients, 515 (49%) were allocated to the usual group, and 533 (51%) to the intensive group. The reductions in day- and night-time 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure were similar (usual group: 4.6 ± 13.5/2.8 ± 82 mmHg; intensive group: 5.6 ± 13.0/3.5 ± 8.2 mmHg; P = 0.27/P = 0.20). Cardiovascular risk scores were reduced in both groups at follow-up, but more so in the intensive than in the usual group (P = 0.02). An intensive blood pressure monitoring strategy led to a similar blood pressure reduction to conventional monitoring. However, the intensive strategy appeared to improve patients' cardiovascular risk profile through other effects than a reduction of blood pressure. Clinical Trials NCT00244660.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Klarskov, Pia","Bang, Lia E","Schultz-Larsen, Peter","Petersen, Hans Gregers","Benee Olsen, David","Berg, Ronan M G","Abrahamsen, Henrik","Wiinberg, Niels"],"cuid":["S02-096.69-035797"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Wiinberg, Niels"],"keyword":["24 Hour ambulatory blood pressure","Cardiovascular risk","Essential hypertension","Home blood pressure","Office blood pressure","White coat effect"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Pharmacy Svalen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intensive versus conventional blood pressure monitoring in a general practice population the blood pressure reduction in danish general practice trial a randomized controlled parallel group trial","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055259510","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.69-035797","identifier":[{"id":"000439794800012","type":"wos"},{"id":"29351658","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85055259510","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8b4aeb83-7c27-425d-85a3-53e28b6e5c71","ku-e0c07012-0562-434d-89f6-7f29e1e4afd7"],"keyword":["24-Hour ambulatory blood pressure","Cardiovascular risk","Essential hypertension","Home blood pressure","Office blood pressure","White coat effect"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FAF5FE2D8CE94587249DD36783977436"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pharmacy Svalen"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Pia","key":"klarskovpau","last":"Klarskov","name":"Klarskov, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lia E.","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, Lia E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"schultzlarsenpau","last":"Schultz-Larsen","name":"Schultz-Larsen, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Gregers","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1de4d06b-df83-4571-a60c-0620bd72aec6","name":"Petersen, Hans Gregers","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"gregerspetersenpau","last":"Gregers-Petersen","name":"Gregers-Petersen, Hans","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"David Benee","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"10e728fe-3022-47b5-9e0a-c53dc42ee8cd","name":"Olsen, David Benee","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Ronan M. G.","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","name":"Berg, Ronan M. G.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","name":"Abrahamsen, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels","key":"wiinbergpau","last":"Wiinberg","name":"Wiinberg, Niels","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29351658"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/fampra/cmx106","issn":["02632136","14602229"],"issn_org":["02632136"],"issue":"4","journal":"Family Practice","pages":"433-439","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Family Practice","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055259510"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","general practice"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8b4aeb83-7c27-425d-85a3-53e28b6e5c71","ku-e0c07012-0562-434d-89f6-7f29e1e4afd7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Intensive versus conventional blood pressure monitoring in a general practice population. The Blood Pressure Reduction in Danish General Practice trial: a randomized controlled parallel group trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.69-035797","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective This paper aims to demonstrate how the use of participatory action research (PAR) helped us identify ways to respond to communication challenges associated with shared decision-making (SDM) training. Methods Patients, relatives, researchers, and health professionals were involved in a PAR process that included: (1) two theatre workshops, (2) a pilot study of an SDM training module involving questionnaires and evaluation meetings, and (3) three reflection workshops. Results The PAR process revealed that health professionals often struggled with addressing existential issues such as concerns about life, relationships, meaning, and ability to lead responsive dialogue. Following the PAR process, a communication programme that included communication on existential issues and coaching was drafted. Conclusion By involving multiple stakeholders in a comprehensive PAR process, valuable communication skills addressing a broader understanding of SDM were identified. A communication programme aimed to enhance skills in a mindful and responsive clinical dialogue on the expectations, values, and hopes of patients and their relatives was drafted. Practical implications Before integrating new communication concepts such as SDM in communication training, research methods such as PAR can be used to improve understanding and identify the needs and priorities of both patients and health professionals.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Ammentorp, Jette","Wolderslund, Maiken","Timmermann, Connie","Larsen, Henry","Dahl Steffensen, Karina","Nielsen, Annegrethe","Lau, Marianne","Winther, Bodil","Jensen, Lars Henrik","Assing Hvidt, Elisabeth","Hvidt, Niels Christian","Gulbrandsen, Pål"],"cuid":["S02-097.86-048545"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Communication skills training","Existential communication","Fælles beslutningstagen","Participatory action research","Patient involvement","Shared decision making","Theatre workshop","kommunikationstræning"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Mental Health Services, Capital Region of Denmark, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how participatory action research changed our view of the challenges of shared decision making training","src":["sdu","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/145636224/How_participatory_action_research_changed_our_view_of_the_challenges_of_shared_decision_making_training.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-097.86-048545","identifier":[{"id":"85033578375","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29137836","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-0e2771ae-c6d2-41d9-8739-dde0e705e95c","ucn-c7ff3465-5236-48e6-943f-bb3c609852ff"],"keyword":["Communication skills training","Existential communication","Fælles beslutningstagen","Participatory action research","Patient involvement","Shared decision-making","Theatre workshop","kommunikationstræning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-152FEDE5FFED1E172ACECF52753C3CCB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/145636224/How_participatory_action_research_changed_our_view_of_the_challenges_of_shared_decision_making_training.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018"