,"University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0e2771ae-c6d2-41d9-8739-dde0e705e95c","ucn-c7ff3465-5236-48e6-943f-bb3c609852ff"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"How participatory action research changed our view of the challenges of shared decision-making training","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.86-048545","year":"2018","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Interferon-α2 reduces elevated blood cell counts and splenomegaly in patients with myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPN) and may restore polyclonal hematopoiesis. Its use is limited by inflammation-mediated toxicity, leading to treatment discontinuation in 10-30% of patients. Ruxolitinib, a potent anti-inflammatory agent, has demonstrated benefit in myelofibrosis (MF) and polycythemia vera (PV) patients. Combination therapy (CT) with these two agents may be more efficacious than monotherapy with either, potentially improving tolerability of interferon-α2 as well. We report the preliminary results from a phase II study of CT with pegylated interferon-α2 and ruxolitinib in 50 MPN patients (PV, n = 32; low-/intermediate-1-risk MF, n = 18), the majority (n = 47) being resistant and/or intolerant to interferon-α2 monotherapy. Objectives included remission (2013 revised criteria encompassing histologic, hematologic, and clinical responses), complete hematologic response (CHR), molecular response, and toxicity. Follow-up was 12 months. Partial remission (PR) and sustained CHR were achieved in 9% and 44% of PV patients, respectively. In MF patients, complete or partial remission was achieved in 39%, and sustained CHR in 58%. The median JAK2V617F allele burden declined significantly in both groups. Hematologic toxicity was the most common adverse event and was managed by dose reduction. Thirty-seven serious adverse events were recorded in 23 patients; the discontinuation rate was 20%. We conclude that CT with interferon-α2 and ruxolitinib is efficacious in patients with low-/intermediate-1-risk MF and, to a lesser extent, in patients with PV. These preliminary results encourage phase III studies as well as a study with CT in newly diagnosed MPN patients.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Stine Ulrik","Kjaer, Lasse","Bjørn, Mads Emil","Knudsen, Trine Alma","Sørensen, Anders Lindholm","Andersen, Christen Lykkegaard","Bjerrum, Ole Weis","Brochmann, Nana","El Fassi, Daniel","Kruse, Torben A","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","Mourits-Andersen, Hans Torben","Nielsen, Claus Henrik","Pallisgaard, Niels","Thomassen, Mads","Skov, Vibe","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl"],"cuid":["S02-098.53-047603"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hasselbalch, Hans Carl"],"keyword":["Combination therapy","Interferon alpha","Myeloproliferative neoplasms","Polycythemia Vera","Primary Myelofibrosis","Ruxolitinib"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safety and efficacy of combination therapy of interferon α000000000002 and ruxolitinib in polycythemia vera and myelofibrosis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cam4.1619","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study is supported in part by research funding from the manufacturer of Ruxolitinib (Jakavi®), Novartis A/S, who also provided ruxolitinib study medication. Novartis A/S was not involved in the data analyses or preparation of the manuscript. Stine Ulrik Mikkelsen has received a travel grant from Novartis Oncology. Stine Ulrik Mikkelsen and Niels Pallisgaard have received a travel grant from Novartis Oncology. Hans Carl Hasselbalch, Claus Henrik Nielsen, Niels Pallisgaard, and Mads Emil Bjørn have received research funding from Novartis Oncology. Niels Pallisgaard is in the Novartis Speakers Bureau. Ole Weis Bjerrum and Daniel El Fassi have conducted educational activities for Novartis. All other authors have no relationships to disclose."],"id":"S02-098.53-047603","identifier":[{"id":"85051502948","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6089176","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29932310","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-facb8461-7963-4022-b1e9-25c03bae2e0b","sdu-ba99a688-6982-45f9-bd0a-eb0b7812e729"],"keyword":["combination therapy","interferon-alpha","myeloproliferative neoplasms","polycythemia vera","primary myelofibrosis","ruxolitinib"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F35DF0521B5ADC7156523857E4FB77FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cam4.1619","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/218399659/Mikkelsen_et_al_2018_Cancer_Medicine.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/142548000/Safety_and_efficacy_of_combination_therapy_of_interferon_2_and_ruxolitinib_in_polycythemia_vera_and_myelofibrosis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Grønbæk Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capit