"last":"Sejersten","name":"Sejersten, Maria","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yochai","key":"birnbaumpau","last":"Birnbaum","name":"Birnbaum, Yochai","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29103621"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2017.09.013","issn":["00220736","15328430"],"issn_org":["00220736"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Electrocardiology","pages":"218-223","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Electrocardiology","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034967746"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d89a8138-2bfa-459b-abe7-c4cd8cd20d1a","sdu-40bc8ecd-0d4a-48bd-81ce-3a9b4e1df2ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Appropriateness of anteroseptal myocardial infarction nomenclature evaluated by late gadolinium enhancement cardiovascular magnetic resonance imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.73-010344","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Terminal \"QRS distortion\" on the electrocardiogram (ECG) (based on Sclarovsky-Birnbaum's Grades of Ischemia Score) is a sign of severe ischemia, associated with adverse cardiovascular outcome in ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). In addition, ECG indices of the acuteness of ischemia (based on Anderson-Wilkins Acuteness Score) indicate myocardial salvage potential. We assessed whether severe ischemia with or without acute ischemia is predictive of infarct size (IS), myocardial salvage index (MSI) and left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) in anterior versus inferior infarct locations. METHODS: In STEMI patients, the severity and acuteness scores were obtained from the admission ECG. Based on the ECG patients were assigned with severe or non-severe ischemia and acute or non-acute ischemia. Cardiac magnetic resonance (CMR) was performed 2-6days after primary percutaneous coronary intervention (pPCI). LVEF was measured by echocardiography 30days after pPCI. RESULTS: ECG analysis of 85 patients with available CMR resulted in 20 (23%) cases with severe and non-acute ischemia, 43 (51%) with non-severe and non-acute ischemia, 17 (20%) with non-severe and acute ischemia, and 5 (6%) patients with severe and acute ischemia. In patients with anterior STEMI (n=35), ECG measures of severity and acuteness of ischemia identified significant and stepwise differences in myocardial damage and function. Patients with severe and non-acute ischemia had the largest IS, smallest MSI and lowest LVEF. In contrast, no difference was observed in patients with inferior STEMI (n=50). CONCLUSIONS: The applicability of ECG indices of severity and acuteness of myocardial ischemia to estimate myocardial damage and salvage potential in STEMI patients treated with pPCI, is confined to anterior myocardial infarction.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Fakhri, Yama","Sejersten, Maria","Schoos, Mikkel Malby","Hansen, Henrik Steen","Dubois-Rande, Jean-Luc","Hall, Trygve S","Larsen, Alf-Inge","Jensen, Svend Eggert","Engblom, Henrik","Arheden, Hakon","Kastrup, Jens","Atar, Dan","Clemmensen, Peter"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-009212"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris","Department of Cardiology B, Oslo University Hospital, Norway, and Institute of Clinical Sciences, University of Oslo, Oslo, Norway.","Department of Clinical Physiology, Lund University, Skåne University Hospital, Lund, Sweden.","Hospital Henri Mondor","Lund University","Oslo University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","Stavanger University hospital","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University of Bergen","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Acuteness of myocardial ischemia","Double Blind Method","ECG","Electrocardiography","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Myocardial Ischemia diagnostic imaging","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Prospective Studies","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction diagnostic imaging","STEMI","Severity of Illness Index","Severity of myocardial ischemia","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Department of Cardiology, Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev, 2730 Herlev, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrocardiographic scores of severity and acuteness of myocardial ischemia predict myocardial salvage in patients with anterior st segment elevation myocardial infarction","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134672119/Electrocardiographic_Scores_of_Severity_and_Acuteness_of_Myocardial_Ischemia_Predict_Myocardial_Salvage_in_Patients_with_Anterior_ST.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-009212","identifier":[{"id":"29174706","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85034993757","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bf05e4d9-fe9f-42cf-a6c6-727893016dd6","ku-ba1c5bf4-af8b-4309-aa39-f3899d1ae2a8","sdu-5b79f9fa-5b40-4f01-85a7-377ca4f1eff0"],"keyword":["Acuteness of myocardial ischemia","Double-Blind Method","ECG","Electrocardiography","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Myocardial Ischemia/diagnostic imaging","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Prospective Studies","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction/diagnostic imaging","STEMI","Severity of Illness Index","Severity of myocardial ischemia","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-848D8CA6A05D9A6E827688AC854172B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134672119/Electrocardiographic_Scores_of_Severity_and_Acuteness_of_Myocardial_Ischemia_Predict_Myocardial_Salvage_in_Patients_with_Anterior_ST.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/319302966/Electrocardiographic_Scores_of_Severity_and_Acuteness_of_Myocardial_Ischemia_Predict_Myocardial_Salvage_in_Patients_with_Anterior_ST.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Ca