{"abstract":"Dynamic Contrast-Enhanced MR (DCE-MR) perfusion assessment with gadolinium contrast agents is currently the most widely used cerebral perfusion MR method. Hyperpolarized water has recently been shown to succeed 13C probes as angiography probe. In this study, we demonstrate the feasibility of hyperpolarized water for visualizing the brain vasculature of a large animal in a clinically relevant setting. In detail, reference perfusion values were obtained and large to small arteries could be identified.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","Lipsø, Hans Kasper Wigh","Tougaard, Rasmus Stilling","Laustsen, Christoffer","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-181458"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-27","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2017-04-22","title":"ISMRM 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized water perfusion in the porcine brain a pilot study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-181458","ids":["au-5b71436e-dd50-40e4-b37a-e56aa30cca3d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8AD82FB9B59ED2584F1E61B8FBDF01E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark (DTU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"søvsøszocskahansenpau","last":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen","locid":"2ea5821e-bbda-4f7e-a18a-0b9eb3b993f0","name":"Søvsø Szocska Hansen, Esben","orcid":"0000-0001-5512-9870","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Kasper Wigh","key":"lipsøpau","last":"Lipsø","name":"Lipsø, Hans Kasper Wigh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Stilling","key":"tougaardpau","last":"Tougaard","locid":"ed4f8644-8a58-424c-9f0c-dac467df4a24","name":"Tougaard, Rasmus Stilling","orcid":"0000-0003-2199-0405","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","name":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"ISMRM 2017 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5b71436e-dd50-40e4-b37a-e56aa30cca3d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hyperpolarized Water Perfusion in the Porcine Brain – a Pilot Study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-181458","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The effects of storage conditions on the shelf-life of hydrolysed-lactose ultra-high-temperature (UHT) milk was evaluated using proteomics. Lactose content was initially reduced to approximately 40% by ultra- and nanofiltration before hydrolysis. Increased peptide and amino acid levels were observed in the milk over a seven-month storage period at room temperature. Potentially bitter peptides (Q-value > 1400 cal mol −1) increased in levels from 86 to 116 days of storage, which coincided with the shelf-life (three months) of this milk, as found by sensory analysis. Sensory descriptive analysis was used to describe the sensory characteristics of the milk during storage. Bitterness intensity significantly increased over time and was correlated with the level of peptides released via either enzymatic (proteolytic side activity of the enzyme used in lactose hydrolysis) or non-enzymatic pathways (heat and storage induction). This study reveals a relationship between proteolysis and decreased shelf-life of hydrolysed-lactose UHT milk compared with conventional UHT milk.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","Jansson, Therese","Le, Thao Thi Thu","Jensen, Sidsel","Eggers, Nina","M. Rauh, Valentin","Sundekilde, Ulrik Kræmer","Sørensen, John","Andersen, Henrik J.","Bertram, Hanne Christine S.","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-203042"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Correlation","Peptides","Sensory","Storage","UHT milk"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"correlation between sensory properties and peptides derived from hydrolysed lactose uht milk during storage","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85009724416","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-203042","identifier":[{"id":"85009724416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-80eea168-b10c-4a4e-b50e-051d00b383ca"],"keyword":["Correlation","STORAGE","Sensory","UHT milk","hydrolysed-lactose","peptides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35CDD0ECBDECDB4F577456BEF877638A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Drud-Heydary","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"030ede5c-2e12-40c1-9d0c-543f0c5ffadf","name":"Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Therese","key":"janssonpau","last":"Jansson","locid":"6f9cac6c-7d35-4c4b-a1c8-4dc77ddbfe4c","name":"Jansson, Therese","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thao Thi Thu","key":"lepau","last":"Le","locid":"f114fe35-c2f1-437d-b00b-8beded4747a9","name":"Le, Thao Thi Thu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidsel","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4efa5bb5-7bc4-441e-809a-70cbb1a01b92","name":"Jensen, Sidsel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"eggerspau","last":"Eggers","locid":"5b19fad0-712d-43f5-9146-a2f6995c94fc","name":"Eggers, Nina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentin","key":"mrauhpau","last":"M. Rauh","name":"M. Rauh, Valentin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik Kræmer","key":"sundekildepau","last":"Sundekilde","locid":"7c17646c-186b-46af-a2e1-fd5e2200649d","name":"Sundekilde, Ulrik Kræmer","orcid":"0000-0003-4849-0996","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, John","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik J.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Henrik J.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Christine S.","key":"bertrampau","last":"Bertram","locid":"9ad2a927-38d2-4267-9382-a851bf3c7e06","name":"Bertram, Hanne Christine S.","orcid":"0000-0002-1882-5321","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.idairyj.2016.12.013","issn":["09586946","18790143"],"issn_org":["09586946"],"journal":"International Dairy Journal","pages":"23-31","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Dairy Journal","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009724416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-80eea168-b10c-4a4e-b50e-051d00b383ca"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Correlation between sensory properties and peptides derived from hydrolysed-lactose UHT milk during storage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-203042","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Previous studies have documented links between sub-clinical narcissism and the active pursuit of short-term mating strategies (e.g., unrestricted sociosexuality, marital infidelity, mate poaching). Nearly all of these investigations have relied solely on samples from Western cultures. In the current study, responses from a cross-cultural survey of 30,470 people across 53 nations spanning 11 world regions (North America, Central/South America, Northern Europe, Western Europe, Eastern Europe, Southern Europe, Middle East, Africa, Oceania, Southeast Asia, and East Asia) were used to evaluate whether narcissism (as measured by the Narcissistic Personality Inventory; NPI) was universally associated with short-term mating. Results revealed narcissism scores (including two broad factors and seven traditional facets as measured by the NPI) were functionally equivalent across cultures, reliably associating with key sexual outcomes (e.g., more active pursuit of short-term mating, intimate partner violence, and sexual aggression) and sex-related personality traits (e.g., higher extraversion and openness to experience). Whereas some features of personality (e.g., subjective well-being) were universally associated with socially adaptive facets of Narcissism (e.g., self-sufficiency), most indicators of short-term mating (e.g., unrestricted sociosexuality and marital infidelity) were universally associated with the socially maladaptive facets of narcissism (e.g., exploitativeness). Discussion addresses limitations of these cross-culturally universal findings and presents suggestions for future research into revealing the precise psychological features of narcissism that facilitate the strategic pursuit of short-term mating.","author_count":193,"contributors":["Schmitt, David P.","Alcalay, Lidia","Allik, Jüri","Alves, I. C.B.","Anderson, Craig A.","Angelini, A. L.","Asendorpf, Jens B.","Austers, Ivars","Balaguer, Isabel","Baptista, Américo","Bender, Sóley S.","Bennett,