syl transferase, ExAD","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-451528","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We sketch an outline of a model for analyzing the use of ICT-tools, in particular CAS, in teaching designs employed by ‘generic’ teachers. Our model uses the business economics concepts out- and insourcing as metaphors within the dialectics of tool and content in planning of teaching. Outsourcing is done in order to enhance outcome through external partners. The converse concept of insourcing refers to internal sourcing. We shall adhere to the framework of the anthropological theory of the didactic, viewing out- and insourcing primarily as decisions about the technology component of praxeologies. We use the model on a concrete example from Danish upper secondary mathematics to uncover what underlies teachers’ decisions (deliberate or colloquial) on incorporating instrumented approaches.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bang, Henrik Peter","Grønbæk, Niels","Larsen, Claus Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482837"],"event":{"end":"2017-02-05","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2017-02-01","title":"Congress of the European Society for Research in Mathematics Education","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Christianshavns Gymnsasium"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"out and insourcing an analysis model for use of instrumented techniques","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://keynote.conference-services.net/resources/444/5118/pdf/CERME10_0039.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-482837","ids":["ku-95a44e3e-5fdf-4ff6-8283-38e8718e0ad8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3108A984B2ADBC9C75B1BEA78AE7B1A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://keynote.conference-services.net/resources/444/5118/pdf/CERME10_0039.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Christianshavns Gymnsasium"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Didactics of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Peter","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, Henrik Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"92b1622e-630d-49e3-a623-55c283a2db0f","name":"Grønbæk, Niels","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-856X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus Richard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Claus Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"T.","key":"dooleypedh","last":"Dooley","name":"Dooley, T.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"G,","key":"gueudetpedh","last":"Gueudet","name":"Gueudet, G,","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"place":"Dublin","publisher":"DCU Institute of Education and ERME","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Tenth Congress of the European Society for Research in Mathematics Education"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-95a44e3e-5fdf-4ff6-8283-38e8718e0ad8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Out- and insourcing, an analysis model for use of instrumented techniques","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482837","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To study visual outcome and number of annual injections in treatment-naïve patients with neovascular age-related macular degeneration (nAMD) before and after a change in first-line therapy from ranibizumab to aflibercept in a high-volume clinical practice. METHODS: This was a retrospective chart review of routine clinical practice. The study included 1027 treatment-naïve patients, 559 of whom started intravitreal ranibizumab therapy in 2011-2012 and 468 of whom started intravitreal aflibercept therapy in 2013-2014, a fixed loading dose of three injections followed by a pro re nata treatment regimen used in both periods. RESULTS: Snellen best-corrected visual acuity (BCVA) at baseline and after one year was 0.23 and 0.31 (p < 0.0001), respectively, for patients treated with ranibizumab and 0.25 and 0.33 (p < 0.0001) for patients treated with aflibercept, last observation carried forward. The share of patients (73%) still in treatment with ranibizumab at year 1 had a baseline BCVA of 0.26 but 0.40 at year 1 (p < 0.0001), and the patients (75%) still in treatment with aflibercept at year 1 had a baseline BCVA of 0.28 but 0.42 at year 1 (p < 0.0001). Proportional visual gains for both cohorts were comparable for one year (p = 0.14). The number of injections given within year 1 including first injection was 6.9 for ranibizumab and 5.9 for aflibercept (p < 0.0001). In patients continuing treatment through year 1, the number of injections was 8.0 for ranibizumab and 6.6 for aflibercept (p < 0.0001). The two cohorts had similar cause-of-discontinuation profiles. CONCLUSION: Treatment of nAMD at a single centre in two sequential cohorts yielded comparable BCVA outcomes with 15% fewer injections of aflibercept compared to ranibizumab.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Annette","Sander, Birgit","Larsen, Michael","Brandi, Sara","Fuchs, Josefine","Hansen, Louise H","Lund-Andersen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494920"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Angiogenesis Inhibitors administration dosage","Dose Response Relationship Drug","Drug Administration Schedule","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Intravitreal Injections","Macular Degeneration diagnosis","Male","Ranibizumab administration dosage","Receptors Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor administration dosage","Recombinant Fusion Proteins administration dosage","Retrospective Studies","Tomography Optical Coherence","Treatment Outcome","Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor A antagonists inhibitors","Visual Acuity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neovascular age related macular degeneration treated with ranibizumab or aflibercept in the same large clinical setting visual outcome and number of injections","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-494920","identifier":[{"id":"27535819","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84994404259","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a9e99f53-055f-4425-9b7f-a477d9362d53"],"keyword":["Aged","Angiogenesis Inhibitors/administration & dosage","Choroidal Neovascularization/complications","Dose-Response Relationship, Drug","Drug Administration Schedule","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Intravitreal Injections","Macular Degeneration/diagnosis","Male","Ranibizumab/administration & dosage","Receptors, Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor/administration & dosage","Recombinant Fusion Proteins/administration & dosage","Retrospective Studies","Tomography, Optical Coherence","Treatment Outcome","Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor A/antagonists & inhibitors","Visual Acuity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-338A22E793C5B9DDE9B64D96D0F95991"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Annette","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Annette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgit","key":"sanderpau","last":"Sander","name":"Sander, Birgit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sara","key":"brandipau","last":"Brandi","name":"Brandi, Sara","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Josefine","key":"fuchspau","last":"Fuchs","name":"Fuchs, Josefine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise H","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Louise H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27535819"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.13233","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"128-132","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994404259"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a9e99f53-055f-4425-9b7f-a477d9362d53"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neovascular age-related macular degeneration treated with ranibizumab or aflibercept in the same large clinical setting : visual outcome and number of injections","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494920","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, A","Fuchs, J","Hansen, L H","Larsen, M","Sander, B","Lund-Andersen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514822"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neovascular age related macular degeneration is it worthwhile treating an eye with poor visual acuity if the visual acuity of the fellow eye is good","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-514822","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5518829","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28106891","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85020384110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cb43b1a8-8c55-46c3-86a6-2da8740f7805"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D5F15B4055E41A5F7D552C9840E1FFBC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"A","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J","key":"fuchspau","last":"Fuchs","name":"Fuchs, J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L H","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, L H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B","key":"sanderpau","last":"Sander","name":"Sander, B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","name_org":"Lund-Andersen, H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28106891"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/eye.2016.324","issn":["0950222X","14765454"],"issn_org":["0950222X"],"journal":"Eye","pages":"978-980","status":"p","title":"Eye","volume":"31"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020384110"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb43b1a8-8c55-46c3-86a6-2da8740f7805"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neovascular age-related macular degeneration : is it worthwhile treating an eye with poor visual acuity, if the visual acuity of the fellow eye is good?","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514822","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Mosses collected decades ago and stored in herbaria are often used to assess historical nitrogen deposition. This method is effectively based on the assumption that tissue N concentration remains constant during storage. The present study raises serious doubt about the generality of that assumption. We measured tissue N and C concentrations as well as δ15N, δ13C, Pb and Mg in herbarium and present day samples of seven bryophyte species from six sites across Denmark. While an increase in nitrogen deposition during the last century is well-documented for the study site, we surprisingly found foliar N concentration to be higher in historical samples than in modern samples. Based on δ15N values and Pb concentration, we find nitrogen contamination of herbarium specimens during storage to be the most likely cause, possibly in combination with dilution though growth and/or decomposition during storage. We suggest ways to assess contamination and recommend caution to be taken when using herbarium specimens to assess historical pollution if exposure during storage cannot be ruled out. Analyses of moss tissue stored in a herbarium for a century raises serious concern about the reliability of this data source to past levels of nitrogen deposition.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Tora Finderup","Larsen, Jesper Ruf","Michelsen, Anders","Bruun, Hans Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are herbarium mosses reliable indicators of historical nitrogen deposition","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85017462742&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-530551","identifier":[{"id":"85017462742","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28420490","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e59d0b24-7fc8-468e-8c42-abf1cf5997a5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59A724F19A71400E80260C361C0B4B31"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tora Finderup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"146e37d6-2d54-4b3c-b84b-fba5211074c9","name":"Nielsen, Tora Finderup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Ruf","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d03015cd-ca5d-4992-aa52-fc7cbd94d0d5","name":"Larsen, Jesper Ruf","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"michelsenpau","last":"Michelsen","locid":"5f62798d-50c6-41c3-8018-18babf5e5046","name":"Michelsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-9541-8658","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Henrik","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"5d597e2b-61e5-45ea-8816-0c37431329f0","name":"Bruun, Hans Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0674-2577","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28420490"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envpol.2017.04.020","issn":["02697491","18736424"],"issn_org":["02697491"],"issue":"Part 1","journal":"Environmental Pollution","pages":"1201-1207","status":"p","title":"Environmental Pollution","volume":"231"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017462742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e59d0b24-7fc8-468e-8c42-abf1cf5997a5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Are herbarium mosses reliable indicators of historical nitrogen deposition?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-530551","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
