{"abstract":"The glenoid fossa is involved in approximately 10% of all scapular fractures.Glenoid fossa incongruity is surprisingly well tolerated.Surgery is recommended when 20% or more of the anterior glenoid fossa is involved.Glenoid rim fractures often lead to chronic shoulder instability.Unstable glenoid neck fractures need surgical treatment and stable fractures can be treated conservatively.CT examination with 3D reformations of the glenoid fossa has improved insight into fracture morphology and fracture patterns and is very helpful for clinical decision makers. Cite this article: EFORT Open Rev 2017;2. DOI: 10.1302/2058-5241.2.160082. Originally published online at www.efortopenreviews.org.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Frich, Lars Henrik","Larsen, Morten Schultz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-617011"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-02","place":"Wien, at","start":"2017-05-31","title":"18th EFORT Congress","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Classification","Glenoid","Instability"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to deal with a glenoid fracture","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1302/2058-5241.2.160082","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-617011","identifier":[{"id":"85041375656","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5467683","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28630753","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-98f83bd1-2714-4c83-bc2f-948edb8be4f2"],"keyword":["3D CT reformations","Classification","Fossa fracture","Glenoid","Instability","Neck fracture"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-840F74434B63A698027D2683CF68A62C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125251653/How_to_deal_with_a_glenoid_fracture.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1302/2058-5241.2.160082","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.efortopenreviews.org/content/2/5/151","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Henrik","key":"frichpau","last":"Frich","locid":"f5e4ebc5-0851-429f-ae70-b627b21b3d91","name":"Frich, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0147-4211","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Schultz","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"c510b13d-1eca-4264-9a6d-8bcc331cf1c2","name":"Larsen, Morten Schultz","orcid":"0000-0002-4448-3556","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28630753"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1302/2058-5241.2.160082","issn":["20585241","23967544"],"issn_org":["23967544"],"issue":"5","journal":"EFORT Open Reviews","pages":"151-157","publisher":"BioScientifica Ltd.","status":"p","title":"EFORT Open Reviews","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041375656"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-98f83bd1-2714-4c83-bc2f-948edb8be4f2"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How to deal with a glenoid fracture","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-617011","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Aims Chronic pain is a significant clinical problem with few effective therapies. Objectives of this clinical registry are (1) to assist clinical decision-making, and (2) facilitate quality assurance and research projects to improve understanding and optimize treatment of patients with chronic pain. Methods PainData is an electronic software system developed for online data capture and clinical reporting, currently implemented in public pain clinics in Odense, Silkeborg, Aalborg, Næstved, Køge and Holbæk. The system captures patient-specific information across several bio-psychosocial domains of pain before the first consultation at the pain clinic as well as immediately after treatment, and 12 months after treatment. The registry also includes information from clinicians (e.g. pain diagnosis, and standardized pain sensitivity testing). PainData is registered as a clinical and research database with the Danish Data Protection Agency (16/39398, 14/44319). Results Since February 1st 2015 more than 3000 patients have completed questionnaires in PainData. The current completion rate at baseline is >80% and at follow-up is close to 50%. Pain-related data (e.g. pain-distribution, psychological distress and use of analgesics) from the registry will be presented on the poster. Conclusions The clinical pain registry contains data from a large cohort of consecutively referred chronic pain patients attending public pain clinics for multidisciplinary assessment and treatment. It contains detailed baseline and outcome data on a broad range of bio-psychosocial factors. The database has significant clinical relevance as it will contribute to an increased understanding of chronic pain conditions as well as contribute to substantial knowledge on how various psychological factors influence the experience of pain and disability in patients with chronic pain. In addition, early prediction of treatment efficacy and future stratification of patients with chronic pain has the potential to optimize treatment outcome. This will be of great interest to both the individual patient and to society.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","Høybye, Mette Terp","Larsen, S K","Hansen, O B","Pedersen, C B","Jensen, P B F","Handberg, G"],"cuid":["S02-080.00-013272"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-28","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2017-04-27","title":"Annual Meeting of the Scandinavian Association for the Study of Pain","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paindata a clinical pain registry in denmark","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-080.00-013272","identifier":[{"id":"29864980","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0942085e-84e8-4def-8785-d2df78912339","sdu-0291c4a3-0f45-465c-a406-00802534a3d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BBEC272253C3801CA736C0E971EAE927"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"