{"abstract":"Myrer og ledere ligner hinanden på en række punkter: De står i spidsen for avancerede organisationer, bygger hierarkier, samarbejder, arbejder hårdt og erobrer fjendtligt land.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-279600"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jagten på årets leder er gået ind","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","text":"Undefined","type":"url","url":"https://finans.dk/debat/ECE9956307/jagten-paa-aarets-leder-er-gaaet-ind/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-279600","ids":["cbs-2c9d3aa2-a7c3-4f9e-968d-fe30af181af8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A3CB3B670052A65A433ABF8C7A551EF2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-2c9d3aa2-a7c3-4f9e-968d-fe30af181af8"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Jagten på årets leder er gået ind","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-279600","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this project by the University of Stuttgart, DTU Wind Energy and CENER, a real-time blade-pitch control system was implemented on a scaled model in a combined wind-and-wave tank. A simplified low-order simulation model including aerodynamics, hydrodynamics, mooring dynamics and structural dynamics was used to design the controller. Some effort has been made to investigate the influence of different gain scheduling methodologies of the collective blade-pitch controller on the dynamic behavior of the floating wind turbine. The issue relating to the negative aerodynamic damping is also investigated in order to find out whether the effects seen in simulation models can be equally reproduced by model tests. Additionally, wind and wave-induced responses with different gain scheduling methodologies and the difference to the tests without blade-pitch control are discussed. A solution for the hardware implementation of the real-time controller has been introduced. The developed controller is proven to function throughout the test campaign, which also proves the reliability of the simplified simulation model for controller design. It has been shown that with the low-Reynolds rotor it is possible to control the rotor speed at Froude-scaled frequencies by actuating the blade pitch angle.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Yu, Wenye","Lemmer, F.","Bredmose, Henrik","Borg, Michael","Pegalajar-Jurado, Antonio","Mikkelsen, Robert Flemming","Larsen, T. Stoklund","Fjelstrup, T.","Lomholt, Anders Kjær","Boehm, L.","Schlipf, D.","Armendariz, J. Azcona","Cheng, P.W."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308291"],"event":{"end":"2017-01-20","place":"Trondheim, no","start":"2017-01-18","title":"14th Deep Sea Offshore Wind R&amp;D Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Renewable Energy Center","University of Stuttgart"],"keyword":["Controller design","Floating wind turbine","Scaled model test"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the triple spar campaign implementation and test of a blade pitch controller on a scaled floating wind turbine model","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/140797769/filestore_50_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-308291","identifier":[{"id":"85040313765","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0c63e321-74ce-4210-b1b9-3a6e3eb9e16f"],"keyword":["Floating wind turbine","controller design","controller implementation","scaled model test"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8410C68DCC91132AF8AB53A293C37D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/140797769/filestore_50_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of stuttgart","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Stuttgart","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Fluid Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"national renewable energy center","loc"