o":"","first":"Jens Peter","key":"skovsgaardpau","last":"Skovsgaard","name":"Skovsgaard, Jens Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1139/cjfr-2016-0430","issn":["00455067","12086037"],"issn_org":["00455067"],"issue":"6","journal":"Canadian Journal of Forest Research","pages":"765-776","status":"p","title":"Canadian Journal of Forest Research","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020111834"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f92aad98-4f9b-4b36-85e7-0ac6ecd3608b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simultaneous estimation of biomass models for 13 tree species : effects of compatible additivity requirements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542142","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND/AIMS: Congenital hyperinsulinism (CHI) is a heterogeneous disease most frequently caused by KATP-channel (ABCC8 and KCNJ11) mutations, with neonatal or later onset, variable severity, and with focal or diffuse pancreatic involvement as the two major histological types. CHI confers a high risk of neurological impairment; however, sparsely studied in larger patient series. We assessed the neurodevelopmental outcome in children with CHI at follow-up in a mixed international cohort. METHODS: In two hyperinsulinism expert centers, 75 CHI patients were included (Russian, n = 33, referred non-Scandinavian, treated in Denmark n = 27, Scandinavian, n = 15). Hospital files were reviewed. At follow-up, neurodevelopmental impairment and neurodevelopmental, cognitive and motor function scores were assessed. RESULTS: Median (range) age at follow-up was 3.7 years (3.3 months-18.2 years). Neurodevelopmental impairment was seen in 35 (47%). Impairment was associated with abnormal brain magnetic resonance imaging (MRI); odds ratio (OR) (95% CI) 15.0 (3.0-74.3), p = 0.001; lowest recorded blood glucose ≤1 mmol/L; OR 3.8 (1.3-11.3), p = 0.015, being non-Scandinavian patient, OR 3.8 (1.2-11.9), p = 0.023; and treatment delay from first symptom to expert center >5 days; OR 4.0 (1.0-16.6), trend p = 0.05. In multivariate analysis (n = 31) for early predictors with exclusion of brain MRI, treatment delay from first symptom to expert center >5 days conferred a significantly increased risk of neurodevelopment impairment, adjusted OR (aOR) 15.6 (1.6-146.7), p = 0.016, while lowest blood glucose ≤1 mmol/L had a trend toward increased risk, aOR 3.5 (1.1-14.3), p = 0.058. No associations for early vs. late disease onset, KATP-channel mutations, disease severity, focal vs. diffuse disease, or age at follow-up were seen in uni- or multivariate analysis. CONCLUSION: Not only very low blood glucose, but also insufficient treatment as expressed by delay until expert center hospitalization, increased the risk of neurodevelopmental impairment. This novel finding calls for improvements in spread of knowledge about CHI among health-care personnel and rapid contact with an expert CHI center on suspicion of CHI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov","Melikyan, Maria","Globa, Evgenia","Shcherderkina, Inna","Portner, Fani Juel","Larsen, Anna Marie","Filipsen, Karen","Brusgaard, Klaus","Christiansen, Charlotte Dahl","Hansen, Lars Kjærsgaard","Christesen, Henrik Thybo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-619665"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU"],"country":["Russia","Ukraine"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pediatric Endocrinology, Ukrainian Centre of Endocrine Surgery,","Russian Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Congenital hyperinsulinism","Hypoglycemia","Neurodevelopmental impairment","Neurological outcome","Treatment delay"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Pediatric, Endocrinology Scientific Centre, Moscow, Russia."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"both low blood glucose and insufficient treatment confer risk of neurodevelopmental impairment in congenital hyperinsulinism a multinational cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2017.00156","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-619665","identifier":[{"id":"28740482","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85025434167","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5502348","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-a2596165-dfc6-47f1-b984-694215bdd7ed"],"keyword":["Congenital hyperinsulinism","Hypoglycemia","Neurodevelopmental impairment","Neurological outcome","Treatment delay"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C016AA0F569748480BC34E4AD93C187"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2017.00156","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125528780/Both_Low_Blood_Glucose_and_Insufficient_Treatment_Confer_Risk_of_Neurodevelopmental_Impairment_in_Congenital_Hyperinsulinism.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ru","key":"russian academy of sciences","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Russian Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ua","key":"pediatric endocrinology ukrainian centre of endocrine surgery","loc":["Ukraine","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Pediatric Endocrinology, Ukrainian Centre of Endocrine Surgery,","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pediatric, Endocrinology Scientific Centre, Moscow, Russia."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annett Helleskov","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"5e6d18d0-56bd-4173-808e-7be947059c9f","name":"Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov","orcid":"0000-0001-7122-4114","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"m