Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-1612-4089","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin R","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4ecd87f8-6fb1-4d10-b8a3-6d0657129eef","name":"Larsen, Martin Røssel","name_org":"Larsen, Martin R","orcid":"0000-0001-6203-0123","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik J","key":"ditzelpau","last":"Ditzel","locid":"f10637d7-ca3b-4956-a007-100f66737838","name":"Ditzel, Henrik","name_org":"Ditzel, Henrik J","orcid":"0000-0003-3927-5135","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28600813"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/stem.2654","issn":["10665099","15494918"],"issn_org":["10665099"],"issue":"8","journal":"Stem Cells","pages":"1898-1912","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Stem Cells","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021343833"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f43e4cb6-661b-4354-830f-b5a5833d6d29","sdu-7a3e311c-20c3-4c7a-9509-22dd09c05a69"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Elucidation of Altered Pathways in Tumor-Initiating Cells of Triple-Negative Breast Cancer : A Useful Cell Model System for Drug Screening","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.81-047397","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Muscle pain may reorganize trunk muscle activity but interactions with exercise-related muscle fatigue and delayed onset muscle soreness (DOMS) is to be clarified. METHODS: In 19 healthy participants, the trunk muscle activity during 20 multi-directional unpredictable surface perturbations were recorded after bilateral isotonic saline injections (control) and during unilateral and bilateral hypertonic saline-induced low back pain (LBP) in conditions of back muscle fatigue (Day-1) and DOMS (Day-2). Pain intensity and distribution were assessed by visual analogue scale (VAS) scores and pain drawings. The degree of fatigue and DOMS were assessed by Likert scale scores. Root-mean-square electromyographic (RMS-EMG) signals were recorded post-perturbation from six bilateral trunk muscles and the difference from baseline conditions (Delta-RMS-EMG) was extracted and averaged across abdominal and back muscles. RESULTS: In DOMS, peak VAS scores were higher during bilateral control and bilateral saline-induced pain than fatigue (p < 0.001) and during bilateral compared with unilateral pain (p < 0.001). The saline-induced pain areas were larger during DOMS than fatigue (p < 0.01). In response to surface perturbations during fatigue and DOMS, the back muscle Delta-RMS-EMG increased during bilateral compared with unilateral pain and control injections (p < 0.001) and decreased during unilateral pain compared with control injections (p < 0.04). In DOMS compared with fatigue, the post-perturbation Delta-RMS-EMG in back muscles was higher during bilateral pain and lower during unilateral pain (p < 0.001). The abdominal Delta-RMS-EMG was not significantly affected. CONCLUSION: Facilitated and attenuated back muscle responses to surface perturbations in bilateral and unilateral LBP, respectively, was more expressed during exercise-induced back muscle soreness compared with fatigue. SIGNIFICANCE: Back muscle activity decreased during unilateral and increased during bilateral pain after unpredictable surface perturbations during muscle fatigue and DOMS. Accumulation effects of DOMS on pain intensity and spreading and trunk muscle activity after pain-induction.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars Henrik","Hirata, Rogerio Pessoto","Graven-Nielsen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-001216"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Rygsmerter","health nutrition and quality of life","pains"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain evoked trunk muscle activity changes during fatigue and doms","src":["aau","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/272382790/Pain_evoked_trunk_muscle_activity_changes_during_fatigue_and_DOMS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-001216","identifier":[{"id":"85010601141","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000399452100014","type":"wos"},{"id":"28106312","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-179d741a-4bb6-4dff-abb4-d194b7083096","ucn-053a83b9-53c5-4bdf-9901-378c6d579c92"],"keyword":["health, nutrition and quality of life","pains","rygsmerter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3343523DBA4707985331A8C8E4FCCDC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/272382790/Pain_evoked_trunk_muscle_activity_changes_during_fatigue_and_DOMS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7cb7d78e-7196-4a42-a161-7b1eebf9e0ac","name":"Larsen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7830-1186","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rogerio Pessoto","key":"hiratapau","last":"Hirata","locid":"a8f714d2-931d-4b16-a957-38bd1b321fe6","name":"Hirata, Rogerio Pessoto","orcid":"0000-0002-9943-2713","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"gravennielsenpau","last":"Graven-Nielsen","locid":"474a635b-4e83-4b02-a90b-80d417d37e52","name":"Graven-Nielsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7787-4860","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28106312"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejp.993","issn":["10903801","15322149"],"issn_org":["10903801"],"issue":"5","journal":"European Journal of Pain","pages":"907-917","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pain","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85010601141"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-179d741a-4bb6-4dff-abb4-d194b7083096","ucn-053a83b9-53c5-4bdf-9901-378c6d579c92"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Pain-evoked trunk muscle activity changes during fatigue and DOMS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-001216","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Most Staphylococcus aureus isolates can cause invasive disease given the right circumstances, but it is unknown if some isolates are more likely to cause severe infections than others. S. aureus bloodstream isolates from 120 patients with definite infective endocarditis and 121 with S. aureus bacteraemia without infective endocarditis underwent whole-genome sequencing. Genome-wide association analysis was performed using a variety of bioinformatics approaches including SNP analysis, accessory genome analysis and k-mer based analysis. Core and accessory genome analyses found no association with either of the two clinical groups. In this study, the genome sequences of S. aureus bloodstream isolates did not discriminate between bacteraemia and infective endocarditis. Based on our study and the current literature, it is not convincing that a specific S. aureus genotype is clearly associated to infective endocarditis in patients with S. aureus bacteraemia.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Lilje, Berit","Rasmussen, Rasmus Vedby","Dahl, Anders","Stegger, Marc","Skov, Robert Leo","Fowler, Vance G","Ng, Kim Lee","Kiil, Kristoffer","Larsen, Anders Rhod","Petersen, Andreas","Johansen, Helle Krogh","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Arpi, Magnus","Rosenvinge, Flemming S","Korup, Eva","Høst, Ulla","Hassager, Christian","Gill, Sabine Ute Alice","Hansen, Thomas Fritz","Johannesen, Thor Bech","Smit, Jesper","Søgaard, Peter","Skytt Andersen, Paal","Bruun, Niels Eske"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-009199"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University Medical Center","Translational Genomics North"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"whole genome sequencing of bloodstream staphylococcus aureus isolates does not distinguish bacteraemia from endocarditis","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/mgen.0.000138","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-009199","identifier":[{"id":"29208121","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5729915","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85058279262","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000431155700002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-bea56647-f66e-409c-9de1-d84762b81dfa","sdu-0421c805-04d4-4529-8f7e-71f21a3fda55"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-422B030F010AF8C8C6B48930E55F82B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/mgen.0.000138","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266899079/mgen000138.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129592975/Whole_genome_sequencing_of_bloodstream_Staphylococcus_aureus_isolates_does_not_distinguish_bacteraemia_from_endocarditis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","ke