:"Smit","locid":"29aa2e66-1f20-4693-9114-5f988949c879","name":"Smit, Jesper","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"30606c01-a86b-4eee-90ef-b4268fedaee9","name":"Søgaard, Peter","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Paal","key":"skyttandersenpau","last":"Skytt Andersen","name":"Skytt Andersen, Paal","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"eskebruunpau","last":"Eske-Bruun","locid":"0c4812c1-bd38-4a3f-94a9-1e3367d1af8d","name":"Bruun, Niels Eske","name_org":"Eske-Bruun, Niels","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29208121"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1099/mgen.0.000138","issn":["20575858"],"issue":"11","journal":"Microbial Genomics","publisher":"Microbiology Society","status":"p","title":"Microbial Genomics","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058279262"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bea56647-f66e-409c-9de1-d84762b81dfa","sdu-0421c805-04d4-4529-8f7e-71f21a3fda55"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Whole-genome sequencing of bloodstream Staphylococcus aureus isolates does not distinguish bacteraemia from endocarditis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-009199","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Structural characterizations of three different solid-gas reaction products, recently obtained from abraded solid-state silicate free radicals reacting with two isotopically enriched methane gases, 13CH4 and CD4 (a possible sink for methane on MARS) and with 13CO2, are derived from various dynamic solid-state NMR experiments. These include cross-polarization/depolarization zero-cross times (ZCTs), variable temperature (VT) NMR to study 3-site jump CH3/CD3 activation energies (Ea), and 13CO2/13CH3 molecular species as a spy to determine the approximate diameters for the channel structures for some of these structures. Literature Ea data indicate that l-alanine and 4-CH3-phenanthrene exhibit the highest known Ea values (= 20-22.6 kJ/mol) for CH3 3-site jump motions. The ZCTs for these two compounds are 120 and 162 μs, respectively, indicative of the high Ea values for CH3/CD3 groups. Determination of Ea for 4-CD3-phenanthrene by lowerature 2H MAS NMR experiments supplemented the previously reported liquid-state Ea value (Ea = 21 kJ/mol) for 4-CH3-phenanthrene. Finally, such experiments also revealed the structural difference for the free-radical reaction products with 13CH4 and CD4, i.e, a change from helical to chain structure.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Hans Jørgen","Lindhardt, Anders Thyboe","Bildsøe, Henrik K.","Skibsted, Jørgen","Gan, Zhehong","Hung, Ivan","Larsen, Flemming H."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jakobsen, Hans Jørgen"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Florida State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic solid state nmr experiments reveal structural changes for a methyl silicate nanostructure on deuterium substitution","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85037158532","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-014735","identifier":[{"id":"85037158532","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1d72d90b-605b-4d21-8c85-307d2913b465","ku-ae102f0d-e7ea-46b5-93ab-212bf6c4b61b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-25CF4CD672994AA993C44A20C0005C0B"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, iNANO-huset","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Applied Surface Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"florida state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Florida State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Analytics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans J.","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"2c14e457-bc3a-4fe9-a952-c67daf60ffb8","name":"Jakobsen, Hans Jørgen","name_org":"Jakobsen, Hans J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders T.","key":"lindhardtpau","last":"Lindhardt","locid":"14a66f7a-665d-469e-81f7-df24b20795ea","name":"Lindhardt, Anders Thyboe","name_org":"Lindhardt, Anders T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bildsøepau","last":"Bildsøe","locid":"ed9b2cea-ee92-4c02-8372-b5c7e65be24b","name":"Bildsøe, Henrik K.","name_org":"Bildsøe, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"skibstedpau","last":"Skibsted","locid":"861c686f-c84f-4ad0-8581-c8e4fe22bdf9","name":"Skibsted, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-1534-4466","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhehong","key":"ganpau","last":"Gan","name":"Gan, Zhehong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"hungpau","last":"Hung","name":"Hung, Ivan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Flemming Hofmann","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"eda11dab-a7a0-43f1-91cc-0087bd5538b5","name":"Larsen, Flemming Hofmann","orcid":"0000-0001-5180-6870","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpcc.7b08826","issn":["19327447","19327455"],"issn_org":["19327447"],"issue":"47","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","pages":"26507-26518","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","volume":"121"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85037158532"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1d72d90b-605b-4d21-8c85-307d2913b465","ku-ae102f0d-e7ea-46b5-93ab-212bf6c4b61b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamic Solid-State NMR Experiments Reveal Structural Changes for a Methyl Silicate Nanostructure on Deuterium Substitution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-014735","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In a longitudinal study including 642 healthy 8-11-year-old Danish children, we investigated associations between vitamin D dependent SNP and serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D (25(OH)D) concentrations across a school year (August-June). Serum 25(OH)D was measured three times for every child, which approximated measurements in three seasons (autumn, winter, spring). Dietary and supplement intake, physical activity, BMI and parathyroid hormone were likewise measured at each time point. In all, eleven SNP in four vitamin D-related genes: Cytochrome P450 subfamily IIR1 (CYP2R1); 7-dehydrocholesterol reductase/nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide synthetase-1(DHCR7/NADSYN1); group-specific complement (GC); and vitamin D receptor were genotyped. We found minor alleles of CYP2R1 rs10500804, and of GC rs4588 and rs7041 to be associated with lower serum 25(OH)D concentrations across the three seasons (all P<0·01), with estimated 25(OH)D differences of -5·8 to -10·6 nmol/l from major to minor alleles homozygosity. In contrast, minor alleles homozygosity of rs10741657 and rs1562902 in CYP2R1 was associated with higher serum 25(OH)D concentrations compared with major alleles homozygosity (all P<0·001). Interestingly, the association between season and serum 25(OH)D concentrations was modified by GC rs7041 (P interaction=0·044), observed as absence of increase in serum 25(OH)D from winter to spring among children with minor alleles homozygous genotypes compared with the two other genotypes of rs7041 (P<0·001). Our results suggest that common genetic variants are associated with lower serum 25(OH)D concentrations across a school year. Potentially due to modified serum 25(OH)D response to UVB sunlight exposure. Further confirmation and paediatric studies investigating vitamin D-related health outcomes of these genotypic differences are needed.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Petersen, Rikke A","Larsen, Lesli H","Damsgaard, Camilla T","Sørensen, Louise B","Hjorth, Mads F","An