{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Although the pathogenesis of hidradenitis suppurativa (HS) remains enigmatic, several factors point to potential involvement of the cutaneous microbiome. Insight into the cutaneous microbiome in HS using next-generation sequencing may provide novel data on the microbiological diversity of the skin.  OBJECTIVE: To investigate the follicular skin microbiome in patients with HS and in healthy controls.  DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: This case-control study obtained punch biopsy specimens from patients with HS (lesional and nonlesional) and healthy controls between October 1, 2014, and August 1, 2016. Data were analyzed from March to November 2016. Patients with HS were recruited from the Department of Dermatology, Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde, Denmark. Biopsy specimens were analyzed at the Department of Microbiology and Infection Control, Statens Serum Institut, Copenhagen, Denmark. None of the participants received any antibiotics (systemic or topical therapy) within 1 month before the study. In patients with HS, biopsy specimens were obtained from lesional skin (axilla or groin) and nonlesional skin. Only nodules containing at least 1 visible hair follicle were biopsied. Biopsy specimens from healthy controls were obtained from the axilla only.  MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: The different microbiomes were investigated using next-generation sequencing targeting 16S and 18S ribosomal RNA.  RESULTS: The skin microbiome was characterized in 30 patients with HS (mean [SD] age, 46.9 [14.0] years; 19 [63% female]) and 24 healthy controls (mean [SD] age, 32.2 [12.0] years; 13 [54% female]). The next-generation sequencing data provided a previously unreported (to our knowledge) characterization of the skin microbiome in HS. The study demonstrated that the microbiome in HS differs significantly from that in healthy controls in lesional and nonlesional skin. Overall, the following 5 microbiome types were identified: Corynebacterium species (type I), Acinetobacter and Moraxella species (type II), Staphylococcus epidermidis (type III), Porphyromonas and Peptoniphilus species (type IV), and Propionibacterium acnes (type V). In lesional skin, microbiome types consisted predominantly of type I or type IV. Microbiome type IV was not detected in healthy controls. Several taxa, including Propionibacterium, showed a significantly higher relative abundance in healthy controls vs HS skin, indicating that Propionibacterium may be part of the pathogenesis in HS.  CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: The study findings suggest a link between a dysbiotic cutaneous microbiome and HS.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Ring, Hans Christian","Thorsen, Jonathan","Saunte, Ditte Marie Lindhardt","Lilje, Berit","Bay, Lene","Riis, Peter Theut","Larsen, Niels","Andersen, Lee O’Brien","Nielsen, Henrik V.","Miller, Iben M.","Bjarnsholt, Thomas","Fuursted, Kurt","Jemec, Gregor B E"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-432123"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Danish Genome Institute"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the follicular skin microbiome in patients with hidradenitis suppurativa and healthy controls","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-432123","identifier":[{"id":"85029534056","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28538949","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5710430","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-40a9f7d1-1726-422b-95e9-0760366106cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-207DE95D986D10699029DFA8AD9FD4E5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Genome Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Christian","key":"ringpau","last":"Ring","name":"Ring, Hans Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jonathan","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","name":"Thorsen, Jonathan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ditte M.","key":"sauntepau","last":"Saunte","locid":"7131c49a-fd53-415c-9262-44d2c738c731","name":"Saunte, Ditte Marie Lindhardt","name_org":"Saunte, Ditte M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Berit","key":"liljepau","last":"Lilje","name":"Lilje, Berit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lene","key":"baypau","last":"Bay","locid":"22f49c41-e569-43c4-8978-94bc9e411869","name":"Bay, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-4164-5900","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Theut","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","name":"Riis, Peter Theut","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Niels","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lee O’Brien","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lee O’Brien","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Henrik V.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik V.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Iben M.","key":"millerpau","last":"Miller","name":"Miller, Iben M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas","key":"bjarnsholtpau","last":"Bjarnsholt","locid":"cb3ccb7d-0415-40e5-9bba-c9bc26b6316d","name":"Bjarnsholt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8003-7414","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Kurt","key":"fuurstedpau","last":"Fuursted","locid":"067cf1fa-082a-4edd-bf12-bdd3034b4ef5","name":"Fuursted, Kurt","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gregor Borut","key":"jemecpau","last":"Jemec","locid":"b963b007-18b6-4432-897f-28b6a08275be","name":"Jemec, Gregor B E","name_org":"Jemec, Gregor Borut","orcid":"0000-0002-0712-2540","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28538949"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamadermatol.2017.0904","issn":["11301910","21686068"],"issn_org":["21686068"],"issue":"9","journal":"JAMA Dermatology","pages":"897-905","status":"p","title":"JAMA Dermatology","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029534056"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-40a9f7d1-1726-422b-95e9-0760366106cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The follicular skin microbiome in patients with hidradenitis suppurativa and healthy controls","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432123","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) is the common name for a heterogeneous group of highly drug-resistant staphylococci. Two major MRSA classes are distinguished based on epidemiology, namely community-associated (CA) and hospital-associated (HA) MRSA. Notably, the distinction of CA- and HA-MRSA based on molecular traits remains difficult due to the high genomic plasticity of S. aureus. Here we sought to pinpoint global distinguishing features of CA- and HA-MRSA through a comparative genome and proteome analysis of the notorious MRSA lineage USA300. We show for the first time that CA- and HA-MRSA isolates can be distinguished by 2 distinct extracellular protein abundance clusters that are predictive not only for epidemiologic behavior, but also for their growth and survival within epithelial cells. This ‘exoproteome profiling’ also groups more distantly related HA-MRSA isolates into the HA exoproteome cluster. Comparative genome analysis suggests that these distinctive features of CA- and HA-MRSA isolates relate predominantly to the accessory genome. Intriguingly, the identified exoproteome clusters differ in the relative abundance of typical cytoplasmic proteins, suggesting that signatures of cytoplasmic proteins in the exoproteome represent a new distinguishing feature of CA- and HA-MRSA. Our comparative genome and proteome analysis focuses attention on potentially distinctive roles of ‘liberated’ cytoplasmic proteins in the epidemiology and intracellular survival of CA- and HA-MRSA isolates. Such extracellular cytoplasmic proteins were recently invoked in staphylococcal virulence, but their implication in the epidemiology of MRSA is unprecedented.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Mekonnen, Solomon A.","Palma Medina, Laura M.","Glasner, Corinna","Tsompanidou, Eleni","de Jong, Anne","Grasso, Stefano","Schaffer, Marc","Mäder, Ulrike","Larsen, Anders R.","Gumpert, Heidi","Westh, Henrik","Völker, Uwe","Otto, Andreas","Becher, Dörte","van Dijl, Jan Maarten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482828"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community","Epithelial Cells","Exoproteome","Hospital","MRSA","Protein secretion","Staphylococcus","USA300","Virulence factor","moonlighting"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"signatures of cytoplasmic proteins in the exoproteome distinguish community and hospital associated methicillin resistant i staphylococcus aureus i usa000000000300 lineages","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/21505594.2017.1325064","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-482828","identifier":[{"id":"28475476","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85019601862","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5626246","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-95a0fd90-7c13-4c5c-a8b9-e20e8366fa17"],"keyword":["MRSA","Staphylococcus","USA300","community","epithelial cells","exoproteome","hospital","moonlighting","protein secretion","virulence factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47664240597D8DDA0EDC674FF12B5540"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/189450546/Signatures_of_cytoplasmic_proteins_in_the_exoproteome_distinguish_community_and_hospital_associated_methicillin_resistant_Staphylococcus_aureus.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/21505594.2017.1325064","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Microbiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Solomon A.","key":"mekonnenpau","last":"Mekonnen","name":"Mekonnen, Solomon A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Laura M.","key":"palmamedinapau","last":"Palma Medina","name":"Palma Medina, Laura M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Corinna","key":"glasnerpau","last":"Glasner","name":"Glasner, Corinna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eleni","key":"tsompanidoupau","last":"Tsompanidou","name":"Tsompanidou, Eleni","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"dejongpau","last":"de Jong","name":"de Jong, Anne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefano","key":"grassopau","last":"Grasso","name":"Grasso, Stefano","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marc","key":"schafferpau","last":"Schaffer","name":"Schaffer, Marc","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrike","key":"mäderpau","last":"Mäder","name":"Mäder, Ulrike","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders R.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders R.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Heidi","key":"gumpertpau","last":"Gumpert","name":"Gumpert, Heidi","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Uwe","key":"völkerpau","last":"Völker","name":"Völker, Uwe","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"ottopau","last":"Otto","name":"Otto, Andreas","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dörte","key":"becherpau","last":"Becher","name":"Becher, Dörte","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan Maarten","key":"vandijlpau","last":"van Dijl","name":"van Dijl, Jan Maarten","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28475476"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/21505594.2017.1325064","issn":["21505594","21505608"],"issn_org":["21505594"],"issue":"6","journal":"Virulence","pages":"891-907","status":"p","title":"Virulence","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019601862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-95a0fd90-7c13-4c5c-a8b9-e20e8366fa17"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Signatures of cytoplasmic proteins in the exoproteome distinguish community- and hospital-associated methicillin-resistant <i>Staphylococcus aureus</i> USA300 lineages","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482828","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The cadherin (cdh) superfamily of adhesion molecules carry O-linked mannose (O-Man) glycans at highly conserved sites localized to specific β-strands of their extracellular cdh (EC) domains. These O-Man glycans do not appear to be elongated like O-Man glycans found on α-dystroglycan (α-DG), and we recently demonstrated that initiation of cdh/protocadherin (pcdh) O-Man glycosylation is not dependent on the evolutionary conserved POMT1/POMT2 enzymes that initiate O-Man glycosylation on α-DG. Here, we used a CRISPR/Cas9 genetic dissection strategy combined with sensitive and quantitative O-Man glycoproteomics to identify a homologous family of four putative protein O-mannosyltransferases encoded by the TMTC1-4 genes, which were found to be imperative for cdh and pcdh O-Man glycosylation. KO of all four TMTC genes in HEK293 cells resulted in specific loss of cdh and pcdh O-Man glycosylation, whereas combined KO of TMTC1 and TMTC3 resulted in selective loss of O-Man glycans on specific β-strands of EC domains, suggesting that each isoenzyme serves a different function. In addition, O-Man glycosylation of IPT/TIG domains of plexins and hepatocyte growth factor receptor was not affected in TMTC KO cells, suggesting the existence of yet another O-Man glycosylation machinery. Our study demonstrates that regulation of O-mannosylation in higher eukaryotes is more complex than envisioned, and the discovery of the functions of TMTCs provide insight into cobblestone lissencephaly caused by deficiency in TMTC3.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Larsen, Ida Signe Bohse","Narimatsu, Yoshiki","Joshi, Hiren J.","Siukstaite, Lina","Harrison, Oliver J","Brasch, Julia","Goodman, Kerry M","Hansen, Lars","Shapiro, Lawrence","Honig, Barry","Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","Clausen, Henrik","Halim, Adnan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-486480"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovery of an o mannosylation pathway selectively serving cadherins and protocadherins","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5651762?pdf=render","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-486480","identifier":[{"id":"85031317570","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5651762","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28973932","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9b9ffdbc-5e09-4255-9429-b8ab0db9a4f5"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE197C2D73CB634DCBBF8D9C9CD18AA5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5651762?pdf=render","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ida Signe Bohse","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f2869bf8-54a4-49ae-9db2-434d2714b362","name":"Larsen, Ida Signe Bohse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yoshiki","key":"narimatsupau","last":"Narimatsu","locid":"d9d8a2cb-0c61-43eb-9b4c-4b4248e71f06","name":"Narimatsu, Yoshiki","orcid":"0000-0003-1428-5695","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hiren Jitendra","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","locid":"59e7c6d1-b66a-49df-a6f5-4dd110dd7e03","name":"Joshi, Hiren J.","name_org":"Joshi, Hiren Jitendra","orcid":"0000-0002-8192-2829","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lina","key":"siukstaitepau","last":"Siukstaite","locid":"575e6acc-cf19-41d5-9c64-84dd64adafdf","name":"Siukstaite, Lina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Oliver J","key":"harrisonpau","last":"Harrison","name":"Harrison, Oliver J","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julia","key":"braschpau","last":"Brasch","name":"Brasch, Julia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kerry M","key":"goodmanpau","last":"Goodman","name":"Goodman, Kerry M","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ba4afa63-58c1-4441-a8b2-c1eae8279ca9","name":"Hansen, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lawrence","key":"shapiropau","last":"Shapiro","name":"Shapiro, Lawrence","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Barry","key":"honigpau","last":"Honig","name":"Honig, Barry","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sergey Y","key":"vakhrushevpau","last":"Vakhrushev","locid":"9d7a6af7-6053-4ce2-93ea-a93a65c04343","name":"Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","name_org":"Vakhrushev, Sergey Y","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"a7882c09-1275-4857-8b5b-7e3efc1d088d","name":"Clausen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0915-5055","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adnan","key":"halimpau","last":"Halim","locid":"65f08640-6203-4f49-ad7e-f95cb9c070b8","name":"Halim, Adnan","orcid":"0000-0003-1629-187X","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28973932"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1708319114","issn":["00278424","10916490"],"issn_org":["00278424"],"issue":"42","journal":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","pages":"11163-11168","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031317570"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9b9ffdbc-5e09-4255-9429-b8ab0db9a4f5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discovery of an O-mannosylation pathway selectively serving cadherins and protocadherins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-486480","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Denmark is a low prevalence country with regard to methicillin resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA). In 2008 and 2014, two neonatal wards in the Copenhagen area experienced outbreaks with a typical community acquired MRSA belonging to the same spa type and sequence type (t015:ST45) and both were PVL and ACME negative. In outbreak 1, the isolates harbored SCCmec IVa and in outbreak 2 SCCmec V. The clinical presentation differed between the two outbreaks, as none of five MRSA positive mothers in outbreak 1 had mastitis vs. five of six MRSA positive mothers in outbreak 2 (p < 0.02). To investigate if whole-genome sequencing could identify virulence genes associated with mastitis, t015:ST45 isolates from Denmark (N = 101) were whole-genome sequenced. Sequence analysis confirmed two separate outbreaks with no sign of sustained spread into the community. Analysis of the accessory genome between isolates from the two outbreaks revealed a S. aureus pathogenicity island containing enterotoxin C and enterotoxin-like L only in isolates from outbreak 2. Enterotoxin C and enterotoxin-like L carrying S. aureus are associated with bovine mastitis and our findings indicate that these may also be important virulence factors for human mastitis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Franck, Kristina Træholt","Gumpert, Heidi","Olesen, Bente","Larsen, Anders Rhod","Petersen, Andreas","Bangsborg, Jette","Albertsen, Per","Westh, Henrik","Bartels, Mette Damkjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i staphylococcal aureus i enterotoxin c and enterotoxin like l associated with post partum mastitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2017.00173","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-494131","identifier":[{"id":"85014536946","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28223977","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5293744","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a892820b-a0fa-4016-a42c-50ddddd42838"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C837BEAEADA52B5FB6515BDAEA357984"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2017.00173","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/195290685/fmicb_08_00173.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Træholt","key":"franckpau","last":"Franck","name":"Franck, Kristina Træholt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Heidi","key":"gumpertpau","last":"Gumpert","name":"Gumpert, Heidi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Bente","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Rhod","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Rhod","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Andreas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette","key":"bangsborgpau","last":"Bangsborg","name":"Bangsborg, Jette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Per","key":"albertsenpau","last":"Albertsen","locid":"062615dc-f574-44bd-b7e9-9affd540dd7e","name":"Albertsen, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Henrik T.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, Henrik T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Damkjær","key":"bartelspau","last":"Bartels","name":"Bartels, Mette Damkjær","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28223977"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2017.00173","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"173","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014536946"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a892820b-a0fa-4016-a42c-50ddddd42838"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"<i>Staphylococcal aureus</i> Enterotoxin C and Enterotoxin-Like L Associated with Post-partum Mastitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494131","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The extensive use of CAS at upper secondary school in Denmark provides a laboratory for research on the development of standards for CAS teaching. The poster focuses on action research into teachers developing lessons and student activities in an ongoing collaboration between university and high schools on use of CAS in mathematics teaching. Coaches1 mediate design processes, reflection and documentation, and enable sharing. We discuss coaching as a valuable part of action research, and how to draw findings from the collaboration.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bang, Henrik Peter","Grønbæk, Niels","Larsen, Claus Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-498878"],"event":{"end":"2017-02-05","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2017-02-01","title":"Congress of the European Society for Research in Mathematics Education","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Christianshavns Gymnasium"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coaching and engaging developing teaching with cas in high school","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://keynote.conference-services.net/resources/444/5118/pdf/CERME10_0218.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-498878","ids":["ku-b0867787-fb53-4b76-badf-570271055832"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EA6208311E73259215B3A863E63E4F9F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://keynote.conference-services.net/resources/444/5118/pdf/CERME10_0218.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Christianshavns Gymnasium"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Didactics of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Peter","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, Henrik Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"92b1622e-630d-49e3-a623-55c283a2db0f","name":"Grønbæk, Niels","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-856X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus Richard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Claus Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b0867787-fb53-4b76-badf-570271055832"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coaching and engaging. Developing teaching with CAS in High School","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-498878","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper is based on a systematic literature search aiming at identifying research on the role of libraries as institutions underpinning a sustainable public sphere in a digital age. The major research questions are: 1. Is systematic literature search a fruitful method when it comes to a social scientific/cultural scientific undertakings such as the ALMPUB research project? 2. How does research approach libraries as public sphere institutions? Which topics are dealt with? What about theoretical approaches and what about empirical research versus theoretical contributions and position papers? Some of the major findings are: Research on libraries as public sphere institutions cover a wide range of topics the dominating being freedom of access to information, often related to social inclusion, empowerment and justice. Contributions are often normative and non-empirical, but the proportion of empirically based research is increasing. This paper focuses on contributions related to public libraries.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Audunson, Ragnar","Svandhild, Aabø,","Blomgren, Roger","Evjen, Sunniva","Jahnsen, Heidi","Jochumsen, Henrik","Larsen, Håkon","Rasmussen, Casper Hvenegaard","Ødemark, Ingjerd Leigred"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501175"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-25","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2017-08-23","title":"nccpr 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community building","Faculty of Humanities","Public libraries","Public sphere","Social inclusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"public libraries as an infrastructure for a sustainable public sphere a systematic review of research a preliminary paper","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":