194-d3df-49ab-ae7a-cf4251cc7fd5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Challenges in Teaching Praxis When CAS Is Used in Upper Secondary Mathematics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509365","year":"2017","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Protein O-mannosylation is found in yeast and metazoans and a family of conserved orthologous protein O-mannosyltransferases is believed to initiate this important post-translational modification. We recently discovered that the cadherin superfamily carries O-linked mannose (O-Man) glycans at highly conserved residues in specific extracellular cadherin domains, and it was suggested that the function of E-cadherin was dependent on the O-Man glycans. Deficiencies in enzymes catalyzing O-Man biosynthesis, including the two human protein O-mannosyltransferases, POMT1 and POMT2, underlie a subgroup of congenital muscular dystrophies (CMD) designated α-dystroglycanopathies, because deficient O-Man glycosylation of -dystroglycan disrupts laminin interaction with -dystroglycan and the extracellular matrix. In order to explore the functions of O-Man glycans on cadherins and protocadherins we used a combinatorial gene editing strategy in multiple cell lines to evaluate the role of the two POMTs initiating O-Man glycosylation and the major enzyme elongating O-Man glycans, the protein O-mannose β-1,2-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase, POMGnT1. Surprisingly, O-mannosylation of cadherins and protocadherins do not require POMT1 and/or POMT2 in contrast to -dystroglycan, and moreover the O-Man glycans on cadherins are not elongated. Thus, the classical and evolutionary conserved POMT O-mannosylation pathway is essentially dedicated to -dystroglycan and a few other proteins, while a novel O-mannosylation process in mammalian cells is predicted to serve the large cadherin superfamily and other proteins.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Larsen, Ida Signe Bohse","Narimatsu, Yoshiki","Joshi, Hiren J.","Yang, Zhang","Harrison, Oliver J","Brasch, Julia","Shapiro, Lawrence","Honig, Barry","Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","Clausen, Henrik","Halim, Adnan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-536649"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mammalian o mannosylation of cadherins and plexins is independent of protein o mannosyltransferase 000000000001 and 000000000002","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5500819?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-536649","identifier":[{"id":"28512129","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5500819","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85023620334","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f001301a-ff8c-40b0-88aa-5abc0dc2201a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E1F7D414EA1CC070B7857F953653870"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5500819?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ida Signe Bohse","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f2869bf8-54a4-49ae-9db2-434d2714b362","name":"Larsen, Ida Signe Bohse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yoshiki","key":"narimatsupau","last":"Narimatsu","locid":"d9d8a2cb-0c61-43eb-9b4c-4b4248e71f06","name":"Narimatsu, Yoshiki","orcid":"0000-0003-1428-5695","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hiren Jitendra","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","locid":"59e7c6d1-b66a-49df-a6f5-4dd110dd7e03","name":"Joshi, Hiren J.","name_org":"Joshi, Hiren Jitendra","orcid":"0000-0002-8192-2829","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhang","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"69786fb3-302a-41d6-b1f4-a3565265efc7","name":"Yang, Zhang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Oliver J","key":"harrisonpau","last":"Harrison","name":"Harrison, Oliver J","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julia","key":"braschpau","last":"Brasch","name":"Brasch, Julia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lawrence","key":"shapiropau","last":"Shapiro","name":"Shapiro, Lawrence","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Barry","key":"honigpau","last":"Honig","name":"Honig, Barry","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sergey Y","key":"vakhrushevpau","last":"Vakhrushev","locid":"9d7a6af7-6053-4ce2-93ea-a93a65c04343","name":"Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","name_org":"Vakhrushev, Sergey Y","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"a7882c09-1275-4857-8b5b-7e3efc1d088d","name":"Clausen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0915-5055","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adnan","key":"halimpau","last":"Halim","locid":"65f08640-6203-4f49-ad7e-f95cb9c070b8","name":"Halim, Adnan","orcid":"0000-0003-1629-187X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28512129"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m117.794487","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"11586-11598","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","title_org":"The Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"292"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85023620334"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f001301a-ff8c-40b0-88aa-5abc0dc2201a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mammalian O-mannosylation of Cadherins and Plexins is Independent of Protein O-mannosyltransferase 1 and 2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-536649","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Phase separation of in situ forming poly (lactide-co-glycolide acid) (PLGA) implants with agarose hydrogels as the provider of nonsolvent (water) mimicking subcutaneous tissue was investigated using a novel UV-vis imaging-based analytical platform. In situ forming implants of PLGA-1-methyl-2-pyrrolidinone and PLGA-triacetin representing fast and slow phase separating systems, respectively, were evaluated using this platform. Upon contact with the agarose hydrogel, the phase separation of the systems was followed by the study of changes in light transmission and absorbance as a function of time and position. For the PLGA-1-methyl-2-pyrrolidinone system, the rate of spatial phase separation was determined and found to decrease with increasing the PLGA concentration from 20% to 40% (w/w). Hydrogels with different agarose concentrations (1% and 10% (w/v)) were prepared for providing the nonsolvent, water, to the in situ forming PLGA implants simulating the injection site environment. The resulting implant morphology depended on the stiffness of hydrogel matrix, indicating that the matrix in which implants are formed is of importance. Overall, the work showed that the UV-vis imaging-based platform with an agarose hydrogel mimicking the subcutaneous tissue holds potential in providing bio-relevant and mechanistic information on the phase separation processes of in situ forming implants.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sun, Yu","Jensen, Henrik","Petersen, Nickolaj J.","Larsen, Susan Weng","Østergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541924"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phase separation of in situ forming poly lactide co glycolide acid implants investigated using a hydrogel based subcutaneous tissue surrogate and uv vis imaging","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-541924","identifier":[{"id":"85029298862","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28803207","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f8ba2692-1a2d-45c3-8a78-fca5cbe93c2e"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8986F8257575FD19A25EFA5225264D16"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yu","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","locid":"e0592935-37d6-4391-8356-4c25939379f1","name":"Sun, Yu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"88cd8faf-69c6-46de-a355-03f93d52eeb1","name":"Jensen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Nickolaj J","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1327012e-b05a-43ca-8332-4001e6730d79","name":"Petersen, Nickolaj J.","name_org":"Petersen, Nickolaj J","orcid":"0000-0001-5101-3571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susan W","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f6980004-978f-4940-b71f-de426f2a084a","name":"Larsen, Susan Weng","name_org":"Larsen, Susan W","orcid":"0000-0002-3818-7275","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28803207"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpba.2017.07.056","issn":["07317085","1873264X"],"issn_org":["07317085"],"journal":"Journal of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Analysis","pages":"682-691","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Analysis","volume":"145"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029298862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f8ba2692-1a2d-45c3-8a78-fca5cbe93c2e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Phase separation of in situ forming poly (lactide-co-glycolide acid) implants investigated using a hydrogel-based subcutaneous tissue surrogate and UV-vis imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541924","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
