rne audiovisuel komik på tværs af medier","title":"Helt til grin"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d53eba56-1b5c-481e-992a-312de9442284"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Syrebad og flertydigheder : om sketchkomediens aktuelle karakteristika","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-251078","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarized (HP) 129Xe have been demonstrated as a useful probe for magnetic resonance (MR) lung imaging and show promise for in vivo perfusion imaging and brown adipose tissue characterization. Reports of large polarization enhancements for 129Xe using dynamic nuclearpolarization (DNP) have raised expectations that DNP can be an alternative to the standard spin exchange optical pumping (SEOP) method. We show that it is possible to produce HP 129Xe gas using the clinical GE SpinLab polarizer, thus extending the practical use of the system beyond the primary purpose of hyperpolarizing liquid biomolecules.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mariager, Christian Østergaard","Ringgaard, Steffen","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Laustsen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263521"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-27","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2017-04-22","title":"ISMRM 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized xenon by d dnp using the clinical ge spinlab polarizer system","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-263521","ids":["au-eb1b2343-da79-4b85-a3bf-2bbb835eee29"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5A4012986FF25DCC83E075BEC16C370F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark (DTU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ge healthcare","name":"GE Healthcare","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"mariagerpau","last":"Mariager","locid":"e647818e-e048-4b35-9ec6-7f5443b9fe72","name":"Mariager, Christian Østergaard","name_org":"Mariager, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen","key":"ringgaardpau","last":"Ringgaard","locid":"56699a63-018d-4902-b5f7-9816f8b7e4fc","name":"Ringgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0001-5353-7379","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","name":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"ISMRM 2017 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eb1b2343-da79-4b85-a3bf-2bbb835eee29"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hyperpolarized xenon by d-DNP using the clinical GE SpinLab polarizer system","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263521","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The X-WiWa project was motivated by Denmark's long term vision for off-shore wind energy and the many technical and scientic challenges in existing methodologies for assessing the design parameters, for both winds and waves. X-WiWa succeeded in developing a most up-to-date modeling system for wind modeling for oshore wind farms. This modeling system consists of the atmospheric Weather Research and Forecasting (WRF) model, the wave model SWAN and an interface the Wave Boundary Layer Model WBLM, within the framework of coupled-ocean-atmosphere-wave-sediment transport modeling system COAWST (Hereinafter the WRF-WBLM-SWAN model). WBLM is implemented in SWAN, and it calculates stress and kinetic energy budgets in the lowest atmospheric layer where the wave-induced stress is introduced to the atmospheric modeling. WBLM ensures consistent calculation of stress for both the atmospheric and wave modeling, which was considered a major improvement to previous attempts in the literature. This methodology thus provides an option to avoid the parametrization of an often used interface parameter, the roughness length. Many parametrization schemes for the roughness length have brought diverse estimates and associated uncertainties to the modelled wind speed. Data validation using measurements from the Baltic Sea and North Sea around Denmark suggests that the coupled modeling system WRF-WBLM-SWAN outperforms the non-coupled, no-wave, WRF modeling of wind; an improvement by 10% or more is present at strong winds, which can aect the choice of the off-shore wind turbine type. X-WiWa examined various methodologies for wave modeling. The offline coupling system using atmospheric data such as WRF or global reanalysis wind field to the MIKE 21 SW model has been improved with considerations of stability, air density, currents and new wind drag relations. X-WiWa suggests that, implementation of an online coupling technology does not necessarily provide better estimation of the waves, if the physics have not been properly described. This is supported by the comparisons of the modeled wave data between offline MIKE 21 SW modeling and the WRF-WBLM-SWAN modeling. The two provide comparably good wave calculations for coastal areas but the latter underestimates the wave height for far offshore areas, which is speculated to be related to the dissipation description in the wave source functions, where further improvement is seen necessary. X-WiWa puts modeling efforts on storms that are defined to be contributors to the extreme wind and extreme significant wave height through the annual maximum method. Thus for 23 years from 1994 to 2016, 429 storm days are simulated for the extreme wind, and for 1994 to 2014, 932 storm days are simulated for the extreme signicant wave height. The 50-year winds at 10 m, 50 m and 100 m over the waters around Denmark are calculated and validated and agreement is satisfactory. The 50-year significant wave height for the Danish waters and surrounding North Sea and Baltic Sea are presented from the online and offline systems. The modeling systems, data, analysis, results and publications are introduced and provided on www.xwiwa.dk. These outputs are expected to be useful for general offshore wind and wave applications such as Operation and Maintenance, Forecasting, and Design.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","Bolanos, Rodolfo","Du, Jianting","Kelly, Mark C.","Kofoed-Hansen, Henrik","Larsen, Søren Ejling","Karagali, Ioanna","Badger, Merete","Hahmann, Andrea N.","Imberger, Marc","Tornfeldt Sørensen, Jacob","Jackson, Sara","Volker, Patrick","Svenstrup Petersen, Ole","Jenkins, Alastair","Graham, Angus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-318496"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uni Research AS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extreme winds and waves for offshore turbines coupling atmosphere and wave modeling for design and operation in coastal zones","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139272513/FinalReport_PSO12020_XWiWa_20171031.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-318496","ids":["dtu-2ee279d3-6310-4a9b-a5a6-d4a236568640"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F0C772F3B815D5022382CFFFF8E22882"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139272513/FinalReport_PSO12020_XWiWa_20171031.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Resource Assessment Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"uni research as","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uni Research AS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoli Guo","key":"larsénpau","last":"Larsén","locid":"b4f442ea-5cb6-4979-b106-e210895b35d8","name":"Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","orcid":"0000-0001-8696-0720","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rodolfo","key":"bolanospau","last":"Bolanos","name":"Bolanos, Rodolfo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jianting","key":"dupau","last":"Du","locid":"4257c79a-e809-47eb-b2ee-5e9bc61ec3e6","name":"Du, Jianting","orcid":"0000-0002-4145-1073","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark C.","key":"kellypau","last":"Kelly","locid":"29c989ab-5faf-4128-b624-22bc306b6918","name":"Kelly, Mark C.","orcid":"0000-0003-2882-4450","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"kofoedhansenpau","last":"Kofoed-Hansen","name":"Kofoed-Hansen, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Ejling","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6fc30efb-9800-4fe7-ba37-bee5bf5243f3","name":"Larsen, Søren Ejling","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ioanna","key":"karagalipau","last":"Karagali","locid":"c79a1545-0be2-4274-99c1-9492136c5f41","name":"Karagali, Ioanna","orcid":"0000-0002-8695-7190","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merete","key":"badgerpau","last":"Badger","locid":"0493bb98-dd30-4b8d-8540-c3889c8a4e55","name":"Badger, Merete","orcid":"0000-0002-2072-8619","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea N.","key":"hahmannpau","last":"Hahmann","locid":"c8315d00-83a0-43f3-85c8-cf51258cdc00","name":"Hahmann, Andrea N.","orcid":"0000-0001-8785-3492","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"imbergerpau","last":"Imberger","locid":"b5a91908-5f3f-4598-893f-2ba90ffc5180","name":"Imberger, Marc","orcid":"0000-0002-4283-5394","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"tornfeldtsørensenpau","last":"Tornfeldt Sørensen","name":"Tornfeldt Sørensen, Jacob","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"jacksonpau","last":"Jackson","name":"Jackson, Sara","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"volkerpau","last":"Volker","locid":"6c7ee776-b4ab-4b52-8ef5-848cf2569621","name":"Volker, Patrick","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"svenstruppetersenpau","last":"Svenstrup Petersen","name":"Svenstrup Petersen, Ole","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alastair","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","name":"Jenkins, Alastair","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Angus","key":"grahampau","last":"Graham","name":"Graham, Angus","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"113","publisher":"DTU Wind Energy","repno":"DTU Wind Energy E","series":"DTU Wind Energy E","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2ee279d3-6310-4a9b-a5a6-d4a236568640"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Extreme winds and waves for offshore turbines: Coupling atmosphere and wave modeling for design and operation in coastal zones","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-318496","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this study we demonstrate how reconstruction for IDEAL spiral CSI (spectroscopic imaging scheme developed for hyperpolarized dynamic metabolic MR imaging) can be improved by using regularization with a sparsity constraint. By exploiting sparsity of the spectral domain, IDEAL spiral CSI can achieve chemical shift encoding by acquisition of only few time-shifted echoes. The minimum number of echoes required to avoid noise amplification can be decreased by means of regularization enforcing spectral sparsity, hereby reducing scan time. Improvements achieved by using regularized reconstruction are demonstrated for in vivo data from a hyperpolarized cardiac study of a pig.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Rie Beck","Mariager, Christian","Laustsen, Christoffer","Schulte, Rolf F.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Hanson, Lars G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350695"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-27","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2017-04-22","title":"ISMRM 25th Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Global Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved reconstruction for ideal spiral csi","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/130823176/Abstract2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350695","ids":["dtu-9aa8990a-ffb1-4534-b9c8-9433b75cf6e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0D3C4821F720897706A11DBD10600D30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/130823176/Abstract2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"ge global research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"GE Global Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rie Beck","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"mariagerpau","last":"Mariager","name":"Mariager, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf F.","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, Rolf F.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars G.","key":"hansonpau","last":"Hanson","locid":"6c7cc6f9-5b6a-47dc-bb02-efe208e52f16","name":"Hanson, Lars G.","orcid":"0000-0002-8204-6912","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9aa8990a-ffb1-4534-b9c8-9433b75cf6e3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved reconstruction for IDEAL spiral CSI","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350695","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a comparison between measured and simulated tower loads for the Danish offshore wind farm Nysted 2. Previously, only limited full scale experimental data containing tower load measurements have been published, and in many cases the measurements include only a limited range of wind speeds. In general, tower loads in wake conditions are very challenging to predict correctly in simulations. The Nysted project offers an improved insight to this field as six wind turbines located in the Nysted II wind farm have been instrumented to measure tower top and tower bottom moments. All recorded structural data have been organized in a database, which in addition contains relevant wind turbine SCADA data as well as relevant meteorological data - e.g. wind speed and wind direction - from an offshore mast located in the immediate vicinity of the wind farm. The database contains data from a period extending over a time span of more than 3 years. Based on the recorded data basic mechanisms driving the increased loading experienced by wind turbines operating in offshore wind farm conditions have been identified, characterized and modeled. The modeling is based on the Dynamic Wake Meandering (DWM) approach in combination with the state-of-the-art aeroelastic model HAWC2, and has previously as well as in this study shown good agreement with the measurements. The conclusions from the study have several parts. In general the tower bending and yaw loads show a good agreement between measurements and simulations. However, there are situations that are still difficult to match. One is tower loads of single-wake operation near rated ambient wind speed for single wake situations for spacing’s around 7-8D. A specific target of the study was to investigate whether the largest tower fatigue loads are associated with a certain downstream distance. This has been identified in both simulations and measurements, though a rather flat optimum is seen in the measurements.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Torben J.","Larsen, Gunner Chr.","Pedersen, Mads Mølgaard","Enevoldsen, Karen","Madsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351332"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-01","place":"Visby, se","start":"2017-05-30","title":"Wake Conference 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of the dynamic wake meander model with focus on tower loads paper","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/142084815/TJLarsen_ver_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351332","ids":["dtu-9cda53ff-bc2b-413a-9e66-7d1a41a653a0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0FA3C3E4349E33CDE168DE33C8C960C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/142084815/TJLarsen_ver_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Wind turbine loads & control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben J.","key":"larsentorbenjppu","last":"Larsen","locid":"965dbaf9-67c6-4f4d-b512-2df4845d740d","name":"Larsen, Torben J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6741-5057","rank":1,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunner Chr.","key":"larsengunnerchrppu","last":"Larsen","locid":"0b53b2aa-2896-42e4-b6a1-4926d8295cbc","name":"Larsen, Gunner Chr.","orcid":"0000-0002-6482-8208","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Mølgaard","key":"pedersenmadsmølgaardppu","last":"Pedersen","locid":"1fa1a82a-9930-4574-a52b-25c847f2534c","name":"Pedersen, Mads Mølgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-1411-6402","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"enevoldsenkarenppu","last":"Enevoldsen","locid":"16907024-8e47-4b94-9bd8-98f75ae6b1de","name":"Enevoldsen, Karen","rank":4,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H. A.","key":"madsenhenrikppu","last":"Madsen","locid":"458e950b-adfd-4f2d-8d0d-ef39dee24bea","name":"Madsen, Henrik","name_org":"Madsen, H. A.","orcid":"0000-0003-0690-3713","rank":5,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9cda53ff-bc2b-413a-9e66-7d1a41a653a0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Validation of the dynamic wake meander model with focus on tower loads : Paper","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-351332","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This chapter discusses principles of nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) and MRI followed by a survey on the major classes of MRI contrast agents (CA), their modes of action, and some of the most significative applications. The two more established classes of MRI-CA are represented by paramagnetic metal complexes (i.e., Gd(III) and Mn(II)) and iron oxide particles, acting on T1 and T2* of the water protons signals, respectively. Along the years many efforts have been devoted to endow these relaxation enhancement agents with improved sensitivity, targeting, and responsive properties that have markedly broadened the range of applications in respect to the clinically used systems. CEST agents represent innovative frequency-encoding probes that yield negative contrast in the MR images upon transfer of saturated magnetization from the agent to the “bulk” water signal. Interesting developments have been attained that markedly increase the number and typology of systems with CEST properties. Currently much attention is also devoted to hyperpolarized molecules that display a sensitivity enhancement sufficient for their direct exploitation for the formation of the MR image. A real breakthrough is provided by the use of molecules (such as pyruvate) that report about the cellular metabolism, thanks to the maintenance of the hyperpolarization in the derived species.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Schroeter, Aileen","Rudin, Markus","Gianolio, Eliana","Viale, Alessandra","Delli Castelli, Daniela","Aime, Silvio","Hövener, Jan-Bernd","Bastiaansen, Jessica A.","Comment, Arnaud","Düwel, Stephan","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Becker, Markus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352808"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bruker Corporation","Lausanne University Hospital","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","Technical University of Munich","University of Freiburg","University of Turin"],"keyword":["13C","CEST","Dissolution DNP","Hyperpolarization","MRI","MRS","MRSI","Metabolism","Molecular imaging","Para hydrogen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mri","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105009171168","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352808","identifier":[{"id":"105009171168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a1a69c76-7bde-4701-9453-4155e6d16b14"],"keyword":["13C","CEST","Dissolution DNP","Hyperpolarization","MRI","MRS","MRSI","Metabolism","Molecular imaging","Para-hydrogen","Paramagnetic probes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1088AB95D4DB50A89DC353132FE728B8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of turin","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Turin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"lausanne university hospital","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lausanne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"6",