{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Sanchez, Juan Diego","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353354"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-27","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2017-04-22","title":"ISMRM 25th Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"practical aspects of preamplifier designs for 000000000013c imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132120310/Johansen_ISMRM17_LNA_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353354","ids":["dtu-a3834013-e65c-4711-b303-e4e2759e62e5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C168ACC5E91F98D1276EC4DE0738E7DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132120310/Johansen_ISMRM17_LNA_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan D.","key":"sánchezherediapau","last":"Sánchez-Heredia","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","name_org":"Sánchez-Heredia, Juan D.","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a3834013-e65c-4711-b303-e4e2759e62e5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Practical Aspects of Preamplifier Designs for 13C Imaging.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-353354","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To investigate the rod-cone and melanopsin pupillary light response (PLR) pathways in choroideremia. METHODS: Eight patients with choroideremia and 18 healthy age-matched controls underwent chromatic pupillometry by applying blue (463 nm) and red light (643 nm) at 100 lux intensity to the right eye while recording pupil diameters. Absolute baseline pupil size (mm), normalized maximal pupil constriction and the early and late postillumination pupillary dilation, from 0 to 10 seconds and 10 to 30 seconds after the end of illumination, respectively, were determined. Postillumination responses to blue light were considered to be primarily driven by melanopsin activation of the intrinsic photosensitive retinal ganglion cells. RESULTS: Baseline pupil diameters were comparable in patients with choroideremia and control subjects (p = 0.48). The maximum pupil constriction in patients with choroideremia was severely weakened in red light but only mildly weakened in blue light (p < 0.05). Postillumination dilation of the pupil was normal after red illumination but extremely protracted after blue illumination. Also, in contrast to healthy subjects, no abrupt change in the dilation curve was seen in the patients after the end of blue illumination, the early-phase dilation being completely abolished (p < 0.01). CONCLUSION: Rod-cone-driven pupil responses were decreased as expected in an outer retinal degeneration, and near-normal pupil constriction in blue light supports that the melanopsin system is normal. In contrast, the lack of brisk early-phase dilation after blue illumination in choroideremia is remarkable and may be interpreted to mean that the absence of photoreceptor inhibition promotes a tonic contraction of the pupil.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ba-Ali, Shakoor","Christensen, Søren Kirchhoff","Sander, Birgit","Rosenberg, Thomas","Larsen, Michael","Lund-Andersen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455691"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choroideremia melanopsin mediated postillumination pupil relaxation is abnormally slow","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-455691","identifier":[{"id":"28271634","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85014583976","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-68474342-bec2-4753-ac61-fbd87ee77199"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-45514F8197BCF64F204171C18C78E4FD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Shakoor","key":"baalipau","last":"Ba-Ali","name":"Ba-Ali, Shakoor","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Kirchhoff","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Søren Kirchhoff","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgit","key":"sanderpau","last":"Sander","name":"Sander, Birgit","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"rosenbergpau","last":"Rosenberg","locid":"ea62ddcf-1ea0-495c-b7b2-a0619184bba4","name":"Rosenberg, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28271634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.13394","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"809-814","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014583976"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-68474342-bec2-4753-ac61-fbd87ee77199"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Choroideremia : melanopsin-mediated postillumination pupil relaxation is abnormally slow","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455691","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We wished to evaluate whether inhibition of the systemic inflammatory response by a single pre-operative dose of methylprednisolone reduced markers of early endothelial damage after fast-track total knee arthroplasty. We randomly allocated 70 patients undergoing elective unilateral total knee arthroplasty (1:1) to receive either pre-operative intravenous methylprednisolone 125 mg (methylprednisolone group) or isotonic saline (control group). All procedures were performed under spinal anaesthesia without a tourniquet, using a standardised multimodal analgesic regime. The outcomes included changes in Syndecan-1 concentrations, a marker of glycocalyx degradation, markers of endothelial cell damage and activation (plasma soluble thrombomodulin and sE-Selectin), and permeability by vascular endothelial growth factor, as well as C-reactive protein concentrations. Blood samples were collected at baseline and 2 h, 6 h and 24 h after surgery, with complete sampling from 63 patients for analyses. Methylprednisolone significantly reduced markers of endothelial damage at 24 h following surgery compared with saline (methylprednisolone group vs. control group, adjusted means (SEM)) expressed by circulating Syndecan-1: 11.6 (1.0) ng.ml(-1) vs. 13.4 (1.1) ng.ml(-1) p = 0.046; soluble thrombomodulin: 5.1 (0.1) ng.ml(-1) vs. 5.7 (0.2) ng.ml(-1) , p = 0.009; sE-Selectin: 64.8 (1.8) ng.ml(-1) vs. 75.7 (1.9) ng.ml(-1) , p = 0.001, and vascular endothelial growth factor: 35.3 (2.7) ng.ml(-1) vs. 58.5 (2.8) ng.ml(-1) , p < 0.001. The effect of the intervention increased with time for soluble thrombomodulin, sE-Selectin and vascular endothelial growth factor, and was more pronounced in patients with high baseline values. Finally, methylprednisolone reduced the C-reactive protein response 24 h postoperatively; 31.1 (1.1) mg.l(-1) vs. 68.4 (1.1) mg.l(-1) , p < 0.001. Pre-operative administration of methylprednisolone 125 mg reduced circulating markers of endothelial activation and damage, as well as the systemic inflammatory response (C-reactive protein) early after fast-track total knee arthroplasty. These findings may have a positive effect on surgical outcome, but require studies in major surgery.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lindberg-Larsen, V","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Lindberg-Larsen, M","Rovsing, M L","Johansson, P I","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-509827"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of pre operative methylprednisolone on early endothelial damage after total knee arthroplasty a randomised double blind placebo controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-509827","identifier":[{"id":"85029087594","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28744857","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c2fd3e7c-e287-4710-987d-aa7f6f7f50c9"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FB44740543680228820E0AAFDF8D0333"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"V","key":"lindberglarsenvpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, V","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"S R","key":"ostrowskisisseryepau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","name_org":"Ostrowski, S R","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"lindberglarsenmpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, M","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M L","key":"rovsingmlpau","last":"Rovsing","name":"Rovsing, M L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"P I","key":"johanssonpipau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, P I","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H","key":"kehlethenrikpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","name_org":"Kehlet, H","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28744857"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/anae.13983","issn":["00032409","13652044"],"issn_org":["00032409"],"issue":"10","journal":"Anaesthesia","pages":"1217-1224","status":"p","title":"Anaesthesia","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029087594"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c2fd3e7c-e287-4710-987d-aa7f6f7f50c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effect of pre-operative methylprednisolone on early endothelial damage after total knee arthroplasty : a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509827","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We explored use of the suction-blister wound model in the assessment of not only epidermal regeneration but also pain, the microvascular response and bacteriology. The effects of topical zinc sulfate were studied to articulate the methodologies in this double-blind trial. One epidermal suction blister (10 mm) was induced on each buttock in 30 healthy volunteers (15 females:15 males) and deroofed on day 0. The wounds were randomized to daily treatment with 1.4% zinc sulfate shower gel (n = 20), placebo (n = 20) or control (n = 20). Digital photography coupled with planimetry, transepidermal water loss (TEWL) measurement and optical coherence tomography (OCT) was benchmarked to the gold standard of histology of 60 full-thickness wound biopsies on day 4. Pain increased after application of the shower gels. Microvessel density, determined from OCT images, increased from day 0 to day 2 in the three groups but increased more with the placebo than with the zinc shower gel (p = 0.003) or the control treatment (p = 0.002) and correlated (rS = 0.313, p = 0.015) with the inflammatory response on day 4, as determined by histology. Coagulase-negative staphylococci were more common in wounds compared with skin (p = 0.002) and was reduced (p = 0.030) with zinc sulfate treatment. Planimetric analysis of digital wound images was not biased (p = 0.234) compared with histology, and TEWL measurements showed no correlation (rS = 0.052, p = 0.691) with epithelialization. Neoepidermal formation, determined by histology, did not differ (p = 0.290) among the groups. Zinc sulfate reduced (p = 0.031) the release of lactate dehydrogenase from cultured gel-treated keratinocytes isolated from the blister roofs. Therefore, combination of the standardized suction-blister wound model with noninvasive planimetry and OCT is a useful tool for assessing wound therapies. Zinc sulfate transiently dampened inflammation and reduced bacterial growth.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Larsen, Heidi F.","Ahlström, Malin G.","Gjerdrum, Lise Mette Rahbek","Mogensen, Mette","Ghathian, Khaled","Calum, Henrik","Sørensen, Anne Lyngholm","Forman, Julie Lyng","Vandeven, Mark","Holerca, Marian N.","Du-Thumm, Laurence","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Ågren, Magnus S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-525259"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Colgate-Palmolive Company"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"noninvasive measurement of reepithelialization and microvascularity of suction blister wounds with benchmarking to histology","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-525259","identifier":[{"id":"85042064156","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29316016","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-dca85d9d-40e0-453c-8470-899db6ead6a4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35E328BFF51E20AA28C8D36519D29179"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"colgate palmolive company","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Colgate-Palmolive Company","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Heidi F.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Heidi F.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malin G.","key":"ahlströmpau","last":"Ahlström","name":"Ahlström, Malin G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise M.R.","key":"gjerdrumpau","last":"Gjerdrum","locid":"0b70cdd9-e7b4-4414-a024-51b77a203fe5","name":"Gjerdrum, Lise Mette Rahbek","name_org":"Gjerdrum, Lise M.R.","orcid":"0000-0003-4377-3209","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mette","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"4a53b078-2e8d-47c4-a208-d8c0a2aa52c8","name":"Mogensen, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Khaled","key":"ghathianpau","last":"Ghathian","name":"Ghathian, Khaled","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"calumpau","last":"Calum","locid":"e69419e2-1d65-4410-a35a-2d219c621576","name":"Calum, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne L.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c72b99a4-378e-4646-9dcf-2d719872c079","name":"Sørensen, Anne Lyngholm","name_org":"Sørensen, Anne L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julie L.","key":"formanpau","last":"Forman","locid":"ddfe2814-4ae0-463d-9748-c1ba0647b469","name":"Forman, Julie Lyng","name_org":"Forman, Julie L.","orcid":"0000-0001-7368-0869","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mark","key":"vandevenpau","last":"Vandeven","name":"Vandeven, Mark","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Marian N.","key":"holercapau","last":"Ho