{"abstract":"In this study we demonstrate how reconstruction for IDEAL spiral CSI (spectroscopic imaging scheme developed for hyperpolarized dynamic metabolic MR imaging) can be improved by using regularization with a sparsity constraint. By exploiting sparsity of the spectral domain, IDEAL spiral CSI can achieve chemical shift encoding by acquisition of only few time-shifted echoes. The minimum number of echoes required to avoid noise amplification can be decreased by means of regularization enforcing spectral sparsity, hereby reducing scan time. Improvements achieved by using regularized reconstruction are demonstrated for in vivo data from a hyperpolarized cardiac study of a pig.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Rie Beck","Mariager, Christian Østergaard","Laustsen, Christoffer","F. Schulte, Rolf","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Hanson, Lars G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-140006"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-27","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2017-04-22","title":"ISMRM 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved reconstruction for ideal spiral csi","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-140006","ids":["au-12732abe-1120-48ac-8ab7-5ee3ff9d32cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3339CC33554C14F34682DC0730D353AC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark (DTU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ge healthcare","name":"GE Healthcare","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rie Beck","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"mariagerpau","last":"Mariager","locid":"e647818e-e048-4b35-9ec6-7f5443b9fe72","name":"Mariager, Christian Østergaard","name_org":"Mariager, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf","key":"fschultepau","last":"F. Schulte","name":"F. Schulte, Rolf","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars G.","key":"hansonpau","last":"Hanson","name":"Hanson, Lars G.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"ISMRM 2017 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-12732abe-1120-48ac-8ab7-5ee3ff9d32cb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Improved reconstruction for IDEAL spiral CSI","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-140006","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background. Genetic risk scores (GRSs) may predict cardiovascular risk in community-based populations. However, studies investigating the association with recurrent cardiovascular events in patients with established coronary artery disease (CAD) are conflicting. Methods. We genotyped 879 patients with high-risk stable CAD and created a GRS based on 45 single nucleotide polymorphisms previously reported to be associated with CAD in genome-wide association studies. Patients were categorised into high or low GRS according to the median GRS and followed for recurrent cardiovascular events using national Danish registries. The primary endpoint was a composite of myocardial infarction, coronary revascularisation, and cardiovascular death. Results. Median (interquartile range) follow-up time was 2.8 (2.4–3.8) years. The cumulative incidence proportions of the primary endpoint at 1 and 3 years were 6.4% and 11.5% in high-GRS patients vs. 2.5% and 7.3% in low-GRS patients. The corresponding relative risks were 2.56 (95% confidence interval (CI) 1.29-5.07), and 1.57 (95% CI 1.02-2.44). The adjusted hazard ratio (HR) of the primary endpoint was 1.50 (95% CI 1.00–2.25). The most pronounced effect of a high GRS was observed on coronary revascularisations (adjusted HR 2.10 [95% CI 1.08–4.07]). Risks of cardiovascular death (adjusted HR 1.07 [95% CI 0.46–2.48]) and all-cause death (adjusted HR 1.15 [95% CI 0.65–2.03]) were unaffected. Conclusions. A GRS predicts recurrent cardiovascular events in high-risk stable CAD patients. The observed effect was mainly driven by coronary revascularisations.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christiansen, Morten Krogh","Nyegaard, Mette","Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Würtz, Morten","Neergaard-Petersen, Søs","Hvas, Anne-Mette","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Kristensen, Steen Dalby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-149431"],"event":{"end":"2017-03-19","place":"Washington, us","start":"2017-03-17","title":"American College of Cardiology","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coronary artery disease","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genetics","Myocardial Infarction","Risk score"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a genetic risk score predicts cardiovascular events in patients with stable coronary artery disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-149431","identifier":[{"id":"85018738881","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-230217bf-03e5-4d9b-beb4-cff36a6cdc1c"],"keyword":["Coronary artery disease","Genetic predisposition to disease","Genetics","Myocardial infarction","Risk score"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0B952A0556E1470E361A3B1078C5717B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Krogh","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"bf2444c5-3e70-45d3-b035-850325ff2f6e","name":"Christiansen, Morten Krogh","orcid":"0000-0002-3894-888X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardpau","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"a34df7ff-0fb5-44b0-8255-6dc2c9b962f3","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Bøjet","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"15c7c979-5236-47ec-b