{"abstract":"The aim of the study was to characterize the different types of muscle hemorrhages in the ham and tenderloin of CO2-stunned slaughter pigs. The distinct types of hemorrhages were characterized according to their distribution and size. The hemorrhages in the ham were multiple, pinpoint hemorrhages predominantly distributed in the caudal part of the muscle. The hemorrhages in the tenderloin were single and circular, located either at the tip or the head. Histologically, three distinct types of hemorrhages were observed. Type 1, which was peracute (< 4 h old), and present in both the ham and the tenderloin. Type 2, which was acute (> 4 h old), and restricted to the ham. Type 3 contained bone marrow and cartilage, was peracute (< 4 h old) and restricted to the tenderloin.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dich-Jørgensen, Kristine","Larsen, Helle Daugaard","Leifsson, Páll S.","Jensen, Henrik Elvang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-474594"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of hemorrhages in the ham topsides and tenderloins of slaughter pigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-474594","identifier":[{"id":"84994291799","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27816853","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-87ade141-8c3e-4a48-a54a-1c2beba7d455"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DD05A6228678589F3659CE6B1B0E70D1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Meat Research Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristine","key":"dichjørgensenpau","last":"Dich-Jørgensen","locid":"511e2cfe-da81-4a6e-a088-50c88e784613","name":"Dich-Jørgensen, Kristine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle Daugaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Helle Daugaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Páll S.","key":"leifssonpau","last":"Leifsson","locid":"691042d9-84a7-4df4-8005-8e60cfb7dc4e","name":"Leifsson, Páll S.","orcid":"0000-0003-1539-9491","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27816853"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.meatsci.2016.10.016","issn":["03091740","18734138"],"issn_org":["03091740"],"journal":"Meat Science","pages":"34-38","status":"p","title":"Meat Science","volume":"124"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994291799"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-87ade141-8c3e-4a48-a54a-1c2beba7d455"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterization of hemorrhages in the ham topsides and tenderloins of slaughter pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-474594","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Clinicians and researchers are becoming increasingly aware of the difficult decision that they are likely to be making within the next years; deciding between the use of two rather different descriptions of the posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) diagnosis. The Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders 5th edition (DSM-5), which describes PTSD as a diagnosis comprised of 20 symptoms belonging to four symptom clusters, and the World Health Organization’s proposed 11th revision of the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-11) set for release in 2018 in which PTSD is comprised by only 6-7 symptoms belonging to three symptom clusters. Numerous studies have supported the latent structure of PTSD according to different models of the DSM-5 and the ICD-11 proposal. The few studies investigating the ICD-11 and the DSM-5 in the same populations appear to suggest that the ICD-11 model may result in better fit than the DSM-5 based models. At the same time, there is also a tendency for ICD-11 to produce lower estimated PTSD prevalence rates than the DSM-5 criteria, which may ultimately affect who is offered treatment. Of note, it is important to stress that there is a lack of studies investigating the latent structure of the ICD-11 and DSM-5 models in the same populations using appreciate measurements of both the ICD-11 and the DSM-5 PTSD. At the same time, it is important to investigate this in different trauma populations as previous research suggest that differences in prevalence rates may only exist following specific types of traumatic exposure. The aim of the present study was to investigate the latent structure of different ICD-11 and DSM-5 models of PTSD in three different trauma populations and compare the estimated diagnostic rates of PTSD based on the DSM-5 and the ICD-11, respectively.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hansen, Maj","Hyland, Philip","Karstoft, Karen-Inge","Bramsen, Rikke Holm","Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","Armour, Cherie","Sternhagen, Anni","Andersen, S. B.","Larsen, Simone","Hørbye, Mette","Andersen, Tonny Elmose"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-589196"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-03","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2017-06-01","title":"15th Conference of European Society for Traumatic Stress","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Ireland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National College of Ireland","Ulster University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VETC"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VETC","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does size really matter a multisite study of competing diagnostic criteria","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134192930/Does_size_really_matter_ESTSS2017.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-589196","ids":["sdu-37f07cdc-8ebb-48c8-aac4-029a7af8b1c0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6E30A494CF0222378BD0F11CDE4ADED9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134192930/Does_size_really_matter_ESTSS2017.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychol