{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The aim of this study was to evaluate the clinical outcome of patients with severe bacterial meningitis where intracranial pressure (ICP) monitoring has been performed. METHODS: A retrospective observational study including patients admitted 1st. January 2005 to 31st. December 2014. Thirty nine patients age 18-89 years were included. All the patients received intensive care with mechanical ventilation, ICP monitoring, sedation, antibiotics and corticosteroids according to current guidelines. Clinical outcome was defined as death during hospitalization or survival at hospital discharge. RESULTS: The most common pathogen was Streptococcus pneumoniae (26; 67%). Thirteen patients died (33%) and neurologic impairment was noted in twenty two (84.6%) surviving patients. In S. pneumoniae cases patients with adverse outcome were significantly older (p = 0.0024) and immunosuppressed (p = 0.034). Lower mean-cerebral perfusion pressure (CPP) was found to correlate with adverse outcome (p = 0.005). Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) was drained in fourteen patients. Increased ICP (>20 mmHg) was observed in twenty four patients. No significant correlation was found between measured ICP and head CT scans with signs of elevated ICP. CONCLUSIONS: Patients with severe meningitis should be admitted to intensive care units and evaluated for ICP monitoring regardless of head CT findings.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Lykke","Poulsen, Frantz R","Nielsen, Troels H","Nordström, Carl-Henrik","Schulz, Mette K","Andersen, Åse Bengård"],"cuid":["S02-094.92-041708"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Drug Monitoring methods","Female","Head diagnostic imaging","Humans","Intracranial pressure","Male","Meningitis Bacterial drug therapy","Middle Aged","Retrospective Studies","Survival Analysis","Tomography X Ray Computed methods","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of intracranial pressure monitoring in bacterial meningitis a 000000000010 year follow up on outcome and intracranial pressure versus head ct scans","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85008235324","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.92-041708","identifier":[{"id":"28049382","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85008235324","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3d9a0f0e-affb-46f0-9a3d-b00d68a7ebee","sdu-9ce02fc2-e1f3-4fdd-87c1-5f6dd3f369d0"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Drug Monitoring/methods","Female","Head/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Intracranial Pressure","Male","Meningitis, Bacterial/drug therapy","Middle Aged","Retrospective Studies","Survival Analysis","Tomography, X-Ray Computed/methods","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A9AE5729861BBD573B1436F504369954"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lykke","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f4fd0451-0508-4d78-8726-1e63c7620925","name":"Larsen, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0002-4113-4182","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frantz","key":"rompoulsenpau","last":"Rom Poulsen","locid":"b50645f6-f0c4-4356-9f63-d44290b0dfd9","name":"Poulsen, Frantz Rom","name_org":"Rom Poulsen, Frantz","orcid":"0000-0001-5715-6901","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frantz R","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Frantz R","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"18f40b9c-d8d6-4d6b-b3af-374f6221676a","name":"Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","name_org":"Nielsen, Troels H","orcid":"0000-0002-3943-8128","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl-Henrik","key":"nordströmpau","last":"Nordström","locid":"832530b4-9bf3-4eb3-bbda-ad9fad3cae33","name":"Nordström, Carl-Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette K","key":"schulzpau","last":"Schulz","locid":"7b7927f3-4205-4c14-81d7-cda980a06d20","name":"Schulz, Mette Katrine","name_org":"Schulz, Mette K","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"Åse B","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","l