{"abstract":"Der anes en tilbøjelighed til, at talentudvikling tænker i eksklusive udviklingsforløb for en elite af vandkæmmede, frembrusende og velklædte videnmedarbejdere med en direktør i maven...","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-298441"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ups talentudvikling forsvandt derfor skal det tilbage","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","text":"Undefined","type":"url","url":"http://www.denoffentlige.dk/ups-talentudvikling-forsvandt-derfor-skal-det-tilbage","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-298441","ids":["cbs-f19fcf2a-33ce-4192-b244-8724c14fcddc"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A5465ED62F27AA8CA7D52EB22632743"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-f19fcf2a-33ce-4192-b244-8724c14fcddc"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Ups, talentudvikling forsvandt, derfor skal det tilbage","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-298441","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The recent introduction of Internet connected hearing instruments offers a paradigm shift in hearing instrument fitting. Potentially this makes it possible for devices to adapt their settings to a changing context, inferred from user interactions. In a pilot study we enabled hearing instrument users to remotely enhance auditory focus and attenuate background noise to improve speech intelligibility. N=5, participants changed program settings and adjusted volume on their hearing instruments using their smartphones. We found that individual behavioral patterns affected the usage of the devices. A significant difference between program usage, and weekdays versus weekends, were found. Users not only changed programs to modify aspects of directionality and noise reduction, but also continuously adjusted the volume. Rethinking hearing instruments as devices that adaptively learn behavioral patterns based on user interaction, might provide a degree of personalization that has not been feasible due to lack of audiological resources.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Johansen, Benjamin","Petersen, Michael Kai","Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik","Sandholm, Per","Larsen, Jakob Eg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319080"],"event":{"end":"2017-05-11","place":"Denver, us","start":"2017-05-06","title":"ACM CHI 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aging","Augmented audio","Health","Hearing impairment","User behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rethinking hearing aid fitting by learning from behavioral patterns","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85019619285","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319080","identifier":[{"id":"85019619285","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-30be38d1-58bb-46ab-a159-44588dc85573"],"keyword":["Aging","Augmented audio","Health","Hearing impairment","User behavior"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-01B962DAB4CEC207752FA14BA32EE7DB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"oticon","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTI","l3nl":"Oticon A/S","l3nn":"Oticon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oticon","namevar":["Eriksholm Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benjamin","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"3c721ddf-2426-4b69-ac27-00a5847c25fd","name":"Johansen, Benjamin","orcid":"0000-0002-6516-4757","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Kai","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Michael Kai","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"pontoppidanpau","last":"Pontoppidan","name":"Pontoppidan, Niels Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"sandholmpau","last":"Sandholm","name":"Sandholm, Per","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Eg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"691c8ae7-9a21-4b98-9b91-5e2d9806a4b9","name":"Larsen, Jakob Eg","orcid":"0000-0002-7461-9901","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3027063.3053156","isbn":["9781450346566"],"pages":"1733-1739","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI’17 Extended Abstracts"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019619285"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Oticon A/S","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-30be38d1-58bb-46ab-a159-44588dc85573"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Rethinking Hearing Aid Fitting by Learning From Behavioral Patterns","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319080","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"During migration, animals are typically limited by their endogenous energetic resources which must be allocated to the physiological costs associated with locomotion, as well as avoiding and/or compensating for oxidative stress. To date, there have been few attempts to understand the role of oxidative status in migration biology, particularly in fish. Semi-anadromous brown trout (Salmo trutta, Linnaeus 1758) exhibit partial migration, where some individuals smoltify and migrate to sea, and others become stream residents, providing us with an excellent model to investigate the link between oxidative stress and migration. Using the brown trout, we obtained blood samples from juveniles from a coastal stream in Denmark in the fall prior to peak seaward migration which occurs in the spring, and assayed for antioxidant capacity (oxygen radical absorbance capacity) and oxidative stress levels (ratio of oxidized to reduced glutathione). We found that individuals that migrated had higher antioxidant capacity than residents and that future migration date was negatively correlated with both antioxidant capacity and body length in the fall. This study provides the first evidence that oxidative status is associated with migration strategy and timing, months in advance of the actual migration, and provides insight into the role of oxidative status in animal migration","author_count":7,"contributors":["Birnie-Gauvin, Kim","Peiman, K. S.","Larsen, Martin Hage","Baktoft, Henrik","Aarestrup, Kim","Willmore, W. G","Cooke, S. J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-345804"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oxidative stress and partial migration in brown trout salmo trutta","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1139/cjz-2016-0312","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-345804","identifier":[{"id":"85033474897","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8a4f5547-38f2-4cb5-b2b4-15553cfd7cf8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DA926AC8005F177F8445F7C3180B31A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1139/cjz-2016-0312","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nrcresearchpress.com.proxy.findit.dtu.dk/doi/abs/10.1139/cjz-2016-0312#.WdtKCTtx270","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134656396/cjz_2016_0312.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Freshwater Fisheries Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"birniegauvinpau","last":"Birnie-Gauvin","locid":"d54ccfbf-3d3c-463d-8dd0-e2481ba6f572","name":"Birnie-Gauvin, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-9242-0560","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"K. S.","key":"peimanpau","last":"Peiman","name":"Peiman, K. S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Hage","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"df4c70da-87a0-45c4-883d-9f9d64e2ffd6","name":"Larsen, Martin Hage","orcid":"0000-0001-9521-835X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"baktoftpau","last":"Baktoft","locid":"642a7cea-4ecc-4866-97f3-0d86f3e47ec0","name":"Baktoft, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3644-4960","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"aarestruppau","last":"Aarestrup","locid":"60987b6f-7027-4bd5-91bc-d2f10390aa63","name":"Aarestrup, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-8521-6270","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"W. G","key":"willmorepau","last":"Willmore","name":"Willmore, W. G","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"S. J.","key":"cookepau","last":"Cooke","name":"Cooke, S. J.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1139/cjz-2016-0312","issn":["00084301","14803283"],"issn_org":["00084301"],"issue":"11","journal":"Canadian Journal of Zoology","pages":"829-835","publisher":"National Research Council of Canada","status":"p","title":"Canadian Journal of Zoology","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85033474897"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8a4f5547-38f2-4cb5-b2b4-15553cfd7cf8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Oxidative stress and partial migration in brown trout (Salmo trutta)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-345804","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Renewable off-grid solutions are steadily growing in both developed and developing countries (R. Kempener et al. 2015). With the decreasing cost and improving performance of small hydro installations, solar power, wind power, and energy storage systems, renewable energy is expected to supplement or replace existing diesel grids on islands and in remote areas.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wu, Qiuwei","Larsen, Esben","Heussen, Kai","Bindner, Henrik W.","Douglass, Philip James"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350158"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Energy Association"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"remote off grid solutions for greenland and denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85020709925","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350158","identifier":[{"id":"85020709925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-98e98e0f-2de0-4810-9a66-0bd207b8be54"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EAC53B7A62D7FBCB77ECB744781450ED"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy, Electric Power Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Energy Association"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qiuwei","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","locid":"271c52b0-febb-4f56-8609-f2cb7b98a801","name":"Wu, Qiuwei","orcid":"0000-0001-7935-2567","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"aa50e83a-93d1-42b1-bd27-feb6ffda7bb9","name":"Larsen, Esben","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kai","key":"heussenpau","last":"Heussen","locid":"7f2cc299-c594-4ade-a884-145d0a1c82e7","name":"Heussen, Kai","orcid":"0000-0003-3623-1372","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik W.","key":"bindnerpau","last":"Bindner","locid":"bcf34e58-6582-4f94-8934-4fc76cf4ec3e","name":"Bindner, Henrik W.","orcid":"0000-0003-1545-6994","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip James","key":"douglasspau","last":"Douglass","name":"Douglass, Philip James","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mele.2017.2685959","issn":["23255889"],"issn_org":["23255987"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Electrification Magazine","pages":"64-73","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Electrification Magazine","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020709925"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-98e98e0f-2de0-4810-9a66-0bd207b8be54"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Remote Off-Grid Solutions for Greenland and Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350158","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this study, we describe a method to obtain improved preamplifier decoupling for receive-only coils. The method relies on the better decoupling obtained when coils are matched to an impedance higher than 50 . Preamplifiers with inductive imaginary impedance and low real impedance, increase the effectiveness of the decoupling. A 2-channel 13C array of 50 mm loop coils show an increase of Q-factor of the coils from 247 to 365. The measured SNR, using two small phantoms, demonstrated a similar improvement.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sanchez, Juan Diego","Johansen, Daniel Højrup","Hansen, Rie Beck","Hansen, Esben S.","Laustsen, Christoffer","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-354584"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-27","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2017-04-22","title":"ISMRM 25th Annual Meeting &amp; Exhibition","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved decoupling for 000000000013c coil arrays using non conventional matching and preamplifier impedance","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132537146/Sanchez_ISMRM_2017_Abstract_v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-354584","ids":["dtu-a79bc54d-24fa-463d-8c1a-46c0bc131840"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ED4BEB25E16B5CF75CB7D56D7D77EBD3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132537146/Sanchez_ISMRM_2017_Abstract_v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Diego","key":"sanchezjuandiegopau","last":"Sanchez","locid":"2d24121b-877e-4bfe-a434-9c7c3e7a34e0","name":"Sanchez, Juan Diego","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Højrup","key":"johansendanielhøjruppau","last":"Johansen","locid":"114285a3-128f-493e-b93a-e30c40bb6e96","name":"Johansen, Daniel Højrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8302-7182","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rie Beck","key":"hansenriebeckpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8214cd7c-cdb4-4678-b17b-bbd3f5d87ece","name":"Hansen, Rie Beck","orcid":"0000-0003-1718-8196","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben S.","key":"hansenesbenspau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Esben S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenchristofferpau","last":"Laustsen","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkovitaliypau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenjanhenrikpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a79bc54d-24fa-463d-8c1a-46c0bc131840"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved Decoupling for 13C coil Arrays Using Non-Conventional Matching and Preamplifier Impedance","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-354584","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"On Nov. 7th 1940 the newly constructed Tacoma Narrows Bridge collapsed due to excessive torsional oscillations caused by the formation and shedding of large coherent vortices. The subsequent wind tunnel tests conducted on both section- and full bridge models concluded that the bridge should have collapsed at a wind speed corresponding to approximately half of the wind speed at the day of the collapse. This discrepancy questions our understanding of the phenomena responsible for the failure of the bridge. The present study aims at clarifying this \"mystery\" by considering historical records made available by the US coast guards, and by performing wind tunnel tests and detailed numerical ow simulations.Our findings indicate that the discrepancy is caused by an until now unnoticed yawed wind direction relative to the bridge, which was present at the day of the collapse.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Walther, Jens Honore","Christensen, D. S.","Malthe, M. G.","Roenne, M.","Spietz, Henrik Juul","Larsen, A.","Larsen, S. V."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356946"],"event":{"end":"2017-11-21","place":"Denver, us","start":"2017-11-19","title":"70th Annual Meeting of the American Physical Society Division of Fluid Dynamics (DFD17)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-FORC"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-FORC","DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the collapse of tacoma narrows bridge a piece to the puzzle","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139802722/266213.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356946","ids":["dtu-af5b3366-fcb9-48a9-bf07-cf182ba411c3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-231F2B1C7EF0DC7E002C00F70A586A50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139802722/266213.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"force technology","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-FORC","l3nn":"FORCE Technology","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"FORCE Technology","namevar":["FORCE Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-FORC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Honore","key":"waltherjenshonorepau","last":"Walther","locid":"9895a63e-6fff-429b-8188-9bcd7f6cac8d","name":"Walther, Jens Honore","orcid":"0000-0001-8100-9178","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"D. S.","key":"christensendspau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, D. S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. G.","key":"malthemgpau","last":"Malthe","name":"Malthe, M. G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"roennempau","last":"Roenne","name":"Roenne, M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Juul","key":"spietzhenrikjuulpau","last":"Spietz","locid":"77b022ad-b7ab-4646-bbc5-d5ca038655ce","name":"Spietz, Henrik Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-7775-0975","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"larsenapau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, A.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"S. V.","key":"larsensvpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, S. V.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-af5b3366-fcb9-48a9-bf07-cf182ba411c3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The collapse of Tacoma Narrows Bridge: a piece to the puzzle","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356946","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Results of a test campaign for a floating wind turbine in simultaneous wind and wave forcing at scale 1:60 are presented. The floater is the Triple Spar floater, a hybrid between a spar buoy and a semi submersible tri-floater, tested here for the first time. The turbine is a model scale version of the DTU 10 MW reference wind turbine, which, also for the first time, is tested with active blade pitch control. The tests focus on the effects of aerodynamic damping and interaction effects between the wind forcing, wave forcing and the blade pitch control algorithm. Special focus is devoted to the instability of the platform pitch natural mode, that can occur if a standard land-based controller is applied.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Bredmose, Henrik","Lemmer, F.","Borg, Michael","Pegalajar-Jurado, Antonio","Mikkelsen, Robert Flemming","Larsen, T. Stoklund","Fjelstrup, T.","Yu, Wenye","Lomholt, Anders Kjær","Boehm, L.","Armendariz, J. Azcona"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357455"],"event":{"end":"2017-01-20","place":"Trondheim, no","start":"2017-01-18","title":"14th Deep Sea Offshore Wind R&amp;D Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Renewable Energy Center","University of Stuttgart"],"keyword":["Control","Experimental analysis","Floating wind turbines","Numerical modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the triple spar campaign model tests of a 000000000010mw floating wind turbine with waves wind and pitch control","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.or