y of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a7a92f48-3890-4b7c-baa6-3f37f76d5611"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spatial separation of the cyanogenic β-glucosidase ZfBGD2 and cyanogenic glucosides in the haemolymph of <i>Zygaena</i> larvae facilitates cyanide release","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493568","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Optic disc drusen (ODD) is hyaline deposits in the optic nerve head seen in 1-2% of the population. Long-term evolution of ODD anatomy and visual field defects in ODD patients is a key factor for learning more about pathophysiology and prognosis of the condition. With a median follow-up period of 56 years, this is the first study that evaluates superficial optic disc anatomy and visual fields in patients with ODD over a life span. Methods: Observational case series investigating progression of superficial optic disc anatomy and visual fields in ODD patients. Eight patients with hereditary ODD were included. Results: Mean age at initial and follow-up examination was, respectively, 16.8 and 73.3 years. The median follow-up time was 56 years. A minimal or non-existing change in superficial ODD anatomy (size and number) was seen in 10 of 12 eyes. There was a tendency towards more anatomical change in subjects younger at first examination. A 27% decrease in Goldmann perimetric visual field area (cm2) was found between initial and follow-up examinations. Conclusion: Minimal or no change in superficial optic disc anatomy and visual fields in ODD patients oldest at the initial examination suggests that anatomical progression of ODD in patients with hereditary ODD happens primarily before adulthood.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lasse Malmqvist","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Hamann, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-498409"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Long term follow up","Optic disc drusen","Optic nerve head drusen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term evolution of superficial optic disc drusen","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-498409","identifier":[{"id":"85007092509","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27996202","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-afc474c2-b1d1-4c11-a57a-39d9a027999e"],"keyword":["Long-term follow-up","Optic disc anatomy","Optic disc drusen","Optic disc drusen evolution","Optic disc drusen progression","Optic nerve head drusen","Progression in visual fields"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1CABA0899D6736DCD0281E67C11AADC4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lasse Malmqvist","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Lasse Malmqvist","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","locid":"4e7d48fd-1aa8-4703-94ec-8ae85794b7d7","name":"Hamann, Steffen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27996202"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.13315","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"352-356","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85007092509"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-afc474c2-b1d1-4c11-a57a-39d9a027999e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term evolution of superficial optic disc drusen","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-498409","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Ethylene sensitivity has for long been of interest in improving ornamental plants e.g., Kalanchöe and Campanula. We aim to investigate changes in ethylene sensitivity in economically important ornamental plants by targeting genes in the ethylene pathway using the novel precise genome editing tool; the Clustered Regularly Interspaced Palindromic Repeats (CRISPR) RNA guided Cas9 DNA nuclease (CRISPR/Cas9). CRISPR/Cas9 may be employed to introduce targeted double-stranded breaks (DSBs) at desired sites in the host genome. The DSBs will be repaired by the non-homologous end-joining (NHEJ) repair mechanism which often results in small indels and consequently gene knockout. The CRISPR/Cas9 system consists of a protein DNA nuclease (Cas9) which is guided to the target sequence by a small RNA molecule (sgRNA) that recognizes a 20 bp target sequence in the genome situated immediately downstream of a 3 bp protospacer adjacent motif (PAM). The sgRNA confers the sequence specificity of the CRISPR/Cas9 complex and may thus be designed to target virtually any sequence, a feature that has made it the method of choice within precise genetic engineering. Although most research with CRISPR/Cas9 has been conducted in prokaryote and mammalian cells, steps have been taken to implement the system in plants. Proof of function has been obtained in various plant species e.g., Arabidopsis, wheat, soybean and orange which makes it plausible that this technique could be applied to ornamental plants as well. The CRISPR/Cas9 system will be delivered using Agrobacterium tumefaciens and explant regeneration of tissue cultures to create stable transformation and mutation events.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kemp, Oliver","Favero, Bruno Trevenzoli","Hegelund, Josefine Nymark","Möller, Svenning Rune","Müller, Renate","Petersen, Bent Larsen","Lütken, Henrik Vlk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501994"],"event":{"end":"2016-03-09","place":"Krabi, th","start":"2016-03-07","title":"International Symposium on Tropical and Subtropical Ornamentals","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modification of ethylene sensitivity in ornamental plants using crispr cas000000000009","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-501994","identifier":[{"id":"85028937606","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b5c3825d-0cbd-4b21-af18-c0facc2c50e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D59ADB326F814270E0D0A0177B70FD9D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Oliver","key":"kemppau","last":"Kemp","name":"Kemp, Oliver","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bruno Trevenzoli","key":"faveropau","last":"Favero","locid":"3ed17e9b-b493-40ef-8bac-cb81c5e7308d","name":"Favero, Bruno Trevenzoli","orcid":"0000-0002-7285-0093","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josefine Nymark","key":"hegelundpau","last":"Hegelund","locid":"a934e5ed-d713-4bc1-8df5-0f4b560bd546","name":"Hegelund, Josefine Nymark","orcid":"0000-0002-5663-9503","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svenning Rune","key":"möllerpau","last":"Möller","locid":"af361420-94a8-4051-8166-7a9104f7db76","name":"Möller, Svenning Rune","orcid":"0000-0003-0392-4631","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Renate","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","locid":"cbb540fa-1b78-4ded-8d1e-f00b5c01699f","name":"Müller, Renate","orcid":"0000-0003-4029-240X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bent L.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0d3fa717-88a9-444e-8096-3163ca10ec75","name":"Petersen, Bent Larsen","name_org":"Petersen, Bent L.","orcid":"0000-0002-2004-9077","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Vlk","key":"lütkenpau","last":"Lütken","locid":"b1b4cd74-3a89-4435-9905-54961540c79c","name":"Lütken, Henrik Vlk","orcid":"0000-0003-3719-8324","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17660/actahortic.2017.1167.40","issn":["05677572"],"pages":"271-280","publisher":"International Society for Horticultural Science (ISHS)","series":"Acta Horticulturae","status":"p","title":"I International Symposium on Tropical and Subtropical Ornamentals"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028937606"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b5c3825d-0cbd-4b21-af18-c0facc2c50e1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modification of ethylene sensitivity in ornamental plants using CRISPR/Cas9","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-501994","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This book argues that theories of European foreign policy are performative: they create the objects they analyse. In this text, Larsen outlines the performativity approach to the role of theories based on the work of Derrida and goes on to examine the performative role of Christopher Hill's concept of Capability-Expectations Gap in the study of European foreign policy. Through examples from relevant literature, Larsen not only demonstrates how this concept sets up standards for the EU as a foreign policy actor (that are not met by most other international actors) but also shows how this curtails analysis of EU foreign policy. The author goes on to discuss how the widespread use of the concept of ‘gap' affects the way in which EU foreign policy has been studied; and that it always produces the same result: the EU is an unfulfilled actor outside the realm of “normal” actors in IR. This volume offers new perspectives on European foreign policy research and advice and serves as an invaluable resource for students of EU foreign policy and, more broadly, European Studies.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-536782"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gaps in eu foreign policy the role of concepts in european studies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.palgrave.com/us/book/9781349951659","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-536782","ids":["ku-f035e492-f5c3-4ce6-a722-69b24ca35342"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-365969A7DC19F1CB9165CA05311E70DE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1057/978-1-349-95166-6_1","eisbn":["9781349951666"],"isbn":["9781349951659"],"pages":"98","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034023575"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f035e492-f5c3-4ce6-a722-69b24ca35342"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gaps in EU Foreign Policy : The Role of Concepts in European Studies","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-536782","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
