{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Morten","Larsen, Christian Albrekt","Lolle, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-061327"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"education and trust exploring the association across social relationships and nations","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0001699316658936","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-061327","identifier":[{"id":"84991785871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-26ddc66f-0699-4c53-a369-2dee941d23ab"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC9C1C11375E111AB4DD08737A23CCE4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0001699316658936","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work, SOSA - Social Work in the field of psychiatry and disability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"4762404b-10bc-4f26-bd0b-7a3166720c25","name":"Frederiksen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-2635-3827","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Albrekt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"24fccad8-9acd-45be-b305-891125b6933e","name":"Larsen, Christian Albrekt","orcid":"0000-0002-3309-3018","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"lollepau","last":"Lolle","locid":"2a35f517-3687-4d09-9e23-9d46a2747581","name":"Lolle, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3039-0201","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0001699316658936","issn":["00016993","15023869"],"issn_org":["00016993"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Sociologica","pages":"293-308","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Acta Sociologica","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991785871"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-26ddc66f-0699-4c53-a369-2dee941d23ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Education and Trust : Exploring the Association across Social Relationships and Nations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061327","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper will introduce and discuss a new model for understanding the relation between narrative and games, by looking at the narrative quality of game mechanics. First, a review of the terms ”Narrative” and ”Game Mechanics” is made, and defined in this context, before a literature review, based on both narratological and ludological sources. From this, the model is presented and described, which encompasses the previous research as well as defining a clear relation between mechanics, context, story, and narrative of games. This model is intended for both design and analysis of games, and has been created to cover a lack of definition of how mechanics create narrative through their own definitions and their relation to the context and storytelling of the game. This model, still in an infant stage, shows potential, but still requires rigorous testing in several areas.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","Schoenau-Fog, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107374"],"event":{"acronym":"ICIDS","end":"2016-11-19","place":"Los Angeles, us","start":"2016-11-15","title":"International Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Game Mechanics","Interactive Storytelling","Narrative","Story"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the narrative quality of game mechanics","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://icids2016.ict.usc.edu/program/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-107374","identifier":[{"id":"84996866912","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c58c4e00-92ce-41f8-bb38-e10859cc47b4"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Brave New Ideas","Game Mechanics","Interactive Storytelling","Narrative","Narrative Quality","Story"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-247D0B39B55AF1DCDCE143EF1E8A9E2F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarke Alexander","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b20b35fc-c929-4058-a942-903b3772a4b1","name":"Larsen, Bjarke Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schoenaufogpau","last":"Schoenau-Fog","locid":"34a35708-1cbb-4d3b-9b7c-53080126b5ef","name":"Schoenau-Fog, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-157X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-48279-8_6","eisbn":["9783319482798"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings","title":"The 9th Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84996866912"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c58c4e00-92ce-41f8-bb38-e10859cc47b4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Narrative Quality of Game Mechanics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107374","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Self-rated health is an essential aspect of life after stroke, and return to work is considered one of the most important outcomes for younger stroke patients. The aim of this study was to examine whether self-rated health 3 months after stroke, clinical and demographic determinants are independently associated with return to work and subsequent work-stability. MATERIAL AND METHODS: A total of 590 patients with first-time stroke were included from a Danish population-based cohort study. All patients were younger than 60 years and working or unemployed at the time of stroke. Information on self-rated health (Short Form 12; SF-12) was collected from questionnaires 3 months after stroke. Employment status was defined on a weekly basis using national register-data on transfer payments. RESULTS: Fifty percent were self-supporting or job-seeking 12 months after stroke, and the same proportion was found after 24 months. More than 70% of the patients who returned to work did not receive sickness benefits in the 12 months following return to work. Good self-rated health 3 months after stroke and minor stroke severity were strongly associated with return to work after 12 and 24 months. CONCLUSION: Self-rated health 3 months after stroke was strongly associated with return to work and work-stability after stroke.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, L. P.","Biering, Karin","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Andersen, Grethe","Hjøllund, Niels Henrik Ingvar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-162919"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cohort Studies","Quality of Life","Return to work","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self rated health and return to work after first time stroke","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84962245606","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-162919","identifier":[{"id":"26936419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84962245606","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3ae229f5-1202-4e50-86af-84e66704fbc8"],"keyword":["Cohort studies","Quality of life","Return to work","Stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-442042DB22F7A394F18E0D4C3F71CC7D"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Hospital unit West (region Midtjylland)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Occupational and Environmental Medicine, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L. P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, L. P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin","key":"bieringpau","last":"Biering","locid":"747fb3a4-9438-4f99-b7c3-d13deeb4442f","name":"Biering, Karin","orcid":"0000-0001-7038-9566","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Soeren Paaske","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"4664f7a0-39e7-4f46-9121-1c3999eb3d09","name":"Johnsen, Søren Paaske","name_org":"Johnsen, Soeren Paaske","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Grethe","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"97e157c9-4cb4-4690-a971-06e4699b50fe","name":"Andersen, Grethe","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-2500","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Henrik Ingvar","key":"hjøllundpau","last":"Hjøllund","locid":"f85b1091-e209-4393-86c7-69c32d4dd518","name":"Hjøllund, Niels Henrik Ingvar","orcid":"0000-0002-6697-6597","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26936419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/16501977-2061","issn":["16501977","16512081"],"issn_org":["16501977"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Rehabilitation Medicine","pages":"339-345","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Journal of Rehabilitation Medicine","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962245606"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3ae229f5-1202-4e50-86af-84e66704fbc8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Self-rated health and return to work after first-time stroke","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-162919","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Oocyte capacity is relevant in understanding decreasing female fertility and in the use of assisted reproductive technologies in human and farm animals. Mitochondria are important to the development of a functionally good oocyte and the oocyte mtDNA copy number has been introduced as a useful parameter for prediction of oocyte competence. The aim of this study was to investigate: (i) if the oocyte donor has an influence on its oocyte's mtDNA copy number; and (ii) the relation between oocyte size and mtDNA copy number using pre- and postpubertal pig oocytes. Cumulus-oocyte complexes were collected from individual donor pigs. The oocytes were allocated into different size-groups, snap-frozen and single-oocyte mtDNA copy number was estimated by quantitative real-time PCR using the genes ND1 and COX1. Results showed that mean mtDNA copy number in oocytes from any individual donor could be categorized as either 'high' (≥100,000) or 'low' (<100,000) with no difference in threshold between pre- and postpubertal oocytes. No linear correlation was detected between oocyte size and mtDNA copy number within pre- and postpubertal oocytes. This study demonstrates the importance of the oocyte donor in relation to oocyte mtDNA copy number, irrespectively of the donor's puberty status and the oocyte's growth stage. Observations from this study facilitate both further investigations of the importance of mtDNA copy number and the unravelling of relations between different mitochondrial parameters and oocyte competence.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Hanne Skovsgaard","Løvendahl, Peter","Larsen, Knud Erik","Madsen, Lone Bruhn","Callesen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-199856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Mitochondria","Oocyte quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"porcine oocyte mtdna copy number is high or low depending on the donor","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84950261840","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-199856","identifier":[{"id":"26679989","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84950261840","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7b43cbe7-a9ea-4f06-a7c3-1eb95042471c"],"keyword":["Mitochondria","Oocyte quality","mtDNA copy number"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-18EDB4608D2597152A929F48CE95FA94"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Reproductive Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Skovsgaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dbbbd39e-77dc-4209-b35f-089ac5d2159a","name":"Pedersen, Hanne Skovsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"løvendahlpau","last":"Løvendahl","locid":"d1d68047-88cc-43f8-93ed-04e289ca5b38","name":"Løvendahl, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46cd3e98-1529-45bf-9054-2978f328044c","name":"Larsen, Knud Erik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone Bruhn","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"1b15cd00-84c2-4290-bbc6-da52f8665222","name":"Madsen, Lone Bruhn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","locid":"7fe33188-4ec4-4b54-bc7a-c922c5ebaa54","name":"Callesen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0185-7300","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26679989"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0967199415000611","issn":["09671994","14698730"],"issn_org":["09671994"],"issue":"4","journal":"Zygote","pages":"617-623","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Zygote","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84950261840"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7b43cbe7-a9ea-4f06-a7c3-1eb95042471c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Porcine oocyte mtDNA copy number is high or low depending on the donor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-199856","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Poulsen, Jane Rosenstand","Ovesen, Niels Bering","Tornbjerg, Henrik","Larsen, Søren Erik","Windolf, Jørgen","Piil, Kristoffer","Kronvang, Brian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-215213"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experience with high frequency nitrate monitoring in danish streams","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-215213","ids":["au-96c7e80e-ccab-4510-b676-941669ca48e9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E8416155B0A92A52417C83C18F599BD9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Catchment Science and Environmental Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Rosenstand","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"75afd449-d29b-41e7-8882-1e910123d9f9","name":"Poulsen, Jane Rosenstand","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bering","key":"ovesenpau","last":"Ovesen","locid":"62cfa396-63d2-45a1-b33a-14529d575319","name":"Ovesen, Niels Bering","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"tornbjergpau","last":"Tornbjerg","locid":"673f9989-b651-4f14-8190-b60c45f9cde2","name":"Tornbjerg, Henrik","orcid":"0009-0008-7385-7490","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"windolfpau","last":"Windolf","locid":"04de6e58-b8ca-4a60-95e7-849dde928efb","name":"Windolf, Jørgen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer","key":"piilpau","last":"Piil","name":"Piil, Kristoffer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian","key":"kronvangpau","last":"Kronvang","locid":"7766931c-a3c9-4a38-9d22-e4cc3a2f4607","name":"Kronvang, Brian","orcid":"0000-0003-1165-1354","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-96c7e80e-ccab-4510-b676-941669ca48e9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Experience with high frequency nitrate monitoring in Danish streams","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-215213","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: A tele-patient-reported outcome (telePRO) model includes outpatients' reports of symptoms and health status from home before or instead of visiting the outpatient clinic. In the generic PRO system, AmbuFlex, telePRO is used to decide whether a patient needs an outpatient visit and is thus a tool for better symptom assessment, more patient-centred care, and more efficient use of resources. Specific PROs are developed for each patient group. In this paper we describe our experiences with large-scale implementations of telePRO as the basis for follow-up in chronic and malignant diseases using the generic PRO system AmbuFlex. METHODS: The AmbuFlex concept consists of three generic elements: PRO data collection, PRO-based automated decision algorithm, and PRO-based graphical overview for clinical decision support. Experiences were described with respect to these elements. RESULTS: By December 2015, AmbuFlex was implemented in nine diagnostic groups in Denmark. A total of 13,135 outpatients from 15 clinics have been individually referred. From epilepsy clinics, about 70 % of all their outpatients were referred. The response rates for the initial questionnaire were 81-98 %. Of 8256 telePRO-based contacts from epilepsy outpatients, up to 48 % were handled without other contact than the PRO assessment. Clinicians as well as patients reported high satisfaction with the system. CONCLUSION: The results indicate that telePRO is feasible and may be recommended as the platform for follow-up in several patient groups with chronic and malignant diseases and with many consecutive outpatient contacts.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schougaard, Liv Marit Valen","Larsen, Louise Pape","Jessen, Anne","Sidenius, Per Christian","Dorflinger, Liv","de Thurah, Annette","Hjøllund, Niels Henrik Ingvar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-250695"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical practice","Outpatient clinic","Outpatient follow up","Patient reported outcomes","ePRO"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ambuflex tele patient reported outcomes telepro as the basis for follow up in chronic and malignant diseases","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84958766335","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-250695","identifier":[{"id":"84958766335","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4759231","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26790427","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d48d3b52-7255-4ba1-802a-ec71c67642cc"],"keyword":["Clinical practice","Outpatient clinic","Outpatient follow-up","Patient-reported outcomes","ePRO","telePRO"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4864142EA8926B3ECFEA78C9C643C5CB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center for Patientrapporterede Oplysninger, RHG","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Occupational and Environmental Medicine, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liv Marit Valen","key":"schougaardpau","last":"Schougaard","locid":"70b078a7-c71c-46f9-bd18-80399ff5b9e4","name":"Schougaard, Liv Marit Valen","orcid":"0000-0003-2928-2569","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Pape","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8439769e-e2f5-4a26-b4f2-abb4ecb05818","name":"Larsen, Louise Pape","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"8c646212-60bb-44f8-a499-a3faa599b30c","name":"Jessen, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"sideniuspau","last":"Sidenius","locid":"849d5d05-5eac-4868-8d5c-5129bbe44335","name":"Sidenius, Per Christian","name_org":"Sidenius, Per","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Liv","key":"dorflingerpau","last":"Dorflinger","name":"Dorflinger, Liv","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"dethurahpau","last":"de Thurah","locid":"6429fc0a-b979-4ddb-ac99-3214574a17af","name":"de Thurah, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-0103-4328","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Henrik Ingvar","key":"hjøllundpau","last":"Hjøllund","locid":"f85b1091-e209-4393-86c7-69c32d4dd518","name":"Hjøllund, Niels Henrik Ingvar","orcid":"0000-0002-6697-6597","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26790427"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11136-015-1207-0","issn":["09629343"],"issue":"3","journal":"Quality of Life Research","pages":"525-34","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Quality of Life Research","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84958766335"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d48d3b52-7255-4ba1-802a-ec71c67642cc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"AmbuFlex : tele-patient-reported outcomes (telePRO) as the basis for follow-up in chronic and malignant diseases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-250695","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Ledelse. Virtuel ledelse bliver mere og mere udbredt. Den fysiske adskillelse mellem leder og medarbejder har en række fordele, men der er også ulemper.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-278096"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nærværende ledelse på afstand","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-278096","ids":["cbs-1cd94f50-eefd-46d3-b1f0-aa09fafd1f08"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-805FEA33E7DEF6E5D58E17A731B60091"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01091182"],"newspaper":"Jyllands-Posten","pages":"28","publisher":"JP/Politikens Hus AS","publisher_org":"JP/Politikens Hus A/S","status":"p","title":"Jyllands-Posten"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-1cd94f50-eefd-46d3-b1f0-aa09fafd1f08"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Nærværende ledelse på afstand","type":"Newspaper Article","url":