{"abstract":"Traditionally, U-bar loop connections with keyed joints have been used in vertical shear connections between precast concrete wall elements. However, in the recent years, connections with looped high strength wire ropes instead of U-bar loops have proven to be a much more construction-friendly solution. The wire ropes have no bending stiffness and therefore allow for an easier vertical installation of the wall elements. During the last 10 – 15 years, a number of shear tests on plane wire rope connections have been carried out. However, to the best knowledge of the authors, tests on wire rope connections for assembly of precast elements in different planes, such as T- and L-connections, have not yet been published. This paper presents the results of a large test series recently conducted at the University of Southern Denmark to study the shear behaviour of high strength wire rope T-connections grouted with mortar. The test results are evaluated based on the experiences gained from test and modelling of similar plane connections. It is found that T-connections, in contrast to the plane connections, are more prone to fail by rupture of the brittle wire ropes rather than crushing of the joint mortar. Even so, it is found that a ductile post peak response can be obtained for T-connections, especially when so-called double wire boxes are used.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Henrik B.","Bryndom, Thor","Larsen, Michael","Hoang, Linh Cao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380383"],"event":{"end":"2016-11-23","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2016-11-21","title":"fib Symposium 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Precast concrete elements","Shear connections","Wire rope loops"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"load carrying capacity of shear wall t connections reinforced with high strength wire ropes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127946266/Joergensen_et_al_fib_CapTown2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380383","ids":["dtu-fd66729d-e4bc-474b-8725-7fd8853ff2d4"],"keyword":["Mortar connections","Precast concrete elements","Shear connections","Wire rope loops"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F170C8967A705ADEF2C93A06A96D4B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127946266/Joergensen_et_al_fib_CapTown2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Section for Structural Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik B.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Henrik B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thor","key":"bryndompau","last":"Bryndom","name":"Bryndom, Thor","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linh Cao","key":"hoangpau","last":"Hoang","locid":"6017dbb4-0828-40d2-a12d-fc78da1ae542","name":"Hoang, Linh Cao","orcid":"0000-0002-5564-1599","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings","title":"fib Symposium 2016: Performance-based approaches for concrete structures"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fd66729d-e4bc-474b-8725-7fd8853ff2d4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Load carrying capacity of shear wall t-connections reinforced with high strength wire ropes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380383","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Muscle hemorrhages are regularly observed in especially the tip of the tenderloin muscles of slaughter pigs. In order to characterize the hemorrhages, a macro- and microscopic examination of tenderloins with (n = 5) and without (n = 4) hemorrhages and the associated vertebral column was carried out. Furthermore, all columns were radiographed and two were CT scanned. Histologically, the muscle hemorrhages contained cells from bone marrow and growth line cartilage. Ventral epiphysiolysis in either the cranial or caudal epiphysis of the first lumbar vertebrae (L1) in 8 out of the 9 vertebral columns was present. In the 5 cases with tenderloin hemorrhage, similar hemorrhage with growth line cartilage was found within the fracture of the epiphysis. The hemorrhages develop secondarily to epiphysiolysis in the lumbar vertebrae, where the tenderloin attaches to the spine. The lesions probably develop around the time of stunning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Dich-Jørgensen, Kristine","McEvoy, Fintan","Larsen, Helle Daugaard","Leifsson, Páll S.","Jensen, Henrik Elvang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479038"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Slaughter pigs","Stunning"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of hemorrhages in the tenderloins of slaughter pigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-479038","identifier":[{"id":"27372280","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84976555442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8f2ddeb0-d5bd-4717-bfcf-60b6f9164825"],"keyword":["Epiphysiolysis","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Muscle hemorrhage","Slaughter pigs","Stunning","Tenderloins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2E820753808F93A22945ABBC2446257"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Meat Research Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristine","key":"dichjørgensenpau","last":"Dich-Jørgensen","locid":"511e2cfe-da81-4a6e-a088-50c88e784613","name":"Dich-Jørgensen, Kristine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fintan","key":"mcevoypau","last":"McEvoy","locid":"38cc3ea7-06d4-43f9-b239-092f41bcd16b","name":"McEvoy, Fintan","orcid":"0000-0003-4195-8816","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle Daugaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Helle Daugaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Páll S.","key":"leifssonpau","last":"Leifsson","locid":"691042d9-84a7-4df4-8005-8e60cfb7dc4e","name":"Leifsson, Páll S.","orcid":"0000-0003-1539-9491","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27372280"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.meatsci.2016.06.026","