{"abstract":"O-Mannosylation is a vital protein modification conserved from fungi to humans. Yeast is a perfect model to study this post-translational modification, because in contrast to mammalsO-mannosylation is the only type ofO-glycosylation. In an essential step toward the full understanding of proteinO-mannosylation we mapped theO-mannose glycoproteome in baker's yeast. Taking advantage of anO-glycan elongation deficient yeast strain to simplify sample complexity, we identified over 500O-glycoproteins from all subcellular compartments for which over 2300O-mannosylation sites were mapped by electron-transfer dissociation (ETD)-based MS/MS. In this study, we focus on the 293O-glycoproteins (over 1900 glycosylation sites identified by ETD-MS/MS) that enter the secretory pathway and are targets of ER-localized proteinO-mannosyltransferases. We find thatO-mannosylation is not only a prominent modification of cell wall and plasma membrane proteins, but also of a large number of proteins from the secretory pathway with crucial functions in protein glycosylation, folding, quality control, and trafficking. The analysis of glycosylation sites revealed thatO-mannosylation is favored in unstructured regions and β-strands. Furthermore,O-mannosylation is impeded in the proximity ofN-glycosylation sites suggesting the interplay of these types of post-translational modifications. The detailed knowledge of the target proteins and theirO-mannosylation sites opens for discovery of new roles of this essential modification in eukaryotes, and for a first glance on the evolution of different types ofO-glycosylation from yeast to mammals.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Neubert, Patrick","Halim, Adnan","Zauser, Martin","Essig, Andreas","Joshi, Hiren J.","Zatorska, Ewa","Larsen, Ida Signe Bohse","Loibl, Martin","Castells-Ballester, Joan","Aebi, Markus","Clausen, Henrik","Strahl, Sabine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-545457"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mapping the o mannose glycoproteome in saccharomyces cerevisiae","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.M115.057505","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-545457","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4824858","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84994881651","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26764011","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fec881bf-3d9c-44f1-852b-a245d7a6ef85"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B22E45AF3ED432AA8D53FCD56B28CF0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/166165790/Mol_Cell_Proteomics_2016_Neubert_1323_37.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.M115.057505","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Patrick","key":"neubertpau","last":"Neubert","name":"Neubert, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adnan","key":"halimpau","last":"Halim","locid":"65f08640-6203-4f49-ad7e-f95cb9c070b8","name":"Halim, Adnan","orcid":"0000-0003-1629-187X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":""