{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Congenital heart disease (CHD) occurs in approximately 1% of all live births, and 3% to 8% of these have until now been considered familial cases, defined as the occurrence of two or more affected individuals in a family. The validity of CHD diagnoses in Danish administrative registry data has only been studied previously in highly selected patient populations. These studies identified high positive predictive values (PPVs) and recurrence risk ratios (RRRs-ratio between probabilities of CHD given family history of CHD and no family history). However, the RRR can be distorted if registry data are used indiscriminately. Here, we investigated the consequences of misclassifications for the RRR using validated diagnoses on Danish patients with familial CHD. METHODS: Danish citizens are assigned a civil registration number (CPR number) at birth or immigration, which acts as a unique identifier in the Danish registries, thus enabling connection of information from several registries. Utilizing the CPR number, we identified Danish patients with familial CHD and reviewed each patient's file. We compared diagnoses from the registries with those manually assigned, which enabled calculation of the PPVs of diagnoses in the Danish registries, and from this, we deduced the false discovery rate (FDR). To measure the consequences on the RRR, the FDR was applied to a simulated data set with true RRR values of 2 and 10. RESULTS: We validated diagnoses of 2,442 patients from 1,593 families. Of these, 874 patients were misclassified corresponding to an FDR of 36%. Applying this FDR on the simulated data sets, we found that the RRR decreased from 2 and 10 to 1.4 and 5.1, respectively. Lastly, we estimated that 11% of all cases with CHD were familial. CONCLUSION: We found that approximately one of nine of all cases with CHD are familial, and we also found that 36% of individuals with CHD in administrative medical registries are misclassified, which distort the RRR in simulated scenarios.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ellesøe, Sabrina Gade","Jensen, Anders Boeck","Ängquist, Lars Henrik","Hjortdal, Vibeke E.","Larsen, Lars Allan","Brunak, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-097.70-019232"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how suitable are registry data for recurrence risk calculations validation of diagnoses on 000000000001 000000000593 families with congenital heart disease","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85050577357","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.70-019232","identifier":[{"id":"85050577357","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26957399","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5a42c5a4-2f06-4da3-90a1-c8f8af38dd14","ku-5b623959-850c-40a1-8681-371f3ac95b72"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-576A5C105C2C0DE1F35C7D8DB7830AA9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Disease Systems Biology Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg og Frederiksberg Universitets Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sabrina Gade","key":"ellesøepau","last":"Ellesøe","locid":"96f79011-b50c-4f93-8668-3286bf7cdd15","name":"Ellesøe, Sabrina Gade","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Boeck","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7eb33d70-4690-45ab-b301-fff23c8389db","name":"Jensen, Anders Boeck","orcid":"0000-0002-5784-308X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"ängquistpau","last":"Ängquist","name":"Ängquist, Lars Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke Elisabeth","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"bc855c56-732d-4e8f-bfb6-0b8cb5a19818","name":"Hjortdal, Vibeke E.","name_org":"Hjortdal, Vibeke Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Allan","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"78031d9d-4c66-4f3b-9dd4-e5aa1d6b19a5","name":"Larsen, Lars Allan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"brunakpau","last":"Brunak","locid":"9398f2a1-bef5-4491-9b57-083e6758eac2","name":"Brunak, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-0316-5866","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26957399"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/2150135115615786","issn":["21501351"],"issue":"2","journal":"World Journal for Pediatric and Congenital Heart Surgery","pages":"169-77","status":"p","title":"World Journal for Pediatric and Congenital Heart Surgery","title_org":"World journal for pediatric & congenital heart surgery","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050577357"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5a42c5a4-2f06-4da3-90a1-c8f8af38dd14","ku-5b623959-850c-40a1-8681-371f3ac95b72"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Suitable Are Registry Data for Recurrence Risk Calculations? : Validation of Diagnoses on 1,593 Families With Congenital Heart Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.70-019232","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Increasing evidence suggests that aspirin use may protect against prostate cancer. In a nationwide case-control study, using Danish high-quality registry data, we evaluated the association between the use of low-dose aspirin or other nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) and the risk of prostate cancer. METHODS: We identified 35,600 patients (cases) with histologically verified prostate cancer during 2000-2012. Cases were matched to 177,992 population controls on age and residence by risk-set sampling. Aspirin and nonaspirin NSAID exposure was defined by type, estimated dose, duration, and consistency of use. We used conditional logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs), with 95 % confidence intervals (CIs), for prostate cancer associated with low-dose aspirin (75-150 mg) or nonaspirin NSAID use, adjusted for potential confounders. RESULTS: Use of low-dose aspirin was associated with an OR for prostate cancer of 0.94 (95 % CI 0.91-0.97). Slightly lower ORs were seen with increasing cumulative amount, duration, and consistency of low-dose aspirin use (continuous use, ≥5 years: OR 0.89; 95 % CI 0.82-0.97; ≥10 years: OR 0.86; 95 % CI 0.70-1.06). Nonaspirin NSAID use was associated with a slightly increased OR for prostate cancer (1.13; 95 % CI 1.10-1.15); however, this association was confined to localized disease and did not vary materially with amount, duration, or consistency of nonaspirin NSAID use. CONCLUSIONS: Our study indicates that long-term, consistent low-dose aspirin use may provide modest protection against prostate cancer. The slightly increased risk of only localized prostate cancer with nonaspirin NSAID use suggests a noncausal explanation of the observed association.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Skriver, Charlotte","Dehlendorff, Christian","Borre, Michael","Brasso, Klaus","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Hallas, Jesper","Larsen, Signe Benzon","Tjønneland, Anne","Friis, Søren"],"cuid":["S03-099.02-025676"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Aspirin","Epidemiology","Journal Article","Nonsteroidal anti inflammatory drugs","Prostate neoplasms","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low dose aspirin or other nonsteroidal anti inflammatory drug use and prostate cancer risk a nationwide study","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84981190747","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.02-025676","identifier":[{"id":"84981190747","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000388415700003","type":"wos"},{"id":"27503490","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b266946b-e02f-4491-b3c4-2384a7825a18","ku-df01067e-9c90-456e-a9f3-6954fd994956","sdu-2b590591-8cfd-43fc-911a-9b9dadd52d93"],"keyword":["Aspirin","Casecontrol study","Epidemiology","Journal Article","Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs","Prostate neoplasms","Risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-8B237953885A1295BF7EFEEE7CF6860C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus universit