{"abstract":"A design of a G-band TE01 mode converter is presented in this work. It consists of a TE01 mode launcher followed by a tapered waveguide section. Full-wave simulated reflection coefficient of stainless steel converter is better than −15 dB and transmission coefficient is better than −1.5 dB in a frequency range from 173 GHz to 193 GHz. The design is useful in applications employing highly overmoded circular waveguides.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rybalko, Oleksandr","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380976"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-30","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2016-09-25","title":"41st International Conference on Infrared, Millimeter and Terahertz Waves","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Attenuation","Conductivity","Copper","Microwave theory and techniques","Silver","Steel","Thermal conductivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"te000000000001 mode converter for highly overmoded circular waveguide at 000000000188 ghz","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85006127157","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380976","identifier":[{"id":"85006127157","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ff28cb98-6dc2-43fd-8224-3cc200ef388a"],"keyword":["Attenuation","Conductivity","Copper","Microwave theory and techniques","Silver","Steel","Thermal conductivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B50805F9C0AC830A1D6034ED19CBD69C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oleksandr","key":"rybalkopau","last":"Rybalko","locid":"35007e3c-be65-457f-99ea-073043576468","name":"Rybalko, Oleksandr","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-6868","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/irmmw-thz.2016.7758709","isbn":["9781467384858"],"issn":["21622027"],"pages":"1-2","publisher":"IEEE","series":"International Conference on Infrared, Millimeter and Terahertz Waves","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2016 41st International Conference on Infrared, Millimeter, and Terahertz waves"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006127157"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ff28cb98-6dc2-43fd-8224-3cc200ef388a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"TE01 mode converter for highly overmoded circular waveguide at 188 GHz","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380976","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this investigation was to examine, within a population-based study of a national cohort comprising Danish survivors of allo-SCT (n = 148), the long-term effects of allo-SCT in children and young adults. Physical and emotional well-being was assessed using the Short Form 36 (SF-36) and the HADS. Allo-SCT-related data were obtained from the participants' medical records. The study includes 148 patients, with an 89% response rate (n = 132). For comparison purposes, norm data from Danish (1994, n = 6000), Swedish (2006, n = 285), and British (2001, n = 1792) population samples were used. Factors negatively influencing the SF-36 subscales included female gender; TBI; stem cells derived from PB; older age at time of questioning; and living alone. Factors significantly (p < 0.05) influencing HADS were transplantation with stem cells derived from PB and being underweight at time of questioning (median values were within normal range). Overall scores of allo-SCT patients were similar to norm data. In conclusion, this national cohort study shows that patients treated with SCT in early life (<25) and whose survival period extended beyond 10 yr (mean) from SCT, showed similar levels of anxiety, depression, and physical and emotional well-being to those of the normal population.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jensen, Josef Nathan","Gøtzsche, Frederik","Heilmann, Carsten","Sengeløv, Henrik","Adamsen, Lis","Christensen, Karl Bang","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-422764"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physical and emotional well being of survivors of childhood and young adult allo sct a danish national cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-422764","identifier":[{"id":"27231147","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84978706297","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3136b729-3ac0-438e-b0b8-6551b7e49b6b"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0795B855FCE0B493DAA9DC11C2D291BD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Josef Nathan","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Josef Nathan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frederik","key":"gøtzschepau","last":"Gøtzsche","name":"Gøtzsche, Frederik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"heilmannpau","last":"Heilmann","name":"Heilmann, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"sengeløvpau","last":"Sengeløv","locid":"ff0cb82b-deb8-4d4e-b871-8f70d359af15","name":"Sengeløv, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lis","key":"adamsenpau","last":"Adamsen","locid":"e2dd2ae3-e721-4895-8f98-a857c3a88e6a","name":"Adamsen, Lis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karl Bang","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"850a805f-c580-4858-822c-8e5c72ac780c","name":"Christensen, Karl Bang","orcid":"0000-0003-4518-5187","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne Bækgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27231147"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/petr.12713","issn":["13973142","13982265"],"issn_org":["13973142"],"issue":"5","journal":"Pediatric Transplantation","pages":"697-706","status":"p","title":"Pediatric Transplantation","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978706297"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3136b729-3ac0-438e-b0b8-6551b7e49b6b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Physical and emotional well-being of survivors of childhood and young adult allo-SCT : A Danish national cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-422764","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Antisense peptide nucleic acid (PNA) oligomers constitute a novel class of potential antibiotics that inhibit bacterial growth via specific knockdown of essential gene expression. However, discovery of efficient, nontoxic delivery vehicles for such PNA oligomers has remained a challenge. In the present study we show that antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) with an intracellular mode of action can be efficient vehicles for bacterial delivery of an antibacterial PNA targeting the essential acpP gene. The results demonstrate that buforin 2-A (BF2-A), drosocin, oncocin 10, Pep-1-K, KLW-9,13-a, (P59→W59)-Tat48-60, BF-2A-RXR, and drosocin-RXR are capable of transporting PNA effectively into E. coli (MICs of 1-4 μM). Importantly, presence of the inner-membrane peptide transporter SbmA was not required for antibacterial activity of PNA-AMP conjugates containing Pep-1-K, KLW-9,13-a, or drosocin-RXR (MICs of 2-4 μM).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Anna Mette","Vedel, Line","Larsen, Camilla Josephine","Yavari, Niloofar","Nielsen, Peter E.","Franzyk, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457453"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antibacterial peptide nucleic acid antimicrobial peptide pna amp conjugates antisense targeting of fatty acid biosynthesis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-457453","identifier":[{"id":"26938833","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84965017823","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6b396019-a1ca-46ad-b3de-7ced4d47330c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9FEA03F7DB1A78F25D23294718CD313"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Mette","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5e81b7fd-9d07-4dc6-8a5e-20d5fa6cc0d0","name":"Hansen, Anna Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-1162-8592","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gitte","key":"bonkepau","last":"Bonke","locid":"2a30ceee-2443-4a22-9599-6b9171ab1461","name":"Vedel, Line","name_org":"Bonke, Gitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Josephine","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Camilla Josephine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niloofar","key":"yavaripau","last":"Yavari","locid":"60d57251-0ca0-4c34-8dde-53422b4f03e4","name":"Yavari, Niloofar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"74cb6e41-3bfc-4d0a-a0df-7bd8fa9c2856","name":"Nielsen, Peter E.","orcid":"0000-0001-8771-330X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"franzykpau","last":"Franzyk","locid":"5120ce68-6886-4ac8-8178-310a47d19261","name":"Franzyk, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2822-1927","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26938833"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.bioconjchem.6b00013","issn":["10431802","15204812"],"issn_org":["10431802"],"issue":"4","journal":"Bioconjugate Chemistry","pages":"863-867","status":"p","title":"Bioconjugate Chemistry","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84965017823"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6b396019-a1ca-46ad-b3de-7ced4d47330c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antibacterial Peptide Nucleic Acid-Antimicrobial Peptide (PNA-AMP) Conjugates : Antisense Targeting of Fatty Acid Biosynthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457453","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Historically, productivity gains have been possible by the application of energy intensive technologies. In the future, new technologies and practices based on energy from renewable resources are central for the development of our food supply system and they will contribute in two different ways. As the energy sector increasingly bases energy supply on renewable sources, the energy requirements of the food sector will automatically substitute renewable energy for non-renewable energy in all stages of food supply. In principle, the food sector does not need to change if renewable energy is sufficient and available as the energy carriers that we are used to today. We may think of this as passive adaptation. A passive adaptation strategy may support a development towards the image ‘high input – high output’. The food sector, however, may also actively adapt to a future without fossil fuels and change production methods, distribution systems etc. to depend on fewer external energy inputs and make better use of the energy and other resources provided by natural processes. Active adaptation may be a characteristic component of a strategy for the image ‘medium input – medium output.’ We expect that the increasing world population and the increasing demand for resource intensive food and life style will require a strategy for the future food supply system centred on energy reduction.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kamp, Andreas","Østergård, Hanne","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-559881"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy consumption in the food supply system","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/61009430/DTU_INTERNATIONAL_ENERGY_REPORT_2016_reduced.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-559881","ids":["ruc-39df0e59-cdfe-44b0-99f4-64bf18d7483d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2434329E7C799358765F05B7F27D3787"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/61009430/DTU_INTERNATIONAL_ENERGY_REPORT_2016_reduced.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kamppau","last":"Kamp","name":"Kamp, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"østergårdpau","last":"Østergård","name":"Østergård, Hanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"0bc8cc02-9199-4a75-9e51-7dd5ceba9583","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8929-9691","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Leif Sønderberg","key":"pedersenpedh","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Leif Sønderberg","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans Hvidtfeldt","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Hans Hvidtfeldt","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788755039735"],"pages":"54-63","place":"Lyngby","publisher":"Danmarks Tekniske Universitet (DTU)","status":"p","subtitle":"The Energy-Water-Food Nexus — from local to global aspects","title":"DTU International Energy Report 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-39df0e59-cdfe-44b0-99f4-64bf18d7483d"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Energy consumption in the food supply system","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-559881","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Heritable disorders that feature high bone mass (HBM) are rare. The etiology is typically a mutation(s) within a gene that regulates the differentiation and function of osteoblasts (OBs) or osteoclasts (OCs). Nevertheless, the molecular basis is unknown for approximately one-fifth of such entities. NF-κB signaling is a key regulator of bone remodeling and acts by enhancing OC survival while impairing OB maturation and function. The NF-κB transcription complex comprises five subunits. In mice, deletion of the p50 and p52 subunits together causes osteopetrosis (OPT). In humans, however, mutations within the genes that encode the NF-κB complex, including the Rela/p65 subunit, have not been reported. We describe a neonate who died suddenly and unexpectedly and was found at postmortem to have HBM documented radiographically and by skeletal histopathology. Serum was not available for study. Radiographic changes resembled malignant OPT, but histopathological investigation showed morphologically normal OCs and evidence of intact bone resorption excluding OPT. Furthermore, mutation analysis was negative for eight genes associated with OPT or HBM. Instead, accelerated bone formation appeared to account for the HBM. Subsequently, trio-based whole exome sequencing revealed a heterozygous de novo missense mutation (c.1534-1535delinsAG, p.Asp512Ser) in exon 11 of RELA encoding Rela/p65. The mutation was then verified using bidirectional Sanger sequencing. Lipopolysaccharide stimulation of patient fibroblasts elicited impaired NF-κB responses compared with healthy control fibroblasts. Five unrelated patients with unexplained HBM did not show a RELA defect. Ours is apparently the first report of a mutation within the NF-κB complex in humans. The missense change is associated with neonatal osteosclerosis from in utero increased OB function rather than failed OC action. These findings demonstrate the importance of the Rela/p65 subunit within the NF-κB pathway for human skeletal homeostasis and represent a new genetic cause of HBM.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Anja Lisbeth","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Brusgaard, Klaus","Norvack, Deborah V","Knudsen, Peter Juel Thiis","Schrøder, Henrik Daa","Qiu, Weimin","Eckhardt, Christina","McAlister, William H","Kassem, Moustapha","Mumm, Steven","Frost, Morten","Whyte, Michael P"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-623998"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Adult","Amino Acid Substitution","Female","Humans","Infant Newborn","Male","Mutation Missense","Osteoblast","Osteoclast","Osteopetrosis","Osteosclerosis","Radiography","Signal Transduction genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Center for Metabolic Bone Disease and Molecular Research, Shriners Hospital for Children; St. Louis, MO, USA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neonatal high bone mass with first mutation of the nf κb complex heterozygous i de novo i missense p asp000000000512ser i rela i rela p000000000065","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5310715/pdf/nihms812908.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-623998","identifier":[{"id":"84957435029","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26178921","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5310715","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-b14bfeaf-8bfe-4138-b8cf-6565ee9f6225"],"keyword":["Adult","Amino Acid Substitution","Female","Genetic Diseases, Inborn/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Infant, Newborn","Male","Mutation, Missense","OSTEOBLAST","OSTEOCLAST","OSTEOPETROSIS","OST