{"abstract":"The lung surfactant (LS) lining is a thin liquid film covering the air-liquid interface of the respiratory tract. LS reduces surface tension, enabling lung surface expansion and contraction with minimal work during respiration. Disruption of surface tension is believed to play a key role in severe lung conditions. Inhalation of aerosols that interfere with the LS may induce a toxic response and as a part of the safety assessment of chemicals and inhaled medicines, it may be relevant to study their impact on LS function. Here we present a novel in vitro method, based on the constrained drop surfactometer, to study LS functionality after aerosol exposure. The applicability of the method was investigated using three inhaled asthma medicines, micronized lactose, a pharmaceutical excipient used in inhaled medication and micronized albumin, a known inhibitor of surfactant function. The surfactometer was modified to allow particles mixed in air to flow through the chamber holding the surfactant drop. The deposited dose was measured with a custom built quartz crystal microbalance. The alterations allowed the study of continuously increasing quantified doses of particles, allowing determination of the dose of particles that affects the LS function. The tested pharmaceuticals did not inhibit the function of a model LS even at extreme doses, neither did lactose. Micronized albumin, however, impaired surfactant function. The method can discriminate between safe inhaled aerosols - as exemplified by the approved inhaled medicines and the pharmaceutical excipient lactose - and albumin known to impair lung functionality by inhibiting LS function","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sørli, Jorid Birkelund","Da, Silva E.","Bäckman, P.","Levin, Dan Henrik Marcus","Thomsen, B.L.","Koponen, Ismo Kalevi","Larsen, Søren Thor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782030"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a proposed in vitro method to assess effects of inhaled particles on lung surfactant function","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963894027","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782030","identifier":[{"id":"84963894027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["nfa-e77756ba-f896-4c3c-9fbe-4bc86477b3eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1B70F215A1F1164FC15E6B66BB2125A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorid Birkelund","key":"sørlipau","last":"Sørli","locid":"0c82c65e-a08d-46fc-baf7-721806799318","name":"Sørli, Jorid Birkelund","orcid":"0000-0001-5453-433X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Silva E.","key":"dapau","last":"Da","name":"Da, Silva E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"bäckmanpau","last":"Bäckman","name":"Bäckman, P.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Henrik Marcus","key":"levinpau","last":"Levin","name":"Levin, Dan Henrik Marcus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B.L.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, B.L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ismo Kalevi","key":"koponenpau","last":"Koponen","name":"Koponen, Ismo Kalevi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Thor","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"32005edc-74a7-4ff2-a0ab-44b3d17409d6","name":"Larsen, Søren Thor","orcid":"0000-0003-1142-7045","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1165/rcmb.2015-0294ma","issn":["10441549","15354989"],"issn_org":["10441549"],"issue":"3","journal":"American Journal of Respiratory Cell and Molecular Biology","pages":"306-311","publisher":"American Thoracic Society","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Respiratory Cell and Molecular Biology","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963894027"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-e77756ba-f896-4c3c-9fbe-4bc86477b3eb"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"A proposed in vitro method to assess effects of inhaled particles on lung surfactant function","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782030","year":"2016","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We describe principles and design of a system for knowledge bases applying a natural logic. Natural logics are forms of logic which appear as stylized fragments of natural language sentences. Accordingly, such knowledge base sentences can be read and understood directly by a domain expert. The system applies a graph form computed from the input natural logic sentences. The graph form generalizes the usual partial-order ontological sub-class structures by accommodation of affirmative sentences comprising recursive phrase structures. In this paper we focus on the logical inference rules for extending the concept graph form enabling deductive querying as well as computation of pathways between the concepts mentioned in the sentences.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Andreasen, Troels","Bulskov, Henrik","Nilsson, Jørgen Fischer","Jensen, Per Anker"],"cuid":["S02-082.75-031359"],"event":{"acronym":"FQAS","end":"2015-10-28","place":"Kraków, pl","start":"2015-10-26","title":"The 11th International Conference on Flexible Query Answering Systems. FQAS 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Deductive querying of natural logic knowledge bases","Logical knowledge bases in bio informatics and medicine","Path finding in knowledge bases"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a system for conceptual pathway finding and deductive querying","src":["cbs","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/45496151/per_anker_jensen_a_system_for_conceptual_pathway_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-082.75-031359","identifier":[{"id":"84983158125","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-3657b898-c5bb-48f4-b208-b899736c6d54","dtu-0da91416-29bb-4bed-b70f-60fe02d761e8"],"keyword":["Deductive querying of natural-logic knowledge bases","Logical knowledge bases in bio-informatics and medicine","Path finding in knowledge bases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2D71C0B05FE1C04D6B4E1C4C8CEC845A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/45496151/per_anker_jensen_a_system_for_conceptual_pathway_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of International Busine