ole":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Adnan","key":"yazicipedh","last":"Yazici","name":"Yazici, Adnan","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sławomir","key":"zadrożnypedh","last":"Zadrożny","name":"Zadrożny, Sławomir","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-26154-6_35","eisbn":["9783319261546"],"isbn":["9783319261539"],"issn":["21945357"],"pages":"461-472","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Advances in Intelligent Systems and Computing","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 11th International Conference FQAS 2015, Cracow, Poland, October 26-28, 2015","title":"Flexible Query Answering Systems 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983158125"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-3657b898-c5bb-48f4-b208-b899736c6d54","dtu-0da91416-29bb-4bed-b70f-60fe02d761e8"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A System for Conceptual Pathway Finding and Deductive Querying","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.75-031359","year":2016,"yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Low back pain changes the trunk muscle activity after external perturbations but the relationship between pain intensities and distributions and their effect on the trunk muscle activity remains unclear. The effects of unilateral and bilateral experimental low back pain on trunk muscle activity were compared during unpredictable multidirectional surface perturbations in 19 healthy participants. Pain intensity and distribution were assessed using a visual analogue scale (VAS) and pain drawings. Root mean square (RMS) of the electromyographic (EMG) signals from 6 trunk muscles bilaterally after each perturbation was extracted and averaged across perturbations. The difference (ΔRMS-EMG) and absolute difference (absolute ΔRMS-EMG) RMS from baseline conditions were extracted for each muscle during pain conditions and averaged bilaterally for back and abdominal muscle groups. Bilateral compared with unilateral pain induced higher VAS scores (P < .005) and larger pain areas (P < .001). Significant correlation was present between VAS scores and muscle activity during unilateral (P < .001) and bilateral pain (P < .001). Compared with control injections ΔRMS-EMG increased in the back (P < .03) and abdominal (P < .05) muscles during bilateral and decreased in the back (P < .01) and abdominal (P < .01) muscles during unilateral pain. Bilateral pain caused greater absolute ΔRMS-EMG changes in the back (P < .01) and abdominal (P < .01) muscle groups than unilateral pain. PERSPECTIVE: This study provided novel observations of differential trunk muscle activity in response to perturbations dependent on pain intensity and/or pain distribution. Because of complex and variable changes the relevance of clinical examination of muscle activity during postural tasks is challenged.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars Henrik","Hirata, Rogerio Pessoto","Graven-Nielsen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-093.94-004991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Physiotherapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reorganized trunk muscle activity during multidirectional floor perturbations after experimental low back pain a comparison of bilateral versus unilateral pain","src":["aau","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/237333016/reorganized_trunk_muscle_activity_during_multidirectional_floor_perturbations_after_experimental_low_back_pain.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-093.94-004991","identifier":[{"id":"84951944240","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000370111600008","type":"wos"},{"id":"84959480409","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6739fecf-c1a4-4511-bbd2-024913bcefea","ucn-134be5c1-6ec9-4ad5-8950-54317ff118ae"],"keyword":["physiotherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4EAC9C4DEB0520EB0F5158797D8AD451"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/237333016/reorganized_trunk_muscle_activity_during_multidirectional_floor_perturbations_after_experimental_low_back_pain.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Depa