ll,"first":"Marianne Søgaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"bd958850-3e0e-4df2-8824-d02163a83e3a","name":"Andersen, Marianne Søgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"38fc12aa-c80d-41b1-84e8-d7f9280de4f2","name":"Friis, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2848-2940","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Rikke","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sanna","key":"fiskerpedh","last":"Fisker","name":"Fisker, Sanna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9788762816657"],"isbn":["9788762814585"],"pages":"424-449","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Livscyklusernæring"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-c07023f2-9498-46c4-a817-62a5ac59ec56","ku-eaee875f-b7f0-4639-adf8-81d046e7a640"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Livscyklusernæring i globalt perspektiv","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.64-039371","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"[Open acess]Selenium (Se) is an essential element with a small difference between physiological and toxic doses. To provide more effective and safe Se dosing regimens, as compared to dosing with ionic selenium, nanoparticle formulations have been developed. However, due to the nano-formulation, unexpected toxic effects may occur. We used metabolite pattern determination in urine to investigate biological and/or toxic effects in rats administered nanoparticles and for comparison included ionic selenium at an equimolar dose in the form of sodium selenite. Low doses of 10 and 100 fold the recommended human high level were employed to study the effects at borderline toxicity. Evaluations of all significantly changed putative metabolites, showed that Se nanoparticles and sodium selenite induced similar dose dependent changes of the metabolite pattern. Putative identified metabolites included increased decenedioic acid and hydroxydecanedioic acid for both Se formulations whereas dipeptides were only increased for selenite. These effects could reflect altered fatty acid and protein metabolism, respectively","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hadrup, Niels","Löschner, Katrin","Skov, Kasper","Ravn-Haren, Gitte","Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","Mortensen, Alicja","Lam, Henrik R.","Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz"],"cuid":["S02-096.83-768352"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Nanoparticle","Pharmacology","Selenium","Toxicology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of 000000000014 day oral low dose selenium nanoparticles and selenite in rat as determined by metabolite pattern determination","src":["dtu","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj.2601","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.83-768352","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5075706","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27781177","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84994476592","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-960ed237-54d1-423c-af7e-ab708ece7971","nfa-35df9270-666c-4588-ba5b-e2e523ff342a"],"keyword":["Food Science and Technology","Metabolic Sciences","Metabolomic pattern recognition","Nanoparticle","Pharmacology","Selenium","Toxicology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-48D825D11DC1D2E7CC11423A946B689E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj.2601","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126822366/Hadrup_et_al_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://peerj.com/articles/2601/","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"hadruppau","last":"Hadrup","locid":"4384548f-118a-4c3c-aedf-f0d203046277","name":"Hadrup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-1188-445X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrin","key":"löschnerpau","last":"Löschner","locid":"d7b22217-70e4-4c54-bd53-3f02c2d23a6f","name":"Löschner, Katrin","orcid":"0000-0003-1741-8406","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"loeschnerpau","last":"Loeschner","name":"Loeschner, K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"be2372a7-55be-4b66-a423-0af493a79e3e","name":"Skov, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"ravnharenpau","last":"Ravn-Haren","locid":"c3832c3d-f3a5-4eb3-9e1e-7a7eb66d87a4","name":"Ravn-Haren, Gitte","orcid":"0000-0002-4587-089X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Huusfeldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9528940a-884f-4a63-b068-b739d7551006","name":"Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alicja","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"2cbb8a58-bb77-4b14-9b9b-16408c39d2c4","name":"Mortensen, Alicja","orcid":"0000-0001-6992-7750","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik R.","key":"lampau","last":"Lam","name":"Lam, Henrik R.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Lauritz","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"7f8f5328-37cb-4aa3-a2e1-1b519b8e1c83","name":"Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz","orcid":"0000-0002-1905-8144","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27781177"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7717/peerj.2601","issn":["21678359"],"journal":"PeerJ","paperid":"e2601","publisher":"PeerJ Inc.","status":"p","title":"PeerJ","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994476592"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-960ed237-54d1-423c-af7e-ab708ece7971","nfa-35df9270-666c-4588-ba5b-e2e523ff342a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Effects of 14-day oral low dose selenium nanoparticles and selenite in rat—as determined by metabolite pattern determination","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.83-768352","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In the field of drug delivery to the articular cartilage, it is advantageous to apply artificial tissue models as surrogates of cartilage for investigating drug transport and release properties. In this study, artificial cartilage models consisting of 0.5% (w/v) agarose gel containing 0.5% (w/v) chondroitin sulfate or 0.5% (w/v) hyaluronic acid were developed, and their rheological and morphological properties were characterized. UV imaging was utilized to quantify the transport properties of the following four model compounds in the agarose gel and in the developed artificial cartilage models: H-Ala-β-naphthylamide, H-Lys-Lys-β-naphthylamide, lysozyme, and α-lactalbumin. The obtained results showed that the incorporation of the polyelectrolytes chondroitin sulfate or hyaluronic acid into agarose gel induced a significant reduction in the apparent diffusivities of the cationic model compounds as compared to the pure agarose gel. The decrease in apparent diffusivity of the cationic compounds was not caused by a change in the gel structure since a similar reduction in apparent diffusivity was not observed for the net negatively charged protein α-lactalbumin. The apparent diffusivity of the cationic compounds in the negatively charged hydrogels was highly dependent on the ionic strength, pointing out the importance of electrostatic interactions between the diffusant and the polyelectrolytes. Solution based affinity studies between the model compounds and the two investigated polyelectrolytes further confirmed the electrostatic nature of their interactions. The results obtained from the UV imaging diffusion studies are important for understanding the effect of drug physicochemical properties on the transport in articular cartilage. The extracted information may be useful in the development of hydrogels for in vitro release testing having features resembling the articular cartilage.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ye, Fengbin","Baldursdottir, Stefania G.","Hvidt, Søren","Jensen, Henrik","Larsen, Susan Weng","Yaghmur, Anan","Larsen, Claus Selch","Østergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-098.08-042218"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Chondroitin sulfate","Diffusion","Drug delivery","Electrostatic interactions","Hyaluronic acid","Hydrogel","Journal Article","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Transport","UV imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"role of electrostatic interactions on the transport of druglike molecules in hydrogel based articular cartilage mimics implications for drug delivery","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-098.08-042218","identifier":[{"id":"84960158282","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26808484","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4c3a192e-1756-4655-9180-9bd6660b9e2a","ruc-27bd9530-2b64-4d6a-b687-c491444bedcb"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","UV imaging","cartilage mimic","chondroitin sulfate","diffusion","drug delivery","electrostatic interactions","hyaluronic acid","hydrogel","transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9A8B3E2917FC4DF8DD0CBB3F22DE5378"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceuticals, processes and products"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Fengbin","key":"yefengbinpau","last":"Ye","locid":"980648a3-6e03-4240-868c-d93ea67c9371","name":"Ye, Fengbin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefania","key":"baldursdottirstefaniagpau","last":"Baldursdottir","locid":"3a65c5eb-19d2-43e1-a269-b0085edb0108","name":"Baldursdottir, Stefania G.","name_org":"Baldursdottir, Stefania","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"hvidtsørenpau","last":"Hvidt","locid":"cb3e146b-c69e-43ee-9e1f-2496db59cf37","name":"Hvidt, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"jensenhenrikpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"88cd8faf-69c6-46de-a355-03f93d52eeb1","name":"Jensen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susan W","key":"larsensusanwengpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f6980004-978f-4940-b71f-de426f2a084a","name":"Larsen, Susan Weng","name_org":"Larsen, Susan W","orcid":"0000-0002-3818-7275","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anan","key":"yaghmurananpau","last":"Yaghmur","locid":"a910866e-d3b9-4a69-b238-005ea9906b8f","name":"Yaghmur, Anan","orcid":"0000-0003-1608-773X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"larsenclausselchpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"38dcfe91-cef0-4a89-911b-30e3383ffdec","name":"Larsen, Claus Selch","name_org":"Larsen, Claus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardjesperpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26808484"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.molpharmaceut.5b00725","issn":["15438384","15438392"],"issn_org":["15438384"],"issue":"3","journal":"Molecular Pharmaceutics","pages":"820-828","status":"p","title":"Molecular Pharmaceutics","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960158282"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4c3a192e-1756-4655-9180-9bd6660b9e2a","ruc-27bd9530-2b64-4d6a-b687-c491444bedcb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Role of Electrostatic Interactions on the Transport of Druglike Molecules in Hydrogel-Based Articular Cartilage Mimics : Implications for Drug Delivery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.08-042218","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Metal oxide nanoparticles are used in a broad range of industrial processes and workers may be exposed to aerosols of the particles both during production and handling. Despite the widespread use of these particles, relatively few studies have been performed to investigate the toxicological effects in the airways following inhalation. In the present study, the acute (24 h) and persistent (13 weeks) effects in the airways after a single exposure to metal oxide nanoparticles were studied using a murine inhalation model. Mice were exposed 60 min to aerosols of either ZnO, TiO2, Al2O3 or CeO2 and the deposited doses in the upper and lower respiratory tracts were calculated. Endpoints were acute airway irritation, pulmonary inflammation based on analyses of bronchoalveolar lavage (BAL) cell composition, DNA damage assessed by the comet assay and pulmonary toxicity assessed by protein level in BAL fluid and histology. All studied particles reduced the tidal volume in a concentration-dependent manner accompanied with an increase in the respiratory rate. In addition, ZnO and TiO2 induced nasal irritation. BAL cell analyses revealed both neutrophilic and lymphocytic inflammation 24-h post-exposure to all particles except TiO2. The ranking of potency regarding induction of acute lung inflammation was Al2O3 = TiO2 < CeO2 ≪ ZnO. Exposure to CeO2 gave rise to a more persistent inflammation; both neutrophilic and lymphocytic inflammation was seen 13 weeks after exposure. As the only particles, ZnO caused a significant toxic effect in the airways while TiO2 gave rise to DNA-strand break as shown by the comet assay.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Søren T","Jackson, Petra","Poulsen, Steen Seier","Levin, Marcus","Jensen, Keld A","Wallin, Håkan","Nielsen, Gunnar D","Koponen, Ismo K."],"cuid":["S02-098.09-768814"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"airway irritation inflammation and toxicity in mice following inhalation of metal oxide nanoparticles","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17435390.2016.1202350","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.09-768814","identifier":[{"id":"84978646647","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27323801","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5020351","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-486ece3d-d16d-4f9a-8921-c9defed9bbe9","nfa-3983762b-0cb3-45de-955c-f8032d208336"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8D1F509CFB380D2CFCE707524C600C69"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17435390.2016.1202350","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/177384159/Airway_irritation_inflammation_and_toxicity_in_mice_following_inhalation_of_metal_oxide_nanoparticles.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Translational Metabolic Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Thor","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"32005edc-74a7-4ff2-a0ab-44b3d17409d6","name":"Larsen, Søren Thor","orcid":"0000-0003-1142-7045","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petra","key":"jacksonpau","last":"Jackson","locid":"0abaa90f-0899-49f0-8183-54d237c022a2","name":"Jackson, Petra","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steen S","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8959d81d-fe64-4ef4-86b7-003b7b637e8e","name":"Poulsen, Steen Seier","name_org":"Poulsen, Steen S","orcid":"0000-0003-4419-4911","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Henrik Marcus","key":"levinpau","last":"Levin","name":"Levin, Dan Henrik Marcus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Keld Alstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5b93ba18-9ef8-4419-8d4f-5b7c9634ba2f","name":"Jensen, Keld Alstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2764-3634","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Håkan Richard","key":"wallinpau","last":"Wallin","locid":"5acb38c3-e32b-433d-a6aa-b1a3a8d2adbf","name":"Wallin, Erik Håkan Richard","orcid":"0000-0001-7716-0166","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar Damgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Gunnar Damgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ismo Kalevi","key":"koponenpau","last":"Koponen","name":"Koponen, Ismo Kalevi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27323801"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17435390.2016.1202350","issn":["17435390","17435404"],"issn_org":["17435390"],"issue":"9","journal":"Nanotoxicology","pages":"1254-1262","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Nanotoxicology","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978646647"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-486ece3d-d16d-4f9a-8921-c9defed9bbe9","nfa-3983762b-0cb3-45de-955c-f8032d208336"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Airway irritation, inflammation, and toxicity in mice following inhalation of metal oxide nanoparticles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.09-768814","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The purpose of this study was to identify subgroups of breast cancer patients and their partners based on distinct trajectories of depressive symptoms, to examine how relationship quality and medical and sociodemographic factors were associated with these trajectories, and to explore whether patients and partners had similar trajectories. METHODS: A nationwide, population-based cohort of couples dealing with breast cancer was established in Denmark. Participants completed the Center for Epidemiologic Studies-Depression Scale at baseline and 5 and 12 months later. Sociodemographic and medical characteristics were retrieved from registers. A trajectory finite mixture model was used to identify trajectories. RESULTS: The trajectories of depressive symptoms over time were analyzed in 546 patients and 508 partners. Among patients, 13 % had a high stable trajectory, 38 % an intermediate decreasing trajectory, and 49 % a low trajectory. Similar trajectories were found for partners (11, 22, and 67 %, respectively). Compared to the low trajectory, trajectories with higher depressive symptoms were associated with poorer relationship quality and previous use of antidepressants for patients and partners and with younger age, comorbidity, basic education, and chemotherapy for patients. The trajectories of patients and their partners were weakly correlated. CONCLUSIONS: A considerable minority of patients and partners had a persistently high level of depressive symptoms. Poorer relationship quality and previous antidepressant use most consistently characterized patients and partners with higher depressive symptom trajectories. IMPLICATIONS FOR CANCER SURVIVORS: In clinical practice, attention to differences in depressive symptom trajectories is important to identify and target patients and partners who might need support.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rottmann, Nina","Hansen, Dorte Gilså","Hagedoorn, Mariët","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Nicolaisen, Anne","Bidstrup, Pernille Envold","Würtzen, Hanne","Flyger, Henrik","Kroman, Niels","Johansen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S02-099.04-040811"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"depressive symptom trajectories in women affected by breast cancer and their male partners a nationwide prospective cohort study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963741615","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.04-040811","identifier":[{"id":"84963741615","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27084710","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2233a60e-ff10-4655-b057-3b3371ac4a1d","sdu-da233dea-4259-4576-947a-d5941a5aea6f"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2FDC8F279AB5E54037E3A583E34F1FFA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, Eksistentiel og humanistisk forskning","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, INSIDE","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nina","key":"rottmannpau","last":"Rottmann","locid":"16e7c8cc-cee3-43aa-8651-e2a1414f2426","name":"Rottmann, Nina","orcid":"0000-0002-7262-6788","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Gilså","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2826791-eb97-4bca-8af7-448b0940e6e5","name":"Hansen, Dorte Gilså","orcid":"0000-0002-5946-9968","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mariët","key":"hagedoornpau","last":"Hagedoorn","name":"Hagedoorn, Mariët","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Veldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"nicolaisenpau","last":"Nicolaisen","locid":"1c1d730b-acab-4f96-a824-90f2fcb3017d","name":"Nicolaisen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-5696-7144","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pernille Envold","key":"bidstruppau","last":"Bidstrup","name":"Bidstrup, Pernille Envold","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne","key":"würtzenpau","last":"Würtzen","name":"Würtzen, Hanne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"flygerpau","last":"Flyger","name":"Flyger, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels","key":"kromanpau","last":"Kroman","locid":"e120d8b8-6f8e-4b09-a51f-4eca94999f55","name":"Kroman, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-6631-2993","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"18d62c73-2f35-499d-ac94-134ecd806296","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27084710"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11764-016-0538-3","issn":["19322259","19322267"],"issn_org":["19322259"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Cancer Survivorship","pages":"915-926","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cancer Survivorship","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963741615"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2233a60e-ff10-4655-b057-3b3371ac4a1d","sdu-da233dea-4259-4576-947a-d5941a5aea6f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Depressive symptom trajectories in women affected by breast cancer and their male partners : A nationwide prospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.04-040811","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The human serotonin transporter is the primary target of several antidepressant drugs, and the importance of a primary, high affinity binding site (S1) for antidepressant binding is well documented. The existence of a lower affinity, secondary binding site (S2) has, however, been debated. Herein we report the synthesis of 3-position coupled imipramine ligands from clomipramine using a copper free Sonogashira reaction. Ligand design was inspired by results from docking and steered molecular dynamics simulations, and the ligands were utilized in a structure-activity relationship study of the positional relationship between the S1 and S2 sites. The computer simulations suggested that the S2 site does indeed exist although with lower affinity for imipramine than observed within the S1 site. Additionally, it was possible to dock the 3-linked imipramine analogs into positions which occupy the S1 and the S2 site simultaneously. The structure activity relationship study showed that the shortest ligands were the most potent, and mutations enlarging the proposed S2 site were found to affect the larger ligands positively, while the smaller ligands were mostly unaffected.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Brinkø, Anne","Larsen, Maja Thim","Koldsø, Heidi","Besenbacher, Louise Morck","Kolind, Anders","Schiøtt, Birgit","Sinning, Steffen","Jensen, Henrik Helligsø"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-209256"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antidepressants","Depression","Serotonin","Sonogashira coupling","Transporter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthesis and inhibitory evaluation of 000000000003 linked imipramines for the exploration of the s000000000002 site of the human serotonin transporter","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bmc.2016.04.039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-209256","identifier":[{"id":"27160055","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84965000197","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8c17f38f-9025-420b-8938-791ed2d96b0e"],"keyword":["Antidepressants","Bivalent ligands","Depression","Serotonin","Sonogashira coupling","Transporter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86AD70C131E129C8381EE1DF36AC5F8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bmc.2016.04.039","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/100299356/1_s2.0_S0968089616302826_main.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"brinkøpau","last":"Brinkø","locid":"b6dd5da0-7eb1-4564-aade-624cdc9c64d5","name":"Brinkø, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Thim","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6193b02f-9d19-47db-b0d9-6adc4cc660c8","name":"Larsen, Maja Thim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heidi","key":"koldsøpau","last":"Koldsø","locid":"2ea209b6-134a-4a12-b21e-c554e69089ea","name":"Koldsø, Heidi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Morck","key":"besenbacherpau","last":"Besenbacher","locid":"bd723396-7a59-44a6-8950-73434362f700","name":"Besenbacher, Louise Morck","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"kolindpau","last":"Kolind","name":"Kolind, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"schiøttpau","last":"Schiøtt","locid":"27c1af35-c8f3-471f-a448-02fd2fbd18bf","name":"Schiøtt, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0001-9937-1562","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen","key":"sinningpau","last":"Sinning","locid":"f013fd4e-77bb-4d7e-b247-adecd127ec67","name":"Sinning, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0001-6971-6929","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Helligsø","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"877378e2-5b43-446a-87c2-cc8353cc42f3","name":"Jensen, Henrik Helligsø","orcid":"0000-0003-2738-4502","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27160055"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bmc.2016.04.039","issn":["09680896","14643391"],"issn_org":["09680896"],"issue":"12","journal":"Bioorganic & Medicinal Chemistry","pages":"2725-2738","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Bioorganic & Medicinal Chemistry","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84965000197"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8c17f38f-9025-420b-8938-791ed2d96b0e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Synthesis and inhibitory evaluation of 3-linked imipramines for the exploration of the S2 site of the human serotonin transporter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-209256","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Orphan receptor NURR1 (also termed NR4A2) belongs to the nuclear receptor superfamily and functions as a regulatory factor of differentiation, migration, maturation and maintenance of mesencephalic dopaminergic neurons. NURR1 plays an important role in nigrostriatal dopamine neuron development and is therefore implicated in the pathogenesis of neurodegenerative diseases linked to the dopamine system of the midbrain. Here we report the isolation and characterization of porcine NURR1 cDNA. The NURR1 cDNA was RT-PCR cloned using NURR1-specific oligonucleotide primers derived from in silico sequences. The porcine NURR1 cDNA encodes a polypeptide of 598 amino acids, displaying a very high similarity with bovine, human and mouse (99%) NURR1 protein. Expression analysis revealed a differential NURR1 mRNA expression in various organs and tissues. NURR1 transcripts could be detected as early as at 60 days of embryo development in different brain tissues. A significant increase in NURR1 transcript in the cerebellum and a decrease in NURR1 transcript in the basal ganglia was observed during embryo development. The porcine NURR1 gene was mapped to chromosome 15. Two missense mutations were found in exon 3, the first coding exon of NURR1. Methylation analysis of the porcine NURR1 gene body revealed a high methylation degree in brain tissue, whereas methylation of the promoter was very low. A decrease in DNA methylation in a discrete region of the NURR1 promoter was observed in pig frontal cortex during pig embryo development. This observation correlated with an increase in NURR1 transcripts. Therefore, methylation might be a determinant of NURR1 expression at certain time points in embryo development.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Knud Erik","Momeni, Jamal","Farajzadeh, Leila","Callesen, Henrik","Bendixen, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-256413"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DNA methylation","Parkinson s disease","Pig","SNP","Transcription factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular characterization and analysis of the porcine nurr000000000001 gene","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84981489618","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-256413","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5801910","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84981489618","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29450128","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-de9d541c-6f9a-4ab4-9fd0-ffcec5b997cc"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","NURR1","Parkinson's disease","Pig","SNP","Transcription factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-19DE19A880B91E4F8CE81C3C09224CA9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Genetics and Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46cd3e98-1529-45bf-9054-2978f328044c","name":"Larsen, Knud Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jamal","key":"momenipau","last":"Momeni","locid":"ea915fbe-97e0-4485-83f1-c5a356866ce7","name":"Momeni, Jamal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leila","key":"farajzadehpau","last":"Farajzadeh","locid":"f3a29052-305e-4352-8a70-c4eeecf24cf3","name":"Farajzadeh, Leila","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","locid":"7fe33188-4ec4-4b54-bc7a-c922c5ebaa54","name":"Callesen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0185-7300","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"bendixenpau","last":"Bendixen","locid":"527e8fa7-a9e1-4eac-a0bf-c84d3d2f9655","name":"Bendixen, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29450128"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biopen.2016.07.001","issn":["03009084","16386183"],"issn_org":["03009084"],"journal":"Biochimie","pages":"26-39","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Biochimie","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84981489618"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-de9d541c-6f9a-4ab4-9fd0-ffcec5b997cc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Molecular characterization and analysis of the porcine NURR1 gene","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-256413","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (D-DNP) has become a method of choice to enhance signals in nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR). Recently, we have proposed to combine cross-polarization (CP) with D-DNP to provide high polarization P((13)C) in short build-up times. In this paper, we show that switching microwave irradiation off for a few hundreds of milliseconds prior to CP can significantly boost the efficiency. By implementing microwave gating, (13)C polarizations on sodium [1-(13)C]acetate as high as 64% could be achieved with a polarization build-up time constant as short as 160 s. A polarization of P((13)C) = 78% could even be reached for [(13)C]urea.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bornet, Aurélien","Pinon, Arthur","Jhajharia, Aditya","Baudin, Mathieu","Ji, Xiao","Emsley, Lyndon","Bodenhausen, Geoffrey","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Jannin, Sami"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327212"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sorbonne Université","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microwave gated dynamic nuclear polarization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132996965/uWGated_DNP_210916.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327212","identifier":[{"id":"27782260","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-4c1f7ef4-b0e2-430d-81f6-77b1b73c656c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-553590302D5BBCF7EF8D61929B36D87D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132996965/uWGated_DNP_210916.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"sorbonne université","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sorbonne Université","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Automation","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aurélien","key":"bornetpau","last":"Bornet","name":"Bornet, Aurélien","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arthur","key":"pinonpau","last":"Pinon","name":"Pinon, Arthur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aditya","key":"jhajhariapau","last":"Jhajharia","name":"Jhajharia, Aditya","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathieu","key":"baudinpau","last":"Baudin","name":"Baudin, Mathieu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"jipau","last":"Ji","name":"Ji, Xiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lyndon","key":"emsleypau","last":"Emsley","name":"Emsley, Lyndon","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Geoffrey","key":"bodenhausenpau","last":"Bodenhausen","name":"Bodenhausen, Geoffrey","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami","key":"janninpau","last":"Jannin","name":"Jannin, Sami","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27782260"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c6cp05587g","issn":["14639076","14639084"],"issn_org":["14639076"],"journal":"Physical Chemistry Chemical Physics","pages":"30530-30535","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Physical Chemistry Chemical Physics","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4c1f7ef4-b0e2-430d-81f6-77b1b73c656c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Microwave-gated dynamic nuclear polarization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327212","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Loads from extreme waves can be dimensioning for the substructures of offshore wind turbines. The DeRisk project (2015-2019) aims at an improved load evaluation procedure for extreme waves through application of advanced wave models, laboratory tests of load effects, development of hydrodynamic load models, aero-elastic response calculations and statistical analysis. This first paper from the project outlines the content and philosophy behind DeRisk. Next, the first results from laboratory tests with irregular waves are presented, including results for 2D and 3D focused wave groups. The results of focused wave group tests and a 6-hour (full scale duration) test are reproduced numerically by re-application of the wave paddle signal in a fully nonlinear potential flow wave model. A good match for the free surface elevation and associated exceedance probability curve is obtained. Finally, the utilization of DeRisk's results in practical design is discussed. (C) 2016 Published by Elsevier Ltd.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Bredmose, Henrik","Dixen, Martin","Ghadirian, Amin","Larsen, Torben J.","Schløer, Signe","Andersen, Søren Juhl","Wang, Shaofeng","Bingham, Harry B.","Lindberg, Ole","Christensen, Erik Damgaard","Vested, Malene Hovgaard","Carstensen, Stefan","Engsig-Karup, Allan Peter","Petersen, Ole Skov","Hansen, H. F.","Mariegaard, Jesper Sandvig","Taylor, P. H.","Adcock, T. A. A.","Obhrai, C.","Gudmestad, O. T.","Tarp-Johansen, Niels Jacob","Meyer, C. P.","Krokstad, J. R.","Suja-Thauvin, L.","Hanson, T. D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-366367"],"event":{"end":"2016-01-22","place":"Trondheim, no","start":"2016-01-20","title":"13th Deep Sea Offshore Wind R&amp;D Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Equinor ASA","Statkraft AS","University of O