Lars Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rogerio Pessoto","key":"hiratapau","last":"Hirata","locid":"a8f714d2-931d-4b16-a957-38bd1b321fe6","name":"Hirata, Rogerio Pessoto","orcid":"0000-0002-9943-2713","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"gravennielsenpau","last":"Graven-Nielsen","locid":"474a635b-4e83-4b02-a90b-80d417d37e52","name":"Graven-Nielsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7787-4860","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-17a81d89-76c6-4fb3-947d-414b509e04d1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Effects of unilateral and bilateral experimental low-back pain on trunk muscle activity during stair walking in healthy and recurrent low-back pain patients","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-057000","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Staphylococcus aureus gene expression has been sparsely studied in deep-sited infections in humans. Here, we characterized the staphylococcal transcriptome in vivo and the joint fluid metabolome in a prosthetic joint infection with an acute presentation using deep RNA sequencing and nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy, respectively. We compared our findings with the genome, transcriptome and metabolome of the S. aureus joint fluid isolate grown in vitro. RESULT: From the transcriptome analysis we found increased expression of siderophore synthesis genes and multiple known virulence genes. The regulatory pattern of catabolic pathway genes indicated that the bacterial infection was sustained on amino acids, glycans and nucleosides. Upregulation of fermentation genes and the presence of ethanol in joint fluid indicated severe oxygen limitation in vivo. CONCLUSION: This single case study highlights the capacity of combined transcriptome and metabolome analyses for elucidating the pathogenesis of prosthetic infections of major clinical importance.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Xu, Yijuan","Maltesen, Raluca","Larsen, Lone Heimann","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Le, Vang","Nielsen, Jeppe Lund","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Thomsen, Trine Rolighed","Nielsen, Kåre Lehmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-062486"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo gene expression in a staphylococcus aureus prosthetic joint infection characterized by rna sequencing and metabolomics a pilot study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12866-016-0695-6","version":"Published Version"},"id