{"abstract":"Network alignment is a challenging computational problem that identifies node or edge mappings between two or more networks, with the aim to unravel common patterns among them. Pairwise network alignment is already intractable, making multiple network comparison even more difficult. Here, we introduce a heuristic algorithm for the multiple maximum common edge subgraph problem that is able to detect large common substructures shared across multiple, real-world size networks efficiently. Our algorithm uses a combination of iterated local search, simulated annealing and a pheromone-based perturbation strategy. We implemented multiple local search strategies and annealing schedules, that were evaluated on a range of synthetic networks and real protein-protein interaction networks. Our method is parallelized and well-suited to exploit current multi-core CPU architectures. While it is generic, we apply it to unravel a biochemical backbone inherent in different species, modeled as multiple maximum common subgraphs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Simon J.","Alkærsig, Frederik G.","Ditzel, Henrik","Jurisica, Igor","Alcaraz, Nicolas","Baumbach, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-578652"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","end":"2016-07-24","place":"Denver, us","start":"2016-07-20","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Princess Margaret Cancer Centre","University of Toronto"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Ant colony optimization","Bioinformatics","Graph algorithms","Heuristics","Local search","Network alignment","Networks","Simulated annealing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a simulated annealing algorithm for maximum common edge subgraph detection in biological networks","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84985919788","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-578652","identifier":[{"id":"84985919788","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1325b414-fe61-4e78-9721-614164ded8b0"],"keyword":["Ant colony optimization","Graph algorithms","Heuristics","Local search","Network alignment","Simulated annealing","algorithms","bioinformatics","networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D81B99894E4CB7A458A92FFABF09348C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"princess margaret cancer centre","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Princess Margaret Cancer Centre","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6a743e09-98a6-4bab-887a-bbcb080c5d06","name":"Larsen, Simon J.","name_org":"Larsen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-8076-5035","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frederik G.","key":"alkærsigpau","last":"Alkærsig","locid":"b27c659f-7927-4cb3-831e-cb0a25c9ec3e","name":"Alkærsig, Frederik G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pa