 Asbjørn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"asbjørnneergaardpedh","last":"Asbjørn Neergaard","name":"Asbjørn Neergaard, Mette","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788762812260"],"pages":"33-50","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","series":"Kliniske lærebøger","status":"p","title":"Palliativ medicin - en lærebog"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-de7668d6-4f8e-4601-9abf-382fa21827ef"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Organisering af den palliative indsats i Danmark","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526338","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In recent years there has been an immense development of new targeted anti-cancer drugs. For practicing precision medicine, a sensitive method imaging for non-invasive, assessment of early treatment response and for assisting in developing new drugs is warranted. Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy (MRS) is a potent technique for non-invasive in vivo investigation of tissue chemistry and cellular metabolism. Hyperpolarization by Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (DNP) is capable of creating solutions of molecules with polarized nuclear spins in a range of biological molecules and has enabled the real-time investigation of in vivo metabolism. The development of this new method has been demonstrated to enhance the nuclear polarization more than 10,000-fold, thereby significantly increasing the sensitivity of the MRS with a spatial resolution to the millimeters and a temporal resolution at the subsecond range. Furthermore, the method enables measuring kinetics of conversion of substrates into cell metabolites and can be integrated with anatomical proton magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Many nuclei and substrates have been hyperpolarized using the DNP method. Currently, the most widely used compound is 13C-pyruvate due to favoring technicalities. Intravenous injection of the hyperpolarized 13C-pyruvate results in appearance of 13C-lactate, 13C-alanine and 13C-bicarbonate resonance peaks depending on the tissue, disease and the metabolic state probed. In cancer, the lactate level is increased due to increased glycolysis. The use of DNP enhanced 13C-pyruvate has in preclinical studies shown to be a sensitive method for detecting cancer and for assessment of early treatment response in a variety of cancers. Recently, a first-in-man 31-patient study was conducted with the primary objective to assess the safety of hyperpolarized 13C-pyruvate in healthy subjects and prostate cancer patients. The study showed an elevated 13C-lactate/13C-pyruvate ratio in regions of biopsy-proven prostate cancer compared to noncancerous tissue. However, more studies are needed in order to establish use of hyperpolarized 13C MRS imaging of cancer.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Borgwardt, Henrik Gutte","Hansen, Adam Espe","Johannesen, Helle Hjorth","Clemmensen, Andreas","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Kjaer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-534806"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the use of dynamic nuclear polarization sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate mrs in cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ajnmmi.us/ajnmmi_V5N5.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-534806","identifier":[{"id":"26550544","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-eccd05c0-b333-4ddf-90a0-22180e2e6f10"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-C01691BCA79362151BDA8257C00B7D8A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ajnmmi.us/ajnmmi_V5N5.html","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ajnmmi.us/files/ajnmmi0010834.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Gutte","key":"borgwardtpau","last":"Borgwardt","locid":"c7c7ba68-3373-4d28-9c52-1df481849fb7","name":"Borgwardt, Henrik Gutte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam","key":"espehansenpau","last":"Espe Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Espe Hansen, Adam","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle","key":"hjortjohannesenpau","last":"Hjort Johannesen","locid":"ead1439c-87ec-4797-b428-4cc80b58f663","name":"Johannesen, Helle Hjorth","name_org":"Hjort Johannesen, Helle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas Ettrup","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"5f1471f7-ae5b-4864-bdab-f57d5e4b8566","name":"Clemmensen, Andreas","name_org":"Clemmensen, Andreas Ettrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"haagennielsenpau","last":"Haagen Nielsen","locid":"aefb223a-8c5c-41c6-9e69-fade0a04bf90","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","name_org":"Haagen Nielsen, Carsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","name_org":"Kjær, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26550544"],"pub":{"issn":["21608407"],"issue":"5","journal":"American Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"548-560","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-eccd05c0-b333-4ddf-90a0-22180e2e6f10"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The use of dynamic nuclear polarization <sup>13</sup>C-pyruvate MRS in cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-534806","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We aimed to assess the relative contribution of genes and environment in the aetiology of Dupuytren's disease by studying Danish twins born between 1870 and 2000. Twins with a diagnosis (n = 365) and the subgroup who also had an operation (n = 259) after 1977 were identified through linkage with a nationwide hospital registry among 30,330 monozygotic and same-sexed dizygotic twin pairs. Since monozygotic twins share all their genes and dizygotic twins share on average half of their genetic material, greater phenotypic similarity is expected in monozygotic than in dizygotic twins if a genetic component is involved. The number of concordant male twin pairs with Dupuytren's disease was 17 and 7 (monozygotic and dizygotic pairs, respectively), compared with 60 and 174 discordant monozygotic and dizygotic pairs, yielding probandwise concordance rates of 0.37 (95% confidence interval (CI): 0.26 to 0.50) and 0.07 (95% CI: 0.04 to 0.14), respectively. The heritability of Dupuytren's disease was approximately 80%. We conclude that genetic factors play a major role in the development of Dupuytren's disease.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Søren","Krogsgaard, D G","Larsen, Lisbeth Aagaard","Iachina, Maria","Skytthe, Axel","Frederiksen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-588769"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dupuytren s disease","Genetic","Hereditary","Twin study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic and environmental influences in dupuytren s disease a study of 000000000030 000000000330 danish twin pairs","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1753193414535720","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-588769","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4810018","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24835475","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84921636197","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3674b656-b35c-4bc0-bdd0-44dff9ef6252"],"keyword":["Dupuytren's disease","Genetic","Hereditary","Twin study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6066D508601D7ED32D26D30830DD5C93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1753193414535720","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"larsensørenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"df2018cb-4f10-45a5-9547-0153300e96c5","name":"Larsen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D G","key":"krogsgaarddgpau","last":"Krogsgaard","name":"Krogsgaard, D G","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lisbeth Aagaard","key":"larsenlisbethaagaardpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"34281bd8-ae16-4a86-bd14-0ca8d46f1892","name":"Larsen, Lisbeth Aagaard","orcid":"0000