{"abstract":"In this communication the mismatch between simultaneous (18)F-FDG-PET and a (13)C-lactate imaging (hyperPET) in a biopsy verified squamous cell carcinoma in the right tonsil of a canine cancer patient is shown. The results demonstrate that (18)F-FDG-PET may not always reflect the Warburg effect in all tumors.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gutte, Henrik","Hansen, Adam E","Larsen, Majbrit M E","Rahbek, Sofie","Johannesen, Helle H","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Kristensen, Annemarie T","Højgaard, Liselotte","Kjær, Andreas"],"cuid":["S02-091.98-033587"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["13C pyruvate","18F FDG PET","Cancer","Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarized","MR","Molecular imaging","PET MR","hyperPET"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i in vivo i phenotyping of tumor metabolism in a canine cancer patient with simultaneous sup 000000000018 sup f fdg pet and hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate magnetic resonance spectroscopic imaging hyperpet mismatch demonstrates that fdg may not always reflect the warburg effect","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics5030287","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.98-033587","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4665599","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26854154","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85013438220","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2d825eea-631e-40fd-bee9-bfde7287557e","ku-e5184164-2595-4b68-8df8-473b4940e075"],"keyword":["13C-pyruvate","18F-FDG-PET","Cancer","Dynamic nuclear polarization","HyperPET","Hyperpolarized","MR","Molecular imaging","PET/MR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-16769FA0C2C971DA228656D7ECF393A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/121693054/diagnostics_05_00287.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/162712023/In_Vivo_phenotyping_of_tumor_metabolism_in_a_canine_cancer_patient.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics5030287","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Hyperpolarization in Magnetic Resonance","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Gutte","key":"borgwardtpau","last":"Borgwardt","locid":"c7c7ba68-3373-4d28-9c52-1df481849fb7","name":"Borgwardt, Henrik Gutte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Adam Espe","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Majbritt Maria","key":"estruplarsenpau","last":"Estrup Larsen","name":"Estrup Larsen, Majbritt Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sofie","key":"rahbekpau","last":"Rahbek","name":"Rahbek, Sofie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle Hjorth","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Helle Hjorth","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Annemarie Thuri","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a7007b3a-f743-46be-8a05-6473fd440756","name":"Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Liselotte","key":"højgaardpau","last":"Højgaard","locid":"fc298245-aff6-430a-bb2e-5ea4eb85604c","name":"Højgaard, Liselotte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","name_org":"Kjær, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26854154"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/diagnostics5030287","issn":["20754418"],"issue":"3","journal":"Diagnostics","pages":"287-289","publisher":"MDPI AG","status":"p","title":"Diagnostics","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013438220"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2d825eea-631e-40fd-bee9-bfde7287557e","ku-e5184164-2595-4b68-8df8-473b4940e075"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"In Vivo Phenotyping of Tumor Metabolism in a Canine Cancer Patient with Simultaneous (18)F-FDG-PET and Hyperpolarized (13)C-Pyruvate Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopic Imaging (hyperPET): Mismatch Demonstrates that FDG may not Always Reflect the Warburg Effect","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.98-033587","year":"2015","yearsub":2016}
{"abstract":"With the introduction of combined PET/MR spectroscopic (MRS) imaging, it is now possible to directly and indirectly image the Warburg effect with hyperpolarized (13)C-pyruvate and (18)F-FDG PET imaging, respectively, via a technique we have named hyperPET. The main purpose of this present study was to establish a practical workflow for performing (18)F-FDG PET and hyperpolarized (13)C-pyruvate MRS imaging simultaneously for tumor tissue characterization and on a larger scale test its feasibility. In addition, we evaluated the correlation between (18)F-FDG uptake and (13)C-lactate production. METHODS: Ten dogs with biopsy-verified spontaneous malignant tumors were included for imaging. All dogs underwent a protocol of simultaneous (18)F-FDG PET, anatomic MR, and hyperpolarized dynamic nuclear polarization with (13)C-pyruvate imaging. The data were acquired using a combined clinical PET/MR imaging scanner. RESULTS: We found that combined (18)F-FDG PET and (13)C-pyruvate MRS imaging was possible in a single session of approximately 2 h. A continuous workflow was obtained with the injection of (18)F-FDG when the dogs was placed in the PET/MR scanner. (13)C-MRS dynamic acquisition demonstrated in an axial slab increased (13)C-lactate production in 9 of 10 dogs. For the 9 dogs, the (13)C-lactate was detected after a mean of 25 s (range, 17-33 s), with a mean to peak of (13)C-lactate at 49 s (range, 40-62 s). (13)C-pyruvate could be detected on average after 13 s (range, 5-26 s) and peaked on average after 25 s (range, 13-42 s). We noticed concordance of (18)F-FDG uptake and production of (13)C-lactate in most, but not all, axial slices. CONCLUSION: In this study, we have shown in a series of dogs with cancer that hyperPET can easily be performed within 2 h. We showed mostly correspondence between (13)C-lactate production and (18)F-FDG uptake and expect the combined modalities to reveal additional metabolic information to improve prognostic value and improve response monitoring.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gutte, Henrik","Hansen, Adam E","Larsen, Majbrit M E","Rahbek, Sofie","Henriksen, Sarah T","Johannesen, Helle H","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Kristensen, Annemarie T","Højgaard, Liselotte","Kjær, Andreas"],"cuid":["S02-097.54-035295"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["13C pyruvate","18F FDG PET","Cancer","Dynamic nuclear polarization","Hyperpolarized","MR","Molecular imaging","PET MR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simultaneous hyperpolarized sup 000000000013 sup c pyruvate mri and sup 000000000018 sup f fdg pet hyperpet in 000000000010 dogs with cancer","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84946593720","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.54-035295","identifier":[{"id":"84946593720","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26338899","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-75e82e67-0203-4060-ac9c-1ce10990c2db","ku-13602fcb-2429-41ab-a54f-840d1dde46b0"],"keyword":["13C-pyruvate","18F-FDG PET","MR","PET/MR","cancer","dynamic nuclear polarization","hyperpolarized","molecular imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-535822C66761C9E0C5AD5A313A30DEFF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Gutte","key":"borgwardtpau","last":"Borgwardt","locid":"c7c7ba68-3373-4d28-9c52-1df481849fb7","name":"Borgwardt, Henrik Gutte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Adam Espe","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Majbrit M. E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Majbrit M. E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sofie","key":"rahbekpau","last":"Rahbek","name":"Rahbek, Sofie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle Hjorth","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","locid":"ead1439c-87ec-4797-b428-4cc80b58f663","name":"Johannesen, Helle Hjorth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Annemarie Thuri","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a7007b3a-f743-46be-8a05-6473fd440756","name":"Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Liselotte","key":"højgaardpau","last":"Højgaard","locid":"fc298245-aff6-430a-bb2e-5ea4eb85604c","name":"Højgaard, Liselotte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","name_org":"Kjær, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26338899"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2967/jnumed.115.156364","issn":["01615505","15355667"],"issn_org":["01615505"],"issue":"11","journal":"The Journal of Nuclear Medicine","pages":"1786-92","publisher":"Society of Nuclear Medicine Inc.","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Nuclear Medicine","title_org":"Journal of Nuclear Medicine","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84946593720"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-75e82e67-0203-4060-ac9c-1ce10990c2db","ku-13602fcb-2429-41ab-a54f-840d1dde46b0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simultaneous Hyperpolarized 13C-Pyruvate MRI and 18F-FDG PET (HyperPET) in 10 Dogs with Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.54-035295","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"During the last 17 years, considerable advancements have been achieved in the production of pigs, transgenic and non-transgenic, by methods of somatic cell nuclear transfer, in vitro fertilisation, intracytoplasmic sperm injection, microinjection and sperm-mediated gene transfer by artificial insemination. Therefore, a review of the overall efficiency for the developmental competence of embryos produced by these in vitro methods would be useful in order to obtain a more thorough overview of this growing area with respect to its development and present status. In this review a meta-analysis was used to analyse data collected from all published articles with a focus on zygotes and embryos for transfer, pregnancy, full-term development and piglets born. It was generally concluded that an increasing level of in vitro manipulation of porcine embryos decreased the overall efficiency for production of piglets. The techniques of nuclear transfer have been developed markedly through the increasing number of studies performed, and the results have become more stable. Prolonged in vitro culture period did not lead to any negative effect on nuclear transfer embryos after their transfer and it resulted in a similar or even higher litter size. More complete information is needed in future scientific articles about these in vitro manipulation techniques to establish a more solid basis for the evaluation of their status and to reveal and further investigate any eventual problems","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liu, Ying","Li, Juan","Løvendahl, Peter","Schmidt, Mette","Larsen, Knud Erik","Callesen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-022327"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vitro manipulation techniques of porcine embryos a meta analysis related to transfers pregnancies and piglets","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1071/RD13329","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-022327","identifier":[{"id":"25482653","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84924814331","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-848b3fed-f02d-40cf-9a18-ce4b3aaa0e6a","ku-b7e2bac3-cab6-4946-9688-131d46d7be35"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-94FC7B38F782C1564DD0936A76642E2A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1071/RD13329","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Reproductive Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Husdyrvidenskab - Forplantningsbiologi"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Section for Veterinary Reproduction and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"4d0cfc77-a33e-41e0-b0e6-5bc7f148222a","name":"Liu, Ying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"cf549557-d235-4834-af88-c301ce2b633c","name":"Li, Juan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"løvendahlpau","last":"Løvendahl","locid":"d1d68047-88cc-43f8-93ed-04e289ca5b38","name":"Løvendahl, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Mette","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"82963f6a-a967-4928-9c4f-1ba8093d382e","name":"Schmidt, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46cd3e98-1529-45bf-9054-2978f328044c","name":"Larsen, Knud Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","locid":"7fe33188-4ec4-4b54-bc7a-c922c5ebaa54","name":"Callesen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0185-7300","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25482653"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1071/rd13329","issn":["10313613","14485990"],"issn_org":["10313613"],"journal":"Reproduction, Fertility and Development","pages":"429-439","publisher":"CSIRO Publishing","status":"p","title":"Reproduction, Fertility and Development","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924814331"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-848b3fed-f02d-40cf-9a18-ce4b3aaa0e6a","ku-b7e2bac3-cab6-4946-9688-131d46d7be35"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"In vitro manipulation techniques of porcine embryos: a meta-analysis related to transfers, pregnancies and piglets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-022327","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: In clinical practice, joint kinematics during running are primarily quantified by two-dimensional (2D) video recordings and motion-analysis software. The applicability of this approach depends on the clinicians' ability to quantify kinematics in a reliable manner. The reliability of quantifying knee- and hip angles at foot strike is uninvestigated. OBJECTIVE: To investigate the intra- and inter-rater reliability within and between days of clinicians' ability to quantify the knee- and hip angles at foot strike during running. METHODS: Eighteen recreational runners were recorded twice using a clinical 2D video setup during treadmill running. Two blinded raters quantified joint angles on each video twice with freeware motion analysis software (Kinovea 0.8.15). RESULTS: The range from the lower prediction limit to the upper prediction limit of the 95% prediction interval varied three to eight degrees (within day) and nine to 14 degrees (between day) for the knee angles. Similarly, the hip angles varied three to seven degrees (within day) and nine to 11 degrees (between day). CONCLUSION: The intra- and inter rater reliability of within and between day quantifications of the knee- and hip angle based on a clinical 2D video setup is sufficient to encourage clinicians to keep using 2D motion analysis techniques in clinical practice to quantify the knee- and hip angles in healthy runners. However, the interpretation should include critical evaluation of the physical set-up of the 2D motion analysis system prior to the recordings and conclusions should take measurement variations (3-8 degrees and 9-14 degrees for within and between day, respectively) into account. LEVEL OF EVIDENCE: 3.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Damsted, Camma","Nielsen, Rasmus Oestergaard","Larsen, Lars Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-095.46-020922"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Kinematics","Physiotherapy","Reliability","Running"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reliability of video based quantification of the knee and hip angle at foot strike during running","src":["au","sdu","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4387722/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-095.46-020922","identifier":[{"id":"25883863","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4387722","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-70c33d8d-a058-4df9-b7cf-dd4e7a6c3a16","sdu-ef21934a-80d1-44a9-8fd9-e5648c314f69","ucn-493b62b9-c5f3-453f-9c64-a953168066b0"],"keyword":["kinematics","knee- and hip angles","motion-analysis software","physiotherapy","reliability","running"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4B4E08B0C34919141BD1FD06482834E3"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Musculoskeletal Function and Physiotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Sport Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camma","key":"damstedpau","last":"Damsted","locid":"0f094006-2170-42ea-b2ca-2f40fb0be18a","name":"Damsted, Camma","orcid":"0000-0002-4627-1338","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R.O.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2d1ea8cb-28f5-48df-baa8-9724c2e17005","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus Oestergaard","name_org":"Nielsen, R.O.","orcid":"0000-0001-5757-1806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a997ad4d-e8d1-47b2-8b96-d5b9b748e4c5","name":"Larsen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7830-1186","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25883863"],"pub":{"issn":["15586162","21592896"],"issn_org":["21592896"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","pages":"147-154","publisher":"American Physical Therapy Association, Sports Physical Therapy Section","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70c33d8d-a058-4df9-b7cf-dd4e7a6c3a16","sdu-ef21934a-80d1-44a9-8fd9-e5648c314f69","ucn-493b62b9-c5f3-453f-9c64-a953168066b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Reliability of video-based quantification of the knee- and hip angle at foot strike during running","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.46-020922","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Although deliberate self-harm is a strong predictor of suicide, evidence for effective interventions is missing. The aim of this study was to examine whether psychosocial therapy after self-harm was linked to lower risks of repeated self-harm, suicide, and general mortality. METHODS: In this matched cohort study all people who, after deliberate self-harm, received a psychosocial therapy intervention at suicide prevention clinics in Denmark during 1992-2010 were compared with people who did not receive the psychosocial therapy intervention after deliberate self-harm. We applied propensity score matching with a 1:3 ratio and 31 matching factors, and calculated odds ratios for 1, 5, 10, and 20 years of follow-up. The primary endpoints were repeated self-harm, death by suicide, and death by any cause. FINDINGS: 5678 recipients of psychosocial therapy (followed up for 42·828 person-years) were matched with 17,034 individuals with no psychosocial therapy in a 1:8 ratio. During 20 year follow-up, 937 (16·5%) recipients of psychosocial therapy repeated the act of self-harm, and 391 (6·9%) died, 93 (16%) by suicide. The psychosocial therapy intervention was linked to lower risks of self-harm than was no psychosocial therapy (odds ratio [OR] 0·73, 95% CI 0·65-0·82) and death by any cause (0·62, 0·47-0·82) within a year. Long-term effects were identified for repeated self-harm (0·84, 0·77-0·91; absolute risk reduction [ARR] 2·6%, 1·5-3·7; numbers needed to treat [NNT] 39, 95% CI 27-69), deaths by suicide (OR 0·75, 0·60-0·94; ARR 0·5%, 0·1-0·9; NNT 188, 108-725), and death by any cause (OR 0·69, 0·62-0·78; ARR 2·7%, 2·0-3·5; NNT 37, 29-52), implying that 145 self-harm episodes and 153 deaths, including 30 deaths by suicide, were prevented. INTERPRETATION: Our findings show a lower risk of repeated deliberate self-harm and general mortality in recipients of psychosocial therapy after short-term and long-term follow-up, and a protective effect for suicide after long-term follow-up, which favour the use of psychosocial therapy interventions after deliberate self-harm. FUNDING: Danish Health Insurance Foundation; the Research Council of Psychiatry, Region of Southern Denmark; the Research Council of Psychiatry, Capital Region of Denmark; and the Strategic Research Grant from Health Sciences, Capital Region of Denmark.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Erlangsen, Annette","Lind, Bertel Dam","Stuart, Elizabeth A.","Qin, Ping","Stenager, Elsebeth","Juul Larsen, Kim","Wang, August G","Hvid, Marianne","Nielsen, Ann Coleen","Pedersen, Christian Møller","Winsløv, Jan-Henrik","Langhoff, Charlotte","Mühlmann, Charlotte","Nordentoft, Merete"],"cuid":["S03-097.17-003540"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short term and long term effects of psychosocial therapy for people after deliberate self harm a register based nationwide multicentre study using propensity score matching","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84920830695","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.17-003540","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000352705600024","type":"wos"},{"id":"84920830695","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26359612","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-48d65267-c7a4-45b6-a253-1c797a41e2a3","ku-e4961f3e-5ac2-48c2-8568-510b32a49415","sdu-61b67062-2c88-4f3c-9661-3f8edad5cb57"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B504F9C9E4C7DB8C69B816448E2091F9"],"oai"