{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The aim of this nationwide study was to investigate the early morbidity after bilateral simultaneous and staged total knee arthroplasty (TKA) in order to clarify potential benefits of a well-established fast-track regime. METHODS: The Danish National Patient Registry was searched for all bilateral simultaneous and staged TKA procedures from 2010 to 2011. The staged procedures were defined as two separate procedures done within 0-6 months or within 7-18 months. RESULTS: A total of 157 patients had bilateral simultaneous TKA, 346 patients had bilateral staged TKA within 0-6 months and 292 patients had bilateral staged TKA within 7-18 months. The median length of stay in hospital (LOS) was 4 days (interquartile range, IQR: 3) after bilateral simultaneous TKA versus cumulated LOS of 6 days (IQR: 3) in both of the bilateral staged groups (p < 0.001). There were no deaths after bilateral simultaneous TKA versus three deaths (0.9 and 1.0 %) in each of the bilateral staged groups within 90 days of surgery (n.s.). The total readmission rate within 30 days of surgery was lower after bilateral simultaneous TKA (7 %, CI 4.0-12.0) and bilateral staged TKA within 0-6 months (9 %, CI 6.4-12.4) compared with 14 % (CI 11.5-20.1) after bilateral staged TKA within 7-18 months. CONCLUSIONS: The results from this nationwide study indicate that bilateral simultaneous TKA can safely be performed in a fast-track set-up.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Jørgensen, Christoffer Calov","Husted, Henrik","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394415"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee","Female","Humans","Length of Stay","Male","Middle Aged","Osteoarthritis Knee","Patient Readmission","Registries","Retrospective Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early morbidity after simultaneous and staged bilateral total knee arthroplasty","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-394415","identifier":[{"id":"84893164499","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24503963","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-018f0ddf-c377-42f2-a9cc-f16df3ccde8d"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee","Female","Humans","Length of Stay","Male","Middle Aged","Osteoarthritis, Knee","Patient Readmission","Registries","Retrospective Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B964B2D867F7E976B0E540206D45F2B8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer Calov","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1fe3c897-7a55-4930-b8f8-9a3f66f61d5d","name":"Jørgensen, Christoffer Calov","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","locid":"f8dc9a5b-bf7f-45e7-b210-3b25c01cfa24","name":"Husted, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24503963"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00167-014-2880-1","issn":["09422056","14337347"],"issn_org":["09422056"],"issue":"3","journal":"Knee Surgery, Sports Traumatology, Arthroscopy","pages":"831-7","status":"p","title":"Knee Surgery, Sports Traumatology, Arthroscopy","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84893164499"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-018f0ddf-c377-42f2-a9cc-f16df3ccde8d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Early morbidity after simultaneous and staged bilateral total knee arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394415","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES: Transfusion of red blood cells (RBC) is beneficial for the patient but can also be harmful, as randomized trials have demonstrated increased infection rates, bleeding and mortality. The study aim was to investigate the response of the vascular system (the haemostatic function and the endothelium) to RBC transfusion. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Blood was sampled from patients with various transfusion-dependent haematologic diseases before 1 and 24 h after RBC transfusion. Primary and secondary haemostasis was evaluated by whole-blood impedance aggregometry (Multiplate) and by thromboelastography (TEG). Samples were analysed by ELISA for biomarkers reflecting endothelial activation and damage (sICAM-1, syndecan-1, sThrombomodulin (sTM), sVE-Cadherin), platelet activation (sCD40L) and inflammation (hsCRP). RESULTS: A total of 58 patients were enrolled in the study. Median age was 71 years. Compared to before transfusion, patients had slightly reduced coagulability 1 h after RBC transfusion, assessed by TEG. However, transfusion of older RBC products (>14 days) was associated with increased coagulability (all P < 0·05). The level of syndecan-1 increased slightly 24 h after transfusion (median 12·4 (IQR 9-23) vs. 13·2 (9-25) ng/ml, P < 0·01), indicating increased glycocalyx degradation. CONCLUSION: Overall, RBC transfusion was associated with reduced coagulability and endothelial glycocalyx degradation. Transfusion of older RBCs was however associated with increased coagulability. The changes observed were small to moderate and the clinical relevance of these findings should be investigated in larger studies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, A M","Leinøe, E B","Johansson, P I","Birgens, Henrik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405942"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antigens CD","Biomarkers","C Reactive Protein","CD40 Ligand","Cadherins","Enzyme Linked Immunosorbent Assay","Erythrocyte Transfusion","Erythrocytes","Female","Hematologic Diseases","Humans","Intercellular Adhesion Molecule 1","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Syndecan 1","Thrombelastography","Thrombomodulin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"haemostatic function and biomarkers of endothelial damage before and after rbc transfusion in patients with haematologic disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-405942","identifier":[{"id":"84931574412","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25754541","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-14f35186-46d1-4033-ab98-67b6d92c73c9"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antigens, CD","Biomarkers","C-Reactive Protein","CD40 Ligand","Cadherins","Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay","Erythrocyte Transfusion","Erythrocytes","Female","Hematologic Diseases","Humans","Intercellular Adhesion Molecule-1","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Syndecan-1","Thrombelastography","Thrombomodulin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-97D614A14E11EE7D59A747651C2EB4CA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"A M","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, A M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E B","key":"leinøepau","last":"Leinøe","name":"Leinøe, E B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"P I","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, P I","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H","key":"birgenspau","last":"Birgens","locid":"74d48d40-228f-412c-837c-52d6b4d6e3d4","name":"Birgens, Henrik","name_org":"Birgens, H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"S R","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","name_org":"Ostrowski, S R","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25754541"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/vox.12249","issn":["00429007","02580330"],"issn_org":["00429007"],"issue":"1","journal":"Vox Sanguinis","pages":"52-61","status":"p","title":"Vox Sanguinis","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84931574412"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-14f35186-46d1-4033-ab98-67b6d92c73c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Haemostatic function and biomarkers of endothelial damage before and after RBC transfusion in patients with haematologic disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405942","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Pain after Caesarean section is often treated with opioids with a risk of side effects. Wound infiltration with local anaesthetics is effective and has few side effects, but volume vs. dose concentration has not been examined. METHODS: Ninety patients scheduled for elective Caesarean section included in a randomised, double-blinded, placebo-controlled trial receiving infiltration with 50 ml ropivacaine 0.5% or 125 ml ropivacaine 0.2% or 50 ml 0.9% saline (placebo) during surgery. Surgery was performed under lumbar spinal anaesthesia. Primary endpoint was post-operative pain. Secondary endpoints were rescue analgesic, post-operative nausea and vomiting, time spent in the postanesthesia care unit (PACU) and time to first mobilisation. RESULTS: No difference in pain response between groups, but time until maximum pain score was prolonged in the ropivacaine 0.5% group compared with the placebo group (P = 0.0493). The administration of ketobemidone at 24 h post-operatively in the ropivacaine 0.5% group was reduced compared with the placebo group (P = 0.020), and between the ropivacaine 0.2% group and the ropivacaine 0.5% group (P = 0.044). No significant differences between groups were found concerning time spent in the PACU, to first mobilisation or in number of women with nausea/vomiting (P ≥ 0.05). No complications related to ropivacaine were observed. CONCLUSIONS: Systematic infiltration with a high concentration, low volume compared with low concentration, high volume showed no significant effect on post-operative pain intensity. However, a statistically significant, but clinically limited opioid sparing effect was demonstrated compared with placebo in the high concentration, low volume group.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Klaus Richter","Kristensen, B B","Rasmussen, M A","Rasmussen, Y H","Weber, T.","Kristensen, B","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-407534"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Amides","Analgesia Obstetrical","Analgesics Opioid","Anesthesia Local","Anesthetics Local","Cesarean Section","Double Blind Method","Endpoint Determination","Female","Humans","Infant Newborn","Pain Measurement","Pain Postoperative","Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting","Pregnancy","Sufentanil"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of high volume systematic local infiltration analgesia in caesarean section a randomised placebo controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-407534","identifier":[{"id":"84927799743","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25786811","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-17a02fc6-cda0-4be2-a0cf-8e55f26786da"],"keyword":["Adult","Amides","Analgesia, Obstetrical","Analgesics, Opioid","Anesthesia, Local","Anesthetics, Local","Cesarean Section","Double-Blind Method","Endpoint Determination","Female","Humans","Infant, Newborn","Pain Measurement","Pain, Postoperative","Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting","Pregnancy","Sufentanil"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-84A1B302B3C65602F8D79465847BAC29"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus Richter","key":"larsenklausrichterpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"43fd2d53-9005-42a7-a130-ffa48b2b8d7b","name":"Larsen, Klaus Richter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B B","key":"kristensenbbpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, B B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M A","key":"rasmussenmapau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, M A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Y H","key":"rasmussenyhpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Y H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"T.","key":"webertpau","last":"Weber","name":"Weber, T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B","key":"kristensenbpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, B","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H","key":"kehlethenrikpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","name_org":"Kehlet, H","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25786811"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.12509","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"5","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"632-9","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927799743"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-17a02fc6-cda0-4be2-a0cf-8e55f26786da"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of high-volume systematic local infiltration analgesia in Caesarean section : a randomised, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-407534","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Arthur Francis George Kerr's life is reviewed and related to a previously published account. Kerr's collecting activity is analysed using an expanded version of the Thai Biogeography Group's database of collections. 8,666 of the total 48,970 collections are Kerr's and 3,178 are those of his colleagues and friends. Therefore, the total number of collections made by Kerr and his acquaintances is likely to be larger and more diverse than previously believed. Mapping of these data using GIS show that Kerr's collecting activities focussed on particular regions of Thailand at particular times. Also large areas of the country remained unexplored by Kerr and his acquaintances: a pattern that, to some extent, persists to this day. The large, but dispersed, archive of Kerr's photographs, maps, living collections and correspondence indicate that he was a skilled photographer (taking at least 3,000 images), cartographer (producing many hand-drawn maps) and exceptionally acute, accurate and detailed observer (fi lling numerous notebooks and leaving other records). It is clear that digitising these collections to form an on-line dedicated website is highly desirable to further progress on the fl ora of Thailand and surrounding countries and would form an unique record of the social history of early 20thC Thailand.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Parnell, J. A. N.","Pilla, F.","Simpson, D. A.","Van Welzen, P. C.","Chayamarit, K.","Chantaranothai, P.","Boyce, P. C.","Bygrave, P.","Byrne, C.","Chen, S.","Couch, C.","Curtis, T.","Dransfield, S.","Duyfjes, B. E. E.","Eianthong, W.","Esser, H. J.","Grote, P. J.","Hua, Z.","Jebb, M. H. P.","Kirkup, D. W.","Loc, P. Ke","Larsen, Supree S.","Macklin, J.","Madern, A.","Meade, C.","Merklinger, F.","Middleton, D. J.","Moat, J.","Muasya, A. M.","Nakmuenwai, P.","Pedersen, Henrik Ærenlund","Pendry, C. A.","Prajaksood, A.","Pooma, R.","Preusapan, K.","Puglisi, C.","Sathapattayanon, A.","Sukkharak, P.","Staples, G.","Strijk, J.","Suddee, S.","Sungkaew, S.","Tangjitman, K.","Teerwatananon, A.","Tovaranonte, J.","Ung, T.","Blasi, A. Trias","De Wilde, W. J. J. O.","Wilkin, P.","Yahara, T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-410543"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Germany","Ireland","Japan","Malaysia","Netherlands","Singapore","South Africa","Thailand","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["120 the Government Complex Commemorating His Majesty","All Global Affiliations","Bangkok Herbarium","Burapha University","Chiang Mai University","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Department of National Parks, Wildlife and Plant Conservation","Guangxi University","Herbarium","Kasetsart University","Khon Kaen University","Kumming Division of Xishuangbanna Tropical Botanical Garden","Kyushu University","Mae Fah Luang University","Maynooth University","National Botanic Gardens","Naturalis Biodiversity Center","Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew","Royal Forest Department","Srinakharinwirot University","Suranaree University of Technology","Trinity College Dublin","University of Cape Town","University of Malaysia Sarawak","University of Strasbourg"],"keyword":["GIS","Socio economic history","Thailand"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a re examination of the life and work of a f g kerr and of his colleagues and friends","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/161082761/Parnell_2015_A_re_examination.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-410543","identifier":[{"id":"84952012349","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1cb315a3-4fac-41b