{"abstract":"Fluorescent base analogues comprise a group of increasingly important molecules for the investigation of nucleic acid structure, dynamics, and interactions with other molecules. Herein, we report on the quantum chemical calculation aided design, synthesis, and characterization of four new putative quadracyclic adenine analogues. The compounds were efficiently synthesized from a common intermediate through a two-step pathway with the Suzuki-Miyaura coupling as the key step. Two of the compounds, qAN1 and qAN4, display brightnesses (epsilon Phi(F)) of 1700 and 2300, respectively, in water and behave as wavelength-ratiometric pH probes under acidic conditions. The other two, qAN2 and qAN3, display lower brightnesses but exhibit polarity-sensitive dual-band emissions that could prove useful to investigate DNA structural changes induced by DNA-protein or -drug interactions. The four qANs are very promising microenvironment- sensitive fluorescent adenine analogues that display considerable brightness for such compounds.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Dumat, Blaise","Bood, Mattias","Wranne, Moa S.","Lawson, Christopher P.","Larsen, Anders Foller","Preus, Søren","Streling, Jens","Graden, Henrik","Wellner, Eric","Grøtli, Morten","Wilhelmsson, L. Marcus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177939"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","AstraZeneca UK","Chalmers University of Technology","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Aromatic substitution","BASE ANALOG","C C coupling","CYTOSINE ANALOG","Cross coupling reactions","DNA protein interactions","Fluorescent probes","Nucleic acids","Nucleobases","Nucleosides","Photophysical properties","Systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"second generation fluorescent quadracyclic adenine analogues environment responsive probes with enhanced brightness","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84941599154","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177939","identifier":[{"id":"25641628","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000350762400026","type":"wos"},{"id":"84941599154","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-553c33c7-d45c-4c06-a57f-39636305fea2"],"keyword":["BASE ANALOG","C-C coupling","CROSS-COUPLING REACTIONS","CYTOSINE ANALOG","DNA-PROTEIN INTERACTIONS","INTERMOLECULAR PROTON-TRANSFER","LIVE CELLS","NUCLEOSIDES","PHOTOPHYSICAL PROPERTIES","SYSTEMS","aromatic substitution","fluorescent probes","nucleic acids","nucleobases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE2DED7660DC6FE45DF96DE576AAC836"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"astrazeneca uk","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"AstraZeneca UK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"