{"abstract":"Ledelse: Danske chefer kan sagtens skære igennem og træffe en beslutning. Men de dumper med at brag, når de skal udvikle talenter, kommunikere mål og retning, løse en konflikt eller skabe et arbejdsmiljø, hvor medarbejderne bliver dygtigere af at gå på arbejde.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-291652"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cheferne svigter personalet","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-291652","ids":["cbs-ab24e5d0-67a2-4cc4-bba9-1a819f603694"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-81C443FFF00510A0C33CB50D5F1D9CB6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Holt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","name_org":"Larsen, Henrik Holt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01091182"],"newspaper":"Jyllands-Posten","pages":"28","publisher":"JP/Politikens Hus AS","publisher_org":"JP/Politikens Hus A/S","status":"p","title":"Jyllands-Posten"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-ab24e5d0-67a2-4cc4-bba9-1a819f603694"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Cheferne svigter personalet","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-291652","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Det er kendt, men ikke nødvendigvis erkendt, at god ledelse har afgørende betydning for konkurrencekraften, vækstpotentialet, produktiviteten og indtjeningsevnen i danske virksomheder. Det viser hovedparten af de analyser om ledelse, der er gennemført i de senere år i Danmark og udlandet. En netop udkommet rapport viser således, at forbedret ledelse i danske virksomheder ville kunne gavne samfundsøkonomien med et meget stort, årligt milliardbeløb (Ugebrevet A4, 27.4.2015). Det ville især kræve inddragelse af medarbejderne i tilrettelæggelsen af det daglige arbejde, socialt ansvar og omsorg for medarbejderne samt bedre evne til at levere nye produkter, omstille sig og samarbejde med leverandører. Derfor er det et interessant spørgsmål i en tid, hvor fornyelse, vækst og produktivitet står på dagsordenen både samfundsmæssigt og i virksomheder, hvad der kendetegner dansk ledelse anno 2015. Det spørgsmål har Dansk Selskab for Virksomhedsledelse ønsket at belyse som optakt til VL Døgnet i maj 2015, der samtidig markerer 50 års jubilæet for organisationen. Derfor var det også naturligt at spørge medlemmerne om, hvordan ledelse i dag udøves i de virksomheder, de repræsenterer. Det er resultaterne fra denne undersøgelse, som i det følgende vil blive præsenteret.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik","Poulfelt, Flemming","Nielsen, Rikke Kristine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-299420"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ny dansk ledelse når ledere taler om ledelse vl analyse 000000002015","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58805697/vl_analyse_2015.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-299420","ids":["cbs-fb864f05-19e7-45ee-92f4-bc50671bb832"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4AD388991BC155D298F0F415C9628E27"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58805697/vl_analyse_2015.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"poulfeltpau","last":"Poulfelt","locid":"1fdce38a-9ede-4ec1-bae5-b0476d9366b6","name":"Poulfelt, Flemming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Kristine","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Kristine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"15","place":"Hellerup","publisher":"Dansk Selskab for Virksomhedsledelse","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-fb864f05-19e7-45ee-92f4-bc50671bb832"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Ny dansk ledelse : Når ledere taler om ledelse: VL-analyse 2015","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-299420","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the Spring of 2013, NMR spectroscopists convened at the Weizmann Institute in Israel to brainstorm on approaches to improve the sensitivity of NMR experiments, particularly when applied in biomolecular settings. This multi‐author interdisciplinary Review presents a state‐of‐the‐art description of the primary approaches that were considered. Topics discussed included the future of ultrahigh‐field NMR systems, emerging NMR detection technologies, new approaches to nuclear hyperpolarization, and progress in sample preparation. All of these are orthogonal efforts, whose gains could multiply and thereby enhance the sensitivity of solid‐ and liquid‐state experiments. While substantial advances have been made in all these areas, numerous challenges remain in the quest of endowing NMR spectroscopy with the sensitivity that has characterized forms of spectroscopies based on electrical or optical measurements. These challenges, and the ways by which scientists and engineers are striving to solve them, are also addressed.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Boebinger, Gregory S.","Comment, Arnaud","Duckett, Simon","Edison, Arthur S.","Engelke, Frank","Griesinger, Christian","Griffin, Robert G.","Hilty, Christian","Maeda, Hidaeki","Parigi, Giacomo","Prisner, Thomas","Ravera, Enrico","van Bentum, Jan","Vega, Shimon","Webb, Andrew","Luchinat, Claudio","Schwalbe, Harald","Frydman, Lucio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335701"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Israel","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bruker Corporation","Florida State University","Goethe University Frankfurt","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Biophysical Chemistry","RIKEN","Radboud University Nijmegen","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","Texas A&M University","University of Florence","University of Florida","University of York","Weizmann Institute of Science"],"keyword":["NMR spectroscopy","Sensitivity enhancement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"facing and overcoming sensitivity challenges in biomolecular nmr spectroscopy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.201410653","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335701","identifier":[{"id":"84938205018","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26136394","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4943876","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-683f9b05-d3c0-4375-a08d-adbb6a1448e4"],"keyword":["NMR probeheads","NMR spectroscopy","Nuclear hyperpolarization","Sensitivity enhancement","Ultrahigh magnetic fields"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35AE05233A2B0A9FAA04D4DC411402AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.201410653","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"florida state university","loc":["United States","America