{"abstract":"DDGS er et proteinrigt fodermiddel fra produktionen af bio-etanol baseret på korn og majs, og det forventes på markedet i stigende mængder. Kornbaseret DDGS kan være et godt proteinfoder som uden negativ effekt på mælkeproduktion eller -kvalitet kan indgå med 15 % af rationens tørstof og kan erstatte halvdelen af gode proteinkilder som sojaskrå og rapskage i rationen til malkekøer. Ved højere niveauer af DDGS i rationen kan der være mindre, negative effekter på protein- og mælkeydelsen. Der kan være stor variation i foderværdien af DDGS, og det anbefales at rekvirere analysecertifikat fra leverandøren, når DDGS skal anvendes i fodringen. DDGS har en relativt lav klimabelastning i forhold til mere traditionelle proteinfodermidler som sojaskrå og rapskage.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sehested, Jakob","Sørensen, Martin Tang","Weisbjerg, Martin Riis","Vestergaard, Mogens","Larsen, Mette Krogh","Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","Martinussen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-153348"],"event":{"end":"2015-04-23","place":"Foulum, dk","start":"2015-04-23","title":"Temamøde: Malkekoens ernæring","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bærme ddgs som proteinfoder til malkekøer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-153348","ids":["au-29eb8a3f-bec9-4f87-853b-cfce50ff8157"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F12DF5E5AE2C578C9171C8FEA85E72B7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"sehestedpau","last":"Sehested","locid":"877cccec-c84c-4d5c-94a0-26731a4a157a","name":"Sehested, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0001-6977-6972","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Tang","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fefc1862-587c-4b1f-9e20-694246b18221","name":"Sørensen, Martin Tang","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-4282","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Riis","key":"weisbjergpau","last":"Weisbjerg","locid":"501c877c-de2b-4cd2-9f3c-42e223238a40","name":"Weisbjerg, Martin Riis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f886731d-42d7-485e-b44c-f48981a245e7","name":"Vestergaard, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-3630-1396","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Krogh","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5ce6d5da-bd09-4304-a9d9-495e00e51fdd","name":"Larsen, Mette Krogh","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Brøgger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"4fbc8c90-2c05-4233-a45a-b80c6cbab818","name":"Pedersen, Mads Brøgger","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"martinussenpau","last":"Martinussen","name":"Martinussen, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"lundpedh","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Peter","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793176737"],"pages":"75-84","publisher":"DCA - Nationalt Center for Fødevarer og Jordbrug","status":"p","subtitle":"- Fodringsstrategier målrettet produktivitet og miljøhensyn","title":"Malkekoens ernæring","volume":"60"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-29eb8a3f-bec9-4f87-853b-cfce50ff8157"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bærme (DDGS) som proteinfoder til malkekøer","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-153348","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Fluorescent base analogues (FBAs) comprise a family of increasingly important molecules for the investigation of nucleic acid structure and dynamics. We recently reported the quantum chemical calculation supported development of four microenvironment sensitive analogues of the quadracyclic adenine (qA) scaffold, the qANs, with highly promising absorptive and fluorescence properties that were very well predicted by TDDFT calculations. Herein, we report on the efficient synthesis, experimental and theoretical characterization of nine novel quadracyclic adenine derivatives. The brightest derivative, 2-CNqA, displays a 13-fold increased brightness (epsilon Phi(F) = 4500) compared with the parent compound qA and has the additional benefit of being a virtually microenvironment-insensitive fluorophore, making it a suitable candidate for nucleic acid incorporation and use in quantitative FRET and anisotropy experiments. TDDFT calculations, conducted on the nine novel qAs a posteriori, successfully describe the relative fluorescence quantum yield and brightness of all qA derivatives. This observation suggests that the TDDFT-based rational design strategy may be employed for the development of bright fluorophores built up from a common scaffold to reduce the otherwise costly and time-consuming screening process usually required to obtain useful and bright FBAs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Anders Foller","Dumat, Blaise","Wranne, Moa S.","Lawson, Christopher P.","Preus, Søren","Bood, Mattias","Graden, Henrik","Wilhelmsson, L. Marcus","Grøtli, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-232450"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wilhelmsson, L. Marcus"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","AstraZeneca UK","Chalmers University of Technology"],"keyword":["BASE ANALOG","CYTOSINE ANALOG","Density","Fluorophore","Nucleic acid","Nucleoside","Oligonucleotides","Photophysical properties","Probes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of bright fluorescent quadracyclic adenine analogues tddft calculation supported rational design","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep12653","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-232450","identifier":[{"id":"84938537201","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000358770900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"26227585","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4530663","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-b4b974a2-ba3d-479f-876e-2f7f59a0fbae"],"keyword":["BASE ANALOG","CYTOSINE ANALOG","DENSITY","FLUOROPHORE","NUCLEIC-ACID","NUCLEOSIDE","OLIGONUCLEOTIDES","PHOTOPHYSICAL PROPERTIES","PROBES","PYRROLO-DC"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE7EEDE1E649843B481C90DBF9CADFDB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep12653","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"astrazeneca uk","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"AstraZeneca UK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Foller","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Foller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Blaise","key":"dumatpau","last":"Dumat","name":"Dumat, Blaise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Moa S.","key":"wrannepau","last":"Wranne","name":"Wranne, Moa S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher P.","key":"lawsonpau","last":"Lawson","name":"Lawson, Christopher P.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"preuspau","last":"Preus","locid":"ba854e1c-fb47-47b1-a5d8-00d1931ecb93","name":"Preus, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mattias","key":"boodpau","last":"Bood","name":"Bood, Mattias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"gradenpau","last":"Graden","name":"Graden, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L. Marcus","key":"wilhelmssonpau","last":"Wilhelmsson","name":"Wilhelmsson, L. Marcus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"grøtlipau","last":"Grøtli","name":"Grøtli, Morten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26227585"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/srep12653","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"12653","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938537201"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b4b974a2-ba3d-479f-876e-2f7f59a0fbae"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Development of bright fluorescent quadracyclic adenine analogues : TDDFT-calculation supported rational design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-232450","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Dissolution-dynamic nuclear polarization (dissolution-DNP) for magnetic resonance (MR) spectroscopic imaging has recently emerged as a novel technique for noninvasive studies of the metabolic fate of biomolecules in vivo. Since acetate is the most abundant extra- and intracellular short-chain fatty acid, we focused on [1-13C]acetate as a promising candidate for a chemical probe to study the myocardial metabolism of a beating heart. The dissolution-DNP procedure of Na[1-13C]acetate for in vivo cardiac applications with a 3 T MR scanner was optimized in pigs during bolus injection of doses of up to 3 mmol. The Na[1-13C]acetate formulation was characterized by a liquid-state polarization of 14.2% and a T1Eff in vivo of 17.6 ± 1.7 s. In vivo Na[1-13C]acetate kinetics displayed a bimodal shape: [1-13C]acetyl carnitine (AcC) was detected in a slice covering the cardiac volume, and the signal of 13C-acetate and 13C-AcC was modeled using the total area under the curve (AUC) for kinetic analysis. A good correlation was found between the ratio AUC(AcC)/AUC(acetate) and the apparent kinetic constant of metabolic conversion, from [1-13C]acetate to [1-13C]AcC (kAcC), divided by the AcC longitudinal relaxation rate (r1). Our study proved the feasibility and the limitations of administration of large doses of hyperpolarized [1-13C]acetate to study the myocardial conversion of [1-13C]acetate in [1-13C]acetyl-carnitine generated by acetyltransferase in healthy pigs","author_count":13,"contributors":["Flori, Alessandra","Liserani, Matteo","Frijia, Francesca","Giovannetti, Giulio","Lionetti, Vincenzo","Casieri, Valentina","Positano, Vincenzo","Aquaro, Giovanni Donato","Recchia, Fabio A.","Santarelli, Maria Filomena","Landini, Luigi","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Menichetti, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-307237"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fondazione CNR/Regione Toscana G. Monasterio","National Research Council of Italy","Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","University of Pisa"],"keyword":["Hyperpolarization","Magnetic resonance spectroscopy MRS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real time cardiac metabolism assessed with hyperpolarized 000000000001 000000000013c acetate in a large animal model","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cmmi.1618","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-307237","identifier":[{"id":"25201079","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84930931623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4362963","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-08d64abf-aa4c-4f58-b767-c81bd5c6c8e7"],"keyword":["Dynamic nuclear polarization (DNP)","Free fatty acid (FA) metabolism","Heart metabolism","Hyperpolarization","Magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS)","Trityl radical","[1- 13 C]acetate","[1- 13 C]acetyl-carnitine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49BD23E96FEB249C54B3AC18A09DFC10"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cmmi.1618","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"sant anna school of advanced studies","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of pisa","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Pisa","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"fondazione cnr regione toscana g monasterio","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fondazione CNR/Regione Toscana G. Monasterio","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandra","key":"floripau","last":"Flori","name":"Flori, Alessandra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"liseranipau","last":"Liserani","name":"Liserani, Matteo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"frijiapau","last":"Frijia","name":"Frijia, Francesca","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Giulio","key":"giovannettipau","last":"Giovannetti","name":"Giovannetti, Giulio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo","key":"lionettipau","last":"Lionetti","name":"Lionetti, Vincenzo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina","key":"casieripau","last":"Casieri","name":"Casieri, Valentina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo","key":"positanopau","last":"Positano","name":"Positano, Vincenzo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni Donato","key":"aquaropau","last":"Aquaro","name":"Aquaro, Giovanni Donato","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio A.","key":"recchiapau","last":"Recchia","name":"Recchia, Fabio A.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Filomena","key":"santarellipau","last":"Santarelli","name":"Santarelli, Maria Filomena","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Luigi","key":"landinipau","last":"Landini","name":"Landini, Luigi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"menichettipau","last":"Menichetti","name":"Menichetti, Luca","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25201079"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cmmi.1618","issn":["15554309","15554317"],"issn_org":["15554309"],"issue":"3","journal":"Contrast Media & Molecular Imaging","pages":"194-202","publisher":"Hindawi Limited","status":"p","title":"Contrast Media & Molecular Imaging","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930931623"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-08d64abf-aa4c-4f58-b767-c81bd5c6c8e7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Real-time cardiac metabolism assessed with hyperpolarized [1-13C]acetate in a large-animal model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-307237","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Vortex methods are numerical methods for simulating uid ow. They use a simple formulation where only the trajectories of discrete vortex particles are simulated. In our method we combine a high order particle-mesh based vortex method with an iterative penalization method to simulate external ows around arbitrary geometries such as bridge decks. The method only uses a discretized ge- ometry as input and can easily simulate an arbitrary motion of the geometry. As vorticity is a bounded quantity and the velocity eld can easily be calculated for a mixture of free-space- and periodic boundary conditions, the method allows for a minimized domain and hence minimal computational resources. However in an external ow problem, vorticity is produced in the boundary layers and transported downstream, consequently the computational domain must grow in time to encap- sulate the entire vorticity eld. We present a method for truncating this domain by supplementing the free-space- and periodic conditions with an out ow condition. The method is conveniently applied within the eld of bridge aerodynamics as it can be used for the calculation of the aerodynamic net forces, which depend highly on the geometry and the wake forming behind it. This is demonstrated in 2D and 3D simulations","author_count":4,"contributors":["Spietz, Henrik Juul","Hejlesen, Mads Mølholm","Walther, Jens Honore","Larsen, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308609"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-24","place":"Boston, us","start":"2015-11-22","title":"68th Annual Meeting of the American Physical Society's Division of Fluid Dynamics (DFD)","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulating external flow using vortex method in two and three dimensions","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/118309370/MWS_DFD15_2015_000983.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-308609","ids":["dtu-0d583436-5896-4f3d-8281-bdd348cb1ee6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B8C09EDB6699E62C4E4DAB5CBCCB3FB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/118309370/MWS_DFD15_2015_000983.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Juul","key":"spietzpau","last":"Spietz","locid":"77b022ad-b7ab-4646-bbc5-d5ca038655ce","name":"Spietz, Henrik Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-7775-0975","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Mølholm","key":"hejlesenpau","last":"Hejlesen","locid":"d47de8f8-7fdf-4adb-a76f-696a9a76cd46","name":"Hejlesen, Mads Mølholm","orcid":"0000-0001-6443-5511","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Honore","key":"waltherpau","last":"Walther","locid":"9895a63e-6fff-429b-8188-9bcd7f6cac8d","name":"Walther, Jens Honore","orcid":"0000-0001-8100-9178","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Allan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0d583436-5896-4f3d-8281-bdd348cb1ee6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simulating external flow using vortex method in two- and three dimensions","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-308609","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In this study, a method to opto-electronically probe the individual junctions and carrier transport across interfaces in fully printed and coated tandem polymer solar cells is described, enabling the identification of efficiency limiting printing/coating defects. The methods used are light beam induced current (LBIC) mapping, External quantum efficiency (EQE) measurements, and monochromatic current-voltage (I-V) characterization. Using these methods, inherent limitations to the accuracy of EQE and LBIC measurements on non-ideal tandem solar cells are identified and described through the use of a small-signal electrical model. The model is able to predict the EQE spectrum of the non-ideal polymer tandem solar cell, using extracted values of shunt- and series resistance of the individual junction of the tandem cell. This finally enables LBIC mapping of the individual junctions of the tandem polymer solar cells, using a combination of light and voltage-biasing.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen-Olsen, Thue Trofod","Andersen, Thomas Rieks","Dam, Henrik Friis","Jørgensen, Mikkel","Krebs, Frederik C"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316906"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Characterization","Electric resistance","Mapping","Organic photovoltaics","Plastic coatings","Polymers","Roll to roll","Solar cells","Solar power generation","Tandem solar cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"probing individal subcells of fully printed and coated polymer tandem solar cells using multichromatic opto electronic characterization methods","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.solmat.2015.01.030","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316906","identifier":[{"id":"84923594644","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-298228a4-3bf3-4b56-94db-d7a188ff3a2c"],"keyword":["Characterization","EQE","Electric resistance","Induced currents","LBIC","Mapping","Organic photovoltaics","Plastic coatings","Polymers","Roll-to-roll","Solar cells","Solar power generation","Tandem solar cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A0C647948F40EA2E9148D32F4936018"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.solmat.2015.01.030","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Functional organic materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thue Trofod","key":"larsenolsenpau","last":"Larsen-Olsen","locid":"e03ae801-6940-4a24-b4a7-b23383928558","name":"Larsen-Olsen, Thue Trofod","orcid":"0000-0001-5373-898X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Rieks","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5b565ee7-484f-4110-b464-da7f775fd3d3","name":"Andersen, Thomas Rieks","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Friis","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"1765cec1-6a56-4ea5-9e7f-5dc2db4436d6","name":"Dam, Henrik Friis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1d0a433e-d24f-4213-8227-181ea4b33688","name":"Jørgensen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-7729-1497","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frederik C","key":"krebspau","last":"Krebs","locid":"abb371a8-55a5-4346-af79-437546c2e627","name":"Krebs, Frederik C","orcid":"0000-0003-1148-4314","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.solmat.2015.01.030","issn":["09270248"],"journal":"Solar Energy Materials & Solar Cells","pages":"154-163","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Solar Energy Materials & Solar Cells","title_org":"Solar Energy Materials and Solar Cells","volume":"137"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923594644"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-298228a4-3bf3-4b56-94db-d7a188ff3a2c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Probing individal subcells of fully printed and coated polymer tandem solar cells using multichromatic opto-electronic characterization methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316906","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The New Nordic Diet (NND) was developed in 2004 by chefs and food professionals from the five Nordic countries. The goal for the NND was that it should be based on traditional regional food products but healthier than the traditional eating habits. The NND builds on four key principles: Nordic identity, health, gastronomic potential and sustainability.Objectives: Can the NND be used as a model for a sustainable diet in other geographical regions?Methods/design: The NND can be described by a few overall guidelines: 1) more calories from plant foods and fewer from meat; 2) more foods from the wild countryside and 3) more foods from sea and lakes. In many ways, the New NND is very similar to a Mediterranean diet but relies on rapeseed (canola) oil instead of olive oil and ramson instead of garlic. The diets differ in their types of produce due to regional differences in climate, soil and water.Results: The health effects and sustainability of the NND has been tested in a number of scientific studies, including the OPUS project (Optimal Well-Being, Development and Health for Danish Children through a Healthy New Nordic Diet) supported by the Nordea foundation (http://foodoflife.ku.dk/opus/english/nyheder/publikationer/) in which the NND was compared to the Average Danish Diet (ADD). The use of mostly local products and reduction of the meat intake were of both socioeconomic and environmental advantage. Including organic produce increased environmental impact of the NND.Conclusion: In line with the Mediterranean diet the NND is a predominantly plant-based diet, and although the two have not been directly compared, it would be fairly safe to assume that they are equally healthy. Overall, the NND is just a regional interpretation of the tenets of healthy eating. Basically the principles of the NND could be incorporated into any regional diet.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bugel, Susanne","Damsgaard, C. T.","Larsen, T. M.","Saxe, Henrik","Astrup, Arne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335437"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-23","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2015-10-20","title":"12th European Nutrition Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organic food for sustainable and healthy diets lessons from the nordic diet","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/124167680/Berlin_2015_Abstract.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335437","identifier":[{"id":"27161414","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-6751c385-5d33-498c-9064-9cd4dc7d118d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-086369005B91C3290A66A967F42CABF6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/124167680/Berlin_2015_Abstract.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"bugelpau","last":"Bugel","name":"Bugel, Susanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C. T.","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","name":"Damsgaard, C. T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T. M.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, T. M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"saxepau","last":"Saxe","locid":"113d1954-1e97-47a9-980e-47805cf05398","name":"Saxe, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-3918-7055","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","name":"Astrup, Arne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27161414"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000440895","issn":["02506807","10189688"],"issn_org":["02506807"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Annals of Nutrition and Metabolism","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Annals of Nutrition and Metabolism","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6751c385-5d33-498c-9064-9cd4dc7d118d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Organic food for sustainable and healthy diets - lessons from the nordic diet?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335437","year":"2015","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Karlsson, Kenneth Bernard","Skytte, Klaus","Morthorst, Poul Erik","Bacher, Peder","Madsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-345570"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrated energy systems modelling","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/119583447/DTU_International_Energy_Report_2015_rev.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-345570","identifier":[{"id":"84938779411","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8988e258-711f-4f05-b958-26e5562382a7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8F9AC0131ED1804D231DE7191A5ED6BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/119583447/DTU_International_Energy_Report_2015_rev.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Systems Analysis","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Systems Analysis, Energy Systems Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"4b874dbb-1bb4-4e19-b658-c0714cb60a06","name":"Karlsson, Kenneth Bernard","name_org":"Karlsson, Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0001-7749-254X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"skyttepau","last":"Skytte","locid":"dd0253e7-e01d-4d0b-933a-66ea70da996c","name":"Skytte, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0003-3587-3285","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul Erik","key":"morthorstpau","last":"Morthorst","locid":"ffe4b1d0-55d5-4dc7-914c-a1faf6bedae2","name":"Morthorst, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-4977-1976","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peder","key":"bacherpau","last":"Bacher","locid":"c0c28383-2363-4876-8bdc-450ca6c749c1","name":"Bacher, Peder","orcid":"0000-0001-5456-2576","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"458e950b-adfd-4f2d-8d0d-ef39dee24bea","name":"Madsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0690-3713","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"hvidtfeldtlarsenpedh","last":"Hvidtfeldt Larsen","name":"Hvidtfeldt Larsen, Hans","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Leif","key":"sønderbergpetersenpedh","last":"Sønderberg Petersen","name":"Sønderberg Petersen, Leif","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788755039704"],"pages":"23-33","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p","subtitle":"Energy systems integration for the transition to non-fossil energy systems","title":"DTU International Energy Report 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8988e258-711f-4f05-b958-26e5562382a7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Integrated energy systems modelling","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-345570","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Gold nanoparticles (AuNPs) are relevant in nanomedicine for drug delivery in the vascular system, where endothelial cells are the first point of contact. We investigated the uptake of 80 nm AuNPs in primary human umbilical vein endothelial cells (HUVECs) by flow cytometry, 3D confocal microscopy, nano-scale 3D-imaging using focused ion beam/scanning electron microscopy (FIB/SEM), and single particle inductively coupled plasma-mass spectrometry (spICP-MS). HUVECs were cultured for 3 h or 24 h in medium with AuNPs in a concentration range of 1.25–10 μg ml−1. There was a concentration-dependent increase of AuNPs inside cells measured by flow cytometry, spICP-MS and 3D confocal microscopy. The latter also showed that AuNPs were located in the cytosol. This was supported by FIB/SEM, showing that AuNPs were located in membrane enclosures in the cytoplasm as single particles or agglomerates of 2–3 or more particles. Pre-treatment with chlorpromazine inhibited the AuNP-uptake in HUVECs, indicating that internalisation occurred mainly by clathrin-mediated endocytosis. Cell activation by exposure to tumour necrosis factor or lipopolysaccharide had a slight or no effect on the uptake of AuNPs, respectively. The AuNP exposure did not influence cell cytotoxicity, whereas the intracellular reactive oxygen species production was slightly increased. In conclusion, the uptake of AuNPs by endothelial cells can be addressed quantitatively by several methods with high throughput and/or high specificity. Uptake of AuNPs in HUVECs occurred mainly by clathrin-mediated endocytosis and trafficking to membrane enclosures in the form of single particles and agglomerates of 2–3 particles.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Klingberg, Henrik","Oddershede, Lene B.","Löschner, Katrin","Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","Loft, Steffen","Møller, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357574"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uptake of gold nanoparticles in primary human endothelial cells","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/C4TX00061G","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357574","identifier":[{"id":"84928811631","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b16c6c7f-52f8-44c3-b59a-c81643bd8a27"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B9D2C86A34C41490263976320E176BDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/C4TX00061G","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Food Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research group for Nano-Bio Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"klingbergpau","last":"Klingberg","name":"Klingberg, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene B.","key":"oddershedepau","last":"Oddershede","name":"Oddershede, Lene B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrin","key":"löschnerpau","last":"Löschner","locid":"d7b22217-70e4-4c54-bd53-3f02c2d23a6f","name":"Löschner, Katrin","orcid":"0000-0003-1741-8406","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Huusfeldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9528940a-884f-4a63-b068-b739d7551006","name":"Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft","name":"Loft, Steffen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c4tx00061g","issn":["10960929","10966080"],"issn_org":["10966080"],"journal":"Toxicological Sciences","pages":"655-666","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Toxicological Sciences","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84928811631"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b16c6c7f-52f8-44c3-b59a-c81643bd8a27"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Uptake of gold nanoparticles in primary human endothelial cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357574","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We report on the evaluation of Schottky barrier diode GaAs multipliers at cryogenic temperatures. A GaAs Schottky barrier diode model is developed for theoretical estimation of doubler performance. The model is used to predict efficiency of doublers from room to cryogenic temperatures. The theoretical estimation is verified experimentally using a 78 GHz doubler cooled down to 14 K. The observed efficiency improvement due to cooling is approximately 4 % per 100 degrees.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Johansen, Tom Keinicke","Rybalko, Oleksandr","Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","Bowen, Sean","Hesler, Jeffrey","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-377246"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-06","place":"Porto de Galinhas, br","start":"2015-11-03","title":"2015 SBMO/IEEE MTT-S International Microwave and Optoelectronics Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Virginia Diodes, Inc."],"keyword":["Cryogenic temperature","Frequency multiplier","Millimeter wave"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling of schottky barrier diode millimeter wave multipliers at cryogenic temperatures","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/119787489/Modeling_of_Schottky_Barrier_Diode_Millimeter_Wave.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-377246","identifier":[{"id":"84964523911","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f2cb262e-d91b-4299-b9d2-5eb4babea290"],"keyword":["Cryogenic temperature","Frequency multiplier","GaAs diodes","Millimeter wave","Varactor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F269E76E666BF8254577110BE9C29C2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/119787489/Modeling_of_Schottky_Barrier_Diode_Millimeter_Wave.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electromagnetic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"virginia diodes inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Virginia Diodes, Inc.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tom K.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"7b44a94d-ae22-4678-87e4-8024f351462c","name":"Johansen, Tom Keinicke","name_org":"Johansen, Tom K.","orcid":"0000-0001-8182-1051","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oleksandr","key":"rybalkopau","last":"Rybalko","locid":"35007e3c-be65-457f-99ea-073043576468","name":"Rybalko, Oleksandr","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-6868","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vitaliy","key":"zhurbenkopau","last":"Zhurbenko","locid":"8449f428-fe8f-4ade-ad94-2e052869c1f4","name":"Zhurbenko, Vitaliy","orcid":"0000-0002-1515-733X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sean","key":"bowenpau","last":"Bowen","locid":"77cc622d-d330-44a7-8947-f1463e9c8cef","name":"Bowen, Sean","orcid":"0000-0003-1047-4325","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeffrey","key":"heslerpau","last":"Hesler","name":"Hesler, Jeffrey","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/imoc.2015.7369088","isbn":["9781509004317"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings. 2015 SBMO/IEEE MTT-S International Microwave and Optoelectronics Conference (IMOC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964523911"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f2cb262e-d91b-4299-b9d2-5eb4babea290"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Modeling of Schottky Barrier Diode Millimeter-Wave Multipliers at Cryogenic Temperatures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-377246","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To establish and validate a rapid, cost-effective and accurate screening assay for the simultaneous testing of human naturally occurring anti-cytokine autoantibodies (c-aAb) targeting interleukin-1α (IL-1α), interleukin-6 (IL-6), interleukin-10 (IL-10), granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF), and interferon α (IFNα). Because the c-aAbs can be transferred to patients through blood transfusion, the assay was used to assess c-aAb levels in a cohort of patients who were receiving blood transfusions and subsequently presented with or without febrile reactions. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The microsphere-based Luminex platform was used. Recombinant forms of human IL-1α, IL-6, IL-10, GM-CSF, and IFNα were gently coupled to MAG-PLEX beads. Plasma IgG binding was measured with phycoerythrin (PE)-labeled secondary antibodies. Previously confirmed c-aAb positive and negative donor plasma samples and pooled normal immunoglobulin preparations were used to validate the assay. Plasma samples from 98 transfusion recipients, half of whom presented with febrile reactions, were tested by the assay. RESULTS: The assay detected specific and saturable immunoglobulin G (IgG) binding to each of the tested cytokines in previously confirmed c-aAb positive plasmas and in preparations of pooled normal immunoglobulin. Confirmed c-aAb negative plasmas gave no saturable binding. The detection limit of the cytokine autoantibodies was estimated to be between 1 pM and 10 pM. The recovery of confirmed cytokine autoantibodies quantities in the negative plasma samples ranged between 80% and 125%. The analytical intra- and inter-assay variations were 4% and 11%, respectively. Varying c-aAb levels were detectable in the transfusion recipients. There was no difference in c-aAb frequency between the patients with or without febrile transfusion reactions. The c-aAb level before and after the blood transfusions varied only slightly and in an irregular manner. CONCLUSION: This assay simultaneously detected up to five different c-aAbs in pooled human IgG and in plasma from individual blood donors, and it was deemed suitable for larger screenings. Based on confirmed antibody binding characteristics and the resultant reactivity in this multiplex assay, a classification of the c-aAb levels was suggested. The screening results of the recipients who received blood transfusions indicate that more studies are needed to clarify the role of antibodies, if any, in transfusion medicine and in high-dose immunoglobulin treatment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Guldager, Daniel Kring Rasmussen","von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","Larsen, Rune","Bay, Jakob T","Galle, Pia Søndergaard","Svenson, Morten","Ullum, Henrik","Hansen, Morten Bagge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-478261"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autoantibodies","Biological Assay","Cytokines","Granulocyte Macrophage Colony Stimulating Factor","Humans","Immunoglobulin G","Interferon alpha","Interleukin 10","Interleukin 1alpha","Interleukin 6","Plasma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a rapid accurate and robust particle based assay for the simultaneous screening of plasma samples for the presence of five different anti cytokine autoantibodies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-478261","identifier":[{"id":"84943665577","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26080061","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8ddc8463-285a-492f-9889-5cc1e2e258bc"],"keyword":["Autoantibodies","Biological Assay","Cytokines","Granulocyte-Macrophage Colony-Stimulating Factor","Humans","Immunoglobulin G","Interferon-alpha","Interleukin-10","Interleukin-1alpha","Interleukin-6","Plasma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EF71E9612F22E979CDE84DF6DFE1BF81"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Daniel Kring Rasmussen","key":"guldagerpau","last":"Guldager","name":"Guldager, Daniel Kring Rasmussen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Hjorth","key":"vonstemannpau","last":"von Stemann","name":"von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rune","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Rune","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Thaning","key":"baypau","last":"Bay","locid":"68f216f4-a404-4a1e-9465-13fdb7ab2690","name":"Bay, Jakob T","name_org":"Bay, Jakob Thaning","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pia Søndergaard","key":"gallepau","last":"Galle","name":"Galle, Pia Søndergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"svensonpau","last":"Svenson","name":"Svenson, Morten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","locid":"ef594d49-5aeb-4d32-80b4-4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Bagge","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"31f07839-f4e2-44f2-8668-3bd6d1a24b2f","name":"Hansen, Morten Bagge","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26080061"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jim.2015.06.010","issn":["00221759","18727905"],"issn_org":["00221759"],"journal":"Journal of Immunological Methods","pages":"62-8","status":"p","title":"Journal of Immunological Methods","volume":"425"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84943665577"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8ddc8463-285a-492f-9889-5cc1e2e258bc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A rapid, accurate and robust particle-based assay for the simultaneous screening of plasma samples for the presence of five different anti-cytokine autoantibodies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-478261","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
