8F-FDG-PET in cancer (hyperPET) : feasibility of a new imaging concept using a clinical PET/MRI scanner","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.98-037613","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms are at increased risk of new solid or haematological cancers, but how prognosis is affected in patients with preceding myeloproliferative neoplasms is unclear. Methods: We used data from population-based medical databases in Denmark from 1980 to 2011 to compare survival between cancer patients with and without a preceding diagnosis of myeloproliferative neoplasm, matched for age, sex, year of diagnosis, and type of cancer. We assessed outcomes by cancer stage and comorbidities. Findings: Data were available for 1246 patients with a history of myeloproliferative neoplasms and we matched 5155 patients without a history of myeloproliferative neoplasm for comparison. Among patients with new localised solid cancers, 5-year survival was 49·8% (95% CI 39·1-59·6) for patients with preceding essential thrombocythaemia, 47·9% (42·1-53·4) for those with preceding polycythaemia vera, and 48·0% (34·1-60·7) for those with preceding chronic myeloid leukaemia. The values were 72·4% (68·4-76·0), 63·9% (61·5-66·2), and 74·3% (68·2-79·4), respectively, in matched patients without preceding myeloproliferative neoplasms. The risk of death among patients with a solid tumour and preceding myeloproliferative neoplasm was 1·21-2·28 times higher than in patients without myeloproliferative neoplasms. Excess mortality risk was observed irrespective of whether new cancers were diagnosed within 5 years or 5 years or more after myeloproliferative neoplasm. Interpretation: Preceding myeloproliferative neoplasm is a predictor for poor outlook in patients who develop new primary cancers. Funding: Lundbeck and Novo Nordisk Foundation Programme for Clinical Research Infrastructure, Danish Cancer Society, and Aarhus University Research Foundation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Henrik","Farkas, Dóra Körmendiné","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Stentoft, Jesper","Toft Sørensen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014524"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"survival of patients with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms and new primary cancers a population based cohort study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2352-3026(15)00092-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-014524","identifier":[{"id":"26688384","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84955695732","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1ab94c31-5ef3-4a0b-9d94-6fe3bf869d25","sdu-6c2862ae-b80a-42b7-9ba0-25106454047f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-42CD57EE6F9704AB9210C2FE111EB6AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/118198051/Survival_of_patients_with_chronic_myeloproliferative.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2352-3026(15)00092-7","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Roskilde Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dóra Körmendiné","key":"farkaspau","last":"Farkas","locid":"573f7202-6799-4977-bf11-f1e017ac21a2","name":"Farkas, Dóra Körmendiné","orcid":"0000-0002-8577-048X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Fynbo","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"b1104ec4-1322-428f-af8f-7771361930bb","name":"Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","orcid":"0000-0002-0727-953X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Stauffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dd2de49b-c3d9-49cb-bb8d-e92119e0b2d1","name":"Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Carl","key":"hasselbalchpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stentoftpau","last":"Stentoft","locid":"f4c6679c-d7fa-434d-9a23-cb5d6561f719","name":"Stentoft, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26688384"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2352-3026(15)00092-7","issn":["23523026"],"issue":"7","journal":"The Lancet Haematology","publisher":"The Lancet Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Haematology","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84955695732"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1ab94c31-5ef3-4a0b-9d94-6fe3bf869d25","sdu-6c2862ae-b80a-42b7-9ba0-25106454047f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Survival of patients with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms and new primary cancers : a population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-014524","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: The supply of long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids (LC-PUFA) during pregnancy and early lactation has been shown to affect cognitive development in preterm infants, but the effect on early neurodevelopment of late-preterm infants has not yet been examined. Aim: To examine the fatty acid composition of late-preterm human milk and identify possible associations between infant LC-PUFA status and perinatal as well as 1-year neurobehavioral outcomes. Methods: Mother’s milk and erythrocytes (RBC) were sampled from 53 Danish late-preterm infants (33-36 weeks of gestation) 1 week and 1 month after delivery, and 3 months corrected age. Fatty acid composition was determined by gas-liquid chromatography. Neurodevelopmental outcomes were assessed by the Nicu Network Neurobehavioral Scale (NNNS) at 1 week and 1 month and the Bayley Scales (BSID-III) at 1 year corrected age. Results: We found that breast-milk content of arachidonic acid (AA) and docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) was similar to reported fatty acid compositions of term human milk. Infant RBC-AA decreased from 1 week to 1 month of age and the size of the decrease was associated with better NNNS-scores at 1 month, specifically on regulation (p=0.03). Infant RBC-AA at 1 month was also associated with a lower 1-year corrected age BSID-III score of receptive language (p=0.05) and fine motor development (p=0.03). Infant RBC-DHA did not ecrease significantly after delivery and was not associated with any of the developmental outcomes. Conclusion: Breast-milk LC-PUFA content was reflected in the RBC LC-PUFA status of the infant. Early RBC-AA status was associated with both early and long-term neurobehavioral development, but not in a consistent way.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brøndum Andersen, Stine","I. Hellgren, Lars","Larsen, Mette Krogh","Verder, Henrik","Lauritzen, Lotte"],"cuid":["S03-095.30-018465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Breastfeeding","Erythrocytes","Human milk","Late preterm infant","Long chain polyunsaturated fatty acid","Neurodevelopment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long chain polyunsaturated fatty acids in breast milk and erythrocytes and neurodevelopmental outcomes in danish late preterm infants","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4172/2376-127x.1000160","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-095.30-018465","ids":["au-4f90d9d6-2bca-4048-9247-b3e6bf7915a7","dtu-fa28297f-15c5-43ef-8ff1-bc9bc918565c","ku-5f82bc80-5c69-4d76-ae68-146a0b4958ee"],"keyword":["Breastfeeding","Erythrocytes","Human milk","Late-preterm infant","Long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acid","Neurodevelopment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E3156CDED7CB1238410D74A2BCEB04F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4172/2376-127x.1000160","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/118708383/Long_chain_polyunsaturated_fatty_acids_in_breast_milk_and_erythrocytes_and_neurodevelopmental_outcomes_in_Danish_late_preterm_infants.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/153757526/Andersen_et_al_Journal_of_Pregnancy_and_Child_Health_2015_Vol_2_3_1000160.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/87157304/Long_Chain_Polyunsaturated_Fa