order to reduce the risk of venous thromboembolism. A systematic review.","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-074182","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to compare 111In-labeled leukocyte single-photon emission computed tomography (SPECT) and 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose (18F-FDG) positron emission tomography (PET) to PET with tracers that potentially could improve detection of osteomyelitis. We chose 11C-methionine, 11C-PK11195 and 68Ga-citrate and validated their diagnostic utility in a porcine haematogenous osteomyelitis model. Four juvenile 14-15 weeks old female pigs were scanned seven days after intra-arterial inoculation in the right femoral artery with a porcine strain of Staphylococcus aureus using a sequential scan protocol with 18F-FDG, 68Ga-citrate, 11C-methionine, 11C-PK11195, 99mTc-Nanocoll and 111In-labelled autologous leukocytes. This was followed by necropsy of the pigs and gross pathology, histopathology and microbial examination. The pigs developed a total of five osteomyelitis lesions, five lesions characterized as abscesses/cellulitis, arthritis in three joints and five enlarged lymph nodes. None of the tracers accumulated in joints with arthritis. By comparing the 10 infectious lesions, 18F-FDG accumulated in nine, 111In-leukocytes in eight, 11C-methionine in six, 68Ga-citrate in four and 11C-PK11195 accumulated in only one lesion. Overall, 18F-FDG PET was superior to 111In-leukocyte SPECT in marking infectious and proliferative, i.e. hyperplastic, lesions. However, leukocyte SPECT was performed as early scans, approximately 6 h after injection of the leukocytes, to match the requirements of the 18 h long scan protocol. 11C-methionine and possibly 68Ga-citrate may be useful for diagnosis of soft issue lesions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nielsen, Ole L.","Afzelius, Pia","Bender, Dirk","Schønheyder, Henrik C.","Leifsson, Páll S.","Nielsen, Karin M.","Larsen, Jytte O.","Jensen, Svend B.","Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-185937"],"event":{"end":"2014-11-21","place":"København, dk","start":"2014-11-21","title":"SPECT and PET imaging in porcine inflammation and infection models","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of autologous 000000000111in leukocytes 000000000018f fdg 000000000011c methionine 000000000011c pk000000011195 and 000000000068ga citrate for diagnostic nuclear imaging in a juvenile porcine haematogenous staphylococcus aureus osteomyelitis model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-185937","ids":["au-6324ce6e-79e1-401f-a1c4-f7e0202c717b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-09EF2211D69E88F69D02DFCD0A792CC0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Nuclear Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole L.","key":"nielsenolelpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Ole L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia","key":"afzeliuspiapau","last":"Afzelius","name":"Afzelius, Pia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dirk","key":"benderdirkpau","last":"Bender","locid":"8dc9c132-74d9-4440-97e8-c6b77d48785b","name":"Bender, Dirk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik C.","key":"schønheyderhenrikcpau","last":"Schønheyder","name":"Schønheyder, Henrik C.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Páll S.","key":"leifssonpállspau","last":"Leifsson","name":"Leifsson, Páll S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin M.","key":"nielsenkarinmpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Karin M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jytte O.","key":"larsenjytteopau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jytte O.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Svend B.","key":"jensensvendbpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Svend B.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aage Kristian Olsen","key":"alstrupaagekristianolsenpau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"fa66f5b8-0468-4e85-b570-969776c5ebde","name":"Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","orcid":"0000-0002-0084-9122","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6324ce6e-79e1-401f-a1c4-f7e0202c717b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Comparison of autologous 111In-leukocytes, 18F-FDG, 11C-methionine, 11C-PK11195 and 68Ga-citrate for diagnostic nuclear imaging in a juvenile porcine haematogenous Staphylococcus aureus osteomyelitis model","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-185937","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A new MR methodology, hyperpolarized MR spectroscopy (MRS), enhances the MRS signals by more than a factor 10,000, enabling fast and unique insight into in situ metabolic processes. So far the method has provided new and exciting metabolic details in prostate, heart, brain, kidney and liver examinations. In diseases characterized by abnormal metabolic profiles, such as in diabetes and tumour tissue, hyperpolarized MRS provides highly detailed spatial information as well as quantitative estimates of individual steps in glycolysis and real-time amino acid metabolism.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Laustsen, Christoffer","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Pedersen, Michael","Ringgaard, Steffen","Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-230176"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolariseret magnetisk resonans kan in vivo kvantificere cellulær metabolisme","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk/files/ugeskriftet.dk/artikel_11562.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-230176","identifier":[{"id":"84906832152","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25292470","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b0c13c2e-ea7f-4fec-adeb-438f6830920f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6CDEBED50DCECF17B077F0DE9B2CE1D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk/files/ugeskriftet.dk/artikel_11562.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus Uni