{"abstract":"An important and voluminous literature on the external perceptions of the EU has emerged, providing insights into how the world sees the EU. This review article argues that the literature on external perceptions is helpful for understanding the outside world’s approach to the EU from a constructivist perspective. The external perception literature also makes an important contribution to the debate about how and whether to look at the EU as a normative power in international politics. The external perception literature also points to a difference between the way in which the EU presents itself and the perception of the EU by other nations. This gap is viewed in the external perception literature as a problem for the EU as an international actor – the EU is presented as less than a full blown international actor in spite of what it assumes to be its potential in international politics. The main argument made in this article is that this view of the gap is a problem for the EU as an international actor and has broad implications. The articulation of the gap as a problem works to singling out the EU as an international actor with special problems and thus may contribute to creating or reinforcing the predicament that it is observing.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541016"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the external perceptions litterature and the construction of gaps in european union foreign policy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1057/ipr.2014.6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-541016","ids":["ku-f73818ef-88bd-4253-b25d-a808ef8c147c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-38886D1B2E3BB3325EC1C1FE50CEF48F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1057/ipr.2014.6","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for European Politics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"36bbf99a-f2ff-4406-b1ca-f9cb7be18f17","name":"Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1057/ipr.2014.6","issn":["20502982","20502990"],"issn_org":["20502982"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Politics Review","pages":"11-18","status":"p","title":"International Politics Review","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f73818ef-88bd-4253-b25d-a808ef8c147c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The external perceptions litterature and the construction of gaps in European Union Foreign Policy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541016","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Lars Henrik","Eriksen, Anne Haahr Mellergaard","Høgdall, Dan","Larsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-591848"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness study of gemcitabine oxaliplatin and capecitabine as first line treatment for nonresectable biliary tract cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://meeting.ascopubs.org/cgi/content/abstract/32/3_suppl/334?sid=4c6d7841-4301-4f39-9085-ca2f4755945e","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-591848","ids":["sdu-40f9afa9-d59e-4c41-b07e-3d27ab321f8a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-810DBFE044FFCB17A7BF15EE3FA056B2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5b427622-91b5-4f6e-b14f-2945da9dad8c","name":"Jensen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0020-1537","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Haahr Mellergaard","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"a10198b9-6d46-4804-ac34-edf31e841dd1","name":"Eriksen, Anne Haahr Mellergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","name":"Høgdall, Dan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0732183X","15277755"],"issn_org":["0732183X"],"issue":"3 Suppl.","journal":"Journal of Clinical Oncology","paperid":"334","publisher":"American Society of Clinical Oncology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Oncology","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-40f9afa9-d59e-4c41-b07e-3d27ab321f8a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effectiveness study of gemcitabine, oxaliplatin, and capecitabine as first-line treatment for nonresectable biliary tract cancer","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-591848","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Diagnosis of T-cell large granular lymphocytic leukemia (T-LGL) is often challenging because clinical and laboratory characteristics are overlapping with nonneoplastic conditions. Recently, mutation in the STAT3 gene has been identified as a recurrent genetic abnormality in T-LGL. STAT3 mutation, therefore, represents a promising marker in T-LGL diagnostics. We developed a new quantitative next-generation sequencing assay that allows sensitive analysis of the STAT3 gene. The assay was used to study the utility of STAT3 mutation analysis as a diagnostic tool in T-LGL. The study included 16 T-LGL patients. A total of 15 mutations, including 2 new mutations (G618R and K658R), were detected in 12 patients (75%), with mutation levels ranging from 2.5% to 45.6% mutation-positive alleles. Next-generation sequencing detected 50% more mutations than Sanger sequencing. Blood samples from 20 healthy blood donors all tested negative, thus demonstrating the specificity of the assay. The results also indicated that mutation levels in blood and bone marrow are not systematically different, and next-generation sequencing-based STAT3 mutation analysis represents a sensitive method for monitoring residual disease as demonstrated in a patient receiving pentostatin. We demonstrate the clinical relevance of next-generation sequencing-based STAT3 mutation analysis, which represents a sensitive and specific diagnostic marker in T-LGL that allows assessment of molecular residual disease, which may improve clinical decision making.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kielsgaard Kristensen, Thomas","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Rewes, Annika","Frederiksen, Henrik","Thomassen, Mads","Møller, Michael Boe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-644462"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical relevance of sensitive and quantitative stat000000000003 mutation analysis using next generation sequencing in t cell large granular lymphocytic leukemia","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmoldx.2014.02.005","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-644462","identifier":[{"id":"84902995583","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24797340","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-f8ead498-4218-4fba-b0c0-37c23a1f4beb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-42D1825407335E18535680286C7F1AA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmoldx.2014.02.005","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Pathology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"kielsgaardkristensenpau","last":"Kielsgaard Kristensen","locid":"856a2e2c-1086-494e-8865-77215baac167","name":"Kielsgaard Kristensen, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7cfc93bc-88f4-48fa-86de-6b0147dc2825","name":"Larsen, Martin Jakob","name_org":"Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0003-4107-8771","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"rewespau","last":"Rewes","locid":"55130775-4710-4f55-b865-88054ff8b4c9","name":"Rewes, Annika","ran