{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Recent evidence suggests that there is an association between infection and venous thromboembolism (VTE). Here, we examined the risk of VTE after Staphylococcus aureus bacteraemia (SAB) compared to the risk in control subjects. DESIGN AND SETTING: Register-based nationwide observational cohort study of hospitalized patients and matched control subjects from the general population in Denmark between 1995 and 2008. RESULTS: Amongst 15 669 SAB cases and 156 690 controls, 182 and 511, respectively, experienced VTE within 1 year. The overall incidence rate (IR) of VTE amongst cases was highest within the first 30 days [IR of deep vein thrombosis (DVT), 39.3 (95% confidence interval (CI) 28.9-53.4)/1000 person-years (PYs); IR of pulmonary embolism (PE), 16.3 (95% CI 10.1-26.2)/1000 PYs]. IRs of DVT were particularly increased amongst cases with a previous diagnosis of VTE, community-acquired infection, a history of injection drug use and in younger age groups. The overall hazard ratio of VTE for cases compared to controls declined from 15.6 (95% CI 10.3-23.5) in the first 30 days after SAB to 4.5 (95% CI 3.2-6.2) from 181 to 365 days after infection. The increased risk of VTE amongst SAB patients persisted after excluding cases with identified VTE risk factors. CONCLUSIONS: There was a particularly high risk of VTE during the first month following an episode of SAB. The risk declined over time, but remained at a threefold increased level compared to control subjects, suggesting that there are shared risk factors for SAB and VTE. Patients with SAB and well-documented risk factors for VTE may benefit from thromboprophylaxis.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Mejer, Niels","Westh, Henrik T.","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Jensen, A G","Larsen, A R","Skov, R","Benfield, Thomas Lars Vibe"],"cuid":["S02-092.83-010121"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Danish Staphylococcal Bacteraemia Study Group","The Danish Staphylococcal Bacteraemia Study Group"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Age Distribution","Aged","Bacteremia","Case Control Studies","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Humans","Incidence","Inpatients","Male","Middle Aged","Registries","Risk Factors","Staphylococcal Infections","Staphylococcus aureus","Substance Abuse Intravenous","Venous thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased risk of venous thromboembolism within the first year after staphylococcus aureus bacteraemia a nationwide observational matched cohort study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/joim.12147","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.83-010121","identifier":[{"id":"24118528","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84897028877","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000333310700005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d365d363-4a52-40e6-bc9a-5ac59c8f9179","ku-b38a6565-168d-42d0-88bb-1e95d2fec38a"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Age Distribution","Aged","Bacteremia","Case-Control Studies","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Humans","Incidence","Inpatients","Male","Middle Aged","Registries","Risk Factors","Staphylococcal Infections","Staphylococcus aureus","Substance Abuse, Intravenous","Venous Thromboembolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6B68049F4725F27386AD8BF93D972F35"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/joim.12147","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Microbiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"the danish staphylococcal bacteraemia study group","name":"The Danish Staphylococcal Bacteraemia Study Group","role":"oau"},{"affno":4,"key":"danish staphylococcal bacteraemia study group","name":"Danish Staphylococcal Bacteraemia Study Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"mejerpau","last":"Mejer","name":"Mejer, Niels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Carl","key":"schønheyderpau","last":"Schønheyder","locid":"d35b264a-6efc-467d-ac9d-e558542ef8a8","name":"Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"A G","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, A G","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"A R","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, A R","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"R","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, R","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"T","key":"benfieldpau","last":"Benfield","locid":"03fdbbba-4bc0-41aa-845b-81ba0bded9ba","name":"Benfield, Thomas","name_org":"Benfield, T","orcid":"0000-0003-0698-9385","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24118528"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/joim.12147","issn":["09546820","09557873"],"issn_org":["09546820"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Internal Medicine","pages":"387-397","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of Internal Medicine","volume":"275"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897028877"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d365d363-4a52-40e6-bc9a-5ac59c8f9179","ku-b38a6565-168d-42d0-88bb-1e95d2fec38a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Increased risk of venous thromboembolism within the first year after Staphylococcus aureus bacteraemia : A nationwide observational matched cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.83-010121","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Good glycemic control is crucial to prevent the onset and progression of late diabetic complications, but insulin treatment often fails to achieve normalization of glycemic control to the level seen in healthy controls. In fact, recent experimental studies indicate that insufficient treatment with insulin, resulting in poor glycemic control, has an additional effect on progression of late diabetic complications, than poor glycemic control on its own. We therefore compared renal metabolic alterations during conditions of poor glycemic control with and without suboptimal insulin administration, which did not restore glycemic control, to streptozotocin (STZ)-diabetic rats using noninvasive hyperpolarized (13)C-pyruvate magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and blood oxygenation level-dependent (BOLD) (1)H-MRI to determine renal metabolic flux and oxygen availability, respectively. Suboptimal insulin administration increased pyruvate utilization and metabolic flux via both anaerobic and aerobic pathways in diabetic rats even though insulin did not affect kidney oxygen availability, HbA1c, or oxidative stress. These results imply direct effects of insulin in the regulation of cellular substrate utilization and metabolic fluxes during conditions of poor glycemic control. The study demonstrates that poor glycemic control in combination with suboptimal insulin administration accelerates metabolic alterations by increasing both anaerobic and aerobic metabolism resulting in increased utilization of energy substrates. The results demonstrate the importance of tight glycemic control in insulinopenic diabetes, and that insulin, when administered insufficiently, adds an additional burden on top of poor glycemic control.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Laustsen, Christoffer","Lipsø, Kasper","Østergaard, Jakob Appel","Nørregaard, Rikke","Flyvbjerg, Allan","Pedersen, Michael","Palm, Fredrik","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan-Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-098.22-026419"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","Linköping University"],"keyword":["Hyperpolarization","Kidney","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Renal metabolism","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insufficient insulin administration to diabetic rats increases substrate utilization and maintains lactate production in the kidney","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/104362999/phy212233.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.22-026419","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4332212","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85003475029","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25501426","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bd3ba6f2-e453-41c4-b69f-7124c20db94d","dtu-2e341459-82d0-403f-91ae-672dc4f52f48"],"keyword":["Hyperpolarization","Kidney","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Renal metabolism","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AF39179102A2DCB70B7CDFA4AA9D3C22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/104362999/phy212233.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.12233","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"linköping university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linköping University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ge healthcare","name":"GE Healthcare","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Kasper Wigh","key":"lipsøpau","last":"Lipsø","locid":"68c4d525-3c44-4330-8725-7d6bc61ccc8f","name":"Lipsø, Hans Kasper Wigh","orcid":"0000-0002-8791-9997","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Appel","key":"ostergaardpau","last":"Ostergaard","locid":"e6e06b1e-ca0c-4f92-99c3-66e7d3704b09","name":"Østergaard, Jakob Appel","name_org":"Ostergaard, Jakob Appel","orcid":"0000-0002-9877-5327","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"nørregaardpau","last":"Nørregaard","locid":"1475b841-344f-4845-8ed0-f6569b97452c","name":"Nørregaard, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-0580-373X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"flyvbjergpau","last":"Flyvbjerg","locid":"29cf36bd-c1a0-4026-8c90-a70cb1f46402","name":"Flyvbjerg, Allan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"871199c4-33bb-4fac-95ef-9a2266f30695","name":"Pedersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1146-0382","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fredrik","key":"palmpau","last":"Palm","name":"Palm, Fredrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25501426"],"pub":{"doi":"10.14814/phy2.12233","issn":["2051817X"],"issue":"12","journal":"Physiological Reports","pages":"1-8","paperid":"2","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Physiological Reports","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85003475029"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bd3ba6f2-e453-41c4-b69f-7124c20db94d","dtu-2e341459-82d0-403f-91ae-672dc4f52f48"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Insufficient insulin administration to diabetic rats increases substrate utilization and maintains lactate production in the kidney","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.22-026419","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: It is important that patients are well-informed about risks and benefits of therapies to help them decide whether to accept medical therapy. Different numerical formats can be used in risk communication but It remains unclear how the different formats affect decisions made by real-life patients. AIM: To compare the impact of using Prolongation Of Life (POL) and Absolute Risk Reduction (ARR) information formats to express effectiveness of cholesterol-lowering therapy on patients' redemptions of statin prescriptions, and on patients' confidence in their decision and satisfaction with the risk communication. DESIGN AND SETTING: Cluster-randomised clinical trial in general practices. Thirty-four Danish GPs from 23 practices participated in a primary care-based clinical trial concerning use of quantitative effectiveness formats for risk communication in health prevention consultations. METHOD: GPs were cluster-randomised (treating practices as clusters) to inform patients about cardiovascular mortality risk and the effectiveness of statin treatment using either POL or ARR formats. Patients' redemptions of statin prescriptions were obtained from a regional prescription database. The COMRADE questionnaire was used to measure patients' confidence in their decision and satisfaction with the risk communication. RESULTS: Of the 240 patients included for analyses, 112 were allocated to POL information and 128 to ARR. Patients redeeming a statin prescription totalled six (5.4%) when informed using POL, and 32 (25.0%) when using ARR. The level of confidence in decision and satisfaction with risk communication did not differ between the risk formats. CONCLUSION: Patients redeemed statin prescriptions less often when their GP communicated treatment effectiveness using POL compared with ARR.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Harmsen, Charlotte Gry","Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Nexøe, Jørgen","Støvring, Henrik","Gyrd-Hansen, Dorte","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Edwards, Adrian","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016653"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cardiovascular disease","Decision making","General practice","Patient Participation","Risk Assessment","Risk communication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"communicating risk using absolute risk reduction or prolongation of life formats cluster randomised trial in general practice","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3399/bjgp14X677824","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-016653","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3964454","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24686884","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84898728989","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-36fe1d0b-da6b-44ce-9533-fb2c023e06e0","sdu-f29921a7-1439-43dd-88c0-df8daeb3ddee"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular disease","Decision making","General practice","Patient participation","Risk assessment","Risk communication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E2627E48C0967C904CF980BABC7C9E23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3399/bjgp14X677824","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Gry","key":"harmsenpau","last":"Harmsen","locid":"90a39c48-5b46-4168-bde9-f9b50f1aa516","name":"Harmsen, Charlotte Gry","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivar Sønbø","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Veldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"nexøepau","last":"Nexøe","locid":"c0ef955d-56da-4dd2-b269-235028a380fa","name":"Nexøe, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-3806-5139","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"støvringpau","last":"Støvring","locid":"c19fb430-dcd1-4a13-995f-4247f8ebc11d","name":"Støvring, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-5821-2351","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"gyrdhansenpau","last":"Gyrd-Hansen","name":"Gyrd-Hansen, Dorte","orcid":"0000-0003-1137-2304","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","name":"Edwards, Adrian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24686884"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3399/bjgp14x677824","issn":["09601643","14785242"],"issn_org":["09601643"],"issue":"621","journal":"British Journal of General Practice","publisher":"Royal College of General Practitioners","status":"p","title":"British Journal of General Practice","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84898728989"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-36fe1d0b-da6b-44ce-9533-fb2c023e06e0","sdu-f29921a7-1439-43dd-88c0-df8daeb3ddee"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Communicating risk using absolute risk reduction or prolongation of life formats : cluster-randomised trial in general practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-016653","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To assess mortality in patients with central retinal vein occlusion (CRVO). DESIGN: Registry-based cohort study. PARTICIPANTS AND CONTROLS: Four hundred thirty-nine photographically verified CRVO patients and a control cohort of 2195 unexposed subjects matched by age and gender and alive on the date CRVO was diagnosed in the corresponding case. METHODS: Data from nationwide registries were used to compare mortality rates in CRVO patients with a control cohort over a mean follow-up of 5.1 years for cases and of 5.7 years for controls. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Hazard ratios (HRs) obtained by Cox regression and standardized mortality ratios (SMRs) stratified by age and gender served as measures of relative mortality risk. RESULTS: Mortality was higher in patients with CRVO (HR, 1.45; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.19-1.76) than in the control cohort, adjusted for age, gender, and time of diagnosis. Mortality was comparable between the 2 groups (HR, 1.19; 95% CI, 0.96-1.46) when adjusting for overall occurrence of cardiovascular disease and diabetes. Subgroup analysis found that the age-stratified mortality rate was increased significantly in the total group of men (SMR, 1.27; 95% CI, 1.03-1.56) and in women 60 to 69 years of age (SMR, 1.94; 95% CI, 1.22-3.08). CONCLUSIONS: Central retinal vein occlusion was associated with an overall increase in mortality compared with controls that was attributed statistically to cardiovascular disorders and diabetes. We recommend treatment of hypertension and diabetes, if present, and referral of patients found to have CRVO who are not already being treated by a primary care physician.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bertelsen, Mette","Linneberg, Allan","Christoffersen, Nynne","Vorum, Henrik","Gade, Else","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S03-091.18-000965"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Bertelsen, Mette"],"keyword":["Age Distribution","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Fluorescein Angiography","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Photography","Proportional Hazards Models","Registries","Retinal vein occlusion","Risk Factors","Sex Distribution"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mortality in patients with central retinal vein occlusion","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ophtha.2013.07.025","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-091.18-000965","identifier":[{"id":"24053999","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000332401800012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84896734212","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1260d0ab-4479-4d62-a3fb-3819aab964b9","ku-68a0c4db-7a8a-4b3b-802b-8f794396b3aa","sdu-8d7b19c8-f762-4f65-9e3d-d44173eefe70"],"keyword":["Age Distribution","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Fluorescein Angiography","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Photography","Proportional Hazards Models","Registries","Retinal Vein Occlusion","Risk Factors","Sex Distribution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-7A39A758CB34986B90F2A6EACC4417BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ophtha.2013.07.025","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Medicinsk Sociologi"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Ophthalmology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Ophthalmology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","name":"Bertelsen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nynne","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","name":"Christoffersen, Nynne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"vorumpau","last":"Vorum","locid":"60554352-1557-4c7b-905d-e4b7c7f8c94a","name":"Vorum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-7600-0731","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Else","key":"gadepau","last":"Gade","locid":"50e08437-f47d-4750-a528-4c1c04f77f34","name":"Gade, Else","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24053999"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ophtha.2013.07.025","issn":["01616420","15494713"],"issn_org":["01616420"],"issue":"3","journal":"Ophthalmology","pages":"637-642","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ophthalmology","volume":"121"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84896734212"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1260d0ab-4479-4d62-a3fb-3819aab964b9","ku-68a0c4db-7a8a-4b3b-802b-8f794396b3aa","sdu-8d7b19c8-f762-4f65-9e3d-d44173eefe70"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mortality in Patients with Central Retinal Vein Occlusion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.18-000965","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES:: To investigate single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in the gene encoding interleukin-7 receptor α (IL7RA) as predictors for CD4 T-cell change after initiation of combination antiretroviral therapy (cART) in HIV-infected whites. DESIGN:: SNPs in IL7RA were determined in the Danish HIV Cohort Study. METHODS:: CD4 T-cell changes were estimated 6 months, 1, 2, and 5 years after initiation of cART in 1683 HIV-infected virally suppressed individuals. Five SNPs in IL7RA were examined as predictors for CD4 T-cell change in the first (0-6 months after initiation of cART) and second phase (>6 months after initiation of cART) of immune recovery. Univariable and multivariable analyses including age, sex, calendar period, CD4 nadir, and baseline CD4 T-cell count and viral load as covariates were performed. RESULTS:: Individuals carrying two T-alleles in rs6897932 had faster CD4 T-cell recovery compared with individuals carrying a C-allele in the first phase of immune recovery [mean CD4 T-cell change, cells/μL (95% confidence interval), in TT: 177 (151-203), CT: 131 (119-143), CC: 141 (132-151), P = 0.018]. No isolated effect of rs6897932 on CD4 T-cell change was found in the second phase of immune recovery; however, the initial difference in CD4 T-cell recovery remained during 5 years. The effect was most pronounced in individuals above 40 years of age. CONCLUSION:: T-allele homozygosity in rs6897932 is a predictor for faster CD4 T-cell recovery after initiation of cART in HIV-infected whites, however, only in the first phase of immune recovery.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hartling, Hans J","Thørner, Lise W","Erikstrup, Christian","Harritshøj, Lene H","Kronborg, Gitte","Pedersen, Court","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Helleberg, Marie","Gerstoft, Jan","Obel, Niels","Ullum, Henrik","Nielsen, Susanne D"],"cuid":["S03-093.36-012869"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Combination antiretroviral therapy","Interleukin 7 receptor","Single nucleotide polymorphisms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"polymorphism in interleukin 000000000007 receptor α gene is associated with faster cd000000000004 t cell recovery after initiation of combination antiretroviral therapy","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAD.0000000000000354","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-093.36-012869","identifier":[{"id":"84904160711","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24911352","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-03b2f01d-6c59-485c-a01c-31d8203864c4","ku-0b647c45-157d-493b-b4c3-aec7eb679833","sdu-1c723a51-b5d9-4aac-a76c-73f5573ef0b6"],"keyword":["HIV,immune recovery","combination antiretroviral therapy","interleukin-7 receptor","rs6897932","single-nucleotide polymorphisms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-439C174A34A66C6FA6CE75448DF65F44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAD.0000000000000354","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans J","key":"hartlingpau","last":"Hartling","name":"Hartling, Hans J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise W","key":"thørnerpau","last":"Thørner","name":"Thørner, Lise W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","locid":"523ae417-65a9-46aa-b665-0d88271dc0b9","name":"Erikstrup, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6551-6647","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene H","key":"harritshøjpau","last":"Harritshøj","name":"Harritshøj, Lene H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gitte","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"6dfd64b6-b92a-46ff-9008-4c065e9cbddb","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Court","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7f2e0dec-1687-4283-ac30-53e73c124437","name":"Pedersen, Court","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten S","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2435cb82-03bd-498b-909d-1ef0e99443fe","name":"Larsen, Carsten Schade","name_org":"Larsen, Carsten S","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"hellebergpau","last":"Helleberg","name":"Helleberg, Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jan","key":"gerstoftpau","last":"Gerstoft","locid":"c7e948db-fe0f-4a67-9b86-7ccc43ae64f5","name":"Gerstoft, Jan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Niels","key":"obelpau","last":"Obel","locid":"47b44abc-6c99-4a76-b8b0-ca53b033951b","name":"Obel, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-5031-0045","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","locid":"ef594d49-5aeb-4d32-80b4-4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne D","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Susanne D","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24911352"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/qad.0000000000000354","issn":["02699370"],"issue":"12","journal":"AIDS","pages":"1739-1748","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"AIDS","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904160711"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-03b2f01d-6c59-485c-a01c-31d8203864c4","ku-0b647c45-157d-493b-b4c3-aec7eb679833","sdu-1c723a51-b5d9-4aac-a76c-73f5573ef0b6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Polymorphism in interleukin-7 receptor α gene is associated with faster CD4 T-cell recovery after initiation of combination antiretroviral therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.36-012869","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Partial migration is common in many animal taxa; however, the physiological variation underpinning migration strategies remains poorly understood. Among salmonid fishes, brown trout (Salmo trutta) is one of the species that exhibits the most complex variation in sympatric migration strategies, expressed as a migration continuum, ranging from residency to anadromy. In looking at brown trout, our objective with this study was to test the hypothesis that variation in migration strategies is underpinned by physiological variation. Prior to migration, physiological samples were taken from fish in the stream and then released at the capture site. Using telemetry, we subsequently classified fish as resident, short-distance migrants (potamodromous), or long-distance migrants (potentially anadromous). Our results revealed that fish belonging to the resident strategy differed from those exhibiting any of the two migratory strategies. Gill Na,K-ATPase activity, condition factor, and indicators of nutritional status suggested that trout from the two migratory strategies were smoltified and energetically depleted before leaving the stream, compared to those in the resident strategy. The trout belonging to the two migratory strategies were generally similar; however, lower triacylglycerides levels in the short-distance migrants indicated that they were more lipid depleted prior to migration compared with the long-distance migrants. In the context of migration cost, we suggest that additional lipid depletion makes migrants more inclined to terminate migration at the first given feeding opportunity, whereas individuals that are less lipid depleted will migrate farther. Collectively, our data suggest that the energetic state of individual fish provides a possible mechanism underpinning the migration continuum in brown trout.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Boel, Mikkel","Aarestrup, Kim","Baktoft, Henrik","Larsen, Torben","Madsen, Steffen","Malte, Hans","Skov, Christian","Svendsen, Jon Christian","Koed, Anders"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-014086"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Boel, Mikkel"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Porto"],"keyword":["10069 Biochemistry studies Minerals","10802 Enzymes General and comparative studies coenzymes","16004 Respiratory system Physiology and biochemistry","Animal Migration","Animal Nutritional Physiological Phenomena","Animals","Arctic charr","Biochemistry and Molecular Biophysics","Body composition","CHAR SALVELINUS ALPINUS","Denmark","Energy Metabolism","Enzyme activity","Enzymology","JUVENILE ATLANTIC SALMON","Life history variation","Lipid Metabolism","Na K ATPase activity","Niche shift","Nutritional Status","PARR SMOLT TRANSFORMATION","Partial migration","Physiology","Respiration","Respiratory System","Rivers","STEELHEAD TROUT","Seasonal variations","Trout","Zoology","gill respiratory system","northern Norway","physiological basis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the physiological basis of the migration continuum in brown trout salmo trutta","src":["au","dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1086/674869","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-100.00-014086","identifier":[{"id":"24642550","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000332923400014","type":"wos"},{"id":"84896465147","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-14b01061-bf9f-47bb-96d8-ae404529de94","au-45df200e-5fd6-4385-9564-6ae109f622d3","dtu-018e8537-5a1f-47d9-b479-2023a9d1cc03","sdu-92e7997c-bd56-4