enaar, J. A.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Annalisa","key":"pantostipau","last":"Pantosti","name":"Pantosti, Annalisa","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"hallinpau","last":"Hallin","name":"Hallin, Marie","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc J.","key":"struelenspau","last":"Struelens","name":"Struelens, Marc J.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Giles","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","name":"Edwards, Giles","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"boesepau","last":"Boese","name":"Boese, R.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrich","key":"nuebelpau","last":"Nuebel","name":"Nuebel, Ulrich","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wolfgang","key":"wittepau","last":"Witte","name":"Witte, Wolfgang","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0088083","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"2","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e88083","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84894613414"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-34c550af-7f5a-4dcb-a184-950b7319877c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Phylogenetic Analysis of Staphylococcus aureus CC398 Reveals a Sub-Lineage Epidemiologically Associated with Infections in Horses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-320286","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"One of the first issues that emerges when a prokaryotic organism of interest is encountered is the question of what it is--that is, which species it is. The 16S rRNA gene formed the basis of the first method for sequence-based taxonomy and has had a tremendous impact on the field of microbiology. Nevertheless, the method has been found to have a number of shortcomings. In the current study, we trained and benchmarked five methods for whole-genome sequence-based prokaryotic species identification on a common data set of complete genomes: (i) SpeciesFinder, which is based on the complete 16S rRNA gene; (ii) Reads2Type that searches for species-specific 50-mers in either the 16S rRNA gene or the gyrB gene (for the Enterobacteraceae family); (iii) the ribosomal multilocus sequence typing (rMLST) method that samples up to 53 ribosomal genes; (iv) TaxonomyFinder, which is based on species-specific functional protein domain profiles; and finally (v) KmerFinder, which examines the number of cooccurring k-mers (substrings of k nucleotides in DNA sequence data). The performances of the methods were subsequently evaluated on three data sets of short sequence reads or draft genomes from public databases. In total, the evaluation sets constituted sequence data from more than 11,000 isolates covering 159 genera and 243 species. Our results indicate that methods that sample only chromosomal, core genes have difficulties in distinguishing closely related species which only recently diverged. The KmerFinder method had the overall highest accuracy and correctly identified from 93% to 97% of the isolates in the evaluations sets.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Mette Voldby","Cosentino, Salvatore","Lukjancenko, Oksana","Saputra, Dhany","Rasmussen, Simon","Hasman, Henrik","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Aarestrup, Frank Møller","Ussery, David","Lund, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-321635"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"benchmarking of methods for genomic taxonomy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.02981-13","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-321635","identifier":[{"id":"24574292","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84899530047","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3993634","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-396f1e23-6fca-4502-ac22-81c646e3bfb7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EAFB63DE954AF88C6024587BC8308DB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.02981-13","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Voldby","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"48f90aec-1c95-444e-a7e5-d7b3ddcf1b7e","name":"Larsen, Mette Voldby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Salvatore","key":"cosentinopau","last":"Cosentino","locid":"4bb9e1cb-cf15-49ec-8242-51af37011a9b","name":"Cosentino, Salvatore","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"lukjancenkopau","last":"Lukjancenko","locid":"21a7ee27-6d90-489b-b8be-207b1e8e7b28","name":"Lukjancenko, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-0102-0364","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dhany","key":"saputrapau","last":"Saputra","locid":"e4761740-b4e8-442f-9716-2cb8833e0da5","name":"Saputra, Dhany","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7dcb9d6e-8054-4bcf-a087-82517b291a32","name":"Rasmussen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-6323-9041","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hasmanpau","last":"Hasman","locid":"2aeb80b4-d42a-4da2-9212-86b697184f40","name":"Hasman, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"sicheritzponténpau","last":"Sicheritz-Pontén","locid":"cc8e7daa-b78f-45ad-a86a-5053a353f74e","name":"Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank Møller","key":"aarestruppau","last":"Aarestrup","locid":"8a1eb030-2c37-4557-bce1-7bc6d5c75aaa","name":"Aarestrup, Frank Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-7116-2723","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"David","key":"usserypau","last":"Ussery","locid":"de2c5cb4-22c8-4ef4-a1e6-752a08f73bbd","name":"Ussery, David","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"d2f5060c-0c9a-4875-820f-91180f3bb685","name":"Lund, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-1108-0491","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24574292"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/jcm.02981-13","issn":["00951137","1070633X"],"issn_org":["00951137"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Clinical Microbiology","pages":"1529-1539","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Microbiology","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84899530047"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-396f1e23-6fca-4502-ac22-81c646e3bfb7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Benchmarking of methods for genomic taxonomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-321635","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The combination of hyperpolarized MRS with diffusion weighting (dw) allows for determination of the apparent diffusion coefficient (ADC), which is indicative of the intra‐ or extracellular localization of the metabolite. Here, a slice‐selective pulsed‐gradient spin echo sequence was implemented to acquire a series of dw spectra from rat muscle in vivo to determine the ADCs of multiple metabolites after a single injection of hyperpolarized [1‐13C]pyruvate. An optimal control optimized universal‐rotation pulse was used for refocusing to minimize signal loss caused by B1 imperfections. Non‐dw spectra were acquired interleaved with the dw spectra and these were used to correct for signal decay during the acquisition as a result of T1 decay, pulse imperfections, flow etc. The data showed that the ADC values for [1‐13C]lactate (0.4–0.7 µm2/ms) and [1‐13C]alanine (0.4–0.9 µm2/ms) were about a factor of two lower than the ADC of [1‐13C]pyruvate (1.1–1.5 µm2/ms). This indicates a more restricted diffusion space for the former two metabolites consistent with lactate and alanine being intracellular. The higher ADC for pyruvate (similar to the proton ADC) reflected that the injected substance was not confined inside the muscle cells but also present extracellular. Copyright © 2014 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Søgaard, Lise Vejby","Schilling, Franz","Janich, Martin A.","Menzel, Marion I.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-323791"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Global Research","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Hyperpolarized 13C","Optimal control","Pyruvate metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo measurement of apparent diffusion coefficients of hyperpolarized 000000000013c labeled metabolites","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.3093","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-323791","identifier":[{"id":"84897964447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4096fc70-2def-4d80-964b-8c219478a9bc"],"keyword":["13C diffusion in vivo","Diffusion-weighted NMR spectroscopy","Hyperpolarized 13C","Intracellular ADC","Optimal control","Pyruvate metabolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7AAB8A1D38935178807BC8F15599D4CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.3093","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"ge global research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"GE Global Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Vejby","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","name":"Søgaard, Lise Vejby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Franz","key":"schillingpau","last":"Schilling","name":"Schilling, Franz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin A.","key":"janichpau","last":"Janich","name":"Janich, Martin A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marion I.","key":"menzelpau","last":"Menzel","name":"Menzel, Marion I.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.3093","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"5","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","pages":"561-569","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","title_org":"N M R in Biomedicine","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897964447"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4096fc70-2def-4d80-964b-8c219478a9bc"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"In vivo measurement of apparent diffusion coefficients of hyperpolarized 13C‐labeled metabolites","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-323791","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarization of [1-13C]pyruvate in solution allows real-time measurement of uptake and metabolism using MR spectroscopic methods. After injection and perfusion, pyruvate is taken up by the cells and enzymatically metabolized into downstream metabolites such as lactate, alanine, and bicarbonate. In this work, we present comprehensive methods for the quantification and interpretation of hyperpolarized 13C metabolite signals. First, a time-domain spectral fitting method is described for the decomposition of FID signals into their metabolic constituents. For this purpose, the required chemical shift frequencies are automatically estimated using a matching pursuit algorithm. Second, a time-discretized formulation of the two-site exchange kinetic model is used to quantify metabolite signal dynamics by two characteristic rate constants in the form of (i) an apparent build-up rate (quantifying the build-up of downstream metabolites from the pyruvate substrate) and (ii) an effective decay rate (summarizing signal depletion due to repetitive excitation, T1-relaxation and backward conversion). The presented spectral and kinetic quantification were experimentally verified in vitro and in vivo using hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate. Using temporally resolved IDEAL spiral CSI, spatially resolved apparent rate constant maps are also extracted. In comparison to single metabolite images, apparent build-up rate constant maps provide improved contrast by emphasizing metabolically active tissues (e.g. tumors) and suppression of high perfusion regions with low conversion (e.g. blood vessels). Apparent build-up rate constant mapping provides a novel quantitative image contrast for the characterization of metabolic activity. Its possible implementation as a quantitative standard will be subject to further studies. Copyright © 2014 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Khegai, O.","Schulte, R. F.","Janich, M. A.","Menzel, M. I.","Farrell, E.","Otto, A. M.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Glaser, S. J.","Haase, A.","Schwaiger, M.","Wiesinger, F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379529"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Global Research","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["1 13C pyruvate","Hyperpolarized 13C","Kinetic modeling","MRSI","Metabolic exchange rate"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"apparent rate constant mapping using hyperpolarized 000000000001 000000000013 c pyruvate","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.3174","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379529","identifier":[{"id":"25156807","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84908031259","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fa859fdc-a5c0-412d-a939-c93265eb088c"],"keyword":["MRSI","[1‐13C]pyruvate","dynamic metabolic imaging","hyperpolarized 13C","kinetic modeling","metabolic exchange rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9374ACEFE235C29727130ABFC7922A6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.3174","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ge global research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"GE Global Research","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"O.","key":"khegaipau","last":"Khegai","name":"Khegai, O.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R. F.","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, R. F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. A.","key":"janichpau","last":"Janich","name":"Janich, M. A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. I.","key":"menzelpau","last":"Menzel","name":"Menzel, M. I.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"farrellpau","last":"Farrell","name":"Farrell, E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A. M.","key":"ottopau","last":"Otto","name":"Otto, A. M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S. J.","key":"glaserpau","last":"Glaser","name":"Glaser, S. J.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"haasepau","last":"Haase","name":"Haase, A.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"schwaigerpau","last":"Schwaiger","name":"Schwaiger, M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"wiesingerpau","last":"Wiesinger","name":"Wiesinger, F.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25156807"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.3174","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"10","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","pages":"1256-1265","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84908031259"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fa859fdc-a5c0-412d-a939-c93265eb088c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Apparent rate constant mapping using hyperpolarized [1-(13) C]pyruvate.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379529","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Following the principles of Reduced Impact Logging (RIL) the construction of roads and log landings together with logging gaps are the most profound direct impacts that a forest operation has on the forest. While the effects of logging gaps have been studied in detail, the impacts of road and log landing construction, and how the forest regenerates after such disturbances, remain poorly understood. This paper investigates the regeneration success of a range of well/lesser-known timber species in a tierra-firme forest concession in Peru. Sample plots (100 m2) were established in areas with three different types of logging induced disturbances: skid trails caused by log extraction, secondary roads and log landings/patios. Seedling establishment of 16 different commercially targeted species groups was examined for these three types of disturbances using a chronosequence of 5 years. As 100 plots were inventoried for each type of disturbance an area of 3 hectares was sampled in total. The regenerative success was compared across disturbance categories, and each species’ response to environmental variables was investigated using zero-inflated negative binomial regression. Regenerative success varied across species groups, with the majority either regenerating significantly better at the least disturbed sites (n = 6) or showing statistically indistinguishable results (n = 9) because of limited regeneration. One species group, Cariniana spp., regenerated best at intermediate sites. The varying response across species groups indicates a need for a more varied forest management. For species with poor regeneration it is recommended to plant saplings (enrichment planting) to ensure forest recovery and species preservation at the landscape level.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Karsten, Rune Juelsborg","Meilby, Henrik","Larsen, Jørgen Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-439670"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regeneration and management of lesser known timber species in the peruvian amazon following disturbance by logging","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foreco.2014.04.035","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-439670","identifier":[{"id":"84901243858","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4d8e3b53-b21a-440d-a78c-1e4ca6b1e60f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FB01390CED55A2C9FB404E8907696870"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0378112714002746","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foreco.2014.04.035","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Environment and Natural Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rune Juelsborg","key":"karstenpau","last":"Karsten","locid":"20d06a78-411f-4425-8aaf-192ff06f01bf","name":"Karsten, Rune Juelsborg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"meilbypau","last":"Meilby","locid":"0ddac490-e5da-4c91-82ba-c64fbcd81e27","name":"Meilby, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3770-3880","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen Bo","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"60b50685-4577-48b2-bc5b-e3d08a155959","name":"Larsen, Jørgen Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.foreco.2014.04.035","issn":["03781127","18727042"],"issn_org":["03781127"],"journal":"Forest Ecology and Management","pages":"76-85","status":"p","title":"Forest Ecology and Management","volume":"327"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901243858"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4d8e3b53-b21a-440d-a78c-1e4ca6b1e60f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Regeneration and management of lesser known timber species in the Peruvian Amazon following disturbance by logging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-439670","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this study we investigate the effects of heritage taxation rules on the economic performance of forestry and, more importantly, on decision making at the forest property level. In Denmark, when a property is handed over from one generation to the next, a heritage tax has to be paid. Apart from this, there is also a tax on the revenue caused by increase in property value during the ownership period. We analyse how the rotation age in model forest properties with given species composition and initial age structure is affected by these two taxes for a planned generational change every 30 years, compared to an unplanned change and a reference model with no tax on heritage or property value increase (or no change of ownership). As the point of departure we apply model properties including 1000 ha of forest and with species compositions representative for different regions in Denmark. This allows us to analyse the basic conditions for private forest owners’ management, but also to examine whether and to what extent the taxation causes changes in management that are sub-optimal from a social point of view.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Meilby, Henrik","Thorsen, Bo Jellesmark","Nord-Larsen, Thomas","Johannsen, Vivian Kvist","Jacobsen, Jette Bredahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-473671"],"event":{"end":"2014-05-24","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2014-05-21","title":"Biennial Meeting of the Scandinavian Society of Forest Economics","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of heritage taxation in danish forestry","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/132142213/Scandinavian_Forest_Economics_No_45.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-473671","ids":["ku-862662dc-914f-41e8-9abb-f94c5c60acbf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-738E7C9B33C9E590F7655D1D6D85072D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/132142213/Scandinavian_Forest_Economics_No_45.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Environment and Natural Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"meilbypau","last":"Meilby","locid":"0ddac490-e5da-4c91-82ba-c64fbcd81e27","name":"Meilby, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3770-3880","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Jellesmark","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","locid":"a11f0f2d-120f-475b-9d08-eadc2de0f6b6","name":"Thorsen, Bo Jellesmark","orcid":"0000-0002-3305-8343","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"nordlarsenpau","last":"Nord-Larsen","locid":"d5b3bda9-5a06-45e4-8c9a-07e768bef87a","name":"Nord-Larsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-5341-6435","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vivian Kvist","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","locid":"50454320-c098-4230-8b34-90829dbe308c","name":"Johannsen, Vivian Kvist","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-9787","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette Bredahl","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"c865ba8d-b14d-4b86-8337-ba9970d36302","name":"Jacobsen, Jette Bredahl","orcid":"0000-0002-1313-6228","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0355032X"],"journal":"Scandinavian Forest Economics","pages":"100","status":"