":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["InMold Biosystems A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thor Christian","key":"hobækpau","last":"Hobæk","locid":"466cc5d8-a472-4572-85ad-6e645e49eab4","name":"Hobæk, Thor Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"pranovpau","last":"Pranov","name":"Pranov, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bent","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7a727b09-e209-47ab-80f7-9df731c2178f","name":"Larsen, Niels Bent","orcid":"0000-0001-6506-3991","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Fourth International Workshop on Analytical Miniaturization and NANOtechnologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","inmold biosystems a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-041f3060-f169-49c7-b33b-3145542bdf2d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Direct Immobilization of Capture Antibodies on Injection Molded Thermoplastics","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305835","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Inline printing and coating methods have been demonstrated to enable a high technical yield of fully roll-to-roll processed polymer tandem solar cell modules. We demonstrate generality by employing different material sets and also describe how the ink systems must be carefully co-developed in order to reach the ambitious objective of a fully printed and coated 14-layer flexible tandem solar cell stack. The roll-to-roll methodologies involved are flexographic printing, rotary screen printing, slot-die coating, X-ray scattering, electrical testing and UV-lamination. Their combination enables the manufacture of completely functional devices in exceptionally high yields. Critical to the ink and process development is a carefully chosen technology transfer to industry method where first a roll coater is employed enabling contactless stack build up, followed by a small roll-to-roll coater fitted to an X-ray machine enabling in situ studies of wet ink deposition and drying mechanisms, ultimately elucidating how a robust inline processed recombination layer is key to a high technical yield. Finally, the transfer to full roll-to-roll processing is demonstrated.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Andersen, Thomas Rieks","Dam, Henrik Friis","Hösel, Markus","Helgesen, Martin","Carlé, Jon Eggert","Larsen-Olsen, Thue Trofod","Gevorgyan, Suren","Andreasen, Jens Wenzel","Adams, Jens","Li, Ning","Machui, Florian","Spyropoulos, George D.","Ameri, Tayebeh","Lemaıtre, Noella","Legros, Mathilde","Scheel, Arnulf","Gaiser, Detlef","Kreul, Kilian","Berny, Stephane","Lozman, Owen R.","Nordman, Sirpa","Välimäki, Marja","Vilkman, Marja","Søndergaard, Roar R.","Jørgensen, Mikkel","Brabec, Christoph J.","Krebs, Frederik C"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg"