{"abstract":"A 59-year old man with idiopathic CD4 lymphopenia presented with extensive disseminated Cryptococcus neoformans infection including a large rib cryptoccocoma, vertebral spondylitis and pleural empyema. Complete resection of the affected part of the rib was necessary after failure of initial antifungal treatment. The vertebral spondylitis has been successfully managed at 3 years of follow-up by continuous itraconazole treatment and regular MRI combined with leucocyte scintigraphy assessment.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Legarth, Rebecca","Christensen, Merete","Calum, Henrik","Katzenstein, Terese L","Helweg-Larsen, Jannik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417444"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cryptococcal rib osteomyelitis as primary and only symptom of idiopathic cd000000000004 penia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mmcr.2014.02.002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-417444","identifier":[{"id":"24624326","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3950534","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84896749305","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-28267463-2dd9-4d61-8490-b6a7853e5422"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-823775F31AA023F368AE3151C5FDA9FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mmcr.2014.02.002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rebecca A","key":"legarthpau","last":"Legarth","locid":"5f68c29a-3efc-410b-a546-781fc4b8edf0","name":"Legarth, Rebecca","name_org":"Legarth, Rebecca A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Merete","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"calumpau","last":"Calum","name":"Calum, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Terese L","key":"katzensteinpau","last":"Katzenstein","locid":"7ff54094-7ab3-471a-89d8-575332708b34","name":"Katzenstein, Terese L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jannik","key":"helweglarsenpau","last":"Helweg-Larsen","locid":"6031d979-32ba-4050-8508-152a14bb98b6","name":"Helweg-Larsen, Jannik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24624326"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mmcr.2014.02.002","issn":["22117539"],"journal":"Medical Mycology Case Reports","pages":"16-18","status":"p","title":"Medical Mycology Case Reports","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84896749305"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-28267463-2dd9-4d61-8490-b6a7853e5422"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cryptococcal rib osteomyelitis as primary and only symptom of idiopathic CD4 penia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-417444","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Migraine sufferers with aura often report photosensitivity and visual discomfort outside of attacks and many consider bright or flickering light an attack-precipitating factor. The nature of this visual hypersensitivity and its relation to the underlying pathophysiology of the migraine aura is unknown. Using fMRI measurements during visual stimulation we examined the visual cortical responsiveness of patients with migraine with aura. We applied a within-patient design by assessing functional interhemispheric differences in patients consistently experiencing visual aura in the same visual hemifield. We recruited 20 patients with frequent side-fixed visual aura attacks (≥90% of auras occurring in the same visual hemifield) and 20 age and sex matched healthy controls and compared the fMRI blood oxygenation level dependent (BOLD) responses to visual stimulation between symptomatic and asymptomatic hemispheres during the interictal phase and between migraine patients and controls. BOLD responses were selectively increased in the symptomatic hemispheres. This was found in the inferior parietal lobule (P = 0.002), the inferior frontal gyrus (P = 0.003), and the superior parietal lobule (P = 0.017). The affected cortical areas comprise a visually driven functional network involved in oculomotor control, guidance of movement, motion perception, visual attention, and visual spatial memory. The patients also had significantly increased response in the same cortical areas when compared to controls (P < 0.05). We discovered a lateralized alteration of a visually driven functional network in patients with side-fixed aura. These findings suggest a hyperexcitability of the visual system in the interictal phase of migraine with visual aura.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hougaard, Anders","Amin, Faisal Mohammad","Hoffmann, Michael B","Rostrup, Egill","Larsson, Henrik B W","Asghar, Mohammad Sohail","Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","Olesen, Jes","Ashina, Messoud"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440220"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Brain","Brain Mapping","Cerebral Cortex","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Female","Functional Laterality","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Middle Aged","Migraine with Aura","Oxygen","Photic Stimulation","Visual Pathways","Visual Perception","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interhemispheric differences of fmri responses to visual stimuli in patients with side fixed migraine aura","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/hbm.22361","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-440220","identifier":[{"id":"84899124148","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24038870","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4e6842ec-6506-479e-8ced-c6d85543d039"],"keyword":["Adult","Brain","Brain Mapping","Cerebral Cortex","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Female","Functional Laterality","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Middle Aged","Migraine with Aura","Oxygen","Photic Stimulation","Visual Pathways","Visual Perception","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-75765D26D634B417A66EA6F30FE08FF0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/hbm.22361","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"hougaardpau","last":"Hougaard","locid":"c2b82de4-63e4-4f80-919c-9ab3b1eaf2bf","name":"Hougaard, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Faisal Mohammad","key":"aminpau","last":"Amin","name":"Amin, Faisal Mohammad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael B","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","name":"Hoffmann, Michael B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Egill","key":"rostruppau","last":"Rostrup","locid":"e32a8e1c-7044-4731-a725-5d883aef9c96","name":"Rostrup, Egill","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik B W","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","locid":"3c09e175-dfd1-4df5-9132-536a42c19373","name":"Larsson, Henrik B W","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohammad Sohail","key":"asgharpau","last":"Asghar","name":"Asghar, Mohammad Sohail","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vibeke Andrée","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jes","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"c5fe564b-1354-4d3c-8173-9778df35d33f","name":"Olesen, Jes","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Messoud","key":"ashinapau","last":"Ashina","locid":"0e941844-26c5-4777-a66a-64a163c19cd2","name":"Ashina, Messoud","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24038870"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/hbm.22361","issn":["10659471","10970193"],"issn_org":["10659471"],"issue":"6","journal":"Human Brain Mapping","pages":"2714-2723","status":"p","title":"Human Brain Mapping","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84899124148"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4e6842ec-6506-479e-8ced-c6d85543d039"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interhemispheric differences of fMRI responses to visual stimuli in patients with side-fixed migraine aura","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-440220","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Data on early morbidity and complications after revision total hip replacement (THR) are limited. The aim of this nationwide study was to describe and quantify early morbidity after aseptic revision THR and relate the morbidity to the extent of the revision surgical procedure. We analysed all aseptic revision THRs from 1st October 2009 to 30th September 2011 using the Danish National Patient Registry, with additional information from the Danish Hip Arthroplasty Registry. There were 1553 procedures (1490 patients) performed in 40 centres and we divided them into total revisions, acetabular component revisions, femoral stem revisions and partial revisions. The mean age of the patients was 70.4 years (25 to 98) and the median hospital stay was five days (interquartile range 3 to 7). Within 90 days of surgery, the readmission rate was 18.3%, mortality rate 1.4%, re-operation rate 6.1%, dislocation rate 7.0% and infection rate 3.0%. There were no differences in these outcomes between high- and low-volume centres. Of all readmissions, 255 (63.9%) were due to 'surgical' complications versus 144 (36.1%) 'medical' complications. Importantly, we found no differences in early morbidity across the surgical subgroups, despite major differences in the extent and complexity of operations. However, dislocations and the resulting morbidity represent the major challenge for improvement in aseptic revision THR.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lindberg-Larsen, M","Jørgensen, C C","Hansen, T B","Solgaard, S","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460902"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arthroplasty Replacement Hip","Denmark","Female","Follow Up Studies","Hip Dislocation","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Morbidity","Osteoarthritis Hip","Postoperative Complications","Prosthesis Failure","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early morbidity after aseptic revision hip arthroplasty in denmark a two year nationwide study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1302/0301-620X.96B11.33949","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460902","identifier":[{"id":"84922332556","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25371458","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-70f32e43-cee4-41c9-b3fc-4ab7b2516730"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Hip","Denmark","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Hip Dislocation","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Morbidity","Osteoarthritis, Hip","Postoperative Complications","Prosthesis Failure","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-2D52C3C3263D4C24DA76E1A1BBA75FCF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1302/0301-620X.96B11.33949","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C C","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, C C","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"T B","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, T B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"S","key":"solgaardpau","last":"Solgaard","name":"Solgaard, S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","name_org":"Kehlet, H","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25371458"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1302/0301-620x.96b11.33949","issn":["20494394","20494408"],"issn_org":["0301620X"],"issue":"11","journal":"The Bone & Joint Journal","pages":"1464-1471","status":"p","title":"The Bone & Joint Journal","title_org":"Journal of Bone and Joint Surgery: British Volume","volume":"96-B"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84922332556"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-70f32e43-cee4-41c9-b3fc-4ab7b2516730"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Early morbidity after aseptic revision hip arthroplasty in Denmark : a two-year nationwide study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460902","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The carbonic anhydrase inhibitor acetazolamide causes extracellular acidosis and dilatation of cerebral arterioles. In this study, we tested the hypothesis that acetazolamide also may induce headache and dilatation of cranial arteries. In a randomized double-blind crossover study design, 12 young healthy women were allocated to injection of 1 g acetazolamide or placebo on 2 separate days. We recorded headache on a verbal rating scale from 0 to 10 during an immediate phase (0-90 minutes) and a delayed phase (2-12 hours). The circumference of cranial arteries was measured using 3T high-resolution magnetic resonance angiography 30 and 60 minutes after injection. Acetazolamide provoked immediate headache in 9 participants compared to 3 participants after placebo (P=.031). Eleven participants reported headache in the delayed phase after acetazolamide, compared with 4 after placebo (P=.016). The area under the curve for headache was increased after acetazolamide compared to placebo in the delayed phase (2-12 h) (P=.005). Compared to placebo, arterial circumference increased after acetazolamide in the basilar artery (P=.002) as well as the cerebral (P=.003), cavernous (P=.002), and cervical (P=.005) parts of the internal carotid artery, but no other extracranial arteries changed after acetazolamide. In conclusion, acetazolamide caused immediate and delayed headache as well as dilatation of intracranial arteries in healthy volunteers. It is possible that extracellular acidosis induced by acetazolamide causes sensitization of cephalic perivascular nociceptors, which, in combination with vasodilatation, leads to delayed headache.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Arngrim, Nanna","Schytz, Henrik Winther","Asghar, Mohammad Sohail","Amin, Faisal Mohammad","Hougaard, Anders","Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","de Koning, Patrick J H","Larsson, Henrik B W","Olesen, Jes","Ashina, Messoud"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-487349"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of acetazolamide infusion with headache and cranial artery dilation in healthy volunteers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pain.2014.05.019","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-487349","identifier":[{"id":"24861583","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84904658894","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9d1c638e-4d7d-47ab-9f5f-dcafdec5ad0d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7DC5B9A27852BAFE0C6EC969E5320C14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pain.2014.05.019","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Nanna","key":"arngrimpau","last":"Arngrim","name":"Arngrim, Nanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Winther","key":"schytzpau","last":"Schytz","name":"Schytz, Henrik Winther","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohammad Sohail","key":"asgharpau","last":"Asghar","name":"Asghar, Mohammad Sohail","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Faisal Mohammad","key":"aminpau","last":"Amin","name":"Amin, Faisal Mohammad","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","fir