us":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4030a0aa-35e7-406f-8825-e1cedf542419"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The risk of muscular skeletal disorders in a cohort of Danish baggage handlers","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-591616","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Recent studies have shown that Abs that target the cell-surface enzyme CD73 (ecto-5'-nucleotidase) reduce growth of primary tumors and metastasis in syngenic mice by inhibiting the catalytic activity of CD73, and thus increasing the activity of cytotoxic T lymphocytes. In this article, we report another anticancer mechanism of anti-CD73 Abs and show that an anti-CD73 mAb (AD2) inhibits metastasis formation by a mechanism independent of CD73 catalytic activity and inhibition of primary tumor growth. This mechanism involves clustering and internalization of CD73, but does not require cross-linking of CD73, because both whole IgG anti-CD73 AD2 mAb and Fab' fragments thereof exhibited this effect. Ex vivo treatment of different breast cancer cell lines with anti-CD73 AD2 mAb before i.v. injection into mice inhibited extravasation/colonization of circulating tumor cells and significantly reduced metastasis development. This effect was also observed when the cancer cell-surface expression of CD73 was significantly reduced by small interfering RNA knockdown. The antimetastatic activity is epitope specific, as another Ab that efficiently binds CD73-expressing live cancer cells did not lead to CD73 internalization and metastasis inhibition. Furthermore, anti-CD73 AD2 mAb inhibited development of metastasis in a spontaneous animal model of human metastatic breast cancer. Our study shows that some anti-CD73 mAbs cause cell-surface clustering of CD73 followed by internalization, thus inhibiting the ability of circulating tumor cells to extravasate and colonize, leading to inhibition of metastasis. Ab-based CD73 cancer therapy should include a combination of Abs that target the catalytic activity of CD73, as well as those with the characteristics described in this article.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Terp, Mikkel Green","Olesen, Kristina A","Arnspang, Eva C.","Lund, Rikke Raaen","Lagerholm, B. Christoffer","Ditzel, Henrik","Leth-Larsen, Rikke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["5 Nucleotidase","Animals","Antibodies Monoclonal","Biological Transport","Breast Neoplasms","Cell Line Tumor","Cell Movement","Female","Humans","Immunoglobulin Fab Fragments","Mice","Neoplasm Metastasis","Neoplasm Transplantation","Neoplastic Cells Circulating","RNA Interference","RNA Small Interfering","Xenograft Model Antitumor Assays"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anti human cd000000000073 monoclonal antibody inhibits metastasis formation in human breast cancer by inducing clustering and internalization of cd000000000073 expressed on the surface of cancer cells","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4049/jimmunol.1301274","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-616159","identifier":[{"id":"84885437317","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24043904","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-95f74dec-2dad-4a85-8d33-e8c87fc781dd"],"keyword":["5'-Nucleotidase","Animals","Antibodies, Monoclonal","Biological Transport","Breast Neoplasms","Cell Line, Tumor","Cell Movement","Female","Humans","Immunoglobulin Fab Fragments","Mice","Neoplasm Metastasis","Neoplasm Transplantation","Neoplastic Cells, Circulating","RNA Interference","RNA, Small Interfering","Xenograft Model Antitumor Assays"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D68B38B30888765FF4E7AB3F10AD945C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4049/jimmunol.1301274","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Ditzel group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel G","key":"terppau","last":"Terp","locid":"31863af3-7d3a-48d5-ae0a-e76e938a23fb","name":"Terp, Mikkel Green","name_org":"Terp, Mikkel G","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-6900","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina A","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"a38d2bdb-13b0-44a1-9782-0b019c683c4e","name":"Olesen, Kristina A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Arnspang","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"400511b0-9aec-496e-abc0-9b44c1abb4ed","name":"Arnspang, Eva C.","name_org":"Christensen, Eva Arnspang","orcid":"0000-0002-3095-4070","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke R","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"d2d19374-e4bd-45f3-87c1-dfbaae8fa898","name":"Lund, Rikke Raaen","name_org":"Lund, Rikke R","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B Christoffer","key":"lagerholmpau","last":"Lagerholm","locid":"13cf7d5e-4770-402f-a0ef-117522d44611","name":"Lagerholm, B. Christoffer","name_org":"Lagerholm, B Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik J","key":"ditzelpau","last":"Ditzel","locid":"f10637d7-ca3b-4956-a007-100f66737838","name":"Ditzel, Henrik","name_org":"Ditzel, Henrik J","orcid":"0000-0003-3927-5135","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"lethlarsenpau","last":"Leth-Larsen","locid":"66fd89b9-b81d-4e74-bf02-9a0ea313ee3e","name":"Leth-Larsen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-1612-4089","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24043904"],"pub":{"doi":"10.4049/jimmunol.1301274","issn":["00221767","15506606"],"issn_org":["00221767"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Immunology","pages":"4165-4173","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Immunology","title_org":"The Journal of Immunology","volume":"191"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84885437317"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-95f74dec-2dad-4a85-8d33-e8c87fc781dd"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Anti-human CD73 monoclonal antibody inhibits metastasis formation in human breast cancer by inducing clustering and internalization of CD73 expressed on the surface of cancer cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-616159","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"BAGGROUND: This experimental study explores a novel magnetic resonance imaging/spectroscopic (MRI/MRS) method that measures changes in renal metabolism in a diabetic rat model. This hyperpolarized metabolic MRI/MRS method allows monitoring of metabolic processes in seconds by >10,000-fold enhancement of the MR signal. The method has shown that the conversion of pyruvate to bicarbonate, i.e. pyruvate dehydrogenase (PDH) activity, is significantly altered in the myocardium already at the onset of diabetes, and the predominant Warburg effect is a valuable cancer maker via the lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) activity, and we hypothesize that a similar change in PDH and LDH could be found in the early diabetic kidney. METHODS: In a streptozotocin rat model of type 1 diabetes, hyperpolarized (13) C-MRI and blood oxygenation level dependent (BOLD) (1) H-MRI was employed to investigate the changes in renal metabolism in the diabetic and the control kidney in vivo. RESULTS: The diabetic kidney showed a 149% increase in the lactate/pyruvate ratio compared to the control rat kidney, while the bicarbonate/pyruvate ratio was unchanged between the diabetic and the control rat kidney, consistent with literature findings. These metabolic findings paralleled a reduced intrarenal oxygen availability as found by BOLD MRI. DISCUSSION: Hyperpolarized (13) C-MRI shows promise in the diagnosis and monitoring of early renal changes associated with diabetes, with the pyruvate/lactate ratio as an imaging biomarker for regional renal changes. Copyright © 2012 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Laustsen, Christoffer","Østergaard, Jakob Appel","Lauritzen, Mette Hauge","Nørregaard, Rikke","Bowen, Sean","Søgaard, Lise Vejby-Christensen","Flyvbjerg, Allan","Pedersen, Michael","Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-081.74-666231"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keywo