hus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Malnutrition induces gut atrophy and increases hepatic fat infiltration : studies in a pig model of childhood malnutrition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.00-023158","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The strong enhancement of NMR signals achieved by hyperpolarization decays, at best, with a time constant of a few minutes. Here, we show that a combination of long-lived singlet states, molecular design, magnetic field cycling, and specific radiofrequency pulse sequences allows repeated observation of the same batch of polarized nuclei over a period of 30 min and more. We report a recycling protocol in which the enhanced nuclear polarization achieved by dissolution-DNP is observed with full intensity and then returned to singlet order. MRI experiments may be run on a portion of the available spin polarization, while the remaining is preserved and made available for a later use. An analogy is drawn with a \"spin bank\" or \"resealable container\" in which highly polarized spin order may be deposited and retrieved. © 2013 American Chemical Society.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Pileio, Giuseppe","Bowen, Sean","Laustsen, Christoffer","Tayler, Michael C D","Hill-Cousins, Joseph T","Brown, Lynda Jane","Brown, Richard Charles Downie","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Levitt, Malcolm H"],"cuid":["S02-097.01-025979"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Southampton"],"keyword":["Nuclear magnetic resonance","Recycling","Spin polarization"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recycling and imaging of nuclear singlet hyperpolarization","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ja312333v","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.01-025979","identifier":[{"id":"84875796487","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23489087","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b6bb206e-abf6-4a3a-90d3-d42bcaf4a426","dtu-1e93b9da-c221-4dd6-a4c4-0988bdc39f17"],"keyword":["Nuclear magnetic resonance","Recycling","Spin polarization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2F3491E22BA90AA02B22BDC96544B230"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ja312333v","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of southampton","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Southampton","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","use