{"abstract":"HRM Nye opgaver, teknologier og pres om at få mere ud af mindre er blot nogle af de kompetencekrav, der skyller ind over danske virksomheder – og dermed den enkelte person. Tre ledelsesgreb bærer på løsningen.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-296231"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genveje til fremtiden","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-296231","ids":["cbs-db2ed701-d971-429e-b868-02ed485f5c1a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-94C0DDF8512C8E6AAAAD97A05A09F79C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01091182"],"newspaper":"Jyllands-Posten","pages":"28","publisher":"JP/Politikens Hus AS","publisher_org":"JP/Politikens Hus A/S","status":"p","title":"Jyllands-Posten"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-db2ed701-d971-429e-b868-02ed485f5c1a"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Genveje til fremtiden","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-296231","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper focuses on the use of Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) to evaluate the performance of seventeen control strategies in wastewater treatment plants (WWTPs). It tackles the importance of using site-specific factors for nutrient enrichment when decision-makers have to select best operating strategies. Therefore, the LCA evaluation is repeated for three different scenarios depending on the limitation of nitrogen (N), phosphorus (P), or both, when evaluating the nutrient enrichment impact in water bodies. The LCA results indicate that for treated effluent discharged into N-deficient aquatic systems (e.g. open coastal areas) the most eco-friendly strategies differ from the ones dealing with discharging into P-deficient (e.g. lakes and rivers) and N&P-deficient systems (e.g. coastal zones). More particularly, the results suggest that strategies that promote increased nutrient removal and/or energy savings present an environmental benefit for N&P and P-deficient systems. This is not the case when addressing N-deficient systems for which the use of chemicals (even for improving N removal efficiencies) is not always beneficial for the environment. A sensitivity analysis on using weighting of the impact categories is conducted to assess how value choices (policy decisions) may affect the management of WWTPs. For the scenarios with only N-limitation, the LCA-based ranking of the control strategies is sensitive to the choice of weighting factors, whereas this is not the case for N&P or P-deficient aquatic systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Corominas, Lluís","Larsen, Henrik Fred","Flores-Alsina, Xavier","Vanrolleghem, Peter A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-314964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Université Laval"],"keyword":["Control","Decision making","LCA","Mathematical modelling","Nutrient removal","Sustainability","Wastewater treatment","Weighting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"including life cycle assessment for decision making in controlling wastewater nutrient removal systems","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jenvman.2013.06.002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-314964","identifier":[{"id":"23856224","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880375205","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-22e9cf34-7050-4cf6-98b5-1a7300760d2e"],"keyword":["ASM3-BioP","Control","Decision making","LCA","Mathematical modelling","Nutrient removal","Sustainability","Wastewater treatment","Weighting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3C4CB0680D51CED29BE74F1263CFB977"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jenvman.2013.06.002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"université laval","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Université Laval","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lluís","key":"corominaspau","last":"Corominas","name":"Corominas, Lluís","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xavier","key":"floresalsinapau","last":"Flores-Alsina","name":"Flores-Alsina, Xavier","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter A.","key":"vanrolleghempau","last":"Vanrolleghem","name":"Vanrolleghem, Peter A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23856224"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jenvman.2013.06.002","issn":["03014797","10958630"],"issn_org":["03014797"],"journal":"Journal of Environmental Management","pages":"759-767","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Environmental Management","volume":"128"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880375205"],"sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","13. Climate Action","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-22e9cf34-7050-4cf6-98b5-1a7300760d2e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Including Life Cycle Assessment for decision-making in controlling wastewater nutrient removal systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-314964","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Solid oxide fuel cell (SOFC) cathodes were prepared by impregnating the nitrates corresponding to SrTixFe1-xO3-δ (STF), x= 0; 0.1; 0.2; 0.3; 0.4 and 0.5, into a porous backbone of Ce 0.9Gd0.1O2-δ (CGO). STF was chosen as very high oxygen surface exchange rate, high ionic conductivity and electrochemical stability as a thin film electrode have been reported for these materials. XRD measurements showed a high degree of secondary phase formation in the infiltrate as well as reaction with the CGO backbone. Microstructural analysis showed that the STF infiltrate had formed a coating on the CGO backbone. All prepared electrodes were characterized as symmetric cells using impedance spectroscopy. Within the investigated series the infiltrate with x = 0.1 (STF10) showed the best performance with an area specific resistance (ASR) of ASR ≈ 6.4 Ω cm2 (STF10) at 600°C in air. The relatively poor performance is believed to originate from poor electronic conduction in the electrodes and possibly also reactions between Sr-containing compounds and CGO. To circumvent the low electronic conductivity, backbones of a composite cathode containing LaCo0.4Ni0.6O 3-δ (LCN60) and CGO were also tried infiltrated with STF. The ASR of the backbone was 8.7 Ω cm2 prior to infiltration and this decreased to 0.34 Ω cm2 after infiltration with STF10.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Brinch-Larsen, Mathias","Søgaard, Martin","Hjelm, Johan","Frandsen, Henrik Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-315871"],"event":{"end":"2012-01-27","place":"Daytona Beach, FL, us","start":"2012-01-22","title":"36th International Conference on Advanced Ceramics and Composites","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cathodes","Ceramic materials","Electric conductivity","Impregnation","Iron compounds","Solid oxide fuel cells SOFC"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of novel solid oxide fuel cell cathodes based on impregnation of srtixfe000000000001 xo000000000003 δ into ceria based backbones","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84875716206","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-315871","identifier":[{"id":"84875716206","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-26139541-797f-41cc-bdfc-1329dc2828d0"],"keyword":["Cathodes","Ceramic materials","Electric conductivity","Film preparation","Impregnation","Iron compounds","Solid oxide fuel cells (SOFC)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1A3441F0B797D18AF2696C7BE66AED8D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Mixed Conductors"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"brinchlarsenpau","last":"Brinch-Larsen","locid":"6f0cd54b-a08e-4002-9daf-642eb695a780","name":"Brinch-Larsen, Mathias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"7988016f-37b3-4f99-9617-5bd79fc5cfa3","name":"Søgaard, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johan","key":"hjelmpau","last":"Hjelm","locid":"1f33d9cb-8387-4672-bfa5-091ef2fc1329","name":"Hjelm, Johan","orcid":"0000-0003-0072-5784","rank":