,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"baktoftpau","last":"Baktoft","locid":"642a7cea-4ecc-4866-97f3-0d86f3e47ec0","name":"Baktoft, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3644-4960","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Hage","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"df4c70da-87a0-45c4-883d-9f9d64e2ffd6","name":"Larsen, Martin Hage","orcid":"0000-0001-9521-835X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"koedpau","last":"Koed","locid":"70851536-6d9b-439b-b100-58a92830a28f","name":"Koed, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-2163-0955","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-434430e2-2c94-4447-af72-de4b94d64a25"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Marine survival in wild sea trout (Salmo trutta) post-smolts. Why little fish matter!","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324577","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The effect from fully nonlinear irregular wave forcing on the fatigue life of the foundation and tower of an offshore wind turbine is investigated through aeroelastic calculations. Five representative sea states with increasing significant wave height are considered in a water depth of 40 m. The waves are both linear and fully nonlinear irregular 2D waves. The wind turbine is the NREL 5-MW reference wind turbine. Fatigue analysis is performed in relation to analysis of the sectional forces in the tower and monopile. Impulsive excitation of the sectional force at the bottom of the tower is seen when the waves are large and nonlinear and most notably for small wind speeds. In case of strong velocities and turbulent wind, the excitation is damped out. In the monopile no excitation of the force is seen, but even for turbulent strong wind the wave affects the forces in the pile significantly. The analysis indicates that the nonlinearity of the waves can change the fatigue damage level significantly in particular when the wave and wind direction is misaligned.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schløer, Signe","Bredmose, Henrik","Bingham, Harry B.","Larsen, Torben J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349807"],"event":{"acronym":"OMAE","end":"2012-07-06","place":"Rio de Janeiro, br","start":"2012-07-01","title":"31st ASME International Conference on Ocean, Offshore and Arctic Engineering","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects from fully nonlinear irregular wave forcing on the fatigue life of an offshore wind turbine and its monopile foundation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-349807","ids":["dtu-9797ebea-7e9d-407f-bdd8-6189fa09335d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-45CD23F406BBB8CD31A029409F4BCE32"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Fluid Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe","key":"schløerpau","last":"Schløer","locid":"224e90ba-53af-4bbc-bad5-bbc1fac9884a","name":"Schløer, Signe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bredmosepau","last":"Bredmose","locid":"a46a2dd1-d040-4240-8dfb-bdb22c646a47","name":"Bredmose, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-0753","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harry B.","key":"binghampau","last":"Bingham","locid":"ce245728-e918-4e11-90de-d143c2403110","name":"Bingham, Harry B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7263-442X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben J.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"965dbaf9-67c6-4f4d-b512-2df4845d740d","name":"Larsen, Torben J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6741-5057","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"393-402","publisher":"The American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ASME 31th 2012 International Conference on Ocean, Offshore and Arctic Engineering","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9797ebea-7e9d-407f-bdd8-6189fa09335d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Effects from fully nonlinear irregular wave forcing on the fatigue life of an offshore wind turbine and its monopile foundation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-349807","year":"2013","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This first-in-man imaging study evaluated the safety and feasibility of hyperpolarized [1-¹³C]pyruvate as an agent for noninvasively characterizing alterations in tumor metabolism for patients with prostate cancer. Imaging living systems with hyperpolarized agents can result in more than 10,000-fold enhancement in signal relative to conventional magnetic resonance (MR) imaging. When combined with the rapid acquisition of in vivo ¹³C MR data, it is possible to evaluate the distribution of agents such as [1-¹³C]pyruvate and its metabolic products lactate, alanine, and bicarbonate in a matter of seconds. Preclinical studies in cancer models have detected elevated levels of hyperpolarized [1-¹³C]lactate in tumor, with the ratio of [1-¹³C]lactate/[1-¹³C]pyruvate being increased in high-grade tumors and decreased after successful treatment. Translation of this technology into humans was achieved by modifying the instrument that generates the hyperpolarized agent, constructing specialized radio frequency coils to detect ¹³C nuclei, and developing new pulse sequences to efficiently capture the signal. The study population comprised patients with biopsy-proven prostate cancer, with 31 subjects being injected with hyperpolarized [1-¹³C]pyruvate. The median time to deliver the agent was 66 s, and uptake was observed about 20 s after injection. No dose-limiting toxicities were observed, and the highest dose (0.43 ml/kg of 230 mM agent) gave the best signal-to-noise ratio for hyperpolarized [1-¹³C]pyruvate. The results were extremely promising in not only confirming the safety of the agent but also showing elevated [1-¹³C]lactate/[1-¹³C]pyruvate in regions of biopsy-proven cancer. These findings will be valuable for noninvasive cancer diagnosis and treatment monitoring in future clinical trials.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Nelson, Sarah J","Kurhanewicz, John","Vigneron, Daniel B","Larson, Peder E Z","Harzstark, Andrea L","Ferrone, Marcus","van Criekinge, Mark","Chang, Jose W","Bok, Robert","Park, Ilwoo","Reed, Galen","Carvajal, Lucas","Small, Eric J","Munster, Pamela","Weinberg, Vivian K","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Chen, Albert P","Hurd, Ralph E","Odegardstuen, Liv-Ingrid","Robb, Fraser J","Tropp, James","Murray, Jonathan A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350449"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metabolic imaging of patients with prostate cancer using hyperpolarized 000000000001 c pyruvate","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.3006070","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350449","identifier":[{"id":"84883879044","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23946197","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4201045","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-99f5643d-8c99-4407-b917-db09c467fd84"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6A987F4B84CA8AF308F45676CF7CC56B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.3006070","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":n