"Weinberg, Vivian K","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Albert P","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Albert P","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph E","key":"hurdpau","last":"Hurd","name":"Hurd, Ralph E","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Liv-Ingrid","key":"odegardstuenpau","last":"Odegardstuen","name":"Odegardstuen, Liv-Ingrid","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fraser J","key":"robbpau","last":"Robb","name":"Robb, Fraser J","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"tropppau","last":"Tropp","name":"Tropp, James","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan A","key":"murraypau","last":"Murray","name":"Murray, Jonathan A","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23946197"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1126/scitranslmed.3006070","issn":["19466234","19466242"],"issn_org":["19466234"],"issue":"198","journal":"Science Translational Medicine","publisher":"American Association for the Advancement of Science","status":"p","title":"Science Translational Medicine","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-99f5643d-8c99-4407-b917-db09c467fd84"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Metabolic imaging of patients with prostate cancer using hyperpolarized [1-¹³C]pyruvate.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350449","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper provides a comprehensive summary on modelling of micro-pollutants' (MPs) fate and transport in wastewater. It indicates the motivations of MP modelling and summarises and illustrates the current status. Finally, some recommendations are provided to improve and diffuse the use of such models. In brief, we conclude that, in order to predict the contaminant removal in centralised treatment works, considering the dramatic improvement in monitoring and detecting MPs in wastewater, more mechanistic approaches should be used to complement conventional, heuristic and other fate models. This is crucial, as regional risk assessments and model-based evaluations of pollution discharge from urban areas can potentially be used by decision makers to evaluate effluent quality regulation, and assess upgrading requirements, in the future.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Plósz, Benedek G.","Benedetti, L.","Daigger, G. T.","Langford, K H","Larsen, Henrik Fred","Monteith, H.","Ort, C.","Seth, R.","Steyer, J.-P.","Vanrolleghem, P. A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353692"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CH2M Hill","Ghent University","Hydromantis ESS Inc.","INRAE","University of Windsor","Université Laval"],"keyword":["Trace chemicals"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling micro pollutant fate in wastewater collection and treatment systems status and challenges","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84873813803","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353692","identifier":[{"id":"84873813803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a49120aa-8ba1-400e-a2e0-eb991feb9511"],"keyword":["biotransformation and cometabolism","parent chemical retransformation","risk assessment and regulations","sorption-desorption","trace chemicals"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7707D87000EBC3B40D59CEA410D17985"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Urban Water Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"ghent university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"ch2m hill","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"CH2M Hill","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"hydromantis ess inc","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Hydromantis ESS Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ca","key":"university of windsor","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Windsor","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"inrae","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRAE","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ca","key":"université laval","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Université Laval","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benedek G.","key":"plószpau","last":"Plósz","locid":"f89de989-38da-486a-a878-99afb4aaa604","name":"Plósz, Benedek G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","c