{"abstract":"Biliary tract cancer is a relatively rare disease with a poor prognosis. The disease should be handled in a multidisciplinary setting to ensure proper diagnosis and curative surgery if possible. The majority of patients will, however, need oncologic treatment at a certain time. The standard treatment is combination chemotherapy with gemcitabine and a platinum, and in Denmark the regime consists of gemcitabine, oxaliplatin and capecitabine. Research is focused on tumour markers and clinical trials combining chemotherapy with molecularly targeted agents.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jensen, Lars Henrik","Larsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-641725"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols","Bile Duct Neoplasms","Cholangiocarcinoma","Humans","Molecular Targeted Therapy","Multimodal Imaging","Outcome Assessment Health Care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"onkologisk behandling af galdegangscancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84890887223","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-641725","identifier":[{"id":"84890887223","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24629114","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-ef3995ca-1c9e-4d3a-8cf9-749e8e1b44df"],"keyword":["Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols","Bile Duct Neoplasms","Cholangiocarcinoma","Humans","Molecular Targeted Therapy","Multimodal Imaging","Outcome Assessment (Health Care)"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6151EE6E8FF723EE82F275A2F9A8E8C9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu univ