{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Cosme, Nuno Miguel Dias","Larsen, Henrik Fred","Hauschild, Michael Zwicky"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343258"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-05","place":"York, gb","start":"2013-07-04","title":"All at Sea 2013: An integrated approach to research in the coastal zone","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatially explicit lcia endpoint model for marine eutrophication and application to future climatic driven pressures","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/59451097/All_at_Sea_booklet.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343258","ids":["dtu-8183c8ed-4e8c-4266-8e65-515c00621044"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-34C3EC386F2033E320954AB3996C9362"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.york.ac.uk/conferences/allatsea/index.html","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/59451097/All_at_Sea_booklet.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nuno Miguel Dias","key":"cosmepau","last":"Cosme","locid":"2a8583f1-d4cb-4827-98a6-a9723bc3221c","name":"Cosme, Nuno Miguel Dias","orcid":"0000-0003-1152-9842","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Zwicky","key":"hauschildpau","last":"Hauschild","locid":"5c85fd08-0c76-4c6c-90c3-431093cff94b","name":"Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","orcid":"0000-0002-8331-7390","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"8-9","publisher":"University of York","status":"p","subtitle":"An integrated approach to research in the coastal zone","title":"All at Sea 2013 booklet"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8183c8ed-4e8c-4266-8e65-515c00621044"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Spatially-explicit LCIA endpoint model for marine eutrophication and application to future climatic-driven pressures","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343258","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Radiofrequency coils in Magnetic Resonance systems are used to produce a homogeneous B1 field for exciting the nuclei and to pick up the signals emitted by the nuclei with high signal-to-noise ratio. Accordingly, coil performance affects strongly the quality of the obtained data and images.Coil efficiency, defined as the B1 magnetic field induced at a given point on the square root of supplied power P, is an important parameter that characterizes coil performance, since by maximizing efficiency will also maximize the signal-to-noise ratio.This work describes and compares four methods for coil efficiency estimation, based on different theoretical approaches. Three methods allow efficiency measurement by using “probe techniques” (perturbing loop, perturbing sphere and pick-up coil), which can be used both on the bench and inside the scanner, while an “NMR technique” has been employed for comparison purpose.Methods were tested on a 13C birdcage coil tuned at 32.13MHz.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Giovannetti, Giulio","Frijia, Francesca","Hartwig, Valentina","Menichetti, Luca","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Marchi, Daniele De","Positano, Vincenzo","Landini, Luigi","Lombardi, Massimo","Santarelli, Maria Filomena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348302"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fondazione G. Monasterio","National Research Council of Italy"],"keyword":["Coil efficiency","Magnetic resonance","Radiofrequency coils"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficiency evaluation of a 000000000013c magnetic resonance birdcage coil theory and comparison of four methods","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.measurement.2013.03.015","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-348302","identifier":[{"id":"84877080682","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-92703d26-785b-44b8-b87d-49a13bfa9102"],"keyword":["Coil efficiency","Magnetic Resonance","Radiofrequency coils"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-81F6D8DEF9EA5107D204E5BD0617321D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.measurement.2013.03.015","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"fondazione g monasterio","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fondazione G. Monasterio","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giulio","key":"giovannettipau","last":"Giovannetti","name":"Giovannetti, Giulio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"frijiapau","last":"Frijia","name":"Frijia, Francesca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina","key":"hartwigpau","last":"Hartwig","name":"Hartwig, Valentina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"menichettipau","last":"Menichetti","name":"Menichetti, Luca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjaerlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","name_org":"Ardenkjaer-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele De","key":"marchipau","last":"Marchi","name":"Marchi, Daniele De","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo","key":"positanopau","last":"Positano","name":"Positano, Vincenzo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luigi","key":"landinipau","last":"Landini","name":"Landini, Luigi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Massimo","key":"lombardipau","last":"Lombardi","name":"Lombardi, Massimo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Filomena","key":"santarellipau","last":"Santarelli","name":"Santarelli, Maria Filomena","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.measurement.2013.03.015","issn":["02632241"],"issue":"7","journal":"Measurement: Journal of the International Measurement Confederation","pages":"2201-2205","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Measurement: Journal of the International Measurement Confederation","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84877080682"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-92703d26-785b-44b8-b87d-49a13bfa9102"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Efficiency evaluation of a 13C Magnetic Resonance birdcage coil: Theory and comparison of four methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-348302","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Hyperpolarized 13C magnetic resonance spectroscopy in pig models enables metabolic activity mapping, providing a powerful tool for the study of the heart physiology, but requires the development of dedicated radiofrequency coils, capable of providing large field of view with high signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) data. This work describes the simulations and the tests of a transmit-only (TX) volume coil/receive-only (RX) surface coil both designed for hyperpolarized studies of pig heart with a clinical 3T scanner. The coil characterization is performed by developing an SNR model for coil performance in terms of coil resistance, sample-induced resistance and magnetic field pattern. In particular, coil resistances were calculated from Ohm’s law, while magnetic field patterns and sample-induced resistances were calculated using a numerical finite-difference time-domain algorithm. Experimental phantom chemical shift image, showed good agreement with the theoretical SNR-vs-depth profiles and highlighted the advantage of the novel configuration over the single transmit–receive coils throughout the volume of interest for cardiac imaging in pig. Finally, the TX-birdcage/RX-circular configuration was tested by acquiring metabolic maps with hyperpolarized [1-13C] pyruvate injected i.v. in a pig. The results of the phantom and pig experiments show the ability of the coil configuration to image well the metabolites distribution.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Giovannetti, G.","Frijia, F.","Hartwig, V.","Menichetti, L.","Positano, V.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Lionetti, V.","Aquaro, G. D.","De Marchi, D.","Schulte, R. F.","Wiesinger, F.","Landini, L.","Lombardi, M.","Santarelli, M. F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Global Research","National Research Council of Italy","Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","University of Pisa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transmit only receive only radiofrequency system for hyperpolarized 000000000013c mrs cardiac metabolism studies in pigs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00723-013-0477-3","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-349856","identifier":[{"id":"84883133588","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-97cb5ca2-30b4-40f6-a2d2-5e7ffa35ced5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC275AE8C63F22F407F21AF2A37AEB2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00723-013-0477-3","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"sant anna school of advanced studies","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"ge global research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"GE Global Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university of pisa","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Pisa","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"giovannettipau","last":"Giovannetti","name":"Giovannetti, G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"frijiapau","last":"Frijia","name":"Frijia, F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"hartwigpau","last":"Hartwig","name":"Hartwig, V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"menichettipau","last":"Menichetti","name":"Menichetti, L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"positanopau","last":"Positano","name":"Positano, V.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"lionettipau","last":"Lionetti","name":"Lionetti, V.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G. D.","key":"aquaropau","last":"Aquaro","name":"Aquaro, G. D.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"demarchipau","last":"De Marchi","name":"De Marchi, D.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"R. F.","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, R. F.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"wiesingerpau","last":"Wiesinger","name":"Wiesinger, F.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"landinipau","last":"Landini","name":"Landini, L.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"lombardipau","last":"Lombardi","name":"Lombardi, M.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. F.","key":"santarellipau","last":"Santarelli","name":"Santarelli, M. F.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00723-013-0477-3","issn":["09379347","16137507"],"issn_org":["09379347"],"issue":"10","journal":"Applied Magnetic Resonance","pages":"1125-1138","publisher":"Springer-Verlag Wien","status":"p","title":"Applied Magnetic Resonance","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84883133588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-97cb5ca2-30b4-40f6-a2d2-5e7ffa35ced5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Transmit-Only/Receive-Only Radiofrequency System for Hyperpolarized 13C MRS Cardiac Metabolism Studies in Pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-349856","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The hypoxic nature of tumors results in treatment resistance and poor prognosis. To spare limited oxygen for more crucial pathways, hypoxic cancerous cells suppress mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation and promote glycolysis for energy production. Thereby, inhibition of glycolysis has the potential to overcome treatment resistance of hypoxic tumors. Here, EPR imaging was used to evaluate oxygen dependent efficacy on hypoxia-sensitive drug. The small molecule 3-bromopyruvate blocks glycolysis pathway by inhibiting hypoxia inducible enzymes and enhanced cytotoxicity of 3-bromopyruvate under hypoxic conditions has been reported in vitro. However, the efficacy of 3-bromopyruvate was substantially attenuated in hypoxic tumor regions (pO(2) < 10 mmHg) in vivo using squamous cell carcinoma (SCCVII)-bearing mouse model. Metabolic MRI studies using hyperpolarized (13) C-labeled pyruvate showed that monocarboxylate transporter-1 is the major transporter for pyruvate and the analog 3-bromopyruvate in SCCVII tumor. The discrepant results between in vitro and in vivo data were attributed to biphasic oxygen dependent expression of monocarboxylate transporter-1 in vivo. Expression of monocarboxylate transporter-1 was enhanced in moderately hypoxic (8-15 mmHg) tumor regions but down regulated in severely hypoxic (<5 mmHg) tumor regions. These results emphasize the importance of noninvasive imaging biomarkers to confirm the action of hypoxia-activated drugs.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Matsumoto, Shingo","Saito, Keita","Yasui, Hironobu","Morris, H. Douglas","Munasinghe, Jeeva P.","Lizak, Martin","Merkle, Hellmut","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Choudhuri, Rajani","Devasahayam, Nallathamby","Subramanian, Sankaran","Koretsky, Alan P.","Mitchell, James B.","Krishna, Murali C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364137"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Cancer Institute United States","National Institute of Neurological Disorder and Stroke"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Hypoxic","Monocarboxylate transporter","Oxygen","Pyruvate","Pyruvate metabolism","Transporter","Tumor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epr oxygen imaging and hyperpolarized 000000000013 c mri of pyruvate metabolism as noninvasive biomarkers of tumor treatment response to a glycolysis inhibitor 000000000003 bromopyruvate","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.24355","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364137","identifier":[{"id":"84876494236","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c76f7499-9921-43df-b006-b9aa2d5f9383"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Bromopyruvate","EPR imaging","Glycolysy","Hyperpolarized 13C MRI","Hypoxic","Monocarboxylate","Monocarboxylate transporter","Oxygen","Pyruvate","Pyruvate metabolism","Transporter","Tumor","mmhg","mry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-28EC803EBE9A654C242FBB57379F0792"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.24355","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"national cancer institute united states","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Cancer Institute United States","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"national institute of neurological disorder and stroke","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorder and Stroke","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shingo","key":"matsumotopau","last":"Matsumoto","name":"Matsumoto, Shingo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Keita","key":"saitopau","last":"Saito","name":"Saito, Keita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hironobu","key":"yasuipau","last":"Yasui","name":"Yasui, Hironobu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"H. Douglas","key":"morrispau","last":"Morris","name":"Morris, H. Douglas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeeva P.","key":"munasinghepau","last":"Munasinghe","name":"Munasinghe, Jeeva P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lizakpau","last":"Lizak","name":"Lizak, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hellmut","key":"merklepau","last":"Merkle","name":"Merkle, Hellmut","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rajani","key":"choudhuripau","last":"Choudhuri","name":"Choudhuri, Rajani","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nallathamby","key":"devasahayampau","last":"Devasahayam","name":"Devasahayam, Nallathamby","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sankaran","key":"subramanianpau","last":"S