{"abstract":"Cytokine response plays a vital role in various human lipopolysaccharide (LPS) infectious and inflammatory diseases. This study aimed to find genetic variants that might affect the levels of LPS-induced interleukin (IL)-6, IL-8, IL-10, IL-1ra and tumor necrosis factor (TNF)-α cytokine production.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Margit Hørup","Albrechtsen, Anders","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Werge, Thomas","Hansen, Thomas","Gether, Ulrik","Haastrup, Eva","Ullum, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535745"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association study of genetic variants in lps stimulated il 000000000006 il 000000000008 il 000000000010 il 000000000001ra and tnf α cytokine response in a danish cohort","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/51420154/Genome_Wide_Association_Study_of_Genetic_Variants.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-535745","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3688878","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84879134014","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23823136","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ee6d252e-ea51-48a0-a791-15f83bb48062"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC01E6EFE9103A241609AEABA08300FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/51420154/Genome_Wide_Association_Study_of_Genetic_Variants.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0066262","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Margit Hørup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Margit Hørup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"albrechtsenpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"4b040c73-6b49-4e97-be60-5e34608e0615","name":"Albrechtsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-031X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise Wegner","key":"thørnerpau","last":"Thørner","name":"Thørner, Lise Wegner","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"wergepau","last":"Werge","name":"Werge, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ulrik","key":"getherpau","last":"Gether","locid":"9b3eed37-e0b0-412a-b790-48069d4d1e5e","name":"Gether, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0020-3807","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eva","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","name":"Haastrup, Eva","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","name":"Ullum, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23823136"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0066262","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"6","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e66262","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879134014"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ee6d252e-ea51-48a0-a791-15f83bb48062"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genome-wide association study of genetic variants in LPS-stimulated IL-6, IL-8, IL-10, IL-1ra and TNF-α cytokine response in a Danish Cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535745","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose Blood loss after total knee arthroplasty (TKA) may lead to anemia, blood transfusions, and increased total costs. Also, bleeding into the periarticular tissue may cause swelling and a reduction in quadriceps strength, thus impairing early functional recovery. In this randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study, we analyzed the possible effect of fibrin sealant on blood loss and early functional recovery in a fast-track setting. Methods 24 consecutive patients undergoing bilateral simultaneous TKA were included. 10 mL of fibrin sealant (Evicel) was sprayed onto one knee whereas the contralateral knee had saline. Drain output, the primary outcome, was measured from knee drains removed exactly 24 h after surgery. Secondary outcomes (knee swelling, pain, strength of knee extension, and range of movement (ROM)) were evaluated up to 21 days after surgery. Results The drain output in knees treated with fibrin sealant and placebo was similar (582 mL and 576 mL, respectively). Likewise, no statistically significant differences were found between groups regarding swelling, pain, strength of knee extension, and ROM. Interpretation Fibrin sealant as a local hemostatic in TKA showed no benefit in reducing drain output or in facilitating early functional recovery when used with a tourniquet, tranexamic acid, and a femoral bone plug.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Skovgaard, Christian","Holm, Bente","Troelsen, Anders","Lunn, Troels H","Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","Kehlet, Henrik","Husted, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-545209"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no effect of fibrin sealant on drain output or functional recovery following simultaneous bilateral total knee arthroplasty","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/17453674.2013.769082","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-545209","identifier":[{"id":"23350579","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84876354412","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3639335","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-fe58d139-fc0f-4141-bcdd-9076eebc52a7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF6B530182D07A85A9F9815BED38AF74"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/17453674.2013.769082","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Bente","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","name":"Troelsen, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Troels H","key":"lunnpau","last":"Lunn","name":"Lunn, Troels H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lissi","key":"gaarnlarsenpau","last":"Gaarn-Larsen","name":"Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","name":"Husted, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23350579"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/17453674.2013.769082","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"153-158","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","title_org":"Acta Orthopaedica (Print Edition)","volume":"84"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84876354412"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fe58d139-fc0f-4141-bcdd-9076eebc52a7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"No effect of fibrin sealant on drain output or functional recovery following simultaneous bilateral total knee arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-545209","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Legind","Martin-Bautista, Maria Jose","Vila, Maria Amparo","Andreasen, Troels","Christiansen, Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-566645"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Granada"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flexible query answering systems 000000000010th international conference fqas 000000002013 granada spain september 000000000018 000000000020 000000002013 proceedings","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-566645","ids":["ruc-9e5d1df6-885b-431f-bd69-2374f1bf9546"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C00814F55C46F13AD603F819787AAE6A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"university of granada","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Granada","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Programming, Logic and Intelligent Systems","Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Legind","key":"larsenped","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Henrik Legind","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maria Jose","key":"martinbautistaped","last":"Martin-Bautista","name":"Martin-Bautista, Maria Jose","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maria Amparo","key":"vilaped","last":"Vila","name":"Vila, Maria Amparo","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"andreasenped","last":"Andreasen","locid":"f31701bc-1bef-45ac-b9fa-3e931672bcd4","name":"Andreasen, Troels","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"christiansenped","last":"Christiansen","locid":"d1d3d938-5986-4368-a6db-1e282e894268","name":"Christiansen, Henning","orcid":"0000-0003-4731-9927","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783642407680"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"710","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","volume":"8132"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-9e5d1df6-885b-431f-bd69-2374f1bf9546"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Flexible Query Answering Systems - 10th International Conference, FQAS 2013, Granada, Spain, September 18-20, 2013. Proceedings","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-566645","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We aimed to evaluate whether the HLA-G 14-base pair (bp) polymorphism (rs16375) has an impact on human immunodeficiency virus HIV progression and survival in an antiretroviral therapy-naive Zimbabwean cohort (n = 312). Rs16375 was genotyped using a competitive allele-specific polymerase chain reaction system; CD4 cell counts and HIV RNA were measured with flow cytometry and commercially available polymerase chain reaction; survival was followed up for 4.3 years. The homozygous HLA-G -14-bp genotype is associated with higher viral load (P = .004), lower CD4 cell count (P = .01), and increased mortality (hazard ratio, 1.9; 95% confidence interval, 1.033-3.522; P = .04) compared with HLA-G +14-bp carriers.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Margit Hørup","Zinyama, Rutendo","Kallestrup, Per","Gerstoft, Jan","Gomo, Exnevia","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Berg, Trine Baldorf","Erikstrup, Christian","Ullum, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-081.72-025611"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the human leukocyte antigen g 000000000003 utr 000000000014 bp deletion is associated with poor survival in an hiv 000000000001 infected zimbabwean population","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jis924","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-081.72-025611","identifier":[{"id":"84874263153","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23264673","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b178630a-9b8d-4f4d-8f79-4416b23befdf","ku-60767065-c4e8-4882-8855-6ee5eb715b4d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6B6142C1B652CFEED055670FB8E5B65D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jis924","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Margit Hørup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Margit Hørup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rutendo","key":"zinyamapau","last":"Zinyama","name":"Zinyama, Rutendo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"kallestruppau","last":"Kallestrup","locid":"edc492e6-b4ed-4c50-8948-986e774b6f70","name":"Kallestrup, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-6041-4510","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"gerstoftpau","last":"Gerstoft","name":"Gerstoft, Jan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Exnevia","key":"gomopau","last":"Gomo","name":"Gomo, Exnevia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Wegner","key":"thørnerpau","last":"Thørner","name":"Thørner, Lise Wegner","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Baldorf","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","name":"Berg, Trine Baldorf","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","locid":"523ae417-65a9-46aa-b665-0d88271dc0b9","name":"Erikstrup, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6551-6647","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"erikstuppau","last":"Erikstup","name":"Erikstup, Christian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23264673"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jis924","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"issue":"6","journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"903-6","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","title_org":"Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"207"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874263153"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b178630a-9b8d-4f4d-8f79-4416b23befdf","ku-60767065-c4e8-4882-8855-6ee5eb715b4d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Human Leukocyte Antigen-G 3'UTR 14-bp Deletion is Associated with Poor Survival in an HIV-1-infected Zimbabwean Population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.72-025611","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Exergames have been suggested as an innovative approach to enhance physical activity in the elderly. The objective of this review was to determine the effectiveness of exergames on validated quantitative physical outcomes in healthy elderly individuals. We used Centre for Review and Disseminations guidance to conduct systematic reviews. Four electronic databases were searched. We included randomized controlled trials (RCTs), the study participants were healthy elderly individuals, and the intervention of interest was exergaming. The title and abstract screening of the 1861 citations identified 36 studies as potentially eligible for this review, and an additional nine were identified from reference lists. The full text screening identified seven studies with a total of 311 participants, all reporting RCTs with low-to-moderate methodological quality. Six of the seven studies found a positive effect of exergaming on the health of the elderly. However, the variation of intervention approaches and outcome data collected limited the extent to which studies could be compared. This review demonstrates how exergames have a potential to improve physical health in the elderly. However, there is a need for additional and better-designed studies that assess the effectiveness and long-term adherence of exergames designed specifically for the elderly.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Lisbeth H.","Schou, Lone","Lund, Henrik Hautop","Langberg, Henning"],"cuid":["S02-094.59-036348"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the physical effect of exergames in healthy elderly a systematic review","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1089/g4h.2013.0036","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.59-036348","identifier":[{"id":"26192224","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84992679457","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a5318b47-175f-4640-ba36-dd4ee7dce2c9","ku-7baca891-ed42-47ad-b0f9-65ec69a721b9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-86A2E157F16527A912628BDA1C088C16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1089/g4h.2013.0036","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60336432/ExergamesElderly-SystematicReview.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Centre for Playware","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lisbeth Højkjær","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"332b43b7-7a50-4c2e-be3e-371ab4d4b90f","name":"Larsen, Lisbeth Hoejkjaer","name_org":"Larsen, Lisbeth Højkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-1876-9876","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lone Helle","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"478cfd7b-6c7c-49b7-936d-ffe9245dc0db","name":"Schou, Lone Helle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Hautop","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"51100dd0-5ecf-47c4-84f7-f30f57dd6fb5","name":"Lund, Henrik Hautop","orcid":"0000-0002-0122-5258","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"langbergpau","last":"Langberg","locid":"aa9694cb-06fd-4f81-a6f7-c5862f8d3499","name":"Langberg, Henning","orcid":"0000-0001-8454-6534","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26192224"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1089/g4h.2013.0036","issn":["2161783X","21617856"],"issn_org":["2161783X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Games for Health","pages":"205-212","publisher":"Mary AnnLiebert, Inc. Publishers","status":"p","title":"Games for Health","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84992679457"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a5318b47-175f-4640-ba36-dd4ee7dce2c9","ku-7baca891-ed42-47ad-b0f9-65ec69a721b9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Physical Effect of Exergames in Healthy Elderly—A Systematic Review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.59-036348","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To estimate the positive predictive value (PPV) and completeness of the monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance (MGUS) diagnosis coding in a hospital registry within a population-based health-care setting. Patients and methods: Through the Danish National Patient Registry (DNPR), we identified 627 patients registered with MGUS in two Danish regions during the period January 2001-February 2011. We reviewed the medical records of all patients registered with MGUS at the Department of Hematology, Aalborg University Hospital, and a sample of patients registered at the other three hematological departments in the two regions. We estimated the PPV of the MGUS diagnosis based on this sample of 327 medical records. We also estimated the completeness of the DNPR by linking data from the DNPR and data from a previously validated MGUS cohort of 791 patients identified through the laboratory system covering North Jutland Region. Results: The diagnosis of MGUS was confirmed in 231 patients and assessed as probable in an additional 38 patients, corresponding to a PPV of 82.3% (95% confidence interval [CI] 78.1%-86.4%). By contrast, 58 (17.7%) of the patients did not definitively meet the diagnostic criteria for MGUS. When we excluded patients registered with malignant monoclonal gammopathy recorded prior to or within the first year after registration of MGUS in the DNPR, the PPV increased to 88.3% (95% CI 84.5%-92.1%). The DNPR only registered a diagnosis of MGUS in 133 of the 791 MGUS patients identified through the laboratory system, corresponding to a completeness of 16.8% (95% CI 14.1%-19.6%). Conclusion: The PPV of the diagnosis coding for MGUS in the DNPR is high and can be further improved by simple data restriction. However, the low completeness raises concern that MGUS patients registered in the hospital system may be highly selected.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gregersen, Henrik","Larsen, Caroline Emilie Brenner","Haglund, Anne","Mortensen, Rikke","Andersen, Niels Frost","Nørgaard, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-098.86-010468"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gregersen, Henrik"],"keyword":["Administrative data","Hospital discharge data","ICD 10","Monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data quality of the monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance diagnosis in a hospital registry","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S50757","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.86-010468","identifier":[{"id":"84883311464","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3762761","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24009431","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-db85c023-c674-48f0-b5e0-abc7059ad7f9","au-b99423f8-5c94-4b56-9483-61eccccffbcc"],"keyword":["Administrative data","Hospital discharge data","ICD-10","Monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance","Validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CCBA00A6FAA1F08CBF55C315E9B75A81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S50757","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Blodsygdomme (Hæmatologi) [Klinik Medicin]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Kirurgi og Kræftbehandling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Klinisk Medicin - Klinisk Epidemiologi, SKS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"b2fc6c08-46c8-452a-904f-a5843250f506","name":"Gregersen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline Emilie Brenner","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"223e729e-d623-482d-9659-9696ec8eb9b5","name":"Larsen, Caroline Emilie Brenner","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"haglundpau","last":"Haglund","locid":"69753bcc-e948-40f8-8167-8da2c678228a","name":"Haglund, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"8bdbceab-fde3-41ba-85d1-c0e27cbbac06","name":"Mortensen, Rikke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Frost","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"d1f8badc-e2a8-4075-a157-fe526d01d545","name":"Andersen, Niels Frost","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"3cb2ae19-c1b9-4dad-9928-adbd1c51b4b7","name":"Nørgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5891","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24009431"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s50757","issn":["11791349"],"issue":"1","journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"321-326","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","publisher_org":"Dove Medical Press Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84883311464"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Undetermined","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-db85c023-c674-48f0-b5e0-abc7059ad7f9","au-b99423f8-5c94-4b56-9483-61eccccffbcc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Data quality of the monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance diagnosis in a hospital registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.86-010468","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Lack of animal models with human-like size and pathology hampers translational research in atherosclerosis. Mouse models are missing central features of human atherosclerosis and are too small for intravascular procedures and imaging. Modeling the disease in minipigs may overcome these limitations, but it has proven difficult to induce rapid atherosclerosis in normal pigs by high-fat feeding alone, and genetically modified models similar to those created in mice are not available. D374Y gain-of-function mutations in the proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 (PCSK9) gene cause severe autosomal dominant hypercholesterolemia and accelerates atherosclerosis in humans. Using Sleeping Beauty DNA transposition and cloning by somatic cell nuclear transfer, we created Yucatan minipigs with liver-specific expression of human D374Y-PCSK9. D374Y-PCSK9 transgenic pigs displayed reduced hepatic low-density lipoprotein (LDL) receptor levels, impaired LDL clearance, severe hypercholesterolemia, and spontaneous development of progressive atherosclerotic lesions that could be visualized by noninvasive imaging. This model should prove useful for several types of translational research in atherosclerosis.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Al-Mashhadi, Rozh","Sørensen, Charlotte Brandt","Kragh, Peter M","Christoffersen, Christina","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Tolbod, Lars Poulsen","Thim, Troels","Du, Yutao","Li, Juan","Liu, Ying","Moldt, Brian","Schmidt, Mette","Vajta, Gabor","Larsen, Torben","Purup, Stig","Bolund, Lars","Nielsen, Lars B","Callesen, Henrik","Falk, Erling","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm","Bentzon, Jacob Fog"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animals","Animals Genetically Modified","Atherosclerosis","Cloning Organism","DNA","Disease Models Animal","Female","Humans","Hypercholesterolemia","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Liver","Male","Mutation","Phenotype","Proprotein Convertases","RNA Messenger","Receptors LDL","Serine Endopeptidases","Swine","Swine Miniature","Transgenes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"familial hypercholesterolemia and atherosclerosis in cloned minipigs created by dna transposition of a human pcsk000000000009 gain of function mutant","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.3004853","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-016031","identifier":[{"id":"23283366","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84872013355","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2f185926-017c-443b-a910-76c0809855af","ku-6e4a5a4b-0648-4523-807f-9bb08921f747"],"keyword":["Animals","Animals, Genetically Modified","Atherosclerosis","Cloning, Organism","DNA","Disease Models, Animal","Female","Humans","Hypercholesterolemia","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Liver","Male","Mutation","Phenotype","Proprotein Convertases","RNA, Messenger","Receptors, LDL","Serine Endopeptidases","Swine","Swine, Miniature","Transgenes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FBB2D726AB69E848804C02549A72D74F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.3004853","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, He