","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"baunbæklenepau","last":"Baunbæk","name":"Baunbæk, Lene","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdóttirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771560039"],"issn":["22449981"],"issue":"56","pages":"1202","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Scientific Report from DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy, No. 56","series":"Scientific Report from DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-639aba47-8c56-4960-87b9-d6f0ee0bafce","ku-88aca2aa-6d8b-4a5e-b963-a8338108af42"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denmark's National Inventory Report 2013 : Emission Inventories 1990-2011 - Submitted under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Kyoto Protocol","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.11-672666","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: The web has become a primary information resource about illnesses and treatments for both medical and non-medical users. Standard web search is by far the most common interface for such information. It is therefore of interest to find out how well web search engines work for diagnostic queries and what factors contribute to successes and failures. Among diseases, rare (or orphan) diseases represent an especially challenging and thus interesting class to diagnose as each is rare, diverse in symptoms and usually has scattered resources associated with it. Methods: We use an evaluation approach for web search engines for rare disease diagnosis which includes 56 real life diagnostic cases, state-of-the-art evaluation measures, and curated information resources. In addition, we introduce FindZebra, a specialized (vertical) rare disease search engine. FindZebra is powered by open source search technology and uses curated freely available online medical information. Results: FindZebra outperforms Google Search in both default setup and customised to the resources used by FindZebra. We extend FindZebra with specialized functionalities exploiting medical ontological information and UMLS medical concepts to demonstrate different ways of displaying the retrieved results to medical experts. Conclusions: Our results indicate that a specialized search engine can improve the diagnostic quality without compromising the ease of use of the currently widely popular web search engines. The proposed evaluation approach can be valuable for future development and benchmarking. The FindZebra search engine is available at http://www.findzebra.com/.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Dragusin, Radu","Petcu, Paula","Lioma, Christina Amalia","Larsen, Birger","Jørgensen, Hans Henrik","Cox, Ingemar","Hansen, Lars Kai","Ingwersen, Peter","Winther, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-033708"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Findwise","University College London"],"keyword":["Information retrieval","Rare diseases"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"findzebra a search engine for rare diseases","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/163000659/2013IJMI.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-100.00-033708","identifier":[{"id":"23462700","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84891650295","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-32a166b5-280b-4aa3-bab0-943c4906aa0d","ku-31fd9cb5-47f5-4c16-9e5c-7f88dc614f56"],"keyword":["Evaluation of web search engines","Information retrieval","Rare diseases","Specialised search engine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EE746C952BE4E2E0C90ABB3AD07FFE06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2013.01.005","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/163000659/2013IJMI.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Radu","key":"dragusinpau","last":"Dragusin","name":"Dragusin, Radu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paula","key":"petcupau","last":"Petcu","name":"Petcu, Paula","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3683438d-2cbb-4583-a99d-1b8ed50be5ce","name":"Larsen, Birger","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Henrik","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Hans Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingemar","key":"coxpau","last":"Cox","locid":"aa44faa7-75f8-4c00-bc4e-d4e854ce9285","name":"Cox, Ingemar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Kai","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3bdd1c4b-6c83-462b-a4cd-1ffbdcbff128","name":"Hansen, Lars Kai","orcid":"0000-0003-0442-5877","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"ingwersenpau","last":"Ingwersen","locid":"b7bb0323-445e-4fdf-88c8-33e399df2b46","name":"Ingwersen, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","locid":"197307fd-4be3-4649-8d17-5bbb53d7a351","name":"Winther, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-1966-3205","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23462700"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2013.01.005","issn":["13865056","18728243"],"issn_org":["13865056"],"issue":"6","journal":"International Journal of Medical Informatics","pages":"528-538","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Medical Informatics","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891650295"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-32a166b5-280b-4aa3-bab0-943c4906aa0d","ku-31fd9cb5-47f5-4c16-9e5c-7f88dc614f56"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"FindZebra: A search engine for rare diseases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-033708","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: During cancer treatment children have reduced contact with their social network of friends, and have limited participation in education, sports, and leisure activities. During and following cancer treatment, children describe school related problems, reduced physical fitness, and problems related to interaction with peers.Methods/design: The RESPECT study is a nationwide population-based prospective, controlled, mixed-methods intervention study looking at children aged 6-18 years newly diagnosed with cancer in eastern Denmark (n = 120) and a matched control group in western Denmark (n = 120). RESPECT includes Danish-speaking children diagnosed with cancer and treated at pediatric oncology units in Denmark. Primary endpoints are the level of educational achievement one year after the cessation of first-line cancer therapy, and the value of VO 2max one year after the cessation of first-line cancer therapy. Secondary endpoints are quality of life measured by validated questionnaires and interviews, and physical performance. RESPECT includes a multimodal intervention program, including ambassador-facilitated educational, physical, and social interventions. The educational intervention includes an educational program aimed at the child with cancer, the child's schoolteachers and classmates, and the child's parents. Children with cancer will each have two ambassadors assigned from their class. The ambassadors visit the child with cancer at the hospital at alternating 2-week intervals and participate in the intervention program. The physical and social intervention examines the effect of early, structured, individualized, and continuous physical activity from diagnosis throughout the treatment period. The patients are tested at diagnosis, at 3 and 6 months after diagnosis, and one year after the cessation of treatment. The study is powered to quantify the impact of the combined educational, physical, and social intervention programs.Discussion: RESPECT is the first population-based study to examine the effect of early rehabilitation for children with cancer, and to use healthy classmates as ambassadors to facilitate the normalization of social life in the hospital. For children with cancer, RESPECT contributes to expanding knowledge on rehabilitation that can also facilitate rehabilitation of other children undergoing hospitalization for long-term illness. Trial registration: Clinical Trials.gov: file. NCT01772849 and NCT01772862.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Thorsteinsson, Troels","Helms, Anne Sofie","Adamsen, Lis","Andersen, Lars Bo","Andersen, Karen Vitting","Christensen, Karl Bang","Hasle, Henrik","Heilmann, Carsten","Hejgaard, Nete","Johansen, Christoffer","Madsen, Marianne","Madsen, Svend Aage Lykke","Simovska, Venka","Strange, Birgit","Thing, Lone Friis","Wehner, Peder Skov","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Larsen, Hanne Baekgaard"],"cuid":["S03-096.81-019451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Cancer","Children","Controlled","Education","Intervention","Pediatric","Peers","Physical activity","Quality of Life","Rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study protocol rehabilitation including social and physical activity and education in children and teenagers with cancer respect","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/123722453/Study_protocol_rehabilitation_including_social_and_....pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"