en, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"32a7422d-cc2f-4301-87c9-951639ed3662","name":"Nielsen, Niels Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2978-4366","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23298857"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2012.12.002","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","pages":"57-61","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"227"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84871908743"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3d694e35-0e3a-443c-a2ae-e0b09cf9f92b","dtu-b12fc6a4-7776-4a80-bf6c-71afec2ee87d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dynamic nuclear polarization and optimal control spatial-selective 13C MRI and MRS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.51-017163","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: TH2-biased immune responses are important in allergy pathogenesis. Mechanisms of allergen-specific immunotherapy (SIT) might include the induction of regulatory T cells (Tregs) and immunoglobulin (Ig) G4 blocking antibodies, a reduction in the number of effector cells, and skewing of the cytokine profile towards a TH1-polarized immune response. We investigated the effects of SIT on T cells, on immunomodulation of human leukocyte antigen (HLA)-G, which has been associated with allergy, on regulatory cytokine expression, and on serum allergen-specific antibody subclasses (IgE and IgG4). Methods: Eleven birch and/or grass pollen-allergic patients and 10 healthy nonatopic controls were studied before and during SIT. Tregs, chemokine receptors, soluble HLA-G (sHLA-G), Ig-like transcript (ILT) 2, specific IgE, and IgG4 were studied. Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) were stimulated with pollen extract in vitro and immune factors were evaluated. Results: During SIT, the main changes in the peripheral blood were an increase in CXCR3+CD4+CD25+CD127low/- Tregs and a decrease in CCR4+CD4+CD25+CD127low/- Tregs, an increase in allergen-specific IgG4, and a decrease in sHLA-G during the first half of the treatment period. In the PBMC in vitro experiments, the following changes were observed upon allergen-stimulation: an increase in CD4+CD25+CD127low/- Tregs and ILT2+CD4+CD25+CD127low/- Tregs, an increase in IL-10 and IL-2 levels, and an increase in sHLA-G that was most pronounced at the start of SIT. Conclusions: The changes in CXCR3+CD4+CD25+CD127low/- Treg, IgG4, and sHLA-G levels in the peripheral blood and in ILT2+ Treg, IL-10, IL-2, and sHLA-G levels upon in vitro allergen stimulation suggest an upregulation in immunomodulatory factors and, to some degree, a shift towards TH1 during SIT.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Johnsen, Claus Rikard","Dalgaard, Louise T","Wurtzen, Peter Adler","Kristensen, Bjarne","Larsen, Margit Hørup","Ullum, Henrik","Søes-Petersen, Ulrik","Hviid, Thomas Vauvert F."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045513"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALK","DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-ALK","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human leukocyte antigen g and regulatory t cells during specific immunotherapy for pollen allergy","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000353281","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-045513","identifier":[{"id":"24022071","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84887034663","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b4519b71-b51b-4cd0-9f65-4cfe7b63912e","ruc-1832fc13-434e-4921-9f58-601443b30685"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-23F93EAC7200DEBF0B3518418872C7FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000353281","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Eukaryot Cellebiologi","Roskilde University, The Department of Science, Systems and Models"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":