seppe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin","key":"parkerpau","last":"Parker","locid":"b1e8c193-df46-4389-aeb1-b031abc9ad0f","name":"Parker, Benjamin L","name_org":"Parker, Benjamin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"engholmkellerpau","last":"Engholm-Keller","locid":"21ed59ad-2036-4362-bf68-8149df8e0fa3","name":"Engholm-Keller, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Eun","key":"lendalpau","last":"Lendal","locid":"d6e62008-df94-43af-a0bc-d176d55a2ed2","name":"Lendal, Sara Eun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katarzyna","key":"kulejpau","last":"Kulej","locid":"45330d55-719d-4de7-9f94-8bf20c5117bc","name":"Kulej, Katarzyna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"schulzpau","last":"Schulz","locid":"2ca338ca-a393-444f-8ea8-a1f4db7fea29","name":"Schulz, Melanie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veit","key":"schwämmlepau","last":"Schwämmle","locid":"cf8c1546-8172-4bb7-b4a4-249806add4bd","name":"Schwämmle, Veit","orcid":"0000-0002-9708-6722","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark E","key":"grahampau","last":"Graham","name":"Graham, Mark E","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"saxtorphpau","last":"Saxtorph","locid":"192802e1-3c34-4d93-8c4c-3fd2ad1bf15d","name":"Saxtorph, Henrik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stuart","key":"cordwellpau","last":"Cordwell","locid":"b8dc9a80-b171-45d2-88b7-dde75bfa0742","name":"Cordwell, Stuart J","name_org":"Cordwell, Stuart","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Røssel","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4ecd87f8-6fb1-4d10-b8a3-6d0657129eef","name":"Larsen, Martin Røssel","orcid":"0000-0001-6203-0123","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22843994"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/mcp.m112.017509","issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"issue":"11","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","pages":"1191-1202","publisher":"American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Inc.","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867259125"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9179e0bc-860f-439e-9946-135843153897"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A novel method for the simultaneous enrichment, identification and quantification of phosphopeptides and sialyted glycopeptides applied to a temporal profile of mouse brain development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614905","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Kinomic and phospho-proteomic analysis of breast cancer stem-like cells Rikke Leth-Larsen1, Anne G Christensen1, Sidse Ehmsen1, Mark Møller1, Giuseppe Palmisano2, Martin R Larsen2, Henrik J Ditzel1,3 1Institute of Molecular Medicine, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark 2Institute of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark 3Dept. of Oncology, Odense University Hospital, Odense, Denmark Cancer stem cells are thought to be responsible for tumorigenic potential and to possess resistance mechanisms against chemotherapy- and radiation-induced cancer cell death, while the bulk of a tumor lacks these capacities. The resistance mechanisms may cause these cells to survive and become the source of later tumor recurrence, highlighting the need for therapeutic strategies that specifically target pathways central to these cancer stem cells. The CD44hi/CD24-/low compartment of human breast cancer is enriched in tumor-initiating cells; however the functional heterogeneity within this subpopulation remains poorly defined. From a triple-negative breast cancer cell line we isolated and cloned CD44hi single-cells that exhibited functional heterogeneity according to cancer stem cell features, such as tumor formation in immunodeficient mice, mammosphere formation, invasion and migration abilities and sensitivity to chemotherapeutics. Quantitative proteomic analysis of these clones revealed several proteins, including kinases, exhibiting altered expression levels while other proteins exhibited altered phosphorylation levels. The quantitative proteomic approach was based on post digestion dimethyl labeling followed by TiO2 enrichment of phosphopeptides. Moreover, analysis of the flowthrough fraction revealed quantitative changes in the total proteome. Transcriptomic analysis using Affymetrix Human Gene 1.0 ST Arrays revealed similar alterations at the gene expression level. We used these single cell clones to further investigate the molecular mechanisms underlying the association between selected proteins, some of them phosphorylated, and cancer stem cell features. Furthermore, phosphosite-expression was investigated with NetworKIN that predicts in vivo kinase-substrate relationships. Our studies reveal pathways that are regulated by protein phosphorylation and include relevant kinase targets for drug discovery. Our results support functional heterogeneity in the breast cancer cell compartment and hold promise for further refinements of prognostic marker profiling of cells with cancer stem cell-like features.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Leth-Larsen, Rikke","Christensen, Anne Geske Lindhard","Ehmsen, Sidse","Møller, Mark","Palmisano, Giuseppe","Larsen, Martin Røssel","Ditzel, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627288"],"event":{"end":"2012-12-08","place":"San Antonio, Texas, us","start":"2012-12-04","title":"35th Annual SABCS","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kinomic and phospho proteomic analysis of breast cancer stem like cells","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-627288","ids":["sdu-bca06f7e-54e2-4928-bb7a-39605dc760b2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7374488B8F152A2C5824B3AF064C204E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Ditzel group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"lethlarsenpau","last":"Leth-Larsen","locid":"66fd89b9-b81d-4e74-bf02-9a0ea313ee3e","name":"Leth-Larsen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-1612-4089","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Geske Lindhard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"a50038ec-672b-4935-9dcf-2826ec1cca77","name":"Christensen, Anne Geske Lindhard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidse","key":"ehmsenpau","last":"Ehmsen","locid":"c839634d-08df-43e0-9e69-c8abc04d56cc","name":"Ehmsen, Sidse","orcid":"0000-0002-4807-6325","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"8dac4fbe-74f2-4061-8bc2-c77a3562ccc4","name":"Møller, Mark","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppe","key":"palmisanopau","last":"Palmisano","locid":"6837e2ae-fde3-4177-818f-14001d010e76","name":"Palmisano, Giuseppe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Røssel","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4ecd87f8-6fb1-4d10-b8a3-6d0657129eef","name":"Larsen, Martin Røssel","orcid":"0000-0001-6203-0123","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"ditzelpau","last":"Ditzel","locid":"f10637d7-ca3b-4956-a007-100f66737838","name":"Ditzel, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-3927-5135","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bca06f7e-54e2-4928-bb7a-39605dc760b2"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Kinomic and phospho-proteomic analysis of breast cancer stem-like cells","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627288","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The aim of the study was to investigate the distribution of net joint moments in the lower extremities during walking on high-heeled shoes compared with barefooted walking at identical speed. Fourteen female subjects walked at 4 km/h across three force platforms while they were filmed by five digital video cameras operating at 50 frames/second. Both barefooted walking and walking on high-heeled shoes (heel height: 9 cm) were recorded. Net joint moments were calculated by 3D inverse dynamics. EMG was recorded from eight leg muscles. The knee extensor moment peak in the first half of the stance phase was doubled when walking on high heels. The knee joint angle showed that high-heeled walking caused the subjects to flex the knee joint significantly more in the first half of the stance phase. In the frontal plane a significant increase was observed in the knee joint abductor moment and the hip joint abductor moment. Several EMG parameters increased significantly when walking on high-heels. The results indicate a large increase in bone-on-bone forces in the knee joint directly caused by the increased knee joint extensor moment during high-heeled walking, which may explain the observed higher incidence of osteoarthritis in the knee joint in women as compared with men.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Simonsen, Erik B","Svendsen, Morten Bo Søndergaard","Nørreslet, Andreas","Baldvinsson, Henrik Koblauch","Heilskov-Hansen, Thomas","Larsen, Peter Kastmand","Alkjær, Tine","Henriksen, Marius"],"cuid":["S02-080.65-666737"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["EMG","Inverse dynamics","Walking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"walking on high heels changes muscle activity and the dynamics of human walking significantly","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84859053663","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-080.65-666737","identifier":[{"id":"22431211","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84859053663","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-42b4223b-1e24-49f4-a13b-0818766d5c4d","ku-569a1909-f6b8-4257-82ff-843772d12e71"],"keyword":["EMG","High-heeled shoes","Inverse dynamics","Walking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-798DA1CB23197A6D03CF110E4BE0D1F2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCC (ophørt), Fysioterapeutuddannelsen, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen, Underviser"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Erik B","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"bf237e56-a718-4d23-973e-1774b5a861c5","name":"Simonsen, Erik B","orcid":"0000-0002-6378-6595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"koblauchpau","last":"Koblauch","locid":"e4f33489-8e36-4fdf-a7f7-9e380d7bf9bf","name":"Koblauch, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten Bo Søndergaard","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"b8bbbb95-b2d0-458d-b8a1-dfec67c88f53","name":"Svendsen, Morten Bo Søndergaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4492-3750","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"nørresletpau","last":"Nørreslet","name":"Nørreslet, Andreas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik K","key":"baldvinssonpau","last":"Baldvinsson","locid":"51f1498f-8f12-4131-893c-2710ab7e2eea","name":"Baldvinsson, Henrik Koblauch","name_org":"Baldvinsson, Henrik K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"heilskovhansenpau","last":"Heilskov-Hansen","name":"Heilskov-Hansen, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter K","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"40901ff4-3fcc-4f8f-a02a-96dabb3b0e8c","name":"Larsen, Peter Kastmand","name_org":"Larsen, Peter K","orcid":"0000-0002-8820-2058","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tine","key":"alkjærpau","last":"Alkjær","locid":"d0ff1f22-b755-48d5-b5c9-94a9ef4367ac","name":"Alkjær, Tine","orcid":"0000-0002-9105-3882","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marius","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"0cadf7d6-9539-4ade-9bc4-98402453e742","name":"Henriksen, Marius","orcid":"0000-0003-1091-2962","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22431211"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1123/jab.28.1.20","issn":["10658483","15432688"],"issn_org":["10658483"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Applied Biomechanics","pages":"20-28","publisher":"Human Kinetics Publishers Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Biomechanics","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84859053663"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-42b4223b-1e24-49f4-a13b-0818766d5c4d","ku-569a1909-f6b8-4257-82ff-843772d12e71"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Walking on high heels changes muscle activity and the dynamics of human walking significantly","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.65-666737","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The development of metastasis is a complex, multistep process that remains poorly defined. To identify proteins involved in the colonization phase of the metastatic process, we compared the proteome of tumors derived from inoculation of a panel of isogenic human cancer cell lines with different metastatic capabilities into the mammary fat pad of immunodeficient mice. Using a protein standard generated by SILAC-labeling, a total of 675 proteins were identified and 30 were differentially expressed between at least two of the tumors. The protein standard contained the proteomes of seven cell lines from multiple histogenic origins and displayed superior features compared to standard super-SILAC. The expression of some proteins correlated with metastatic capabilities, such as myosin-9 (nonmuscle myosin II A) and L-lactate dehydrogenase A, while the expression of elongation factor tu correlated inversely to metastatic capabilities. The expression of these proteins was biochemically validated, and expression of myosin-9 in clinical breast cancer samples was further shown to be altered in primary tumors versus corresponding lymph node metastasis. Our study demonstrates an improved strategy for quantitative comparison of an unlimited number of tumor tissues, and provides novel insights into key proteins associated with the colonization phase of metastasis formation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lund, Rikke","Terp, Mikkel Green","Lænkholm, Anne-Vibeke","Jensen, Ole Nørregaard","Leth-Larsen, Rikke","Ditzel, Henrik Jørn"],"cuid":["S02-098.62-043377"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animals","Breast Neoplasms genetics","Breast metabolism","Cell Line Tumor","Female","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Humans","Isotope Labeling methods","Mice","Mice SCID","Neoplasm Metastasis genetics","Neoplasms genetics","Proteins analysis","Proteomics methods","Tandem Mass Spectrometry methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantitative proteomics of primary tumors with varying metastatic capabilities using stable isotope labeled proteins of multiple histogenic origins","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pmic.201100490","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.62-043377","identifier":[{"id":"84864017230","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22623409","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-705c3094-a1e2-4450-aa31-4d0e10dc3b6c","sdu-c260ce7b-a7d9-4d4b-a201-908fc39c9a1e"],"keyword":["Animals","Breast Neoplasms/genetics","Breast/metabolism","Cell Line, Tumor","Female","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Humans","Isotope Labeling/methods","Mice","Mice, SCID","Myosins/analysis","Neoplasm Metastasis/genetics","Neoplasms/genetics","Proteins/analysis","Proteomics/methods","Tandem Mass Spectrometry/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-584E34B2AC9BF33366B6C1DB7EED3EFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pmic.201100490","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Ditzel group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Rikke Raaen","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"ffd99d7e-c38d-413f-9761-cb8b1c770e7d","name":"Lund, Rikke","name_org":"Lund, Rikke Raaen","orcid":"0000-0002-0381-4291","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Green","key":"terppau","last":"Terp","locid":"31863af3-7d3a-48d5-ae0a-e76e938a23fb","name":"Terp, Mikkel Green","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-6900","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne-Vibeke","key":"laenkholmpau","last":"Laenkholm","locid":"13a69661-098a-4035-8245-0b75d9011883","name":"Lænkholm, Anne-Vibeke","name_org":"Laenkholm, Anne-Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0003-2166-8686","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Nørregaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d918f237-468a-4785-ab50-d716d3ecb613","name":"Jensen, Ole Nørregaard","orcid":"0000-0003-1862-8528","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"lethlarsenpau","last":"Leth-Larsen","locid":"66fd89b9-b81d-4e74-bf02-9a0ea313ee3e","name":"Leth-Larsen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-1612-4089","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Henrik Jørn","key":"ditzelpau","last":"Ditzel","locid":"49a4d2d7-b63d-478b-9864-51d674b43427","name":"Ditzel, Henrik Jørn","orcid":"0000-0003-3927-5135","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22623409"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pmic.201100490","issn":["16159853","16159861"],"issn_org":["16159853"],"issue":"13","journal":"Proteomics","pages":"2139-2148","publisher":"Wiley-VCH","status":"p","title":"Proteomics","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864017230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-705c3094-a1e2-4450-aa31-4d0e10dc3b6c","sdu-c260ce7b-a7d9-4d4b-a201-908fc39c9a1e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Quantitative proteomics of primary tumors with varying metastatic capabilities using stable isotope-labeled proteins of multiple histogenic origins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.62-043377","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE:: Detection of coronary artery calcification (CAC) has been proposed for population screening. It remains unknown whether such a strategy would result in unnecessary concern among participants. Therefore, we set out to assess whether CAC screening affects the psychological well-being of screening participants. MATERIALS AND METHODS:: A random sample of 1825 middle-aged subjects (men and women, 50 or 60 y old) were invited for health screening. The European HeartScore was calculated, and a CAC score was measured using a cardiac computed tomography scanner. Therapeutic interventions as a result of the observations were at the discretion of the individual general practitioner. Before screening and at 6-month follow-up a depression test (Major Depression Inventory) was conducted, and the use of psychoactive medication was recorded. RESULTS:: A total of 1257 (69%) subjects agreed to participate. Because of known cardiovascular disease or diabetes mellitus, 88 persons were excluded. Of the remaining 1169, 47% were men, and one half were 50 years old. At 6-month follow-up, significant reductions were observed in the Major Depression Inventory score from 5.3 to 3.9 (P","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anders Daldorph","Videbech, Poul","Gerke, Oke","Petersen, Henrik","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Sand, Niels Peter","Egstrup, Kenneth","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Mickley, Hans","Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt"],"cuid":["S02-098.72-022308"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Daldorph Nielsen, Anders"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"population screening for coronary artery calcification does not increase mental distress and the use of psychoactive medication","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/RTI.0b013e31824752bd","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.72-022308","identifier":[{"id":"22336666","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84860010825","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-844f4d34-7e32-4115-b913-9535a074250c","sdu-11a2f487-a034-4f65-951d-e9aa484ced68"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AABB7688BA4FAAA1D209C23CAC9CA616"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/RTI.0b013e31824752bd","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of General Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Daldorph","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"41273198-772a-4897-bec1-31feee63cd48","name":"Daldorph Nielsen, Anders","name_org":"Nielsen, Anders Daldorph","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"videbehpau","last":"Videbeh","locid":"5133ad1e-4d6c-49f3-9d2d-86c4cd33870a","name":"Videbech, Poul","name_org":"Videbeh, Poul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"videbechpau","last":"Videbech","name":"Videbech, Poul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oke","key":"gerkepau","last":"Gerke","locid":"596baeb1-6754-4d53-948f-30470dd1d976","name":"Gerke, Oke","orcid":"0000-0001-6335-3303","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ea635371-4294-4379-9655-3da538fecf13","name":"Petersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1118-1500","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Peter Rønnow","key":"sandpau","last":"Sand","locid":"167f1566-1eb7-495f-be19-63a30a43aff1","name":"Sand, Niels Peter","name_org":"Sand, Niels Peter Rønnow","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"egstruppau","last":"Egstrup","locid":"12389a61-a119-4ff8-ba31-4b0accb0bbc5","name":"Egstrup, Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0002-6214-8751","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens Lytken","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0b7868d1-86b5-490e-bcf2-95fc4e33319f","name":"Larsen, Mogens Lytken","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"mickleypau","last":"Mickley","locid":"f6789f9a-e23b-4ab8-bd7d-a3c168107cdb","name":"Mickley, Hans","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel Cosmus Pyndt","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","locid":"d84be6bc-52bf-4710-9f66-0209cfab4f54","name":"Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-1285-4826","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22336666"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/rti.0b013e31824752bd","issn":["08835993","15360237"],"issn_org":["08835993"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Thoracic Imaging","pages":"202-206","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Thoracic Imaging","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860010825"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-844f4d34-7e32-4115-b913-9535a074250c","sdu-11a2f487-a034-4f65-951d-e9aa484ced68"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Population Screening for Coronary Artery Calcification Does Not Increase Mental Distress and the Use of Psychoactive Medication","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.72-022308","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The CD44(hi) compartment in human breast cancer is enriched in tumor-initiating cells; however, the functional heterogeneity within this subpopulation remains poorly defined. We used a triple-negative breast cancer cell line with a known bilineage phenotype to isolate and clone CD44(hi) single cells that exhibited mesenchymal/basal B and luminal/basal A features, respectively. Herein, we demonstrate in this and other triple-negative breast cancer cell lines that, rather than CD44(hi)/CD24(-) mesenchymal-like basal B cells, the CD44(hi)/CD24(lo) epithelioid basal A cells retained classic cancer stem cell features, such as tumor-initiating capacity in vivo, mammosphere formation and resistance to standard chemotherapy. These results complement previous findings using oncogene-transformed normal mammary cells showing that only cell clones with a mesenchymal phenotype exhibit cancer stem cell features. Further, we performed comparative quantitative proteomic and gene array analyses of these cells and identified potential novel markers of breast cancer cells with tumor-initiating features, such as lipolysis-stimulated lipoprotein receptor (LSR), RAB25, S100A14 and mucin 1 (MUC1), as well as a novel 31-gene signature capable of predicting distant metastasis in cohorts of estrogen receptor-negative human breast cancers. These findings strongly favor functional heterogeneity in the breast cancer cell compartment and hold promise for further refinements of prognostic marker profiling. Our work confirms that, in addition to cancer stem cells with mesenchymal-like morphology, those tumor-initiating cells with epithelial-like morphology should also be the focus of drug development.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Leth-Larsen, Rikke","Terp, Mikkel Green","Christensen, Anne G","Elias, Daniel","Kühlwein, Thorsten","Jensen, Ole N","Petersen, Ole William","Ditzel, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.39-045254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Ditzel-gruppen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional heterogeneity within the cd000000000044 high human breast cancer stem cell like compartment reveals a gene signature predictive of distant metastasis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2119/molmed.2012.00091","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.39-045254","identifier":[{"id":"22692575","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3474436","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84866746710","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ac6ac2e4-1aa1-46d5-8a19-a259a614b5d3","sdu-bdcfcb6a-0e1f-4bc9-91d5-1715e19850dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2120AD55F36E949F7E32AF624C79D5A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2119/molmed.2012.00091","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.molmed.org/journal/articles/27/1533","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Ditzel group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Ditz