},{"affno":"3","first":"Susanne Bødtker","key":"petersensusannebødtkerpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Susanne Bødtker","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"baunbæklenepau","last":"Baunbæk","name":"Baunbæk, Lene","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdóttirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Maria Gunnleivsdottir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdottirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdottir","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["978879282536"],"issn":["22450203"],"issue":"56","pages":"1202","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","publisher_org":"Aarhus University, DCE – Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Scientiﬁc Report from DCE – Danish Centre for Environment and Energy, No. 56","series":"Scientiﬁc Report from DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8b440646-6584-4892-bb09-ebcef027022f","ku-0e7fad36-64ae-4481-8412-1167e9c78987","ku-1eab3343-5ee5-4ccd-ad8b-0548442a040d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denmark’s National Inventory Report 2012 : Emission Inventories 1990-2010 - Submitted under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Kyoto Protocol","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-089.83-672719","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Expanded newborn screening for selected inborn errors of metabolism (IEM) in Denmark, the Faroe Islands and Greenland was introduced in 2002. We now present clinical, biochemical, and statistical results of expanded screening (excluding PKU) of 504,049 newborns during nine years as well as diagnoses and clinical findings in 82,930 unscreened newborns born in the same period. The frequencies of diagnoses made within the panel of disorders screened for are compared with the frequencies of the disorders in the decade preceding expanded newborn screening. The expanded screening was performed as a pilot study during the first seven years, and the experience obtained during these years was used in the development of the routine neonatal screening program introduced in 2009. Methods for screening included tandem mass spectrometry and an assay for determination of biotinidase activity. A total of 310 samples from 504,049 newborns gave positive screening results. Of the 310 results, 114 were true positive, including results from 12 newborns in which the disease in question was subsequently diagnosed in their mothers. Thus, the overall frequency of an IEM in the screening panel was 1:4942 (mothers excluded) or 1:4421 (mothers included). The false positive rate was 0.038% and positive predictive value 37%. Overall specificity was 99.99%. All patients with true positive results were followed in The Center for Inherited Metabolic Disorders in Copenhagen, and the mean follow-up period was 45 months (range 2109 months). There were no deaths among the 102 children, and 94% had no clinically significant sequelae at last follow-up. Our study confirms the higher frequency of selected IEM after implementation of expanded newborn screening and suggests an improved outcome for several disorders. We argue that newborn screening for these disorders should be standard of care, though unresolved issues remain, e.g. about newborns with a potential for remaining asymptomatic throughout life. Well organized logistics of the screening program from screening laboratory to centralized, clinical management is important.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Lund, Allan Meldgaard","Hougaard, David Michael","Simonsen, Henrik","Andresen, Brage Storstein","Christensen, Mette","Dunø, Morten","Skogstrand, Kristin","Olsen, Rikke Katrine Jentoft","Jensen, Ulrich Glümer","Cohen, Arieh","Larsen, Nanna","Saugmann-Jensen, Peter","Gregersen, Niels","Brandt, Niels Jacob","Christensen, Ernst","Skovby, Flemming","Nørgaard-Pedersen, Bent"],"cuid":["S03-097.68-028662"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Institut for Klinisk Medicin - Molekylær Medicinsk Forsk.enhed"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biochemical screening of 000000000504 000000000049 newborns in denmark the faroe islands and greenland experience and development of a routine program for expanded newborn screening","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ymgme.2012.06.006","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.68-028662","identifier":[{"id":"22795865","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84867897278","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-dc897e6d-db52-4940-8bb3-c6eb87130dd6","ku-161e2a0b-cf18-4944-95fd-b211963e776f","sdu-6ea32b3b-6c8a-4bf1-9c26-c2df6024a7e9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-D650026D8EC032C4D23A7D0531777897"],"oa_link":[{"acc