{"abstract":"MRS of hyperpolarized 13C‐labeled compounds represents a promising technique for in vivo metabolic studies. However, robust quantification and metabolic modeling are still important areas of investigation. In particular, time and spatial resolution constraints may lead to the analysis of MRS signals with low signal‐to‐noise ratio (SNR). The relationship between SNR and the precision of quantitative analysis for the evaluation of the in vivo kinetic behavior of metabolites is unknown. In this article, this topic is addressed by Monte Carlo simulations, covering the problem of MRS signal model parameter estimation, with strong emphasis on the peak amplitude and kinetic model parameters. The results of Monte Carlo simulation were confirmed by in vivo experiments on medium‐sized animals injected with hyperpolarized [1‐13C]pyruvate. The results of this study may be useful for the establishment of experimental planning and for the optimization of kinetic model estimation as a function of the SNR value.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Santarelli, Maria Filomena","Positano, Vincenzo","Giovannetti, Giulio","Frijia, Francesca","Menichetti, Luca","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","De Marchi, Daniele","Lionetti, Vincenzo","Aquaro, Giovanni","Lombardi, Massimo","Landini, Luigi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324488"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Research Council of Italy","Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","University of Pisa"],"keyword":["Kinetic model","MRS","Signal to noise ratio","dynamic MRS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how the signal to noise ratio influences hyperpolarized 000000000013c dynamic mrs data fitting and parameter estimation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.1813","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324488","identifier":[{"id":"84862313772","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22213413","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-42f252ec-7c36-4233-bce0-89c425f7a8e8"],"keyword":["Dynamic MRS","Hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate","Hyperpolarized nuclei","In vivo cardiac metabolism","Kinetic model","MRS","Signal-to-noise ratio"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-334D7272C3A8B96832F708DFF6A5BECF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.1813","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"sant anna school of advanced studies","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of pisa","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Pisa","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Filomena","key":"santarellipau","last":"Santarelli","name":"Santarelli, Maria Filomena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo","key":"positanopau","last":"Positano","name":"Positano, Vincenzo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giulio","key":"giovannettipau","last":"Giovannetti","name":"Giovannetti, Giulio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"frijiapau","last":"Frijia","name":"Frijia, Francesca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"menichettipau","last":"Menichetti","name":"Menichetti, Luca","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"demarchipau","last":"De Marchi","name":"De Marchi, Daniele","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo","key":"lionettipau","last":"Lionetti","name":"Lionetti, Vincenzo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"aquaropau","last":"Aquaro","name":"Aquaro, Giovanni","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Massimo","key":"lombardipau","last":"Lombardi","name":"Lombardi, Massimo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luigi","key":"landinipau","last":"Landini","name":"Landini, Luigi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22213413"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.1813","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"7","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","pages":"925-934","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","title_org":"N M R in Biomedicine","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84862313772"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-42f252ec-7c36-4233-bce0-89c425f7a8e8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"How the signal‐to‐noise ratio influences hyperpolarized 13C dynamic MRS data fitting and parameter estimation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324488","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In the EU and in Denmark, the aim is to reduce dependence on fossil fuels and to use energy more efficiently. District heating and combined heat and power have significant potential with regard to achieving this aim. New technologies may make individual solutions such as electric heating, heat pumps and micro-CHP more attractive than previously. Therefore, the competitive conditions between district heating and other types of heating may change in the future. The question is therefore whether district heating can contribute to ensuring the sustainability of future energy systems? Denmark is used as a case as the country has a high share of district heating and produces 20% of the electricity with wind power. The analyses are carried out using the electricity market model Balmorel, which facilitates cost optimization of operation and investments in energy production plants as well as electricity transmission. To be able to perform the analysis an extension of the model is developed, where it is also possible to optimize between investments in individual heating plants or in expansion of the district heating networks, depending on investment costs, energy density of the potential areas and their distance to existing district heating networks. Results show that district heating may contribute to the sustainability and security of supply of future energy systems and that under the given assumptions it is cost effective to increase the share of district heating up to 55e57% of the heat demand although substantial heat saving measures are installed.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Münster, Marie","Morthorst, Poul Erik","Larsen, Helge V.","Bregnbæk, Lars","Werling, Jesper","Lindboe, Hans henrik","Ravn, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-337651"],"event":{"end":"2011-09-29","place":"Dubrovnik, hr","start":"2011-09-25","title":"6th Dubrovnik Conference on Sustainable Development of Energy, Water and Environment Systems","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["District heating","Energy system analysis","Optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of district heating in the future danish energy system","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164675952/Efficient_district_heating_data_and_results_120420_resubmission_heading.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-337651","identifier":[{"id":"84869887421","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6ec4e8f3-6ec9-4f26-959e-3271d961377f"],"keyword":["District heating","Energy system analysis","Optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD075DE8A0647AAE3B01800674FB18D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164675952/Efficient_district_heating_data_and_results_120420_resubmission_heading.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Systems Analysis","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Systems Analysis, Energy Systems Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["EA Energy Analysis A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"münsterpau","last":"Münster","locid":"48791cb0-5c40-4de1-8659-e6cfb586f16a","name":"Münster, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-5543-547X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul Erik","key":"morthorstpau","last":"Morthorst","locid":"ffe4b1d0-55d5-4dc7-914c-a1faf6bedae2","name":"Morthorst, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-4977-1976","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge V.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e4953c9e-e90b-49f3-9f6e-b9ec7fb4e1c0","name":"Larsen, Helge V.","orcid":"0000-0002-2619-2405","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"bregnbækpau","last":"Bregnbæk","name":"Bregnbæk, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"werlingpau","last":"Werling","name":"Werling, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans henrik","key":"lindboepau","last":"Lindboe","name":"Lindboe, Hans henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, Hans","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.energy.2012.06.011","issn":["03605442","18736785"],"issn_org":["03605442"],"issue":"1","journal":"Energy","pages":"47-55","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Energy","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84869887421"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","ea energy analysis