","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Vedby","key":"rasmussenmikkelvedbypau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"40de0356-32fa-4c3a-a03f-7e8952dd21cb","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Vedby","orcid":"0000-0003-1427-6211","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars Bangert","key":"struwelarsbangertpau","last":"Struwe","locid":"3224baff-52ad-4d6b-85ca-4395566e6997","name":"Struwe, Lars Bangert","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Esben Salling","key":"larsenesbensallingpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3f60ffd7-91d2-4215-9dc9-c54f72495a02","name":"Larsen, Esben Salling","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Knus","key":"larsenkristianknuspau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8be7327b-0875-49aa-9c53-3a4775defc80","name":"Larsen, Kristian Knus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"pradhanblachflemmingpau","last":"Pradhan-Blach","locid":"01274442-f4fd-4731-badf-e640c7004299","name":"Pradhan-Blach, Flemming","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Ø.","key":"breitenbauchhenrikøpau","last":"Breitenbauch","locid":"981ff35b-9e40-42ed-95b9-ea5b3e5aac30","name":"Breitenbauch, Henrik Ø.","orcid":"0000-0001-6302-3670","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Søby","key":"kristensenkristiansøbypau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"271c23b9-c5b2-49d9-9b0f-b55a9340e189","name":"Kristensen, Kristian Søby","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-8014","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788773936658"],"pages":"45","place":"Kbh.","publisher":"Center for militære studier","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-183e2845-b0e0-426b-b25e-c3f9c80235a3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"En analyse af vilkår for dansk forsvarspolitik – strategiske valg 2012","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-407905","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Upon subcutaneous administration, the distribution of drug between the delivery vehicle and the biological tissue critically affects the absorption of drug substances. Utilization of physical models resembling the native tissues appears promising for obtaining a detailed understanding of the performance of drug delivery systems based on in vitro experiments. The objective of this study was to evaluate a UV imaging-based method for real-time characterization of the release and transport of piroxicam in hydrogel-based subcutaneous tissue mimics/surrogates. Piroxicam partitioning from medium chain triglyceride (MCT) into 0.5% (w/v) agarose or 25% (w/v) F127-based hydrogels was investigated by monitoring the concentration profiles of the drug in the gels. The effect of pH on piroxicam distribution and diffusion coefficients was studied. For both hydrogel systems, the diffusion of piroxicam in the gels was not affected significantly by the pH change from 4.0 to 7.4 but a considerable change in the oil-gel distribution coefficients was found (24 and 34 times less at pH 7.4 as compared those observed at pH 4.0 for F127 and agarose gels, respectively). In addition, the release and transport processes of piroxicam upon the injection of aqueous or MCT solutions into an agarose-based hydrogel were investigated by UV imaging. The spatial distribution of piroxicam around the injection site in the gel matrix was monitored in real-time. The disappearance profiles of piroxicam from the injected aqueous solution were obtained. This study shows that the UV imaging methodology has considerable potential for characterizing transport properties in hydrogels, including monitoring the real-time spatial concentration distribution in vitro after administration by injection.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ye, Fengbin","Larsen, Susan Weng","Yaghmur, Anan","Jensen, Henrik","Larsen, Claus Selch","Østergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-422307"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug release into hydrogel based subcutaneous surrogates studied by uv imaging","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpba.2012.07.024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-422307","identifier":[{"id":"22889608","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84866746572","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-306f19c0-620d-4334-8e69-647d6ca5a5af"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-228E5C68EA5D8F7E806321CEA1468784"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpba.2012.07.024","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Fengbin","key":"yefengbinpau","last":"Ye","locid":"980648a3-6e03-4240-868c-d93ea67c9371","name":"Ye, Fengbin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Susan Weng","key":"larsensusanwengpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f6980004-978f-4940-b71f-de426f2a084a","name":"Larsen, Susan Weng","orcid":"0000-0002-3818-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anan","key":"yaghmurananpau","last":"Yaghmur","locid":"a910866e-d3b9-4a69-b238-005ea9906b8f","name":"Yaghmur, Anan","orcid":"0000-0003-1608-773X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"jensenhenrikpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"88cd8faf-69c6-46de-a355-03f93d52eeb1","name":"Jensen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus Selch","key":"larsenclausselchpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"38dcfe91-cef0-4a89-911b-30e3383ffdec","name":"Larsen, Claus Selch","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardjesperpau","last":"Ostergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","name_org":"Ostergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22889608"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpba.2012.07.024","issn":["07317085","1873264X"],"journal":"Journal of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Analysis","pages":"27-34","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Analysis","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866746572"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-306f19c0-620d-4334-8e69-647d6ca5a5af"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Drug release into hydrogel-based subcutaneous surrogates studied by UV imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-422307","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Cystic echinococcosis (CE) of the liver can be treated with ultrasound-guided puncture, aspiration, injection, and re-aspiration (PAIR), with surgery and with benzimidazole derivatives. The aim of this study was to review available data concerning treatment modality and outcome for patients treated for CE of the liver in a Danish tertiary reference center.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Branci, Sonia","Ewertsen, Caroline","Thybo, Søren","Nielsen, Henrik V","Jensen, Flemming","Wettergren, André","Larsen, Peter N","Bygbjerg, Ib Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472045"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Albendazole","Anthelmintics","Cysts","Denmark","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Liver","Male","Middle Aged","Punctures","Retrospective Studies","Suction","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cystic echinococcosis of the liver experience from a danish tertiary reference center 000000002002 000000002010","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1708-8305.2011.00577.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-472045","identifier":[{"id":"22221809","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84855505063","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-835949fd-3ed7-41c7-a9b9-ff881ef07179"],"keyword":["Adult","Albendazole","Anthelmintics","Cysts","Denmark","Echinococcosis, Hepatic","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Liver","Male","Middle Aged","Punctures","Retrospective Studies","Suction","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-291025CF25DC53AE8919FD899540D0B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1708-8305.2011.00577.x","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1708-8305.2011.00577.x/abstract","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Morphogenesis and Differentiation Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sonia","key":"brancipau","last":"Branci","locid":"4d395346-61db-4e51-9a11-b138b9e984bf","name":"Branci, Sonia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Caroline","key":"ewertsenpau","last":"Ewertsen","locid":"51880e6f-4b00-4868-9005-6a0464367816","name":"Ewertsen, Caroline","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren","key":"thybopau","last":"Thybo","locid":"c0307672-535d-4419-88fd-4e80393fbd8b","name":"Thybo, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik V","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik V","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Flemming","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"88ddabc4-adcb-4502-900e-8eda1dfae892","name":"Jensen, Flemming","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"André","key":"wettergrenpau","last":"Wettergren","locid":"0ca6b192-53f1-497b-9f9f-d8c66b945320","name":"Wettergren, André","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter N","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"443a21ab-2266-47a3-9db7-6757ca35147e","name":"Larsen, Peter N","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ib C","key":"bygbjergpau","last":"Bygbjerg","locid":"acec49c2-8e30-45f6-8785-19112c22d379","name":"Bygbjerg, Ib Christian","name_org":"Bygbjerg, Ib C","orcid":"0000-0001-9100-2754","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22221809"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1708-8305.2011.00577.x","issn":["11951982","17088305"],"issn_org":["11951982"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Travel Medicine","pages":"28-34","status":"p","title":"Journal of Travel Medicine","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855505063"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-835949fd-3ed7-41c7-a9b9-ff881ef07179"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cystic echinococcosis of the liver : experience from a Danish tertiary reference center (2002-2010)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472045","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Over several years, Danish Defence and the Danish Emergency Management Agency have acquired extensive experience respectively deploying to conflict zones and disasters. Therefore we can naturally consider if Danish Defence and the Danish Emergency Management Agency can work in a complementary fashion. This report suggests that when considering the use of armed forces in an emergency you should consider the following four points: 1) Is it demanded: Internationally, e.g. by the UN and the state that has experienced the disaster, and/or by developments in Danish domestic politics? 2) Timeliness of the deployment. 3) Is the deployment „modular¿, for instance, in the form of: a) Personnel; b) equipment; c) management? 4) The nature of interaction. Could increased „jointery¿ and interoperability possibly be ensured through frequent exercises, and the creation of a fixed overall management team? In an disaster a professional approach is required. The military must therefore be used for what they are specialized in doing. The military does not need to develop new capabilities, but the current capabilities can be better used to support the Danish Emergency Management Agency. This will require a small joint management and planning unit. Overall the report raises five mutually independent propositions: • Pragmatism - in emergencies there is a need for improvisation and pragmatism, therefore one must be careful not to be overwhelmed or constrained by comprehensive legal regulation. • Transport and mobility - there is an absolute need for agility of movement during an emergency, and the military can provide this capability on land, sea and air. • Use of the The Absalon-class support ships: They were originally developed in the 1990s to include amongst their roles support to UN operations in disaster zones, as a platform for staff, and the ships can transport materiel and up to 200 men. • ISR - Intelligence, Surveillance & Reconnaissance. There is a great need for ISR support when the Danish Emergency Management Agency is deployed. The military has a wide range of ISR platforms and capabilities that should be exploited to a much greater degree for the purpose of supporting DEMA. • Security – the military can protect itself, and establish the necessary security for both organisations¿ personnel, materiel, and for emergency relief. Since complex emergencies often happen in relation to wars, the § 3 of the Danish Emergency Law (beredskabsloven) should be changed, so that the words \"in peacetime\" are removed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Struwe, Lars Bangert","Larsen, Esben Salling","Breitenbauch, Henrik Ø."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472675"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"til nytte rapport om anvendelse af forsvarets kapaciteter til internationale beredskabsindsatser","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375964000/download.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-472675","ids":["ku-846439a5-44c4-4e09-8969-0419080e8b01"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-89504C968FF2C6B12903609819AA1FA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375964000/download.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://cms.polsci.ku.dk/pdf/pub/Rapport_om_forsvarets_mulige_st_tte_til_beredskabsstyrelsen.pdf/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Centre for Military Studies","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bangert","key":"struwepau","last":"Struwe","locid":"3224baff-52ad-4d6b-85ca-4395566e6997","name":"Struwe, Lars Bangert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Esben Salling","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3f60ffd7-91d2-4215-9dc9-c54f72495a02","name":"Larsen, Esben Salling","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Ø.","key":"breitenbauchpau","last":"Breitenbauch","locid":"981ff35b-9e40-42ed-95b9-ea5b3e5aac30","name":"Breitenbauch, Henrik Ø.","orcid":"0000-0001-6302-3670","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-846439a5-44c4-4e09-8969-0419080e8b01"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Til nytte : rapport om anvendelse af forsvarets kapaciteter til internationale beredskabsindsatser","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472675","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Background: Several tools have been created to assess competence in bronchoscopy. However, educational guidelines still use an arbitrary number of performed procedures to decide when basic competency is acquired. Objectives: The purpose of this study was to define pass/fail scores for two bronchoscopy assessment tools, and investigate how these scores relate to physicians' experience regarding the number of bronchoscopy procedures performed. Methods: We studied two assessment tools and used two standard setting methods to create cut scores: the contrasting-groups method and the extended Angoff method. In the first we compared bronchoscopy performance scores of 14 novices with the scores of 14 experienced consultants to find the score that best discriminated between the two groups. In the second we asked an expert group of 7 experienced bronchoscopists to judge how a borderline trainee would perform on each item of the test. Results: Using the contrasting-groups method we found a standard that would fail all novices and pass all consultants. A clear pass related to prior experience of 75 procedures. The consequences of using the extended Angoff method were also acceptable: all trainees who had performed less than 50 bronchoscopies failed the test and all consultants passed. A clear pass related to 80 procedures. Conclusions: Our proposed pass/fail scores for these two methods seem appropriate in terms of consequences. Prior experience with the performance of 75 and 80 bronchoscopies, respectively, seemed to ensure basic competency. In the future objective assessment tools could become an important aid in the certification of physicians performing bronchoscopies.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Konge, Lars","Clementsen, Paul","Larsen, Klaus Richter","Arendrup, Henrik","Buchwald, Christian","Ringsted, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493409"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level"