t":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik Kjaerulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"tfelthansenpau","last":"Tfelt-Hansen","name":"Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jytte","key":"bannerpau","last":"Banner","locid":"9d2aead6-d3bf-46f7-b967-ef864b0748ec","name":"Banner, Jytte","orcid":"0000-0002-7559-1285","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22882672"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1540-8167.2012.02371.x","issn":["10453873","15408167"],"issn_org":["10453873"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","pages":"1092-8","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867742485"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e6af5bf0-0a17-4a3b-a62e-a4cc80e46d45","ku-8fca984f-5e15-41a3-a662-032186ebb13a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The prevalence of mutations in KCNQ1, KCNH2, and SCN5A in an unselected national cohort of young sudden unexplained death cases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.30-029386","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Improving diagnosis of prosthetic joint infections (PJIs) has become an increasing challenge due to a steadily rising number of patients with prosthetic implants. Based on a systematic literature search we have ascertained the evidence base for improvement of culture diagnosis. We searched Pub Med/MEDLINE using the medical subject heading (MeSH) 'prosthesis-related infections' 1995 through 2010 without further restrictions. An analogous search was conducted for ISI Web of Knowledge. A total of 1409 reports were screened for original results, obtained by methods described in sufficient detail to make replication possible. We gave priority to methods for sample preparation, culture media, culture methods and incubation time. Clinical sensitivity and specificity were calculated where possible. We found evidence to support superiority of cultures obtained from the diluent after sonication of prosthetic implants in comparison with culturing tissue biopsies. Sonication parameters and accessory steps have been studied extensively, and thresholds for significant growth have been defined. Conversely, methods for processing of soft tissue biopsies have been studied to a limited extent. Culture of synovial fluid in blood culture vials has been shown to be more sensitive (90-92%) than intraoperative swab cultures (68-76%) and tissue cultures (77-82%). Formal evaluation of agar media for culturing PJI specimens seemed to be lacking. The polymicrobial nature of PJIs supports the routine use of an assortment of media suitable for recovery of fastidious, slow-growing, anaerobic and sub lethally damaged bacteria. A number of studies supported an incubation period for up to 14 days. Although we identified evidence-based improvements of culture methods, there is a need for more studies especially with regard to tissue biopsies. Culturing remains an important means to identify and characterize pathogenic micro-organisms and supplements the increasing number of culture-independent assays.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Lone Heimann","Lange, Jeppe","Xu, Yijuan","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl"],"cuid":["S02-098.78-000469"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Clinical Microbiology, Aalborg Hospital, Aarhus University Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimizing culture methods for diagnosis of prosthetic joint infections a summary of modifications and improvements reported since 000000001995","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.035303-0","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.78-000469","identifier":[{"id":"84863135996","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22222201","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000301033400001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-08f33b6b-1fbd-442b-a743-e60a300add5c","au-137c1831-4546-41ad-86b1-60fa9b6860d8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-15189600A7192FE7CD1585CEFBF8AD0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jmm.sgmjournals.org/content/61/3/309","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.035303-0","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Clinical Microbiology, Aalborg Hospital, Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2