{"abstract":"Background: Coronary artery calcification (CAC) is an independent and incremental risk marker. This marker has previously not been compared to the HeartScore risk model. Design: A random sample of 1825 citizens (men and women, 50 or 60 years of age) was invited for screening. Methods: Using the HeartScore model, the 10-year risk of fatal cardiovascular events based on gender, age, smoking, systolic blood pressure, and total cholesterol was estimated. A low risk was defined as","author_count":13,"contributors":["Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","Sand, Niels Peter","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Lambrechtsen, Jess","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Munkholm, Henrik","Aziz, Ahmed","Gerke, Oke","Egstrup, Kenneth","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Petersen, Henrik","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","Mickley, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-601870"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discrepancy between coronary artery calcium score and heartscore in middle aged danes the danrisk study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84862870005","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-601870","identifier":[{"id":"21525124","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84862870005","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-642a4bcb-2fec-468d-aa5a-f4ad5845966e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-6792292C481A0BBAD494409C1CE030AF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"nam