name":"Ditzel, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-3927-5135","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"lethlarsenpau","last":"Leth-Larsen","locid":"66fd89b9-b81d-4e74-bf02-9a0ea313ee3e","name":"Leth-Larsen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-1612-4089","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-99e5f24e-91d1-4ea6-a1af-680bc2de8ed0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Heterogeneity within the Cancer Stem Cell Population of the Triple-Negative Breast Cancer Subtype","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-617277","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores the social dimension of innovation and discusses alternative approaches to deal with paradox and conflict across what is typically called knowledge boundaries when innovating together. We propose an understanding of innovation as socially shaped in the ongoing negotiation of different intentions. We explore two cases to develop the theoretical argument of our approach. We argue that the traditional way to approach the challenge of innovation through objective measurement and reason is not taking into account the political themes because the challenge of crossing the previously constructed boundaries goes beyond the scope in which such reason and measurement would be justified by all participants. This implies a new perspective on management away from control of results based on objective measures, towards engaging in complex relations where (new) justified meaning is negotiated from different perspectives in subjective local interaction. We describe this as social shaping of innovation. We contribute to theory by developing an understanding of the role of social practice in the innovation processes. Further, we outline limitations of established approaches, showing how social shaping can complement them. Based on the experience we gathered in the described cases, we contribute to practice with ideas about how to deal with the outlined challenges and opportunities in everyday life.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sproedt, Henrik","Larsen, Henry"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-618213"],"event":{"acronym":"CINet Conference","end":"2012-09-18","place":"Rome, it","start":"2012-09-16","title":"13th International CINet Conference","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Complexity","Innovation management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social shaping of innovation the practice of dealing with paradox and conflict","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-618213","ids":["sdu-9d1719f3-57be-4f62-be68-3c9f622033cc"],"keyword":["Complexity","Innovation Management","Social Shaping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0FB677707C6402D81FE8F6E06CC1E944"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation, SDU Technology Entrepreneurship and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"sproedtpau","last":"Sproedt","locid":"1dffc0cb-d58e-4145-94b2-9a0b950b3070","name":"Sproedt, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henry","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"835e9c6e-81a1-4eec-909b-8d02dabd55f3","name":"Larsen, Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-1776-3947","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789077360256"],"pages":"1003-1015","status":"p","subtitle":"Business Development and Co-creation","title":"Proceedings of the 14th International CINet Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9d1719f3-57be-4f62-be68-3c9f622033cc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Social Shaping of Innovation – the Practice of Dealing with Paradox, and Conflict","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-618213","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To evaluate comorbidity before and after the diagnosis of branch retinal vein occlusion to determine whether it is a consequence of arterial thickening and therefore could serve as a diagnostic marker for other comorbidities and to evaluate the risk factors for the development of such occlusion. DESIGN: Case-control study with prospective follow-up data from Danish national registries. SETTING: Four secondary referral centres covering about 80% of the Danish population (4.4 million). PARTICIPANTS: 1168 patients with photographically verified branch retinal vein occlusion and 116,800 controls alive and aged ≥ 40 when the occlusion was diagnosed in the corresponding case. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: The risk of comorbidity 10 years and 1 year before the diagnosis of branch retinal vein occlusion and the incident comorbidity in a mean period of seven years after the diagnosis, with odds ratios and incidence rate ratios adjusted for age, sex, and year of diagnosis. RESULTS: Risk factors present 10 years and 1 year before the diagnosis of branch retinal vein occlusion included peripheral artery disease (odds ratio 1.83, 95% confidence interval 1.14 to 2.95), diabetes (1.74, 1.40 to 2.17) and arterial hypertension (2.16, 1.86 to 2.51). After the diagnosis, patients had an increased risk of developing arterial hypertension (incidence rate ratio 1.37, 95% confidence interval 1.15 to 1.57), diabetes (1.51, 1.17 to 2.04), congestive heart failure (1.41, 1.12 to 1.68), and cerebrovascular disease (1.49, 1.27 to 1.76). CONCLUSION: Diabetes, hypertension, and peripheral artery disease are associated with an increased risk of developing branch retinal vein occlusion up to a decade later. Branch retinal vein occlusion was associated with an increased risk of subsequently developing hypertension, diabetes, congestive heart failure, and cerebrovascular disease, emphasising the importance of preventive initiatives. These results fit the assumption that branch retinal vein occlusion is a consequence of arterial thickening and that the arteriovenous crossing signs that precede it are hallmarks of arterial disease.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bertelsen, Mette","Linneberg, Allan","Rosenberg, Thomas","Christoffersen, Nynne","Vorum, Henrik","Gade, Else","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811111"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Age Distribution","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Comorbidity","Denmark epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus epidemiology","Epidemiologic Methods","Female","Humans","Hypertension epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Peripheral Arterial Disease epidemiology","Retinal Vein Occlusion epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comorbidity in patients with branch retinal vein occlusion case control study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-811111","identifier":[{"id":"23204001","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84871104315","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3510781","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d2a7699c-3cc5-42e4-a4e9-810adc407a33"],"keyword":["Adult","Age Distribution","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Comorbidity","Denmark/epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus/epidemiology","Epidemiologic Methods","Female","Humans","Hypertension/epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Peripheral Arterial Disease/epidemiology","Retinal Vein Occlusion/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-44CF8BFF0016BDA8C0C1ED03C68FA89B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","locid":"5443e9ff-9db4-4322-9065-636e3183c685","name":"Bertelsen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"rosenbergpau","last":"Rosenberg","name":"Rosenberg, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nynne","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","name":"Christoffersen, Nynne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"vorumpau","last":"Vorum","name":"Vorum, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Else","key":"gadepau","last":"Gade","name":"Gade, Else","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1a555c4a-f5eb-40fe-8f79-6442177ac676","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23204001"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmj.e7885","issn":["09598146","17561833"],"issn_org":["09598138"],"journal":"BMJ","status":"p","title":"BMJ","title_org":"B M J (Clinical Research Edition)","volume":"345"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84871104315"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d2a7699c-3cc5-42e4-a4e9-810adc407a33"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comorbidity in patients with branch retinal vein occlusion : case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811111","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Skeletal muscle mitochondrial content varies extensively between human subjects. Biochemical measures of mitochondrial proteins, enzyme activities and lipids are often used as markers of mitochondrial content and muscle oxidative capacity (OXPHOS). The purpose of this study was to determine how closely associated these commonly used biochemical measures are to muscle mitochondrial content and muscle oxidative capacity (OXPHOS).Sixteen young healthy male subjects were recruited for this study. Subjects completed a graded exercise test to determine maximal oxygen uptake (VO(2peak)) and muscle biopsies were obtained from the vastus lateralis. Mitochondrial content was determined using transmission electron microscopy imaging and OXPHOS was determined as the maximal coupled respiration in permeabilized fibers. Biomarkers of interest were citrate synthase (CS) activity, cardiolipin content, mitochondrial DNA content, complex I-V protein content, and complex I-IV activity. Spearman correlation coefficient tests and Lin's concordance tests were applied to assess the absolute and relative association between the markers and mitochondrial content or OXPHOS.Subjects had a large range in VO(2peak) (range 29.9 -71.6 ml/min/kg) and in mitochondrial content (4-15% of cell volume). Cardiolipin content showed the strongest association to mitochondrial content followed by CS- and complex I activity. mtDNA was not related to mitochondrial content. Complex IV activity showed the strongest association to muscle oxidative capacity followed by complex II activity.We conclude that cardiolipin content, CS and complex I activity are the biomarkers that exhibit the strongest association to mitochondrial content, while complex IV activity is strongly associated with OXPHOS capacity in human skeletal muscle.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Larsen, Steen","Nielsen, Joachim","Neigaard Nielsen, Christina","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Wibrand, Flemming","Stride, Nis","Schroder, Henrik Daa","Boushel, Robert Christopher","Helge, Jørn Wulff","Dela, Flemming","Hey-Mogensen, Martin"],"cuid":["S02-090.20-044254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biomarkers of mitochondrial content in skeletal muscle of healthy young human subjects","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.2012.230185","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.20-044254","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3459047","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84864151903","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22586215","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8c74ae6b-b85d-4096-9f07-2f96b9eb0548","sdu-86de8e8c-2d0f-401f-a885-79acc70aa0aa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-77F77D71810B545A82ACC4488E25FC3E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.2012.230185","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Muscle Physiology and Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Steen","key":"larsensteenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7a869b1b-85f0-4d92-a44f-cbd16750054b","name":"Larsen, Steen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"nielsenjoachimpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"aac42667-e2b1-4512-b026-a36af52546d7","name":"Nielsen, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0003-1730-3094","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christina","key":"neigaardnielsenchristinapau","last":"Neigaard Nielsen","name":"Neigaard Nielsen, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Neigaard","key":"hansenchristinaneigaardpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Christina Neigaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"wibrandflemmingpau","last":"Wibrand","locid":"c386d723-668c-4c4c-9546-540e0f300c13","name":"Wibrand, Flemming","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nis","key":"stridenispau","last":"Stride","locid":"56b6f494-8e4b-4919-b2ea-fd8652ba11d3","name":"Stride, Nis","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nis Ottesen","key":"stridenisottesenpau","last":"Stride","name":"Stride, Nis Ottesen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Daa","key":"schrøderhenrikdaapau","last":"Schroder","locid":"45f34f3c-9832-41b5-813a-585261681c55","name":"Schrøder, Henrik Daa","name_org":"Schroder, Henrik Daa","orcid":"0000-0001-7588-235X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Daa","key":"schroderhenrikdaapau","last":"Schroder","name":"Schro