{"abstract":"Hvis engagementet er lig nul, banker det arbejdspræstationen ned under gulvbrædderne. Derfor er tidens negative stemningsbillede gift for mange virksomheder.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-289858"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sorte skyer over jobmarkedet","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-289858","ids":["cbs-97c69b5c-5e67-44c7-b524-33bfd3022281"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E72F448DF66876018A5E71041E2D32AF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01091182"],"journal":"Jyllands-Posten","pages":"32","publisher":"JP/Politikens Hus AS","publisher_org":"JP/Politikens Hus A/S","status":"p","title":"Jyllands-Posten"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-97c69b5c-5e67-44c7-b524-33bfd3022281"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Sorte skyer over jobmarkedet","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-289858","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The present report constitutes the Protocol Manual for ensuring harmonisation of offshore wind and wave simulation being implemented at MaRINET facilities. Wind and wave climates for five offshore wind sites in the North Sea and the Baltic Sea have been presented in terms of probability distributions for wind speed along with a series of lumped sea states and turbulence intensity values, parameterised with respect to the wind speed. Further, extreme values for wind speed and significant wave height have been provided. Further to the wind distributions and lumped characteristics, the Weibull parameters for the wind distribution and explicit formulas for the turbulence intensity and significant wave height are provided. For the correlation of wave peak period and significant wave height, a standard formula from the IEC‐61400‐3 code have been found to cover the scatter in the data, although one coefficient in this formula must be decided upon by the user. Further, the value of γ, the JONSWAP peak enhancement parameter must be chosen by the user. This can be done either from an explicit formula or by the standard choices of γ=1.0 or γ=3.3. Hereby a full description of a unidirectional wind‐wave climate can be constructed. If needed, this climate can be supplemented by the user with the combined directional distribution of wind and waves, either based on data or in terms of parametric studies. The scaling method proposed is the dynamic‐elastic scaling, which maintains the ratios between hydrodynamic, aerodynamic, stiffness‐induced and gravitational forces. This scaling preserves the Froude number for the water phase and the tip speed ratio for the rotor. The Reynolds numbers for air and water, however, are not conserved. A redesign of the model‐scale blades will therefore be needed. Here the scaled thrust‐curve must be matched. Further, if possible, the torque from the airfoil should be matched. This requirement, however, is difficult to achieve due to the change in lift/drag ratio at low Reynolds number. It is therefore foreseen, that the aerodynamic torque and thus produced power will not be scaled correctly. As a consequence, roll‐forcing induced by the dynamic change in generator moment will not scale correctly. However, the correct scaling of rotor thrust is found to have higher priority and thus justifies the scaling choice. An example of down‐scaling of wind and wave conditions has been supplied. The example also demonstrates how the structure (a floating wind turbine) should be scaled. It is demonstrated that the proposed scaling yields modelscale results for thrust‐ and wave‐ induced motion that can be up‐scaled to prototype scale with a perfect match.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bredmose, Henrik","Larsen, Søren Ejling","Matha, D.","Rettenmeier, A.","Marino, E.","Saettran, L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-336831"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","University of Florence","University of Stuttgart"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collation of offshore wind wave dynamics marine renewables infrastructure network for emerging energy technologies d000000000002 000000000004","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60086212/Collation_of_offshore.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-336831","ids":["dtu-6bfa8f7d-5894-4f39-8bb8-5c7e33758d6f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-148F168E4F8A8DEE139CC82B077AA238"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60086212/Collation_of_offshore.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Fluid Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of stuttgart","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Stuttgart","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of florence","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Florence","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bredmosepau","last":"Bredmose","locid":"a46a2dd1-d040-4240-8dfb-bdb22c646a47","name":"Bredmose, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-0753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Ejling","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6fc30efb-9800-4fe7-ba37-bee5bf5243f3","name":"Larsen, Søren Ejling","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"mathapau","last":"Matha","name":"Matha, D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"rettenmeierpau","last":"Rettenmeier","name":"Rettenmeier, A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"marinopau","last":"Marino","name":"Marino, E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"saettranpau","last":"Saettran","name":"Saettran, L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"50","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["13. Climate Action","14. Life Below Water","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6bfa8f7d-5894-4f39-8bb8-5c7e33758d6f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Collation of offshore wind‐wave dynamics : Marine Renewables Infrastructure Network for Emerging Energy Technologies D2.4","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-336831","year":"2012","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This article describes the basic physics of dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization (dissolution‐DNP), and the impact of the resulting highly nonequilibrium spin states, on the physics of magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) detection. The hardware requirements for clinical translation of this technology are also presented. For studies that allow the use of externally administered agents, hyperpolarization offers a way to overcome normal magnetic resonance sensitivity limitations, at least for a brief T1‐dependent observation window. A 10,000–100,000‐fold signal‐to‐noise advantage provides an avenue for real‐time measurement of perfusion, metabolite transport, exchange, and metabolism. The principles behind these measurements, as well as the choice of agent, and progress toward the application of hyperpolarized 13C metabolic imaging in oncology, cardiology, and neurology are reviewed. J. Magn. Reson. Imaging 2012; 36:1314–1328. © 2012 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hurd, Ralph E.","Yen, Yi‐Fen","Chen, Albert","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340504"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized 000000000013c metabolic imaging using dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jmri.23753","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340504","identifier":[{"id":"23165733","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84869416639","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7862adac-36db-4ade-82b7-9477d1145894"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D8DAB1C5401886725FF060B1AF73F656"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jmri.23753","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"ge healthcare","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GE Healthcare","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph E.","key":"hurdpau","last":"Hurd","name":"Hurd, Ralph E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi‐Fen","key":"yenpau","last":"Yen","name":"Yen, Yi‐Fen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Albert","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Albert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23165733"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jmri.23753","issn":["10531807","15222586"],"issn_org":["10531807"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance Imaging","pages":"1314-1328","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance Imaging","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84869416639"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7862adac-36db-4ade-82b7-9477d1145894"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Hyperpolarized 13C metabolic imaging using dissolution dynamic nuclear polarization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340504","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Real‐time in vivo measurements of metabolites are performed by signal enhancement of [1‐13C]pyruvate using dynamic nuclear polarization, rapid dissolution and intravenous injection, acquisition of free induction decay signals and subsequent quantification of spectra. The commonly injected dose of hyperpolarized pyruvate is larger than typical tracer doses, with measurement before complete dilution of the injected bolus. Pyruvate is in exchange with its downstream metabolites lactate, alanine and bicarbonate. A transient exposure to high pyruvate blood concentrations may cause the saturation of cellular uptake and metabolic conversion. The goal of this study was to examine the effects of a [1‐13C]pyruvate bolus on metabolic conversion in vivo. Spectra were quantified by three different methods: frequency‐domain fitting with LCModel, time‐domain fitting with AMARES and simple linear least‐squares fitting in the time domain. Since the simple linear least‐squares approach showed bleeding artifacts and LCModel produced noisier time signals. AMARES performed best in the quantification of in vivo hyperpolarized pyruvate spectra. We examined pyruvate doses of 0.1–0.4 mmol/kg (body mass) in male Wistar rats by acquiring slice‐selective free induction decay signals in slices dominated by heart, liver and kidney tissue. Dose effects were noted in all cases, except for alanine in the cardiac slice below the dose of 0.2 mmol/kg. Our results indicate unlimited cellular uptake of pyruvate up to this dose and limited enzymatic activity of lactate dehydrogenase. In the cardiac slice above 0.2 mmol/kg and in liver and kidney slices, reflect limited cellular uptake or enzymatic activity, or a combination of both effects. The results indicate that the dose of pyruvate must be recognized as an important determinant for metabolic tissue kinetics, and saturation effects must be taken into account for the quantitative interpretation of the observed results. Copyright © 2011 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Janich, M. A.","Menzel, M. I.","Wiesinger, F.","Weidl, E.","Khegai, O.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Glaser, S. J.","Haase, A.","Schulte, R. F.","Schwaiger, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340694"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Global Research","Technical University of Munich"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of pyruvate dose on in vivo metabolism and quantification of hyperpolarized 000000000013c spectra","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.1726","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340694","identifier":[{"id":"84855867248","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-79039566-e3f4-44cf-8a50-2034aee83e2b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6F2B2E913BA2EE080956C054E1B21DF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.1726","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ge global research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"GE Global Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. A.","key":"janichpau","last":"Janich","name":"Janich, M. A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. I.","key":"menzelpau","last":"Menzel","name":"Menzel, M. I.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"wiesingerpau","last":"Wiesinger","name":"Wiesinger, F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"weidlpau","last":"Weidl","name":"Weidl, E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"O.","key":"khegaipau","last":"Khegai","name":"Khegai, O.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S. J.","key":"glaserpau","last":"Glaser","name":"Glaser, S. J.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"haasepau","last":"Haase","name":"Haase, A.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"R. F.","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, R. F.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"schwaigerpau","last":"Schwaiger","name":"Schwaiger, M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.1726","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"1","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","pages":"142-151","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","title_org":"N M R in Biomedicine","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855867248"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-79039566-e3f4-44cf-8a50-2034aee83e2b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Effects of pyruvate dose on in vivo metabolism and quantification of hyperpolarized 13C spectra","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340694","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Experimental studies in animals, healthy volunteers, and patients with chronic pain suggest exercise to provide analgesia in several types of pain conditions and after various nociceptive stimuli. To our knowledge, there is no data on the effects of exercise on pain and nociceptive function in surgical patients despite early mobilisation being an important factor to enhance recovery. We therefore investigated possible effects of mobilisation on post-operative pain and nociceptive function after total knee arthroplasty (TKA). METHODS: Thirty patients undergoing TKA under standardised anaesthesia and analgesia underwent an exercise (mobilisation) strategy on the first post-operative morning consisting of 25-m walking twice, with a 20-min interval. Pain was assessed at rest and during passive hip and knee flexion before, and 5 and 20 min after walk, as well as during walk. Nociceptive function (pain threshold and tolerance) was assessed with pressure algometry and an electrical stimulus. RESULTS: Pain at rest (supine) and during hip and knee flexion was significantly reduced 5 min (P ","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lunn, T H","Kristensen, B B","Gaarn-Larsen, L","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440709"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"possible effects of mobilisation on acute post operative pain and nociceptive function after total knee arthroplasty","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1399-6576.2012.02744.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-440709","identifier":[{"id":"84867573345","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22881199","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4f32d881-8bf4-41ef-bcd3-875debb93c22"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB1CE1B3C5B7EDE5AF796D8566AF1743"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1399-6576.2012.02744.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"T H","key":"lunnpau","last":"Lunn","name":"Lunn, T H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B B","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, B B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L","key":"gaarnlarsenpau","last":"Gaarn-Larsen","name":"Gaarn-Larsen, L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","name_org":"Kehlet, H","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22881199"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1399-6576.2012.02744.x","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"10","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"1234-1240","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867573345"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4f32d881-8bf4-41ef-bcd3-875debb93c22"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Possible effects of mobilisation on acute post-operative pain and nociceptive function after total knee arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.f