versity","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","institut for klinisk medicin - ortopædkirurgisk afdeling e, thg"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1de22ded-4f5e-48ae-bd1d-c9898b1a5293","ku-13533f97-0315-4c7f-a93d-01889f452029"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patient-reported outcome after fast-track knee arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.73-014772","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Subacute toxicity of 14 nm nanoparticulate silver (Ag-NP) stabilised with polyvinylpyrrolidone and ionic silver in the form of silver acetate (Ag-acetate) was investigated in four-week-old Wistar rats. Animals received orally by gavage the following: vehicle control (10 $, 6 #); Ag-NP at doses: 2.25 (8 $), 4.5 (8 $) or 9 mg/kg bw/day (10 $, 6 #); or Ag-acetate 9 mg silver/kg bw/day (8 $) for 28 days. Clinical, haematolological and biochemical parameters, organ weights, macro- and microscopic pathological changes were investigated. Caecal bacterial phyla and their silver resistance genes were quantified. For the Ag-NP groups, no toxicological effects were recorded. For Ag-acetate, lower body weight gain (day 4–7, 11–14, 14–16, P\\0.05; overall, day 1–28, P\\0.01), increased plasma alkaline phosphatase (P\\0.05), decreased plasma urea (P\\0.05) and lower absolute (P\\0.01) and relative (P\\0.05) thymus weight were recorded. In conclusion, these findings indicate toxicity of 9 mg/kg bw/day ionic silver but not of an equimolar Ag- NP dose. This is in accordance with previously reported data showing that oral Ag-acetate, in comparison with an equimolar dose of Ag-NP, resulted in higher silver plasma and organ concentrations.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hadrup, Niels","Löschner, Katrin","Bergström, Anders","Wilcks, Andrea","Gao, Xueyun","Vogel, Ulla Birgitte","Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz","Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","Lam, Henrik R.","Mortensen, Alicja"],"cuid":["S02-097.38-768317"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subacute oral toxicity investigation of nanoparticulate and ionic silver in rats","src":["dtu","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00204-011-0759-1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.38-768317","identifier":[{"id":"21969074","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84862856783","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-835d8631-e951-4ebf-94cc-1a56543043cf","nfa-f15f5f60-c42f-4bbe-8c9e-bea4003c22e7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-55BCAB5049692FB11F28B9C8A0142764"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00204-011-0759-1","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Toxicology and Risk Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"hadruppau","last":"Hadrup","locid":"4384548f-118a-4c3c-aedf-f0d203046277","name":"Hadrup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-1188-445X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrin","key":"löschnerpau","last":"Löschner","locid":"d7b22217-70e4-4c54-bd53-3f02c2d23a6f","name":"Löschner, Katrin","orcid":"0000-0003-1741-8406","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"loeschnerpau","last":"Loeschner","name":"Loeschner, K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"bergströmpau","last":"Bergström","locid":"0d713b3e-4609-47dc-9997-f8a542798b05","name":"Bergström, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0961-0799","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"wilckspau","last":"Wilcks","locid":"6aacd625-74d9-4ffb-bd02-0aa5adf84f00","name":"Wilcks, Andrea","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xueyun","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Xueyun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Birgitte","key":"vogelpau","last":"Vogel","locid":"b09b3c47-5cc7-474a-af05-a4b378c96531","name":"Vogel, Ulla Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-1524","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Lauritz","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"7f8f5328-37cb-4aa3-a2e1-1b519b8e1c83","name":"Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz","orcid":"0000-0002-1905-8144","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Huusfeldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9528940a-884f-4a63-b068-b739d7551006","name":"Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik R.","key":"lampau","last":"Lam","name":"Lam, Henrik R.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alicja","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"2cbb8a58-bb77-4b14-9b9b-16408c39d2c4","name":"Mortensen, Alicja","orcid":"0000-0001-6992-7750","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21969074"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00204-011-0759-1","issn":["03405761","14320738"],"issn_org":["03405761"],"issue":"4","journal":"Archives of Toxicology","pages":"543-551","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Archives of Toxicology","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84862856783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-835d8631-e951-4ebf-94cc-1a56543043cf","nfa-f15f5f60-c42f-4bbe-8c9e-bea4003c22e7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Subacute oral toxicity investigation of nanoparticulate and ionic silver in rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.38-768317","year":"2012","yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"Mucin-type O-glycosylation is an important post-translational modification that confers a variety of biological properties and functions to proteins. This post-translational modification has a particularly complex and differentially regulated biosynthesis rendering prediction and control of where O-glycans are attached to proteins, and which structures are formed, difficult. Because plants are devoid of GalNAc-type O-glycosylation, we have assessed requirements for establishing human GalNAc O-glycosylation de novo in plants with the aim of developing cell systems with custom-designed O-glycosylation capacity. Transient expression of a Pseudomonas aeruginosa Glc(NAc) C4-epimerase and a human polypeptide GalNAc-transferase in leaves of Nicotiana benthamiana resulted in GalNAc O-glycosylation of co-expressed human O-glycoprotein substrates. A chimeric YFP construct containing a 3.5 tandem repeat sequence of MUC1 was glycosylated with up to three and five GalNAc residues when co-expressed with GalNAc-T2 and a combination of GalNAc-T2 and GalNAc-T4, respectively, as determined by mass spectrometry. O-Glycosylation was furthermore demonstrated on a tandem repeat of MUC16 and interferon α2b. In plants, prolines in certain classes of proteins are hydroxylated and further substituted with plant-specific O-glycosylation; unsubstituted hydroxyprolines were identified in our MUC1 construct. In summary, this study demonstrates that mammalian type O-glycosylation can be established in plants and that plants may serve as a host cell for production of recombinant O-glycoproteins with custom-designed O-glycosylation. The observed hydroxyproline modifications, however, call for additional future engineering efforts.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Yang, Zhang","Drew, Damian P","Jørgensen, Bodil","Mandel, Ulla","Bach, Søren S","Ulvskov, Peter","Levery, Steven B","Bennett, Eric P","Clausen, Henrik","Petersen, Bent L"],"cuid":["S02-098.88-024382"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engineering mammalian mucin type em o em glycosylation in plants","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M111.312918","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.88-024382","identifier":[{"id":"22334671","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3320939","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84859494355","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a013c15a-ba57-4db8-8fc4-50f82c75c9ba","ku-de8f2bf8-a484-4a81-8710-46369b2e9939"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6DF0B3740AB8206F4FAA06A547A8FA8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M111.312918","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhang","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"1c251a6b-6ca6-4c1d-bd5a-aa2bcbc6a482","name":"Yang, Zhang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Damian P","key":"drewpau","last":"Drew","locid":"3bfb890c-9fb1-4917-ab4c-217cd60f95d3","name":"Drew, Damian Paul","name_org":"Drew, Damian P","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Bodil","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ab0f85f4-70e2-443b-bdde-331840596eea","name":"Jørgensen, Bodil","orcid":"0000-0002-0453-1277","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Ulla","key":"mandelpau","last":"Mandel","locid":"5b548729-0f0e-4986-910e-ae324c866105","name":"Mandel, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0001-7012-9836","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Søren S","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","locid":"521af136-3e74-42fc-86e9-d7b66bc28c5e","name":"Bach, Søren Spanner","name_org":"Bach, Søren S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Peter","key":"ulvskovpau","last":"Ulvskov","locid":"de14452b-f78b-4de5-b473-5bdd5abd6ac9","name":"Ulvskov, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-3776-818X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Steven B","key":"leverypau","last":"Levery","locid":"d4195b2b-1f0d-4a00-83fd-e0c67c5c94c4","name":"Levery, Steven B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Eric P","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","locid":"985ebfda-1253-424b-8e7d-d5918fa165bf","name":"Bennett, Eric P","orcid":"0000-0002-4976-0647","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Henrik","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"a7882c09-1275-4857-8b5b-7e3efc1d088d","name":"Clausen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0915-5055","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Bent L","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0d3fa717-88a9-444e-8096-3163ca10ec75","name":"Petersen, Bent Larsen","name_org":"Petersen, Bent L","orcid":"0000-0002-2004-9077","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22334671"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m111.312918","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"11911-11923","publisher":"American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"287"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84859494355"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a013c15a-ba57-4db8-8fc4-50f82c75c9ba","ku-de8f2bf8-a484-4a81-8710-46369b2e9939"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Engineering Mammalian Mucin-Type <em>O</em>-Glycosylation in Plants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.88-024382","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Nuclear spin hyperpolarization makes a significant advance toward overcoming the sensitivity limitations of in vivo magnetic resonance imaging, particularly in the case of low-gamma nuclei. The sensitivity may be improved further by storing the hyperpolarization in slowly relaxing singlet populations of spin- 1/2 pairs. Here, we report hyperpolarized 13C spin order transferred into and retrieved from singlet spin order using a small animal magnetic resonance imaging scanner. For spins in sites with very similar chemical shifts, singlet spin order is sustained in high magnetic field without requiring strong radiofrequency irradiation. The demonstration of robust singlet-to-magnetization conversion, and vice versa, on a small animal scanner, is promising for future in vivo and clinical deployments.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Laustsen, Christoffer","Pileio, Giuseppe","Tayler, Michael C. D.","Brown, Lynda J.","Brown, Richard C. D.","Levitt, Malcolm H.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024546"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Southampton"],"keyword":["DNP","Hyperpolarization"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized singlet nmr on a small animal imaging system","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.24430","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024546","identifier":[{"id":"22851334","type":"pmid"},{