","University of Southern Denmark","øjenafdelingen (oftalmologi), nbg"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f7e21621-c2a7-4a92-9d4f-3d028b37cc33","ku-3effb530-02d2-42b0-814d-0ff2973d39fa","sdu-3db85fa7-a678-418b-8401-23f6488ec6c5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comorbidity in patients with branch retinal vein occlusion : case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-086.03-666585","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION:: Hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer (HNPCC) is an autosomal dominant condition accounting for 2% to 4% of all colorectal cancer cases worldwide. Families with germ line mutations in 1 of 6 mismatch repair genes are known as Lynch syndrome families. The largest number of mutations has been detected in the mismatch repair genes MLH1 and MSH2, but several mutations in MSH6 have also been demonstrated. AIM:: Whether HNPCC families are screened for mutations in mismatch repair genes often relies on their immunohistochemical profile. The aim of the present study was to evaluate this approach in Lynch families carrying mutations in MSH6. MATERIALS AND METHODS:: Results of the screening of the MSH6 gene in HNPCC families were compared with those obtained on immunohistochemical protein analysis. RESULTS:: In 56 (7%) of 815 families, at least 1 MSH6 mutation, 23 definitively pathogenic mutations and 38 missense mutations or unclassified variants, and several polymorphisms in the MSH6 gene were detected. In families carrying a pathogenic MSH6 mutation, 69.6% of 23 colon adenocarcinomas showed absence of pMSH6 in tumor tissue by immunohistochemical analysis. In 34.5%, all proteins could be detected, whereas in 34.5% pMSH6 was present and pMLH1/pPMS2 was absent. CONCLUSIONS:: If genetic screening of HNPCC families depended on immunohistochemical results, a substantial number of families harboring a pathogenic mutation in MSH6 and the vast majority of families harboring an MSH6 unclassified variant would not be detected.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Okkels, Henrik","Larsen, K.L.","Thorlacius-Ussing, O.","Vyberg, Mogens","Lindebjerg, Jan","Sunde, Lone","Bernstein, Inge Thomsen","Klarskov, Louise Laurberg","Holck, Susanne","Krarup, H.B."],"cuid":["S03-091.34-015913"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"msh000000000006 mutations are frequent in hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer families with normal pmsh000000000006 expression as detected by immunohistochemistry","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/PAI.0b013e318249739b","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-091.34-015913","identifier":[{"id":"84866604260","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22495361","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2d48f7e7-7e58-4193-9532-054ce37d3089","ku-d39726b4-9806-4396-9842-762f5f95ba11","sdu-6b48e893-bbdf-488e-81c4-d2b9a9b410d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-00BCAEB39547880CBD68BB94E33F5C52"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/PAI.0b013e318249739b","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - FBE Klinisk Biokemisk Syd, Aalborg Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"d