{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Torben J.","Verelst, David Robert","Bredmose, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-307432"],"event":{"end":"2012-05-16","place":"Boulder, us","start":"2012-05-15","title":"2012 Experts Meeting on Computer Code Validation for Offshore Wind System Modeling","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experiences with the poseidon measurement campaign and more","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/8167948/Experiences_with_the_Poseidon.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-307432","ids":["dtu-09732c4f-755f-436c-b953-503363e8e349"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2DA8E1091C1237674B44069566708ACC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/8167948/Experiences_with_the_Poseidon.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Aeroelastic Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben J.","key":"larsenppu","last":"Larsen","locid":"965dbaf9-67c6-4f4d-b512-2df4845d740d","name":"Larsen, Torben J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6741-5057","rank":1,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David Robert","key":"verelstppu","last":"Verelst","locid":"67d280f9-3b48-4301-a6d4-c403faf66ea7","name":"Verelst, David Robert","orcid":"0000-0002-3687-0636","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bredmoseppu","last":"Bredmose","locid":"a46a2dd1-d040-4240-8dfb-bdb22c646a47","name":"Bredmose, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6961-0753","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-09732c4f-755f-436c-b953-503363e8e349"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Experiences with the Poseidon measurement campaign and more","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-307432","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Bridge hanger vibrations have been reported under icy conditions. In this paper, the results from a series of static and dynamic wind tunnel tests on a circular cylinder representing a bridge hanger with simulated thin ice accretions are presented. The experiments focus on ice accretions produced for wind perpendicular to the cylinder at velocities below 30 m/s and for temperatures between -5C and -1C. Aerodynamic drag, lift and moment coefficients are obtained from the static tests, whilst mean and fluctuating responses are obtained from the dynamic tests. The influence of varying surface roughness is also examined. The static force coefficients are used to predict parameter regions where aerodynamic instability of the iced bridge hanger might be expected to occur, through use of an adapted theoretical 3- DOF quasi-steady galloping instability model, which accounts for sectional axial rotation. A comparison between the 3-DOF model and the instabilities found through two degree-of-freedom (2-DOF) dynamic tests is presented. It is shown that, although there is good agreement between the instabilities found through use of the quasi-steady theory and the dynamic tests, discrepancies exist-indicating the possible inability of quasi-steady theory to fully predict these vibrational instabilities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gjelstrup, Henrik","Georgakis, Christos T.","Larsen, A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327489"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aerodynamic instability","Bridge hangers","Circular cylinder","Ice accretion","Low temperatures","Wind tunnel tests"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an evaluation of iced bridge hanger vibrations through wind tunnel testing and quasi steady theory","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/10647637/was1505003.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327489","identifier":[{"id":"84865213230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4d00ab7c-d577-4209-a863-ec6bf8b399a9"],"keyword":["Aerodynamic instability","Bridge hangers","Circular cylinder","Ice accretion","Low temperatures","Quasi-steady aerodynamics","Wind tunnel tests"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C2EE539D676084C12771F7752FA34DA7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/10647637/was1505003.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"gjelstruppau","last":"Gjelstrup","locid":"94df0727-f84f-4779-8061-af9b3cad729e","name":"Gjelstrup, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christos T.","key":"georgakispau","last":"Georgakis","locid":"4141776d-8868-43c6-9ddf-c979925fcc19","name":"Georgakis, Christos T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.12989/was.2012.15.5.385","issn":["12266116","15986225"],"issn_org":["12266116"],"issue":"5","journal":"Wind & Structures","pages":"385-407","publisher":"Techno-Press","status":"p","title":"Wind & Structures","title_org":"Wind and Structures, An International Journal","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865213230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4d00ab7c-d577-4209-a863-ec6bf8b399a9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"An evaluation of iced bridge hanger vibrations through wind tunnel testing and quasi-steady theory","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327489","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The metabolically inactive hyperpolarized agents HP001 (bis-1,1-(hydroxymethyl)-[1-13C]cyclopropane-d8) and urea enable a new type of perfusion magnetic resonance imaging based on a direct signal source that is background-free. The addition of perfusion information to metabolic information obtained by spectroscopic imaging of hyperpolarized [1-13C]pyruvate would be of great value in exploring the relationship between perfusion and metabolism in cancer. In preclinical normal murine and cancer model studies, we performed both dynamic multislice imaging of the specialized hyperpolarized perfusion compound HP001 (T1=95 s ex vivo, 32 s in vivo at 3 T) using a pulse sequence with balanced steady-state free precession and ramped flip angle over time for efficient utilization of the hyperpolarized magnetization and three-dimensional echo-planar spectroscopic imaging of urea copolarized with [1-13C]pyruvate, with compressed sensing for resolution enhancement. For the dynamic data, peak signal maps and blood flow maps derived from perfusion modeling were generated. The spatial heterogeneity of perfusion was increased 2.9-fold in tumor tissues (P=.05), and slower washout was observed in the dynamic data. The results of separate dynamic HP001 imaging and copolarized pyruvate/urea imaging were compared. A strong and significant correlation (R=0.73, P=.02) detected between the urea and HP001 data confirmed the value of copolarizing urea with pyruvate for simultaneous assessment of perfusion and metabolism.","author_count":8,"contributors":["von Morze, Cornelius","Larson, Peder E.Z.","Hu, Simon","Yoshihara, Hikari A.I.","Bok, Robert A.","Goga, Andrei","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","Vigneron, Daniel B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352520"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at San Diego"],"keyword":["C13","HP001","Hyperpolarized","Perfusion","Pyruvate","Urea"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating tumor perfusion and metabolism using multiple hyperpolarized 000000000013c compounds hp000000000001 pyruvate and urea","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mri.2011.09.026","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352520","identifier":[{"id":"84857114595","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3393100","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"22169407","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-a0ae2f3b-9583-4e35-8e94-0aeafeb0b980"],"keyword":["C13","HP001","Hyperpolarized","Perfusion","Pyruvate","Urea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50686355AC58F08464992CFF16599ACD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mri.2011.09.026","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california at san diego","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at San Diego","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cornelius","key":"vonmorzepau","last":"von Morze","name":"von Morze, Cornelius","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peder E.Z.","key":"larsonpau","last":"Larson","name":"Larson, Peder E.Z.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Simon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hikari A.I.","key":"yoshiharapau","last":"Yoshihara","name":"Yoshihara, Hikari A.I.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert A.","key":"bokpau","last":"Bok","name":"Bok, Robert A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrei","key":"gogapau","last":"Goga","name":"Goga, Andrei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel B.","key":"vigneronpau","last":"Vigneron","name":"Vigneron, Daniel B.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22169407"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mri.2011.09.026","issn":["0730725X","18735894"],"issn_org":["0730725X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Magnetic Resonance Imaging","pages":"305-311","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Magnetic Resonance Imaging","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857114595"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a0ae2f3b-9583-4e35-8e94-0aeafeb0b980"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Investigating tumor perfusion and metabolism using multiple hyperpolarized 13C compounds: HP001, pyruvate and urea","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352520","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"ObjectivesIdentification of antimicrobial resistance genes is important for understanding the underlying mechanisms and the epidemiology of antimicrobial resistance. As the costs of whole-genome sequencing (WGS) continue to decline, it becomes increasingly available in routine diagnostic laboratories and is anticipated to substitute traditional methods for resistance gene identification. Thus, the current challenge is to extract the relevant information from the large amount of generated data.MethodsWe developed a web-based method, ResFinder that uses BLAST for identification of acquired antimicrobial resistance genes in whole-genome data. As input, the method can use both pre-assembled, complete or partial genomes, and short sequence reads from four different sequencing platforms. The method was evaluated on 1862 GenBank files containing 1411 different resistance genes, as well as on 23 de-novo-sequenced isolates.ResultsWhen testing the 1862 GenBank files, the method identified the resistance genes with an ID = 100% (100% identity) to the genes in ResFinder. Agreement between in silico predictions and phenotypic testing was found when the method was further tested on 23 isolates of five different bacterial species, with available phenotypes. Furthermore, ResFinder was evaluated on WGS chromosomes and plasmids of 30 isolates. Seven of these isolates were annotated to have antimicrobial resistance, and in all cases, annotations were compatible with the ResFinder results.ConclusionsA web server providing a convenient way of identifying acquired antimicrobial resistance genes in completely sequenced isolates was created. ResFinder can be accessed at www.genomicepidemiology.org. ResFinder will continuously be updated as new resistance genes are identified.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zankari, Ea","Hasman, Henrik","Cosentino, Salvatore","Vestergaard, Martin","Rasmussen, Simon","Lund, Ole","Aarestrup, Frank Møller","Larsen, Mette Voldby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-366794"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antibiotic resistance","Genotype"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of acquired antimicrobial resistance genes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jac/dks261","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-366794","identifier":[{"id":"22782487","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3468078","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84867587461","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d0565c5c-fb03-4d78-b53d-0af4a2316eb9"],"keyword":["ResFinder","antibiotic resistance","genotype","resistance gene identification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7305B5333B4A9307A041F2DE4FE6C85F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jac/dks261","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Epidemiology and Microbial Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ea","key":"zankaripau","last":"Zankari","locid":"11bde48b-fac1-4faa-a538-50d6ef3144ca","name":"Zankari, Ea","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","fir