l University of Denmark"],"title":"Identification of acquired antimicrobial resistance genes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-366794","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The implementation of the EU REACH regulation will most probably promote substitution within sectors handling a lot of different chemicals such as the printing industry. With the aim of being at the cutting edge of this development, the Danish printing industry started up a substitution project in 2006. A major part of the work has been mapping the presence of chemicals, which are the potential candidates for substitution (e.g., PBT, CMR, vPvB, EDS). The mapping comprises a combination of a literature study and an investigation of the actual (2007) presence of candidate substances at 15 Danish printing houses including the examination of almost 900 MSDSs (i.e., products). Furthermore, a focused search in the Danish Product Register has been included. More than 200 of the mapped substances are candidates for substitution according to Danish legislation (List of Undesirable Substances) and about 60 of these substances fulfill one or more of the criteria (e.g., CMR, EDS) for the REACH Annex XIV candidate list (Authorisation List). This case study presents the results of the mapping of chemical substitution candidates some of which may be relevant regarding accumulation of additives/impurities in globally recycled paper.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Fred"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367291"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Printing industry","REACH"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"case study on printed matter in denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.springerlink.com/content/4t17237356k42856/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367291","identifier":[{"id":"84928092219","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d1e8bd6a-13ec-4c23-a539-36e63e64eabd"],"keyword":["Chemical substitution candidates","Printing industry","REACH","Recycled paper","Sustances of very high concern (SVHC)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FE45266C5A1DAE5FB5BEED682CE45762"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.springerlink.com/content/4t17237356k42856/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"18","pages":"167-181","publisher":"Springer","series":"The Handbook of Environmental Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Global Risk-Based Management of Chemical Additives Volume 1: Production, Usage and Environmental Occurrence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d1e8bd6a-13ec-4c23-a539-36e63e64eabd"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Case Study on Printed Matter in Denmark","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367291","year":"2012","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: Intestinal absorption via membrane transporters may determine the pharmacokinetics of drug compounds. The hypothesis is that oral absorption of gaboxadol (4, 5, 6, 7-tetrahydroisoxazolo [5,4-c] pyridine-3-ol) in rats occurs via the proton-coupled amino acid transporter, rPAT1 (encoded by the gene rSlc36a1). The aim is consequently to elucidate the in vivo role of rPAT1 in the absorption of gaboxadol from various intestinal segments. EXPERIMENTAL APPROACH: The absorption of gaboxadol was investigated following administration in four different intestinal segments. The intestinal expression of rSlc36a1 mRNA was measured by quantitative real-time PCR (q-RT-PCR). Furthermore, the hPAT1-/rPAT1-mediated transport of gaboxadol or L-proline was studied in hPAT1-expressing X. laevis oocytes, Caco-2 cell monolayers and excised segments of the rat intestine. KEY RESULTS: The absorption fraction of gaboxadol was high (81.3-91.3%) following administration in the stomach, duodenum and jejunum, but low (4.2%) after administration in the colon. The pharmacokinetics of gaboxadol was modified by the co-administration of L-tryptophan (a hPAT1 inhibitor) and L-proline (a hPAT1 substrate). The in vitro carrier-mediated uptake rate of L-proline in the excised intestinal segments was highest in the mid jejunum and low in the colon. The in vitro uptake and the in vivo absorption correlated with the expression of rSlc36a1 mRNA along the rat intestine. CONCLUSIONS AND IMPLICATIONS: The results suggest that PAT1 mediates the intestinal absorption of gaboxadol and therefore determines the oral bioavailability. This has implications for the in vivo role of PAT1 and for formulation design of its substrates. © 2012 The Authors. British Journal of Pharmacology © 2012 The British Pharmacological Society.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Broberg, Mie Larsen","Holm, Rasmus Koldborg","Tønsberg, Henrik","Frølund, Sidsel Balsgaard","Ewon, K. B.","Nielsen, A. L.","Brodin, Birger","Jensen, Anne","Kall, M. A.","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","Christensen, K. V."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-448655"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"function and expression of the proton coupled amino acid transporter slc000000000036a000000000001 along the rat gastrointestinal tract implications for intestinal absorption of gaboxadol","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1476-5381.2012.02030.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-448655","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3449268","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84865996494","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22577815","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5c3dffe8-b44f-41cb-8378-e4d7649cc3b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD9B954675B1EACA79E60860C0000B53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1476-5381.2012.02030.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","count