{"abstract":"Patients with hypertension are primarily treated in general practice. However, major studies of patients with hypertension are rarely based on populations from primary care. Knowledge of blood pressure (BP) control rates in patients with diabetes and/or cardiovascular diseases (CVDs), who have additional comorbidities, is lacking. We aimed to investigate the association of comorbidities with BP control using a large cohort of hypertensive patients from primary care practices.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Paulsen, Maja Skov","Andersen, Morten","Thomsen, Janus Laust","Schroll, Henrik","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Lykkegaard, Jesper","Jacobsen, Ib Abildgaard","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Christensen, Bo","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-591550"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multimorbidity and blood pressure control in 000000000037 000000000651 hypertensive patients from danish general practice","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.112.004531","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-591550","identifier":[{"id":"23525411","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3603256","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84884178199","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3fe845ac-2a21-41eb-9983-3a40ebeef31e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-F4DF86C69472F550157CCB1FCFE1CADC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.112.004531","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU Un