{"abstract":"We compared the neurotoxic effects of 14nm silver nanoparticles (AgNPs) and ionic silver, in the form of silver acetate (AgAc), in vivo and in vitro. In female rats, we found that AgNPs (4.5 and 9mg AgNP/kg bw/day) and ionic silver (9mg Ag/kg bw/day) increased the dopamine concentration in the brain following 28 days of oral administration. The concentration of 5-hydroxytryptamine (5-HT) in the brain was increased only by AgNP at a dose of 9mg Ag/kg bw/day. Only AgAc (9mg Ag/kg bw/day) was found to increase noradrenaline concentration in the brain. In contrast to the results obtained from a 28-day exposure, the dopamine concentration in the brain was decreased by AgNPs (2.25 and 4.5mg/kg bw/day) following a 14-day exposure. These data suggest that there are differential effects of silver on dopamine depending on the length of exposure. In vitro, AgNPs, AgAc and a 12kDa filtered sub-nano AgNP fraction were used to investigate cell death mechanisms in neuronal-like PC12 cells. AgNPs and the 12kDa filtered fraction decreased cell viability to a similar extent, whereas AgAc was relatively more potent. AgNPs did not induce necrosis. However, apoptosis was found to be equally increased in cells exposed to AgNPs and the 12kDa filtered fraction, with AgAc showing a greater potency. Both the mitochondrial and the death receptor pathways were found to be involved in AgNP- and AgAc-induced apoptosis. In conclusion, 14nm AgNPs and AgAc affected brain neurotransmitter concentrations. AgNP affected 5-HT, AgAc affected noradrenaline, whereas both silver formulations affected dopamine. Furthermore, apoptosis was observed in neuronal-like cells exposed to AgNPs, a 12kDa filtered fraction of AgNP, and AgAc. These findings suggest that ionic silver and a 14nm AgNP preparation have similar neurotoxic effects; a possible explanation for this could be the release and action of ionic silver from the surface of AgNPs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hadrup, Niels","Löschner, Katrin","Mortensen, Alicja","Sharma, Anoop Kumar","Qvortrup, Klaus","Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","Lam, Henrik Rye"],"cuid":["S02-098.91-035766"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["5 Hydroxytryptamine","Dopamine","Nanoparticle","Neurotoxicology","Noradrenaline","Silver"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the similar neurotoxic effects of nanoparticulate and ionic silver in vivo and in vitro","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuro.2012.04.008","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.91-035766","identifier":[{"id":"84861185887","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22531227","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-8a100675-aea1-4cac-8385-6ef7aa4da53f","ku-e18cdd05-3a1d-41fe-91e2-6eb00f93c999"],"keyword":["5-Hydroxytryptamine","Dopamine","Nanoparticle","Neurotoxicology","Noradrenaline","Silver"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6B1A65A1A5AEB50B26210629F5C57DAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuro.2012.04.008","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Toxicology and Risk Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Division of Toxicology and Risk Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Core Facility for Integrated Microscopy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"hadruppau","last":"Hadrup","locid":"4384548f-118a-4c3c-aedf-f0d203046277","name":"Hadrup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-1188-445X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrin","key":"loeschnerpau","last":"Loeschner","locid":"d7b22217-70e4-4c54-bd53-3f02c2d23a6f","name":"Löschner, Katrin","name_org":"Loeschner, Katrin","orcid":"0000-0003-1741-8406","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alicja","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"2cbb8a58-bb77-4b14-9b9b-16408c39d2c4","name":"Mortensen, Alicja","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anoop Kumar","key":"sharmapau","last":"Sharma","locid":"de2d4701-4a22-49b3-a2b2-3481eb2368e2","name":"Sharma, Anoop Kumar","orcid":"0000-0003-2491-4117","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Klaus","key":"qvortruppau","last":"Qvortrup","locid":"e7d5e238-9367-4780-9b26-e468bcdff739","name":"Qvortrup, Klaus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Huusfeldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9528940a-884f-4a63-b068-b739d7551006","name":"Larsen, Erik Huusfeldt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Rye","key":"lampau","last":"Lam","locid":"25a47516-ea9f-4315-88c7-7567267e8f7d","name":"Lam, Henrik Rye","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22531227"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.neuro.2012.04.008","issn":["0161813X","18729711"],"issn_org":["0161813X"],"issue":"3","journal":"NeuroToxicology","pages":"416-423","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"NeuroToxicology","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861185887"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8a100675-aea1-4cac-8385-6ef7aa4da53f","ku-e18cdd05-3a1d-41fe-91e2-6eb00f93c999"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The similar neurotoxic effects of nanoparticulate and ionic silver in vivo and in vitro","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.91-035766","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"  Familial hypercholesterolemia (FH) is a genetic disorder that may lead to premature coronary heart disease (CHD) and sudden cardiac death (SCD). Mutations in the LDLR or APOB genes cause FH. We have screened the LDLR and the ligand-binding region of APOB genes in 52 cases of SCD. Deceased patients were younger than 40 years of age and were suspected of having FH. The LDLR and APOB genes were examined via PCR, high-resolution melting, and DNA sequencing. Therein, it was observed that 7.7% of the screened patients exhibited a rare sequence variant in the LDLR gene, with 5.7% suspected of being pathogenic mutations. Lipid profiles and genetic testing for FH could be considered when autopsy reveals significant atherosclerosis of the coronary arteries in young adults. First-degree family members are advised to seek medical advice and testing to determine their own risks of atherosclerosis to prevent premature CHD and SCD.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Maiken Kudahl","Nissen, Peter H","Kristensen, Ingrid Bayer","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Banner, Jytte"],"cuid":["S02-099.32-026353"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Apolipoproteins B","Coronary Vessels","Coronary artery disease","Death Sudden Cardiac","Denmark","Exons","Female","Forensic genetics","Forensic pathology","Genetic Testing","Humans","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Hypertension","Introns","Male","Mutation","Myocardial Infarction","Myocardium","Overweight","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Receptors LDL","Risk Factors","Sequence Analysis DNA","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sudden cardiac death in young adults environmental risk factors and genetic aspects of premature atherosclerosis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1556-4029.2011.02028.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.32-026353","identifier":[{"id":"84860170141","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22220933","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bc42ed8e-f238-4465-ab61-28b271146e2d","ku-4be8b06d-3246-4cc1-a4f0-0daf968f7964"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Apolipoproteins B","Coronary Artery Disease","Coronary Vessels","Death, Sudden, Cardiac","Denmark","Exons","Female","Forensic Genetics","Forensic Pathology","Genetic Testing","Humans","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Hypertension","Introns","Male","Mutation","Myocardial Infarction","Myocardium","Overweight","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Receptors, LDL","Risk Factors","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-61502D57231B3D54F8BECDB766E1B3E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1556-4029.2011.02028.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine, Section of Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken K","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5dec5e73-3ad6-468f-8ee7-4fa887c20851","name":"Larsen, Maiken Kudahl","name_org":"Larsen, Maiken K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter H","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"ed8b934a-4322-42da-a44a-574b1eb4ddcd","name":"Nissen, Peter H","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-1306","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid B","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"c9bbcc94-82fe-47a6-b381-a02c3fa6d4ef","name":"Kristensen, Ingrid Bayer","name_org":"Kristensen, Ingrid B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik K","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jytte","key":"bannerpau","last":"Banner","locid":"9d2aead6-d3bf-46f7-b967-ef864b0748ec","name":"Banner, Jytte","orcid":"0000-0002-7559-1285","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22220933"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1556-4029.2011.02028.x","issn":["00221198","15564029"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Forensic Sciences","pages":"658-62","status":"p","title":"Journal of Forensic Sciences","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860170141"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bc42ed8e-f238-4465-ab61-28b271146e2d","ku-4be8b06d-3246-4cc1-a4f0-0daf968f7964"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sudden Cardiac Death in Young Adults: Environmental Risk Factors and Genetic Aspects of Premature Atherosclerosis*(,) †","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.32-026353","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Glycosylation is the most abundant and complex posttranslational modification to be considered for recombinant production of therapeutic proteins. Mucin-type (N-acetylgalactosamine [GalNAc]-type) O-glycosylation is found in eumetazoan cells but absent in plants and yeast, making these cell types an obvious choice for de novo engineering of this O-glycosylation pathway. We previously showed that transient implementation of O-glycosylation capacity in plants requires introduction of the synthesis of the donor substrate UDP-GalNAc and one or more polypeptide GalNAc-transferases for incorporating GalNAc residues into proteins. Here, we have stably engineered O-glycosylation capacity in two plant cell systems, soil-grown Arabidopsis (Arabidopsis thaliana) and tobacco (Nicotiana tabacum) Bright Yellow-2 suspension culture cells. Efficient GalNAc O-glycosylation of two stably coexpressed substrate O-glycoproteins was obtained, but a high degree of proline hydroxylation and hydroxyproline-linked arabinosides, on a mucin (MUC1)-derived substrate, was also observed. Addition of the prolyl 4-hydroxylase inhibitor 2,2-dipyridyl, however, effectively suppressed proline hydroxylation and arabinosylation of MUC1 in Bright Yellow-2 cells. In summary, stably engineered mammalian type O-glycosylation was established in transgenic plants, demonstrating that plants may serve as host cells for the production of recombinant O-glycoproteins. However, the present stable implementation further strengthens the notion that elimination of endogenous posttranslational modifications may be needed for the production of protein therapeutics.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Yang, Zhang","Bennett, Eric Paul","Jørgensen, Bodil","Drew, Damian Paul","Arigi, Emma Adhiambo","Mandel, Ulla","Ulvskov, Peter","Levery, Steven Bruce","Clausen, Henrik","Petersen, Bent L"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-025713"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Acetylgalactosamine","Arabidopsis","Bacterial Proteins","Cell Culture Techniques","Culture Media","Genetic engineering","Glycosylation","Humans","Hydroxylation","Luminescent Proteins","Mucin 1","Plant Cells","Plant Proteins","Plants Genetically Modified","Proline","Protein Stability","Proteolysis","Recombinant Proteins","Tobacco"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Molekylær Genetik og Bioteknologi"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward stable genetic engineering of human o glycosylation in plants","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/52608230/450.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-025713","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3440218","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84865858922","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22791304","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b31f1d89-341d-4eaa-a5ed-299bea102598","ku-d13531a9-ac98-4bd8-b34e-a49d063a3c8b"],"keyword":["Acetylgalactosamine","Arabidopsis","Bacterial Proteins","Cell Culture Techniques","Culture Media","Genetic Engineering","Glycosylation","Humans","Hydroxylation","Luminescent Proteins","Mucin-1","Plant Cells","Plant Proteins","Plants, Genetically Modified","Proline","Protein Stability","Proteolysis","Recombinant Proteins","Tobacco"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E3FEA569C624EBD7F2484BEFD22B46AA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/52608230/450.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.112.198200","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Molekylær Genetik og Bioteknologi"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 03 - Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhang","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"1c251a6b-6ca6-4c1d-bd5a-aa2bcbc6a482","name":"Yang, Zhang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Eric Paul","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","locid":"985ebfda-1253-424b-8e7d-d5918fa165bf","name":"Bennett, Eric P","name_org":"Bennett, Eric Paul","orcid":"0000-0002-4976-0647","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Bodil","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ab0f85f4-70e2-443b-bdde-331840596eea","name":"Jørgensen, Bodil","orcid":"0000-0002-0453-1277","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Damian Paul","key":"drewpau","last":"Drew","locid":"3bfb890c-9fb1-4917-ab4c-217cd60f95d3","name":"Drew, Damian Paul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Emma Adhiambo","key":"arigipau","last":"Arigi","locid":"b50bd999-9fc8-4feb-91b2-0d928224a15c","name":"Arigi, Emma Adhiambo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ulla","key":"mandelpau","last":"Mandel","locid":"5b548729-0f0e-4986-910e-ae324c866105","name":"Mandel, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0001-7012-9836","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Peter","key":"ulvskovpau","last":"Ulvskov","locid":"de14452b-f78b-4de5-b473-5bdd5abd6ac9","name":"Ulvskov, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-3776-818X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Steven B","key":"leverypau","last":"Levery","locid":"d4195b2b-1f0d-4a00-83fd-e0c67c5c94c4","name":"Levery, Steven B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Henrik","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"a7882c09-1275-4857-8b5b-7e3efc1d088d","name":"Clausen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0915-5055","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Bent L","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0d3fa717-88a9-444e-8096-3163ca10ec75","name":"Petersen, Bent Larsen","name_org":"Petersen, Bent L","orcid":"0000-0002-2004-9077","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22791304"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1104/pp.112.198200","issn":["00320889","15322548"],"issn_org":["00320889"],"issue":"1","journal":"Plant Physiology","pages":"450-463","publisher":"American Society of Plant Biologists","status":"p","title":"Plant Physiology","volume":"160"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865858922"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b31f1d89-341d-4eaa-a5ed-299bea102598","ku-d13531a9-ac98-4bd8-b34e-a49d063a3c8b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Toward stable genetic engineering of human O-glycosylation in plants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-025713","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: BACKGROUND: Reporting of symptoms which may signal cancer is the first step in the diagnostic pathway of cancer diseases. Cancer alarm symptoms are common in the general population. Public awareness and knowledge of cancer symptoms are sparse, however, and many people do not seek medical help when having possible cancer symptoms. As social inequality is associated with cancer knowledge, cancer awareness, and information-seeking, our hypothesis is that social inequality may also exist in the general population with respect to reporting of cancer alarm symptoms. The aim of this study was to investigate possible associations between socioeconomic and demographic determinants and reporting of common cancer alarm symptoms. METHODS: A cross-sectional questionnaire survey was performed based on a stratified sample of the Danish general population. A total of 13 777 randomly selected persons aged 20 years and older participated. Our main outcome measures were weighted prevalence estimates of self-reporting one of the following cancer alarm symptoms during the preceding 12 months: a lump in the breast, blood in bowel movements, blood in urine, or coughing for more than six weeks. Logistic regression models were used to calculate unadjusted and adjusted odds ratios with 95% confidence intervals for the associations between each covariate and reporting of cancer alarm symptoms. RESULTS: A total of 2 098 (15.7%) of the participants reported one or more cancer alarm symptoms within the preceding 12 months. Women, subjects out of the workforce, and subjects with a cancer diagnosis had statistically significantly higher odds of reporting one or more cancer alarm symptoms. Subjects with older age and subjects living with a partner had lower odds of reporting one or more cancer alarm symptoms. When analysing the four alarm symptoms of cancer separately most tendencies persisted. CONCLUSIONS: Socioeconomic and demographic determinants are associated with self-reporting of common cancer alarm symptoms.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Svendsen, Rikke Pilsgaard","Paulsen, Maja Skov","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Hansen, Bjarne Lühr","Støvring, Henrik","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-025860"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between reporting of cancer alarm symptoms and socioeconomic and demographic determinants a population based cross sectional study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-12-686","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-025860","identifier":[{"id":"22914003","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3560107","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84865175022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b50be1bd-6c02-4fba-bf4b-1e78a7bbd13a","sdu-7f30ee0f-d15f-4170-8f12-69ad9038d51d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-18635137D57FA5C4A50A3D03C03CAB89"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-12-686","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Pilsgaard","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"50a5117f-6f91-43cc-9db3-d4e1fccba747","name":"Svendsen, Rikke Pilsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja S","key":"paulsenpau","last":"Paulsen","locid":"7288551b-43b2-4400-bdc3-b78ad9c0ccc3","name":"Paulsen, Maja Skov","name_org":"Paulsen, Maja S","orcid":"0000-0003-0360-0039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia V","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","name_org":"Larsen, Pia V","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne L","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b566d112-e4e1-439d-92a2-5ad412c39552","name":"Hansen, Bjarne L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"støvringpau","last":"Støvring","locid":"c19fb430-dcd1-4a13-995f-4247f8ebc11d","name":"Støvring, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-5821-2351","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte E","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","name_org":"Jarbøl, Dorte E","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22914003"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2458-12-686","issn":["14712458"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Public Health","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Public Health","title_org":"B M C Public Health","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865175022"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b50be1bd-6c02-4fba-bf4b-1e78a7bbd13a","sdu-7f30ee0f-d15f-4170-8f12-69ad9038d51d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations between reporting of cancer alarm symptoms and socioeconomic and demographic determinants : a population-based, cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-025860","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In Denmark and Greenland, extensive surveillance of avian influenza (AI) viruses in wild bird populations has been conducted from 2007 through 2010. In Denmark, the surveillance consisted of passive surveillance of wild birds found dead or sick across Denmark and active surveillance of apparently healthy live birds in waterfowl reservoirs and along migratory flyways, birds living in proximity to domestic poultry, and hunted game birds. Dead birds were sampled by oropharyngeal swabbing. Healthy live wild birds were captured with nets, traps, or by hand and were sampled by swabbing of the oropharyngeal and cloacal tracts, or swabs were collected from fresh fecal droppings. Hunted game birds were delivered to game-handling establishments, where each bird was sampled by oropharyngeal and cloacal swabbing. During the 2007–10 period, a total of 11,055 wild birds were sampled in Denmark, of which 396 were birds that were found dead. In Greenland, samples were collected mainly from fecal droppings in breeding areas. Samples from 3555 live and apparently healthy wild birds were tested. All swab samples were tested by pan-influenza reverse transcriptase–PCR (RT-PCR), and the positive samples were further tested by H5/H7 specific RT-PCRs. H5/H7-positive samples were subjected to hemagglutination cleavage site sequencing for pathotyping. In addition, all RT-PCR–positive samples were subjected to virus isolation, and the virus isolates were subsequently subtyped. In Denmark, low pathogenic (LP) H5 viruses were detected throughout the period, in addition to a few LPAI H7 and several other subtypes. In Greenland, very few samples were positive for AI. None of them were found to be of the H5 or H7 subtypes by RT-PCR. Isolation of these viruses in eggs was unsuccessful; thus, they were not subtyped further. The findings did, however, demonstrate the presence of LPAI viruses in Greenland. For several water bird species overwintering in North America and northwest Europe, respectively, Greenland constitutes a common breeding area. This raises the possibility that viruses could be transmitted to North America via Greenland and vice versa. In Denmark, the screenings for AI showed LPAI viruses to be naturally occurring in the wild bird population, particularly in waterfowl. The occurrence of AI viruses in the wild bird population may pose a risk for AI infections in Danish poultry.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Trebbien, Ramona","Handberg, Kurt J.","Therkildsen, Ole Roland","Madsen, Jesper Johannes","Thorup, Kasper","Baroch, John A.","DeLiberto, Thomas J.","Larsen, Lars Erik","Jørgensen, Poul Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-084.85-023648"],"event":{"end":"2012-04-04","place":"London, gb","start":"2012-04-01","title":"8th International Symposium on Avian Influenza","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","United States Department of Agriculture"],"keyword":["Avian influenza virus","Denmark","Greenland","Surveillance","Wild birds"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surveillance for avian influenza viruses in wild birds in denmark and greenland 000000002007 000000000010","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1637/10190-041012-ResNote.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-084.85-023648","identifier":[{"id":"23402125","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000313136200029","type":"wos"},{"id":"84871963311","t