{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Holt Larsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-293905"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvad og hvordan kan man lære af ekstreme begivenheder","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-293905","ids":["cbs-c2d6f90b-9269-4338-99d9-c5cd39aed730"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C1B8A87ED506C04C63762994E633B37B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"holtlarsenpau","last":"Holt Larsen","locid":"8ae11131-8aa8-43f3-a839-8e8910f1cf07","name":"Holt Larsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"7","journal":"NOCAnyt","publisher":"Network of Corporate Academies","status":"p","title":"NOCAnyt","volume":"6"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-c2d6f90b-9269-4338-99d9-c5cd39aed730"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Hvad og hvordan kan man lære af ekstreme begivenheder?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-293905","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"As part of the ongoing EU FP7 project LC-Impact (www.lc-impact.eu) new life cycle impact assessment (LCIA) methods are going to be developed and tested on industry cases. Among the life cycle assessment (LCA) impact categories in focus are aquatic eutrophication. As related to especially the marine environment very few and restricted attempts have yet been done on trying to include eutrophication in LCA. The aim of LC-Impact is to develop both a global and a spatial (and temporal) differentiated model, as both central fate processes, sensitivities of receiving environments (e.g. differences in limiting nutrient and variations in this over the year) and the resulting damage can show important spatial variations. Both midpoint and endpoint (damage) modelling are included and the aim is to base the damage modelling on dose-response curves expressing the correlation between the (increase in) nutrient concentration and the potentially affected fraction of species in the marine ecosystem. This poster will present a review of the very limited existing attempts on how to include marine eutrophication in LCA and discuss alternative methodologies on how to model the environmental mechanism of this impact category.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Fred"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309457"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-19","place":"Milano, it","start":"2011-05-15","title":"SETAC Europe 21st Annual Meeting","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Damage modeling","Marine eutrophication","Review"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"review on methodology for lcia of marine eutrophication","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5712394/Poster_%20Review%20on%20LCIA%20of%20marine%20eutrophication-SETAC-Milan-May-2011.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309457","ids":["dtu-1020231c-f277-45ad-b6ce-ee761f8c2731"],"keyword":["Damage modeling","LCIA methodology","Marine eutrophication","Review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-150E07FBBA4A18F5219BABFF2ADFF582"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5712394/Poster_%20Review%20on%20LCIA%20of%20marine%20eutrophication-SETAC-Milan-May-2011.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","14. Life Below Water","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1020231c-f277-45ad-b6ce-ee761f8c2731"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Review on methodology for LCIA of marine eutrophication","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309457","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The USEtox model was developed in a scientific consensus process involving comparison of and harmonization between existing environmental multimedia fate models. For freshwater ecosystem toxicity, it covers the entire impact pathway, i.e., transforming a chemical emission into potential impacts based on quantitative modeling of fate, exposure, and ecotoxicity effects. Taken together, these are represented as chemical-specific characterization factors (CFs). Through analysis of freshwater CFs for approximately 2500 organic chemicals, with special focus on a subset of chemicals with characteristic properties, this work provides understanding of the basis for calculations of CFs in USEtox. In addition, it offers insight into the chemical properties and critical mechanisms covering the continuum from chemical emission to freshwater ecosystem toxicity. For an emission directly to water, the effect factor, which is obtained from laboratory measurements of substance toxicity to different phyla, strongly controls freshwater ecotoxicity, with a range of up to 10 orders of magnitude. Chemical-specific differences in multimedia transfer influence the CF for freshwater emissions by less than two orders of magnitude. However, for an emission to air or soil, differences in chemical properties may decrease the CF by up to 10 orders of magnitude, as a result of intermedia transfer and degradation. This result brings new clarity to the relative contributions of fate and freshwater ecotoxicity to the overall characterization factor.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andrew D, Henderson","Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","Van de Meent, Dik","Huijbregts, Mark AJ","Larsen, Henrik Fred","Margni, Manuele","McKone, Thomas E","Payet, Jerôme","Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","Jolliet, Olivier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-318048"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","France","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cycleco","Polytechnique Montreal","Radboud University Nijmegen","University of California at Berkeley","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"],"keyword":["Characterization factors","Fate modeling","Freshwater ecotoxicity","Life cycle impact assessment","Model comparison","USEtox"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"usetox fate and ecotoxicity factors for comparative assessment of toxic emissions in life cycle analysis sensitivity to key chemical properties","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11367-011-0294-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-318048","identifier":[{"id":"80052772707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2d52469c-80db-442e-bd7a-ef52c589a823"],"keyword":["Characterization factors","Fate modeling","Freshwater ecotoxicity","Life Cycle Impact Assessment","Model comparison","USEtox."],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B29F73467EFCC9A3DD968B9E5CD1A857"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11367-011-0294-6","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"polytechnique montreal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnique Montreal","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"cycleco","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Cycleco","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henderson","key":"andrewdpau","last":"Andrew D","name":"Andrew D, Henderson","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Zwicky","key":"hauschildpau","last":"Hauschild","locid":"5c85fd08-0c76-4c6c-90c3-431093cff94b","name":"Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","orcid":"0000-0002-8331-7390","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dik","key":"vandemeentpau","last":"Van de Meent","name":"Van de Meent, Dik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark AJ","key":"huijbregtspau","last":"Huijbregts","name":"Huijbregts, Mark AJ","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuele","key":"margnipau","last":"Margni","name":"Margni, Manuele","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas E","key":"mckonepau","last":"McKone","name":"McKone, Thomas E","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jerôme","key":"payetpau","last":"Payet","name":"Payet, Jerôme","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph K.","key":"rosenbaumpau","last":"Rosenbaum","locid":"c09ddfbe-dc02-4fd1-9962-f27ae586db0e","name":"Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivier","key":"jollietpau","last":"Jolliet","name":"Jolliet, Olivier","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11367-011-0294-6","issn":["09483349","16147502"],"issn_org":["09483349"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Journal of Life Cycle Assessment","pages":"710-727","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Life Cycle Assessment","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052772707"],"sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","15. Life on Land","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2d52469c-80db-442e-bd7a-ef52c589a823"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"USEtox fate and ecotoxicity factors for comparative assessment of toxic emissions in Life Cycle Analysis : Sensitivity to key chemical properties","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-318048","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Characterization of metal toxic impacts in comparative risk assessment and life cycle impact assessment (LCIA) should take into account metal speciation and interactions with soil/water organic constituents, because these mechanisms control metal bioavailability and may influence their toxic properties. In a comparative context we are faced with the need to characterise thousands of substances, but the limitation of the available data calls for reliable indicators suitable for extrapolation from the limited data that is available. Indeed, free metal ion concentration has in some cases been shown to be a sufficient indicator of metal toxicity for both aquatic and terrestrial species. With the aim of deriving extrapolations to predict terrestrial toxic impacts of metals from aquatic effect data, we compared copper toxicity of aquatic organisms with that of terrestrial organisms, testing the hypothesis that the free metal ion is an appropriate “general”descriptor of metal toxicity. Results for 128 laboratory tests on Daphnia magna exposed to copper ions (Cu2+) in water show that variation of several orders of magnitude are observed between the toxicity tests. These variations may be a result of the inability of the free metal ion concentration to reflect toxicity, as the presence of protons and other cations reacting with biological binding sites has been shown to affect the toxicity of copper to D. magna. Similar patterns, albeit with smaller variations, are observed for terrestrial organisms. Up to three orders of magnitude difference occur for the extreme case of barley (Hordeum vulgare). Given the scarcity of terrestrial effect data compared to aquatic data, reliable and transparent, mechanistic-based predictions of terrestrial toxic impacts from aquatic effect data would be an important step ahead in the context of LCIA or comparative risk. Here we demonstrate that the overall ability of the free metal ion to reflect toxicity of metals for aquatic and terrestrial organisms is limited. This has consequences if potential terrestrial toxic effects are based on extrapolations from aquatic data, because the use of more sophisticated models such as the Biotic Ligand Model (BLM) would be required. However, extrapolation models based on an improved free ion approach might still be a good proxy, particularly when the comparative nature of life cycle assessment is taken into account.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Owsianiak, Mikolaj","Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","Larsen, Henrik Fred","Hauschild, Michael Zwicky"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349468"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-19","place":"Milano, it","start":"2011-05-15","title":"SETAC Europe 21st Annual Meeting","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of metal toxic impacts between aquatic and terrestrial organisms is the free ion concentration a sufficient descriptor","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-349468","ids":["dtu-967d8002-5d0f-4e16-aa17-fdc2a4adfc1b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B9311B7B0DA3E43A478349C9E6735704"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikolaj","key":"owsianiakpau","last":"Owsianiak","locid":"445e4fd6-d05d-4b38-b2f2-f114dd5a16ca","name":"Owsianiak, Mikolaj","orcid":"0000-0002-6834-6249","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph K.","key":"rosenbaumpau","last":"Rosenbaum","locid":"c09ddfbe-dc02-4fd1-9962-f27ae586db0e","name":"Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Zwicky","key":"hauschildpau","last":"Hauschild","locid":"5c85fd08-0c76-4c6c-90c3-431093cff94b","name":"Hauschild, Michael Zwicky","orcid":"0000-0002-8331-7390","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"SETAC Europe 21st Annual Meeting Abstract Book"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-967d8002-5d0f-4e16-aa17-fdc2a4adfc1b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Comparison of metal toxic impacts between aquatic and terrestrial organisms: is the free ion concentration a sufficient descriptor?","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-349468","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
