{"abstract":"Background and purpose High-volume infiltration analgesia may be effective in postoperative pain management after hip arthroplasty but methodological problems prevent exact interpretation of previous studies. Methods In a randomized, double-blind placebo-controlled trial in 12 patients undergoing bilateral total hip arthroplasty (THA) in a fast-track setting, saline or high-volume (170 mL) ropivacaine (0.2%) with epinephrine (1:100,000) was administered to the wound intraoperatively along with supplementary postoperative injections via an intraarticular epidural catheter. Oral analgesia was instituted preoperatively with a multimodal regimen (gabapentin, celecoxib, and acetaminophen). Pain was assessed repeatedly for 48 hours postoperatively, at rest and with 45° hip flexion. Results Pain scores were low and similar between ropivacaine and saline administration. Median hospital stay was 4 (range 2-7) days. Interpretation Intraoperative high-volume infiltration with 0.2% ropivacaine with repeated intraarticular injections postoperatively may not give a clinically relevant analgesic effect in THA when combined with a multimodal oral analgesic regimen with gabapentin, celecoxib, and acetaminophen.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Lasse Ø","Otte, Niels Kristian Stahl","Husted, Henrik","Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","Kristensen, Billy","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489244"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high volume infiltration analgesia in bilateral hip arthroplasty","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/17453674.2011.596063","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-489244","identifier":[{"id":"80052504384","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a03ccfdc-6937-402c-95a8-ca645f2ea328"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-36ACEE6EEAF2F9344C65B92344DE90F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/17453674.2011.596063","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lasse Ø","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lasse Ø","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Kristian Stahl","key":"ottepau","last":"Otte","name":"Otte, Niels Kristian Stahl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","name":"Husted, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lissi","key":"gaarnlarsenpau","last":"Gaarn-Larsen","name":"Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Billy","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Billy","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/17453674.2011.596063","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"423-6","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","title_org":"Acta Orthopaedica (Print Edition)","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052504384"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a03ccfdc-6937-402c-95a8-ca645f2ea328"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"High-volume infiltration analgesia in bilateral hip arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489244","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
