{"abstract":"The Frank polyphase sequence has been applied to pulsed EPR of triarylmethyl radicals at 256MHz (9.1mT magnetic field), using 256 phase pulses. In EPR, as in NMR, use of a Frank sequence of phase steps permits pulsed FID signal acquisition with very low power microwave/RF pulses (ca. 1.5mW in the application reported here) relative to standard pulsed EPR. A 0.2mM aqueous solution of a triarylmethyl radical was studied using a 16mm diameter cross-loop resonator to isolate the EPR signal detection system from the incident pulses. Keyword: Correlation spectroscopy,Multi-pulse EPR,Low power pulses,NMR,EPR,Frank sequence","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tseitlin, Mark","Quine, Richard W.","Eaton, Sandra S.","Eaton, Gareth R.","Halpern, Howard J.","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-304835"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Chicago","University of Denver"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of the frank sequence in pulsed epr","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6425123/elsevier%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-304835","identifier":[{"id":"79953198602","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-01130514-08ec-4749-a9a9-4fb5ceb99a21"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-696F52C052F1E046207D2ED5FA457958"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6425123/elsevier%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmr.2011.01.032","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of denver","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Denver","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"the university of chicago","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"The University of Chicago","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"tseitlinmarkpau","last":"Tseitlin","name":"Tseitlin, Mark","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard W.","key":"quinerichardwpau","last":"Quine","name":"Quine, Richard W.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra S.","key":"eatonsandraspau","last":"Eaton","name":"Eaton, Sandra S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gareth R.","key":"eatongarethrpau","last":"Eaton","name":"Eaton, Gareth R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Howard J.","key":"halpernhowardjpau","last":"Halpern","name":"Halpern, Howard J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenjanhenrikpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2011.01.032","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","pages":"306-309","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953198602"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-01130514-08ec-4749-a9a9-4fb5ceb99a21"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Use of the Frank sequence in pulsed EPR","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-304835","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Concerns about possible toxic effects from additives/impurities accumulated in globally recycled waste/resources like paper and plastics was one of the main reasons for starting up the EU FP7 Coordination Action project RiskCycle (www.wadef.com/projects/riskcycle). A key aim of the project is to identify research needs within this area focusing on both risk assessment (RA) and life cycle assessment (LCA). Besides the sectors on paper and plastics also lubricants, textiles, electronics and leather are included in RiskCycle. On plastics a literature review regarding the state of knowledge on additives/impurities in LCA has been performed within RiskCycle. Several inventory databases (LCI data) have been investigated and the result shows that most LCI databases use PlasticsEurope data for plastics production. Most of these data are aggregated and do not include additives. Regarding the production of additives only data on metals and DEHP was identified. As regards LCAs on plastics 110 papers has been reviewed. Only 25 of these mention additives but they are not included in the emissions list. Only a few studies include additives in the impact assessment and additives are never mentioned as important for the outcome. Regarding LCAs on printed matter (including paper) only a few studies have been done – mostly focusing on the energy part. However, one of the most recent and comprehensive studies actually include toxic impacts from chemical emissions – mostly printing chemicals like printing ink of which some components may accumulate in recycled paper. Even though recycling is included in this recent study there is no special focus on the additives/impurities in the recycled paper. Anyway, the study shows that potential toxic impacts from the production and use of chemicals like pigments, solvents, metals, AOX and biocides may play a very significant role in the impact profile of printed matter. Regarding the life cycle impact assessment (LCIA) part an investigation of the availability of characterisation factors (aquatic ecotox) for the about 17 additives/impurities to be included in RiskCycle have been done. These additives belong to 15 chemical groups/chemicals like PFOS, PFOA, NPAA, HBCDD, triclosan and more. The best practice LCIA “consensus” model USEtox was chosen. For only nine of the 17 substances characterisation factors exists and four of these are preliminary (interim). Regarding the rest, factors have to be calculated - if possible.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Fred","von der Voet, Ester","Van Oers L, Lauran","Yang, Gao","Rydberg, Tomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-307075"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-19","place":"Milan, it","start":"2011-05-15","title":"SETAC Europe's 21st Annual Meeting","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University","Swedish Environmental Research Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"life cycle assessment and additives state of knowledge","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5728272/SETAC_%20RISKCYCLE_Presentation_Life%20cycle%20assessment%20and%20additives_%20HFL_DTU.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-307075","ids":["dtu-0859f31f-c61e-4c1e-add9-3df30801aa8c"],"keyword":["LCA, additives, recycling, waste"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B48DEB0BD744DBB7AF3FBA21E0FCFA43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5728272/SETAC_%20RISKCYCLE_Presentation_Life%20cycle%20assessment%20and%20additives_%20HFL_DTU.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5728273/Extended%20abstract%20for%20RiskCycle%20presentation%20on%20LCA%20and%20additives%20Milano-2011-word.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"leiden university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leiden University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"swedish environmental research institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish Environmental Research Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenppu","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":1,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ester","key":"vondervoetppu","last":"von der Voet","name":"von der Voet, Ester","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lauran","key":"vanoerslppu","last":"Van Oers L","name":"Van Oers L, Lauran","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gao","key":"yangppu","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Gao","rank":4,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomas","key":"rydbergppu","last":"Rydberg","name":"Rydberg, Tomas","rank":5,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0859f31f-c61e-4c1e-add9-3df30801aa8c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Life cycle assessment and additives: state of knowledge","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-307075","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The aim of the project is to analyse the potential synergistic interplay that may arise between the power sector and the transport sector, if parts of the road transport energy needs are based on electricity via the utilisation of plug-in hybrid electric vehicles and pure electric vehicles. The project focuses on the technical elements in the chain that comprises: 1: The electric vehicle status, potentials and expected development. Electric batteries are in focus in this part of the analysis. 2: Analysis of plug-in hybrid electric vehicle interacting with a local grid. 3: Analysis of grid-vehicle connection systems including technical regulation options and analysis of needs for standardisation. 4: Setting up scenarios covering potential developments for utilizing electric drive trains in road transport. Period: Up to year 2030. 5: Analysis of capacity constraints in the electricity grid (transmission and distribution) as consequence of increasing electricity demand, and new flexible consumption patterns from segments in the transport sector, and as consequence of increasing capacity on wind power in the system. 6: Setting up and analysis of combined scenarios covering both the heat and power system and the transport sector.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lars Henrik","Ravn, Hans","Meibom, Peter","Juul, Nina","Hedegaard, Karsten","Larsen, Helge V.","Jørgensen, Kaj","Larsen, Esben","Horstmann, Jørgen Peter Frederik","Nørgård, Per Bromand","Bavnhøj Hansen, Anders","Pedersen, Jens","Kipp, Nicolai Anders","Abildgaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316588"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ENER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ENER","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electricity for road transport flexible power systems and wind power","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7598196/ris_r_1804.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316588","ids":["dtu-2864354d-f582-4fb1-82f7-a836b4c98f7b"],"keyword":["Risø-R-1804","Risø-R-1804(EN)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FD5C5B77CDB13BBF4949AC33794750E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7598196/ris_r_1804.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Systems Analysis Division","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Systems Analysis Division, Energy Systems Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"energinet","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ENER","l3nl":"Energinet SOV","l3nn":"Energinet","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Energinet","namevar":["Energinet.dk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ENER","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"nielsenlarshenrikpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"220ab16a-65f5-4a2a-92b5-f52c88e5c034","name":"Nielsen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-5054-6149","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"ravnhanspau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, Hans","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P