"yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The implementation of the EU REACH regulation will most probably promote substitution within sectors handling a lot of different chemicals like the printing industry. With the aim of being at the cutting edge of this development the Danish EPA together with the Danish printing industry and IPU are running a substitution project. A major part of the work has been mapping the presence of chemicals which are potential candidates for substitution (e.g. PBT, CMR, vPvB, EDS) within the Danish printing industry and this work was recently finished. The mapping comprises a combination of a literature study and an investigation of the actual (2007) presence of candidate substances at 15 Danish printing houses including the examination of almost 900 MSDS’s (i.e. products). Furthermore, a focused search in the Danish Product Register has been included. More than 150 of the mapped substances are candidates for substitution according to Danish legislation (List of Undesirable Substances) and about 40 of these substances fulfil one or more of the criteria (e.g. CMR, EDS) for the REACH Annex XIV candidate list (authorisation). Three substances (phthalates) out of the first and recently published Annex XIV candidate list (in total 15 substances) were found in the Danish printing industry.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Fred","Bøg, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-333512"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chemical substitution","Chemicals","Printing","REACH"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Grafisk Arbejdsgiverforening"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kemikaliesubstitution i grafisk branche","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5276420/Kemikaliesub.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-333512","ids":["dtu-612dfbcd-e771-490e-a632-8662ab726da1"],"keyword":["REACH","chemical substitution","chemicals","hazard ranking","printing,"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5B14C38580BFEB3B214D54AA2B96F42E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5276420/Kemikaliesub.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Grafisk Arbejdsgiverforening"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"bøgpau","last":"Bøg","name":"Bøg, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"1354","pages":"75","publisher":"Miljøstyrelsen","repno":"Miljøprojekter, No. 1354","series":"Miljøprojekter","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-612dfbcd-e771-490e-a632-8662ab726da1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Kemikaliesubstitution i grafisk branche","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-333512","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Denne rapport indeholder en evaluering af værktøjet Critical Dilution Volume (CDV), der anvendes ved miljømærkning af produkter under både det nordiske mærke Svanen og EU's mærke Blomsten. Følgende spørgsmål er besvaret:  Hvilken miljømæssig værdi giver værktøjet? Tager man hensyn til væsentlige parametre, af betydning for produktets miljøprofil?  Rammer det rigtigt i de fleste tilfælde – altså betyder høj CDV også typisk, at produkterne har nogle dårlige miljøegenskaber (vandmiljø)?  Hvordan med forskellen mellem akut CDV og kronisk CDV. Vi har ofte valgfrihed. Bør vi altid stille krav til både akut og kronisk, skal vi fokusere alene på kronisk, eller er det OK som vi gør i dag?  Kan man lave tilpasninger til CDV-værktøjet for at forbedre det? … eller findes der noget andet, vi kan bruge i stedet, der er bedre end CDV og som kan tilfredsstille de samme behov for lettilgængelighed – også for SME’er?","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Henrik Fred"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335286"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluering af cdv værktøjet evaluation of the cdv tool","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-335286","ids":["dtu-66d710b9-e407-42c4-aa0e-03fac13cf02e"],"keyword":["Critical dilution volume (CDV), scoring and ranking systems, eco-labeling, hazard assessment, chemicals,"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-030A331AB6F64935F208FF650F0ED4D8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"20","place":"Lyngby","publisher":"Danmarks Tekniske Universitet, Risø Nationallaboratoriet for Bæredygtig Energi","status":"p","volume":"Rapport 2011, DTU Management"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-66d710b9-e407-42c4-aa0e-03fac13cf02e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Evaluering af CDV-værktøjet (Evaluation of the CDV-tool)","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335286","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The project has aimed to characterize mesoscale meteorological phenomenon for the North Sea and the Inner Danish waters, and additionally aimed on improving the predictability and quality of the power production from offshore windfarms. The meso-scale meteorology has been characterized with respect to the physical processes, climatology, spectral characteristics and correlation properties based on measurements from wind farms, satellite data (SAR) and mesoscale numerical modeling (WRF). The abilities of the WRF model to characterize and predict relevant mesoscale phenomenon has been proven. Additionally application of statistical forecasting, using a Markov switching approach that can be related to the meteorological conditions, to analyze and short term predict the power production from an offshore wind farms have been documented. Two PhD studies have been conducted in connection with the project. The project has been a cooperative project between Risø DTU, IMM DTU, DONG Energy, Vattenfall and VESTAS. It is registered as Energinet.dk, project no. 2007-1-7141.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Søren Ejling","Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","Vincent, Claire Louise","Sørensen, Poul Ejnar","Pinson, Pierre","Trombe, Pierre-Julien","Madsen, Henrik","Cutululis, Nicolaos Antonio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360423"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"meso scale wind variability final report","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6305535/ris-r-1794.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360423","ids":["dtu-bacc4f01-72cc-4cdb-a9fe-acc34def8ec0"],"keyword":[