{"abstract":"This document describes common methodological issues for the case studies within LC-IMPACT. There will be five case studies in three areas performed within the project. The case studies are: Tomatoes, Margarine, Fish, Paper and printing and finally car manufacture and operation. In each case study several LCIA methods developed in other parts of LC-IMPACT will be applied and evaluated, but established LCIA methods will also be used and the studies shall be ILCD compliant. All case studies will follow the ILCD Handbook and this report describes common methodological choices needed and describes how data inventory is to be done and how deviations from the stated goals shall be managed and reported. A description of the external review is also presented.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sonesson, Ulf","Anton, Assumpcio","Ohlau, Katrin","Larsen, Henrik Fred"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316899"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Spain","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institut de Recerca i Tecnologia Agroalimentàries","Swedish Institute for Food and Biotechnology","University of Stuttgart"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"description of common methodology used in all case studies following the ilcd methodology guide and the iso standards for lca iso 000000014040 and 000000014044","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lc-impact.eu/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316899","ids":["dtu-2975a753-8a37-4a4d-9dde-2d6c9e6592af"],"keyword":["LCA case studies","common methodology","new LCIA methodology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A35881687B99822842EA23549F03E86E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lc-impact.eu/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"swedish institute for food and biotechnology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish Institute for Food and Biotechnology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"institut de recerca i tecnologia agroalimentàries","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institut de Recerca i Tecnologia Agroalimentàries","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of stuttgart","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Stuttgart","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulf","key":"sonessonpau","last":"Sonesson","name":"Sonesson, Ulf","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Assumpcio","key":"antonpau","last":"Anton","name":"Anton, Assumpcio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrin","key":"ohlaupau","last":"Ohlau","name":"Ohlau, Katrin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Fred","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dffb5d96-c7e7-4b4a-bf49-ec006eae9a66","name":"Larsen, Henrik Fred","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"4.1","pages":"76","repno":"EU FP7 project, deliverable, 4.1","series":"EU FP7 project, deliverable","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2975a753-8a37-4a4d-9dde-2d6c9e6592af"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Description of common methodology used in all case studies, following the ILCD methodology guide and the ISO standards for LCA (ISO 14040 and 14044)","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316899","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Metal partitioning between solid and aqueous phases and speciation in soil pore water control the bioavailability of toxic forms of metals, while protons and base cations can mitigate metal ecotoxicity by competitive interactions with biotic ligands. e employment of BLMs to evaluate toxicity potential of metals in soils results in site-specic toxicity scores due to large variability of soil properties and dierences in ionic composition. Unfortunately, terrestrial BMLs are available only for few metals and few organisms, thus their applicability to hazard ranking or toxic impact assessment is low and alternatives must be found. In this study, we compared published terrestrial BLMs and their potential alternatives such as free ion activity models (FIAM), for applicability in addressing metal toxic impacts in terrestrial environments. A set of 1300 soils representative for the whole world is employed to calculate EC50 and thereafter hazardous concentration HC50 (geometric mean of all EC50) for these terrestrial organisms, for which both TBLMs and FIAMs are available. Results showed that median HC50 for all soils predicted with BLMs range 2 and 3 orders of magnitude for copper and nickel, respectively. In all cases, predictions of FIAMs fall within the range of values predicted with BLMs, and toxicity ratio of copper to nickel is accurately predicted with both models. us, both models are able to distinguish between the two metals in terms of their average toxicity. Given that the calculated toxicity scores show large variability even for soils located in close proximity to each other, selection of FIAMs is also justied in deriving soil quality criteria. It remains to be investigated at what spatial scale the FIAMs are a good alternative to TBLMs in evaluating metal toxic impacts in terrestrial environments.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Owsianiak, Mikolaj","Rosenbaum, Ralph K.","Larsen, Henrik Fred","Hauschild, Michael Zwicky"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331985"],"event":{"end":"2011-11-17","place":"Boston, us","start":"2011-11-13","title":"Society of Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are free ion activity models sufficient alternatives to biotic ligand models in evaluating metal toxic impacts in terrestrial environments","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6352082/prod11324284440901.setac_north_america_2011_abstract_book%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331985","ids":["dtu-5c2e75eb-6be4-4632-a221-4ce905c553d0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8BFA7D0E423038AB0BF96DB88DE9EBC6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6352082/prod11324284440901.setac_north_america_2011_abstract_book%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikolaj","key":"owsianiakpau","last":"Owsianiak","locid":"445e4fd6-d05d-4b38-b2f2-f114dd5a16ca","name":"Owsianiak, Mikolaj","orcid":"0000-0002-6834-6249","