{"abstract":": High-volume local infiltration analgesia (LIA) is widely applied as part of a multimodal pain management strategy in total hip arthroplasty (THA). However, methodological problems hinder the exact interpretation of previous trials, and the evidence for LIA in THA remains to be clarified. Therefore, we evaluated whether intraoperative high-volume LIA, in addition to a multimodal oral analgesic regimen, would further reduce acute postoperative pain after THA.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lunn, Troels H","Husted, Henrik","Solgaard, Søren","Kristensen, Billy B","Otte, Niels Kristian Stahl","Kjersgaard, Anne G","Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intraoperative local infiltration analgesia for early analgesia after total hip arthroplasty a randomized double blind placebo controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/AAP.0b013e3182186866","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-501991","identifier":[{"id":"80053590216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b5c229df-eba9-4b9d-8672-3dcf8b4debdd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9764C19419AA98D252A72023FE641A04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/AAP.0b013e3182186866","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Kø