{"abstract":"BACKGROUND:: We aimed to estimate the impact of comorbidity acquired before HIV diagnosis on mortality in HIV-infected individuals METHODS:: This cohort study compared two different cohorts. The prospective population-based nationwide observational Danish HIV Cohort Study was used to compare all adults diagnosed with HIV in Denmark from 1997 with a matched general population cohort. Comorbidity history was ascertained from the Danish National Patient Registry and vital statistics obtained from Denmark's Civil Registration System. Cox regression was used to estimate impact of Charlson Comorbidity Index (CCI) and hepatitis C virus coinfection (HCV) on mortality, and Population Attributable Risk to assess the proportional impact of comorbidity on mortality. RESULTS:: CCI comorbidity was present before HIV diagnosis in 11.3% of 1,638 persons with HIV, and in 8.0% of 156,506 persons in the general population. The risk of death in HIV patients with at least one CCI point was 1.84 times higher than in those with no CCI points (adjusted mortality rate ratio, 95% confidence interval: 1.32-2.57). The annual risk of dying for HIV patients vs general population with 0, 1, 2, and 3+ CCI points was 1.70% (1.44-2.00) vs 0.27% (0.26-0.28), 4.37% (3.01-6.32) vs 1.36% (1.26-1.47), 8.06% (4.94-13.16) vs 2.44% (2.22-2.68), and 10.15% (5.08-20.30) vs 5.84% (5.19-6.58), respectively. Comorbidity acquired before HIV, HCV, and background mortality accounted for 45% of total mortality in the HIV-infected population. CONCLUSIONS:: Almost half of deaths in persons diagnosed with HIV in a health care setting with free access to HAART stemmed from factors unrelated to HIV disease.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lohse, Nicolai","Gerstoft, Jan","Kronborg, Gitte","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Pedersen, Court","Pedersen, Gitte","Nielsen, Lars","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Obel, Niels"],"cuid":["S03-095.41-014900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comorbidity acquired before hiv diagnosis and mortality in hiv infected and uninfected persons a danish population based cohort study","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAI.0b013e31821d34ed","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-095.41-014900","identifier":[{"id":"21522017","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79959947558","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1f83f75a-5117-4342-9b16-d12b0fd6e434","ku-2af5c68a-0a77-4a82-b9d1-5110f40bd0ce","sdu-0915af5e-4b17-4d2e-b96a-a48fd4fb72c4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-9B3A4295606B71306B8CA5D7542ED07B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAI.0b013e31821d34ed","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, The Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Orthopaedics and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai","key":"lohsenicolaipau","last":"Lohse","locid":"478827c6-cc64-4e5a-a513-139a4b284d7f","name":"Lohse, Nicolai","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"gerstoftjanpau","last":"Gerstoft","name":"Gerstoft, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"kronborggittepau","last":"Kronborg","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Schade","key":"larsencarstenschadepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2435cb82-03bd-498b-909d-1ef0e99443fe","name":"Larsen, Carsten Schade","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Court","key":"pedersencourtpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7f2e0dec-1687-4283-ac30-53e73c124437","name":"Pedersen, Court","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"pedersengittepau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"03b23acd-948c-47f7-80f8-38dc1d456f53","name":"Pedersen, Gitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"nielsenlarspau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lars","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenhenriktoftpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"obelnielspau","last":"Obel","name":"Obel, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-5031-0045","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21522017"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/qai.0b013e31821d34ed","issn":["15254135","19447884"],"issn_org":["15254135"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of acquired immune deficiency syndromes","pages":"334-9","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"Journal of acquired immune deficiency syndromes","title_org":"JAIDS: Journal of Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndromes","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79959947558"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1f83f75a-5117-4342-9b16-d12b0fd6e434","ku-2af5c68a-0a77-4a82-b9d1-5110f40bd0ce","sdu-0915af5e-4b17-4d2e-b96a-a48fd4fb72c4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comorbidity Acquired before HIV Diagnosis and Mortality in HIV-infected and Uninfected Persons: A Danish population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.41-014900","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The Danish HNPCC register is a publically financed national database. The register gathers epidemiological and genomic data in HNPCC families to improve prognosis by screening and identifying family members at risk. Diagnostic data are generated throughout the country and collected over several decades. Until recently, paper-based reports were sent to the register and typed into the database. In the EC cofunded-INFOBIOMED network of excellence, the register was a model for electronic exchange of epidemiological and genomic data between diagnosing/treating departments and the central database. The aim of digitization was to optimize the organization of screening by facilitating combination of genotype-phenotype information, and to generate IT-tools sufficiently usable and generic to be implemented in other countries and for other oncogenetic diseases. The focus was on integration of heterogeneous data, elaboration, and dissemination of classification systems and development of communication standards. At the conclusion of the EU project in 2007 the system was implemented in 12 pilot departments. In the surgical departments this resulted in a 192% increase of reports to the database. Several gaps were identified: lack of standards for data to be exchanged, lack of local databases suitable for direct communication, reporting being time-consuming and dependent on interest and feedback. Hum Mutat 32:551-556, 2011. (C) 2011 Wiley-Liss, Inc.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Bernstein, Inge Thomsen","Larsen, K.L.","Timshel, Susanne","Brandt, Carsten","Dinesen, Birger","Fenger, Mogens","Gerdes, Anne-Marie Axø","Iversen, Lene Hjerrild","Madsen, Mogens Rørbæk","Okkels, Henrik","Sunde, Lone","Rahr, Hans B","Wikman, Friedrik P","Rossing, Niels"],"cuid":["S03-098.29-015595"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Colorectal Neoplasms Hereditary Nonpolyposis","Computational Biology","Delivery of Health Care","Denmark","Humans","Medical Informatics Applications","Registries","Software"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biomedical informatics as support to individual healthcare in hereditary colon cancer the danish hnpcc system","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/humu.21435","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-098.29-015595","identifier":[{"id":"21520332","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79955043825","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-292967c3-d33b-4bde-a589-69233cb582af","ku-1850bef3-abea-4e6c-9657-320b3105c93e","sdu-22e5813c-fe56-488e-93ba-6dd107a6711a"],"keyword":["Colorectal Neoplasms, Hereditary Nonpolyposis","Computational Biology","Delivery of Health Care","Denmark","Humans","Medical Informatics Applications","Registries","Software"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-FE9FCD291D4F661D95B425341261C861"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/humu.21435","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Kirurgisk Gastroenterologisk afdeling A, AAL"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","N