{"abstract":"Analytical platforms for the fast detection, identification and quantification of circulating drugs with a narrow therapeutic range are vital in clinical pharmacology. As a result of low drug concentrations, analytical tools need to provide high sensitivity and specificity. Dynamic nuclear polarization‐NMR (DNP‐NMR) in the form of the hyperpolarization–dissolution method should afford the sensitivity and spectral resolution for the direct detection and quantification of numerous isotopically labeled circulating drugs and their metabolites in single liquid‐state NMR transients. This study explores the capability of quantitative in vitro DNP‐NMR to assay drug metabolites in blood plasma. The lower limit of detection for the anti‐epileptic drug 13C‐carbamazepine and its pharmacologically active metabolite 13C‐carbamazepine‐10,11‐epoxide is 0.08 µg/mL in rabbit blood plasma analyzed by single‐scan 13C DNP‐NMR. An internal standard is used for the accurate quantification of drug and metabolite. Comparison of quantitative DNP‐NMR data with an established analytical method (liquid chromatography‐mass spectrometry) yields a Pearson correlation coefficient r of 0.99. Notably, all DNP‐NMR determinations were performed without analyte derivatization or sample purification other than plasma protein precipitation. Quantitative DNP‐NMR is an emerging methodology which requires little sample preparation and yields quantitative data with high sensitivity for therapeutic drug monitoring. Copyright © 2010 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd. Keyword: Blood plasma,DNP-NMR,Carbamazepine,Drug metabolism,C NMR,Therapeutic drug monitoring","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","Meier, Sebastian","Jensen, Pernille Rose","Hustvedt, Svein‐Olaf","Karlsson, Magnus","Duus, Jens Øllgaard","Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343727"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CARL"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CARL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantitative dynamic nuclear polarization nmr on blood plasma for assays of drug metabolism","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.1561","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343727","identifier":[{"id":"78851470658","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-831c1d7c-eaa8-488c-a7b0-db6673e31865"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-64BDDC067383DEADA347881810A4DBC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nbm.1561","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Albeda Research ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"carlsberg foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CARL","l3nn":"Carlsberg Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Carlsberg Foundation","namevar":["Carlsberg Research Center"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CARL","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"ge healthcare","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GE Healthcare","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde Hauge","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","name":"Lerche, Mathilde Hauge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Sebastian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Rose","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Pernille Rose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Svein‐Olaf","key":"hustvedtpau","last":"Hustvedt","name":"Hustvedt, Svein‐Olaf","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","name":"Karlsson, Magnus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Øllgaard","key":"duuspau","last":"Duus","name":"Duus, Jens Øllgaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Henrik","key":"ardenkjærlarsenpau","last":"Ardenkjær-Larsen","locid":"ae9519c9-1b64-4426-b89f-4c36d08c1836","name":"Ardenkjær-Larsen, Jan Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6167-6926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.1561","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"1","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","pages":"96-103","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","title_org":"N M R in Biomedicine","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78851470658"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","albeda research aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-831c1d7c-eaa8-488c-a7b0-db6673e31865"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Quantitative dynamic nuclear polarization‐NMR on blood plasma for assays of drug metabolism","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343727","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents how using a correspondence-based interpolation scheme for 3D image registration improves the registration accuracy. The interpolator takes into account correspondences across slices, which is an advantage, particularly when the volume has thick slices, and where anatomies lie non-parallel to the slice direction. We use our previously presented approach for correspondence-based interpolation and demonstrate results on two different datasets, brain and cardiac MRI. The results are evaluated (i) qualitatively by examination of gradient images and cardiac pig atlases and (ii) quantitatively by registering downsampled brain data using two different interpolators and subsequently applying the deformation fields to the original data. The results show that the interpolator provides better gradient images and a more sharp cardiac atlas. Moreover, it provides better deformation fields on downsampled data, increasing the registration accuracy of original data to 5.8% on average with respect to a standard interpolator.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ólafsdóttir, Hildur","Pedersen, Henrik","Hansen, Michael Sass","Larsson, Henrik","Larsen, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-359695"],"event":{"end":"2011-04-02","place":"Chicago, us","start":"2011-03-30","title":"2011 IEEE International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atlas","Image gradient","Image registration","Magnetic Resonance Imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving image registration by correspondence interpolation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISBI.2011.5872691","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-359695","identifier":[{"id":"80055038004","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b86a1f37-0581-4c66-af00-0266bb2c2866"],"keyword":["Atlas","Image gradient","Image interpolation","Image registration","Magnetic resonance imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0CBA5D6CF2ED318C908336C0BFD473D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISBI.2011.5872691","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.biomedicalimaging.org/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling, Image Analysis and Computer Graphics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hildur","key":"ólafsdóttirpau","last":"Ólafsdóttir","locid":"dab35ee2-fd98-47e1-865c-7c78c50c05b9","name":"Ólafsdóttir, Hildur","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Sass","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d38ca301-d2b2-41f2-a924-a8a9ebb102bc","name":"Hansen, Michael Sass","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","name":"Larsson, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b3ea098f-fc7a-48a0-94ae-ae033577d7f1","name":"Larsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-8507-0523","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/isbi.2011.5872691","isbn":["9781424441280"],"pages":"1524-1527","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings","title":"2011 8th IEEE International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging: From Nano to Macro"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80055038004"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b86a1f37-0581-4c66-af00-0266bb2c2866"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improving image registration by correspondence interpolation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-359695","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
