{"abstract":"Total knee arthroplasty (TKA) is associated with severe pain and inflammation despite an extensive multimodal analgesic approach, but the effect of high-dose glucocorticoid administration has not been studied.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lunn, Troels","Kristensen, Billy Bjarne","Andersen, Lasse","Husted, Henrik","Otte, K S","Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","Kehlet, H","Otte, Niels Kristian Stahl","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453095"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of high dose preoperative methylprednisolone on pain and recovery after total knee arthroplasty a randomized placebo controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bja/aeq333","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453095","identifier":[{"id":"78751547607","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-63c6ec50-1d79-4316-adfc-4c25df0c5ab8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CA4BE9A465423B5E4935CEF4163ECCEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bja/aeq333","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Troels","key":"lunntroelspau","last":"Lunn","name":"Lunn, Troels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Billy Bjarne","key":"kristensenbillybjarnepau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Billy Bjarne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lasse","key":"andersenlassepau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lasse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H","key":"hustedhenrikpau","last":"Husted","locid":"f8dc9a5b-bf7f-45e7-b210-3b25c01cfa24","name":"Husted, Henrik","name_org":"Husted, H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"K S","key":"ottekspau","last":"Otte","name":"Otte, K S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L","key":"gaarnlarsenlissipau","last":"Gaarn-Larsen","locid":"dd299835-fdf5-485b-9a11-3c1b59db8901","name":"Gaarn-Larsen, Lissi","name_org":"Gaarn-Larsen, L","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H","key":"kehlethpau","last":"Kehlet","name":"Kehlet, H","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Kristian Stahl","key":"ottenielskristianstahlpau","last":"Otte","name":"Otte, Niels Kristian Stahl","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"kehlethenrikpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/bja/aeq333","issn":["00070912","14716771"],"issn_org":["00070912"],"issue":"2","journal":"British Journal of Anaesthesia","pages":"230-8","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Anaesthesia","volume":"106"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78751547607"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-63c6ec50-1d79-4316-adfc-4c25df0c5ab8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of high-dose preoperative methylprednisolone on pain and recovery after total knee arthroplasty: a randomized, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453095","year":"2011","yearsub":"2010"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: To assess cumulative glycemia, microvascular characteristics, and associated risk factors for diabetes in subjects with impaired glucose regulation. METHODS: Cross-sectional, population-based study comprising systemic characteristics in 6487 participants and ocular characteristics in 970 participants. RESULTS: Lens fluorescence, a quantitative index of life-long cumulative glycemia, was increased by 7.5% (CI(95) 0.37-15.1%) in subjects with impaired fasting glucose, by 13.0% (CI(95) 5.5-21%) in subjects with combined impaired fasting glucose and impaired glucose tolerance (IFG+IGT), and by 11.8% (CI(95) 6.8-17.1%) in subjects with screen-detected diabetes compared to normoglycemic subjects, adjusted for age, sex, and smoking. The prevalences of microalbuminuria and retinopathy were significantly increased in subjects with screen-detected diabetes after adjusting for age, sex and systolic blood pressure. The prevalences of associated risk factors for diabetes were elevated in all categories of abnormal glucose regulation compared to normoglycemic subjects. CONCLUSIONS: Life-long cumulative glycemia, microangiopathy, and associated risk factors for diabetes were significantly elevated in subjects with abnormal glucose metabolism, most prominently in subjects with IFG+IGT and in subjects with screen-detected diabetes. These results provide the first objective evidence that cumulative glycemic load is increased at the earliest stage of impaired glucose regulation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Munch, Inger Christine","Larsen, Michael","Kessel, Line","Borch-Johnsen, Knut","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Glümer, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-480627"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cumulative glycemia and microangiopathy in subjects with impaired glucose regulation in the inter000000000099 study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2010.10.017","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-480627","identifier":[{"id":"21130512","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79952042630","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-91eb0361-66a2-4e8b-81f6-7feead3f5952"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BE7CC8EE6FA24763057B638E3DF9C0A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2010.10.017","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Knut","key":"borchjohnsenpau","last":"Borch-Johnsen","name":"Borch-Johnsen, Knut","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"glümerpau","last":"Glümer","name":"Glümer, Charlotte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21130512"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.diabres.2010.10.017","issn":["01688227","15721671"],"issn_org":["01688227"],"issue":"2","journal":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","pages":"226-32","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","volume":"91"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952042630"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-91eb0361-66a2-4e8b-81f6-7feead3f5952"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cumulative glycemia and microangiopathy in subjects with impaired glucose regulation in the Inter99 study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-480627","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Birch-allergic patients often experience oral allergy syndrome upon ingestion of vegetables and fruits, most prominently apple, that is caused by antibody cross-reactivity of the IgE antibodies in patients to proteins sharing molecular surface structures with the major birch pollen group 1 allergen from Betula verrucosa (Bet v 1). Still, to what extent two molecular surfaces need to be similar for clinically relevant antibody cross-reactivity to occur is unknown. Here, we describe the grafting of a defined conformational antibody epitope from Bet v 1 onto the surface of the homologous apple allergen Malus domestica group 1 (Mal d 1). Engineering of the epitope was accomplished by genetic engineering substituting amino acid residues in Mal d 1 differing between Bet v 1 and Mal d 1 within the epitope defined by the mAb BV16. The kinetic parameters characterizing the antibody binding interaction to Bet v 1 and to the mutated Mal d 1 variant, respectively, were assessed by Biacore experiments demonstrating indistinguishable binding kinetics. This demonstrates that a conformational epitope defined by a high affinity antibody-allergen interaction can successfully be grafted onto a homologous scaffold molecule without loss of epitope functionality. Furthermore, we show that increasing surface similarity to Bet v 1 of Mal d 1 variants by substitution of 6-8 residues increased the ability to trigger basophil histamine release with blood from birch-allergic patients not responding to natural Mal d 1. Conversely, reducing surface similarity to Bet v 1 of a Mal d 1 variant by substitution of three residues abolished histamine release in one patient reacting to Mal d 1.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Holm, Jens","Ferreras, Mercedes","Ipsen, Henrik","Würtzen, Peter A","Gajhede, Michael","Larsen, Jørgen N","Lund, Kaare","Spangfort, Michael D"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524062"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALK","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ALK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epitope grafting re creating a conformational bet v 000000000001 antibody epitope on the surface of the homologous apple allergen mal d 000000000001","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M110.194878","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524062","identifier":[{"id":"21454600","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79955953910","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3093831","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-dab64cb7-c49c-4649-9370-b5621a3c15b7"],"keyword":["Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46E4B82726BB990D37A7DC8314CB7B71"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M110.194878","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"alk abello","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ALK","l3nl":"ALK-Abello A/S","l3nn":"ALK-Abello","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ALK-Abello","namevar":["ALK-Abelló"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ALK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mercedes","key":"ferreraspau","last":"Ferreras","name":"Ferreras, Mercedes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"ipsenpau","last":"Ipsen","name":"Ipsen, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter A","key":"würtzenpau","last":"Würtzen","name":"Würtzen, Peter A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"gajhedepau","last":"Gajhede","locid":"0d155f9b-0684-4eeb-a060-a7af8508cc95","name":"Gajhede, Michael","orcid":"0000-0001-9864-2287","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen N","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jørgen N","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kaare","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Kaare","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael D","key":"spangfortpau","last":"Spangfort","name":"Spangfort, Michael D","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21454600"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m110.194878","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"issue":"20","journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"17569-17578","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"286"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79955953910"],"search":{"DAF":["ALK-Abello A/S","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dab64cb7-c49c-4649-9370-b5621a3c15b7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Epitope grafting, re-creating a conformational Bet v 1 antibody epitope on the surface of the homologous apple allergen Mal d 1","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524062","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
