{"abstract":"Imaging studies of spontaneous migraine aura have proved challenging because of the episodic and unpredictable nature of migraine attacks. Two patients with signs of acute ischemic stroke were evaluated for thrombolysis and turned out to suffer from familial hemiplegic migraine. It was possible to record the early phase of the hemiplegic aura with computed tomography with perfusion sequences and magnetic resonance imaging. We found cerebral hypoperfusion in the relevant cortical areas within the first hour after onset of aura symptoms. This report supports the concept that migraine aura across the migraine spectrum is caused by similar mechanisms. In a setting with efficient cooperation between headache and stroke neurologists, thrombolysis centers provide the set-up and opportunity to record aura symptoms at an early phase. Furthermore, in the time of ready access to acute systemic thrombolysis treatment, these cases underscore the importance of an accurate headache history, especially in younger patients.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Jakob M","Schytz, Henrik W","Larsen, Vibeke A","Iversen, Helle K","Ashina, Messoud"],"cuid":["S02-080.65-042198"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute Disease","Adult","Brain Ischemia","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Diffusion tensor imaging","Disease Progression","Hemiplegia","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Migraine with Aura"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hemiplegic migraine aura begins with cerebral hypoperfusion imaging in the acute phase","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1526-4610.2011.01963.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-080.65-042198","identifier":[{"id":"80052414632","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21797860","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4bbf742a-b4f4-4043-ac37-309a6f4e0d1b","ku-e5101942-cebf-4c0a-8d2d-d8c2f9410a98"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Adult","Brain Ischemia","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Diffusion Tensor Imaging","Disease Progression","Hemiplegia","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Migraine with Aura"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9D07FF97EF1C860779CC26BAD8FF8926"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1526-4610.2011.01963.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jakob M","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jakob M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik W","key":"schytzpau","last":"Schytz","name":"Schytz, Henrik W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vibeke A","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle Klingenberg","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"02552302-5333-48e0-acde-b9a821eab783","name":"Iversen, Helle Klingenberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Messoud","key":"ashinapau","last":"Ashina","locid":"0e941844-26c5-4777-a66a-64a163c19cd2","name":"Ashina, Messoud","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21797860"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1526-4610.2011.01963.x","issn":["00178748","15264610"],"issn_org":["15264610"],"issue":"8","journal":"Headache","pages":"1289-96","status":"p","title":"Headache","title_org":"Headache Online","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052414632"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4bbf742a-b4f4-4043-ac37-309a6f4e0d1b","ku-e5101942-cebf-4c0a-8d2d-d8c2f9410a98"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hemiplegic migraine aura begins with cerebral hypoperfusion : imaging in the acute phase","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.65-042198","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
